{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_2","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"This is a massive game-building objective.\n\nSTAGE.md instructs building the game described in PLAN.md. TASK.md provides file names and hand-in requirements. PROGRESS.md tracks progress for resuming after context compaction.\n\nThe plan targets a complete original game inspired by Trauma Center: Second Opinion, built with the shardfall engine and delivered as a single HTML file plus exit-interview.json.\n\nIt will specify OUTCOMES rather than architecture. Module layouts, class names, and function names are excluded. Acceptance criteria will be small, ideally three to five items. For interactive elements, verification will anchor on static structural checks, unit tests, and browser launch validation instead of requiring manual playthrough.\n\nThe objective names an established canon game, so the plan writer must first research Trauma Center: Second Opinion with web_search before proceeding.\n\nThe frozen plan is the implementer's contract on observable outcomes. PLAN.md is the definitive specification. TASK.md frames the result as an original inspired by the source rather than a clone. The objective covers all computer-performed PLAN.md work plus every TASK.md hand-in requirement.\n\nThe deliverables are being mapped to acceptance criteria. The plan will require a single HTML file with a specific naming pattern, a matching dev subfolder, exit-interview.json in the root, a feature-complete vertical slice, passing tests via one command, source attribution in credits, and a title chosen by random selection.\n\nThe acceptance criteria are being grouped into the required three to five items. Core mechanics such as audio, multiplayer, and controller modes will not be silently omitted. The plan must also require no TODOs or stubs.\n\nThe deliverable is an original game inspired by Trauma Center, not a clone. PLAN.md already defines the core mechanics and world, so the plan will anchor on those original specifications rather than source canon.\n\nThe engine is remote. PLAN.md already documents shardfall and the AI Hub protocol extensively, so only Trauma Center: Second Opinion needs a brief web search to confirm its defining mechanics.\n\nThe defining mechanics of Trauma Center: Second Opinion are now identified. These include pointer-precision surgical gestures under a timer, patient vitals as the health bar, a time-slow special power, complications and twists in operations, score rankings, visual-novel story segments between procedures, and impossible disease bosses.\n\nPLAN.md already translates these into the game design. The acceptance criteria will therefore capture observable outcomes rather than restate the full architecture.\n\nThe first acceptance criterion is being drafted. It covers deliverables, the About screen, and the title.\n\nThe second acceptance criterion is being drafted. It requires a fully playable surgical loop with the eight instruments, gesture-based operations, vitals and heartbeat clocking, rating and rank systems, completion of campaign cases zero through seven plus Code Blue, and story frames in the specified world tone.\n\nThe third acceptance criterion covers the UX contract. It requires a 10-foot controller-first interface with native keyboard and mouse support, prompts that follow the last device used, title and menu screens, an attract mode after ten seconds of idle time, a touch-only message, dev mode from pause with live sliders and reset, and settings including music defaulting to ten percent.\n\nThe fourth acceptance criterion establishes the audio and art identity. It mandates procedural audio for music, sound effects, and voices without external files, a music bus default of zero point one, animalese voices, the specified operative field and paper-theatre story look, and new instrument and strain assets.\n\nThe fifth acceptance criterion covers multiplayer and testing. It requires local one-to-four player Code Blue, AI Hub shared-world Code Blue per protocol, a single test command that prints only failures and a count, passing Rust, browser, and hub checks, and HTML running from file://.\n\nThe plan now has five criteria covering all must-haves. The writer is refining them to be more independently checkable while still grouping closely related mechanics into single outcomes.\n\nThe first acceptance criterion is being tightened. It now specifies the exact HTML filename pattern, requires exit-interview.json to parse with required keys and a usage field set to \"added on import\", and mandates that about-data JSON in the page matches the interview data.\n\nThe surgical campaign criterion is being drafted. It requires a headless bot to win every case and Code Blue, while an idle or spam player loses. All tools, hazards, strains, gifts, and codes must be exercised. Ratings, chain, on-beat, ranks through ENCORE, vitals and BPM coupling, and checkpoint retry must behave as specified. Deterministic rewind and replay are also required.\n\nHub multiplayer is now defined as a standalone game outside sessions, with one shared-world Code Blue round inside using the protocol's session.js unmodified first script, tags, card, host-authoritative snapshots, and client mirror. Harness scenarios must pass.\n\nThe launch criterion requires the HTML to boot from file:// in Chromium with WebGPU flags, no engine overlay chrome, correct title, and a driven input that changes game state. The primary observable is the operative or title surface substantially rendered, or captured evidence that the launcher cannot run.\n\nThe surgical campaign and UX criteria remain large, but they will be treated as single independently checkable outcomes. The verification plan must map concrete steps to each criterion. For browser pages, the harness will run pure logic unit tests, confirm scripts load in a browser-like environment, gate launch with Playwright by checking zero page errors, render surface dimensions, substantial fill, and visible change from driven input, and require multiple consistent successful runs.\n\nThe plan must require the game to run from a single HTML file opened directly from disk with embedded WASM. The verification plan must include real in-repo tests, captured output under a scratch directory, and one gating step that adds or updates tests. The implementer writes both the game and its tests; the goal plan only specifies what evidence to produce. File layout will not be prescribed, since PLAN.md already defines it in detail.\n\nImplementation guidance will be provided without becoming the acceptance contract. Non-goals include FPS optimization, source IP reuse, physical controllers, real iOS, second human players, audio files, touch controls, and dense web UI. The assumed scope is a workspace folder containing a cloned shardfall engine in a dev subfolder, an ai-hub session client, a single HTML output, exit-interview.json, and PROGRESS.md.\n\nScope is enormous for one implementer. PLAN.md permits cutting sets, waves, and case length but never tools, gifts, screens, or cases three and seven.\n\nWebGPU headless screenshots may be blank. PLAN.md requires SwiftShader flags to render real pixels. The goal plan should treat blank readback as the app's fault.\n\nEarlyoom kills browsers. Shared machines must not kill other processes.\n\nThe title is RNG-chosen. Verification must match the filename pattern rather than a specific title.\n\nTests must run before the engine target folder is deleted, or they must live outside it. Physical controllers, touch devices, real listeners, second players, real iPhones, and TVs are unavailable; stand-ins are the bar. The engine target directory should be removed after verification so the HTML output is the sole deliverable. The writer will research Trauma Center and review shardfall's START_HERE to avoid inventing false engine facts.\n\nThe plan is being validated against Trauma Center defining mechanics. The game requires Wii remote pointer surgery, nunchuk tool selection, dropping vital signs, a Healing Touch star-draw ability that slows time, operation missions with story, score ranks from XS to C, and GUILT strains named after days.\n\nThe plan forbids using source names, so acceptance criteria must require the PLAN's translated mechanics rather than literal source terms. A potential contradiction between TASK's single HTML filename and its subfolder requirement also needs checking.\n\nThe source title \"Trauma Center: Second Opinion\" contains colons and spaces. PLAN.md forbids naming the deliverable, so the filename pattern must substitute GameTitle and SOURCE tokens literally without sanitization.","signature":""},{"type":"text","text":"The stage file points at a full game spec. I’ll confirm Trauma Center’s defining mechanics, then freeze only the outcomes that spec actually requires."},{"type":"server_tool_use","id":"ws_83409307-0730-91a9-b167-3b374932a5bb_call-6a05e1d3-4d50-4b62-b03b-38567b7a89c6-5","name":"web_search","input":{"query":"Trauma Center: Second Opinion gameplay mechanics tools vitals Healing Touch GUILT ranks operations"}},{"type":"web_search_tool_result","tool_use_id":"ws_83409307-0730-91a9-b167-3b374932a5bb_call-6a05e1d3-4d50-4b62-b03b-38567b7a89c6-5","content":[{"type":"web_search_result","url":"https://strategywiki.org/wiki/Trauma_Center:_Second_Opinion/Gameplay","title":"https://strategywiki.org/wiki/Trauma_Center:_Second_Opinion/Gameplay"},{"type":"web_search_result","url":"https://traumacentergame.fandom.com/wiki/Vitals","title":"https://traumacentergame.fandom.com/wiki/Vitals"},{"type":"web_search_result","url":"https://scathingaccuracy.com/guides/trauma-center-second-opinion-xs-guide/","title":"https://scathingaccuracy.com/guides/trauma-center-second-opinion-xs-guide/"},{"type":"web_search_result","url":"https://traumacentergame.fandom.com/wiki/Surgical_Tools","title":"https://traumacentergame.fandom.com/wiki/Surgical_Tools"},{"type":"web_search_result","url":"https://gamefaqs.gamespot.com/wii/933018-trauma-center-second-opinion/faqs/45940","title":"https://gamefaqs.gamespot.com/wii/933018-trauma-center-second-opinion/faqs/45940"}]},{"type":"server_tool_use","id":"ws_83409307-0730-91a9-b167-3b374932a5bb_call-6a05e1d3-4d50-4b62-b03b-38567b7a89c6-6","name":"web_search","input":{"query":"Trauma Center Second Opinion Wii tool selection nunchuk pointer operation scoring vital signs"}},{"type":"web_search_tool_result","tool_use_id":"ws_83409307-0730-91a9-b167-3b374932a5bb_call-6a05e1d3-4d50-4b62-b03b-38567b7a89c6-6","content":[{"type":"web_search_result","url":"https://gamefaqs.gamespot.com/wii/933018-trauma-center-second-opinion/faqs/46894","title":"https://gamefaqs.gamespot.com/wii/933018-trauma-center-second-opinion/faqs/46894"},{"type":"web_search_result","url":"https://www.nintendolife.com/reviews/2007/01/trauma_center_second_opinion_wii","title":"https://www.nintendolife.com/reviews/2007/01/trauma_center_second_opinion_wii"},{"type":"web_search_result","url":"https://gamefaqs.gamespot.com/wii/933018-trauma-center-second-opinion/faqs/51560","title":"https://gamefaqs.gamespot.com/wii/933018-trauma-center-second-opinion/faqs/51560"}]},{"type":"text","text":"Defining mechanics match the spec: timed pointer surgery, vitals, ranks, a special gift, and operation-story pacing. I’ll freeze those as outcomes, not a file layout."},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-6a05e1d3-4d50-4b62-b03b-38567b7a89c6-7","name":"write","input":{"file_path":"/home/micha/.grok/sessions/%2Fhome%2Fmicha%2Fdev%2Fcc-matrix%2Fruns%2Fgrok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224015__x42677a%2Fwork/01a1aa38-de6f-7dc0-ae0d-e0f717ed75f2/goal/plan-01a1aa38-e139-77b1-9a87-6ecdfcbae02e.md","content":"# Plan: Build the original surgical-action drama in workspace PLAN.md and hand in the TASK.md package\n\n## Goal kind\ncode-change\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n1. The work folder contains `PROGRESS.md`, a dev subfolder, and beside it one self-contained HTML file whose basename is `{GameTitle}-Trauma Center: Second Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-224015` (the same name as the dev subfolder). `{GameTitle}` is one playful riff on the source name, chosen with a real RNG and stored so the title screen, page title, hub card, and About screen match. `exit-interview.json` in that same root parses as one object in TASK.md’s exact shape: `usage` is exactly `added on import`; feedback arrays follow the question order; `aiHub` is filled. The page embeds those answers in `<script type=\"application/json\" id=\"about-data\">` and the About screen shows Source Information, Testing Feedback, Engine Feedback, and Prompt Feedback. Shipped game content has no TODOs, placeholders, or stubbed features, and does not use the source’s world (Hope Hospital, Caduceus, Stiles, GUILT, Healing Touch, COOL/XS, or its other proper names).\n2. From each case’s own start, a deterministic sim (no GPU) plays surgeon slots on a fixed overhead field: eight-way tool select with no menu; Scalpel, Forceps, Suture, Suction, Laser, Gel, Scanner, IV Push, plus contextual Cryoprobe, Dressing, and Defibrillator, each with its own gesture, rating, and misuse; the hazards, vitals 0–100, one heartbeat clock (BPM rises as vitals fall), on-beat window, Code with timed defibrillation, chains, and ranks C/B/A/S/ENCORE; gifts the Hush, the Echo, and the Duet. Cases 0–7 (The First Movement, original cast and R.E.Q.U.I.E.M. strains Introit, Lacrimosa, Dies Irae, Libera Me) and Code Blue each finish under the bot at skill 1.0 and are lost by an idle or random-tool player. A campaign run from its start exercises every tool, hazard, strain phase, gift, and Code. Retry after death restores the last checkpoint. Rewind and replay hashes match.\n3. The same screens serve a standard-mapping pad and mouse/keyboard (PLAN control table): prompts switch immediately to PlayStation glyphs, Xbox glyphs when that setting is on, or keys/mouse, matching the last device. Title and main menu (Continue, New Game, Case Files, Code Blue, Settings, About) go to attract after 10 seconds without input; any key, mouse move/click, pad button/stick, or tap returns to the title. Touch-only shows “Controller or keyboard required” and a Settings control, with no touch gameplay, and attract still runs. Pause opens Dev Mode with the live balance sliders, defaults marked, and Reset All. Music, effects, and voices are synthesized in code with no audio files; voices are short gibberish syllables; the music bus and Music setting default to 10% (gain 0.10). Story text is original, earnest medical melodrama between operations and short clinical lines during them.\n4. With no hub, the title and campaign run normally and Code Blue plus cases accept 1–4 local surgeons. In a hub session the only round is shared-world Code Blue, seats 1–4, 4 minutes, with the required `hub:session*` tags, unmodified `session.js` as the first script, a pre-op card, host-authoritative snapshots, and a client mirror. The harness passes `players=4&latency=150&jitter=50&loss=5`, the same with `scenario=host-leave`, `players=2&scenario=server`, and `players=1` (auto). A second page’s input moves that surgeon’s cursor on the host, and both pages report the same vitals. `AIHub.server` runs the world without a local slot or drawing.\n5. The packed HTML starts from `file://` in Chromium (WebGPU software flags). Two consecutive launches each show no page errors, the chosen title rather than Shardfall overlays, a render surface whose drawing size equals the requested viewport and is substantially painted, and a driven pad or mouse input that changes reported game state the same way both times. The single test command prints only failures and one `N passed, M failed` line, and that run is green, including the sim, shell, audio, browser, and hub checks above.\n\n## Verification plan\n1. gating: From the dev folder, run the one suite command (expected `tests/run_all.py` without `python -I`) after it includes real tests that construct each case, tool, hazard, gift, Code, rank, chain, beat window, and checkpoint from the shipped sim’s start state — not a reimplementation or a mid-scene skip. Capture stdout/stderr to `{SCRATCH}/suite.txt`. Must show exit 0, no failure lines, and `N passed, 0 failed`. Must include: bot wins every case and the campaign on 10 seeds at skill 1.0; idle and random-tool play lose every case; snapshot, rewind, and replay hashes match; coverage counters fire for every tool, hazard, strain phase, gift, and Code; content lint parses with no empty line and no TODO; music default gain 0.10; every cue, voice, and track renders non-silent offline.\n2. gating: The same suite, or a headless UI driver it calls, sends pad, keyboard, and mouse through every screen from the title’s initial state. Observations that must pass: hover moves focus; confirm activates; prompts follow the last device and the Xbox setting; attract starts at 10 seconds of no input and exits on key, pad, and mouse; touch-only shows the required sentence and Settings and no touch controls; dev sliders change live values and Reset All restores defaults; About contains every TASK section and `Usage: added on import`.\n3. gating: Launch the root HTML from `file://` twice, new browser each time, Chromium with `--enable-unsafe-webgpu --enable-features=Vulkan --use-webgpu-adapter=swiftshader --use-vulkan=swiftshader --use-angle=swiftshader`, viewport 1920×1080. Stub a standard-mapping DualSense before load. Capture console, `window.__game` status, and a screenshot to `{SCRATCH}/launch-1/` and `{SCRATCH}/launch-2/`. Both runs: zero page errors; title is the chosen game name; no engine boot, stats, guide, hint, toast, or touch overlay; canvas drawing size equals 1920×1080 and the painted area covers most of the surface; status reports music 0.10; a stick/button or mouse input changes focus, screen, or cursor in status the same way both times. A blank or partial buffer from a successful readback fails. If the browser cannot start or is killed by the environment, save that log under `{SCRATCH}/launch-env.txt` and then the green sim/shell suite is the bar — do not invent a screenshot.\n4. gating: Serve the packed game next to the hub harness on `127.0.0.1` and an OS-picked port (`python3 -u -m http.server`). Confirm the body is this game, then require `document.body.dataset.complete === 'true'` and `window.__hubCheck.pass` for the four queries in criterion 4. Then two pages: client aim changes the host cursor for that seat; vitals match. Then one page outside a session: the title is shown and play does not depend on the hub. Write the log to `{SCRATCH}/hub.txt`. Stop only that server PID.\n5. gating: Parse `exit-interview.json` and the page’s `about-data` block; they must match each other and criterion 1. The HTML basename and the dev subfolder must match the pattern. A search of shipped story, UI strings, and ranks must not find the banned source names in criterion 1.\n6. evidence: Save 1920×1080 screenshots of title, operation, story, results, dev, and about under `{SCRATCH}/shots/`. Balance output (wins, time, vitals, suggested par at skills 1.0, 0.7, 0.4, and 0) goes to `{SCRATCH}/balance.txt`. These do not override a green suite.\n\n## Non-goals\n- FPS targets, optimization, or keeping `engine/target` after the final pack (delete it when the HTML is done).\n- Copying Trauma Center’s hospital, cast, GUILT strains, Healing Touch star, organisations, UI, music, or rank words. The source name appears only in the filename, Source Information, and the title riff.\n- A longer campaign than cases 0–7 plus Code Blue. Fewer sets or shorter strain waves are allowed only if every tool, gift, screen, Case 3, and Case 7 remain.\n- Touch gameplay, audio files, a physical DualSense, real iOS Safari, a second human, a TV, or a listening test. Stand-ins in TASK.md are enough.\n- Hub modes other than one shared-world Code Blue round, chat, or pause inside a session.\n- Shardfall’s own pause menu, touch layer, demo overlays, and starter scene as this game’s UI.\n\n## Assumed scope\nWork root only. New dev subfolder; clone `https://github.com/michaelcrosato/shardfall` at or after `49ef2ba` inside it; ai-hub `lib/hub` (`session.js` unmodified, plus harness, bridge, round). Engine crates and `scripts/build-web.sh` / `pack_single_html.py` may change. Embed the OFL Barlow Condensed file from the URL in PLAN.md. Playwright 1.63 (Python), Rust 1.98.1, wasm32 target, and wasm-bindgen 0.2.129 are already installed. Research already done for this plan: Second Opinion is pointer surgery, nunchuk/stick tool wheel (~8 tools), vitals and a timer as fail states, gesture ratings and letter ranks up to XS, chapter story around operations, a limited Healing Touch, and defibrillation. PLAN.md’s original remake of those mechanics is the contract, not a remake of the licensed game.\n\n## Implementation approach\nKeep rules in one deterministic sim the headless tools can tick: surgeon slots, heartbeat, tools, strains, story phases, and the bot live there, with no wall clock, threads, or files. Drive the cursor in real time during the Hush via scaled sim dt, not the engine speed control. Let rendering, egui shell, and audio only read a single frame snapshot plus cue ids, so a browser client can decode the same snapshot. Keep the shell’s input abstract so pad, mouse, and tests share it, including while the sim is paused. Put cases, lines, plates, and rigs in text with file-and-line errors. Expose status, step, and shell commands on `window.__game` for the browser. Pack one HTML that works from `file://`. These are structure hints, not a required layout.\n\n## Task checklist\n- [ ] Clone the engine in the dev subfolder, confirm the commit, read its start and make-a-game docs, pick the title with a real RNG, and start `PROGRESS.md`.\n- [ ] Open the sim/input/camera/product seams and ship one overhead operation (field, vitals, heartbeat, one tool, bot win) that also boots in the packed page with the session client in place.\n- [ ] Add every instrument, hazard, rating, chain, Code, death/retry, and cases 0–2 as data; teach the bot; add the cue table and coverage tests.\n- [ ] Add the 10-foot shell: menus, pause, settings, save, glyphs, attract, touch-only, and dev sliders with reset.\n- [ ] Add paper-theatre story, music buses at music gain 0.10, and gibberish voices through case 7’s script.\n- [ ] Add the four strains, Hush, Echo, tremor, Cryoprobe, Duet, cases 3–7, local 1–4 play, and Code Blue.\n- [ ] Add the hub shim, card, mirror scene, and host snapshots; pass the harness and the two-page cursor/vitals check.\n- [ ] Balance, write `exit-interview.json` and the about block, pack the single HTML to the work root, delete `engine/target`, and save the green suite plus two launch captures under `{SCRATCH}`.\n\n## Risks / Contradictions\n- PLAN.md allows cutting sets and strain length if time runs out, but forbids cutting any tool, gift, screen, Case 3, or Case 7. A build that drops a forbidden piece is not done.\n- The HTML basename must contain the source string `Trauma Center: Second Opinion`, including the colon. Do not sanitize it away.\n- The title is chosen at implementation time, so this plan cannot name the file. Match the pattern.\n- Headless WebGPU pixels need the swiftshader flags; a successful blank capture is a game failure. If earlyoom or a missing display kills the browser, keep the log and use the sim/shell bar only in that case.\n- Other agents share this machine. Do not `pkill`, `killall`, or kill a port you did not bind; stop only PIDs this work started. Keep files inside the work folder.\n"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":27771,"output_tokens":13195,"cache_read_input_tokens":55552,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa38-de6f-7dc0-ae0d-e0f717ed75f2","uuid":"2c239ae2-4266-474b-b843-6cdcb70fee6c"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-6a05e1d3-4d50-4b62-b03b-38567b7a89c6-7","content":"{\"type\":\"SearchReplace\",\"EditsApplied\":{\"old_string\":\"\",\"new_string\":\"# Plan: Build the original surgical-action drama in workspace PLAN.md and hand in the TASK.md package\\n\\n## Goal kind\\ncode-change\\n\\n## Acceptance criteria\\n1. The work folder contains `PROGRESS.md`, a dev subfolder, and beside it one self-contained HTML file whose basename is `{GameTitle}-Trauma Center: Second Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-224015` (the same name as the dev subfolder). `{GameTitle}` is one playful riff on the source name, chosen with a real RNG and stored so the title screen, page title, hub card, and About screen match. `exit-interview.json` in that same root parses as one object in TASK.md’s exact shape: `usage` is exactly `added on import`; feedback arrays follow the question order; `aiHub` is filled. The page embeds those answers in `<script type=\\\"application/json\\\" id=\\\"about-data\\\">` and the About screen shows Source Information, Testing Feedback, Engine Feedback, and Prompt Feedback. Shipped game content has no TODOs, placeholders, or stubbed features, and does not use the source’s world (Hope Hospital, Caduceus, Stiles, GUILT, Healing Touch, COOL/XS, or its other proper names).\\n2. From each case’s own start, a deterministic sim (no GPU) plays surgeon slots on a fixed overhead field: eight-way tool select with no menu; Scalpel, Forceps, Suture, Suction, Laser, Gel, Scanner, IV Push, plus contextual Cryoprobe, Dressing, and Defibrillator, each with its own gesture, rating, and misuse; the hazards, vitals 0–100, one heartbeat clock (BPM rises as vitals fall), on-beat window, Code with timed defibrillation, chains, and ranks C/B/A/S/ENCORE; gifts the Hush, the Echo, and the Duet. Cases 0–7 (The First Movement, original cast and R.E.Q.U.I.E.M. strains Introit, Lacrimosa, Dies Irae, Libera Me) and Code Blue each finish under the bot at skill 1.0 and are lost by an idle or random-tool player. A campaign run from its start exercises every tool, hazard, strain phase, gift, and Code. Retry after death restores the last checkpoint. Rewind and replay hashes match.\\n3. The same screens serve a standard-mapping pad and mouse/keyboard (PLAN control table): prompts switch immediately to PlayStation glyphs, Xbox glyphs when that setting is on, or keys/mouse, matching the last device. Title and main menu (Continue, New Game, Case Files, Code Blue, Settings, About) go to attract after 10 seconds without input; any key, mouse move/click, pad button/stick, or tap returns to the title. Touch-only shows “Controller or keyboard required” and a Settings control, with no touch gameplay, and attract still runs. Pause opens Dev Mode with the live balance sliders, defaults marked, and Reset All. Music, effects, and voices are synthesized in code with no audio files; voices are short gibberish syllables; the music bus and Music setting default to 10% (gain 0.10). Story text is original, earnest medical melodrama between operations and short clinical lines during them.\\n4. With no hub, the title and campaign run normally and Code Blue plus cases accept 1–4 local surgeons. In a hub session the only round is shared-world Code Blue, seats 1–4, 4 minutes, with the required `hub:session*` tags, unmodified `session.js` as the first script, a pre-op card, host-authoritative snapshots, and a client mirror. The harness passes `players=4&latency=150&jitter=50&loss=5`, the same with `scenario=host-leave`, `players=2&scenario=server`, and `players=1` (auto). A second page’s input moves that surgeon’s cursor on the host, and both pages report the same vitals. `AIHub.server` runs the world without a local slot or drawing.\\n5. The packed HTML starts from `file://` in Chromium (WebGPU software flags). Two consecutive launches each show no page errors, the chosen title rather than Shardfall overlays, a render surface whose drawing size equals the requested viewport and is substantially painted, and a driven pad or mouse input that changes reported game state the same way both times. The single test command prints only failures and one `N passed, M failed` line, and that run is green, including the sim, shell, audio, browser, and hub checks above.\\n\\n## Verification plan\\n1. gating: From the dev folder, run the one suite command (expected `tests/run_all.py` without `python -I`) after it includes real tests that construct each case, tool, hazard, gift, Code, rank, chain, beat window, and checkpoint from the shipped sim’s start state — not a reimplementation or a mid-scene skip. Capture stdout/stderr to `{SCRATCH}/suite.txt`. Must show exit 0, no failure lines, and `N passed, 0 failed`. Must include: bot wins every case and the campaign on 10 seeds at skill 1.0; idle and random-tool play lose every case; snapshot, rewind, and replay hashes match; coverage counters fire for every tool, hazard, strain phase, gift, and Code; content lint parses with no empty line and no TODO; music default gain 0.10; every cue, voice, and track renders non-silent offline.\\n2. gating: The same suite, or a headless UI driver it calls, sends pad, keyboard, and mouse through every screen from the title’s initial state. Observations that must pass: hover moves focus; confirm activates; prompts follow the last device and the Xbox setting; attract starts at 10 seconds of no input and exits on key, pad, and mouse; touch-only shows the required sentence and Settings and no touch controls; dev sliders change live values and Reset All restores defaults; About contains every TASK section and `Usage: added on import`.\\n3. gating: Launch the root HTML from `file://` twice, new browser each time, Chromium with `--enable-unsafe-webgpu --enable-features=Vulkan --use-webgpu-adapter=swiftshader --use-vulkan=swiftshader --use-angle=swiftshader`, viewport 1920×1080. Stub a standard-mapping DualSense before load. Capture console, `window.__game` status, and a screenshot to `{SCRATCH}/launch-1/` and `{SCRATCH}/launch-2/`. Both runs: zero page errors; title is the chosen game name; no engine boot, stats, guide, hint, toast, or touch overlay; canvas drawing size equals 1920×1080 and the painted area covers most of the surface; status reports music 0.10; a stick/button or mouse input changes focus, screen, or cursor in status the same way both times. A blank or partial buffer from a successful readback fails. If the browser cannot start or is killed by the environment, save that log under `{SCRATCH}/launch-env.txt` and then the green sim/shell suite is the bar — do not invent a screenshot.\\n4. gating: Serve the packed game next to the hub harness on `127.0.0.1` and an OS-picked port (`python3 -u -m http.server`). Confirm the body is this game, then require `document.body.dataset.complete === 'true'` and `window.__hubCheck.pass` for the four queries in criterion 4. Then two pages: client aim changes the host cursor for that seat; vitals match. Then one page outside a session: the title is shown and play does not depend on the hub. Write the log to `{SCRATCH}/hub.txt`. Stop only that server PID.\\n5. gating: Parse `exit-interview.json` and the page’s `about-data` block; they must match each other and criterion 1. The HTML basename and the dev subfolder must match the pattern. A search of shipped story, UI strings, and ranks must not find the banned source names in criterion 1.\\n6. evidence: Save 1920×1080 screenshots of title, operation, story, results, dev, and about under `{SCRATCH}/shots/`. Balance output (wins, time, vitals, suggested par at skills 1.0, 0.7, 0.4, and 0) goes to `{SCRATCH}/balance.txt`. These do not override a green suite.\\n\\n## Non-goals\\n- FPS targets, optimization, or keeping `engine/target` after the final pack (delete it when the HTML is done).\\n- Copying Trauma Center’s hospital, cast, GUILT strains, Healing Touch star, organisations, UI, music, or rank words. The source name appears only in the filename, Source Information, and the title riff.\\n- A longer campaign than cases 0–7 plus Code Blue. Fewer sets or shorter strain waves are allowed only if every tool, gift, screen, Case 3, and Case 7 remain.\\n- Touch gameplay, audio files, a physical DualSense, real iOS Safari, a second human, a TV, or a listening test. Stand-ins in TASK.md are enough.\\n- Hub modes other than one shared-world Code Blue round, chat, or pause inside a session.\\n- Shardfall’s own pause menu, touch layer, demo overlays, and starter scene as this game’s UI.\\n\\n## Assumed scope\\nWork root only. New dev subfolder; clone `https://github.com/michaelcrosato/shardfall` at or after `49ef2ba` inside it; ai-hub `lib/hub` (`session.js` unmodified, plus harness, bridge, round). Engine crates and `scripts/build-web.sh` / `pack_single_html.py` may change. Embed the OFL Barlow Condensed file from the URL in PLAN.md. Playwright 1.63 (Python), Rust 1.98.1, wasm32 target, and wasm-bindgen 0.2.129 are already installed. Research already done for this plan: Second Opinion is pointer surgery, nunchuk/stick tool wheel (~8 tools), vitals and a timer as fail states, gesture ratings and letter ranks up to XS, chapter story around operations, a limited Healing Touch, and defibrillation. PLAN.md’s original remake of those mechanics is the contract, not a remake of the licensed game.\\n\\n## Implementation approach\\nKeep rules in one deterministic sim the headless tools can tick: surgeon slots, heartbeat, tools, strains, story phases, and the bot live there, with no wall clock, threads, or files. Drive the cursor in real time during the Hush via scaled sim dt, not the engine speed control. Let rendering, egui shell, and audio only read a single frame snapshot plus cue ids, so a browser client can decode the same snapshot. Keep the shell’s input abstract so pad, mouse, and tests share it, including while the sim is paused. Put cases, lines, plates, and rigs in text with file-and-line errors. Expose status, step, and shell commands on `window.__game` for the browser. Pack one HTML that works from `file://`. These are structure hints, not a required layout.\\n\\n## Task checklist\\n- [ ] Clone the engine in the dev subfolder, confirm the commit, read its start and make-a-game docs, pick the title with a real RNG, and start `PROGRESS.md`.\\n- [ ] Open the sim/input/camera/product seams and ship one overhead operation (field, vitals, heartbeat, one tool, bot win) that also boots in the packed page with the session client in place.\\n- [ ] Add every instrument, hazard, rating, chain, Code, death/retry, and cases 0–2 as data; teach the bot; add the cue table and coverage tests.\\n- [ ] Add the 10-foot shell: menus, pause, settings, save, glyphs, attract, touch-only, and dev sliders with reset.\\n- [ ] Add paper-theatre story, music buses at music gain 0.10, and gibberish voices through case 7’s script.\\n- [ ] Add the four strains, Hush, Echo, tremor, Cryoprobe, Duet, cases 3–7, local 1–4 play, and Code Blue.\\n- [ ] Add the hub shim, card, mirror scene, and host snapshots; pass the harness and the two-page cursor/vitals check.\\n- [ ] Balance, write `exit-interview.json` and the about block, pack the single HTML to the work root, delete `engine/target`, and save the green suite plus two launch captures under `{SCRATCH}`.\\n\\n## Risks / Contradictions\\n- PLAN.md allows cutting sets and strain length if time runs out, but forbids cutting any tool, gift, screen, Case 3, or Case 7. A build that drops a forbidden piece is not done.\\n- The HTML basename must contain the source string `Trauma Center: Second Opinion`, including the colon. Do not sanitize it away.\\n- The title is chosen at implementation time, so this plan cannot name the file. Match the pattern.\\n- Headless WebGPU pixels need the swiftshader flags; a successful blank capture is a game failure. If earlyoom or a missing display kills the browser, keep the log and use the sim/shell bar only in that case.\\n- Other agents share this machine. Do not `pkill`, `killall`, or kill a port you did not bind; stop only PIDs this work started. Keep files inside the work folder.\\n\",\"tool_output_for_prompt\":\"The file /home/micha/.grok/sessions/%2Fhome%2Fmicha%2Fdev%2Fcc-matrix%2Fruns%2Fgrok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224015__x42677a%2Fwork/01a1aa38-de6f-7dc0-ae0d-e0f717ed75f2/goal/plan-01a1aa38-e139-77b1-9a87-6ecdfcbae02e.md has been created.\",\"tool_output_for_prompt_concise\":\"The file /home/micha/.grok/sessions/%2Fhome%2Fmicha%2Fdev%2Fcc-matrix%2Fruns%2Fgrok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224015__x42677a%2Fwork/01a1aa38-de6f-7dc0-ae0d-e0f717ed75f2/goal/plan-01a1aa38-e139-77b1-9a87-6ecdfcbae02e.md has been created.\",\"absolute_path\":\"/home/micha/.grok/sessions/%2Fhome%2Fmicha%2Fdev%2Fcc-matrix%2Fruns%2Fgrok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224015__x42677a%2Fwork/01a1aa38-de6f-7dc0-ae0d-e0f717ed75f2/goal/plan-01a1aa38-e139-77b1-9a87-6ecdfcbae02e.md\",\"edits\":{\"details\":[{\"old_string\":\"\",\"old_line\":1,\"new_string\":\"# Plan: Build the original surgical-action drama in workspace PLAN.md and hand in the TASK.md package\\n\\n## Goal kind\\ncode-change\\n\\n## Acceptance criteria\\n1. The work folder contains `PROGRESS.md`, a dev subfolder, and beside it one self-contained HTML file whose basename is `{GameTitle}-Trauma Center: Second Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-224015` (the same name as the dev subfolder). `{GameTitle}` is one playful riff on the source name, chosen with a real RNG and stored so the title screen, page title, hub card, and About screen match. `exit-interview.json` in that same root parses as one object in TASK.md’s exact shape: `usage` is exactly `added on import`; feedback arrays follow the question order; `aiHub` is filled. The page embeds those answers in `<script type=\\\"application/json\\\" id=\\\"about-data\\\">` and the About screen shows Source Information, Testing Feedback, Engine Feedback, and Prompt Feedback. Shipped game content has no TODOs, placeholders, or stubbed features, and does not use the source’s world (Hope Hospital, Caduceus, Stiles, GUILT, Healing Touch, COOL/XS, or its other proper names).\\n2. From each case’s own start, a deterministic sim (no GPU) plays surgeon slots on a fixed overhead field: eight-way tool select with no menu; Scalpel, Forceps, Suture, Suction, Laser, Gel, Scanner, IV Push, plus contextual Cryoprobe, Dressing, and Defibrillator, each with its own gesture, rating, and misuse; the hazards, vitals 0–100, one heartbeat clock (BPM rises as vitals fall), on-beat window, Code with timed defibrillation, chains, and ranks C/B/A/S/ENCORE; gifts the Hush, the Echo, and the Duet. Cases 0–7 (The First Movement, original cast and R.E.Q.U.I.E.M. strains Introit, Lacrimosa, Dies Irae, Libera Me) and Code Blue each finish under the bot at skill 1.0 and are lost by an idle or random-tool player. A campaign run from its start exercises every tool, hazard, strain phase, gift, and Code. Retry after death restores the last checkpoint. Rewind and replay hashes match.\\n3. The same screens serve a standard-mapping pad and mouse/keyboard (PLAN control table): prompts switch immediately to PlayStation glyphs, Xbox glyphs when that setting is on, or keys/mouse, matching the last device. Title and main menu (Continue, New Game, Case Files, Code Blue, Settings, About) go to attract after 10 seconds without input; any key, mouse move/click, pad button/stick, or tap returns to the title. Touch-only shows “Controller or keyboard required” and a Settings control, with no touch gameplay, and attract still runs. Pause opens Dev Mode with the live balance sliders, defaults marked, and Reset All. Music, effects, and voices are synthesized in code with no audio files; voices are short gibberish syllables; the music bus and Music setting default to 10% (gain 0.10). Story text is original, earnest medical melodrama between operations and short clinical lines during them.\\n4. With no hub, the title and campaign run normally and Code Blue plus cases accept 1–4 local surgeons. In a hub session the only round is shared-world Code Blue, seats 1–4, 4 minutes, with the required `hub:session*` tags, unmodified `session.js` as the first script, a pre-op card, host-authoritative snapshots, and a client mirror. The harness passes `players=4&latency=150&jitter=50&loss=5`, the same with `scenario=host-leave`, `players=2&scenario=server`, and `players=1` (auto). A second page’s input moves that surgeon’s cursor on the host, and both pages report the same vitals. `AIHub.server` runs the world without a local slot or drawing.\\n5. The packed HTML starts from `file://` in Chromium (WebGPU software flags). Two consecutive launches each show no page errors, the chosen title rather than Shardfall overlays, a render surface whose drawing size equals the requested viewport and is substantially painted, and a driven pad or mouse input that changes reported game state the same way both times. The single test command prints only failures and one `N passed, M failed` line, and that run is green, including the sim, shell, audio, browser, and hub checks above.\\n\\n## Verification plan\\n1. gating: From the dev folder, run the one suite command (expected `tests/run_all.py` without `python -I`) after it includes real tests that construct each case, tool, hazard, gift, Code, rank, chain, beat window, and checkpoint from the shipped sim’s start state — not a reimplementation or a mid-scene skip. Capture stdout/stderr to `{SCRATCH}/suite.txt`. Must show exit 0, no failure lines, and `N passed, 0 failed`. Must include: bot wins every case and the campaign on 10 seeds at skill 1.0; idle and random-tool play lose every case; snapshot, rewind, and replay hashes match; coverage counters fire for every tool, hazard, strain phase, gift, and Code; content lint parses with no empty line and no TODO; music default gain 0.10; every cue, voice, and track renders non-silent offline.\\n2. gating: The same suite, or a headless UI driver it calls, sends pad, keyboard, and mouse through every screen from the title’s initial state. Observations that must pass: hover moves focus; confirm activates; prompts follow the last device and the Xbox setting; attract starts at 10 seconds of no input and exits on key, pad, and mouse; touch-only shows the required sentence and Settings and no touch controls; dev sliders change live values and Reset All restores defaults; About contains every TASK section and `Usage: added on import`.\\n3. gating: Launch the root HTML from `file://` twice, new browser each time, Chromium with `--enable-unsafe-webgpu --enable-features=Vulkan --use-webgpu-adapter=swiftshader --use-vulkan=swiftshader --use-angle=swiftshader`, viewport 1920×1080. Stub a standard-mapping DualSense before load. Capture console, `window.__game` status, and a screenshot to `{SCRATCH}/launch-1/` and `{SCRATCH}/launch-2/`. Both runs: zero page errors; title is the chosen game name; no engine boot, stats, guide, hint, toast, or touch overlay; canvas drawing size equals 1920×1080 and the painted area covers most of the surface; status reports music 0.10; a stick/button or mouse input changes focus, screen, or cursor in status the same way both times. A blank or partial buffer from a successful readback fails. If the browser cannot start or is killed by the environment, save that log under `{SCRATCH}/launch-env.txt` and then the green sim/shell suite is the bar — do not invent a screenshot.\\n4. gating: Serve the packed game next to the hub harness on `127.0.0.1` and an OS-picked port (`python3 -u -m http.server`). Confirm the body is this game, then require `document.body.dataset.complete === 'true'` and `window.__hubCheck.pass` for the four queries in criterion 4. Then two pages: client aim changes the host cursor for that seat; vitals match. Then one page outside a session: the title is shown and play does not depend on the hub. Write the log to `{SCRATCH}/hub.txt`. Stop only that server PID.\\n5. gating: Parse `exit-interview.json` and the page’s `about-data` block; they must match each other and criterion 1. The HTML basename and the dev subfolder must match the pattern. A search of shipped story, UI strings, and ranks must not find the banned source names in criterion 1.\\n6. evidence: Save 1920×1080 screenshots of title, operation, story, results, dev, and about under `{SCRATCH}/shots/`. Balance output (wins, time, vitals, suggested par at skills 1.0, 0.7, 0.4, and 0) goes to `{SCRATCH}/balance.txt`. These do not override a green suite.\\n\\n## Non-goals\\n- FPS targets, optimization, or keeping `engine/target` after the final pack (delete it when the HTML is done).\\n- Copying Trauma Center’s hospital, cast, GUILT strains, Healing Touch star, organisations, UI, music, or rank words. The source name appears only in the filename, Source Information, and the title riff.\\n- A longer campaign than cases 0–7 plus Code Blue. Fewer sets or shorter strain waves are allowed only if every tool, gift, screen, Case 3, and Case 7 remain.\\n- Touch gameplay, audio files, a physical DualSense, real iOS Safari, a second human, a TV, or a listening test. Stand-ins in TASK.md are enough.\\n- Hub modes other than one shared-world Code Blue round, chat, or pause inside a session.\\n- Shardfall’s own pause menu, touch layer, demo overlays, and starter scene as this game’s UI.\\n\\n## Assumed scope\\nWork root only. New dev subfolder; clone `https://github.com/michaelcrosato/shardfall` at or after `49ef2ba` inside it; ai-hub `lib/hub` (`session.js` unmodified, plus harness, bridge, round). Engine crates and `scripts/build-web.sh` / `pack_single_html.py` may change. Embed the OFL Barlow Condensed file from the URL in PLAN.md. Playwright 1.63 (Python), Rust 1.98.1, wasm32 target, and wasm-bindgen 0.2.129 are already installed. Research already done for this plan: Second Opinion is pointer surgery, nunchuk/stick tool wheel (~8 tools), vitals and a timer as fail states, gesture ratings and letter ranks up to XS, chapter story around operations, a limited Healing Touch, and defibrillation. PLAN.md’s original remake of those mechanics is the contract, not a remake of the licensed game.\\n\\n## Implementation approach\\nKeep rules in one deterministic sim the headless tools can tick: surgeon slots, heartbeat, tools, strains, story phases, and the bot live there, with no wall clock, threads, or files. Drive the cursor in real time during the Hush via scaled sim dt, not the engine speed control. Let rendering, egui shell, and audio only read a single frame snapshot plus cue ids, so a browser client can decode the same snapshot. Keep the shell’s input abstract so pad, mouse, and tests share it, including while the sim is paused. Put cases, lines, plates, and rigs in text with file-and-line errors. Expose status, step, and shell commands on `window.__game` for the browser. Pack one HTML that works from `file://`. These are structure hints, not a required layout.\\n\\n## Task checklist\\n- [ ] Clone the engine in the dev subfolder, confirm the commit, read its start and make-a-game docs, pick the title with a real RNG, and start `PROGRESS.md`.\\n- [ ] Open the sim/input/camera/product seams and ship one overhead operation (field, vitals, heartbeat, one tool, bot win) that also boots in the packed page with the session client in place.\\n- [ ] Add every instrument, hazard, rating, chain, Code, death/retry, and cases 0–2 as data; teach the bot; add the cue table and coverage tests.\\n- [ ] Add the 10-foot shell: menus, pause, settings, save, glyphs, attract, touch-only, and dev sliders with reset.\\n- [ ] Add paper-theatre story, music buses at music gain 0.10, and gibberish voices through case 7’s script.\\n- [ ] Add the four strains, Hush, Echo, tremor, Cryoprobe, Duet, cases 3–7, local 1–4 play, and Code Blue.\\n- [ ] Add the hub shim, card, mirror scene, and host snapshots; pass the harness and the two-page cursor/vitals check.\\n- [ ] Balance, write `exit-interview.json` and the about block, pack the single HTML to the work root, delete `engine/target`, and save the green suite plus two launch captures under `{SCRATCH}`.\\n\\n## Risks / Contradictions\\n- PLAN.md allows cutting sets and strain length if time runs out, but forbids cutting any tool, gift, screen, Case 3, or Case 7. A build that drops a forbidden piece is not done.\\n- The HTML basename must contain the source string `Trauma Center: Second Opinion`, including the colon. Do not sanitize it away.\\n- The title is chosen at implementation time, so this plan cannot name the file. Match the pattern.\\n- Headless WebGPU pixels need the swiftshader flags; a successful blank capture is a game failure. If earlyoom or a missing display kills the browser, keep the log and use the sim/shell bar only in that case.\\n- Other agents share this machine. Do not `pkill`, `killall`, or kill a port you did not bind; stop only PIDs this work started. Keep files inside the work folder.\\n\",\"new_line\":1,\"context_before\":\"\",\"context_after\":\"\",\"line_prefix\":\"\"}]}}}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa38-de6f-7dc0-ae0d-e0f717ed75f2","uuid":"24daed0b-8127-4734-a262-601654719733"}
