{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_13","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"This is a massive engine. I need to understand how to hook in without breaking anything.\n\nI've mapped the engine's entry points: Sim::frame, Sim::step, RenderFrame constructors, app.rs branching, audio mixer, DynamicMesh API, input parsing, tests, pack script, headless UI, and WASM window access. The plan is to isolate almost all game logic in pav_core/src/games/surgery/ for headless testing without a GPU. Rendering will be handled by a SurgeryFrame consumed by the view.\n\nWebGPU must render the operative field to satisfy the 1920×1080 canvas verification. I need to locate the DynamicMesh API for this. A headless egui shell will also be drawn in the app to support menu-driven tests.\n\nThe browser test inspects the WebGPU canvas directly, not an egui overlay. A large tissue mesh filling the camera view will paint the canvas and satisfy the verification requirement.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-67a32919-f0cb-4544-827c-555954f2a850-20","name":"grep","input":{"pattern":"struct DynamicMesh|fn emit\\(|DynamicMesh \\{","glob":"**/*.rs","path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224015__x42677a/work/Hands of Harbor: Second Opinion-Trauma Center: Second Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-224015/engine/crates","head_limit":40}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-67a32919-f0cb-4544-827c-555954f2a850-21","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224015__x42677a/work/Hands of Harbor: Second Opinion-Trauma Center: Second Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-224015/engine/crates/pav_core/src/sim.rs","offset":470,"limit":50}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-67a32919-f0cb-4544-827c-555954f2a850-22","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224015__x42677a/work/Hands of Harbor: Second Opini