.rs\",\"matches\":[{\"line_number\":662,\"content\":\"pub fn srgb(r: u8, g: u8, b: u8) -> Vec3 {\"},{\"line_number\":676,\"content\":\"pub fn srgb_to_linear(c: f32) -> f32 {\"}]},{\"path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224015__x42677a/work/Hands of Harbor: Second Opinion-Trauma Center: Second Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-224015/engine/crates/pav_tools/src/import/scene.rs\",\"matches\":[{\"line_number\":228,\"content\":\"pub fn srgb_to_linear(c: u8) -> f64 {\"}]}]}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa38-de6f-7dc0-ae0d-e0f717ed75f2","uuid":"ae142284-8030-4f4f-b6d1-ced87e2af591"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_19","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The plan is clear. Implementation begins now.\n\nThe game title is set to \"Hands of Harbor: Second Opinion\". The dev folder and root PROGRESS.md are ready. Core simulation files like `tune.rs` will be written next.\n\nThe implementation plan now covers thirteen modules. These include heart rhythm, surgeon input, field hazards, four strain state machines, case director data, story playback, paper geometry, bot planning, frame logic, network snapshots, and game phase control. Content TOML files are also included.\n\nThe operation model will be discrete and deterministic. Bot completion conditions are simple enough to satisfy at skill 1.0.\n\nEach hazard carries a unified state: kind, position, work units needed, current work, primary tool, stage, drain rate, hidden flag, auxiliary value, and alive flag.\n\nThe surgeon cursor moves toward the aim point. Holding use with the correct tool within radius applies work scaled by pressure and delta time. Quality is tracked by distance error.\n\nCompletion rating is based on average error once work meets the need. Wrong tools trigger a chain reset and callout with zero work applied.\n\nEach tool has distinct parameters:\n- Scalpel: 0.35 radius, 1.2/s along checkpoints, rated by deviation\n- Forceps: 0.45 radius, requires pulling along an axis, rated by angle\n- Suture: 0.4 radius, requires alternating cursor sides, rated by spacing variance\n- Suction: 0.7 radius, work scales with pressure, always Good\n- Laser: 0.4 radius, heat rises until released in a timing band, rated by timing\n\nThe remaining tools are now defined. Gel and dressing use paint coverage. Scanner uses sweep time. IV, cryoprobe, and defib rely on charge-and-release timing windows. The bot algorithm will select the defib, hold charge for 1.2 seconds, and release when the heart phase is in the correct window. It will also trigger gifts on beats when vitals or strain require it.\n\nThe bot will target the highest-priority alive hazard it can handle. It selects the tool, moves the cursor to the gesture point, holds use with the right pressure, and releases at the correct time.\n\nSkill scales cursor speed from 0.15 at level zero up to 1.0. At level zero the surgeon misses everything with a 3.0 unit error and moves at speed 0.2. This guarantees that skill 0 always loses.\n\nSkill 0.4 yields a 0.55 error and 0.45 speed. Skill 0.7 yields 0.22 error and 0.75 speed. Skill 1.0 yields 0.02 error and full speed.\n\nGuided cases use larger hit radii. Later cases use tighter radii and faster drains.\n\nIdle death counts as lost. Every case opens with hazards that drain vitals. The timer also expires.\n\nRandom tool selection is unlikely to succeed. Sustained correct gestures require roughly 1.5 seconds of precise contact, and the probability of randomly landing inside a 0.4 radius target on an 18×8 field is only about 0.3%. Over four minutes, random hits are too sparse to complete multi-stage tasks. Suction is the only exception, since its large radius and always-good rating could theoretically let random play win a case that needs only a few suction hits.\n\nEvery case will require a precise tool sequence, so random play cannot finish the phase list. Phases only advance when clear.\n\nVitals drain even if the player never treats them. Resident code chance is 2 percent. Incorrect defibrillation causes death; random players cannot hit the beat reliably. Two failed codes or missed windows kill the patient. If vitals reach zero while codes remain, a five-second grace period begins.\n\nThe defibrillation gesture now requires both a full 1.2-second charge and release within an ±110 ms window. Random players constantly switch tools, so they cannot hold the charge long enough to succeed.\n\nCases are structured as sequences of phases. Each phase spawns its own hazards, and the next phase begins only after every hazard in that phase is cleared.\n\nCase 0 \"Barbs\" targets Mara's forearm. It opens with suction pools and foreign hooks, then a hidden barb twist requiring scanner and forceps, followed by a laceration suture and dressing.\n\nCase 1 \"Routine\" targets the abdomen. It opens with a scalpel incision, then a polyp cluster treated with laser and gel, a vitals-dropping twist with suture and IV push, and ends with dressing.\n\nCase 2 \"Shrapnel\" targets the chest. It opens with an incision.\n\nCase 2 \"Shrapnel\" continues with hidden shards and pools, a scripted code that resets vitals without counting against the code budget, and a laceration suture followed by dressing.\n\nThe remaining cases are now defined. Case 3 \"Introit\" targets the liver with a three-stage tumor and unlocks the Hush skill. Case 4 \"Lacrimosa\" targets the lung. Case 5 \"Femur\" targets the pet's bone with echo and tremor. Case 6 \"Dies Irae\" targets the pericardium with a cryoprobe. Case 7 \"Libera Me\" is a heart duet with a partner bot in slot one. The Code Blue mode is a four-minute hazard wave that ends when the timer expires.\n\nCode Blue is a survival mode. The team wins if the patient is alive when the timer hits zero. This differs from regular cases, where timer zero means death. The hub round lasts four minutes and serves as the Code Blue timer.\n\nStrain states will use real state machines with named phases so coverage counters fire correctly.\n\nIntroit phases are wander, split, smalls, and amen. Lacrimosa uses wave1, wave2, wave3, and eye. Dies Irae uses embers, merge, and furnace. Libera Me uses a, b, c, stop, soloist, tendril, and close.\n\nEach phase spawns hazards the bot already knows how to clear. The strain director advances only when those hazards clear. This means the bot needs no special strain logic beyond clearing tools plus a few edge cases like heat ring lift-off, defib on ghost beats, and hush or echo triggers.\n\nA heat ring is a timed sweep hazard that cannot be cleared by a normal tool.\n\nA held use gesture during a heat ring sweep causes scorch. The bot releases the button to avoid it.\n\nHush triggers when vitals fall below 35 or a flag is set. The bot holds the gift and releases it on the beat. During hush, rule updates run at 30 percent speed while the cursor moves at full speed. Coverage counter gift_hush fires.\n\nEcho is the pet's gift. It repeats the last completed action on the next target that needs that tool. Coverage counter gift_echo tracks this.\n\nDuet in Libera Me triggers both Hush and Echo together.\n\nTremor adds a deterministic 0.12-unit wander to the pet cursor unless precision, echo, or setting-off is active. The bot can hold precision to disable it. At skill 1.0 the combined error of 0.14 stays inside the 0.45 hit radius.\n\nCryoprobe is tool 8 and behaves like laser with a one-second duration.\n\nScripted codes in cases 2 and 7 set a `scripted_code` flag so they do not consume the code budget.\n\nPar is set to 4500 so a perfect case scores an S. An ENCORE requires 5175 or more.\n\nRating thresholds are defined by average scalpel deviation. Immaculate is under 0.25. Clean is under 0.4. Good is under 0.6. Anything higher is sloppy.\n\nSkill 1.0 noise is 0.02 times random variance. The 0.25 deviation threshold keeps perfect play immaculate.\n\nChain bonuses extend when clean ratings stack, with multipliers at five, ten, and twenty consecutive clean hits.\n\nThe campaign will use roughly two hundred lines of story text in TOML. The bot holds skip to confirm each line and advance the narrative between cases. Story phases do not fail.\n\nA full campaign spans about sixteen thousand ticks per seed, or one hundred sixty-four thousand ticks across all ten seeds.\n\nA perfect bot should clear each case in roughly ninety-six hundred ticks, or about sixteen seconds.\n\nCase 7 is estimated at roughly two thousand five hundred ticks, or about three minutes. The full campaign averages around twelve thousand ticks plus story, which is acceptable.\n\nDifficulty settings are now defined. Resident mode uses normal drain, timer, strain, and two codes. Attending mode increases drain to 1.25, shortens the timer to 0.85, raises strain to 1.15, and reduces codes to one. Chief mode pushes drain to 1.5, timer to 0.7, and strain to 1.3, with zero codes. Tests will run on the default resident level.\n\nCheckpoints save a compact surgery state or phase index whenever a phase begins with a checkpoint flag. A death screen then allows retry from that saved point. The bot does not need to die and retry in normal gameplay; only a unit test requires this behavior.\n\nThe checkpoint stores phase index, vitals, score, chain, hazard snapshot, heart state, and timer. Retry restores these fields exactly.\n\nCampaign scene auto-starts story and operations without menus. `pav play scene=surgery/campaign bot=true` works directly.\n\nScene routing is split: the shell owns title screens, but the sim can enter Title mode for headless runs. A bot on the title screen cannot win.\n\nShell tests will live in pav_ui or pav_core. They will exercise Shell methods directly without rendering, since `cargo test` can drive the shell headlessly. The Shell struct will expose a pure `tick` method that takes input and delta time and returns commands. Tests will verify hover focus movement, confirm activation, and prompt behavior.\n\nShell settings will include an Xbox toggle, a ten-second attract mode that exits on input or mouse, a touch-only notice, and dev sliders for music, effects, and voices. The about screen will list sections.\n\nThe Mixer will gain three new volume controls: music at 0.10, effects at 0.80, and voices at 0.70. Voice routing will use a bus enum. Patch definitions will accept optional formant fields for band-pass filtering, defaulting to zero so existing patches remain valid. A new SimEvent::Cue will carry sound id, position, gain, and pitch, with the sound system resolving cues through a lookup table.\n\nA `render_track` function will synthesize melodies offline for headless tests. The app will also use a sequencer for live playback.\n\nTests in `pav_audio` will assert that every cue, voice, and track produces non-silent audio. They will also verify the default music volume is 0.10.\n\nThe browser product path is flagged as the riskiest part.\n\nThe packed HTML must boot cleanly, show the title, render a 1920×1080 canvas, keep music at 0.10, and expose `window.__game.status`, `step`, and `do` for input. The plan is to branch at the top of `App::frame` when the scene starts with \"surgery\", routing directly into a new `frame_surgery` method instead of using the full frame loop.\n\nThe `frame_surgery` method must live in `app.rs` or use `pub(crate)` fields, because child modules cannot access parent module private fields.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-ce696e16-da8e-4f94-9ac9-1d9c7e2548f4-45","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224015__x42677a/work/Hands of Harbor: Second Opinion-Trauma Center: Second Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-224015/engine/crates/pav_app/src/app.rs","offset":1145,"limit":180}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-ce696e16-da8e-4f94-9ac9-1d9c7e2548f4-46","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224015__x42677a/work/Hands of Harbor: Second Opinion-Trauma Center: Second Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-224015/engine/crates/pav_app/src/simhost.rs","limit":120}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-ce696e16-da8e-4f94-9ac9-1d9c7e2548f4-47","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224015__x42677a/work/Hands of Harbor: Second Opinion-Trauma Center: Second Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-224015/engine/crates/pav_view/src/build.rs","offset":1380,"limit":120}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-ce696e16-da8e-4f94-9ac9-1d9c7e2548f4-48","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224015__x42677a/work/Hands of Harbor: Second Opinion-Trauma Center: Second Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-224015/engine/crates/pav_app/src/app.rs","offset":2120,"limit":80}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":3478,"output_tokens":4656,"cache_read_input_tokens":99712,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa38-de6f-7dc0-ae0d-e0f717ed75f2","uuid":"0a91b819-e045-4733-8f7e-c643a099abc2"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-ce696e16-da8e-4f94-9ac9-1d9c7e2548f4-45","content":"{\"type\":\"ReadFile\",\"FileContent\":{\"content\":\"1145→\\n        // Game input -> the simulation thread.\\n        let (w, h) = self.gfx.as_ref().unwrap().size();\\n        let size = Vec2::new(w as f32, h as f32);\\n        let over_ui = self.egui_ctx.egui_wants_pointer_input();\\n1150→        let left_tap = self.input.take_mouse_tap(MouseButton::Left) && !over_ui;\\n        if over_ui {\\n            self.input.mouse_taps.clear();\\n        }\\n        let (mut held, mut pressed) = self.input.buttons();\\n        // Touch: the stick, the buttons and auto-attack.\\n        let touch_game = curr.game.as_deref().filter(|_| game_input).map(|g| (g, feet, facing));\\n        let rig = &self.rig;\\n        let intent = self.touch.intent(touch_game, |v| rig.relative_move(v), self.prefs.auto_attack);\\n        if game_input {\\n1160→            held |= intent.held;\\n            pressed |= intent.pressed;\\n        }\\n        if pressed & pav_core::input::buttons::INTERACT != 0 {\\n            if let Some(g) = &curr.game {\\n                if let Some(c) = self.game_ui.interact(g) {\\n                    host.shared.command(c);\\n                }\\n            }\\n        }\\n1170→        if pressed != 0 && self.input.last_device == Device::Gamepad {\\n            // Gamepad presses are timed from when they were polled (gilrs queues them).\\n            self.latency.press();\\n        }\\n        let room_id = self.hud.current.as_ref().map(|r| r.id);\\n        let left = self.input.mouse.contains(&MouseButton::Left) && !over_ui;\\n        if left_tap && !self.editor.on && game_input {\\n            pressed |= pav_core::input::buttons::PRIMARY;\\n        }\\n        if !studio_active && self.editor.update(host, &self.rig, self.input.cursor, size, left, left_tap, room_id) {\\n1180→            held &= !pav_core::input::buttons::PRIMARY;\\n            pressed &= !pav_core::input::buttons::PRIMARY;\\n        }\\n        let aim = match self.input.last_device {\\n            Device::KeyboardMouse => self.rig.ground_point(self.input.cursor, size, feet.y),\\n            Device::Gamepad => {\\n                let r = self.input.pad.right;\\n                if r.length() > 0.2 {\\n                    let d = self.rig.relative_move(r);\\n                    Some(feet + Vec3::new(d.x, 0.0, d.y) * self.sim_config.bombs.throw_range * r.length().min(1.0))\\n1190→                } else {\\n                    Some(feet + Vec3::new(facing.sin(), 0.0, facing.cos()) * 4.0)\\n                }\\n            }\\n            Device::Touch => intent.aim.or(Some(feet + Vec3::new(facing.sin(), 0.0, facing.cos()) * 4.0)),\\n        };\\n        {\\n            let mut i = host.shared.input.lock().unwrap();\\n            if game_input {\\n                let axis = (self.input.move_axis() + intent.move_axis).clamp_length_max(1.0);\\n1200→                i.move_dir = match intent.move_world {\\n                    // Auto-attack stepping in to a foe (only while the stick is still).\\n                    Some(m) if axis == Vec2::ZERO => m,\\n                    _ => self.rig.relative_move(axis),\\n                };\\n                i.held = held;\\n                i.pressed |= pressed;\\n                i.aim = aim;\\n                if let Some(t) = self.latency.pending.take() {\\n                    host.shared.input_stamp.lock().unwrap().get_or_insert(t);\\n1210→                }\\n            } else {\\n                *i = InputFrame::default();\\n            }\\n        }\\n\\n        self.rig.update(focus, dt);\\n        self.builder.now = self.started.elapsed().as_secs_f64();\\n        let events: Vec<_> = std::mem::take(&mut *host.shared.events.lock().unwrap());\\n        let events = if studio_active { Vec::new() } else { events };\\n1220→        self.builder.add_events(&events);\\n        // Save the hero on every arrival somewhere, and once a minute while playing.\\n        let travelled = events.iter().any(|e| matches!(e, pav_core::SimEvent::Travel { .. }));\\n        if curr.game.is_some() && (travelled || self.last_save.elapsed().as_secs() >= 60) {\\n            self.last_save = Instant::now();\\n            host.exec(|sim| crate::save::save_from(sim));\\n        }\\n        if let Some(a) = &self.audio {\\n            let (_, right) = self.rig.ground_axes();\\n            let l = pav_audio::Listener { pos: self.rig.target, right };\\n1230→            for e in &events {\\n                if matches!(e, pav_core::SimEvent::Step { .. }) && !self.audio_settings.footsteps {\\n                    continue;\\n                }\\n                a.play_event(e, &l, self.audio_settings.sfx);\\n            }\\n        }\\n        // The look layer (Look & Filters) over the scene's own settings.\\n        let mut view = self.view.clone();\\n        self.look_ui.apply(&mut view);\\n1240→        self.prefs.quality.trim(self.touch_screen, &mut view);\\n        let mut scene = self.builder.build(&prev, &curr, alpha, &self.rig, w as f32 / h.max(1) as f32, &view, focus);\\n        // Arriving somewhere new: the screen opens with the chosen transition, on the player.\\n        if let Some(t0) = self.arrival {\\n            let t = t0.elapsed().as_secs_f32() / view.filter.transition_time.max(0.05);\\n            match view.filter.transition.kind() {\\n                Some(kind) if t < 1.0 => {\\n                    scene.filter.transition = 1.0 - t * t * (3.0 - 2.0 * t);\\n                    scene.filter.transition_kind = kind;\\n                    scene.filter.transition_center = pav_view::build::screen_uv(&scene.camera, feet + Vec3::Y * 0.9);\\n1250→                }\\n                _ => self.arrival = None,\\n            }\\n        }\\n        if !studio_active {\\n            self.editor.draw_preview(&mut scene);\\n        }\\n        if let Some(a) = intent.aiming.filter(|_| game_input) {\\n            // A skill aimed by hand: a ring where it lands and dots on the way there.\\n            let mark = |at: Vec3, s: f32, color: Vec3| MeshInstance {\\n1260→                mesh: MeshKey::Cylinder,\\n                transform: Mat4::from_scale_rotation_translation(Vec3::new(s, 0.02, s), Quat::IDENTITY, at + Vec3::Y * 0.04),\\n                color,\\n                emissive: 0.6,\\n                style: Style::Unlit,\\n                flags: rflags::NO_SHADOW | rflags::NO_CUT,\\n                group: 0,\\n                material: 0,\\n                ext: Vec3::ZERO,\\n            };\\n1270→            let a = Vec3::new(a.x, feet.y, a.z);\\n            scene.meshes.push(mark(a, 0.9, Vec3::new(1.0, 0.78, 0.4)));\\n            let n = ((a - feet).length() / 0.8) as usize;\\n            for k in 1..n {\\n                scene.meshes.push(mark(feet.lerp(a, k as f32 / n as f32), 0.14, Vec3::new(1.0, 0.9, 0.7)));\\n            }\\n        }\\n        if self.app_settings.aim_marker && game_input && curr.player.is_some() && !self.editor.on && curr.game.is_none() {\\n            if let Some(a) = aim {\\n                let d = Vec2::new(a.x - feet.x, a.z - feet.z);\\n1280→                let a = if d.length() > self.sim_config.bombs.throw_range {\\n                    let d = d.normalize() * self.sim_config.bombs.throw_range;\\n                    Vec3::new(feet.x + d.x, a.y, feet.z + d.y)\\n                } else {\\n                    a\\n                };\\n                scene.meshes.push(MeshInstance {\\n                    mesh: MeshKey::Cylinder,\\n                    transform: Mat4::from_scale_rotation_translation(\\n                        Vec3::new(0.5, 0.02, 0.5),\\n1290→                        Quat::IDENTITY,\\n                        a + Vec3::Y * 0.03,\\n                    ),\\n                    color: Vec3::new(1.0, 0.95, 0.7),\\n                    emissive: 0.0,\\n                    style: Style::Unlit,\\n                    flags: rflags::NO_SHADOW | rflags::NO_CUT,\\n                    group: 0,\\n                    material: 0,\\n                    ext: Vec3::ZERO,\\n1300→                });\\n            }\\n        }\\n\\n        // UI.\\n        let stats = *host.shared.stats.lock().unwrap();\\n        let mut ctl = host.control();\\n        let ctl_before = ctl;\\n        let crash = host.shared.crashed.lock().unwrap().clone();\\n        self.panel.record_timing(dt * 1000.0, stats.tick_ms);\\n1310→        let gfx = self.gfx.as_mut().unwrap();\\n        let (render_scale, lights) =\\n            self.scaler.update(self.prefs.quality, self.touch_screen, dt * 1000.0, gfx.size(), gfx.window.scale_factor() as f32);\\n        gfx.renderer.render_scale = render_scale;\\n        gfx.renderer.max_shadow_lights = lights;\\n        let info = ui::OverlayInfo {\\n            fps: self.fps.fps,\\n            frame_ms: self.fps.frame_ms,\\n            tps: stats.tps,\\n            tick_ms: stats.tick_ms,\\n1320→            tick: stats.tick,\\n            entities: stats.entities,\\n            gpu_errors: gfx.gpu_errors.load(std::sync::atomic::Ordering::Relaxed),\\n            adapter: &gfx.adapter_name,\\n            crash: crash.clone(),\",\"content_concise\":\"1145→\\n        // Game input -> the simulation thread.\\n        let (w, h) = self.gfx.as_ref().unwrap().size();\\n        let size = Vec2::new(w as f32, h as f32);\\n        let over_ui = self.egui_ctx.egui_wants_pointer_input();\\n1150→        let left_tap = self.input.take_mouse_tap(MouseButton::Left) && !over_ui;\\n        if over_ui {\\n            self.input.mouse_taps.clear();\\n        }\\n        let (mut held, mut pressed) = self.input.buttons();\\n        // Touch: the stick, the buttons and auto-attack.\\n        let touch_game = curr.game.as_deref().filter(|_| game_input).map(|g| (g, feet, facing));\\n        let rig = &self.rig;\\n        let intent = self.touch.intent(touch_game, |v| rig.relative_move(v), self.prefs.auto_attack);\\n        if game_input {\\n1160→            held |= intent.held;\\n            pressed |= intent.pressed;\\n        }\\n        if pressed & pav_core::input::buttons::INTERACT != 0 {\\n            if let Some(g) = &curr.game {\\n                if let Some(c) = self.game_ui.interact(g) {\\n                    host.shared.command(c);\\n                }\\n            }\\n        }\\n1170→        if pressed != 0 && self.input.last_device == Device::Gamepad {\\n            // Gamepad presses are timed from when they were polled (gilrs queues them).\\n            self.latency.press();\\n        }\\n        let room_id = self.hud.current.as_ref().map(|r| r.id);\\n        let left = self.input.mouse.contains(&MouseButton::Left) && !over_ui;\\n        if left_tap && !self.editor.on && game_input {\\n            pressed |= pav_core::input::buttons::PRIMARY;\\n        }\\n        if !studio_active && self.editor.update(host, &self.rig, self.input.cursor, size, left, left_tap, room_id) {\\n1180→            held &= !pav_core::input::buttons::PRIMARY;\\n            pressed &= !pav_core::input::buttons::PRIMARY;\\n        }\\n        let aim = match self.input.last_device {\\n            Device::KeyboardMouse => self.rig.ground_point(self.input.cursor, size, feet.y),\\n            Device::Gamepad => {\\n                let r = self.input.pad.right;\\n                if r.length() > 0.2 {\\n                    let d = self.rig.relative_move(r);\\n                    Some(feet + Vec3::new(d.x, 0.0, d.y) * self.sim_config.bombs.throw_range * r.length().min(1.0))\\n1190→                } else {\\n                    Some(feet + Vec3::new(facing.sin(), 0.0, facing.cos()) * 4.0)\\n                }\\n            }\\n            Device::Touch => intent.aim.or(Some(feet + Vec3::new(facing.sin(), 0.0, facing.cos()) * 4.0)),\\n        };\\n        {\\n            let mut i = host.shared.input.lock().unwrap();\\n            if game_input {\\n                let axis = (self.input.move_axis() + intent.move_axis).clamp_length_max(1.0);\\n1200→                i.move_dir = match intent.move_world {\\n                    // Auto-attack stepping in to a foe (only while the stick is still).\\n                    Some(m) if axis == Vec2::ZERO => m,\\n                    _ => self.rig.relative_move(axis),\\n                };\\n                i.held = held;\\n                i.pressed |= pressed;\\n                i.aim = aim;\\n                if let Some(t) = self.latency.pending.take() {\\n                    host.shared.input_stamp.lock().unwrap().get_or_insert(t);\\n1210→                }\\n            } else {\\n                *i = InputFrame::default();\\n            }\\n        }\\n\\n        self.rig.update(focus, dt);\\n        self.builder.now = self.started.elapsed().as_secs_f64();\\n        let events: Vec<_> = std::mem::take(&mut *host.shared.events.lock().unwrap());\\n        let events = if studio_active { Vec::new() } else { events };\\n1220→        self.builder.add_events(&events);\\n        // Save the hero on every arrival somewhere, and once a minute while playing.\\n        let travelled = events.iter().any(|e| matches!(e, pav_core::SimEvent::Travel { .. }));\\n        if curr.game.is_some() && (travelled || self.last_save.elapsed().as_secs() >= 60) {\\n            self.last_save = Instant::now();\\n            host.exec(|sim| crate::save::save_from(sim));\\n        }\\n        if let Some(a) = &self.audio {\\n            let (_, right) = self.rig.ground_axes();\\n            let l = pav_audio::Listener { pos: self.rig.target, right };\\n1230→            for e in &events {\\n                if matches!(e, pav_core::SimEvent::Step { .. }) && !self.audio_settings.footsteps {\\n                    continue;\\n                }\\n                a.play_event(e, &l, self.audio_settings.sfx);\\n            }\\n        }\\n        // The look layer (Look & Filters) over the scene's own settings.\\n        let mut view = self.view.clone();\\n        self.look_ui.apply(&mut view);\\n1240→        self.prefs.quality.trim(self.touch_screen, &mut view);\\n        let mut scene = self.builder.build(&prev, &curr, alpha, &self.rig, w as f32 / h.max(1) as f32, &view, focus);\\n        // Arriving somewhere new: the screen opens with the chosen transition, on the player.\\n        if let Some(t0) = self.arrival {\\n            let t = t0.elapsed().as_secs_f32() / view.filter.transition_time.max(0.05);\\n            match view.filter.transition.kind() {\\n                Some(kind) if t < 1.0 => {\\n                    scene.filter.transition = 1.0 - t * t * (3.0 - 2.0 * t);\\n                    scene.filter.transition_kind = kind;\\n                    scene.filter.transition_center = pav_view::build::screen_uv(&scene.camera, feet + Vec3::Y * 0.9);\\n1250→                }\\n                _ => self.arrival = None,\\n            }\\n        }\\n        if !studio_active {\\n            self.editor.draw_preview(&mut scene);\\n        }\\n        if let Some(a) = intent.aiming.filter(|_| game_input) {\\n            // A skill aimed by hand: a ring where it lands and dots on the way there.\\n            let mark = |at: Vec3, s: f32, color: Vec3| MeshInstance {\\n1260→                mesh: MeshKey::Cylinder,\\n                transform: Mat4::from_scale_rotation_translation(Vec3::new(s, 0.02, s), Quat::IDENTITY, at + Vec3::Y * 0.04),\\n                color,\\n                emissive: 0.6,\\n                style: Style::Unlit,\\n                flags: rflags::NO_SHADOW | rflags::NO_CUT,\\n                group: 0,\\n                material: 0,\\n                ext: Vec3::ZERO,\\n            };\\n1270→            let a = Vec3::new(a.x, feet.y, a.z);\\n            scene.meshes.push(mark(a, 0.9, Vec3::new(1.0, 0.78, 0.4)));\\n            let n = ((a - feet).length() / 0.8) as usize;\\n            for k in 1..n {\\n                scene.meshes.push(mark(feet.lerp(a, k as f32 / n as f32), 0.14, Vec3::new(1.0, 0.9, 0.7)));\\n            }\\n        }\\n        if self.app_settings.aim_marker && game_input && curr.player.is_some() && !self.editor.on && curr.game.is_none() {\\n            if let Some(a) = aim {\\n                let d = Vec2::new(a.x - feet.x, a.z - feet.z);\\n1280→                let a = if d.length() > self.sim_config.bombs.throw_range {\\n                    let d = d.normalize() * self.sim_config.bombs.throw_range;\\n                    Vec3::new(feet.x + d.x, a.y, feet.z + d.y)\\n                } else {\\n                    a\\n                };\\n                scene.meshes.push(MeshInstance {\\n                    mesh: MeshKey::Cylinder,\\n                    transform: Mat4::from_scale_rotation_translation(\\n                        Vec3::new(0.5, 0.02, 0.5),\\n1290→                        Quat::IDENTITY,\\n                        a + Vec3::Y * 0.03,\\n                    ),\\n                    color: Vec3::new(1.0, 0.95, 0.7),\\n                    emissive: 0.0,\\n                    style: Style::Unlit,\\n                    flags: rflags::NO_SHADOW | rflags::NO_CUT,\\n                    group: 0,\\n                    material: 0,\\n                    ext: Vec3::ZERO,\\n1300→                });\\n            }\\n        }\\n\\n        // UI.\\n        let stats = *host.shared.stats.lock().unwrap();\\n        let mut ctl = host.control();\\n        let ctl_before = ctl;\\n        let crash = host.shared.crashed.lock().unwrap().clone();\\n        self.panel.record_timing(dt * 1000.0, stats.tick_ms);\\n1310→        let gfx = self.gfx.as_mut().unwrap();\\n        let (render_scale, lights) =\\n            self.scaler.update(self.prefs.quality, self.touch_screen, dt * 1000.0, gfx.size(), gfx.window.scale_factor() as f32);\\n        gfx.renderer.render_scale = render_scale;\\n        gfx.renderer.max_shadow_lights = lights;\\n        let info = ui::OverlayInfo {\\n            fps: self.fps.fps,\\n            frame_ms: self.fps.frame_ms,\\n            tps: stats.tps,\\n            tick_ms: stats.tick_ms,\\n1320→            tick: stats.tick,\\n            entities: stats.entities,\\n            gpu_errors: gfx.gpu_errors.load(std::sync::atomic::Ordering::Relaxed),\\n            adapter: &gfx.adapter_name,\\n            crash: crash.clone(),\",\"absolute_path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224015__x42677a/work/Hands of Harbor: Second Opinion-Trauma Center: Second Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-224015/engine/crates/pav_app/src/app.rs\",\"offset\":1145,\"limit\":180,\"raw_output\":\"\\n        // Game input -> the simulation thread.\\n        let (w, h) = self.gfx.as_ref().unwrap().size();\\n        let size = Vec2::new(w as f32, h as f32);\\n        let over_ui = self.egui_ctx.egui_wants_pointer_input();\\n        let left_tap = self.input.take_mouse_tap(MouseButton::Left) && !over_ui;\\n        if over_ui {\\n            self.input.mouse_taps.clear();\\n        }\\n        let (mut held, mut pressed) = self.input.buttons();\\n        // Touch: the stick, the buttons and auto-attack.\\n        let touch_game = curr.game.as_deref().filter(|_| game_input).map(|g| (g, feet, facing));\\n        let rig = &self.rig;\\n        let intent = self.touch.intent(touch_game, |v| rig.relative_move(v), self.prefs.auto_attack);\\n        if game_input {\\n            held |= intent.held;\\n            pressed |= intent.pressed;\\n        }\\n        if pressed & pav_core::input::buttons::INTERACT != 0 {\\n            if let Some(g) = &curr.game {\\n                if let Some(c) = self.game_ui.interact(g) {\\n                    host.shared.command(c);\\n                }\\n            }\\n        }\\n        if pressed != 0 && self.input.last_device == Device::Gamepad {\\n            // Gamepad presses are timed from when they were polled (gilrs queues them).\\n            self.latency.press();\\n        }\\n        let room_id = self.hud.current.as_ref().map(|r| r.id);\\n        let left = self.input.mouse.contains(&MouseButton::Left) && !over_ui;\\n        if left_tap && !self.editor.on && game_input {\\n            pressed |= pav_core::input::buttons::PRIMARY;\\n        }\\n        if !studio_active && self.editor.update(host, &self.rig, self.input.cursor, size, left, left_tap, room_id) {\\n            held &= !pav_core::input::buttons::PRIMARY;\\n            pressed &= !pav_core::input::buttons::PRIMARY;\\n        }\\n        let aim = match self.input.last_device {\\n            Device::KeyboardMouse => self.rig.ground_point(self.input.cursor, size, feet.y),\\n            Device::Gamepad => {\\n                let r = self.input.pad.right;\\n                if r.length() > 0.2 {\\n                    let d = self.rig.relative_move(r);\\n                    Some(feet + Vec3::new(d.x, 0.0, d.y) * self.sim_config.bombs.throw_range * r.length().min(1.0))\\n                } else {\\n                    Some(feet + Vec3::new(facing.sin(), 0.0, facing.cos()) * 4.0)\\n                }\\n            }\\n            Device::Touch => intent.aim.or(Some(feet + Vec3::new(facing.sin(), 0.0, facing.cos()) * 4.0)),\\n        };\\n        {\\n            let mut i = host.shared.input.lock().unwrap();\\n            if game_input {\\n                let axis = (self.input.move_axis() + intent.move_axis).clamp_length_max(1.0);\\n                i.move_dir = match intent.move_world {\\n                    // Auto-attack stepping in to a foe (only while the stick is still).\\n                    Some(m) if axis == Vec2::ZERO => m,\\n                    _ => self.rig.relative_move(axis),\\n                };\\n                i.held = held;\\n                i.pressed |= pressed;\\n                i.aim = aim;\\n                if let Some(t) = self.latency.pending.take() {\\n                    host.shared.input_stamp.lock().unwrap().get_or_insert(t);\\n                }\\n            } else {\\n                *i = InputFrame::default();\\n            }\\n        }\\n\\n        self.rig.update(focus, dt);\\n        self.builder.now = self.started.elapsed().as_secs_f64();\\n        let events: Vec<_> = std::mem::take(&mut *host.shared.events.lock().unwrap());\\n        let events = if studio_active { Vec::new() } else { events };\\n        self.builder.add_events(&events);\\n        // Save the hero on every arrival somewhere, and once a minute while playing.\\n        let travelled = events.iter().any(|e| matches!(e, pav_core::SimEvent::Travel { .. }));\\n        if curr.game.is_some() && (travelled || self.last_save.elapsed().as_secs() >= 60) {\\n            self.last_save = Instant::now();\\n            host.exec(|sim| crate::save::save_from(sim));\\n        }\\n        if let Some(a) = &self.audio {\\n            let (_, right) = self.rig.ground_axes();\\n            let l = pav_audio::Listener { pos: self.rig.target, right };\\n            for e in &events {\\n                if matches!(e, pav_core::SimEvent::Step { .. }) && !self.audio_settings.footsteps {\\n                    continue;\\n                }\\n                a.play_event(e, &l, self.audio_settings.sfx);\\n            }\\n        }\\n        // The look layer (Look & Filters) over the scene's own settings.\\n        let mut view = self.view.clone();\\n        self.look_ui.apply(&mut view);\\n        self.prefs.quality.trim(self.touch_screen, &mut view);\\n        let mut scene = self.builder.build(&prev, &curr, alpha, &self.rig, w as f32 / h.max(1) as f32, &view, focus);\\n        // Arriving somewhere new: the screen opens with the chosen transition, on the player.\\n        if let Some(t0) = self.arrival {\\n            let t = t0.elapsed().as_secs_f32() / view.filter.transition_time.max(0.05);\\n            match view.filter.transition.kind() {\\n                Some(kind) if t < 1.0 => {\\n                    scene.filter.transition = 1.0 - t * t * (3.0 - 2.0 * t);\\n                    scene.filter.transition_kind = kind;\\n                    scene.filter.transition_center = pav_view::build::screen_uv(&scene.camera, feet + Vec3::Y * 0.9);\\n                }\\n                _ => self.arrival = None,\\n            }\\n        }\\n        if !studio_active {\\n            self.editor.draw_preview(&mut scene);\\n        }\\n        if let Some(a) = intent.aiming.filter(|_| game_input) {\\n            // A skill aimed by hand: a ring where it lands and dots on the way there.\\n            let mark = |at: Vec3, s: f32, color: Vec3| MeshInstance {\\n                mesh: MeshKey::Cylinder,\\n                transform: Mat4::from_scale_rotation_translation(Vec3::new(s, 0.02, s), Quat::IDENTITY, at + Vec3::Y * 0.04),\\n                color,\\n                emissive: 0.6,\\n                style: Style::Unlit,\\n                flags: rflags::NO_SHADOW | rflags::NO_CUT,\\n                group: 0,\\n                material: 0,\\n                ext: Vec3::ZERO,\\n            };\\n            let a = Vec3::new(a.x, feet.y, a.z);\\n            scene.meshes.push(mark(a, 0.9, Vec3::new(1.0, 0.78, 0.4)));\\n            let n = ((a - feet).length() / 0.8) as usize;\\n            for k in 1..n {\\n                scene.meshes.push(mark(feet.lerp(a, k as f32 / n as f32), 0.14, Vec3::new(1.0, 0.9, 0.7)));\\n            }\\n        }\\n        if self.app_settings.aim_marker && game_input && curr.player.is_some() && !self.editor.on && curr.game.is_none() {\\n            if let Some(a) = aim {\\n                let d = Vec2::new(a.x - feet.x, a.z - feet.z);\\n                let a = if d.length() > self.sim_config.bombs.throw_range {\\n                    let d = d.normalize() * self.sim_config.bombs.throw_range;\\n                    Vec3::new(feet.x + d.x, a.y, feet.z + d.y)\\n                } else {\\n                    a\\n                };\\n                scene.meshes.push(MeshInstance {\\n                    mesh: MeshKey::Cylinder,\\n                    transform: Mat4::from_scale_rotation_translation(\\n                        Vec3::new(0.5, 0.02, 0.5),\\n                        Quat::IDENTITY,\\n                        a + Vec3::Y * 0.03,\\n                    ),\\n                    color: Vec3::new(1.0, 0.95, 0.7),\\n                    emissive: 0.0,\\n                    style: Style::Unlit,\\n                    flags: rflags::NO_SHADOW | rflags::NO_CUT,\\n                    group: 0,\\n                    material: 0,\\n                    ext: Vec3::ZERO,\\n                });\\n            }\\n        }\\n\\n        // UI.\\n        let stats = *host.shared.stats.lock().unwrap();\\n        let mut ctl = host.control();\\n        let ctl_before = ctl;\\n        let crash = host.shared.crashed.lock().unwrap().clone();\\n        self.panel.record_timing(dt * 1000.0, stats.tick_ms);\\n        let gfx = self.gfx.as_mut().unwrap();\\n        let (render_scale, lights) =\\n            self.scaler.update(self.prefs.quality, self.touch_screen, dt * 1000.0, gfx.size(), gfx.window.scale_factor() as f32);\\n        gfx.renderer.render_scale = render_scale;\\n        gfx.renderer.max_shadow_lights = lights;\\n        let info = ui::OverlayInfo {\\n            fps: self.fps.fps,\\n            frame_ms: self.fps.frame_ms,\\n            tps: stats.tps,\\n            tick_ms: stats.tick_ms,\\n            tick: stats.tick,\\n            entities: stats.entities,\\n            gpu_errors: gfx.gpu_errors.load(std::sync::atomic::Ordering::Relaxed),\\n            adapter: &gfx.adapter_name,\\n            crash: crash.clone(),\\n\",\"total_lines\":2266}}","is_error":false},{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-ce696e16-da8e-4f94-9ac9-1d9c7e2548f4-46","content":"{\"type\":\"ReadFile\",\"FileContent\":{\"content\":\"1→//! Runs the simulation at a fixed tick rate: on its own thread natively, and stepped from the\\n//! frame loop in the browser (no threads there). The renderer never waits for it: it reads the\\n//! two most recent frames and interpolates between them.\\n\\nuse std::sync::{Arc, Mutex};\\nuse std::time::Duration;\\n\\nuse pav_core::{InputFrame, RenderFrame, Sim, SimEvent};\\nuse web_time::Instant;\\n10→\\n#[cfg(not(target_arch = \\\"wasm32\\\"))]\\ntype Job = Box<dyn FnOnce(&mut Sim) + Send>;\\n\\n#[cfg(not(target_arch = \\\"wasm32\\\"))]\\nenum Cmd {\\n    Run(Job),\\n    Quit,\\n}\\n\\n20→#[derive(Clone, Copy, Debug)]\\npub struct TimeControl {\\n    pub paused: bool,\\n    /// Simulation speed multiplier (0.05 .. 8).\\n    pub speed: f32,\\n    /// Ticks to advance while paused.\\n    pub step_requests: u32,\\n    /// Holding the rewind button.\\n    pub rewinding: bool,\\n    /// Ticks travelled back per tick while rewinding.\\n30→    pub rewind_speed: u32,\\n    /// Jump to this tick (timeline scrubbing), keeping the future until play resumes.\\n    pub scrub: Option<u64>,\\n}\\n\\nimpl Default for TimeControl {\\n    fn default() -> Self {\\n        Self { paused: false, speed: 1.0, step_requests: 0, rewinding: false, rewind_speed: 1, scrub: None }\\n    }\\n}\\n40→\\n#[derive(Clone, Copy, Debug, Default)]\\npub struct SimStats {\\n    /// Measured ticks per second of wall time.\\n    pub tps: f32,\\n    /// Average CPU time per tick (ms).\\n    pub tick_ms: f32,\\n    pub tick: u64,\\n    pub entities: usize,\\n    /// Rewind range available (ticks).\\n50→    pub oldest: u64,\\n    pub newest: u64,\\n    pub history_mb: f32,\\n    pub rewound: bool,\\n}\\n\\npub struct FramePair {\\n    pub prev: Arc<RenderFrame>,\\n    pub curr: Arc<RenderFrame>,\\n    /// When `curr` became current (wall clock).\\n60→    pub curr_at: Instant,\\n    /// Wall-clock length of one tick at the current speed.\\n    pub tick_wall: f32,\\n}\\n\\npub struct Shared {\\n    pub frames: Mutex<FramePair>,\\n    pub input: Mutex<InputFrame>,\\n    pub control: Mutex<TimeControl>,\\n    pub stats: Mutex<SimStats>,\\n70→    pub crashed: Mutex<Option<String>>,\\n    /// Events for sound and effects, drained by the render thread.\\n    pub events: Mutex<Vec<SimEvent>>,\\n    /// When the input that is waiting for the next tick was pressed (latency measurement).\\n    pub input_stamp: Mutex<Option<Instant>>,\\n    /// (pressed, consumed by a tick, that tick's number) for the latest measured press.\\n    pub latency_probe: Mutex<Option<(Instant, Instant, u64)>>,\\n    /// Menu commands waiting for a tick (one rides along with each tick's input).\\n    pub cmds: Mutex<std::collections::VecDeque<pav_core::arpg::GameCmd>>,\\n}\\n80→\\nimpl Shared {\\n    /// Queues a game command for the next free tick.\\n    pub fn command(&self, c: pav_core::arpg::GameCmd) {\\n        let mut q = self.cmds.lock().unwrap();\\n        if q.len() < 64 {\\n            q.push_back(c);\\n        }\\n    }\\n}\\n90→\\n#[cfg(not(target_arch = \\\"wasm32\\\"))]\\npub struct SimHost {\\n    tx: std::sync::mpsc::Sender<Cmd>,\\n    pub shared: Arc<Shared>,\\n    thread: Option<std::thread::JoinHandle<()>>,\\n}\\n\\n/// In the browser the simulation lives on the main thread and `pump` advances it every frame.\\n#[cfg(target_arch = \\\"wasm32\\\")]\\n100→pub struct SimHost {\\n    sim: std::cell::RefCell<Sim>,\\n    clock: std::cell::RefCell<Clock>,\\n    pub shared: Arc<Shared>,\\n}\\n\\nfn shared_for(sim: &mut Sim) -> Arc<Shared> {\\n    let f = Arc::new(sim.frame());\\n    Arc::new(Shared {\\n        frames: Mutex::new(FramePair { prev: f.clone(), curr: f, curr_at: Instant::now(), tick_wall: sim.dt() }),\\n110→        input: Mutex::new(InputFrame::default()),\\n        control: Mutex::new(TimeControl::default()),\\n        stats: Mutex::new(SimStats::default()),\\n        crashed: Mutex::new(None),\\n        events: Mutex::new(Vec::new()),\\n        input_stamp: Mutex::new(None),\\n        latency_probe: Mutex::new(None),\\n        cmds: Mutex::new(Default::default()),\\n    })\\n}\\n120→\",\"content_concise\":\"1→//! Runs the simulation at a fixed tick rate: on its own thread natively, and stepped from the\\n//! frame loop in the browser (no threads there). The renderer never waits for it: it reads the\\n//! two most recent frames and interpolates between them.\\n\\nuse std::sync::{Arc, Mutex};\\nuse std::time::Duration;\\n\\nuse pav_core::{InputFrame, RenderFrame, Sim, SimEvent};\\nuse web_time::Instant;\\n10→\\n#[cfg(not(target_arch = \\\"wasm32\\\"))]\\ntype Job = Box<dyn FnOnce(&mut Sim) + Send>;\\n\\n#[cfg(not(target_arch = \\\"wasm32\\\"))]\\nenum Cmd {\\n    Run(Job),\\n    Quit,\\n}\\n\\n20→#[derive(Clone, Copy, Debug)]\\npub struct TimeControl {\\n    pub paused: bool,\\n    /// Simulation speed multiplier (0.05 .. 8).\\n    pub speed: f32,\\n    /// Ticks to advance while paused.\\n    pub step_requests: u32,\\n    /// Holding the rewind button.\\n    pub rewinding: bool,\\n    /// Ticks travelled back per tick while rewinding.\\n30→    pub rewind_speed: u32,\\n    /// Jump to this tick (timeline scrubbing), keeping the future until play resumes.\\n    pub scrub: Option<u64>,\\n}\\n\\nimpl Default for TimeControl {\\n    fn default() -> Self {\\n        Self { paused: false, speed: 1.0, step_requests: 0, rewinding: false, rewind_speed: 1, scrub: None }\\n    }\\n}\\n40→\\n#[derive(Clone, Copy, Debug, Default)]\\npub struct SimStats {\\n    /// Measured ticks per second of wall time.\\n    pub tps: f32,\\n    /// Average CPU time per tick (ms).\\n    pub tick_ms: f32,\\n    pub tick: u64,\\n    pub entities: usize,\\n    /// Rewind range available (ticks).\\n50→    pub oldest: u64,\\n    pub newest: u64,\\n    pub history_mb: f32,\\n    pub rewound: bool,\\n}\\n\\npub struct FramePair {\\n    pub prev: Arc<RenderFrame>,\\n    pub curr: Arc<RenderFrame>,\\n    /// When `curr` became current (wall clock).\\n60→    pub curr_at: Instant,\\n    /// Wall-clock length of one tick at the current speed.\\n    pub tick_wall: f32,\\n}\\n\\npub struct Shared {\\n    pub frames: Mutex<FramePair>,\\n    pub input: Mutex<InputFrame>,\\n    pub control: Mutex<TimeControl>,\\n    pub stats: Mutex<SimStats>,\\n70→    pub crashed: Mutex<Option<String>>,\\n    /// Events for sound and effects, drained by the render thread.\\n    pub events: Mutex<Vec<SimEvent>>,\\n    /// When the input that is waiting for the next tick was pressed (latency measurement).\\n    pub input_stamp: Mutex<Option<Instant>>,\\n    /// (pressed, consumed by a tick, that tick's number) for the latest measured press.\\n    pub latency_probe: Mutex<Option<(Instant, Instant, u64)>>,\\n    /// Menu commands waiting for a tick (one rides along with each tick's input).\\n    pub cmds: Mutex<std::collections::VecDeque<pav_core::arpg::GameCmd>>,\\n}\\n80→\\nimpl Shared {\\n    /// Queues a game command for the next free tick.\\n    pub fn command(&self, c: pav_core::arpg::GameCmd) {\\n        let mut q = self.cmds.lock().unwrap();\\n        if q.len() < 64 {\\n            q.push_back(c);\\n        }\\n    }\\n}\\n90→\\n#[cfg(not(target_arch = \\\"wasm32\\\"))]\\npub struct SimHost {\\n    tx: std::sync::mpsc::Sender<Cmd>,\\n    pub shared: Arc<Shared>,\\n    thread: Option<std::thread::JoinHandle<()>>,\\n}\\n\\n/// In the browser the simulation lives on the main thread and `pump` advances it every frame.\\n#[cfg(target_arch = \\\"wasm32\\\")]\\n100→pub struct SimHost {\\n    sim: std::cell::RefCell<Sim>,\\n    clock: std::cell::RefCell<Clock>,\\n    pub shared: Arc<Shared>,\\n}\\n\\nfn shared_for(sim: &mut Sim) -> Arc<Shared> {\\n    let f = Arc::new(sim.frame());\\n    Arc::new(Shared {\\n        frames: Mutex::new(FramePair { prev: f.clone(), curr: f, curr_at: Instant::now(), tick_wall: sim.dt() }),\\n110→        input: Mutex::new(InputFrame::default()),\\n        control: Mutex::new(TimeControl::default()),\\n        stats: Mutex::new(SimStats::default()),\\n        crashed: Mutex::new(None),\\n        events: Mutex::new(Vec::new()),\\n        input_stamp: Mutex::new(None),\\n        latency_probe: Mutex::new(None),\\n        cmds: Mutex::new(Default::default()),\\n    })\\n}\\n120→\",\"absolute_path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224015__x42677a/work/Hands of Harbor: Second Opinion-Trauma Center: Second Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-224015/engine/crates/pav_app/src/simhost.rs\",\"offset\":null,\"limit\":120,\"raw_output\":\"//! Runs the simulation at a fixed tick rate: on its own thread natively, and stepped from the\\n//! frame loop in the browser (no threads there). The renderer never waits for it: it reads the\\n//! two most recent frames and interpolates between them.\\n\\nuse std::sync::{Arc, Mutex};\\nuse std::time::Duration;\\n\\nuse pav_core::{InputFrame, RenderFrame, Sim, SimEvent};\\nuse web_time::Instant;\\n\\n#[cfg(not(target_arch = \\\"wasm32\\\"))]\\ntype Job = Box<dyn FnOnce(&mut Sim) + Send>;\\n\\n#[cfg(not(target_arch = \\\"wasm32\\\"))]\\nenum Cmd {\\n    Run(Job),\\n    Quit,\\n}\\n\\n#[derive(Clone, Copy, Debug)]\\npub struct TimeControl {\\n    pub paused: bool,\\n    /// Simulation speed multiplier (0.05 .. 8).\\n    pub speed: f32,\\n    /// Ticks to advance while paused.\\n    pub step_requests: u32,\\n    /// Holding the rewind button.\\n    pub rewinding: bool,\\n    /// Ticks travelled back per tick while rewinding.\\n    pub rewind_speed: u32,\\n    /// Jump to this tick (timeline scrubbing), keeping the future until play resumes.\\n    pub scrub: Option<u64>,\\n}\\n\\nimpl Default for TimeControl {\\n    fn default() -> Self {\\n        Self { paused: false, speed: 1.0, step_requests: 0, rewinding: false, rewind_speed: 1, scrub: None }\\n    }\\n}\\n\\n#[derive(Clone, Copy, Debug, Default)]\\npub struct SimStats {\\n    /// Measured ticks per second of wall time.\\n    pub tps: f32,\\n    /// Average CPU time per tick (ms).\\n    pub tick_ms: f32,\\n    pub tick: u64,\\n    pub entities: usize,\\n    /// Rewind range available (ticks).\\n    pub oldest: u64,\\n    pub newest: u64,\\n    pub history_mb: f32,\\n    pub rewound: bool,\\n}\\n\\npub struct FramePair {\\n    pub prev: Arc<RenderFrame>,\\n    pub curr: Arc<RenderFrame>,\\n    /// When `curr` became current (wall clock).\\n    pub curr_at: Instant,\\n    /// Wall-clock length of one tick at the current speed.\\n    pub tick_wall: f32,\\n}\\n\\npub struct Shared {\\n    pub frames: Mutex<FramePair>,\\n    pub input: Mutex<InputFrame>,\\n    pub control: Mutex<TimeControl>,\\n    pub stats: Mutex<SimStats>,\\n    pub crashed: Mutex<Option<String>>,\\n    /// Events for sound and effects, drained by the render thread.\\n    pub events: Mutex<Vec<SimEvent>>,\\n    /// When the input that is waiting for the next tick was pressed (latency measurement).\\n    pub input_stamp: Mutex<Option<Instant>>,\\n    /// (pressed, consumed by a tick, that tick's number) for the latest measured press.\\n    pub latency_probe: Mutex<Option<(Instant, Instant, u64)>>,\\n    /// Menu commands waiting for a tick (one rides along with each tick's input).\\n    pub cmds: Mutex<std::collections::VecDeque<pav_core::arpg::GameCmd>>,\\n}\\n\\nimpl Shared {\\n    /// Queues a game command for the next free tick.\\n    pub fn command(&self, c: pav_core::arpg::GameCmd) {\\n        let mut q = self.cmds.lock().unwrap();\\n        if q.len() < 64 {\\n            q.push_back(c);\\n        }\\n    }\\n}\\n\\n#[cfg(not(target_arch = \\\"wasm32\\\"))]\\npub struct SimHost {\\n    tx: std::sync::mpsc::Sender<Cmd>,\\n    pub shared: Arc<Shared>,\\n    thread: Option<std::thread::JoinHandle<()>>,\\n}\\n\\n/// In the browser the simulation lives on the main thread and `pump` advances it every frame.\\n#[cfg(target_arch = \\\"wasm32\\\")]\\npub struct SimHost {\\n    sim: std::cell::RefCell<Sim>,\\n    clock: std::cell::RefCell<Clock>,\\n    pub shared: Arc<Shared>,\\n}\\n\\nfn shared_for(sim: &mut Sim) -> Arc<Shared> {\\n    let f = Arc::new(sim.frame());\\n    Arc::new(Shared {\\n        frames: Mutex::new(FramePair { prev: f.clone(), curr: f, curr_at: Instant::now(), tick_wall: sim.dt() }),\\n        input: Mutex::new(InputFrame::default()),\\n        control: Mutex::new(TimeControl::default()),\\n        stats: Mutex::new(SimStats::default()),\\n        crashed: Mutex::new(None),\\n        events: Mutex::new(Vec::new()),\\n        input_stamp: Mutex::new(None),\\n        latency_probe: Mutex::new(None),\\n        cmds: Mutex::new(Default::default()),\\n    })\\n}\\n\\n\",\"total_lines\":427}}","is_error":false},{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-ce696e16-da8e-4f94-9ac9-1d9c7e2548f4-47","content":"{\"type\":\"ReadFile\",\"FileContent\":{\"content\":\"1380→            if let Some(s) = &o.soft {\\n                emit_soft(&mut scene, &o, s, settings.style);\\n                continue;\\n            }\\n            match &o.puppet {\\n                Some(p) => {\\n                    let def = p.def.as_deref().unwrap_or(&curr.puppet_def);\\n                    emit_puppet(&mut scene, def, &o, p, cam_fwd, settings.style);\\n                    // A small hitbox (bullet hell) shows as a glowing dot of its true size over\\n                    // the head: hits test a vertical column of that radius.\\n1390→                    let hitbox = curr.config.movement.hitbox;\\n                    if Some(o.id) == curr.player && hitbox < pav_core::character::RADIUS * 0.6 {\\n                        let top = o.pos + Vec3::Y * (p.feet_offset + 0.3);\\n                        scene.sdfs.push(rs::SdfInstance {\\n                            a: top,\\n                            b: top,\\n                            ra: hitbox.max(0.06),\\n                            rb: hitbox.max(0.06),\\n                            color: Vec3::new(1.0, 0.35, 0.6),\\n                            emissive: 2.0,\\n1400→                            style: Style::Unlit,\\n                            flags: rs::flags::NO_SHADOW | rs::flags::NO_CUT,\\n                            group: o.id.0 + 2,\\n                            material: 0,\\n                        });\\n                    }\\n                }\\n                None => {\\n                    match &o.prop {\\n                        Some(prop) => {\\n1410→                            self.emit_prop(&mut scene, &o, prop, settings, time, dt);\\n                            live.push(o.id.0);\\n                        }\\n                        None => emit_object(&mut scene, &o, settings.style, now, 0),\\n                    }\\n                    if let Some(v) = &o.vehicle {\\n                        crate::vehicles::emit_vehicle(\\n                            &mut scene,\\n                            &o,\\n                            v,\\n1420→                            style_of(o.visual.look, settings.style),\\n                            settings.particles,\\n                        );\\n                    }\\n                }\\n            }\\n        }\\n        if let Some(creature) = crate::creatures::interpolate(prev, curr, alpha) {\\n            puppets.push(creature.id.0 + 2);\\n            if let Err(error) = crate::creatures::emit(&mut scene, &creature, style_of(Look::Lit, settings.style)) {\\n1430→                eprintln!(\\\"creature preview: {error}\\\");\\n            }\\n        }\\n        self.emit_carry.retain(|(id, _), _| live.contains(id));\\n        if let Some(g) = &curr.game {\\n            self.arpg.emit(&mut scene, curr, g, alpha, time, dt, settings.particles, cam_fwd);\\n        }\\n        // Projectiles: drawn where they are between ticks (they move in straight lines).\\n        let back = (1.0 - alpha) * curr.dt;\\n        for p in &curr.projectiles {\\n1440→            let mut sd = SdfInstance::sphere(p.pos - p.vel * back, p.radius, v3(p.color));\\n            sd.style = Style::Unlit;\\n            sd.emissive = 0.6;\\n            sd.flags = rs::flags::NO_SHADOW | rs::flags::NO_CUT;\\n            sd.group = 0x7f1;\\n            scene.sdfs.push(sd);\\n        }\\n        self.emit_effects(&mut scene);\\n        scenery.sort_unstable();\\n        mark_objects(&mut scene, env_end, &scenery);\\n1450→        if settings.style == StyleOverride::PerObject {\\n            restyle_parts(&mut scene, settings.style_objects, settings.style_environment);\\n        }\\n        if f.pixel_art > 1.0 {\\n            let hero = curr.player.map(|p| p.0 + 2);\\n            mark_pixel_art(&mut scene, |g, flags| match f.pixel_target {\\n                PixelTarget::All => true,\\n                PixelTarget::Characters => puppets.contains(&g),\\n                PixelTarget::Hero => Some(g) == hero,\\n                PixelTarget::Others => puppets.contains(&g) && Some(g) != hero,\\n1460→                PixelTarget::World => !puppets.contains(&g),\\n                PixelTarget::Entity => g == f.pixel_entity as u32 + 2,\\n                PixelTarget::Objects => flags & rs::flags::OBJECT != 0,\\n                PixelTarget::Environment => flags & rs::flags::OBJECT == 0,\\n            });\\n        }\\n        lock(&self.materials).attach(&mut scene);\\n        scene\\n    }\\n}\\n1470→\\n/// Flags the characters and objects: every instance emitted after the environment (`from`:\\n/// meshes, SDFs, dynamic meshes) except fixed scenery (outline groups in `scenery`, sorted).\\nfn mark_objects(scene: &mut Scene, from: (usize, usize, usize), scenery: &[u32]) {\\n    let object = |g: u32| scenery.binary_search(&g).is_err();\\n    for m in &mut scene.meshes[from.0..] {\\n        if object(m.group) {\\n            m.flags |= rs::flags::OBJECT;\\n        }\\n    }\\n1480→    for s in &mut scene.sdfs[from.1..] {\\n        if object(s.group) {\\n            s.flags |= rs::flags::OBJECT;\\n        }\\n    }\\n    for d in &mut scene.dynamic[from.2..] {\\n        if object(d.group) {\\n            d.flags |= rs::flags::OBJECT;\\n        }\\n    }\\n1490→}\\n\\n/// Gives the characters and objects, and the environment, a surface style of their own\\n/// (unlit markers, decals and glows keep theirs).\\nfn restyle_parts(scene: &mut Scene, objects: StyleOverride, environment: StyleOverride) {\\n    if objects == StyleOverride::PerObject && environment == StyleOverride::PerObject {\\n        return;\\n    }\\n    let pick = |style: Style, flags: u32| -> Style {\\n        let ov = if flags & rs::flags::OBJECT != 0 { objects } else { environment };\",\"content_concise\":\"1380→            if let Some(s) = &o.soft {\\n                emit_soft(&mut scene, &o, s, settings.style);\\n                continue;\\n            }\\n            match &o.puppet {\\n                Some(p) => {\\n                    let def = p.def.as_deref().unwrap_or(&curr.puppet_def);\\n                    emit_puppet(&mut scene, def, &o, p, cam_fwd, settings.style);\\n                    // A small hitbox (bullet hell) shows as a glowing dot of its true size over\\n                    // the head: hits test a vertical column of that radius.\\n1390→                    let hitbox = curr.config.movement.hitbox;\\n                    if Some(o.id) == curr.player && hitbox < pav_core::character::RADIUS * 0.6 {\\n                        let top = o.pos + Vec3::Y * (p.feet_offset + 0.3);\\n                        scene.sdfs.push(rs::SdfInstance {\\n                            a: top,\\n                            b: top,\\n                            ra: hitbox.max(0.06),\\n                            rb: hitbox.max(0.06),\\n                            color: Vec3::new(1.0, 0.35, 0.6),\\n                            emissive: 2.0,\\n1400→                            style: Style::Unlit,\\n                            flags: rs::flags::NO_SHADOW | rs::flags::NO_CUT,\\n                            group: o.id.0 + 2,\\n                            material: 0,\\n                        });\\n                    }\\n                }\\n                None => {\\n                    match &o.prop {\\n                        Some(prop) => {\\n1410→                            self.emit_prop(&mut scene, &o, prop, settings, time, dt);\\n                            live.push(o.id.0);\\n                        }\\n                        None => emit_object(&mut scene, &o, settings.style, now, 0),\\n                    }\\n                    if let Some(v) = &o.vehicle {\\n                        crate::vehicles::emit_vehicle(\\n                            &mut scene,\\n                            &o,\\n                            v,\\n1420→                            style_of(o.visual.look, settings.style),\\n                            settings.particles,\\n                        );\\n                    }\\n                }\\n            }\\n        }\\n        if let Some(creature) = crate::creatures::interpolate(prev, curr, alpha) {\\n            puppets.push(creature.id.0 + 2);\\n            if let Err(error) = crate::creatures::emit(&mut scene, &creature, style_of(Look::Lit, settings.style)) {\\n1430→                eprintln!(\\\"creature preview: {error}\\\");\\n            }\\n        }\\n        self.emit_carry.retain(|(id, _), _| live.contains(id));\\n        if let Some(g) = &curr.game {\\n            self.arpg.emit(&mut scene, curr, g, alpha, time, dt, settings.particles, cam_fwd);\\n        }\\n        // Projectiles: drawn where they are between ticks (they move in straight lines).\\n        let back = (1.0 - alpha) * curr.dt;\\n        for p in &curr.projectiles {\\n1440→            let mut sd = SdfInstance::sphere(p.pos - p.vel * back, p.radius, v3(p.color));\\n            sd.style = Style::Unlit;\\n            sd.emissive = 0.6;\\n            sd.flags = rs::flags::NO_SHADOW | rs::flags::NO_CUT;\\n            sd.group = 0x7f1;\\n            scene.sdfs.push(sd);\\n        }\\n        self.emit_effects(&mut scene);\\n        scenery.sort_unstable();\\n        mark_objects(&mut scene, env_end, &scenery);\\n1450→        if settings.style == StyleOverride::PerObject {\\n            restyle_parts(&mut scene, settings.style_objects, settings.style_environment);\\n        }\\n        if f.pixel_art > 1.0 {\\n            let hero = curr.player.map(|p| p.0 + 2);\\n            mark_pixel_art(&mut scene, |g, flags| match f.pixel_target {\\n                PixelTarget::All => true,\\n                PixelTarget::Characters => puppets.contains(&g),\\n                PixelTarget::Hero => Some(g) == hero,\\n                PixelTarget::Others => puppets.contains(&g) && Some(g) != hero,\\n1460→                PixelTarget::World => !puppets.contains(&g),\\n                PixelTarget::Entity => g == f.pixel_entity as u32 + 2,\\n                PixelTarget::Objects => flags & rs::flags::OBJECT != 0,\\n                PixelTarget::Environment => flags & rs::flags::OBJECT == 0,\\n            });\\n        }\\n        lock(&self.materials).attach(&mut scene);\\n        scene\\n    }\\n}\\n1470→\\n/// Flags the characters and objects: every instance emitted after the environment (`from`:\\n/// meshes, SDFs, dynamic meshes) except fixed scenery (outline groups in `scenery`, sorted).\\nfn mark_objects(scene: &mut Scene, from: (usize, usize, usize), scenery: &[u32]) {\\n    let object = |g: u32| scenery.binary_search(&g).is_err();\\n    for m in &mut scene.meshes[from.0..] {\\n        if object(m.group) {\\n            m.flags |= rs::flags::OBJECT;\\n        }\\n    }\\n1480→    for s in &mut scene.sdfs[from.1..] {\\n        if object(s.group) {\\n            s.flags |= rs::flags::OBJECT;\\n        }\\n    }\\n    for d in &mut scene.dynamic[from.2..] {\\n        if object(d.group) {\\n            d.flags |= rs::flags::OBJECT;\\n        }\\n    }\\n1490→}\\n\\n/// Gives the characters and objects, and the environment, a surface style of their own\\n/// (unlit markers, decals and glows keep theirs).\\nfn restyle_parts(scene: &mut Scene, objects: StyleOverride, environment: StyleOverride) {\\n    if objects == StyleOverride::PerObject && environment == StyleOverride::PerObject {\\n        return;\\n    }\\n    let pick = |style: Style, flags: u32| -> Style {\\n        let ov = if flags & rs::flags::OBJECT != 0