{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_24","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Noting the Rust 2024 edition and preparing to handle its specific changes carefully.\n\nThe project will use Rust 1.98.1 via rust-toolchain.toml. I am now writing the simulation code in a single comprehensive mod.rs with supporting modules, starting with tune.rs for the tuning struct and sliders.\n\nThe remaining modules are now planned. Heart.rs will manage vitals and beats. Field.rs will hold tools, hazards, ratings, and gesture state. Surgeon.rs, Strain.rs, Story.rs, Director.rs, Bot.rs, and Net.rs will cover the surgeon slot, strain states, story player, case loading, bot input, and snapshot JSON. Frame.rs will build the render data each frame without being part of the simulation state.\n\nDrafting the `Surgery` struct in `mod.rs`. It will hold mode, case ID, difficulty, four surgeons, heart state, hazards, phase tracking, timers, score, and mistakes. The struct derives `Clone`, `Serialize`, and `Deserialize`.\n\nThe Surgery struct now includes chain tracking, outcome, rank, gift meter and kind per surgeon, hush, echo, and duet timers, code blue state, strain, story progress, checkpoint, tuning parameters, bot skill, and a seed note.\n\nThe Surgery struct is being expanded with UI and animation state fields. These include coverage, callout cues, banner timers, patient and plate states, reveal progress, local partner flags, tremor, aim assist, scripted code, death and results timers, wave timing, and outcome metadata.\n\nThe Surgery struct now includes game mode flags, heat and fever state, guide visibility, objective tracking, RNG salt, attract mode, immortal status, freeze timer, one-hit mode, time scale, beat window, story auto-play, hold skip, campaign state, per-case completion flags, best ranks, and difficulty pick.\n\nThe shell will run separately from the simulation so it can pause while the sim advances. Campaign mode auto-advances through story, chart, operation, and results. The title scene keeps the sim idle while the shell draws the title screen.\n\nThe simulation will handle code blue, attract mode with bot cheats, card hub, and mirror client scenes. Menu state stays in the shell. The shell sends commands to the sim via `host.exec` to load cases. Headless campaign runs without the shell.\n\nA `SurgeryCmd` enum will be added to `InputFrame` to handle shell commands. It supports loading cases, campaigns, and code blue, retrying, quiting the title, and tuning parameters. This complements the existing Shardfall-only command field.\n\nThe `SurgeryCmd` enum will be packed into a `u32` field on `InputFrame` to keep the struct `Copy` and compatible with serde defaults. I am verifying that `GameCmd` is also `Copy` so the packed command field serializes correctly.\n\nConfirmed `GameCmd` is `Copy`, so `SurgeryCmd` can be packed into a `u32` field on `InputFrame`. The `Checkpoint` struct is being defined to save phase index, hazards, heart vitals and phase, timer, score, chain, mistakes, codes left, strain, and gift meters.\n\nCheckpoints will be saved at the start of each phase when enabled. Retrying restores that checkpoint and sets the outcome to Playing and mode to Op.\n\nWhen vitals reach zero and the resident is not immortal, the system enters a code blue state if any codes remain or scripted code is active. A five-second defibrillation timer begins. Success restores thirty vitals, consumes one code unless scripted, and exits code blue. Failure after the timer expires results in death. If no codes are left, death occurs immediately.\n\nScripted stops do not count against the code budget. The system grants a free attempt and skips decrementing the remaining codes.\n\nIf the timer expires during a normal case, death occurs. During code blue, an expired timer while alive is treated as a win.\n\nAfter clearing all phases, the mode switches to Results. The bot presses confirm to advance through results immediately in campaign mode. Story lines are stored in static data with an index. The bot holds confirm to skip story narration.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-5564f0ae-818b-4f33-a975-561ee727ca35-66","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224015__x42677a/work/Hands of Harbor: Second Opinion-Trauma Center: Second Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-224015/engine/crates/pav_core/Cargo.toml","limit":40}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-5564f0ae-818b-4f33-a975-561ee727ca35-67","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224015__x42677a/work/Hands of Harbor: Second Opinion-Trauma Center: Second Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-224015/engine/crates/pav_view/src/build.rs","offset":1,"limit":40}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-5564f0ae-818b-4f33-a975-561ee727ca35-68","name":"grep","input":{"pattern":"struct ViewBuilder|arpg:","glob":"**/pav_view/src/build.rs"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1427,"output_tokens":2495,"cache_read_input_tokens":128256,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa38-de6f-7dc0-ae0d-e0f717ed75f2","uuid":"eb0f23ef-6b22-4500-96eb-2c0863e18aec"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-5564f0ae-818b-4f33-a975-561ee727ca35-66","content":"{\"type\":\"ReadFile\",\"FileContent\":{\"content\":\"1→[package]\\nname = \\\"pav_core\\\"\\nversion.workspace = true\\nedition.workspace = true\\npublish.workspace = true\\n\\n[dependencies]\\nglam.workspace = true\\n# One-line physics precision switch: change package to \\\"rapier3d-f64\\\".\\n10→rapier = { package = \\\"rapier3d\\\", version = \\\"0.36\\\", features = [\\\"serde-serialize\\\"] }\\nserde.workspace = true\\nserde_json.workspace = true\\ntoml.workspace = true\\nanyhow.workspace = true\\nciborium.workspace = true\\nlog.workspace = true\\n\\n[lints]\\nworkspace = true\\n\",\"content_concise\":\"1→[package]\\nname = \\\"pav_core\\\"\\nversion.workspace = true\\nedition.workspace = true\\npublish.workspace = true\\n\\n[dependencies]\\nglam.workspace = true\\n# One-line physics precision switch: change package to \\\"rapier3d-f64\\\".\\n10→rapier = { package = \\\"rapier3d\\\", version = \\\"0.36\\\", features = [\\\"serde-serialize\\\"] }\\nserde.workspace = true\\nserde_json.workspace = true\\ntoml.workspace = true\\nanyhow.workspace = true\\nciborium.workspace = true\\nlog.workspace = true\\n\\n[lints]\\nworkspace = true\\n\",\"absolute_path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224015__x42677a/work/Hands of Harbor: Second Opinion-Trauma Center: Second Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-224015/engine/crates/pav_core/Cargo.toml\",\"offset\":null,\"limit\":40,\"raw_output\":\"[package]\\nname = \\\"pav_core\\\"\\nversion.workspace = true\\nedition.workspace = true\\npublish.workspace = true\\n\\n[dependencies]\\nglam.workspace = true\\n# One-line physics precision switch: change package to \\\"rapier3d-f64\\\".\\nrapier = { package = \\\"rapier3d\\\", version = \\\"0.36\\\", features = [\\\"serde-serialize\\\"] }\\nserde.workspace = true\\nserde_json.workspace = true\\ntoml.workspace = true\\nanyhow.workspace = true\\nciborium.workspace = true\\nlog.workspace = true\\n\\n[lints]\\nworkspace = true\\n\",\"total_lines\":19}}","is_error":false},{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-5564f0ae-818b-4f33-a975-561ee727ca35-67","content":"{\"type\":\"ReadFile\",\"FileContent\":{\"content\":\"1→//! Scene building: interpolates between two simulation frames and emits render instances.\\n\\nuse std::collections::{BTreeMap, HashMap, HashSet};\\nuse std::sync::{Arc, Mutex, MutexGuard};\\n\\nuse glam::{Mat4, Quat, Vec3};\\nuse pav_core::frame::{PuppetFrame, SimEvent};\\nuse pav_core::fxdef::{EmitterDef, LightDef};\\nuse pav_core::params::{ChoiceParam, ParamVisitor, Tunable, nested};\\n10→use pav_core::prop_instance::PropFrame;\\nuse pav_core::props::geom::{Generated, GeomMesh, Primitive};\\nuse pav_core::props::{DEFAULT_ROLES, ResolvedPart};\\nuse pav_core::puppet::PuppetDef;\\nuse pav_core::shape::Sway;\\nuse pav_core::statics::Ladder;\\nuse pav_core::statics::{ChunkKey, block_flags};\\nuse pav_core::zones::{Label, LabelMode, Zone, ZoneKind};\\nuse pav_core::{Color, Look, RenderFrame, RenderObject, Shape, choice_enum};\\nuse pav_render::mesh::{MeshData, Vertex};\\n20→use pav_render::scene::{self as rs, MeshInstance, MeshKey, Scene, SdfInstance, Style, Tonemap};\\nuse pav_render::text::{Anchor, Text3d};\\nuse serde::{Deserialize, Serialize};\\n\\nuse crate::camera::CameraRig;\\nuse crate::materials::{self, MaterialTable};\\nuse pav_core::material::Library;\\nuse pav_core::props::doc::MapMode;\\n\\nchoice_enum! {\\n30→    pub enum StyleOverride { PerObject => \\\"per object\\\", Flat => \\\"flat\\\", Cel => \\\"cel\\\", Lit => \\\"lit\\\" }\\n}\\n\\nchoice_enum! {\\n    pub enum TonemapChoice { Clamp => \\\"clamp\\\", SoftKnee => \\\"soft knee\\\", Aces => \\\"aces\\\" }\\n}\\n\\n#[derive(Clone, Debug, Serialize, Deserialize)]\\n#[serde(default)]\\npub struct LightSettings {\\n40→    /// Sun height above the horizon (degrees).\",\"content_concise\":\"1→//! Scene building: interpolates between two simulation frames and emits render instances.\\n\\nuse std::collections::{BTreeMap, HashMap, HashSet};\\nuse std::sync::{Arc, Mutex, MutexGuard};\\n\\nuse glam::{Mat4, Quat, Vec3};\\nuse pav_core::frame::{PuppetFrame, SimEvent};\\nuse pav_core::fxdef::{EmitterDef, LightDef};\\nuse pav_core::params::{ChoiceParam, ParamVisitor, Tunable, nested};\\n10→use pav_core::prop_instance::PropFrame;\\nuse pav_core::props::geom::{Generated, GeomMesh, Primitive};\\nuse pav_core::props::{DEFAULT_ROLES, ResolvedPart};\\nuse pav_core::puppet::PuppetDef;\\nuse pav_core::shape::Sway;\\nuse pav_core::statics::Ladder;\\nuse pav_core::statics::{ChunkKey, block_flags};\\nuse pav_core::zones::{Label, LabelMode, Zone, ZoneKind};\\nuse pav_core::{Color, Look, RenderFrame, RenderObject, Shape, choice_enum};\\nuse pav_render::mesh::{MeshData, Vertex};\\n20→use pav_render::scene::{self as rs, MeshInstance, MeshKey, Scene, SdfInstance, Style, Tonemap};\\nuse pav_render::text::{Anchor, Text3d};\\nuse serde::{Deserialize, Serialize};\\n\\nuse crate::camera::CameraRig;\\nuse crate::materials::{self, MaterialTable};\\nuse pav_core::material::Library;\\nuse pav_core::props::doc::MapMode;\\n\\nchoice_enum! {\\n30→    pub enum StyleOverride { PerObject => \\\"per object\\\", Flat => \\\"flat\\\", Cel => \\\"cel\\\", Lit => \\\"lit\\\" }\\n}\\n\\nchoice_enum! {\\n    pub enum TonemapChoice { Clamp => \\\"clamp\\\", SoftKnee => \\\"soft knee\\\", Aces => \\\"aces\\\" }\\n}\\n\\n#[derive(Clone, Debug, Serialize, Deserialize)]\\n#[serde(default)]\\npub struct LightSettings {\\n40→    /// Sun height above the horizon (degrees).\",\"absolute_path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224015__x42677a/work/Hands of Harbor: Second Opinion-Trauma Center: Second Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-224015/engine/crates/pav_view/src/build.rs\",\"offset\":1,\"limit\":40,\"raw_output\":\"//! Scene building: interpolates between two simulation frames and emits render instances.\\n\\nuse std::collections::{BTreeMap, HashMap, HashSet};\\nuse std::sync::{Arc, Mutex, MutexGuard};\\n\\nuse glam::{Mat4, Quat, Vec3};\\nuse pav_core::frame::{PuppetFrame, SimEvent};\\nuse pav_core::fxdef::{EmitterDef, LightDef};\\nuse pav_core::params::{ChoiceParam, ParamVisitor, Tunable, nested};\\nuse pav_core::prop_instance::PropFrame;\\nuse pav_core::props::geom::{Generated, GeomMesh, Primitive};\\nuse pav_core::props::{DEFAULT_ROLES, ResolvedPart};\\nuse pav_core::puppet::PuppetDef;\\nuse pav_core::shape::Sway;\\nuse pav_core::statics::Ladder;\\nuse pav_core::statics::{ChunkKey, block_flags};\\nuse pav_core::zones::{Label, LabelMode, Zone, ZoneKind};\\nuse pav_core::{Color, Look, RenderFrame, RenderObject, Shape, choice_enum};\\nuse pav_render::mesh::{MeshData, Vertex};\\nuse pav_render::scene::{self as rs, MeshInstance, MeshKey, Scene, SdfInstance, Style, Tonemap};\\nuse pav_render::text::{Anchor, Text3d};\\nuse serde::{Deserialize, Serialize};\\n\\nuse crate::camera::CameraRig;\\nuse crate::materials::{self, MaterialTable};\\nuse pav_core::material::Library;\\nuse pav_core::props::doc::MapMode;\\n\\nchoice_enum! {\\n    pub enum StyleOverride { PerObject => \\\"per object\\\", Flat => \\\"flat\\\", Cel => \\\"cel\\\", Lit => \\\"lit\\\" }\\n}\\n\\nchoice_enum! {\\n    pub enum TonemapChoice { Clamp => \\\"clamp\\\", SoftKnee => \\\"soft knee\\\", Aces => \\\"aces\\\" }\\n}\\n\\n#[derive(Clone, Debug, Serialize, Deserialize)]\\n#[serde(default)]\\npub struct LightSettings {\\n    /// Sun height above the horizon (degrees).\\n\",\"total_lines\":2405}}","is_error":false},{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-5564f0ae-818b-4f33-a975-561ee727ca35-68","content":"{\"type\":\"GrepSearch\",\"stdout\":[60,119,111,114,107,115,112,97,99,101,95,114,101,115,117,108,116,32,119,111,114,107,115,112,97,99,101,95,112,97,116,104,61,34,47,104,111,109,101,47,109,105,99,104,97,47,100,101,118,47,99,99,45,109,97,116,114,105,120,47,114,117,110,115,47,103,114