MeshData {\"},{\"line_number\":74,\"content\":\"impl MeshData {\"}]}]}","is_error":false},{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-c21a8b1a-efa0-40dd-bfa7-b8391e7158be-78","content":"{\"type\":\"ReadFile\",\"FileContent\":{\"content\":\"650→            dynamic: Vec::new(),\\n            particles: Vec::new(),\\n            distortions: Vec::new(),\\n            wind: Wind::default(),\\n            time: 0.0,\\n            materials: std::sync::Arc::default(),\\n            materials_version: 0,\\n        }\\n    }\\n}\\n660→\\n/// Converts an 8-bit sRGB color to linear RGB.\\npub fn srgb(r: u8, g: u8, b: u8) -> Vec3 {\\n    Vec3::new(srgb_to_linear(r as f32 / 255.0), srgb_to_linear(g as f32 / 255.0), srgb_to_linear(b as f32 / 255.0))\\n}\\n\\n/// Parses \\\"#rrggbb\\\" (or \\\"rrggbb\\\") into linear RGB.\\npub fn hex(s: &str) -> Option<Vec3> {\\n    let s = s.trim_start_matches('#');\\n    if s.len() != 6 {\\n670→        return None;\\n    }\\n    let v = u32::from_str_radix(s, 16).ok()?;\\n    Some(srgb((v >> 16) as u8, (v >> 8) as u8, v as u8))\\n}\\n\\npub fn srgb_to_linear(c: f32) -> f32 {\\n    if c <= 0.04045 { c / 12.92 } else { ((c + 0.055) / 1.055).powf(2.4) }\\n}\\n\\n680→pub fn linear_to_srgb(c: f32) -> f32 {\\n    if c <= 0.0031308 { c * 12.92 } else { 1.055 * c.powf(1.0 / 2.4) - 0.055 }\\n}\\n\",\"content_concise\":\"650→            dynamic: Vec::new(),\\n            particles: Vec::new(),\\n            distortions: Vec::new(),\\n            wind: Wind::default(),\\n            time: 0.0,\\n            materials: std::sync::Arc::default(),\\n            materials_version: 0,\\n        }\\n    }\\n}\\n660→\\n/// Converts an 8-bit sRGB color to linear RGB.\\npub fn srgb(r: u8, g: u8, b: u8) -> Vec3 {\\n    Vec3::new(srgb_to_linear(r as f32 / 255.0), srgb_to_linear(g as f32 / 255.0), srgb_to_linear(b as f32 / 255.0))\\n}\\n\\n/// Parses \\\"#rrggbb\\\" (or \\\"rrggbb\\\") into linear RGB.\\npub fn hex(s: &str) -> Option<Vec3> {\\n    let s = s.trim_start_matches('#');\\n    if s.len() != 6 {\\n670→        return None;\\n    }\\n    let v = u32::from_str_radix(s, 16).ok()?;\\n    Some(srgb((v >> 16) as u8, (v >> 8) as u8, v as u8))\\n}\\n\\npub fn srgb_to_linear(c: f32) -> f32 {\\n    if c <= 0.04045 { c / 12.92 } else { ((c + 0.055) / 1.055).powf(2.4) }\\n}\\n\\n680→pub fn linear_to_srgb(c: f32) -> f32 {\\n    if c <= 0.0031308 { c * 12.92 } else { 1.055 * c.powf(1.0 / 2.4) - 0.055 }\\n}\\n\",\"absolute_path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224015__x42677a/work/Hands of Harbor: Second Opinion-Trauma Center: Second Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-224015/engine/crates/pav_render/src/scene.rs\",\"offset\":650,\"limit\":40,\"raw_output\":\"            dynamic: Vec::new(),\\n            particles: Vec::new(),\\n            distortions: Vec::new(),\\n            wind: Wind::default(),\\n            time: 0.0,\\n            materials: std::sync::Arc::default(),\\n            materials_version: 0,\\n        }\\n    }\\n}\\n\\n/// Converts an 8-bit sRGB color to linear RGB.\\npub fn srgb(r: u8, g: u8, b: u8) -> Vec3 {\\n    Vec3::new(srgb_to_linear(r as f32 / 255.0), srgb_to_linear(g as f32 / 255.0), srgb_to_linear(b as f32 / 255.0))\\n}\\n\\n/// Parses \\\"#rrggbb\\\" (or \\\"rrggbb\\\") into linear RGB.\\npub fn hex(s: &str) -> Option<Vec3> {\\n    let s = s.trim_start_matches('#');\\n    if s.len() != 6 {\\n        return None;\\n    }\\n    let v = u32::from_str_radix(s, 16).ok()?;\\n    Some(srgb((v >> 16) as u8, (v >> 8) as u8, v as u8))\\n}\\n\\npub fn srgb_to_linear(c: f32) -> f32 {\\n    if c <= 0.04045 { c / 12.92 } else { ((c + 0.055) / 1.055).powf(2.4) }\\n}\\n\\npub fn linear_to_srgb(c: f32) -> f32 {\\n    if c <= 0.0031308 { c * 12.92 } else { 1.055 * c.powf(1.0 / 2.4) - 0.055 }\\n}\\n\",\"total_lines\":682}}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa38-de6f-7dc0-ae0d-e0f717ed75f2","uuid":"9e600481-54b9-49f9-a740-cd3e85dbf3b0"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_31","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-978bcbf1-5d08-4f95-a69d-e22b2e7410b1-79","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224015__x42677a/work/Hands of Harbor: Second Opinion-Trauma Center: Second Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-224015/engine/crates/pav_render/src/mesh.rs","offset":1,"limit":90}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":6978,"output_tokens":107,"cache_read_input_tokens":152192,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa38-de6f-7dc0-ae0d-e0f717ed75f2","uuid":"163dd394-5f0a-4900-be08-7ec4541e1224"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-978bcbf1-5d08-4f95-a69d-e22b2e7410b1-79","content":"{\"type\":\"ReadFile\",\"FileContent\":{\"content\":\"1→//! Procedural mesh generation. Every built-in mesh fits the unit cube [-0.5, 0.5]^3\\n//! so an instance's scale equals its size. Winding is counter-clockwise when seen from outside.\\n\\nuse bytemuck::{Pod, Zeroable};\\nuse glam::Vec3;\\n\\n#[repr(C)]\\n#[derive(Clone, Copy, Debug, Default, Pod, Zeroable)]\\npub struct Vertex {\\n10→    pub pos: [f32; 3],\\n    pub normal: [f32; 3],\\n    pub uv: [f32; 2],\\n    /// Multiplied with the instance colour (white for built-in meshes).\\n    pub color: [f32; 4],\\n}\\n\\n#[derive(Clone, Debug, Default)]\\npub struct MeshData {\\n    pub vertices: Vec<Vertex>,\\n20→    pub indices: Vec<u32>,\\n}\\n\\n/// Identifies a mesh. Built-ins and rounded boxes are generated on demand by the renderer;\\n/// `Custom` meshes must be uploaded with `Renderer::upsert_mesh` first.\\n#[derive(Clone, Copy, Debug, PartialEq, Eq, Hash, PartialOrd, Ord)]\\npub enum MeshKey {\\n    Cube,\\n    Sphere,\\n    Cylinder,\\n30→    Cone,\\n    Plane,\\n    /// A tuft of grass: seven tapered, curving blades in the unit box (two-sided).\\n    Tuft,\\n    /// Rounded box with absolute half extents and corner radius, in millimetres.\\n    RoundedBox {\\n        half_mm: [u32; 3],\\n        radius_mm: u32,\\n    },\\n    Custom(u64),\\n40→}\\n\\nimpl MeshKey {\\n    pub fn rounded_box(half: Vec3, radius: f32) -> Self {\\n        let mm = |v: f32| (v.max(0.0) * 1000.0).round() as u32;\\n        MeshKey::RoundedBox { half_mm: [mm(half.x), mm(half.y), mm(half.z)], radius_mm: mm(radius) }\\n    }\\n\\n    pub fn generate(&self) -> Option<MeshData> {\\n        Some(match *self {\\n50→            MeshKey::Cube => MeshData::cube(),\\n            MeshKey::Sphere => MeshData::sphere(32, 16),\\n            MeshKey::Cylinder => MeshData::cylinder(32),\\n            MeshKey::Cone => MeshData::cone(32),\\n            MeshKey::Plane => MeshData::plane(),\\n            MeshKey::Tuft => MeshData::tuft(),\\n            MeshKey::RoundedBox { half_mm, radius_mm } => {\\n                let h = Vec3::new(half_mm[0] as f32, half_mm[1] as f32, half_mm[2] as f32) / 1000.0;\\n                MeshData::rounded_box(h, radius_mm as f32 / 1000.0, 4)\\n            }\\n60→            MeshKey::Custom(_) => return None,\\n        })\\n    }\\n}\\n\\n/// Tangent frame (u, v) for a face with normal n, such that cross(u, v) == n.\\nfn face_frame(n: Vec3) -> (Vec3, Vec3) {\\n    let v = if n.y.abs() > 0.5 { Vec3::Z * n.y.signum() } else { Vec3::Y };\\n    let u = v.cross(n);\\n    (u, v)\\n70→}\\n\\nconst FACES: [Vec3; 6] = [Vec3::X, Vec3::NEG_X, Vec3::Y, Vec3::NEG_Y, Vec3::Z, Vec3::NEG_Z];\\n\\nimpl MeshData {\\n    fn push(&mut self, pos: Vec3, normal: Vec3, uv: [f32; 2]) -> u32 {\\n        self.vertices.push(Vertex { pos: pos.to_array(), normal: normal.to_array(), uv, color: [1.0; 4] });\\n        (self.vertices.len() - 1) as u32\\n    }\\n\\n80→    /// Adds a quad; corners must be counter-clockwise seen from the side `normal` points to.\\n    pub fn push_quad(&mut self, p: [Vec3; 4], normal: Vec3) {\\n        let uvs = [[0.0, 1.0], [1.0, 1.0], [1.0, 0.0], [0.0, 0.0]];\\n        let i0 = self.push(p[0], normal, uvs[0]);\\n        for k in 1..4 {\\n            self.push(p[k], normal, uvs[k]);\\n        }\\n        self.indices.extend_from_slice(&[i0, i0 + 1, i0 + 2, i0, i0 + 2, i0 + 3]);\\n    }\\n\\n90→    pub fn cube() -> Self {\",\"content_concise\":\"1→//! Procedural mesh generation. Every built-in mesh fits the unit cube [-0.5, 0.5]^3\\n//! so an instance's scale equals its size. Winding is counter-clockwise when seen from outside.\\n\\nuse bytemuck::{Pod, Zeroable};\\nuse glam::Vec3;\\n\\n#[repr(C)]\\n#[derive(Clone, Copy, Debug, Default, Pod, Zeroable)]\\npub struct Vertex {\\n10→    pub pos: [f32; 3],\\n    pub normal: [f32; 3],\\n    pub uv: [f32; 2],\\n    /// Multiplied with the instance colour (white for built-in meshes).\\n    pub color: [f32; 4],\\n}\\n\\n#[derive(Clone, Debug, Default)]\\npub struct MeshData {\\n    pub vertices: Vec<Vertex>,\\n20→    pub indices: Vec<u32>,\\n}\\n\\n/// Identifies a mesh. Built-ins and rounded boxes are generated on demand by the renderer;\\n/// `Custom` meshes must be uploaded with `Renderer::upsert_mesh` first.\\n#[derive(Clone, Copy, Debug, PartialEq, Eq, Hash, PartialOrd, Ord)]\\npub enum MeshKey {\\n    Cube,\\n    Sphere,\\n    Cylinder,\\n30→    Cone,\\n    Plane,\\n    /// A tuft of grass: seven tapered, curving blades in the unit box (two-sided).\\n    Tuft,\\n    /// Rounded box with absolute half extents and corner radius, in millimetres.\\n    RoundedBox {\\n        half_mm: [u32; 3],\\n        radius_mm: u32,\\n    },\\n    Custom(u64),\\n40→}\\n\\nimpl MeshKey {\\n    pub fn rounded_box(half: Vec3, radius: f32) -> Self {\\n        let mm = |v: f32| (v.max(0.0) * 1000.0).round() as u32;\\n        MeshKey::RoundedBox { half_mm: [mm(half.x), mm(half.y), mm(half.z)], radius_mm: mm(radius) }\\n    }\\n\\n    pub fn generate(&self) -> Option<MeshData> {\\n        Some(match *self {\\n50→            MeshKey::Cube => MeshData::cube(),\\n            MeshKey::Sphere => MeshData::sphere(32, 16),\\n            MeshKey::Cylinder => MeshData::cylinder(32),\\n            MeshKey::Cone => MeshData::cone(32),\\n            MeshKey::Plane => MeshData::plane(),\\n            MeshKey::Tuft => MeshData::tuft(),\\n            MeshKey::RoundedBox { half_mm, radius_mm } => {\\n                let h = Vec3::new(half_mm[0] as f32, half_mm[1] as f32, half_mm[2] as f32) / 1000.0;\\n                MeshData::rounded_box(h, radius_mm as f32 / 1000.0, 4)\\n            }\\n60→            MeshKey::Custom(_) => return None,\\n        })\\n    }\\n}\\n\\n/// Tangent frame (u, v) for a face with normal n, such that cross(u, v) == n.\\nfn face_frame(n: Vec3) -> (Vec3, Vec3) {\\n    let v = if n.y.abs() > 0.5 { Vec3::Z * n.y.signum() } else { Vec3::Y };\\n    let u = v.cross(n);\\n    (u, v)\\n70→}\\n\\nconst FACES: [Vec3; 6] = [Vec3::X, Vec3::NEG_X, Vec3::Y, Vec3::NEG_Y, Vec3::Z, Vec3::NEG_Z];\\n\\nimpl MeshData {\\n    fn push(&mut self, pos: Vec3, normal: Vec3, uv: [f32; 2]) -> u32 {\\n        self.vertices.push(Vertex { pos: pos.to_array(), normal: normal.to_array(), uv, color: [1.0; 4] });\\n        (self.vertices.len() - 1) as u32\\n    }\\n\\n80→    /// Adds a quad; corners must be counter-clockwise seen from the side `normal` points to.\\n    pub fn push_quad(&mut self, p: [Vec3; 4], normal: Vec3) {\\n        let uvs = [[0.0, 1.0], [1.0, 1.0], [1.0, 0.0], [0.0, 0.0]];\\n        let i0 = self.push(p[0], normal, uvs[0]);\\n        for k in 1..4 {\\n            self.push(p[k], normal, uvs[k]);\\n        }\\n        self.indices.extend_from_slice(&[i0, i0 + 1, i0 + 2, i0, i0 + 2, i0 + 3]);\\n    }\\n\\n90→    pub fn cube() -> Self {\",\"absolute_path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224015__x42677a/work/Hands of Harbor: Second Opinion-Trauma Center: Second Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-224015/engine/crates/pav_render/src/mesh.rs\",\"offset\":1,\"limit\":90,\"raw_output\":\"//! Procedural mesh generation. Every built-in mesh fits the unit cube [-0.5, 0.5]^3\\n//! so an instance's scale equals its size. Winding is counter-clockwise when seen from outside.\\n\\nuse bytemuck::{Pod, Zeroable};\\nuse glam::Vec3;\\n\\n#[repr(C)]\\n#[derive(Clone, Copy, Debug, Default, Pod, Zeroable)]\\npub struct Vertex {\\n    pub pos: [f32; 3],\\n    pub normal: [f32; 3],\\n    pub uv: [f32; 2],\\n    /// Multiplied with the instance colour (white for built-in meshes).\\n    pub color: [f32; 4],\\n}\\n\\n#[derive(Clone, Debug, Default)]\\npub struct MeshData {\\n    pub vertices: Vec<Vertex>,\\n    pub indices: Vec<u32>,\\n}\\n\\n/// Identifies a mesh. Built-ins and rounded boxes are generated on demand by the renderer;\\n/// `Custom` meshes must be uploaded with `Renderer::upsert_mesh` first.\\n#[derive(Clone, Copy, Debug, PartialEq, Eq, Hash, PartialOrd, Ord)]\\npub enum MeshKey {\\n    Cube,\\n    Sphere,\\n    Cylinder,\\n    Cone,\\n    Plane,\\n    /// A tuft of grass: seven tapered, curving blades in the unit box (two-sided).\\n    Tuft,\\n    /// Rounded box with absolute half extents and corner radius, in millimetres.\\n    RoundedBox {\\n        half_mm: [u32; 3],\\n        radius_mm: u32,\\n    },\\n    Custom(u64),\\n}\\n\\nimpl MeshKey {\\n    pub fn rounded_box(half: Vec3, radius: f32) -> Self {\\n        let mm = |v: f32| (v.max(0.0) * 1000.0).round() as u32;\\n        MeshKey::RoundedBox { half_mm: [mm(half.x), mm(half.y), mm(half.z)], radius_mm: mm(radius) }\\n    }\\n\\n    pub fn generate(&self) -> Option<MeshData> {\\n        Some(match *self {\\n            MeshKey::Cube => MeshData::cube(),\\n            MeshKey::Sphere => MeshData::sphere(32, 16),\\n            MeshKey::Cylinder => MeshData::cylinder(32),\\n            MeshKey::Cone => MeshData::cone(32),\\n            MeshKey::Plane => MeshData::plane(),\\n            MeshKey::Tuft => MeshData::tuft(),\\n            MeshKey::RoundedBox { half_mm, radius_mm } => {\\n                let h = Vec3::new(half_mm[0] as f32, half_mm[1] as f32, half_mm[2] as f32) / 1000.0;\\n                MeshData::rounded_box(h, radius_mm as f32 / 1000.0, 4)\\n            }\\n            MeshKey::Custom(_) => return None,\\n        })\\n    }\\n}\\n\\n/// Tangent frame (u, v) for a face with normal n, such that cross(u, v) == n.\\nfn face_frame(n: Vec3) -> (Vec3, Vec3) {\\n    let v = if n.y.abs() > 0.5 { Vec3::Z * n.y.signum() } else { Vec3::Y };\\n    let u = v.cross(n);\\n    (u, v)\\n}\\n\\nconst FACES: [Vec3; 6] = [Vec3::X, Vec3::NEG_X, Vec3::Y, Vec3::NEG_Y, Vec3::Z, Vec3::NEG_Z];\\n\\nimpl MeshData {\\n    fn push(&mut self, pos: Vec3, normal: Vec3, uv: [f32; 2]) -> u32 {\\n        self.vertices.push(Vertex { pos: pos.to_array(), normal: normal.to_array(), uv, color: [1.0; 4] });\\n        (self.vertices.len() - 1) as u32\\n    }\\n\\n    /// Adds a quad; corners must be counter-clockwise seen from the side `normal` points to.\\n    pub fn push_quad(&mut self, p: [Vec3; 4], normal: Vec3) {\\n        let uvs = [[0.0, 1.0], [1.0, 1.0], [1.0, 0.0], [0.0, 0.0]];\\n        let i0 = self.push(p[0], normal, uvs[0]);\\n        for k in 1..4 {\\n            self.push(p[k], normal, uvs[k]);\\n        }\\n        self.indices.extend_from_slice(&[i0, i0 + 1, i0 + 2, i0, i0 + 2, i0 + 3]);\\n    }\\n\\n    pub fn cube() -> Self {\\n\",\"total_lines\":287}}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa38-de6f-7dc0-ae0d-e0f717ed75f2","uuid":"d1766c0d-f58e-41b9-83f6-da1ecd52a4c3"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_32","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"I have everything needed. I will write the code now in large chunks.\n\nI will structure the surgery simulator as a single coherent system. I plan to modify input.rs and create seven modules: tune.rs, heart.rs, field.rs, strain.rs, story.rs, and cases.rs. Case data will be embedded in Rust for reliability, with a mirrored TOML file for designers.\n\nI will embed the TOML case data directly in Rust using `include_str!` and parse it with serde. This keeps designer-editable text files while avoiding separate data synchronization.\n\nI will write the TOML case files directly with the write tool. The Rust code will generate CaseDef structs from those TOML files at runtime, keeping a single source of truth. I am now setting design parameters for the cases, including cursor speed and bot aiming behavior.\n\nCase 0 is now fully defined with specific hazard positions and drain rates. Phase 0 pools and foreign bodies total roughly 1.9 drain per second. The bot can clear all five items in about ten seconds, followed by a five-second phase two dressing, keeping the total time around twenty seconds. Case 1 will use vitals of 84 and a timer of 270.\n\nCase 1 now has a seven-phase structure. Phase zero includes an incision and a pool with drain 0.5, so idle death occurs in about seventy seconds. Phase one reveals three polyps and inflam gel. Phase two applies a bleeder drain of 3.0 plus an IV port. Phase three is dressing.\n\nCase 2 begins with an incision and pool. Phase one requires a scanner for three hidden foreign bodies plus a laceration. Phase two uses scripted code. Phase three sutures the remaining laceration and applies dressing.\n\nCase 3 starts with a three-stage tumor and a pool.\n\nCase 3 Phase 1 will use a strain introit that spawns its own hazards and advances the phase when finished. Cases 4 through 7 are now defined: lacrimosa, bone plus echo with pet tremor, dies irae cryo, and libera with duet and partner. A special code blue case will be handled separately. Strain completion is signaled by a done flag set during tick when the final phase clears. A partner bot is also being planned.\n\nThe partner bot will be driven internally inside `post()` when the second surgeon slot is uncontrolled by a human. The game receives a single `InputFrame` containing all surgeons, so the simulator can detect human control via `input.surgeons[1].active` and fall back to its own bot logic for the partner slot.\n\nThe partner bot will only fill the second surgeon slot when that slot is inactive, preventing double control during automated tests. Echo ghost logic will also be handled inside `post`, completing the next pending hazard when echo is active.\n\nThe echo ghost will render as a separate `echo_cursor` field rather than using a fourth input slot. Surgeon slots are reserved for human players, and the simulator trusts the app's active flags. I will write the code now with the goal of a clean first compile, and I can access the random number generator through `sim.state.rng` inside `post`.\n\nI realized `post` does not receive input, so I cannot store the latest input on the struct. I will keep all logic in `pre()` before physics and skip `post` entirely.\n\n`pre()` will run the entire tick and return an empty `BTreeMap`. `post()` can remain empty or handle cleanup. The simulator can safely use `sim.state.rng` during pre because the game is temporarily removed from the sim. I will push `SimEvent::Cue` events and store outcomes in `self.outcome`.\n\nStatus JSON will carry screen, vitals, tool, score, rank, coverage, tune, and mode. The window status merges shell and simulator state. State will use Vec instead of HashMap for hash stability. f32 determinism is acceptable on the same platform. Divisions will be clamped to prevent NaN. I am now writing field.rs and mod.rs. A Mode enum will define the campaign story player states.\n\nStory mode will use a block-and-line index to advance through campaign segments. The sequence runs before_0, chart, op, results, after_0, before_1, and so on.\n\nDead mode displays the time of death. A bot can press confirm to retry, but idle death leaves the outcome as Lost. Retry restores the checkpoint or restarts the case and returns the outcome to Playing.\n\nThe Results mode will appear immediately after an operation completes and set the outcome to Won so automated tests can return cleanly. The campaign will only mark the final story block as Won once the entire sequence finishes. In Attract mode the simulator runs an immortal bot slice with full gifts, but it does not end itself; the shell returns to Title on any input.\n\nThe shell will accumulate idle time and switch to Attract after ten seconds, exiting back to Title on any input. A touch-only mode will suppress gameplay buttons and show a settings message.\n\nThe shell will be pure logic with egui drawing. It will live in `pav_ui::surgery` and reuse the existing `pav_core` dependency for tune defaults. The BarlowCondensed font will be bundled as an include_bytes asset. I will download the font and hub files while writing the first code files, and I will also write PROGRESS.md.\n\nI will mark the first plan checklist item complete now that PROGRESS.md is written. I am continuing implementation without waiting.\n\nI also spotted a bug in the laser bot logic. The bot must release the use button on the tick immediately after it was pressed, not on the tick before. I will track `was_use` to detect this transition and check heat at the start of each tick. If heat is below 0.90, the bot holds use; otherwise it releases.\n\nThe laser bot will release the use button on the tick immediately after it was pressed. This timing gives roughly eight ticks of margin before heat reaches 1.02.\n\nThe suture bot will alternate its aim side based on cursor position relative to the needle. It targets the opposite side each time, crossing zero near the needle to register stitch completions.\n\nThe suture bot will zigzag continuously by aiming at the opposite side of the needle each tick. The forceps bot will aim at a hazard and hold use while grabbing it, then pull slightly along the axis once grabbed. The scalpel bot will advance its aim forward along the work direction. For hidden objects, the bot will select the scanner to reveal them before using forceps. A goal priority function is being drafted to rank tasks for each surgeon slot.\n\nThe goal priority function now ranks tasks for each surgeon slot. It checks code activation first, then release when the heat ring is in danger while holding use. Gift and IV are next if needed. Then it sorts actionable hazards by drain rate and priority, selecting the highest drain first. Hidden objects are only targeted if they remain unrevealed. An actionable hazard must be alive, match the current phase, and not be hidden or already revealed.\n\nThe heat ring bot will lift off the use button when the heat ring sits between 0.3 and 0.75 unless a defib or gift is active.\n\nA `nz` helper will clamp divisions to prevent NaN. The case blue timer win condition is now defined: mode Op, case_id -1, timer at zero or below, vitals above zero, and no code active yields outcome Won. Difficulty levels will scale drain rate and timer multiplier with values 1.0, 1.25, and 1.5 for drain, and 1.0, 0.85, and 0.7 for timer. Coverage rewards will be added when tools complete.\n\nDifficulty 0 gives 2 codes, difficulty 1 gives 1, and difficulty 2 gives none. The `Tune` struct will hold twelve sliders with default values: drain, timer, tool_power, iv_heal, strain_speed, strain_tough, heart_coupling, beat_window_ms, cursor_speed, aim_assist, gift_gain, and gift_duration.\n\nThe `Tune` struct now includes seven more sliders: hush_scale, echo_duration, chain_window, rating_strict, wrong_penalty, code_window, and score_mul. The chain window defaults to eight seconds; a clean action must occur within that window or the chain resets. Rating strictness scales the thresholds so higher values tighten the immaculate window.\n\nThe immaculate window is 0.25 divided by rating strictness. The code will be split into tune.rs, heart.rs, kinds.rs, field.rs, strain.rs, bot.rs, story.rs, content.rs, frame.rs, net.rs, and mod.rs. Tests will go in pav_core/tests/surgery.rs. I am starting to write the files now.\n\nI will register the surgery game in the global `GAMES` list and add `surgery` to the scene keys test. I am also checking whether `Sim::new` can run without a player entity.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-f8af0ba0-ab0d-48a9-97bc-5c966c3f0c8f-80","name":"grep","input":{"pattern":"clear|sky_color|background","glob":"**/pav_render/src/scene.rs","head_limit":30}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-f8af0ba0-ab0d-48a9-97bc-5c966c3f0c8f-81","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224015__x42677a/work/Hands of Harbor: Second Opinion-Trauma Center: Second Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-224015/engine/crates/pav_view/src/camera.rs","limit":80}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1288,"output_tokens":4273,"cache_read_input_tokens":159104,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa38-de6f-7dc0-ae0d-e0f717ed75f2","uuid":"aff397c3-c076-4fe3-80e1-09ed33602efa"}
