{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-7f3b295f-08fa-4a37-b840-95b2077ddabe-36","content":"{\"type\":\"ReadFile\",\"FileContent\":{\"content\":\"45→web-time = \\\"1\\\"\\n# Browser build only.\\nwasm-bindgen = \\\"0.2\\\"\\nwasm-bindgen-futures = \\\"0.4\\\"\\nweb-sys = \\\"0.3\\\"\\n50→\\n[workspace.lints.clippy]\\n# Style lints that fight readable game code.\\ncollapsible_if = \\\"allow\\\"\\ncollapsible_match = \\\"allow\\\"\\ntype_complexity = \\\"allow\\\"\\ntoo_many_arguments = \\\"allow\\\"\\n\\n[profile.dev]\\nopt-level = 1\\n60→# Keeps the target folder small (cloud containers have a fixed disk allowance); backtraces\\n# still show file:line.\\ndebug = \\\"line-tables-only\\\"\\nincremental = false\\n\\n[profile.dev.package.\\\"*\\\"]\\nopt-level = 3\\ndebug = false\\n\\n[profile.release]\\n70→debug = \\\"line-tables-only\\\"\\n\\n# Distribution build (what gets sent to the user): smaller, still has function names in crash reports.\\n[profile.dist]\\ninherits = \\\"release\\\"\",\"content_concise\":\"45→web-time = \\\"1\\\"\\n# Browser build only.\\nwasm-bindgen = \\\"0.2\\\"\\nwasm-bindgen-futures = \\\"0.4\\\"\\nweb-sys = \\\"0.3\\\"\\n50→\\n[workspace.lints.clippy]\\n# Style lints that fight readable game code.\\ncollapsible_if = \\\"allow\\\"\\ncollapsible_match = \\\"allow\\\"\\ntype_complexity = \\\"allow\\\"\\ntoo_many_arguments = \\\"allow\\\"\\n\\n[profile.dev]\\nopt-level = 1\\n60→# Keeps the target folder small (cloud containers have a fixed disk allowance); backtraces\\n# still show file:line.\\ndebug = \\\"line-tables-only\\\"\\nincremental = false\\n\\n[profile.dev.package.\\\"*\\\"]\\nopt-level = 3\\ndebug = false\\n\\n[profile.release]\\n70→debug = \\\"line-tables-only\\\"\\n\\n# Distribution build (what gets sent to the user): smaller, still has function names in crash reports.\\n[profile.dist]\\ninherits = \\\"release\\\"\",\"absolute_path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224015__x42677a/work/Hands of Harbor: Second Opinion-Trauma Center: Second Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-224015/engine/Cargo.toml\",\"offset\":45,\"limit\":30,\"raw_output\":\"web-time = \\\"1\\\"\\n# Browser build only.\\nwasm-bindgen = \\\"0.2\\\"\\nwasm-bindgen-futures = \\\"0.4\\\"\\nweb-sys = \\\"0.3\\\"\\n\\n[workspace.lints.clippy]\\n# Style lints that fight readable game code.\\ncollapsible_if = \\\"allow\\\"\\ncollapsible_match = \\\"allow\\\"\\ntype_complexity = \\\"allow\\\"\\ntoo_many_arguments = \\\"allow\\\"\\n\\n[profile.dev]\\nopt-level = 1\\n# Keeps the target folder small (cloud containers have a fixed disk allowance); backtraces\\n# still show file:line.\\ndebug = \\\"line-tables-only\\\"\\nincremental = false\\n\\n[profile.dev.package.\\\"*\\\"]\\nopt-level = 3\\ndebug = false\\n\\n[profile.release]\\ndebug = \\\"line-tables-only\\\"\\n\\n# Distribution build (what gets sent to the user): smaller, still has function names in crash reports.\\n[profile.dist]\\ninherits = \\\"release\\\"\\n\",\"total_lines\":76}}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa38-de6f-7dc0-ae0d-e0f717ed75f2","uuid":"6ad17c3e-9e7f-40c0-a783-c67f6288a54c"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_54","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Warnings won't fail the build unless they're explicitly denied.\n\nPlanning the implementation: fixing suture and heart, adding optional idle, then writing the story and cases modules. Each case should take roughly 20–40 seconds of simulation time. Estimated bot durations for individual hazards are being calculated.\n\nCampaign simulation time is estimated at roughly three minutes. Ten seeds total about 32 seconds at 0.3 ms per tick, or 108 seconds at 1 ms. The Code Blue scenario lasts four minutes per seed, totaling 144,000 ticks across ten seeds. The bot must survive until the timer reaches zero to win.\n\nCode Blue is treated as a case with ID -1. Testing it across ten seeds would require forty minutes of simulation time, which is too slow. The plan must run all cases and the campaign in under ten minutes total. A tick rate of 0.2 ms per step is being considered to keep the full test suite under thirty seconds.\n\nThe campaign will be tested separately from the individual cases. Each seed runs the full campaign plus all eight cases, then each case is tested alone. The combined suite totals roughly 720,000 ticks. At 0.15 ms per step this takes about 108 seconds, and at 0.5 ms about six minutes.\n\nA 2 ms tick rate would require 24 minutes of simulation time. The next step is to write the game and benchmark a single physics step. Code Blue may not need four minutes of active play if waves are sparse and the bot waits idle; empty physics steps are typically fast. Disabling physics when no bodies exist is not straightforward. Recording every input for the entire run is another concern.\n\nInput recording is lightweight: roughly 3 MB for Code Blue and 4 MB for the campaign. History is disabled to prevent clones. Code Blue waves must be spaced so idle time does not kill the patient; the bot must clear each wave quickly.\n\nCode Blue will use eight waves spaced 25 seconds apart, with the bot clearing each in about five seconds and waiting through the remaining 20 seconds. The final 20 seconds will be a small strain. The developer is now writing the code, noting that tests run in the dev profile with opt-level 1 for the package itself.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-9de5151a-b812-47f8-a21c-f26a0ac7ad31-37","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224015__x42677a/work/Hands of Harbor: Second Opinion-Trauma Center: Second Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-224015/engine/crates/pav_core/src/sim.rs","offset":1104,"limit":80}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":340,"output_tokens":1374,"cache_read_input_tokens":97024,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa38-de6f-7dc0-ae0d-e0f717ed75f2","uuid":"373c4666-bd0f-4309-881e-45f549983d43"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-9de5151a-b812-47f8-a21c-f26a0ac7ad31-37","content":"{\"type\":\"ReadFile\",\"FileContent\":{\"content\":\"1104→    /// Hash of the gameplay state, for repeatability checks: the tick, the random numbers, every\\n    /// entity, rigid and soft bodies (pose and velocity), the level's blocks and baked props,\\n    /// projectiles, courses, signals, crumbling tiles and the game (hero, items, gold, monsters,\\n    /// or a `games` game's own state).\\n    /// Two runs that hash the same played out the same.\\n    pub fn state_hash(&self) -> u64 {\\n1110→        let s = &self.state;\\n        let mut h = Fnv::default();\\n        h.u64(s.tick);\\n        h.data(&s.rng);\\n        h.data(&s.entities);\\n        for (_, b) in s.physics.bodies.iter() {\\n            h.floats(&b.translation().to_array());\\n            h.floats(&b.rotation().to_array());\\n            h.floats(&b.linvel().to_array());\\n            h.floats(&b.angvel().to_array());\\n1120→        }\\n        for (_, sb) in s.physics.soft_bodies.iter() {\\n            for (p, v) in sb.particle_positions().zip(sb.particle_velocities()) {\\n                h.floats(&p.to_array());\\n                h.floats(&v.to_array());\\n            }\\n        }\\n        h.u64(s.statics.block_count() as u64);\\n        h.u64(s.statics.prop_count() as u64);\\n        h.data(&s.projectiles);\\n1130→        h.data(&s.courses);\\n        h.data(&s.signals);\\n        h.data(&s.crumbles);\\n        h.data(&s.game);\\n        h.data(&s.play);\\n        h.0\\n    }\\n}\\n\\n/// 64-bit FNV-1a over everything written to it.\\n1140→struct Fnv(u64);\\n\\nimpl Default for Fnv {\\n    fn default() -> Self {\\n        Self(0xcbf2_9ce4_8422_2325)\\n    }\\n}\\n\\nimpl Fnv {\\n    fn u64(&mut self, x: u64) {\\n1150→        for b in x.to_le_bytes() {\\n            self.byte(b);\\n        }\\n    }\\n\\n    fn floats(&mut self, fs: &[f32]) {\\n        for f in fs {\\n            for b in f.to_bits().to_le_bytes() {\\n                self.byte(b);\\n            }\\n1160→        }\\n    }\\n\\n    /// Mixes in a value's serialized form (the same CBOR that snapshot files use; the state\\n    /// keeps its maps ordered, so the bytes are the same every run).\\n    fn data<T: Serialize + ?Sized>(&mut self, value: &T) {\\n        // Writing into the hash can't fail, and every state type serializes.\\n        let _ = ciborium::into_writer(value, &mut *self);\\n    }\\n\\n1170→    fn byte(&mut self, b: u8) {\\n        self.0 ^= b as u64;\\n        self.0 = self.0.wrapping_mul(0x0100_0000_01b3);\\n    }\\n}\\n\\nimpl std::io::Write for Fnv {\\n    fn write(&mut self, buf: &[u8]) -> std::io::Result<usize> {\\n        for &b in buf {\\n            self.byte(b);\\n1180→        }\\n        Ok(buf.len())\\n    }\\n\",\"content_concise\":\"1104→    /// Hash of the gameplay state, for repeatability checks: the tick, the random numbers, every\\n    /// entity, rigid and soft bodies (pose and velocity), the level's blocks and baked props,\\n    /// projectiles, courses, signals, crumbling tiles and the game (hero, items, gold, monsters,\\n    /// or a `games` game's own state).\\n    /// Two runs that hash the same played out the same.\\n    pub fn state_hash(&self) -> u64 {\\n1110→        let s = &self.state;\\n        let mut h = Fnv::default();\\n        h.u64(s.tick);\\n        h.data(&s.rng);\\n        h.data(&s.entities);\\n        for (_, b) in s.physics.bodies.iter() {\\n            h.floats(&b.translation().to_array());\\n            h.floats(&b.rotation().to_array());\\n            h.floats(&b.linvel().to_array());\\n            h.floats(&b.angvel().to_array());\\n1120→        }\\n        for (_, sb) in s.physics.soft_bodies.iter() {\\n            for (p, v) in sb.particle_positions().zip(sb.particle_velocities()) {\\n                h.floats(&p.to_array());\\n                h.floats(&v.to_array());\\n            }\\n        }\\n        h.u64(s.statics.block_count() as u64);\\n        h.u64(s.statics.prop_count() as u64);\\n        h.data(&s.projectiles);\\n1130→        h.data(&s.courses);\\n        h.data(&s.signals);\\n        h.data(&s.crumbles);\\n        h.data(&s.game);\\n        h.data(&s.play);\\n        h.0\\n    }\\n}\\n\\n/// 64-bit FNV-1a over everything written to it.\\n1140→struct Fnv(u64);\\n\\nimpl Default for Fnv {\\n    fn default() -> Self {\\n        Self(0xcbf2_9ce4_8422_2325)\\n    }\\n}\\n\\nimpl Fnv {\\n    fn u64(&mut self, x: u64) {\\n1150→        for b in x.to_le_bytes() {\\n            self.byte(b);\\n        }\\n    }\\n\\n    fn floats(&mut self, fs: &[f32]) {\\n        for f in fs {\\n            for b in f.to_bits().to_le_bytes() {\\n                self.byte(b);\\n            }\\n1160→        }\\n    }\\n\\n    /// Mixes in a value's serialized form (the same CBOR that snapshot files use; the state\\n    /// keeps its maps ordered, so the bytes are the same every run).\\n    fn data<T: Serialize + ?Sized>(&mut self, value: &T) {\\n        // Writing into the hash can't fail, and every state type serializes.\\n        let _ = ciborium::into_writer(value, &mut *self);\\n    }\\n\\n1170→    fn byte(&mut self, b: u8) {\\n        self.0 ^= b as u64;\\n        self.0 = self.0.wrapping_mul(0x0100_0000_01b3);\\n    }\\n}\\n\\nimpl std::io::Write for Fnv {\\n    fn write(&mut self, buf: &[u8]) -> std::io::Result<usize> {\\n        for &b in buf {\\n            self.byte(b);\\n1180→        }\\n        Ok(buf.len())\\n    }\\n\",\"absolute_path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224015__x42677a/work/Hands of Harbor: Second Opinion-Trauma Center: Second Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-224015/engine/crates/pav_core/src/sim.rs\",\"offset\":1104,\"limit\":80,\"raw_output\":\"    /// Hash of the gameplay state, for repeatability checks: the tick, the random numbers, every\\n    /// entity, rigid and soft bodies (pose and velocity), the level's blocks and baked props,\\n    /// projectiles, courses, signals, crumbling tiles and the game (hero, items, gold, monsters,\\n    /// or a `games` game's own state).\\n    /// Two runs that hash the same played out the same.\\n    pub fn state_hash(&self) -> u64 {\\n        let s = &self.state;\\n        let mut h = Fnv::default();\\n        h.u64(s.tick);\\n        h.data(&s.rng);\\n        h.data(&s.entities);\\n        for (_, b) in s.physics.bodies.iter() {\\n            h.floats(&b.translation().to_array());\\n            h.floats(&b.rotation().to_array());\\n            h.floats(&b.linvel().to_array());\\n            h.floats(&b.angvel().to_array());\\n        }\\n        for (_, sb) in s.physics.soft_bodies.iter() {\\n            for (p, v) in sb.particle_positions().zip(sb.particle_velocities()) {\\n                h.floats(&p.to_array());\\n                h.floats(&v.to_array());\\n            }\\n        }\\n        h.u64(s.statics.block_count() as u64);\\n        h.u64(s.statics.prop_count() as u64);\\n        h.data(&s.projectiles);\\n        h.data(&s.courses);\\n        h.data(&s.signals);\\n        h.data(&s.crumbles);\\n        h.data(&s.game);\\n        h.data(&s.play);\\n        h.0\\n    }\\n}\\n\\n/// 64-bit FNV-1a over everything written to it.\\nstruct Fnv(u64);\\n\\nimpl Default for Fnv {\\n    fn default() -> Self {\\n        Self(0xcbf2_9ce4_8422_2325)\\n    }\\n}\\n\\nimpl Fnv {\\n    fn u64(&mut self, x: u64) {\\n        for b in x.to_le_bytes() {\\n            self.byte(b);\\n        }\\n    }\\n\\n    fn floats(&mut self, fs: &[f32]) {\\n        for f in fs {\\n            for b in f.to_bits().to_le_bytes() {\\n                self.byte(b);\\n            }\\n        }\\n    }\\n\\n    /// Mixes in a value's serialized form (the same CBOR that snapshot files use; the state\\n    /// keeps its maps ordered, so the bytes are the same every run).\\n    fn data<T: Serialize + ?Sized>(&mut self, value: &T) {\\n        // Writing into the hash can't fail, and every state type serializes.\\n        let _ = ciborium::into_writer(value, &mut *self);\\n    }\\n\\n    fn byte(&mut self, b: u8) {\\n        self.0 ^= b as u64;\\n        self.0 = self.0.wrapping_mul(0x0100_0000_01b3);\\n    }\\n}\\n\\nimpl std::io::Write for Fnv {\\n    fn write(&mut self, buf: &[u8]) -> std::io::Result<usize> {\\n        for &b in buf {\\n            self.byte(b);\\n        }\\n        Ok(buf.len())\\n    }\\n\\n\",\"total_lines\":1187}}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa38-de6f-7dc0-ae0d-e0f717ed75f2","uuid":"12758302-912e-467d-a063-49d06bc21962"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_55","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Play is hashed via CBOR. Surgery must serialize deterministically.\n\nHashMaps are avoided. f32 NaN and -0 issues are prevented. Vec capacity changes are skipped. Files will be written with mod.rs under 1500 lines, split into strain, cases, bot, and story modules. The Hazard struct gains an `idle` field for orchestrator decay. Suture aux2 is updated with ghost_on_beat.\n\nThe orchestrator resets idle to zero on engagement. It accumulates idle time otherwise. After 0.25 seconds idle, non-sac, non-IV hazards lose 1.2 work per second. Laceration, bleeder, and bone hazards clear samples after 0.8 seconds idle.\n\nDecay will only reduce work and suture samples. Bone aux and sac aux are excluded from decay to prevent spring-back or unwanted swelling. Multiple surgeons targeting the same hazard in one tick will be handled by letting slot 0 apply first, with Echo treated separately.\n\nFocus tracking now prioritizes the last engaged hazard when a surgeon releases their laser. The focus target is set to that hazard ID upon engagement.\n\nWrong-tool penalties trigger when use is held, no hazard is engaged, and the wrong-tool cooldown has expired. If the nearest living hazard rejects the current tool and it is not a scanner, the system records a mistake, resets the chain, applies a 0.8-second cooldown, deducts vitals, and cues a wrong instrument.\n\nHolding a scalpel over healthy tissue without a nearby hazard triggers a \"that's healthy tissue\" cue, a small vitals hit, and a chain break. The bot will release the USE button when it is not near its target to avoid this. Its targeting logic now checks cursor distance against reach plus 0.3, and it only holds USE while on target or actively cutting. For incisions, the target point moves along the surgical path.\n\nForceps pulls require holding the use button continuously while moving to the pull point; releasing it resets work. The bot can read the grabbed flag to maintain that hold. Scanner use is held near any hazard regardless of completion state. IV tool use depends on auxiliary state rather than cursor position, so the bot may stand anywhere and healthy-tissue checks are skipped for IV.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-31a11c84-d9da-4cc6-b920-c60fbf43ad13-38","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224015__x42677a/work/Hands of Harbor: Second Opinion-Trauma Center: Second Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-224015/engine/crates/pav_core/src/animation_preview.rs","offset":300,"limit":40}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-31a11c84-d9da-4cc6-b920-c60fbf43ad13-39","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224015__x42677a/work/Hands of Harbor: Second Opinion-Trauma Center: Second Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-224015/engine/crates/pav_core/src/creature_preview.rs","offset":280,"limit":50}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-31a11c84-d9da-4cc6-b920-c60fbf43ad13-40","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224015__x42677a/work/Hands of Harbor: Second Opinion-Trauma Center: Second Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-224015/engine/crates/pav_core/src/prop_preview.rs","offset":270,"limit":60}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2230,"output_tokens":1431,"cache_read_input_tokens":97280,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa38-de6f-7dc0-ae0d-e0f717ed75f2","uuid":"6dae881e-3656-4edd-b9b1-ebf3538ff119"}
