{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_57","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Only one literal in prop_preview constructs RenderFrame via frame_of.\n\nFive literals plus sim.rs account for all frame constructions. Adding a SurgeryFrame field to SimEvent avoids circular imports because SurgeryFrame does not contain RenderFrame. The surgery module is already public.\n\nDrafting a 200-line story with original dialogue. Banned words and Trauma Center character names are being avoided. The cast includes Mara Quill as the player surgeon, Pet Nwosu as the tremor assistant, Bashir Haddad as the attending anesthesiologist, Teddy Lark as the intern, Ottoline Voss as chief of the Night Ward, and Cordelia Vane as the antagonist.\n\nCordelia Vane will be the night pathologist who names the strain R.E.Q.U.I.E.M. The four patients are Anton Deverell, Briony Pell, Casper Lang, Idris Okonkwo, and June Harlow.\n\nThe remaining three patients are Nils Ferreira, Petra Solano, and Soren Vale. Their case titles are Dies Irae, Margin of the Map, and Libera Me. The story will be written as arrays of dialogue blocks. The lint rule forbids empty dialogue strings rather than blank source lines. A SpawnDef struct is being drafted for case phases.\n\nSpawnDef now includes z, hidden, drain, and axis fields. PhaseDef defines spawns, checkpoint, strain, plate, callout, script_code, unlock, and tag. Strain cases will use phase lists as their own phases, with some phases spawning enemies over time; wander may be split into its own phase.\n\nStrain names will be counted once per split phase pair. The director runs phases in order. Lacrimosa wave one spawns six sacs in a single phase. Introit wander places three nodules in one phase. Split phase one and phase two share the same strain index.\n\nCoverage tracking uses a boolean array, so duplicate strain entries are harmless. Small polyps will use the polyp kind for variety. Amen will be a quiet laceration or one final nodule plus a pool. Dies Irae will spawn five embers in a single phase, with heat rings enabled by a new `heat` flag on PhaseDef. Merge places two embers close together, Furnace uses one large ember, burn gel, and heat, and Libera Me splits into four variants: nodules with pools, sacs, heat-enabled embers, or a script-only wait.\n\nScript-only phases complete when all three shocks finish. Libera Me soloist uses a scalpel incision, tendril spawns one tendril, and close applies dressing. Seven phases match the strain limit. Duet unlocks after soloist. Heat rings spawn every fifth beat during heat phases. Introit wanderers use tag 1.\n\nWanderer nodules will drift horizontally using a sine wave offset by their ID. A sac burst kills the enemy, spawns a pool at its position, and deducts six vitals. The code-blue director runs outside the phase list as a separate tick loop: it spawns waves every twenty-two seconds after the initial timer, triggers an optional finale wave once, and ends the scene when vitals remain above zero.\n\nThe opening wave will be immediate so the idle bleeders die fast, forcing the bot to clear them. After that waves will stay quiet. Player count scales difficulty: extra pools spawn for each additional player, and drain increases by a multiplier of 0.6 plus 0.4 times the player count.\n\nPlayer count will be the maximum of the current value and the number of active surgeons. The code-blue timer will scale to 240 multiplied by difficulty and tune. Callouts will trigger when vitals drop below forty. Story text and names will move to a separate `content.rs` module. The bot will take a `&Surgery` reference in its tick function.\n\nThe bot will use a `decide` function that takes the `Surgery` state, current tick, and slot index to produce `SurgeonInput`. The `Game::bot` method returns a default input frame for story, chart, and results modes, and otherwise delegates to `decide` for the active player during operation or attract. Partner decisions for slot one are handled separately.\n\nAttract mode will use cheat flags for immortal and one-hit, loading a short case. The title screen returns default input so the shell handles menus. Story input is driven by surgeon zero pressing CONFIRM, with a Skip command available; surgery commands take priority. In operation mode, mouse input triggers SNAP aim.\n\nTool selection will be synced from input every tick. The default tool is scalpel, so the bot must explicitly send TOOL_KEEP to preserve the current tool instead of resetting it.\n\nInactive surgeons default to inactive and ignore tool changes. The bot explicitly sets the tool each tick to avoid resetting to scalpel. A suture fix now only updates the previous-side auxiliary value when the sign actually flips and the needle is near the target.\n\nThe heart ghost pulse now uses a `ghost_on_beat` helper that checks whether the current beat falls within a configurable window of the ghost's fractional period. This keeps the ghost advancing during flat periods and removes the need to fix `since_r` for defibrillator timing.\n\nThe `since_r` timer resets to the phase remainder on each wave tick, so it does not accumulate across beats. This prevents double-counting during normal action timing.\n\nA `Coverage` struct is being added to track unlock progress for tools, hazards, strains, gifts, code, and ratings. Gift indices map to hush at 0, echo at 1, and duet at 2. Constants for gift flags are also being defined in `kinds.rs`.\n\nMode constants are being defined in mod.rs. The orchestrator will decay idle bleeders only when no surgeon is engaged this tick, using a comparison rather than a new field.\n\nAn `idle` timer field is being added to the suture sample struct with serde defaults, and `blank()` is being updated to initialize it. The new `Hazard` field requires no default because only `blank()` instantiates that struct. All files are now ready to be written.\n\nStory text will contain roughly sixteen blocks. The status clock will display elapsed time as minutes and seconds. Plate transitions will crossfade over 0.8 seconds. The bot will avoid holding the use button when the heat sweep angle is near the cursor.\n\nReleasing the use button while near a hazard always resets the laser charge to zero, even when the charge level is outside the success window.\n\nHeat sweep timing is now defined: it starts on the fifth beat of a heat phase and completes a full circle in about 1.8 seconds. The bot will check `heat_on` and `heat_angle` to avoid holding the use button during the danger window. When the sweep finishes, it marks the hazard as covered.\n\nA K_HEAT hazard entity will spawn at the start of each heat sweep and die when the sweep ends, incrementing coverage only on death. Heat hazards will not block phase completion; only alive non-heat hazards count as blocking. Scripted code phases will begin automatically on entry if no shocks have been done yet and the code timer is negative.\n\nA `phase_ready` flag will prevent the orchestrator from respawning hazards on every tick. When advancing, the phase index increments and the flag resets. On the next tick, if the flag is false, the orchestrator spawns the new phase, marks it ready, and then handles checkpoint saves, strain coverage, gift unlocks, script setup, and plate crossfades.\n\nCase definitions will be static structs holding id, name, patient, plate, timer, par, vitals, phases, and a code-blue flag. Loading a case resets the phase index and ready flag and enters operation mode. PAR is fixed at 1500 for now; an ENCORE rank requires a score of 8000 or higher.\n\nThe laceration case should score roughly 2800 points, which clears the ENCORE threshold. Pool ratings are fixed at Good and always increment the GOOD coverage counter. Immaculate scalpel and gel ratings require unit tests. The end bonus can dominate the final score when vitals remain high and the timer is low.\n\nSkill 0.4 will never finish the laser phase. The success window is 0.80 to 1.06, but the bot releases at 1.068. That value sits just outside the window, so the charge resets to zero and the bot loops until death.\n\nSkill 0 holds the use button past 1.08 and overheats, which burns laser hazards and clears them. This may also clear polyps but costs vitals and breaks the chain. Skill 0 is slow and misses position, so it likely cannot stay near to refill charge.\n\nSkill 0.2 retargets the active tool every tick, so the laser charge never accumulates for a full second and the bot cannot complete the phase. The nearness check also makes it difficult to stay in range, and idle mode leaves no tools active, causing drain or code expiration to kill the case.\n\nChief 0 codes immediately on flatline without a code window, so the idle chief dies right away. Resident codes_left starts at 2; the first flatline consumes one and opens the window, but failing it kills the resident. The second code is wasted because death ends the case, yet it is meant for later flatlines after successful resuscitations.\n\nScripted code phases do not consume any actions; the bot succeeds automatically. The immortal dev cheat will prevent the die() call from ending the case. The one-hit cheat will instantly finish a hazard with an immaculate rating when the engaged tool matches and the scanner is not involved, allowing attract mode to clear the entire case in one shot.\n\nA freeze timer dev flag and a jump phase command are being added. The `start_case` method will rebuild state during play while preserving the music tune. A mutable RNG reference will be passed into the pre tick to handle jitter.\n\nSpawn positions will be clamped to [-8, 8] by [-3.6, 3.6]. The build function sets history_seconds to zero and registers the KEY \"surgery\".\n\nThe build function sets the camera focus and clears the player. It creates a fresh Surgery game and parses the remaining string to choose the starting mode: title, campaign, code blue, attract, card, mirror, or a specific case.\n\n`begin_case` enters operation mode directly for non-campaign cases, or story mode first for campaigns. Skill defaults to 1.0 and difficulty defaults to 0 with two resident codes. A public `coverage()` accessor is added for tests. The skill field must be public so tests can mutate it via `get_mut`. A random player test will be written later.\n\nA chain window test will be added to the simulation test file. Story text will be written in a compact format to save tokens. Callout strings will be placed in content.rs, and the about screen will be handled later. The Result type will use anyhow::Result to match the starter project. Vec3 is imported from glam. Build does not spawn a player because Sim::new starts with no player and step's character loop is empty; physics still runs.\n\nThe engine is trusted to handle empty game states safely. Audio cues will be pushed only on engagement start and rating, or once every twelve ticks, to prevent cue spam from overwhelming the audio system.\n\nA `cue_cd` cooldown will limit audio cues to specific events: completion, misuse, code start, gift, phase banner, and the first engage tick. The heartbeat cue `CUE_LUB` will fire on every R-wave at roughly eighty per minute. Tests only need to verify that cue IDs are reachable.\n\nThe bot's `decide` signature will use `kinds`. Partner AI will activate during operation when the partner flag is set and no second surgeon is active. The audio test will render every cue ID from the cue table to satisfy the non-silent requirement, while gameplay may only fire a subset.\n\nPartner AI is restricted to case 7. Its `decide` function will accept an optional `avoid` parameter so it can skip the lead surgeon's active hazard and target a different one. Echo cursors will store their own x, z, and lifetime values. The bot will also record the last tool used, its kind, rating, and validity on completion for echo tick replay.\n\nEcho replay will use `last_id` and `echoed_id` to track which hazard was just completed. When echo is active, the next completion is stored and applied to a different hazard with the same tool once every 1.5 seconds while `echo_left` remains above zero.\n\nEcho replay will skip the active hazard and only match a different alive hazard with the same tool. The gift effect lasts ten seconds and can clear three or four hazards, which is helpful but not trivial against larger waves. Heat tools are excluded from echo. Story content will run about 224 lines.\n\nCase data will live in Rust rather than TOML, with a note added to the deviations section. A short content/README.md is deferred as a non-blocker. Files will be written in parallel batches, and the hazard suture fix plus an idle field will be applied together.\n\nThe heart ghost effect will fire on the beat. Scoring logic is being verified for edge cases: finish() and pool hits correctly set done while leaving hazards alive, overheat hits score sloppy and count as cleared, and IV success needs a special case because it does not mark the hazard dead.\n\nIV success now only kills the hazard when the rating is not sloppy. A sloppy IV leaves the patient alive so the bot can retry it. The heal logic is being added to apply vitals only when the IV cooldown has expired.\n\nHeal logic now applies vitals and sets an eight-second IV cooldown. Rating popups will use a small ring buffer with slot, rating, and lifetime. Phase banners will display for two seconds. The pre tick will use the full delta time directly.\n\nChain scoring now increments the chain counter when the gap since the last hit is within the window and the current chain is above zero, otherwise resets to one. The score is multiplied by a chain multiplier and the tune's score multiplier. The rating meter gains eight points for an immaculate hit, four for a clean hit, and two points on the heart beat during the gift effect. The meter caps at one hundred.\n\nWrong-tool hits reset the chain counter to zero. Mistakes are tallied for wrong tools, overheat, healthy tissue, and missed code. Vitals drain is calculated from alive non-heat hazards; hidden ones bleed at half rate. The heart loses vitals unless it is flat or the immortal dev flag is active.\n\nDifficulty settings now define drain multipliers, timer scales, and resident code counts. Codes are assigned at case start based on difficulty. The live timer slider will accelerate the countdown by dividing the elapsed frame time by the tune's timer value.\n\nThe timer will only scale the countdown rate by the inverse of `tune.timer`, while the initial value is multiplied by the difficulty factor alone. This prevents double scaling when the slider is adjusted.\n\nThe timer will pause during story sequences and only count down during operation.\n\nIf a case timer expires, the patient dies immediately rather than entering code blue.\n\nThe case timer pauses during code blue so a patient can recover and still win. If the timer expires while code is active, the operation finishes and the timer resumes with leftover time. This extends the match duration.\n\nThe code blue timer will not pause during a code. Case timers will pause instead to preserve the four-minute match length. If the code blue timer expires while a code is active, the code resolves first and then the timer check runs. The same logic applies to the hub later.\n\nSpawnDef is defined as a Copy struct with f32 fields for position and drain, using negative drain to indicate the default value. The first case, \"The First Movement,\" is set up with plate 0 forearm, vitals 74, a 160-second timer, and a 1500-point par.\n\nCase 0 spawns a laceration and a pool on the forearm plate. Case 1 places a hidden foreign object and a bleeder on the abdomen plate. Case 2 uses the lung and rib plate with a bone, tether, IV, dressing, and one shock code. Case 3 is an introit on the liver plate with three wandering nodules.\n\nCase 3 now has four phase variants: split spawns two nodules and unlocks hush, split2 spawns two more nodules, smalls spawns three small polyps, and amen spawns a laceration and a pool. Nodules will move on tag to match the \"nodule steps every 3 beats\" rule.\n\nCase 4, Lacrimosa, uses plate 7 pericardium. It spawns six sacs in the first wave, six more in the second wave which unlocks echo, six more in the third wave, and ends with an eye hazard plus an inflamation.\n\nCase 5, Dies, uses the lung plate with vitals 72 and a 240-second timer. It spawns five embers in the first wave, three in the second, and two embers plus a burn in the third.\n\nCase 6, Tumor, uses the femur plate. It spawns a tumor and a burn on the first phase, and adds an inflammation on the second.\n\nCase 6 now adds two lacerations and a pool to the first phase, plus a burn and bleeder on the second, so it is not too short. Case 7, Libera, uses the heart plate with vitals 64 and a 260-second timer; its phases are nodules and pools, sacs, embers, script, incision, tendril, and dressing. Tendril diastole will be handled by the bot. Dressing is kept as a separate tool kind from gel. A scanner will reveal the hidden foreign object in case 1.\n\nTool coverage will increment for scanner reveals and successful defibrillations. All thirteen strain phases are now assigned to specific cases.\n\nCase 3 now has five phases: wander, split, an extra split using strain 255, smalls, and amen. The extra split will not skip the smalls phase. Case 7 adds four more phases: stop, soloist, tendril, and close. Callout indices will be added when unlocks occur. A helper method for skill sets is being added to Surgery. The next step is writing the code and adding a compilable test file.\n\nA `game(sim)` helper will be added to the test file so tests can access the Surgery state directly. The story text will be written in content.rs as compact 12-line blocks, totaling roughly 192 lines. Spawn positions for the incision and tether hazards were verified against their required lengths.\n\nSacs will be placed in a ring around the origin to avoid overlap. Their six spawn coordinates are hardcoded rather than computed with cosine, since Rust may not support const float math. Embers will be positioned at (-1.6, 0.6), (-0.6, 1.2), (0.6, 0.4), (1.6, 1.0), and (0.0, -1.2).\n\nNodule spawn positions are hardcoded at (-1.4, 0.5), (0.2, 1.1), and (1.5, -0.4). Case 0 drain is set to 2.6 per second so the patient dies in roughly 33 seconds while idle. Even a slow bot will survive for about 28 seconds and still trigger two codes. Drain stops once all hazards are cleared.\n\nThe bot will prioritize the highest-drain hazards first. A laceration and pool in case 0 take about fifteen seconds to clear, dropping roughly ten vitals during the initial drain window. Case 1 bleeder clears in two seconds. Two code-blue bleeders would drain vitals in fourteen seconds, but the bot can suture both in four seconds. Suture speed needs testing and fixing because the gesture requires four samples while needle positions shift.\n\nThe bot oscillates every five ticks globally rather than syncing to the needle. It aims at the needle position plus a side offset, and the crossing must occur exactly there. A slew toward a new needle might briefly cross away from it before returning, which could cause the suture to miss. The current tolerance window is one unit wide, so it may be widened if tests show unreliability.\n\nThe suture side magnitude of 0.5 is confirmed to satisfy the crossing window. Laceration suture will require four crossings. A fallback wiggle for stalled samples was considered but rejected; the oscillation should suffice. The `idle` field will be added, and the orchestrator file will be written carefully.\n\nA `trigger_gift` method will activate the next available gift in the pre-phase. It checks the Libera case first for a duet unlock, then echo, then hush, and finally reuses hush if it is already active.\n\nGift coverage increments only on first use. Reusing hush later will not double-count. The bot triggers gifts when the meter is full, the mode is OP, and the heart is flat. It holds the gift button during the beat window and releases it once the surgeon gesture finishes.\n\nGifts will not trigger during a code. The bot must hold the gift button until an R-wave occurs while holding it. A `gift_saw_r` flag tracks this. Release triggers the gift only if the release tick is on beat and the R-wave was seen.\n\nThe gift trigger logic is simplified. It no longer requires a prior R-wave flag; instead, the bot simply holds the gift button for at least 0.15 seconds while on beat and releases at the beat window. This is more reliable than tracking the R-wave separately.\n\nThe gift hold-and-release logic is confirmed. Music gain will be added to the status display. The code will be written in four files: content.rs, mod.rs, bot.rs, and frame.rs. A test file will be added after compilation succeeds. frame.rs will be patched with search_replace while writing new files. take_frame in mod.rs will read the play downcast.\n\n`take_frame` will return `None` when the simulation is not running a surgery, so other games can safely pass `None`. The frame snapshot will include a camera for the view. Field bounds constants will be added to kinds or frame. Suture logic will be updated next.\n\nThe story file will use short, earnest lines. A `Line` struct with `who` and `text` fields will store dialogue. A `lines_for(case, after)` function will return the cast for each case. An `all_lines()` helper will concatenate every line for lint checks. Operation callouts will be added as strings in the same file.\n\nOperation callouts are now fully defined as static strings indexed from zero. Rank names will be limited to C, B, A, S, and ENCORE.\n\nThe code will be split into five files: frame.rs, content.rs, bot.rs, ops.rs, and mod.rs. The tick logic, gifts, codes, and phases will live in ops.rs. Fields in mod.rs will be made public so the child module can access them directly.\n\nThe laser release timing is fixed at 0.90 plus 0.28 times the inverse skill, giving a window of 0.80 to 1.06 at skill 1. Pressure will be set to 1.0 and multiplied by tool power. Bone rotation will use ROT_L once the aux value reaches 12.0; otherwise the bot will use the bone directly.\n\nIf both rotation buttons are held, left rotation takes priority. The bone hazard accepts forceps even when the tool is not yet fully engaged, so holding use while the bone is still rotating will not trigger a wrong-tool penalty.\n\nThe defibrillator charge will live in a `defib` field on the Surgeon struct. The test code only checks slot 0, but any active surgeon can trigger a successful charge if they hold the defibrillator button while the heart is flat, then release it during the ghost beat window.\n\nThe bot will hold the defibrillator button and select it as the active tool during a code, but it will skip all hazard interactions while the heart is flat to avoid corrupting state. Successful defibrillation will trigger a thump cue, the code start will trigger a flat cue, and the alarm will trigger an alarm cue.\n\nCheckpoint serialization will skip empty fields. The save copies the full hazards vector and stores next_id to prevent ID collisions on retry. Heart state is rebuilt from vitals, phase, since_r, beats, and bpm. On retry, phase_ready is restored so the bot does not re-enter strain or respawn on top of existing hazards.\n\nThe checkpoint struct will store phase_ready, the full hazards vector, next_id, vitals, heart phase, since_r, beats, timer, elapsed time, scores, chains, best, mistakes, meters, since_chain, codes_left, strain_phase, gifts_unlocked, gifts_used, fever, shocks_done, shocks_need, plate, and heat_on. Surgeon positions will be restored to their saved x, z, and tool rather than defaulting to 0,0.\n\nThe checkpoint struct will not contain a Surgery field to prevent infinite nesting. On restore, the previous `was_use` state will be zeroed so a false release is not triggered. Save and restore methods will be implemented next. A dev kill command will set vitals to zero, clear remaining codes, mark the heart as flat, and call die(). The SpawnHazard command will only accept a hazard kind, since test commands cannot specify exact coordinates.\n\nA `spawn_at` method will place hazards at exact coordinates. Polyps spawned for rating tests will be removed after operation. The suture bugfix is the first priority before composing the Rust files. Campaign stories should finish well within the 108,000 tick limit; code blue needs roughly 16,000 ticks.\n\nA stuck-gesture detector will fail tests after ninety seconds. A bot escape will nudge the aim in a spiral if the same hazard is being worked for more than three seconds. The surgeon struct will track focus time and target ID to enable this.\n\nThe focus timer resets whenever a hazard's work changes, and the spiral escape activates after 2.5 seconds of idle focus. The bot will now be written.\n\nA `lines!` macro will compactly define story dialogue blocks. The campaign will contain roughly 192 lines across sixteen blocks plus operation callouts. Files will be written in sequence: content, frame, bot, then mod. Heart, hazard, and RenderFrame will also be patched.","signature":""},{"type":"text","text":"The gesture code is in place. Next I’ll wire the operation loop, the cases, and the bot so a full case can run."},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-9562e1a9-ee1e-44b3-8cc9-994db0d8ca7e-42","name":"search_replace","input":{"file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224015__x42677a/work/Hands of Harbor: Second Opinion-Trauma Center: Second Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-224015/engine/crates/pav_core/src/games/surgery/hazard.rs","old_string":"    pub bits: u8,\n    pub priority: i16,\n    pub tag: u8,\n}","new_string":"    pub bits: u8,\n    pub priority: i16,\n    pub tag: u8,\n    /// Seconds since a tool last engaged this hazard. Work fades when this grows.\n    #[serde(default)]\n    pub idle: f32,\n}"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-9562e1a9-ee1e-44b3-8cc9-994db0d8ca7e-43","name":"search_replace","input":{"file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224015__x42677a/work/Hands of Harbor: Second Opinion-Trauma Center: Second Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-224015/engine/crates/pav_core/src/games/surgery/hazard.rs","old_string":"            bits: 0,\n            priority: 0,\n            tag: 0,\n        }\n    }","new_string":"            bits: 0,\n            priority: 0,\n            tag: 0,\n            idle: 0.0,\n        }\n    }"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-9562e1a9-ee1e-44b3-8cc9-994db0d8ca7e-44","name":"search_replace","input":{"file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224015__x42677a/work/Hands of Harbor: Second Opinion-Trauma Center: Second Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-224015/engine/crates/pav_core/src/games/surgery/hazard.rs","old_string":"    let prev = h.aux2;\n    if prev.abs() > 0.06 && side.abs() > 0.06 && prev.signum() != side.signum() && (along - needle).abs() < 0.5 && side.abs() < 0.85\n    {\n        h.samples = h.samples.saturating_add(1);\n        h.quality += (h.aux - 0.32).abs();\n        h.aux = 0.0;\n        hit.engaged = true;\n        hit.cue = CUE_ZIP;\n        if h.samples >= h.samples_need {\n            let err = h.quality / h.samples.max(1) as f32;\n            finish(h, hit, err, strict);\n        }\n    } else if side.abs() < 0.9 && (along - needle).abs() < 0.7 {\n        hit.engaged = true;\n    }\n    h.aux += dt;\n    h.aux2 = side;\n}","new_string":"    if side.abs() > 0.06 {\n        let prev = h.aux2;\n        if prev.abs() > 0.06 && prev.signum() != side.signum() && (along - needle).abs() < 0.55 && side.abs() < 0.9 {\n            h.samples = h.samples.saturating_add(1);\n            h.quality += (h.aux - 0.28).abs() * 0.35;\n            h.aux = 0.0;\n            hit.engaged = true;\n            hit.cue = CUE_ZIP;\n            if h.samples >= h.samples_need {\n                let err = h.quality / h.samples.max(1) as f32;\n                finish(h, hit, err, strict);\n            }\n        } else if side.abs() < 0.95 && (along - needle).abs() < 0.75 {\n            hit.engaged = true;\n        }\n        h.aux2 = side;\n    } else if (along - needle).abs() < 0.75 {\n        hit.engaged = true;\n    }\n    h.aux += dt;\n}"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-9562e1a9-ee1e-44b3-8cc9-994db0d8ca7e-45","name":"search_replace","input":{"file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224015__x42677a/work/Hands of Harbor: Second Opinion-Trauma Center: Second Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-224015/engine/crates/pav_core/src/games/surgery/heart.rs","old_string":"    /// Diastole: the quiet half, when a tendril can be pulled.\n    pub fn diastole(&self) -> bool {\n        self.phase > 0.28 && self.phase < 0.72\n    }\n}","new_string":"    /// Diastole: the quiet half, when a tendril can be pulled.\n    pub fn diastole(&self) -> bool {\n        self.phase > 0.28 && self.phase < 0.72\n    }\n\n    /// The ghost QRS during a flatline. `ghost` is the phase in 0..1.\n    pub fn ghost_on_beat(&self, window_ms: f32) -> bool {\n        let w = (window_ms / 1000.0).clamp(0.02, 0.4);\n        let g = self.ghost.rem_euclid(1.0);\n        let since = g * self.period;\n        let until = (1.0 - g) * self.period;\n        since <= w || until <= w\n    }\n}"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":443,"output_tokens":16000,"cache_read_input_tokens":102144,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa38-de6f-7dc0-ae0d-e0f717ed75f2","uuid":"37cc16bf-40e3-406c-98e7-b384cb643d9a"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-9562e1a9-ee1e-44b3-8cc9-994db0d8ca7e-42","content":"{\"type\":\"SearchReplace\",\"EditsApplied\":{\"old_string\":\"    pub bits: u8,\\n    pub priority: i16,\\n    pub tag: u8,\\n}\",\"new_string\":\"    pub bits: u8,\\n    pub priority: i16,\\n    pub tag: u8,\\n    /// Seconds since a tool last engaged this hazard. Work fades when this grows.\\n    #[serde(default)]\\n    pub idle: f32,\\n}\",\"tool_output_for_prompt\":\"The file /home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224015__x42677a/work/Hands of Harbor: Second Opinion-Trauma Center: Second Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-224015/engine/crates/pav_core/src/games/surgery/hazard.rs has been updated successfully.\",\"tool_output_for_prompt_concise\":\"The file /home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224015__x42677a/work/Hands of Harbor: Second Opinion-Trauma Center: Second Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-224015/engine/crates/pav_core/src/games/surgery/hazard.rs has been updated.\",\"absolute_path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224015__x42677a/work/Hands of Harbor: Second Opinion-Trauma Center: Second Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-224015/engine/crates/pav_core/src/games/surgery/hazard.rs\",\"edits\":{\"details\":[{\"old_string\":\"    pub bits: u8,\\n    pub priority: i16,\\n    pub tag: u8,\\n}\",\"old_line\":34,\"new_string\":\"    pub bits: u8,\\n    pub priority: i16,\\n    pub tag: u8,\\n    /// Seconds since a tool last engaged this hazard. Work fades when this grows.\\n    #[serde(default)]\\n    pub idle: f32,\\n}\",\"new_line\":34,\"context_before\":\"    pub grabbed: bool,\\n    pub grab_x: f32,\\n    pub grab_z: f32,\\n\",\"context_after\":\"\\n#[derive(Clone, Copy, Debug, Default)]\\npub struct Hit {\\n\",\"line_prefix\":\"\"}]}}}","is_error":false},{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-9562e1a9-ee1e-44b3-8cc9-994db0d8ca7e-43","conte