32,32,32,32,32,32,32,32,103,46,112,104,97,115,101,95,114,101,97,100,121,32,61,32,102,97,108,115,101,59,10,49,57,51,58,102,110,32,101,110,116,101,114,95,112,104,97,115,101,40,103,58,32,38,109,117,116,32,83,117,114,103,101,114,121,44,32,115,105,109,58,32,38,109,117,116,32,83,105,109,44,32,101,118,101,110,116,115,58,32,38,109,117,116,32,86,101,99,60,83,105,109,69,118,101,110,116,62,41,32,123,10,50,53,52,58,32,32,32,32,103,46,112,104,97,115,101,95,114,101,97,100,121,32,61,32,116,114,117,101,59,10,60,47,119,111,114,107,115,112,97,99,101,95,114,101,115,117,108,116,62],\"stderr\":[],\"exit_code\":0,\"match_count\":17,\"file_matches\":[{\"path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224015__x42677a/work/Hands of Harbor: Second Opinion-Trauma Center: Second Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-224015/engine/crates/pav_core/src/games/surgery/mod.rs\",\"matches\":[{\"line_number\":120,\"content\":\"    phase_ready: bool,\"},{\"line_number\":164,\"content\":\"    pub phase_ready: bool,\"},{\"line_number\":235,\"content\":\"            phase_ready: false,\"},{\"line_number\":313,\"content\":\"    fn prepare_case(&mut self, id: u8) {\"},{\"line_number\":325,\"content\":\"        self.phase_ready = false;\"},{\"line_number\":392,\"content\":\"        self.phase_ready = true;\"},{\"line_number\":447,\"content\":\"            phase_ready: self.phase_ready,\"},{\"line_number\":492,\"content\":\"        self.phase_ready = cp.phase_ready;\"},{\"line_number\":697,\"content\":\"                    self.phase_ready = false;\"},{\"line_number\":720,\"content\":\"                self.phase_ready = false;\"},{\"line_number\":919,\"content\":\"    fn pre(&mut self, sim: &mut Sim, input: &InputFrame, dt: f32, events: &mut Vec<SimEvent>) -> std::collections::BTreeMap<crate::entity::EntityId, InputFrame> {\"}]},{\"path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224015__x42677a/work/Hands of Harbor: Second Opinion-Trauma Center: Second Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-224015/engine/crates/pav_core/src/games/surgery/ops.rs\",\"matches\":[{\"line_number\":36,\"content\":\"                g.phase_ready = false;\"},{\"line_number\":101,\"content\":\"    if !g.phase_ready && !g.code_blue {\"},{\"line_number\":102,\"content\":\"        enter_phase(g, sim, events);\"},{\"line_number\":171,\"content\":\"        g.phase_ready = false;\"},{\"line_number\":193,\"content\":\"fn enter_phase(g: &mut Surgery, sim: &mut Sim, events: &mut Vec<SimEvent>) {\"},{\"line_number\":254,\"content\":\"    g.phase_ready = true;\"}]}]}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa38-de6f-7dc0-ae0d-e0f717ed75f2","uuid":"14fd4283-999f-49ec-86bf-b7fe1303ec81"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_87","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The bug is confirmed. The match pattern is being examined.\n\nThe guard applies to the entire or-pattern, so laceration at stage 0 is excluded. The suture crossing logic is also being checked: the bot flips sides every 8 ticks, and the aim point places the cursor at half the axis width across.\n\nThe math confirms the aim point sits exactly 0.5 units across the axis. The along distance equals the needle length, so the suture stays centered and does not drift.\n\nThe crossing logic is sound. The cursor moves 0.25 units per tick, so it takes four ticks to cross the full 1.0 unit span. The aux2 guard correctly ignores small-side movements, and a crossing is counted only when the cursor lands on the opposite side with sufficient distance. A focus_t spiral also triggers after 2.2 seconds if work does not grow.\n\nSuture does not increase `work` until the stitch finishes. The focus_t spiral therefore triggers after 2.2 seconds of stitching, which takes longer than that interval for four stitches. The aim point then spirals by 0.42, potentially throwing off the needle window. The bot also flips sides every 8 ticks based on tick count rather than arrival time.\n\nFour stitches should finish well under 2.2 seconds if suture is actually invoked. Suture tracks progress via samples rather than work, so work decay cannot reset the stitch count. A tick-by-tick `aux` increment also runs continuously inside the suture loop even when no crossing occurs.\n\nThe `aux` tick counter feeds into the quality formula as time-on-tool. At 0.133 seconds per stitch, the error is roughly 0.05, so the rate_error threshold must be checked to confirm this qualifies as IMMACULATE.\n\nThe bot's USE hold logic also needs review. The aim point sits 0.5 units from center plus an along offset, while the laceration radius is 0.7.\n\nThe aim point sits roughly 0.84 units from the hazard center, which is below the 0.98 near threshold. USE therefore stays held during travel and at the target. At skill 1 the bot outputs a clamped step position and the simulation arrives directly at that point. The working point equals the surgeon position because precision is active and there is no tremor.\n\nI will fix the match arm. I also checked other or-patterns for similar guard issues. The foreign, tendril, and tumor pattern is safe because those kinds always use FORCEPS. The polyp, nodule, and ember pattern is safe because their stage-zero tools are laser, laser, and cryo.\n\nThe inflam, burn, dressing, and tumor pattern is safe because those kinds use GEL or DRESSING. The eye and nodule patterns are also correct.\n\nThe aim_point pattern is actually correct. The `|| h.kind != K_BONE` guard lets laceration and bleeder match at stage 0, which is why the bot aimed at stitch points. Bone stage 0 should not suture because it uses rotation; only bone stage 1 and above should. I will fix apply() and verify that suture quality and timing will complete.\n\nThe side coordinate changes by 0.25 each tick, so the cursor passes through zero between ticks. The guard skips that instant, but the sign flips on the next tick and the crossing is still counted. I am also checking whether an along component could make the path non-straight.\n\nThe suture path is perfectly perpendicular to the axis. The along coordinate stays fixed at the needle length while the cursor moves across.\n\nThe dt passed to apply is correct when hush is inactive. Work decay cannot interfere with stitch progress because samples are independent of work.\n\nFour stitches should finish well before vitals expire. The drain rate is 2.8 per second, so vitals last roughly 27 seconds.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-bd5af634-a4c0-4238-8f91-74783294fde0-10","name":"grep","input":{"pattern":"fn rate_error|R_IMMACULATE|fn rank|RANK|par:","glob":"**/surgery/**/*.rs"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-bd5af634-a4c0-4238-8f91-74783294fde0-11","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224015__x42677a/work/Hands of Harbor: Second Opinion-Trauma Center: Second Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-224015/engine/crates/pav_core/src/games/surgery/ops.rs","offset":1,"limit":200}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-bd5af634-a4c0-4238-8f91-74783294fde0-12","name":"grep","input":{"pattern":"case 0|The First|fn cases|CASES","glob":"**/surgery/content.rs"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1586,"output_tokens":2490,"cache_read_input_tokens":51456,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa38-de6f-7dc0-ae0d-e0f717ed75f2","uuid":"10d216ff-204e-4a5a-bd86-164f55df0b2d"}
