{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_90","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Fixing the match pattern. Then running the test.\n\nConfirmed Rust match guard semantics: guards apply to the whole pattern, not just the last alternative. Fixing the suture match and running case0.\n\nSplitting the combined laceration and bleeder arm from the bone arm. The bone suture now requires stage >= 1. Checking match arm ordering against the existing stage 0 bone arm.\n\nMatch arm order is safe. The stage >= 1 and stage == 0 bone guards are mutually exclusive.\n\nChecking if suture crossing fails because the bot's side flip is too fast relative to the previous-side requirement. The aim_toward step clamp may also prevent the cursor from reaching the threshold within the window before the target flips back.\n\nConfirmed that `rules` is correctly passed as `dt` to `apply`, and that `suture` only increments `h.aux` when `use_held` is true.\n\nUSE release mid-cross preserves the previous side, so the cross may still count when USE resumes on the other side.\n\nThe bot hold logic checks distance from the current cursor to the target point, not to the hazard.\n\nThe distance check is not a bug. Once the cursor arrives, USE stays held during the cross because the second clause keeps the hold active even after the target flips away.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-e2086a52-2d79-4bc8-8625-e951b51fbec9-17","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224015__x42677a/work/Hands of Harbor: Second Opinion-Trauma Center: Second Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-224015/engine/crates/pav_core/src/games/surgery/content.rs","offset":1,"limit":170}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1537,"output_tokens":1064,"cache_read_input_tokens":61312,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa38-de6f-7dc0-