\\"close 3rd person\\\", || CameraParams { tilt: 25.0, distance: 7.0, fov: 60.0, height_offset: 1.4, ..Default::default() }),\\n    ];\\n}\\n\\nimpl CameraParams {\\n    /// Blend between two camera setups (yaw takes the short way round; projection switches\\n    /// halfway).\\n    pub fn lerp(&self, o: &CameraParams, t: f32) -> CameraParams {\\n        let l = |a: f32, b: f32| a + (b - a) * t;\\n        let dyaw = ((o.yaw - self.yaw + 540.0).rem_euclid(360.0)) - 180.0;\\n        CameraParams {\\n            tilt: l(self.tilt, o.tilt),\\n            yaw: ((self.yaw + dyaw * t + 540.0).rem_euclid(360.0)) - 180.0,\\n            distance: l(self.distance, o.distance),\\n            fov: l(self.fov, o.fov),\\n            ortho: if t < 0.5 { self.ortho } else { o.ortho },\\n            follow_lag: l(self.follow_lag, o.follow_lag),\\n            height_offset: l(self.height_offset, o.height_offset),\\n        }\\n    }\\n}\\n\\n#[derive(Clone, Debug)]\\npub struct CameraRig {\\n    /// Target parameters (what the panel edits).\\n    pub params: CameraParams,\\n    /// Smoothed focus point.\\n    pub target: Vec3,\\n\",\"total_lines\":216}}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa38-de6f-7dc0-ae0d-e0f717ed75f2","uuid":"203ba952-2c09-4cdd-b3de-014146049602"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_138","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"I need to implement a lot of code.\n\nI'm reviewing the app's startup flow, scene names, WASM entry point, and existing modules to plan the surgery implementation. I'll check PLAN appendix B for the hub shim, input.rs for PadState, and headless.rs structure. The architecture needs careful planning so everything compiles.\n\nI've defined `emit` and `apply_look` in the surgery module. The view builder will call them at the end of scene construction. `apply_look` overwrites sun, ambient, lights, clear, style, post, filter, and camera. A 420x240 plate mesh is acceptable.\n\nThe plate mesh will be built once as a DynamicMesh using deterministic hash noise. Vertex colors will be linear sRGB. Instruments will render as SDF capsules with tool-specific cursor shapes. Hazards will be small meshes or SDFs. The paper theatre will use simple extruded silhouettes for characters and a small portrait card during operations.\n\nI'll read PLAN appendix A briefly. The cleanest branch is at the top of `frame()`: if the scene name starts with \"surgery\" or the host has a surgery state, call `crate::product::surgery_frame(self)` and return early. Because that function needs private fields, I'll either make `product` a nested module inside `app.rs` or expose it as a method.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-d61fc084-a05f-4428-a5ad-874e04657f31-19","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224015__x42677a/work/engine-link/crates/pav_app/src/app.rs","offset":2100,"limit":250}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-d61fc084-a05f-4428-a5ad-874e04657f31-20","name":"grep","input":{"pattern":"mod app|pub mod","path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224015__x42677a/work/engine-link/crates/pav_app/src/lib.rs"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-d61fc084-a05f-4428-a5