{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-f89cdde2-af73-44a4-8c3b-cbe5cad0f9af-118","content":"{\"type\":\"ReadFile\",\"FileContent\":{\"content\":\"640→fn build<T>(device: &cpal::Device, config: cpal::StreamConfig, rx: Receiver<Cmd>, channels: usize) -> anyhow::Result<cpal::Stream>\\nwhere\\n    T: cpal::SizedSample + cpal::FromSample<f32>,\\n{\\n    use cpal::traits::DeviceTrait;\\n    let mut mixer = Mixer::new(config.sample_rate as f32);\\n    let mut buf: Vec<f32> = Vec::new();\\n    let stream = device.build_output_stream::<T, _, _>(\\n        config,\\n        move |data: &mut [T], _| {\\n650→            while let Ok(c) = rx.try_recv() {\\n                match c {\\n                    Cmd::Play(p, pan, gain, delay) => mixer.play(p, pan, gain, delay),\\n                    Cmd::Master(v) => mixer.master = v,\\n                }\\n            }\\n            let frames = data.len() / channels.max(1);\\n            buf.resize(frames * 2, 0.0);\\n            mixer.render(&mut buf);\\n            for (i, frame) in data.chunks_mut(channels.max(1)).enumerate() {\\n660→                for (c, s) in frame.iter_mut().enumerate() {\\n                    *s = T::from_sample(buf[i * 2 + c.min(1)]);\\n                }\\n            }\\n        },\\n        |e| log::warn!(\\\"audio stream error: {e}\\\"),\\n        None,\\n    )?;\\n    Ok(stream)\\n}\\n670→\\n#[cfg(test)]\\nmod tests {\\n    use super::*;\\n\\n    #[test]\\n    fn explosion_is_loud_then_silent() {\\n        let ev = SimEvent::Explosion { pos: Vec3::ZERO, radius: 1.35 };\\n        let out = render_events(&[(0.0, ev)], 2.0, 22050.0, &Listener::default());\\n        let peak_early = out[..22050].iter().fold(0.0f32, |m, s| m.max(s.abs()));\\n680→        let peak_late = out[out.len() - 2000..].iter().fold(0.0f32, |m, s| m.max(s.abs()));\\n        assert!(peak_early > 0.1, \\\"audible: {peak_early}\\\");\\n        assert!(peak_late < 1e-3, \\\"decays: {peak_late}\\\");\\n    }\\n}\\n\",\"content_concise\":\"640→fn build<T>(device: &cpal::Device, config: cpal::StreamConfig, rx: Receiver<Cmd>, channels: usize) -> anyhow::Result<cpal::Stream>\\nwhere\\n    T: cpal::SizedSample + cpal::FromSample<f32>,\\n{\\n    use cpal::traits::DeviceTrait;\\n    let mut mixer = Mixer::new(config.sample_rate as f32);\\n    let mut buf: Vec<f32> = Vec::new();\\n    let stream = device.build_output_stream::<T, _, _>(\\n        config,\\n        move |data: &mut [T], _| {\\n650→            while let Ok(c) = rx.try_recv() {\\n                match c {\\n                    Cmd::Play(p, pan, gain, delay) => mixer.play(p, pan, gain, delay),\\n                    Cmd::Master(v) => mixer.master = v,\\n                }\\n            }\\n            let frames = data.len() / channels.max(1);\\n            buf.resize(frames * 2, 0.0);\\n            mixer.render(&mut buf);\\n            for (i, frame) in data.chunks_mut(channels.max(1)).enumerate() {\\n660→                for (c, s) in frame.iter_mut().enumerate() {\\n                    *s = T::from_sample(buf[i * 2 + c.min(1)]);\\n                }\\n            }\\n        },\\n        |e| log::warn!(\\\"audio stream error: {e}\\\"),\\n        None,\\n    )?;\\n    Ok(stream)\\n}\\n670→\\n#[cfg(test)]\\nmod tests {\\n    use super::*;\\n\\n    #[test]\\n    fn explosion_is_loud_then_silent() {\\n        let ev = SimEvent::Explosion { pos: Vec3::ZERO, radius: 1.35 };\\n        let out = render_events(&[(0.0, ev)], 2.0, 22050.0, &Listener::default());\\n        let peak_early = out[..22050].iter().fold(0.0f32, |m, s| m.max(s.abs()));\\n680→        let peak_late = out[out.len() - 2000..].iter().fold(0.0f32, |m, s| m.max(s.abs()));\\n        assert!(peak_early > 0.1, \\\"audible: {peak_early}\\\");\\n        assert!(peak_late < 1e-3, \\\"decays: {peak_late}\\\");\\n    }\\n}\\n\",\"absolute_path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224015__x42677a/work/Hands of Harbor: Second Opinion-Trauma Center: Second Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-224015/engine/crates/pav_audio/src/lib.rs\",\"offset\":640,\"limit\":50,\"raw_output\":\"fn build<T>(device: &cpal::Device, config: cpal::StreamConfig, rx: Receiver<Cmd>, channels: usize) -> anyhow::Result<cpal::Stream>\\nwhere\\n    T: cpal::SizedSample + cpal::FromSample<f32>,\\n{\\n    use cpal::traits::DeviceTrait;\\n    let mut mixer = Mixer::new(config.sample_rate as f32);\\n    let mut buf: Vec<f32> = Vec::new();\\n    let stream = device.build_output_stream::<T, _, _>(\\n        config,\\n        move |data: &mut [T], _| {\\n            while let Ok(c) = rx.try_recv() {\\n                match c {\\n                    Cmd::Play(p, pan, gain, delay) => mixer.play(p, pan, gain, delay),\\n                    Cmd::Master(v) => mixer.master = v,\\n                }\\n            }\\n            let frames = data.len() / channels.max(1);\\n            buf.resize(frames * 2, 0.0);\\n            mixer.render(&mut buf);\\n            for (i, frame) in data.chunks_mut(channels.max(1)).enumerate() {\\n                for (c, s) in frame.iter_mut().enumerate() {\\n                    *s = T::from_sample(buf[i * 2 + c.min(1)]);\\n                }\\n            }\\n        },\\n        |e| log::warn!(\\\"audio stream error: {e}\\\"),\\n        None,\\n    )?;\\n    Ok(stream)\\n}\\n\\n#[cfg(test)]\\nmod tests {\\n    use super::*;\\n\\n    #[test]\\n    fn explosion_is_loud_then_silent() {\\n        let ev = SimEvent::Explosion { pos: Vec3::ZERO, radius: 1.35 };\\n        let out = render_events(&[(0.0, ev)], 2.0, 22050.0, &Listener::default());\\n        let peak_early = out[..22050].iter().fold(0.0f32, |m, s| m.max(s.abs()));\\n        let peak_late = out[out.len() - 2000..].iter().fold(0.0f32, |m, s| m.max(s.abs()));\\n        assert!(peak_early > 0.1, \\\"audible: {peak_early}\\\");\\n        assert!(peak_late < 1e-3, \\\"decays: {peak_late}\\\");\\n    }\\n}\\n\",\"total_lines\":684}}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa38-de6f-7dc0-ae0d-e0f717ed75f2","uuid":"927c9bc9-d294-4aed-9522-39ab839f353b"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_181","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Adding a fifth `bus` field to the `Play` struct and giving `Bus` gain controls on the mixer.\n\nFormant synthesis will use a two-pole filter when `formant_q` is nonzero, leaving existing patches unchanged. The music module will expose `render_track` to play notes through the mixer on the music bus. `Voice::render_line` will generate audio from text. Cues will match before wildcards and include position, gain, and pitch fields.\n\nA non-silent test will render every cue, track, and voice line to verify peak amplitude. Music gain defaults to 0.10 on both Tune and Mixer. Shell tests will go in pav_ui. A unit test will check that emit produces finite vertices to catch NaN. Product.rs depends on pav_ui::surgery::Shell. App fields remain private but are accessible as a child module.\n\nA `harbor` field of type `product::Harbor` will be added to `App` and initialized in the constructor. `Harbor` will hold the shell, hub, music clock, installed hook, last status, and network cursors. A `surgery_frame` helper will drive the surgery scene. The app will enter surgery mode when the scene name starts with \"surgery\" or a prior surgery state exists.\n\nThe window title and fail message will use the kinds::TITLE constant when the scene starts with \"surgery\". The boot screen is skipped in that mode. The cursor hides during mode operations. Touch-only input is enabled when the app detects a touch screen without a fine pointer, and it clears once a key or pad event arrives. The shell handles the attract timer, and product sends a load command when attract mode requests a scene change.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-e5848f21-ee6f-4612-a237-23a655450b83-119","name":"grep","input":{"pattern":"fn boot_","path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224015__x42677a/work/engine-link/crates/pav_core/src/games/surgery/mod.rs"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":766,"output_tokens":774,"cache_read_input_tokens":144768,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa38-de6f-7dc0-ae0d-e0f717ed75f2","uuid":"2677def6-eeab-4a46-8856-e5f62dfa47f2"}
