{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-f75f5deb-57c5-4a99-9bba-14dc65ba0d93-122","content":"{\"type\":\"ReadFile\",\"FileContent\":{\"content\":\"680→    let mut best = None;\\n    let mut best_d = f32::MAX;\\n    for (i, h) in hazards.iter().enumerate() {\\n        if !h.alive || h.kind == K_HEAT || h.accepts(tool) {\\n            continue;\\n        }\\n        let d = h.dist(x, z);\\n        if d <= h.radius + 0.12 && d < best_d {\\n            best_d = d;\\n            best = Some(i);\\n690→        }\\n    }\\n    best\\n}\\n\\nfn steer(s: &mut Surgeon, inp: SurgeonInput, dt: f32, speed: f32) {\\n    let abs = inp.held & surg::AIM_ABSOLUTE != 0;\\n    let snap = inp.held & surg::SNAP != 0;\\n    if abs && snap {\\n        s.x = inp.aim.x;\\n700→        s.z = inp.aim.y;\\n        return;\\n    }\\n    if abs {\\n        let dx = inp.aim.x - s.x;\\n        let dz = inp.aim.y - s.z;\\n        let d = (dx * dx + dz * dz).sqrt();\\n        let step = speed.max(1.0) * dt;\\n        if d <= step || d < 1e-5 {\\n            s.x = inp.aim.x;\\n710→            s.z = inp.aim.y;\\n        } else {\\n            s.x += dx / d * step;\\n            s.z += dz / d * step;\\n        }\\n    } else if inp.aim.length_squared() > 0.0004 {\\n        s.x += inp.aim.x * speed * dt;\\n        s.z += inp.aim.y * speed * dt;\\n    }\\n}\\n720→\\nfn heat_hit(angle: f32, x: f32, z: f32) -> bool {\\n    let ang = z.atan2(x);\\n    let mut d = (ang - angle).abs();\\n    if d > std::f32::consts::PI {\\n        d = std::f32::consts::TAU - d;\\n    }\\n    let r = (x * x + z * z).sqrt();\\n    d < 0.22 && r > 0.4\\n}\",\"content_concise\":\"680→    let mut best = None;\\n    let mut best_d = f32::MAX;\\n    for (i, h) in hazards.iter().enumerate() {\\n        if !h.alive || h.kind == K_HEAT || h.accepts(tool) {\\n            continue;\\n        }\\n        let d = h.dist(x, z);\\n        if d <= h.radius + 0.12 && d < best_d {\\n            best_d = d;\\n            best = Some(i);\\n690→        }\\n    }\\n    best\\n}\\n\\nfn steer(s: &mut Surgeon, inp: SurgeonInput, dt: f32, speed: f32) {\\n    let abs = inp.held & surg::AIM_ABSOLUTE != 0;\\n    let snap = inp.held & surg::SNAP != 0;\\n    if abs && snap {\\n        s.x = inp.aim.x;\\n700→        s.z = inp.aim.y;\\n        return;\\n    }\\n    if abs {\\n        let dx = inp.aim.x - s.x;\\n        let dz = inp.aim.y - s.z;\\n        let d = (dx * dx + dz * dz).sqrt();\\n        let step = speed.max(1.0) * dt;\\n        if d <= step || d < 1e-5 {\\n            s.x = inp.aim.x;\\n710→            s.z = inp.aim.y;\\n        } else {\\n            s.x += dx / d * step;\\n            s.z += dz / d * step;\\n        }\\n    } else if inp.aim.length_squared() > 0.0004 {\\n        s.x += inp.aim.x * speed * dt;\\n        s.z += inp.aim.y * speed * dt;\\n    }\\n}\\n720→\\nfn heat_hit(angle: f32, x: f32, z: f32) -> bool {\\n    let ang = z.atan2(x);\\n    let mut d = (ang - angle).abs();\\n    if d > std::f32::consts::PI {\\n        d = std::f32::consts::TAU - d;\\n    }\\n    let r = (x * x + z * z).sqrt();\\n    d < 0.22 && r > 0.4\\n}\",\"absolute_path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224015__x42677a/work/Hands of Harbor: Second Opinion-Trauma Center: Second Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-224015/engine/crates/pav_core/src/games/surgery/ops.rs\",\"offset\":680,\"limit\":50,\"raw_output\":\"    let mut best = None;\\n    let mut best_d = f32::MAX;\\n    for (i, h) in hazards.iter().enumerate() {\\n        if !h.alive || h.kind == K_HEAT || h.accepts(tool) {\\n            continue;\\n        }\\n        let d = h.dist(x, z);\\n        if d <= h.radius + 0.12 && d < best_d {\\n            best_d = d;\\n            best = Some(i);\\n        }\\n    }\\n    best\\n}\\n\\nfn steer(s: &mut Surgeon, inp: SurgeonInput, dt: f32, speed: f32) {\\n    let abs = inp.held & surg::AIM_ABSOLUTE != 0;\\n    let snap = inp.held & surg::SNAP != 0;\\n    if abs && snap {\\n        s.x = inp.aim.x;\\n        s.z = inp.aim.y;\\n        return;\\n    }\\n    if abs {\\n        let dx = inp.aim.x - s.x;\\n        let dz = inp.aim.y - s.z;\\n        let d = (dx * dx + dz * dz).sqrt();\\n        let step = speed.max(1.0) * dt;\\n        if d <= step || d < 1e-5 {\\n            s.x = inp.aim.x;\\n            s.z = inp.aim.y;\\n        } else {\\n            s.x += dx / d * step;\\n            s.z += dz / d * step;\\n        }\\n    } else if inp.aim.length_squared() > 0.0004 {\\n        s.x += inp.aim.x * speed * dt;\\n        s.z += inp.aim.y * speed * dt;\\n    }\\n}\\n\\nfn heat_hit(angle: f32, x: f32, z: f32) -> bool {\\n    let ang = z.atan2(x);\\n    let mut d = (ang - angle).abs();\\n    if d > std::f32::consts::PI {\\n        d = std::f32::consts::TAU - d;\\n    }\\n    let r = (x * x + z * z).sqrt();\\n    d < 0.22 && r > 0.4\\n}\\n\",\"total_lines\":747}}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa38-de6f-7dc0-ae0d-e0f717ed75f2","uuid":"361cc194-cbdb-4b7b-9a89-888db44c4251"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_185","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Mouse input is configured for absolute aiming with snapping to world points.\n\nStick input is relative. The right stick Y axis maps to world Z with inverted polarity so upward stick movement decreases the Z coordinate.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-01f985be-f857-4319-926e-b81edbc86cb0-123","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224015__x42677a/work/engine-link/crates/pav_app/src/simhost.rs","offset":233,"limit":80}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":601,"output_tokens":344,"cache_read_input_tokens":148864,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa38-de6f-7dc0-ae0d-e0f717ed75f2","uuid":"122abaef-0ac8-487b-9669-5599adbd8db6"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-01f985be-f857-4319-926e-b81edbc86cb0-123","content":"{\"type\":\"ReadFile\",\"FileContent\":{\"content\":\"233→/// Fixed-rate ticking with time controls (pause, single steps, speed, rewind, scrubbing).\\nstruct Clock {\\n    next: Instant,\\n    window_start: Instant,\\n    window_ticks: u32,\\n    busy: Duration,\\n    rewound: bool,\\n240→    studio_mode: pav_core::prop_preview::StudioMode,\\n}\\n\\nimpl Clock {\\n    fn new() -> Self {\\n        Self {\\n            next: Instant::now(),\\n            window_start: Instant::now(),\\n            window_ticks: 0,\\n            busy: Duration::ZERO,\\n250→            rewound: false,\\n            studio_mode: pav_core::prop_preview::StudioMode::World,\\n        }\\n    }\\n\\n    /// Runs whatever is due now; returns how long until the next tick.\\n    fn advance(&mut self, sim: &mut Sim, sh: &Shared) -> Duration {\\n        let previewing = sim.studio_active();\\n        let mode = sim.studio_mode();\\n        if self.studio_mode != mode {\\n260→            self.studio_mode = mode;\\n            self.next = Instant::now();\\n        }\\n        let ctl = *sh.control.lock().unwrap();\\n        // The animation stage has its own play, pause and speed controls. The world's time\\n        // controls stay untouched, including a paused or rewound game behind the stage.\\n        let tick_wall = if previewing { sim.dt() } else { sim.dt() / ctl.speed.clamp(0.01, 16.0) };\\n        let (busy, window_ticks) = (&mut self.busy, &mut self.window_ticks);\\n        let mut tick_once = |sim: &mut Sim, at: Instant| {\\n            let input = if previewing {\\n270→                InputFrame::default()\\n            } else {\\n                let mut i = sh.input.lock().unwrap();\\n                let mut frame = *i;\\n                i.pressed = 0;\\n                frame.cmd = sh.cmds.lock().unwrap().pop_front();\\n                frame\\n            };\\n            let stamp = if previewing { None } else { sh.input_stamp.lock().unwrap().take() };\\n            let t = Instant::now();\\n280→            sim.step(&input);\\n            *busy += t.elapsed();\\n            if let Some(s) = stamp {\\n                *sh.latency_probe.lock().unwrap() = Some((s, Instant::now(), sim.state.tick));\\n            }\\n            *window_ticks += 1;\\n            publish(sim, sh, tick_wall, at);\\n        };\\n\\n        let now = Instant::now();\\n290→        if previewing {\\n            let mut n = 0;\\n            while now >= self.next && n < 8 {\\n                self.next += Duration::from_secs_f32(tick_wall);\\n                tick_once(sim, self.next);\\n                n += 1;\\n            }\\n            if n == 8 && now > self.next {\\n                self.next = now;\\n            }\\n300→        } else if ctl.rewinding {\\n            if now >= self.next {\\n                self.next = now + Duration::from_secs_f32(sim.dt());\\n                let oldest = sim.history.oldest_tick().unwrap_or(sim.state.tick);\\n                let target = sim.state.tick.saturating_sub(ctl.rewind_speed.max(1) as u64).max(oldest);\\n                if target < sim.state.tick && sim.rewind_to(target) {\\n                    self.rewound = true;\\n                }\\n                let dt = sim.dt();\\n                publish(sim, sh, dt, now);\\n310→            }\\n        } else if let Some(t) = ctl.scrub {\\n            sh.control.lock().unwrap().scrub = None;\",\"content_concise\":\"233→/// Fixed-rate ticking with time controls (pause, single steps, speed, rewind, scrubbing).\\nstruct Clock {\\n    next: Instant,\\n    window_start: Instant,\\n    window_ticks: u32,\\n    busy: Duration,\\n    rewound: bool,\\n240→    studio_mode: pav_core::prop_preview::StudioMode,\\n}\\n\\nimpl Clock {\\n    fn new() -> Self {\\n        Self {\\n            next: Instant::now(),\\n            window_start: Instant::now(),\\n            window_ticks: 0,\\n            busy: Duration::ZERO,\\n250→            rewound: false,\\n            studio_mode: pav_core::prop_preview::StudioMode::World,\\n        }\\n    }\\n\\n    /// Runs whatever is due now; returns how long until the next tick.\\n    fn advance(&mut self, sim: &mut Sim, sh: &Shared) -> Duration {\\n        let previewing = sim.studio_active();\\n        let mode = sim.studio_mode();\\n        if self.studio_mode != mode {\\n260→            self.studio_mode = mode;\\n            self.next = Instant::now();\\n        }\\n        let ctl = *sh.control.lock().unwrap();\\n        // The animation stage has its own play, pause and speed controls. The world's time\\n        // controls stay untouched, including a paused or rewound game behind the stage.\\n        let tick_wall = if previewing { sim.dt() } else { sim.dt() / ctl.speed.clamp(0.01, 16.0) };\\n        let (busy, window_ticks) = (&mut self.busy, &mut self.window_ticks);\\n        let mut tick_once = |sim: &mut Sim, at: Instant| {\\n            let input = if previewing {\\n270→                InputFrame::default()\\n            } else {\\n                let mut i = sh.input.lock().unwrap();\\n                let mut frame = *i;\\n                i.pressed = 0;\\n                frame.cmd = sh.cmds.lock().unwrap().pop_front();\\n                frame\\n            };\\n            let stamp = if previewing { None } else { sh.input_stamp.lock().unwrap().take() };\\n            let t = Instant::now();\\n280→            sim.step(&input);\\n            *busy += t.elapsed();\\n            if let Some(s) = stamp {\\n                *sh.latency_probe.lock().unwrap() = Some((s, Instant::now(), sim.state.tick));\\n            }\\n            *window_ticks += 1;\\n            publish(sim, sh, tick_wall, at);\\n        };\\n\\n        let now = Instant::now();\\n290→        if previewing {\\n            let mut n = 0;\\n            while now >= self.next && n < 8 {\\n                self.next += Duration::from_secs_f32(tick_wall);\\n                tick_once(sim, self.next);\\n                n += 1;\\n            }\\n            if n == 8 && now > self.next {\\n                self.next = now;\\n            }\\n300→        } else if ctl.rewinding {\\n            if now >= self.next {\\n                self.next = now + Duration::from_secs_f32(sim.dt());\\n                let oldest = sim.history.oldest_tick().unwrap_or(sim.state.tick);\\n                let target = sim.state.tick.saturating_sub(ctl.rewind_speed.max(1) as u64).max(oldest);\\n                if target < sim.state.tick && sim.rewind_to(target) {\\n                    self.rewound = true;\\n                }\\n                let dt = sim.dt();\\n                publish(sim, sh, dt, now);\\n310→            }\\n        } else if let Some(t) = ctl.scrub {\\n            sh.control.lock().unwrap().scrub = None;\",\"absolute_path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224015__x42677a/work/Hands of Harbor: Second Opinion-Trauma Center: Second Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-224015/engine/crates/pav_app/src/simhost.rs\",\"offset\":233,\"limit\":80,\"raw_output\":\"/// Fixed-rate ticking with time controls (pause, single steps, speed, rewind, scrubbing).\\nstruct Clock {\\n    next: Instant,\\n    window_start: Instant,\\n    window_ticks: u32,\\n    busy: Duration,\\n    rewound: bool,\\n    studio_mode: pav_core::prop_preview::StudioMode,\\n}\\n\\nimpl Clock {\\n    fn new() -> Self {\\n        Self {\\n            next: Instant::now(),\\n            window_start: Instant::now(),\\n            window_ticks: 0,\\n            busy: Duration::ZERO,\\n            rewound: false,\\n            studio_mode: pav_core::prop_preview::StudioMode::World,\\n        }\\n    }\\n\\n    /// Runs whatever is due now; returns how long until the next tick.\\n    fn advance(&mut self, sim: &mut Sim, sh: &Shared) -> Duration {\\n        let previewing = sim.studio_active();\\n        let mode = sim.studio_mode();\\n        if self.studio_mode != mode {\\n            self.studio_mode = mode;\\n            self.next = Instant::now();\\n        }\\n        let ctl = *sh.control.lock().unwrap();\\n        // The animation stage has its own play, pause and speed controls. The world's time\\n        // controls stay untouched, including a paused or rewound game behind the stage.\\n        let tick_wall = if previewing { sim.dt() } else { sim.dt() / ctl.speed.clamp(0.01, 16.0) };\\n        let (busy, window_ticks) = (&mut self.busy, &mut self.window_ticks);\\n        let mut tick_once = |sim: &mut Sim, at: Instant| {\\n            let input = if previewing {\\n                InputFrame::default()\\n            } else {\\n                let mut i = sh.input.lock().unwrap();\\n                let mut frame = *i;\\n                i.pressed = 0;\\n                frame.cmd = sh.cmds.lock().unwrap().pop_front();\\n                frame\\n            };\\n            let stamp = if previewing { None } else { sh.input_stamp.lock().unwrap().take() };\\n            let t = Instant::now();\\n            sim.step(&input);\\n            *busy += t.elapsed();\\n            if let Some(s) = stamp {\\n                *sh.latency_probe.lock().unwrap() = Some((s, Instant::now(), sim.state.tick));\\n            }\\n            *window_ticks += 1;\\n            publish(sim, sh, tick_wall, at);\\n        };\\n\\n        let now = Instant::now();\\n        if previewing {\\n            let mut n = 0;\\n            while now >= self.next && n < 8 {\\n                self.next += Duration::from_secs_f32(tick_wall);\\n                tick_once(sim, self.next);\\n                n += 1;\\n            }\\n            if n == 8 && now > self.next {\\n                self.next = now;\\n            }\\n        } else if ctl.rewinding {\\n            if now >= self.next {\\n                self.next = now + Duration::from_secs_f32(sim.dt());\\n                let oldest = sim.history.oldest_tick().unwrap_or(sim.state.tick);\\n                let target = sim.state.tick.saturating_sub(ctl.rewind_speed.max(1) as u64).max(oldest);\\n                if target < sim.state.tick && sim.rewind_to(target) {\\n                    self.rewound = true;\\n                }\\n                let dt = sim.dt();\\n                publish(sim, sh, dt, now);\\n            }\\n        } else if let Some(t) = ctl.scrub {\\n            sh.control.lock().unwrap().scrub = None;\\n\",\"total_lines\":427}}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa38-de6f-7dc0-ae0d-e0f717ed75f2","uuid":"c369740e-ec26-49f6-a227-d0bb163b39a5"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_186","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"surgery_cmd is located on InputFrame.\n\nRepeated ticks would re-apply surgery_cmd until cleared. LoadCampaign would restart the campaign every tick. SetTune is safe to repeat.\n\nUsing host.exec once would apply the command immediately. The command field is private, so it cannot be set directly from the product frame.\n\nPatching the clock is too invasive. Instead, Surgery::pre can skip repeated identical commands by storing the last command in an Option and comparing with PartialEq.\n\nA `last_cmd` field will be added to Surgery with serde defaults. It will be cleared when no command is present. Old snapshots remain compatible.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-46e13ef5-e427-4ccf-a0cc-d5f0fdff1ccb-124","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224015__x42677a/work/engine-link/crates/pav_core/src/games/surgery/mod.rs","offset":140,"limit":40}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-46e13ef5-e427-4ccf-a0cc-d5f0fdff1ccb-125","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224015__x42677a/work/engine-link/crates/pav_core/src/games/surgery/mod.rs","offset":910,"limit":20}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1258,"output_tokens":783,"cache_read_input_tokens":149376,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa38-de6f-7dc0-ae0d-e0f717ed75f2","uuid":"18b4edf2-d49a-4284-89d0-af19f03a6abe"}
