ntent\":\"            Section::Outlines => &[\\\"outlines_on\\\", \\\"outlines\\\", \\\"outline_px\\\", \\\"outline_darken\\\"],\"},{\"line_number\":156,\"content\":\"                to.cel_bands = from.cel_bands;\"},{\"line_number\":165,\"content\":\"                to.outline_darken = from.outline_darken;\"}]},{\"path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224015__x42677a/work/engine-link/crates/pav_view/src/build.rs\",\"matches\":[{\"line_number\":358,\"content\":\"    pub outline_darken: f32,\"},{\"line_number\":359,\"content\":\"    pub cel_bands: f32,\"},{\"line_number\":367,\"content\":\"    pub bloom: f32,\"},{\"line_number\":368,\"content\":\"    pub bloom_threshold: f32,\"},{\"line_number\":415,\"content\":\"            outline_darken: 0.35,\"},{\"line_number\":416,\"content\":\"            cel_bands: 2.0,\"},{\"line_number\":497,\"content\":\"        v.float(\\\"outline_darken\\\", &mut self.outline_darken, 0.0, 1.0, \\\"Outline brightness relative to the surface\\\");\"},{\"line_number\":498,\"content\":\"        v.float(\\\"cel_bands\\\", &mut self.cel_bands, 2.0, 6.0, \\\"Light bands in cel style\\\");\"},{\"line_number\":1088,\"content\":\"            cel_bands: settings.cel_bands,\"},{\"line_number\":1095,\"content\":\"        scene.post.outline_darken = settings.outline_darken;\"}]},{\"path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224015__x42677a/work/engine-link/crates/pav_app/src/look_ui.rs\",\"matches\":[{\"line_number\":499,\"content\":\"            c |= slider(ui, &mut v.cel_bands, 2.0..=6.0, \\\"cel bands\\\", \\\"Light bands in cel shading\\\");\"},{\"line_number\":510,\"content\":\"                &mut v.outline_darken,\"}]},{\"path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224015__x42677a/work/engine-link/crates/pav_render/src/renderer.rs\",\"matches\":[{\"line_number\":1080,\"content\":\"            style: [scene.style.flat_shadow, scene.style.cel_bands, scene.style.rim, scene.style.specular],\"},{\"line_number\":1448,\"content\":\"            misc: [p.outline_darken, bloom, if distorted { 1.0 } else { 0.0 }, 0.0],\"}]},{\"path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224015__x42677a/work/engine-link/crates/pav_render/src/scene.rs\",\"matches\":[{\"line_number\":316,\"content\":\"    pub cel_bands: f32,\"},{\"line_number\":323,\"content\":\"        Self { flat_shadow: 0.62, cel_bands: 2.0, rim: 0.25, specular: 0.35 }\"}]}]}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa38-de6f-7dc0-ae0d-e0f717ed75f2","uuid":"6c5e4125-6269-4fcc-a3fa-ea5f966c002a"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_190","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The minimum value for cel_bands in settings is 2.\n\nSetting cel_bands to 3.0 directly bypasses the slider clamp. outline_px will be 1.6 for the field. The plate grid uses 420 by 240 vertices with a 22 by 12.6 meter span. Heights derive from an ellipse.\n\nThe ellipse formula is `1 - dx²/22 - dz²/9` with height 1.25, producing a central mound within the 22 meter span. Noise will be added via a hash function.\n\nThe hash function uses bitwise operations to generate noise values. Colors map to height: low for bed, mid for flesh, high for top. Veins appear where noise exceeds 0.82. Pools form from a second noise layer at mid-height. Hazards darken or raise nearby vertices within their radius. Wet highlights mix toward white when noise is high. Quads use a specific winding order.\n\nChecking the quad winding order against a right-handed Y-up coordinate system. The goal is to ensure normals point upward when viewed from above.\n\nThe cross product of the two edges is Vec3::Y, so the i00, i01, i10 winding order yields a normal pointing upward. The earlier concern about the winding direction was incorrect.\n\nVertex normals will be computed from grid height differences. Instance color is white and vertex colors are linear sRGB. Drape vertices outside the ellipse use a teal low-height color. Steel retractors will be SDF capsules at the edges. Instruments sit at y=0.35. Pools are dark discs and sacs are green emissive spheres.\n\nAdditional hazards include a yellow unlit eye, purple parasite capsules, and a dark laceration line. The plate will always render so the canvas stays painted even in title mode. Character cards will be extruded polygons standing at x=±3.1 and z=-2, visible during story and results modes.\n\nCards will stand at z = -3.5 facing +Z, extruded in Z so they appear as vertical planes. Title mode will use smaller side cards instead. A simple person silhouette is being drafted from a head circle, shoulders, and body.\n\nChaikin smoothing and ear clipping will shape the silhouette. Extrusion depth is 0.08. Four mouth expressions will be added. This keeps the characters as paper theatre rather than SDF busts. A test will verify the surgery scene builds a finite dynamic mesh with camera FOV 36.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-dedb7564-83d4-4f03-968a-0d76577991e6-130","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224015__x42677a/work/engine-link/crates/pav_tools/src/session.rs","offset":246,"limit":40}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-dedb7564-83d4-4f03-968a-0d76577991e6-131","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224015__x42677a/work/engine-link/crates/pav_tools/src/session.rs","offset":330,"limit":70}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-dedb7564-83d4-4f03-968a-0d76577991e6-132","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224015__x42677a/work/engine-link/crates/pav_core/src/games/surgery/mod.rs","offset":215,"limit":40}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1163,"output_tokens":2181,"cache_read_input_tokens":153600,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa38-de6f-7dc0-ae0d-e0f717ed75f2","uuid":"f732441b-510f-4598-a161-20dc5106e493"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-dedb7564-83d4-4f03-968a-0d76577991e6-130","content":"{\"type\":\"ReadFile\",\"FileContent\":{\"content\":\"246→        // Room changes after cues (leaving a room clears its cue first, then restores the camera).\\n        if now != self.room_cam.as_ref().map(|r| r.0) {\\n            if let Some((_, saved)) = self.room_cam.take() {\\n                self.camera.params = saved;\\n250→            }\\n            if let Some(r) = now.and_then(|i| w.rooms.get(i as usize)).filter(|r| !r.def.camera.is_empty()) {\\n                let saved = self.camera.params.clone();\\n                let mut cam = r.def.camera.clone();\\n                let yaw = cam.get(\\\"yaw\\\").and_then(|v| v.as_f64()).unwrap_or(0.0);\\n                cam.insert(\\\"yaw\\\".into(), rot(yaw, r.place.quarters));\\n                apply_map(&mut self.camera.params, &cam);\\n                self.room_cam = Some((r.id, saved));\\n            }\\n        }\\n260→        self.sync_view();\\n    }\\n\\n    /// Takes `params` as the base camera and applies the current room's `[camera]` on top.\\n    pub fn reset_camera(&mut self, params: CameraParams) {\\n        self.camera.params = params;\\n        self.room_cam = None;\\n        self.cue_base = None;\\n        self.sync_camera();\\n    }\\n270→\\n    /// The camera without the current room's defaults.\\n    pub fn camera_base_or_current(&self) -> CameraParams {\\n        self.room_cam.as_ref().map(|(_, c)| c.clone()).unwrap_or_else(|| self.camera.params.clone())\\n    }\\n\\n    /// The view settings without the current room's / pads' overrides.\\n    pub fn view_base_or_current(&self) -> ViewSettings {\\n        self.view_base.clone().unwrap_or_else(|| self.view.clone())\\n    }\\n280→\\n    /// Takes `view` as the base settings and applies the current room's `[view]` table on top.\\n    pub fn reset_view(&mut self, view: ViewSettings) {\\n        self.view = 