{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-550dcac7-dd1c-4164-8374-13f4524d0ad6-135","content":"{\"type\":\"GrepSearch\",\"stdout\":[60,119,111,114,107,115,112,97,99,101,95,114,101,115,117,108,116,32,119,111,114,107,115,112,97,99,101,95,112,97,116,104,61,34,47,104,111,109,101,47,109,105,99,104,97,47,100,101,118,47,99,99,45,109,97,116,114,105,120,47,114,117,110,115,47,103,114,111,107,45,120,104,105,103,104,46,98,117,105,108,100,45,118,50,95,95,50,48,50,54,49,49,48,52,45,50,50,52,48,49,53,95,95,120,52,50,54,55,55,97,47,119,111,114,107,34,62,10,70,111,117,110,100,32,49,32,109,97,116,99,104,105,110,103,32,108,105,110,101,115,10,47,104,111,109,101,47,109,105,99,104,97,47,100,101,118,47,99,99,45,109,97,116,114,105,120,47,114,117,110,115,47,103,114,111,107,45,120,104,105,103,104,46,98,117,105,108,100,45,118,50,95,95,50,48,50,54,49,49,48,52,45,50,50,52,48,49,53,95,95,120,52,50,54,55,55,97,47,119,111,114,107,47,101,110,103,105,110,101,45,108,105,110,107,47,99,114,97,116,101,115,47,112,97,118,95,99,111,114,101,47,115,114,99,47,103,97,109,101,115,47,115,117,114,103,101,114,121,47,109,111,100,46,114,115,10,52,49,56,58,32,32,32,32,112,117,98,40,99,114,97,116,101,41,32,102,110,32,115,112,97,119,110,95,107,105,110,100,95,97,116,40,38,109,117,116,32,115,101,108,102,44,32,107,105,110,100,58,32,117,56,44,32,120,58,32,102,51,50,44,32,122,58,32,102,51,50,44,32,100,114,97,105,110,58,32,102,51,50,41,32,123,10,60,47,119,111,114,107,115,112,97,99,101,95,114,101,115,117,108,116,62],\"stderr\":[],\"exit_code\":0,\"match_count\":1,\"file_matches\":[{\"path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224015__x42677a/work/engine-link/crates/pav_core/src/games/surgery/mod.rs\",\"matches\":[{\"line_number\":418,\"content\":\"    pub(crate) fn spawn_kind_at(&mut self, kind: u8, x: f32, z: f32, drain: f32) {\"}]}]}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa38-de6f-7dc0-ae0d-e0f717ed75f2","uuid":"2e3be752-f73f-4b40-909e-af5920dfdea0"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_193","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"`pub(crate)` items are visible within the `pav_core` crate.\n\n`apply_mirror` is made public so same-module code can call it. Surgeon positions and tools are set from snapshot cursors inside `apply_mirror` to show cursors in the frame.\n\n`apply_mirror` now clears existing hazards and spawns new ones from the snapshot marks. The host snapshot JSON will be kept under 1200 bytes with two-decimal quantization and a maximum of about twenty hazards. After applying the mirror, the client overwrites its own cursor slot with a locally predicted position so the status cursor updates immediately. This ensures the two-page test works: client input moves the host's cursor, and both sides see matching vitals.\n\nHost status will include a `cursors` field listing each surgeon's x and z position. The host applies incoming aim data to the matching surgeon input slot so the cursor moves on the next tick. Clients send aim updates every 80 milliseconds with slot, x, z, tool, and held state.\n\nThe host stores the latest network input per slot and writes it into SurgeonInput with AIM_ABSOLUTE|SNAP so the cursor appears immediately. The local host player uses its own local input; other slots use network data. The server has no local slot, so it relies entirely on network input or bots, and bleeders drain if no useful input arrives. Clients may only send menu navigation keys rather than aim commands.\n\nArrow keys will be treated as aim nudges to keep movement alive, though the harness does not verify cursor motion. The two-page test is separate from the harness and will use a custom script that opens the game URL in two browser pages; it checks that client aim updates the host cursor and both sides report matching vitals.\n\nA `hub_check.py` script will run the four conformance queries. It will then launch a two-player harness round with auto finish disabled, start the round, wait for play to begin, inject aim commands via `__game.do`, and read both frames' `__game.status` to verify matching vitals.\n\nThe harness conformance loop is owned by the page, so a two-page test cannot simply create separate iframes. The plan is to use the harness page with auto=0 and manually start a round via page.evaluate before timeUp, then inject aim commands directly into both frames.\n\nI will implement the protocol correctly before writing the test and fixing any failures. I also need to copy harness.html into tests/hub and verify index.html meta names so the packer replacement works.\n\nHub metadata will be injected by the packer after the charset tag rather than hardcoded in index.html. The about-data script is placed before the closing body tag or inside the head so the WASM shell can read it. The packer inserts a JSON block with id \"about-data\" containing the hub configuration. The exit-interview.json file will live at the work root and is read from a path relative to the engine directory.\n\nThe packer will read `web/about.json` to generate the HTML `about-data` script. The same file will also be copied to the work root as `exit-interview.json`. Both copies must contain identical JSON objects, so a check will compare their parsed contents for equality. The about content is being drafted now with a source timestamp of 2026-11-04 22:40:15.\n\nThe about content is now complete. It cites Trauma Center: Second Opinion as the source material, describes the simulation genre and overhead surgical perspective, lists the Pavilion engine stack, cel-shaded art direction, sim-driven animations, synthesized audio, optional AI Hub multiplayer, and the cargo surgery test suite.\n\nResearch is complete in the plan. The environment is Grok CLI on Linux with model xAI/grok-4.7 and reasoning effort xhigh.\n\nTesting feedback was honest. Three critical issues blocked campaign wins: a Rust or-pattern guard skipped stage-0 sutures, nearest-hazard selection stole forceps pulls, and sac swell shared the laser charge meter. The skill-1 bot survey across every case from a fresh scene was most helpful. A print probe that only dumped state and was removed was least helpful.\n\nEngine feedback is beginning.\n\nEngine feedback is now complete. The game hook, RenderFrame, recorded InputFrame, headless UI, and single-file packer were liked. Rustc breaks when paths contain colons because LD_LIBRARY_PATH joins them; the App::frame demo path also conflicts with new games; and the sounds_for wildcard swallowed Cue. Operative rules, plate mesh, shell, cue bus, and hub shim were built from scratch. Keeping the product frame off the demo camera, menu, and touch layer was the hardest part. Surgery frame, input, and cue seams, view emit, product branch, audio buses, packer injection, and js-sys were changed because the hook cannot draw, hear, or join a hub alone.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-7261b6a8-2098-4474-ba24-a0f2fa46ae29-136","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224015__x42677a/work/TASK.md","offset":90,"limit":80}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":548,"output_tokens":2241,"cache_read_input_tokens":159744,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa38-de6f-7dc0-ae0d-e0f717ed75f2","uuid":"4bc84772-6c3b-4760-b3f0-c70c9e0ddc21"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-7261b6a8-2098-4474-ba24-a0f2fa46ae29-136","content":"{\"type\":\"ReadFile\",\"FileContent\":{\"content\":\"90→No TODOs, placeholders, or stubbed features. The demo is complete.\\n\\n## Source Information\\nCRITICAL: Put Source Information, Testing Feedback, Engine Feedback and Prompt Feedback in your chat reply and an in-game About/Credits screen. Write \\\"unknown\\\" for anything you can't confirm.\\n- Date: 2026-11-04 22:40:15\\n- Source: the work it's based on\\n- Plan: the file name of the plan you were given to build from, or none\\n- Genre and Perspective: genre and camera perspective used\\n- Tech: stack, libraries/engines, with versions if applicable\\n- Art Direction: style used\\n100→- Animation: system used\\n- Audio: music, sound effects and voice used\\n- Online: network features used, or none\\n- Testing: testing parameters allowed\\n- Research: research done, or none\\n- Environment: Grok CLI (headless); Linux\\n- Model: xAI, grok-4.7, reasoning effort xhigh\\n- Usage: write \\\"added on import\\\". You can't see your own cost, so don't estimate it: the runner records the real cost, tokens and time, and the agent that imports the game into AI Hub puts them on your About/Credits screen.\\n\\nExit interview: before you finish, also save these answers as exit-interview.json in this folder's root, beside the game's .html: one JSON object in exactly the shape below, every value filled in (\\\"unknown\\\" for anything you can't confirm). Tools read it (the game's run record and the AI Hub catalogue), so write plain text, and check that the file parses as JSON.\\n110→{\\n  \\\"sourceInformation\\\": {\\\"date\\\": \\\"\\\", \\\"source\\\": \\\"\\\", \\\"plan\\\": \\\"\\\", \\\"genre\\\": \\\"\\\", \\\"perspective\\\": \\\"\\\", \\\"tech\\\": \\\"\\\", \\\"artDirection\\\": \\\"\\\", \\\"animation\\\": \\\"\\\", \\\"audio\\\": \\\"\\\", \\\"online\\\": \\\"\\\", \\\"testing\\\": \\\"\\\", \\\"research\\\": \\\"\\\", \\\"environment\\\": \\\"\\\", \\\"model\\\": \\\"\\\", \\\"usage\\\": \\\"added on import\\\"},\\n  \\\"testingFeedback\\\": [\\\"your answer to each Testing Feedback question, in order\\\"],\\n  \\\"engineFeedback\\\": [\\\"your answer to each Engine Feedback question, in order\\\"],\\n  \\\"promptFeedback\\\": [\\\"your answer to each Prompt Feedback question, in order\\\"],\\n  \\\"aiHub\\\": {\\n    \\\"name\\\": \\\"the game's title, as on its title screen\\\",\\n    \\\"tagline\\\": \\\"a few words to go under the title\\\",\\n    \\\"description\\\": \\\"one or two sentences for the catalogue\\\",\\n    \\\"type\\\": \\\"Game, Tech demo or Tool\\\",\\n120→    \\\"genre\\\": \\\"one of Action, Adventure, Fighting, Flight, Horror, Kids & Learning, Life Sim, Platformer, Puzzle, Racing, RPG, Shooter, Simulation, Sports, Stealth, Strategy\\\",\\n    \\\"source\\\": \\\"the work it's based on, e.g. Moby-Dick\\\",\\n    \\\"series\\\": \\\"its franchise, e.g. Star Fox, or empty\\\",\\n    \\\"players\\\": \\\"how many can play: 1, 1–2 or 1–4\\\",\\n    \\\"controls\\\": \\\"the controls, in one line\\\",\\n    \\\"tags\\\": [\\\"3 to 6 lowercase tags, e.g. 2d, 3d, arcade, story, co-op, versus, first-person, third-person, top-down, side-scrolling, pixel art, low-poly, retro, sci-fi, fantasy, comedy, vehicles, boss fights, exploration\\\"]\\n  }\\n}\\nThe catalogue's model, effort, CLI, date and usage come from the run's record after you finish, so they aren't asked here.\\n\\n130→Testing Feedback\\n\\n- How many issues did testing catch?\\n- How many would be considered critical issues / game breaking?\\n- What was the most helpful test you ran?\\n- What was the least helpful test you ran?\\n\\nEngine Feedback\\n\\n- What did you like most about the engine?\\n140→- Did you get stuck or guess wrong?\\n- What was the most important thing you had to build yourself?\\n- What was the hardest part about using the engine?\\n- What did you change in the engine, and why? (none if nothing)\\n- If you could change one thing about the engine, what would it be?\\n\\nPrompt Feedback\\n\\n- What did you like most about this prompt?\\n- What was confusing?\\n150→- What was the hardest thing to do?\\n- What would you change in this prompt?\\n\",\"content_concise\":\"90→No TODOs, placeholders, or stubbed features. The demo is complete.\\n\\n## Source Information\\nCRITICAL: Put Source Information, Testing Feedback, Engine Feedback and Prompt Feedback in your chat reply and an in-game About/Credits screen. Write \\\"unknown\\\" for anything you can't confirm.\\n- Date: 2026-11-04 22:40:15\\n- Source: the work it's based on\\n- Plan: the file name of the plan you were given to build from, or none\\n- Genre and Perspective: genre and camera perspective used\\n- Tech: stack, libraries/engines, with versions if applicable\\n- Art Direction: style used\\n100→- Animation: system used\\n- Audio: music, sound effects and voice used\\n- Online: network features used, or none\\n- Testing: testing parameters allowed\\n- Research: research done, or none\\n- Environment: Grok CLI (headless); Linux\\n- Model: xAI, grok-4.7, reasoning effort xhigh\\n- Usage: write \\\"added on import\\\". You can't see your own cost, so don't estimate it: the runner records the real cost, tokens and time, and the agent that imports the game into AI Hub puts them on your About/Credits screen.\\n\\nExit interview: before you finish, also save these answers as exit-interview.json in this folder's root, beside the game's .html: one JSON object in exactly the shape below, every value filled in (\\\"unknown\\\" for anything you can't confirm). Tools read it (the game's run record and the AI Hub catalogue), so write plain text, and check that the file parses as JSON.\\n110→{\\n  \\\"sourceInformation\\\": {\\\"date\\\": \\\"\\\", \\\"source\\\": \\\"\\\", \\\"plan\\\": \\\"\\\", \\\"genre\\\": \\\"\\\", \\\"perspective\\\": \\\"\\\",