{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_203","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"App fields are private to the app module.\n\nProduct can access App fields as a child. I will add `harbor: product::Harbor` to App and construct it in `new()`. I will also disable `show_boot`, `show_stats`, and `show_guide` in `new()` or `finish_init` as a safeguard. The cursor will be hidden during operations.\n\nI will read keys directly from `app.input.keys` instead of using engine button helpers. A `prev` key state will be stored in Harbor to detect confirm edges. I also need to extend `AudioOut::play` to accept a bus parameter so music notes can be scheduled per beat.\n\nA `set_buses` method will send bus gains to the audio thread. The audio callback applies them to the mixer each frame. Product will set these from the current tune values every frame. Music, effects, and voices are not standard sliders in the dev panel, so a separate command is needed for them.\n\nA `set_bus` method on Surgery will handle the three extra bus gains. The shell emits a custom command so Product can update them via exec. Default values are 0.10, 0.80, and 0.70. These persist in localStorage with settings.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-bf7b1ebe-8b18-491e-a622-d4bcdfbe3a01-147","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224015__x42677a/work/engine-link/crates/pav_core/src/games/surgery/mod.rs","offset":45,"limit":30}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":327,"output_tokens":943,"cache_read_input_tokens":172416,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa38-de6f-7dc0-ae0d-e0f717ed75f2","uuid":"b486f645-900f-4949-bf0d-3f17fc1bde71"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-bf7b1ebe-8b18-491e-a622-d4bcdfbe3a01-147","content":"{\"type\":\"ReadFile\",\"FileContent\":{\"content\":\"45→pub const X_MIN: f32 = -9.0;\\npub const X_MAX: f32 = 9.0;\\npub const Z_MIN: f32 = -4.0;\\npub const Z_MAX: f32 = 4.2;\\n\\n50→#[derive(Clone, Serialize, Deserialize)]\\npub struct Surgeon {\\n    pub active: bool,\\n    pub x: f32,\\n    pub z: f32,\\n    pub tool: u8,\\n    pub score: i32,\\n    pub chain: u32,\\n    pub best_chain: u32,\\n    pub mistakes: u32,\\n60→    pub since_chain: f32,\\n    pub meter: f32,\\n    pub gift_arm: f32,\\n    pub was_use: bool,\\n    pub was_gift: bool,\\n    pub was_defib: bool,\\n    pub defib: f32,\\n    pub iv_cd: f32,\\n    pub wrong_cd: f32,\\n    pub name_i: u8,\\n70→    pub focus: Option<u32>,\\n    pub focus_t: f32,\\n}\\n\\nimpl Surgeon {\",\"content_concise\":\"45→pub const X_MIN: f32 = -9.0;\\npub const X_MAX: f32 = 9.0;\\npub const Z_MIN: f32 = -4.0;\\npub const Z_MAX: f32 = 4.2;\\n\\n50→#[derive(Clone, Serialize, Deserialize)]\\npub struct Surgeon {\\n    pub active: bool,\\n    pub x: f32,\\n    pub z: f32,\\n    pub tool: u8,\\n    pub score: i32,\\n    pub chain: u32,\\n    pub best_chain: u32,\\n    pub mistakes: u32,\\n60→    pub since_chain: f32,\\n    pub meter: f32,\\n    pub gift_arm: f32,\\n    pub was_use: bool,\\n    pub was_gift: bool,\\n    pub was_defib: bool,\\n    pub defib: f32,\\n    pub iv_cd: f32,\\n    pub wrong_cd: f32,\\n    pub name_i: u8,\\n70→    pub focus: Option<u32>,\\n    pub focus_t: f32,\\n}\\n\\nimpl Surgeon {\",\"absolute_path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224015__x42677a/work/Hands of Harbor: Second Opinion-Trauma Center: Second Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-224015/engine/crates/pav_core/src/games/surgery/mod.rs\",\"offset\":45,\"limit\":30,\"raw_output\":\"pub const X_MIN: f32 = -9.0;\\npub const X_MAX: f32 = 9.0;\\npub const Z_MIN: f32 = -4.0;\\npub const Z_MAX: f32 = 4.2;\\n\\n#[derive(Clone, Serialize, Deserialize)]\\npub struct Surgeon {\\n    pub active: bool,\\n    pub x: f32,\\n    pub z: f32,\\n    pub tool: u8,\\n    pub score: i32,\\n    pub chain: u32,\\n    pub best_chain: u32,\\n    pub mistakes: u32,\\n    pub since_chain: f32,\\n    pub meter: f32,\\n    pub gift_arm: f32,\\n    pub was_use: bool,\\n    pub was_gift: bool,\\n    pub was_defib: bool,\\n    pub defib: f32,\\n    pub iv_cd: f32,\\n    pub wrong_cd: f32,\\n    pub name_i: u8,\\n    pub focus: Option<u32>,\\n    pub focus_t: f32,\\n}\\n\\nimpl Surgeon {\\n\",\"total_lines\":1010}}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa38-de6f-7dc0-ae0d-e0f717ed75f2","uuid":"f65d6d9b-bf4b-4abd-bd78-c1b39cf19b7e"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_204","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"I will now write all the code.\n\nStarting with the largest files in parallel. I'm implementing a Chaikin curve subdivision for polygon smoothing, then planning to use ear clipping or fan triangulation for convex polygons.\n\nFinished the Chaikin subdivision function. Confirmed front face winding for Z-extrusion. The card will be centered with y starting at 0.2. Character parts will be defined as 2D polygons in local space and then transformed.\n\nWriting the view file carefully to ensure it compiles. Instruments will be SDF capsules with a steel color. The plate receives shadows and belongs to group 2.\n\nConfiguring the scene lighting. The sun will cast shadows toward the target with a radius of 16. A single point light at (-1, 7, -1) will provide warm ambient illumination. The clear color is set to a dark blue-gray, and the vignette filter is set to 0.35.\n\nBloom is set to 0.35 with threshold 1.15. NaN vertices will be clamped in release builds and debug-asserted in debug builds.\n\nThe build.rs hook will run after `attach` but before the scene return. It emits surgery meshes and applies the camera look. Lights are set last so they override defaults cleanly.\n\nThe surgery build will not add a floor. I confirmed the RenderFrame surgery field is an Option<Arc<SurgeryFrame>>.\n\nI will write the shell first so it can be tested without egui, then wire the draw function to use egui.\n\nFor headless mode, I will store a Shell inside Headless and add a frame_surgery method that takes a SurgeryFrame, width, height, and ShellInput, returning a Drawn result and a vector of commands.\n\nI will not change Headless::frame's signature to avoid breaking callers. Instead, session.rs will check frame.surgery and route to a new frame_surgery method that creates egui and draws the shell. The Headless struct owns Shell state so tools persist across frames. Shell can also be tested directly without Headless.\n\nShell will be tested directly and rendered headlessly so the UI sees text. Headless input will map to shell pointer events, and a `drive` method will accept `surgery::Input`. The shell uses fixed item rectangles for hit testing and focus, with items stacked at y = 200 + i * 64, x = 200, w = 700, h = 52. Tests will begin by creating a `Shell::new()` instance.\n\nShell tests are being written to verify the menu, attract, and touch-only states. The menu test confirms the title appears and pressing confirm advances to the menu screen. The attract test steps the shell forward by ten seconds to reach the attract screen. The touch-only test checks that a controller prompt is shown and the Settings option remains visible. Device prompt tests validate that gamepad and Xbox button labels render correctly.\n\nShell tests will verify that the confirm prompt renders as \"A\" for gamepads and \"Enter\" for keyboards. A test will navigate from the title screen through settings to change and reset a sound slider. The developer menu is only reachable via the pause screen, which requires an operation, so tests must drive the shell from its initial state.\n\nA `note_mode` method will let the product report the simulation state each frame. When the mode is operation, pressing back opens pause; otherwise the shell stays on the title screen. This lets tests drive the shell from its initial state to reach the developer menu.\n\nThe shell will use a `Screen::Hud` overlay for the operation HUD. A `Shell.overlay` field will hold pause, settings, about, and developer menus when opened on top of the base screen. The base screen will be driven by the simulation mode: title, story, chart, hud, results, dead, card, or attract. This design keeps the shell in its initial title state for tests.\n\nI will add localStorage persistence for settings in the product WASM. I am ready to write the files in batches and will delete the probe test when rewriting surgery.rs.\n\nThe 10-seed test may take a few seconds because compilation is slow. I will run the smaller library tests first, then the larger UI, audio, and view tests, followed by a WASM check, a web build, browser tests, and hub tests.\n\nI will add the `LoadAttract` variant to `SurgeryCmd` and its match arm. The `fresh()` method will use `exec` instead of tracking a `last_cmd` field. The cursor will remain visible during the title screen. I confirmed that `egui_state` is initialized before the first frame, so `surgery_frame` will always find it.\n\nI will guard against a missing egui_state by returning early and drawing only the scene. The window title will be set from the current scene name, using the surgery title when the scene starts with \"surgery\". I will also update the main.rs log.\n\nI will create engine/web/hub_shim.js and engine/web/about.json. The packer reads these files. HTML tags come from a string in the packer. I confirmed session.js does not contain </script. The two-page test uses client do() to set aim. The host receives it via send.\n\nThe game must run inside harness iframes for the protocol. `__game.do` will accept JSON commands like `{\"aim\":[1.5, -0.4]}` to set the local cursor target and send it. The status JSON will include title, screen, music volume, vitals, cursors, focus, device, and prompt. The launch test will assert a music value of 0.10.\n\nThe status JSON will be built with `format!` to guarantee the music value is exactly 0.10 in the text, since serde might serialize it as 0.1. The view code will be kept correct while files are written. A vertex count of 100800 was noted for the 420×240 grid.\n\nThe 420×240 grid uses roughly 600,000 indices. Building it every frame in debug mode may take 20–50 ms, which is acceptable.\n\nA history test will set history_seconds to 8.0 before stepping.\n\nA random_input helper will generate random InputFrame values for automated testing.\n\nThe random input helper generates a rotating aim vector and cycles through tools. Idle mode forces the first surgeon active but leaves it unused, so vitals drain and the case dies within 180 seconds. A 400-second idle test limit is cheap enough.\n\nSkill 1 should win across all ten seeds. The bot uses tick hashes for noise instead of true randomness, so spawn positions vary only slightly between seeds. A rank of S or above requires at least four wins; seed one already achieved ENCORE. If any seed fails to reach that rank, the cause will be identified.\n\nA sloppy test will drive the simulation to verify campaign coverage for all tools, hazards, strains, gifts, and code. It will spawn a polyp hazard at angle zero, aim the laser at it, and hold the tool for about three seconds. If the laser overheat rating or mistake count does not increase, the cause will be debugged.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-3fda6fe3-3cdd-4724-b804-74cca7408fbc-148","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224015__x42677a/work/engine-link/crates/pav_core/src/games/surgery/heart.rs","limit":80}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1265,"output_tokens":3996,"cache_read_input_tokens":172672,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa38-de6f-7dc0-ae0d-e0f717ed75f2","uuid":"da935b42-53a0-4202-bbd1-ce13770f0d85"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-3fda6fe3-3cdd-4724-b804-74cca7408fbc-148","content":"{\"type\":\"ReadFile\",\"FileContent\":{\"content\":\"1→//! One heartbeat clock. Vitals, the ECG, strain steps and on-beat all read it.\\n\\nuse serde::{Deserialize, Serialize};\\n\\n#[derive(Clone, Debug, Serialize, Deserialize)]\\npub struct Heart {\\n    pub vitals: f32,\\n    pub phase: f32,\\n    pub bpm: f32,\\n10→    pub since_r: f32,\\n    pub period: f32,\\n    pub beats: u32,\\n    pub flat: bool,\\n    pub ghost: f32,\\n}\\n\\nimpl Heart {\\n    pub fn new(vitals: f32) -> Self {\\n        let mut h = Self { vitals, phase: 0.0, bpm: 80.0, since_r: 1.0, period: 0.75, beats: 0, flat: false, ghost: 0.0 };\\n20→        h.recompute(1.0);\\n        h\\n    }\\n\\n    pub fn recompute(&mut self, coupling: f32) {\\n        let t = (1.0 - self.vitals.clamp(0.0, 100.0) / 100.0).clamp(0.0, 1.0);\\n        let c = coupling.clamp(0.25, 2.0);\\n        self.bpm = (72.0 + (148.0 - 72.0) * t) * c;\\n        self.period = 60.0 / self.bpm.max(40.0);\\n    }\\n30→\\n    /// Advances the clock. Returns true on an R-wave (world time; a flatline has none).\\n    pub fn tick(&mut self, dt: f32, coupling: f32) -> bool {\\n        self.recompute(coupling);\\n        self.vitals = self.vitals.clamp(0.0, 100.0);\\n        if self.flat {\\n            self.ghost = (self.ghost + dt / self.period).fract();\\n            self.since_r += dt;\\n            return false;\\n        }\\n40→        self.phase += dt / self.period;\\n        if self.phase >= 1.0 {\\n            self.phase = self.phase.fract();\\n            self.since_r = self.phase * self.period;\\n            self.beats = self.beats.wrapping_add(1);\\n            self.ghost = self.phase;\\n            true\\n        } else {\\n            self.since_r += dt;\\n            self.ghost = self.phase;\\n50→            false\\n        }\\n    }\\n\\n    pub fn on_beat(&self, window_ms: f32) -> bool {\\n        let w = (window_ms / 1000.0).clamp(0.02, 0.4);\\n        self.since_r <= w || (self.period - self.since_r) <= w\\n    }\\n\\n    /// Diastole: the quiet half, when a tendril can be pulled.\\n60→    pub fn diastole(&self) -> bool {\\n        self.phase > 0.28 && self.phase < 0.72\\n    }\\n\\n    /// The ghost QRS during a flatline. `ghost` is the phase in 0..1.\\n    pub fn ghost_on_beat(&self, window_ms: f32) -> bool {\\n        let w = (window_ms / 1000.0).clamp(0.02, 0.4);\\n        let g = self.ghost.rem_euclid(1.0);\\n        let since = g * self.period;\\n        let until = (1.0 - g) * self.period;\\n70→        since <= w || until <= w\\n    }\\n}\\n\",\"content_concise\":\"1→//! One heartbeat clock. Vitals, the ECG, strain steps and on-beat all read it.\\n\\nuse serde::{Deserialize, Serialize};\\n\\n#[derive(Clone, Debug, Serialize, Deserialize)]\\npub struct Heart {\\n    pub vitals: f32,\\n    pub phase: f32,\\n    pub bpm: f32,\\n10→    pub since_r: f32,\\n    pub period: f32,\\n    pub beats: u32,\\n    pub flat: bool,\\n    pub ghost: f32,\\n}\\n\\nimpl Heart {\\n    pub fn new(vitals: f32) -> Self {\\n        let mut h = Self { vitals, phase: 0.0, bpm: 80.0, since_r: 1.0, period: 0.75, beats: 0, flat: false, ghost: 0.0 };\\n20→        h.recompute(1.0);\\n        h\\n    }\\n\\n    pub fn recompute(&mut self, coupling: f32) {\\n        let t = (1.0 - self.vitals.clamp(0.0, 100.0) / 100.0).clamp(0.0, 1.0);\\n        let c = coupling.clamp(0.25, 2.0);\\n        self.bpm = (72.0 + (148.0 - 72.0) * t) * c;\\n        self.period = 60.0 / self.bpm.max(40.0);\\n    }\\n30→\\n    /// Advances the clock. Returns true on an R-wave (world time; a flatline has none).\\n    pub fn tick(&mut self, dt: f32, coupling: f32) -> bool {\\n        self.recompute(coupling);\\n        self.vitals = self.vitals.clamp(0.0, 100.0);\\n        if self.flat {\\n            self.ghost = (self.ghost + dt / self.period).fract();\\n            self.since_r += dt;\\n            return false;\\n        }\\n40→        self.phase += dt / self.period;\\n        if self.phase >= 1.0 {\\n            self.phase = self.phase.fract();\\n            self.since_r = self.phase * self.period;\\n            self.beats = self.beats.wrapping_add(1);\\n            self.ghost = self.phase;\\n            true\\n        } else {\\n            self.since_r += dt;\\n            self.ghost = self.phase;\\n50→            false\\n        }\\n    }\\n\\n    pub fn on_beat(&self, window_ms: f32) -> bool {\\n        let w = (window_ms / 1000.0).clamp(0.02, 0.4);\\n        self.since_r <= w || (self.period - self.since_r) <= w\\n    }\\n\\n    /// Diastole: the quiet half, when a tendril can be pulled.\\n60→    pub fn diastole(&self) -> bool {\\n        self.phase > 0.28 && self.phase < 0.72\\n    }\\n\\n    /// The ghost QRS during a flatline. `ghost` is the phase in 0..1.\\n    pub fn ghost_on_beat(&self, window_ms: f32) -> bool {\\n        let w = (window_ms / 1000.0).clamp(0.02, 0.4);\\n        let g = self.ghost.rem_euclid(1.0);\\n        let since = g * self.period;\\n        let until = (1.0 - g) * self.period;\\n70→        since <= w || until <= w\\n    }\\n}\\n\",\"absolute_path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224015__x42677a/work/Hands of Harbor: Second Opinion-Trauma Center: Second Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-224015/engine/crates/pav_core/src/games/surgery/heart.rs\",\"offset\":null,\"limit\":80,\"raw_output\":\"//! One heartbeat clock. Vitals, the ECG, strain steps and on-beat all read it.\\n\\nuse serde::{Deserialize, Serialize};\\n\\n#[derive(Clone, Debug, Serialize, Deserialize)]\\npub struct Heart {\\n    pub vitals: f32,\\n    pub phase: f32,\\n    pub bpm: f32,\\n    pub since_r: f32,\\n    pub period: f32,\\n    pub beats: u32,\\n    pub flat: bool,\\n    pub ghost: f32,\\n}\\n\\nimpl Heart {\\n    pub fn new(vitals: f32) -> Self {\\n        let mut h = Self { vitals, phase: 0.0, bpm: 80.0, since_r: 1.0, period: 0.75, beats: 0, flat: false, ghost: 0.0 };\\n        h.recompute(1.0);\\n        h\\n    }\\n\\n    pub fn recompute(&mut self, coupling: f32) {\\n        let t = (1.0 - self.vitals.clamp(0.0, 100.0) / 100.0).clamp(0.0, 1.0);\\n        let c = coupling.clamp(0.25, 2.0);\\n        self.bpm = (72.0 + (148.0 - 72.0) * t) * c;\\n        self.period = 60.0 / self.bpm.max(40.0);\\n    }\\n\\n    /// Advances the clock. Returns true on an R-wave (world time; a flatline has none).\\n    pub fn tick(&mut self, dt: f32, coupling: f32) -> bool {\\n        self.recompute(coupling);\\n        self.vitals = self.vitals.clamp(0.0, 100.0);\\n        if self.flat {\\n            self.ghost = (self.ghost + dt / self.period).fract();\\n            self.since_r += dt;\\n            return false;\\n        }\\n        self.phase += dt / self.period;\\n        if self.phase >= 1.0 {\\n            self.phase = self.phase.fract();\\n            self.since_r = self.phase * self.period;\\n            self.beats = self.beats.wrapping_add(1);\\n            self.ghost = self.phase;\\n            true\\n        } else {\\n            self.since_r += dt;\\n            self.ghost = self.phase;\\n            false\\n        }\\n    }\\n\\n    pub fn on_beat(&self, window_ms: f32) -> bool {\\n        let w = (window_ms / 1000.0).clamp(0.02, 0.4);\\n        self.since_r <= w || (self.period - self.since_r) <= w\\n    }\\n\\n    /// Diastole: the quiet half, when a tendril can be pulled.\\n    pub fn diastole(&self) -> bool {\\n        self.phase > 0.28 && self.phase < 0.72\\n    }\\n\\n    /// The ghost QRS during a flatline. `ghost` is the phase in 0..1.\\n    pub fn ghost_on_beat(&self, window_ms: f32) -> bool {\\n        let w = (window_ms / 1000.0).clamp(0.02, 0.4);\\n        let g = self.ghost.rem_euclid(1.0);\\n        let since = g * self.period;\\n        let until = (1.0 - g) * self.period;\\n        since <= w || until <= w\\n    }\\n}\\n\",\"total_lines\":72}}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa38-de6f-7dc0-ae0d-e0f717ed75f2","uuid":"6bb6abe4-25bc-4a81-8347-f7846925a369"}
