iles => {\\n                let n = self.focus.min(7) as u8;\\n                cmds.push(Cmd::LoadCase(n));\\n                self.paused = false;\\n                self.screen = Screen::Hud;\\n            }\\n            Screen::Pause => match self.focus {\\n                0 => {\\n                    self.paused = false;\\n                    self.screen = Screen::Hud;\\n                }\\n                1 => cmds.push(Cmd::Retry),\\n                2 => self.screen = Screen::Controls,\\n                3 => self.screen = Screen::Settings,\\n                4 => {\\n                    self.screen = Screen::Dev;\\n                    self.focus = 0;\\n                }\\n                _ => {\\n                    self.paused = false;\\n                    self.screen = Screen::Title;\\n                    cmds.push(Cmd::ToTitle);\\n                }\\n            },\\n            Screen::Dev => {\\n                if self.focus == 0 {\\n                    self.live = !self.live;\\n                } else if self.focus == 1 {\\n                    self.bot_plays = !self.bot_plays;\\n                } else if self.focus >= 6 {\\n                    cmds.push(self.reset_sliders());\\n                }\\n            }\\n            Screen::Settings if self.settings_page == 1 && self.focus == 0 => self.xbox = !self.xbox,\\n            Screen::Dead => cmds.push(Cmd::Retry),\\n            Screen::Story | Screen::Results | Screen::Card => cmds.push(Cmd::ConfirmSim),\\n            Screen::About => self.about_page = (self.about_page + 1) % 5,\\n            _ => {}\\n        }\\n    }\\n\\n    pub fn reset_sliders(&mut self) -> Cmd {\\n        for (i, (_, v, _, _)) in Tune::FIELDS.iter().enumerate() {\\n            self.sliders[i] = *v;\\n        }\\n        self.music = 0.10;\\n        self.effects = 0.80;\\n        self.voices = 0.70;\\n        Cmd::ResetTune\\n    }\\n\\n    pub fn mark_rank(&mut self, case_id: i8, rank: u8) {\\n        if (0..8).contains(&case_id) {\\n            let i = case_id as usize;\\n            if rank > self.best[i] {\\n                self.best[i] = rank;\\n            }\\n        }\\n    }\\n\\n    pub fn open_dev_for_test(&mut self) {\\n        self.paused = true;\\n        self.screen = Screen::Dev;\\n        self.focus = 2;\\n        self.dev_page = 0;\\n    }\\n}\\n\\nfn about_page_title(page: u8) -> &'static str {\\n    match page {\\n        0 => \\\"Credits\\\",\\n        1 => \\\"Source Information\\\",\\n        2 => \\\"Testing Feedback\\\",\\n        3 => \\\"Engine Feedback\\\",\\n        _ => \\\"Prompt Feedback\\\",\\n    }\\n}\\n\\nfn about_lines(page: u8) -> Vec<String> {\\n    let v: serde_json::Value = serde_json::from_str(ABOUT_JSON).unwrap_or(serde_json::json!({}));\\n    match page {\\n        0 => vec![\\n            \\\"Pavilion engine\\\".into(),\\n            \\\"Barlow Condensed, OFL\\\".into(),\\n            \\\"No audio files\\\".into(),\\n        ],\\n        1 => {\\n            let s = &v[\\\"sourceInformation\\\"];\\n            vec![\\n                format!(\\\"Date: {}\\\", s[\\\"date\\\"].as_str().unwrap_or(\\\"\\\")),\\n                format!(\\\"Source: {}\\\", s[\\\"source\\\"].as_str().unwrap_or(\\\"\\\")),\\n                format!(\\\"Plan: {}\\\", s[\\\"plan\\\"].as_str().unwrap_or(\\\"\\\")),\\n                format!(\\\"Genre: {}\\\", s[\\\"genre\\\"].as_str().unwrap_or(\\\"\\\")),\\n                format!(\\\"Perspective: {}\\\", s[\\\"perspective\\\"].as_str().unwrap_or(\\\"\\\")),\\n                format!(\\\"Tech: {}\\\", s[\\\"tech\\\"].as_str().unwrap_or(\\\"\\\")),\\n                format!(\\\"Art Direction: {}\\\", s[\\\"artDirection\\\"].as_str().unwrap_or(\\\"\\\")),\\n                format!(\\\"Animation: {}\\\", s[\\\"animation\\\"].as_str().unwrap_or(\\\"\\\")),\\n\",\"total_lines\":763}}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa38-de6f-7dc0-ae0d-e0f717ed75f2","uuid":"1b1158c6-5320-4169-83b0-99c8d25f3d27"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_230","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"A Dev focus bug exists. Count is 7. Focus 0 toggles live. Focus 1 toggles bot. Focus >= 6 resets.\n\nNudge maps focus < 6 to slider indices dev_page*6+focus. The lines() display uses row(i) for sliders with i 0..6, so focus 0 highlights the first slider. This makes the Dev UI inconsistent: activate toggles Live and Bot, but nudge and lines treat those slots as regular sliders.\n\nThe Dev UI is testable despite the inconsistency. Nudge changes slider values and Reset All restores defaults. The only remaining problem is that focus 0 toggles Live instead of adjusting a slider.\n\nThe Dev test can work by navigating to focus 0, nudging the drain slider, confirming to toggle Live, then moving down to focus 6 to reset. The plan itself is internally inconsistent: it claims 7 focus slots but lists 9 items (Live, Bot, 6 sliders, Reset All).\n\nI will leave the shell logic unchanged unless tests fail. I am fixing lines() so focus 0 highlights Live, focus 1 highlights Bot, and focus 6 highlights Reset All.\n\nThe 7-slot count conflicts with the plan's \"live balance sliders.\" I will expand the Dev focus count to 9: slots 0 through 1 for Live and Bot, 2 through 7 for six sliders, and 8 for Reset All. This aligns the display rows with the nudge indices.\n\nThe nudge formula is now `dev_page * 6 + (focus - 2)`. The test helper sets focus to 2 so the first slider is ready. Hud back navigation is safe: `back()` already opens Pause, so the later check does nothing and focus is not reset twice.\n\nTitle confirm navigates to Menu. Attract mode returns to Title on any input and loads attract after ten seconds of idle time. Touch-only title input opens Settings without allowing further interaction. Settings page 0 nudge emits SetBus, and Reset restores music volume to 0.10. The About page needs a usage field in about.json.\n\nI will verify about.json exists and is valid. The Dev focus bug will be fixed after writing audio but before compiling. Mode 2 is mapped to Story, yet the plan treats Chart as a separate screen; I will check if tests require a dedicated Chart display. The verification requires testing every screen from the title's initial state with pad, keyboard, and mouse.\n\nThe full screen list is now identified. Most screens can be driven without the simulation. Chart may be reachable via note_mode(2), but it likely maps to Story, so a separate Chart screen might not be needed. I will add serde_json to pav_ui and fix the font issue before compiling.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-bedbe949-4bf3-4e61-a02c-faf0fa72e608-39","name":"grep","input":{"pattern":"^pub const (K_|FORCEPS|LASER|CRYO|DEFIB|TOOL_)","path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224015__x42677a/work/engine-link/crates/pav_core/src/games/surgery/kinds.rs"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-bedbe949-4bf3-4e61-a02c-faf0fa72e608-40","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224015__x42677a/work/engine-link/crates/pav_ui/src/surgery/about.json","limit":40}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2812,"output_tokens":1964,"cache_read_input_tokens":72576,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa38-de6f-7dc0-ae0d-e0f717ed75f2","uuid":"1f15e8ee-fe40-41de-9280-a5c769daf765"}
