pub const FORCEPS: u8 = 1;\"},{\"line_number\":9,\"content\":\"pub const LASER: u8 = 4;\"},{\"line_number\":13,\"content\":\"pub const CRYO: u8 = 8;\"},{\"line_number\":15,\"content\":\"pub const DEFIB: u8 = 10;\"},{\"line_number\":16,\"content\":\"pub const TOOL_KEEP: u8 = 255;\"},{\"line_number\":18,\"content\":\"pub const TOOL_NAMES: [&str; 11] =\"},{\"line_number\":23,\"content\":\"pub const K_INCISION: u8 = 0;\"},{\"line_number\":24,\"content\":\"pub const K_LACERATION: u8 = 1;\"},{\"line_number\":25,\"content\":\"pub const K_POOL: u8 = 2;\"},{\"line_number\":26,\"content\":\"pub const K_BLEEDER: u8 = 3;\"},{\"line_number\":27,\"content\":\"pub const K_FOREIGN: u8 = 4;\"},{\"line_number\":28,\"content\":\"pub const K_POLYP: u8 = 5;\"},{\"line_number\":29,\"content\":\"pub const K_TUMOR: u8 = 6;\"},{\"line_number\":30,\"content\":\"pub const K_INFLAM: u8 = 7;\"},{\"line_number\":31,\"content\":\"pub const K_BONE: u8 = 8;\"},{\"line_number\":32,\"content\":\"pub const K_NODULE: u8 = 9;\"},{\"line_number\":33,\"content\":\"pub const K_SAC: u8 = 10;\"},{\"line_number\":34,\"content\":\"pub const K_EYE: u8 = 11;\"},{\"line_number\":35,\"content\":\"pub const K_EMBER: u8 = 12;\"},{\"line_number\":36,\"content\":\"pub const K_HEAT: u8 = 13;\"},{\"line_number\":37,\"content\":\"pub const K_TETHER: u8 = 14;\"},{\"line_number\":38,\"content\":\"pub const K_TENDRIL: u8 = 15;\"},{\"line_number\":39,\"content\":\"pub const K_DRESSING: u8 = 16;\"},{\"line_number\":40,\"content\":\"pub const K_IV: u8 = 17;\"},{\"line_number\":41,\"content\":\"pub const K_BURN: u8 = 18;\"}]}]}","is_error":false},{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-bedbe949-4bf3-4e61-a02c-faf0fa72e608-40","content":"{\"type\":\"ReadFile\",\"FileContent\":{\"content\":\"1→{\\n  \\\"sourceInformation\\\": {\\n    \\\"date\\\": \\\"2026-11-04 22:40:15\\\",\\n    \\\"source\\\": \\\"Trauma Center: Second Opinion\\\",\\n    \\\"plan\\\": \\\"PLAN.md\\\",\\n    \\\"genre\\\": \\\"Simulation\\\",\\n    \\\"perspective\\\": \\\"Fixed overhead view of the operative field\\\",\\n    \\\"tech\\\": \\\"Pavilion engine (Shardfall commit 49ef2ba), Rust 1.98.1, wgpu/WebGPU, wasm-bindgen 0.2.129, egui 0.36.2\\\",\\n    \\\"artDirection\\\": \\\"Cel-shaded overhead operative field painted per vertex, with layered paper-theatre cards for story\\\",\\n10→    \\\"animation\\\": \\\"Simulation-driven tissue, instruments, heartbeat, and paper-card motion\\\",\\n    \\\"audio\\\": \\\"Synthesized music, effects, and short gibberish voices. No audio files. Music bus defaults to 0.10\\\",\\n    \\\"online\\\": \\\"Optional AI Hub shared-world Code Blue for 1-4 surgeons\\\",\\n    \\\"testing\\\": \\\"Deterministic sim suite, headless shell, Chromium file:// launches, hub harness\\\",\\n    \\\"research\\\": \\\"Engine seams and the hub protocol, recorded in PLAN.md\\\",\\n    \\\"environment\\\": \\\"Grok CLI (headless); Linux\\\",\\n    \\\"model\\\": \\\"xAI, grok-4.7, reasoning effort xhigh\\\",\\n    \\\"usage\\\": \\\"added on import\\\"\\n  },\\n  \\\"testingFeedback\\\": [\\n20→    \\\"Testing caught three rule bugs: a Rust or-pattern guard skipped stage-0 sutures, nearest-hazard selection stole forceps pulls, and a sac's swell shared the laser charge meter.\\\",\\n    \\\"3\\\",\\n    \\\"The most helpful test was a skill-1.0 bot playing every case, Code Blue, and the campaign from a fresh scene.\\\",\\n    \\\"The least helpful test was a temporary print probe that only dumped stuck hazards and was removed once the selection bug was fixed.\\\"\\n  ],\\n  \\\"engineFeedback\\\": [\\n    \\\"The Game hook, recorded input, RenderFrame, headless egui, and the single-file packer.\\\",\\n    \\\"Yes. A colon in the project path makes rustc fail joining LD_LIBRARY_PATH, and the demo frame path captures the camera, pause menu, and touch layer unless a game returns first.\\\",\\n    \\\"The operative rules, the plate mesh, the ten-foot shell, the cue and music buses, and the hub shim.\\\",\\n    \\\"Keeping a surgery scene off the demo boot panel, stats, guide, toasts, and the engine pause menu.\\\",\\n30→    \\\"Added the surgery frame, surgeon input, and cue event; a view emit and camera shot; a product frame branch; audio buses and formants; session.js injection in the packer; and js-sys. The hook alone cannot draw, play cues, or join a hub.\\\",\\n    \\\"A first-class per-game frame path, so a new game does not have to outrun the demo loop.\\\"\\n  ],\\n  \\\"promptFeedback\\\": [\\n    \\\"The tested camera, light, and palette numbers, and a hub shim that the harness had already accepted.\\\",\\n    \\\"The deliverable folder name must contain a colon, which Cargo cannot use as its working directory.\\\",\\n    \\\"Shipping one packed page that is the full game, a hub client, and a file:// WebGPU build.\\\",\\n    \\\"Say at the start that the Cargo target directory cannot contain a colon.\\\"\\n  ],\\n  \\\"aiHub\\\": {\\n40→    \\\"name\\\": \\\"Hands of Harbor: Second Opinion\\\",\",\"content_concise\":\"1→{\\n  \\\"sourceInformation\\\": {\\n    \\\"date\\\": \\\"2026-11-04 22:40:15\\\",\\n    \\\"source\\\": \\\"Trauma Center: Second Opinion\\\",\\n    \\\"plan\\\": \\\"PLAN.md\\\",\\n    \\\"genre\\\": \\\"Simulation\\\",\\n    \\\"perspective\\\": \\\"Fixed overhead view of the operative field\\\",\\n    \\\"tech\\\": \\\"Pavilion engine (Shardfall commit 49ef2ba), Rust 1.98.1, wgpu/WebGPU, wasm-bindgen 0.2.129, egui 0.36.2\\\",\\n    \\\"artDirection\\\": \\\"Cel-shaded overhead operative field painted per vertex, with layered paper-theatre cards for story\\\",\\n10→    \\\"animation\\\": \\\"Simulation-driven tissue, instruments, heartbeat, and paper-card motion\\\",\\n    \\\"audio\\\": \\\"Synthesized music, effects, and short gibberish voices. No audio files. Music bus defaults to 0.10\\\",\\n    \\\"online\\\": \\\"Optional AI Hub shared-world Code Blue for 1-4 surgeons\\\",\\n    \\\"testing\\\": \\\"Deterministic sim suite, headless shell, Chromium file:// launches, hub harness\\\",\\n    \\\"research\\\": \\\"Engine seams and the hub protocol, recorded in PLAN.md\\\",\\n    \\\"environment\\\": \\\"Grok CLI (headless); Linux\\\",\\n    \\\"model\\\": \\\"xAI, grok-4.7, reasoning effort xhigh\\\",\\n    \\\"usage\\\": \\\"added on import\\\"\\n  },\\n  \\\"testingFeedback\\\": [\\n20→    \\\"Testing caught three rule bugs: a Rust or-pattern guard skipped stage-0 sutures, nearest-hazard selection stole forceps pulls, and a sac's swell shared the laser charge meter.\\\",\\n    \\\"3\\\",\\n    \\\"The most helpful test was a skill-1.0 bot playing every case, Code Blue, and the campaign from a fresh scene.\\\",\\n    \\\"The least helpful test was a temporary print probe that only dumped stuck hazards and was removed once the selection bug was fixed.\\\"\\n  ],\\n  \\\"engineFeedback\\\": [\\n    \\\"The Game hook, recorded input, RenderFrame, headless egui, and the single-file packer.\\\",\\n    \\\"Yes. A colon in the project path makes rustc fail joining LD_LIBRARY_PATH, and the demo frame path captures the camera, pause menu, and touch layer unless a game returns first.\\\",\\n    \\\"The operative rules, the plate mesh, the ten-foot shell, the cue and music buses, and the hub shim.\\\",\\n    \\\"Keeping a surgery scene off the demo boot panel, stats, guide, toasts, and the engine pause menu.\\\",\\n30→    \\\"Added the surgery frame, surgeon input, and cue event; a view emit and camera shot; a product frame branch; audio buses and formants; session.js injection in the packer; and js-sys. The hook alone cannot draw, play cues, or join a hub.\\\",\\n    \\\"A first-class per-game frame path, so a new game does not have to outrun the demo loop.\\\"\\n  ],\\n  \\\"promptFeedback\\\": [\\n    \\\"The tested camera, light, and palette numbers, and a hub shim that the harness had already accepted.\\\",\\n    \\\"The deliverable folder name must contain a colon, which Cargo cannot use as its working directory.\\\",\\n    \\\"Shipping one packed page that is the full game, a hub client, and a file:// WebGPU build.\\\",\\n    \\\"Say at the start that the Cargo target directory cannot contain a colon.\\\"\\n  ],\\n  \\\"aiHub\\\": {\\n40→    \\\"name\\\": \\\"Hands of Harbor: Second Opinion\\\",\",\"absolute_path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224015__x42677a/work/Hands of Harbor: Second Opinion-Trauma Center: Second Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-224015/engine/crates/pav_ui/src/surgery/about.json\",\"offset\":null,\"limit\":40,\"raw_output\":\"{\\n  \\\"sourceInformation\\\": {\\n    \\\"date\\\": \\\"2026-11-04 22:40:15\\\",\\n    \\\"source\\\": \\\"Trauma Center: Second Opinion\\\",\\n    \\\"plan\\\": \\\"PLAN.md\\\",\\n    \\\"genre\\\": \\\"Simulation\\\",\\n    \\\"perspective\\\": \\\"Fixed overhead view of the operative field\\\",\\n    \\\"tech\\\": \\\"Pavilion engine (Shardfall commit 49ef2ba), Rust 1.98.1, wgpu/WebGPU, wasm-bindgen 0.2.129, egui 0.36.2\\\",\\n    \\\"artDirection\\\": \\\"Cel-shaded overhead operative field painted per vertex, with layered paper-theatre cards for story\\\",\\n    \\\"animation\\\": \\\"Simulation-driven tissue, instruments, heartbeat, and paper-card motion\\\",\\n    \\\"audio\\\": \\\"Synthesized music, effects, and short gibberish voices. No audio files. Music bus defaults to 0.10\\\",\\n    \\\"online\\\": \\\"Optional AI Hub shared-world Code Blue for 1-4 surgeons\\\",\\n    \\\"testing\\\": \\\"Deterministic sim suite, headless shell, Chromium file:// launches, hub harness\\\",\\n    \\\"research\\\": \\\"Engine seams and the hub protocol, recorded in PLAN.md\\\",\\n    \\\"environment\\\": \\\"Grok CLI (headless); Linux\\\",\\n    \\\"model\\\": \\\"xAI, grok-4.7, reasoning effort xhigh\\\",\\n    \\\"usage\\\": \\\"added on import\\\"\\n  },\\n  \\\"testingFeedback\\\": [\\n    \\\"Testing caught three rule bugs: a Rust or-pattern guard skipped stage-0 sutures, nearest-hazard selection stole forceps pulls, and a sac's swell shared the laser charge meter.\\\",\\n    \\\"3\\\",\\n    \\\"The most helpful test was a skill-1.0 bot playing every case, Code Blue, and the campaign from a fresh scene.\\\",\\n    \\\"The least helpful test was a temporary print probe that only dumped stuck hazards and was removed once the selection bug was fixed.\\\"\\n  ],\\n  \\\"engineFeedback\\\": [\\n    \\\"The Game hook, recorded input, RenderFrame, headless egui, and the single-file packer.\\\",\\n    \\\"Yes. A colon in the project path makes rustc fail joining LD_LIBRARY_PATH, and the demo frame path captures the camera, pause menu, and touch layer unless a game returns first.\\\",\\n    \\\"The operative rules, the plate mesh, the ten-foot shell, the cue and music buses, and the hub shim.\\\",\\n    \\\"Keeping a surgery scene off the demo boot panel, stats, guide, toasts, and the engine pause menu.\\\",\\n    \\\"Added the surgery frame, surgeon input, and cue event; a view emit and camera shot; a product frame branch; audio buses and formants; session.js injection in the packer; and js-sys. The hook alone cannot draw, play cues, or join a hub.\\\",\\n    \\\"A first-class per-game frame path, so a new game does not have to outrun the demo loop.\\\"\\n  ],\\n  \\\"promptFeedback\\\": [\\n    \\\"The tested camera, light, and palette numbers, and a hub shim that the harness had already accepted.\\\",\\n    \\\"The deliverable folder name must contain a colon, which Cargo cannot use as its working directory.\\\",\\n    \\\"Shipping one packed page that is the full game, a hub client, and a file:// WebGPU build.\\\",\\n    \\\"Say at the start that the Cargo target directory cannot contain a colon.\\\"\\n  ],\\n  \\\"aiHub\\\": {\\n    \\\"name\\\": \\\"Hands of Harbor: Second Opinion\\\",\\n\",\"total_lines\":51}}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa38-de6f-7dc0-ae0d-e0f717ed75f2","uuid":"7ee41963-c186-44d2-b4e3-deed