{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_238","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The clock copies InputFrame but fails to clear surgery_cmd.\n\nThe clock never clears surgeon pressed bits. I will make `apply_cmd` public and use it via `host.exec` for one-shot commands. Surgeon inputs go into shared.input each frame, and `surgery_cmd` must be cleared after copying edges.\n\nThe sim thread may tick up to eight times per frame. Setting `pressed` once at the start of a frame could let multiple ticks see it. The app must clear `pressed` before the next tick or risk repeated input.\n\nThe clock only clears top-level pressed bits, not surgeon[].pressed. On wasm, pump() runs inside frame(), so all eight ticks in a single frame see the same pressed input. A confirm would advance the story eight times per frame. The correct engine fix is to clear surgeon pressed bits inside the sim after consuming them.\n\nTests step the sim directly with fresh InputFrames each call, so they are unaffected. Replay is also safe because it uses recorded input per tick. The fix belongs in the live app clock: `tick_once` will clear `i.pressed` and `i.surgery_cmd` after copying.\n\nThe copied frame retains pressed bits. The clock should clear `surgery_cmd` and each surgeon's `pressed` immediately after the copy, before the next tick consumes them.\n\nThe clock will zero `i.pressed`, `i.surgery_cmd`, and each surgeon's `pressed` immediately after copying the frame. This prevents stuck commands from looping on both native and wasm. `command()` will be made public as `apply_cmd`.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-60a33814-4bc5-49f6-94b4-91fae53dc245-69","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224015__x42677a/work/engine-link/crates/pav_core/src/input.rs","offset":49,"limit":120}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-60a33814-4bc5-49f6-94b4-91fae53dc245-70","name":"grep","input":{"pattern":"fn boot_attract|fn boot_campaign|fn boot_code|fn boot_single|M_TITLE|fn mode_name|pub music|tune\\.music","path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224015__x42677a/work/engine-link/crates/pav_core/src/games/surgery"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-60a33814-4bc5-49f6-94b4-91fae53dc245-71","name":"grep","input":{"pattern":"pub fn play_event|pub fn play_bus|pub fn set_buses|fn drain_events|SimEvent::Cue","path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224015__x42677a/work/engine-link/crates/pav_audio/src/lib.rs"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-60a33814-4bc5-49f6-94b4-91fae53dc245-72","name":"grep","input":{"pattern":"events\\.lock|drain_events|play_event","path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224015__x42677a/work/engine-link/crates/pav_app/src"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":4672,"output_tokens":1272,"cache_read_input_tokens":100352,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa38-de6f-7dc0-ae0d-e0f717ed75f2","uuid":"00937729-2367-4128-bc89-6ce61955639a"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-60a33814-4bc5-49f6-94b4-91fae53dc245-69","content":"{\"type\":\"ReadFile\",\"FileContent\":{\"content\":\"49→pub struct InputFrame {\\n50→    /// Desired movement on the ground plane: x = world +X, y = world +Z. Length <= 1.\\n    pub move_dir: Vec2,\\n    /// Vertical intent for climbing/flying/swimming (-1..1).\\n    #[serde(default)]\\n    pub vertical: f32,\\n    /// World-space aim point (mouse on the ground plane, or stick projection).\\n    #[serde(default)]\\n    pub aim: Option<Vec3>,\\n    /// Buttons held this tick.\\n    #[serde(default)]\\n60→    pub held: u32,\\n    /// Buttons that went down since the previous tick (never lost, even for short taps).\\n    #[serde(default)]\\n    pub pressed: u32,\\n    /// A menu action this tick (Shardfall: equip, sell, travel...), queued one per tick.\\n    #[serde(default, skip_serializing_if = \\\"Option::is_none\\\")]\\n    pub cmd: Option<crate::arpg::GameCmd>,\\n    /// Up to four local surgeons. Recorded with the tick, so replays include them.\\n    #[serde(default)]\\n    pub surgeons: [SurgeonInput; 4],\\n70→    /// A surgery-shell command (load a case, retry, set a slider). Ignored by other games.\\n    #[serde(default, skip_serializing_if = \\\"Option::is_none\\\")]\\n    pub surgery_cmd: Option<SurgeryCmd>,\\n}\\n\\n/// One surgeon's hands for a tick. `aim` is a world point when `AIM_ABSOLUTE` is set, otherwise\\n/// a stick in -1..1. `tool` 255 means \\\"leave the current tool\\\".\\n#[derive(Clone, Copy, Debug, Default, PartialEq, Serialize, Deserialize)]\\npub struct SurgeonInput {\\n    pub active: bool,\\n80→    pub aim: Vec2,\\n    pub held: u32,\\n    pub pressed: u32,\\n    pub tool: u8,\\n    pub pressure: f32,\\n}\\n\\npub mod surg {\\n    pub const USE: u32 = 1 << 0;\\n    pub const PRECISION: u32 = 1 << 1;\\n90→    pub const CANCEL: u32 = 1 << 2;\\n    pub const GIFT: u32 = 1 << 3;\\n    pub const CHART: u32 = 1 << 4;\\n    pub const DEFIB: u32 = 1 << 5;\\n    pub const AIM_ABSOLUTE: u32 = 1 << 6;\\n    /// Mouse: put the cursor on `aim` this tick. The stick and the bot slew instead.\\n    pub const SNAP: u32 = 1 << 7;\\n    pub const ROT_L: u32 = 1 << 8;\\n    pub const ROT_R: u32 = 1 << 9;\\n    pub const CONFIRM: u32 = 1 << 10;\\n100→    pub const BACK: u32 = 1 << 11;\\n    pub const NAV_UP: u32 = 1 << 12;\\n    pub const NAV_DOWN: u32 = 1 << 13;\\n}\\n\\n/// Commands from the surgery shell. Copy, so they ride in a recorded `InputFrame`.\\n#[derive(Clone, Copy, Debug, PartialEq, Serialize, Deserialize)]\\npub enum SurgeryCmd {\\n    Retry,\\n    Skip,\\n110→    SetTune { id: u8, value: f32 },\\n    ResetTune,\\n    LoadCase(u8),\\n    LoadCampaign,\\n    LoadCode,\\n    SetDifficulty(u8),\\n    /// 0 immortal, 1 freeze timer, 2 full gift, 3 one-hit, 4 force code, 5 kill, 6 win, 7 jump phase.\\n    Dev { what: u8, extra: u8 },\\n    SpawnHazard(u8),\\n}\\n120→\\nimpl InputFrame {\\n    pub fn down(&self, b: u32) -> bool {\\n        self.held & b != 0\\n    }\\n    pub fn just(&self, b: u32) -> bool {\\n        self.pressed & b != 0\\n    }\\n}\\n\",\"content_concise\":\"49→pub struct InputFrame {\\n50→    /// Desired movement on the ground plane: x = world +X, y = world +Z. Length <= 1.\\n    pub move_dir: Vec2,\\n    /// Vertical intent for climbing/flying/swimming (-1..1).\\n    #[serde(default)]\\n    pub vertical: f32,\\n    /// World-space aim point (mouse on the ground plane, or stick projection).\\n    #[serde(default)]\\n    pub aim: Option<Vec3>,\\n    /// Buttons held this tick.\\n    #[serde(default)]\\n60→    pub held: u32,\\n    /// Buttons that went down since the previous tick (never lost, even for short taps).\\n    #[serde(default)]\\n    pub pressed: u32,\\n    /// A menu action this tick (Shardfall: equip, sell, travel...), queued one per tick.\\n    #[serde(default, skip_serializing_if = \\\"Option::is_none\\\")]\\n    pub cmd: Option<crate::arpg::GameCmd>,\\n    /// Up to four local surgeons. Recorded with the tick, so replays include them.\\n    #[serde(default)]\\n    pub surgeons: [SurgeonInput; 4],\\n70→    /// A surgery-shell command (load a case, retry, set a slider). Ignored by other games.\\n    #[serde(default, skip_serializing_if = \\\"Option::is_none\\\")]\\n    pub surgery_cmd: Option<SurgeryCmd>,\\n}\\n\\n/// One surgeon's hands for a tick. `aim` is a world point when `AIM_ABSOLUTE` is set, otherwise\\n/// a stick in -1..1. `tool` 255 means \\\"leave the current tool\\\".\\n#[derive(Clone, Copy, Debug, Default, PartialEq, Serialize, Deserialize)]\\npub struct SurgeonInput {\\n    pub active: bool,\\n80→    pub aim: Vec2,\\n    pub held: u32,\\n    pub pressed: u32,\\n    pub tool: u8,\\n    pub pressure: f32,\\n}\\n\\npub mod surg {\\n    pub const USE: u32 = 1 << 0;\\n    pub const PRECISION: u32 = 1 << 1;\\n90→    pub const CANCEL: u32 = 1 << 2;\\n    pub const GIFT: u32 = 1 << 3;\\n    pub const CHART: u32 = 1 << 4;\\n    pub const DEFIB: u32 = 1 << 5;\\n    pub const AIM_ABSOLUTE: u32 = 1 << 6;\\n    /// Mouse: put the cursor on `aim` this tick. The stick and the bot slew instead.\\n    pub const SNAP: u32 = 1 << 7;\\n    pub const ROT_L: u32 = 1 << 8;\\n    pub const ROT_R: u32 = 1 << 9;\\n    pub const CONFIRM: u32 = 1 << 10;\\n100→    pub const BACK: u32 = 1 << 11;\\n    pub const NAV_UP: u32 = 1 << 12;\\n    pub const NAV_DOWN: u32 = 1 << 13;\\n}\\n\\n/// Commands from the surgery shell. Copy, so they ride in a recorded `InputFrame`.\\n#[derive(Clone, Copy, Debug, PartialEq, Serialize, Deserialize)]\\npub enum SurgeryCmd {\\n    Retry,\\n    Skip,\\n110→    SetTune { id: u8, value: f32 },\\n    ResetTune,\\n    LoadCase(u8),\\n    LoadCampaign,\\n    LoadCode,\\n    SetDifficulty(u8),\\n    /// 0 immortal, 1 freeze timer, 2 full gift, 3 one-hit, 4 force code, 5 kill, 6 win, 7 jump phase.\\n    Dev { what: u8, extra: u8 },\\n    SpawnHazard(u8),\\n}\\n120→\\nimpl InputFrame {\\n    pub fn down(&self, b: u32) -> bool {\\n        self.held & b != 0\\n    }\\n    pub fn just(&self, b: u32) -> bool {\\n        self.pressed & b != 0\\n    }\\n}\\n\",\"absolute_path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224015__x42677a/work/Hands of Harbor: Second Opinion-Trauma Center: Second Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-224015/engine/crates/pav_core/src/input.rs\",\"offset\":49,\"limit\":120,\"raw_output\":\"pub struct InputFrame {\\n    /// Desired movement on the ground plane: x = world +X, y = world +Z. Length <= 1.\\n    pub move_dir: Vec2,\\n    /// Vertical intent for climbing/flying/swimming (-1..1).\\n    #[serde(default)]\\n    pub vertical: f32,\\n    /// World-space aim point (mouse on the ground plane, or stick projection).\\n    #[serde(default)]\\n    pub aim: Option<Vec3>,\\n    /// Buttons held this tick.\\n    #[serde(default)]\\n    pub held: u32,\\n    /// Buttons that went down since the previous tick (never lost, even for short taps).\\n    #[serde(default)]\\n    pub pressed: u32,\\n    /// A menu action this tick (Shardfall: equip, sell, travel...), queued one per tick.\\n    #[serde(default, skip_serializing_if = \\\"Option::is_none\\\")]\\n    pub cmd: Option<crate::arpg::GameCmd>,\\n    /// Up to four local surgeons. Recorded with the tick, so replays include them.\\n    #[serde(default)]\\n    pub surgeons: [SurgeonInput; 4],\\n    /// A surgery-shell command (load a case, retry, set a slider). Ignored by other games.\\n    #[serde(default, skip_serializing_if = \\\"Option::is_none\\\")]\\n    pub surgery_cmd: Option<SurgeryCmd>,\\n}\\n\\n/// One surgeon's hands for a tick. `aim` is a world point when `AIM_ABSOLUTE` is set, otherwise\\n/// a stick in -1..1. `tool` 255 means \\\"leave the current tool\\\".\\n#[derive(Clone, Copy, Debug, Default, PartialEq, Serialize, Deserialize)]\\npub struct SurgeonInput {\\n    pub active: bool,\\n    pub aim: Vec2,\\n    pub held: u32,\\n    pub pressed: u32,\\n    pub tool: u8,\\n    pub pressure: f32,\\n}\\n\\npub mod surg {\\n    pub const USE: u32 = 1 << 0;\\n    pub const PRECISION: u32 = 1 << 1;\\n    pub const CANCEL: u32 = 1 << 2;\\n    pub const GIFT: u32 = 1 << 3;\\n    pub const CHART: u32 = 1 << 4;\\n    pub const DEFIB: u32 = 1 << 5;\\n    pub const AIM_ABSOLUTE: u32 = 1 << 6;\\n    /// Mouse: put the cursor on `aim` this tick. The stick and the bot slew instead.\\n    pub const SNAP: u32 = 1 << 7;\\n    pub const ROT_L: u32 = 1 << 8;\\n    pub const ROT_R: u32 = 1 << 9;\\n    pub const CONFIRM: u32 = 1 << 10;\\n    pub const BACK: u32 = 1 << 11;\\n    pub const NAV_UP: u32 = 1 << 12;\\n    pub const NAV_DOWN: u32 = 1 << 13;\\n}\\n\\n/// Commands from the surgery shell. Copy, so they ride in a recorded `InputFrame`.\\n#[derive(Clone, Copy, Debug, PartialEq, Serialize, Deserialize)]\\npub enum SurgeryCmd {\\n    Retry,\\n    Skip,\\n    SetTune { id: u8, value: f32 },\\n    ResetTune,\\n    LoadCase(u8),\\n    LoadCampaign,\\n    LoadCode,\\n    SetDifficulty(u8),\\n    /// 0 immortal, 1 freeze timer, 2 full gift, 3 one-hit, 4 force code, 5 kill, 6 win, 7 jump phase.\\n    Dev { what: u8, extra: u8 },\\n    SpawnHazard(u8),\\n}\\n\\nimpl InputFrame {\\n    pub fn down(&self, b: u32) -> bool {\\n        self.held & b != 0\\n    }\\n    pub fn just(&self, b: u32) -> bool {\\n        self.pressed & b != 0\\n    }\\n}\\n\",\"total_lines\":128}}","is_error":false},{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-60a33814-4bc5-49f6-94b4-91fae53dc245-70","content":"{\"type\":\"GrepSearch\",\"stdout\":[60,119,111,114,107,115,112,97,99,101,95,114,101,115,117,108,116,32,119,111,114,107,115,112,97,99,101,95,112,97,116,104,61,34,47,104,111,109,101,47,109,105,99,104,97,47,100,101,118,47,99,99,45,109,97,116,114,105,120,47,114,117,110,115,47,103,114,111,107,45,120,104,105,103,104,46,98,117,105,108,100,45,118,50,95,95,50,48,50,54,49,49,48,52,45,50,50,52,48,49,53,95,95,120,52,50,54,55,55,97,47,119,111,114,107,34,62,10,70,111,117,110,100,32,49,