umber\":178,\"content\":\"                crate::game_lines(&ctx, hud_lines);\"}]}]}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa38-de6f-7dc0-ae0d-e0f717ed75f2","uuid":"e543e5bc-fa07-4378-8ae8-c5b2f2c0d686"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_244","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The audio test passed.\n\nChecking pav_view and pav_ui compilation next. Will write the sim API and product while compiling. pub use will silence dead_code warnings. Reviewing session.rs for UI state, camera sync, headless frames, and RenderFrame.surgery population. Planning to poll four gamepads via gilrs GamepadId and use KeyCode for keyboard tools 1-8.\n\nThe product window_event path will route surgery events to `product::surgery_event` and `product::surgery_frame` instead of calling `handle_key`. Touch input in surgery mode will set touch_only and skip gameplay.\n\nTouch on the title will record as a device touch and a click to open settings. Close, resize, and redraw events will route to frame. Keyboard input will be stored in Harbor without calling handle_key or zooming. Mouse position and buttons will be recorded while right-drag camera is disabled. Engine shortcuts will be skipped. surgery_frame will exit early if gfx or host is missing.\n\nGamepad input will be polled directly via gilrs to avoid triggering engine shortcuts like start-to-menu. Events will be drained in product code. The frame pipeline will build shell input from keys, mouse, and pads, step the shell, apply commands through host.exec, write surgeon input, clear shared edges via clock, pump the loop, build the scene, run egui shell, draw, play audio cues and music, manage cursor visibility, and set __game status. Wasm __game setup will happen once.\n\nAdding js-sys to the workspace dependencies. The plan is to expose window.__game as a JS object whose status() method reads a Rust-updated string each frame, using a wasm_bindgen Closure with an Rc<RefCell<String>> to hold the current status.\n\nThe `__game` object will expose `status()` and `step(n)` closures. `step(n)` must advance the simulation immediately, but reaching `SimHost` from a static closure is difficult on wasm. The product code will store a hook to handle this. The harness launch test expects input to change focus, suggesting `__game` is meant for the test driver.\n\nThe `__game` object will expose `status`, `step`, and `do` methods. `status` must return JSON containing the music value as text \"0.10\". On wasm, `SimHost` is nested inside `App`, so `step` and `do` will need a hook to reach the simulation.\n\nSince App is owned by winit, closures cannot directly reach the simulation. The plan is to use static Mutexes for status, pending commands, and step count that surgery_frame will read and update each frame. On wasm, a simple thread-local or RefCell in a lazy static may be safer than std::sync::Mutex.\n\nstd::sync::Mutex is confirmed to work on wasm32-unknown-unknown because simhost already uses it. The step(n) hook will increment a STEP counter so the simulation advances immediately rather than waiting for the next frame.\n\nSimHost::exec is synchronous on wasm, but pump advances by elapsed time rather than a fixed tick count. Adding a `step_n` method to SimHost would still be unreachable from the static closure. The test only requires `__game.status()` to exist and report music 0.10; it does not require `__game.step`.\n\nA thread-local pointer to SimHost will let the `step` and `do` hooks reach the simulation immediately during a JavaScript call. The host is stable inside App until drop, so this is safe.\n\nThe `__game` object will queue commands for the next frame, but if the thread-local SimHost hook is set it will run them immediately. The status string will be updated each frame. Next I need to examine `Sim::step` and its time delta.\n\n`SimHost::burst(n)` will be added only on wasm. It loops `n` times calling `sim.step` with the shared input and publishing each result. The thread-local SimHost hook will be set inside `surgery_frame` each frame.\n\nThe `do(json)` method will accept a JSON object with keys for confirm, back, up, down, aim, tool, and load. The egui draw signature is confirmed as `pub fn draw(ui: &egui::Ui, ...)`. The font will be installed once. `pixels_per_point` will be set to `height / 1080` so the shell is exactly 1080 points tall; egui mouse coordinates are in points.\n\nShell hit-test coordinates map cleanly to a 1920×1080 space when pixels_per_point equals 1. The zoom_factor must be set so that points height equals 1080, using the window’s native scale factor.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-64e691d5-85d0-4b74-912a-2f1c5d4ce5ef-92","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224015__x42677a/work/engine-link/crates/pav_app/src/uiinput.rs","offset":38,"limit":180}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-64e691d5-85d0-4b74-912a-2f1c5d4ce5ef-93","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224015__x42677a/work/engine-link/crates/pav_tools/src/session.rs","offset":400,"limit":80}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-64e691d5-85d0-4b74-912a-2f1c5d4ce5ef-94","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224015__x42677a/work/engine-link/crates/pav_ui/src/headless.rs","offset":100,"limit":90}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-64e691d5-85d0-4b74-912a-2f1c5d4ce5ef-95","name":"grep","input":{"pattern":"surgery:","path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224015__x42677a/work/engine-link/crates/pav_core/src/frame.rs"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2836,"output_tokens":2561,"cache_read_input_tokens":123776,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa38-de6f-7dc0-ae0d-e0f717ed75f2","uuid":"e611dcae-2ad5-4727-90e6-04d1020f0466"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-64e691d5-85d0-4b74-912a-2f1c5d4ce5ef-92","content":"{\"type\":\"ReadFile\",\"FileContent\":{\"content\":\"38→pub struct UiInput {\\n    ctx: egui::Context,\\n40→    raw: egui::RawInput,\\n    pointer: egui::Pos2,\\n    modifiers: egui::Modifiers,\\n    start: web_time::Instant,\\n    max_texture: usize,\\n    cursor: egui::CursorIcon,\\n    /// The finger that is egui's pointer (the first one down).\\n    touch_pointer: Option<u64>,\\n}\\n\\n50→#[cfg(target_arch = \\\"wasm32\\\")]\\nimpl UiInput {\\n    pub fn new(ctx: &egui::Context, _window: &Window, max_texture: usize) -> Self {\\n        Self {\\n            ctx: ctx.clone(),\\n            raw: egui::RawInput::default(),\\n            pointer: egui::Pos2::ZERO,\\n            modifiers: egui::Modifiers::default(),\\n            start: web_time::Instant::now(),\\n            max_texture,\\n60→            cursor: egui::CursorIcon::Default,\\n            touch_pointer: None,\\n        }\\n    }\\n\\n    fn ppp(&self, window: &Window) -> f32 {\\n        self.ctx.zoom_factor() * window.scale_factor() as f32\\n    }\\n\\n    pub fn on_window_event(&mut self, window: &Window, event: &WindowEvent) -> bool {\\n70→        use egui::Event;\\n        use winit::event::{MouseButton, MouseScrollDelta};\\n        let ppp = self.ppp(window);\\n        let over_ui = |c: &egui::Context| c.egui_wants_pointer_input() || c.is_pointer_over_egui();\\n        let ev = &mut self.raw.events;\\n        match event {\\n            WindowEvent::CursorMoved { position, .. } => {\\n                self.pointer = egui::pos2(position.x as f32 / ppp, position.y as f32 / ppp);\\n                ev.push(Event::PointerMoved(self.pointer));\\n                over_ui(&self.ctx)\\n80→            }\\n            WindowEvent::CursorLeft { .. } => {\\n                ev.push(Event::PointerGone);\\n                false\\n            }\\n            WindowEvent::MouseInput { state, button, .. } => {\\n                let button = match button {\\n                    MouseButton::Left => egui::PointerButton::Primary,\\n                    MouseButton::Right => egui::PointerButton::Secondary,\\n                    MouseButton::Middle => egui::PointerButton::Middle,\\n90→                    MouseButton::Back => egui::PointerButton::Extra1,\\n                    MouseButton::Forward => egui::PointerButton::Extra2,\\n                    MouseButton::Other(_) => return false,\\n                };\\n                ev.push(Event::PointerButton {\\n                    pos: self.pointer,\\n                    button,\\n                    pressed: state.is_pressed(),\\n                    modifiers: self.modifiers,\\n                });\\n100→                over_ui(&self.ctx)\\n            }\\n            WindowEvent::MouseWheel { delta, .. } => {\\n                let (unit, delta) = match delta {\\n                    MouseScrollDelta::LineDelta(x, y) => (egui::MouseWheelUnit::Line, egui::vec2(*x, *y)),\\n                    MouseScrollDelta::PixelDelta(p) => (egui::MouseWheelUnit::Point, egui::vec2(p.x as f32, p.y as f32) / ppp),\\n                };\\n                ev.push(Event::MouseWheel { unit, delta, phase: egui::TouchPhase::Move, modifiers: self.modifiers });\\n                over_ui(&self.ctx)\\n            }\\n110→            WindowEvent::ModifiersChanged(m) => {\\n                let s = m.state();\\n                self.modifiers = egui::Modifiers {\\n                    alt: s.alt_key(),\\n                    ctrl: s.control_key(),\\n                    shift: s.shift_key(),\\n                    mac_cmd: false,\\n                    command: s.control_key(),\\n                };\\n                false\\n120→            }\\n            WindowEvent::KeyboardInput { event, .. } => {\\n                use winit::keyboard::Key as K;\\n                let pressed = event.state.is_pressed();\\n                let key = match &event.logical_key {\\n                    K::Named(n) => egui::Key::from_name(&format!(\\\"{n:?}\\\")),\\n                    K::Character(c) => egui::Key::from_name(c.as_str()),\\n                    _ => None,\\n                };\\n                if let Some(key) = key {\\n130→                    ev.push(Event::Key { key, physical_key: None, pressed, repeat: event.repeat, modifiers: self.modifiers });\\n                }\\n                if pressed && !self.modifiers.ctrl {\\n                    if let Some(t) = &event.text {\\n                        let t: String = t.chars().filter(|c| !c.is_control()).collect();\\n                        if !t.is_empty() {\\n                            ev.push(Event::Text(t));\\n                        }\\n                    }\\n                }\\n140→                self.ctx.egui_wants_keyboard_input()\\n            }\\n            WindowEvent::Touch(t) => {\\n                // Like egui-winit: every finger as a touch (pinches), the first also as the pointer.\\n                use winit::event::TouchPhase as P;\\n                let pos = egui::pos2(t.location.x as f32 / ppp, t.location.y as f32 / ppp);\\n                let phase = match t.phase {\\n                    P::Started => egui::TouchPhase::Start,\\n                    P::Moved => egui::TouchPhase::Move,\\n                    P::Ended => egui::TouchPhase::End,\\n150→                    P::Cancelled => egui::TouchPhase::Cancel,\\n                };\\n                ev.push(Event::Touch {\\n                    device_id: egui::TouchDeviceId(0),\\n                    id: egui::TouchId::from(t.id),\\n                    phase,\\n                    pos,\\n                    force: None,\\n                });\\n                if self.touch_pointer.is_none_or(|id| id == t.id) {\\n160→                    let button = |pressed| Event::PointerButton {\\n                        pos,\\n                        button: egui::PointerButton::Primary,\\n                        pressed,\\n                        modifiers: egui::Modifiers::default(),\\n                    };\\n                    match t.phase {\\n                        P::Started => {\\n                            self.touch_pointer = Some(t.id);\\n                            self.pointer = pos;\\n170→                            ev.push(Event::PointerMoved(pos));\\n                            ev.push(button(true));\\n                        }\\n                        P::Moved => {\\n                            self.pointer = pos;\\n                            ev.push(Event::PointerMoved(pos));\\n                        }\\n                        P::Ended => {\\n                            self.touch_pointer = None;\\n                            ev.push(button(false));\\n180→                            ev.push(Event::PointerGone);\\n                        }\\n                        P::Cancelled => {\\n                            self.touch_pointer = None;\\n                            ev.push(Event::PointerGone);\\n                        }\\n                    }\\n                }\\n                true\\n            }\\n190→            WindowEvent::Focused(f) => {\\n                ev.push(Event::WindowFocused(*f));\\n                self.raw.focused = *f;\\n                false\\n            }\\n            _ => false,\\n        }\\n    }\\n\\n    pub fn take(&mut self, window: &Window) -> egui::RawInput {\\n200→        let ppp = self.ppp(window);\\n        let size = window.inner_size();\\n        let points = egui::vec2(size.width as f32, size.height as f32) / ppp;\\n        self.raw.time = Some(self.start.elapsed().as_secs_f64());\\n        self.raw.screen_rect = (points.x > 0.0 && points.y > 0.0).then(|| egui::Rect::from_min_size(egui::Pos2::ZERO, points));\\n        self.raw.viewport_id = egui::ViewportId::ROOT;\\n        self.raw.viewports.entry(egui::ViewportId::ROOT).or_default().native_pixels_per_point =\\n            Some(window.scale_factor() as f32);\\n        self.raw.max_texture_side = Some(self.max_texture);\\n        self.raw.take()\\n210→    }\\n\\n    pub fn platform_output(&mut self, window: &Window, out: egui::PlatformOutput) {\\n        use egui::CursorIcon as E;\\n        use winit::window::CursorIcon as W;\\n        if out.cursor_icon != self.cursor {\\n            self.cursor = out.cursor_icon;\\n            window.set_cursor(match out.cursor_icon {\",\"content_concise\":\"38→pub struct UiInput {\\n    ctx: egui::Context,\\n40→    raw: egui::RawInput,\\n    pointer: egui::Pos2,\\n    modifiers: egui::Modifiers,\\n    start: web_time::Instant,\\n    max_texture: usize,\\n    cursor: egui::CursorIcon,\\n    /// The finger that is egui's pointer (the first one down).\\n    touch_pointer: Option<u64>,\\n}\\n\\n50→#[cfg(target_arch = \\\"wasm32\\\")]\\nimpl UiInput {\\n    pub fn new(ctx: &egui::Context, _window: &Window, max_texture: usize) -> Self {\\n        Self {\\n            ctx: ctx.clone(),\\n            raw: egui::RawInput::default(),\\n            pointer: egui::Pos2::ZERO,\\n            modifiers: egui::Modifiers::default(),\\n            start: web_time::Instant::now(),\\n            max_texture,\\n60→            cursor: egui::CursorIcon::Default,\\n            touch_pointer: None,\\n        }\\n    }\\n\\n    fn ppp(&self, window: &Window) -> f32 {\\n        self.ctx.zoom_factor() * window.scale_factor() as f32\\n    }\\n\\n    pub fn on_window_event(&mut self, window: &Window, event: &WindowEvent) -> bool {\\n70→        use egui::Event;\\n        use winit::event::{MouseButton, MouseScrollDelta};\\n        let ppp = self.ppp(window);\\n        let over_ui = |c: &egui::Context| c.egui_wants_pointer_input() || c.is_pointer_over_egui();\\n        let ev = &mut self.raw.events;\\n        match event {\\n            WindowEvent::CursorMoved { position, .. } => {\\n                self.pointer = egui::pos2(position.x as f32 / ppp, position.y as f32 / ppp);\\n                ev.push(Ev