,99,101,95,114,101,115,117,108,116,62],\"stderr\":[],\"exit_code\":0,\"match_count\":3,\"file_matches\":[{\"path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224015__x42677a/work/engine-link/crates/pav_core/src/games/mod.rs\",\"matches\":[{\"line_number\":138,\"content\":\"    pub fn key(&self) -> &'static str {\"},{\"line_number\":200,\"content\":\"    fn key(&self) -> &'static str;\"},{\"line_number\":214,\"content\":\"    fn key(&self) -> &'static str {\"}]}]}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa38-de6f-7dc0-ae0d-e0f717ed75f2","uuid":"0e953d2f-7276-4cd4-b20a-30aca0f601f2"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_248","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Making `to_frame` public so session and other components can use it.\n\nHardcoding the default shot in `sync_camera` for headless rendering. Headless frames will draw the surgery shell when `frame.surgery` is present. Verification will use `Shell::step` unit tests instead of egui headless.\n\n`has_ui` will include surgery so tools recognize the UI exists. Tests driving `Shell` from the title screen will live in `pav_ui/src/surgery/mod.rs` as `#[cfg(test)]`. The existing headless frame signature does not accept a shell, so egui headless drawing is treated as extra.\n\nA headless egui draw test will verify the surgery shell does not panic. SurgeryCmd gains LoadAttract, ToTitle, and SetBus. Command handlers will expose an apply_cmd method. The HUD returns empty. Status strings format cursors and music with two decimal places.\n\nThe simulation status will remain numeric; the product layer handles formatting for display. Story and content modules will be publicly re-exported. The attract screen will use the bot character. The clock screen will clear the active surgery command and the surgeon pressed state. The product module needs branch frame and window event handlers, a window title update, a fail message, and a harbor field. JavaScript bindings require js-sys. Chart mode maps to Story in the shell; confirming a chart emits ConfirmSim, which advances the simulation to the operation screen.\n\nA new `Chart` screen will display the patient and operation name with a \"Begin\" button. The shell will map mode 2 to this screen, and confirming it will emit `ConfirmSim`. The shell's draw logic, step count, activation, and menuish behavior all need updates to support this new state.\n\nDead retry emits Retry. Results mode is set by note_mode unless paused. LoadCampaign sets Story immediately, then note_mode follows. Attract skips note_mode because it is in the skip list. Leaving attract via ToTitle resets paused and sets Title. Touch input sets shell.touch_only on platforms with touch but no fine pointer, leaving desktop touch_screen false. Gamepad prompts appear when any pad activity occurs.\n\nLeft stick 8-way tool selection will be handled in the product layer. A helper maps the stick angle to one of eight octants, and tool selection fires only when the octant changes from none or shifts to a different tool. Digits 1 through 8 select tools 0 through 7, 9 selects cryo, 0 selects dressing, and minus selects defib.\n\nDuring menus, digit presses will not change tools unless the simulation is in operation mode. During surgery, mouse aim will use absolute ground-point snapping against the camera rig; the rig will be reset to the surgery shot parameters each frame so the cursor maps correctly before calling ground_point. Stick input will use relative aiming without snapping.\n\nThe left stick Y axis is inverted for steering: positive stick Y maps to negative Z movement because yaw 0 faces north. Mouse aim sends world x and z coordinates directly. Slot 0 is always active during local play; slots 1 through 3 activate only when a connected pad is present.\n\nSlot 0 is shared between the keyboard/mouse and the first connected pad. Extra pads map to surgeons 1 through 3. If both a mouse and a pad move in the same frame, the mouse overrides the pad for slot 0.\n\nPad and keyboard inputs will be OR'd for held and pressed bits on slot 0. Pressure maps to R2 analog or full strength when keys or mouse are active. The product module will be lengthy but necessary. A music scheduler using `pav_audio::music` will return patches without exposing the recipe type.\n\nA `cues_for` helper will return `(Patch, pan, gain, delay)` tuples for the scheduler. The product layer will play them when `music_left` reaches zero and then reset the counter to `beats * 60 / bpm`. Track selection maps each simulation mode to a specific cue: title, story ward or night, operation with gift hush and strain banners, results, crisis, and a default fallback. The strain banner strings are not memorized, so the frame will carry the strain index.\n\nA `strain` field will be added to `SurgeryFrame` to carry the current strain phase. The product layer will use this value to select the correct background track: gift hush maps to \"hush\", flat or code mode maps to \"code\", story modes alternate between \"story_ward\" and \"story_night\", and operation modes branch into \"introit\", \"lacrimosa\", \"dies\", or \"libera\" based on the strain index.\n\nStory voice cues are already handled by the simulation advance event, so the product layer must not duplicate them. Music and voices remain separate systems. Bus levels for music, effects, and voices will be updated every frame from the operation state. Server mode plate skipping is deferred to the hub; for now the product always draws.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-2d29ad4f-f4df-43ee-ac12-a264396660be-103","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224015__x42677a/work/engine-link/crates/pav_app/src/gfx.rs","offset":1,"limit":50}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-2d29ad4f-f4df-43ee-ac12-a264396660be-104","name":"grep","input":{"pattern":"pub struct Gfx|pub window|pub renderer","path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224015__x42677a/work/engine-link/crates/pav_app/src/gfx.rs"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-2d29ad4f-f4df-43ee-ac12-a264396660be-105","name":"grep","input":{"pattern":"use winit|KeyCode|ActiveEventLoop|WindowEvent","path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224015__x42677a/work/engine-link/crates/pav_app/src/app.rs","head_limit":30}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1031,"output_tokens":2519,"cache_read_input_tokens":134272,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa38-de6f-7dc0-ae0d-e0f717ed75f2","uuid":"cd986dea-d61e-4d64-bf06-01f113d84d6f"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-2d29ad4f-f4df-43ee-ac12-a264396660be-103","content":"{\"type\":\"ReadFile\",\"FileContent\":{\"content\":\"1→//! Window-bound graphics: surface, device, scene renderer and egui renderer.\\n\\nuse std::sync::Arc;\\n\\nuse anyhow::{Context, Result, anyhow};\\nuse pav_render::gpu::{self, BackendChoice};\\nuse pav_render::wgpu;\\nuse pav_render::{Renderer, Scene};\\nuse winit::window::Window;\\n10→\\nuse crate::boot::{stage, stage_async};\\n\\npub struct Gfx {\\n    pub window: Arc<Window>,\\n    pub surface: wgpu::Surface<'static>,\\n    pub adapter: wgpu::Adapter,\\n    pub device: wgpu::Device,\\n    pub queue: wgpu::Queue,\\n    pub config: wgpu::SurfaceConfiguration,\\n20→    pub renderer: Renderer,\\n    pub egui: egui_wgpu::Renderer,\\n    pub vsync: bool,\\n    pub adapter_name: String,\\n    pub gpu_errors: Arc<std::sync::atomic::AtomicU32>,\\n}\\n\\nimpl Gfx {\\n    #[cfg(not(target_arch = \\\"wasm32\\\"))]\\n    pub fn new(window: Arc<Window>, backend: BackendChoice, vsync: bool) -> Result<Self> {\\n30→        pollster_block(Self::create(window, backend, vsync))\\n    }\\n\\n    /// Creates everything; only the adapter and device requests wait (in the browser).\\n    pub async fn create(window: Arc<Window>, backend: BackendChoice, vsync: bool) -> Result<Self> {\\n        let web = cfg!(target_arch = \\\"wasm32\\\");\\n        let instance = stage(\\\"graphics instance\\\", || {\\n            Ok((gpu::create_instance(backend), format!(\\\"backend: {}\\\", if web { \\\"webgpu\\\" } else { backend.name() })))\\n        })?;\\n        let surface = stage(\\\"window surface\\\", || {\\n40→            let s = instance.create_surface(window.clone()).context(\\\"could not create a drawing surface for the window\\\")?;\\n            Ok((s, String::new()))\\n        })?;\\n        let adapter = stage_async(\\\"graphics adapter\\\", async {\\n            if !web {\\n                let all = gpu::list_adapters(&instance, backend);\\n                for a in &all {\\n                    log::info!(\\\"  found adapter: {}\\\", gpu::describe(a));\\n                }\\n                if all.is_empty() {\\n50→                    return Err(anyhow!(\",\"content_concise\":\"1→//! Window-bound graphics: surface, device, scene renderer and egui renderer.\\n\\nuse std::sync::Arc;\\n\\nuse anyhow::{Context, Result, anyhow};\\nuse pav_render::gpu::{self, BackendChoice};\\nuse pav_render::wgpu;\\nuse pav_render::{Renderer, Scene};\\nuse winit::window::Window;\\n10→\\nuse crate::boot::{stage, stage_async};\\n\\npub struct Gfx {\\n    pub window: Arc<Window>,\\n    pub surface: wgpu::Surface<'static>,\\n    pub adapter: wgpu::Adapter,\\n    pub device: wgpu::Device,\\n    pub queue: wgpu::Queue,\\n    pub config: wgpu::SurfaceConfiguration,\\n20→    pub renderer: Renderer,\\n    pub egui: egui_wgpu::Renderer,\\n    pub vsync: bool,\\n    pub adapter_name: String,\\n    pub gpu_errors: Arc<std::sync::atomic::AtomicU32>,\\n}\\n\\nimpl Gfx {\\n    #[cfg(not(target_arch = \\\"wasm32\\\"))]\\n    pub fn new(window: Arc<Window>, backend: BackendChoice, vsync: bool) -> Result<Self> {\\n30→        pollster_block(Self::create(window, backend, vsync))\\n    }\\n\\n    /// Creates everything; only the adapter and device requests wait (in the browser).\\n    pub async fn create(window: Arc<Window>, backend: BackendChoice, vsync: bool) -> Result<Self> {\\n        let web = cfg!(target_arch = \\\"wasm32\\\");\\n        let instance = stage(\\\"graphics instance\\\", || {\\n            Ok((gpu::create_instance(backend), format!(\\\"backend: {}\\\", if web { \\\"webgpu\\\" } else { backend.name() })))\\n        })?;\\n        let surface = stage(\\\"window surface\\\", || {\\n40→            let s = instance.create_surface(window.clone()).context(\\\"could not create a drawing surface for the window\\\")?;\\n            Ok((s, String::new()))\\n        })?;\\n        let adapter = stage_async(\\\"graphics adapter\\\", async {\\n            if !web {\\n                let all = gpu::list_adapters(&instance, backend);\\n                for a in &all {\\n                    log::info!(\\\"  found adapter: {}\\\", gpu::describe(a));\\n                }\\n                if all.is_empty() {\\n50→                    return Err(anyhow!(\",\"absolute_path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224015__x42677a/work/Hands of Harbor: Second Opinion-Trauma Center: Second Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-224015/engine/crates/pav_app/src/gfx.rs\",\"offset\":1,\"limit\":50,\"raw_output\":\"//! Window-bound graphics: surface, device, scene renderer and egui renderer.\\n\\nuse std::sync::Arc;\\n\\nuse anyhow::{Context, Result, anyhow};\\nuse pav_render::gpu::{self, BackendChoice};\\nuse pav_render::wgpu;\\nuse pav_render::{Renderer, Scene};\\nuse winit::window::Window;\\n\\nuse crate::boot::{stage, stage_async};\\n\\npub struct Gfx {\\n    pub window: Arc<Window>,\\n    pub surface: wgpu::Surface<'static>,\\n    pub adapter: wgpu::Adapter,\\n    pub device: wgpu::Device,\\n    pub queue: wgpu::Queue,\\n    pub config: wgpu::SurfaceConfiguration,\\n    pub renderer: Renderer,\\n    pub egui: egui_wgpu::Renderer,\\n    pub vsync: bool,\\n    pub adapter_name: String,\\n    pub gpu_errors: Arc<std::sync::atomic::AtomicU32>,\\n}\\n\\nimpl Gfx {\\n    #[cfg(not(target_arch = \\\"wasm32\\\"))]\\n    pub fn new(window: Arc<Window>, backend: BackendChoice, vsync: bool) -> Result<Self> {\\n        pollster_block(Self::create(window, backend, vsync))\\n    }\\n\\n    /// Creates everything; only the adapter and device requests wait (in the browser).\\n    pub async fn create(window: Arc<Window>, backend: BackendChoice, vsync: bool) -> Result<Self> {\\n        let web = cfg!(target_arch = \\\"wasm32\\\");\\n        let instance = stage(\\\"graphics instance\\\", || {\\n            Ok((gpu::create_instance(backend), format!(\\\"backend: {}\\\", if web { \\\"webgpu\\\" } else { backend.name() })))\\n        })?;\\n        let surface = stage(\\\"window surface\\\", || {\\n            let s = instance.create_surface(window.clone()).context(\\\"could not create a drawing surface for the window\\\")?;\\n            Ok((s, String::new()))\\n        })?;\\n        let adapter = stage_async(\\\"graphics adapter\\\", async {\\n            if !web {\\n                let all = gpu::list_adapters(&instance, backend);\\n                for a in &all {\\n                    log::info!(\\\"  found adapter: {}\\\", gpu::describe(a));\\n                }\\n                if all.is_empty() {\\n                    return Err(anyhow!(\\n\",\"total_lines\":217}}","is_error":false},{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-2d29ad4f-f4df-43ee-ac12-a264396660be-104","content":"{\"type\":\"GrepSearch\",\"stdout\":[60,119,111,114,107,115,112,97,99,101,95,114,101,115,117,108,116,32,119,111,114,107,115,112,97,99,101,95,112,97,116,104,61,34,47,104,111,109,101,47,109,105,99,104,97,47,100,101,118,47,99,99,45,109,97,116,114,105,120,47,114,117,110,115,47,103,114,111,107,45,120,104,105,103,104,46,98,117,105,108,100,45,118,50,95,95,50,48,50,54,49,49,48,52,45,50,50,52,48,49,53,95,95,120,52,50,54,55,55,97,47,119,111,114,107,34,62,10,70,111,117,110,100,32,51,32,109,97,116,99,104,105,110,103,32,108,105,110,101,115,10,47,104,111,109,101,47,109,105,99,104,97,47,100,101,118,47,99,99,45,109,97,116,114,105,120,47,114,117,110,115,47,103,114,111,107,45,120,104,105,103,104,46,98,117,105,108,100,45,118,50,95,95,50,48,50,54,49,49,48,52,45,50,50,52,48,49,53,95,95,120,52,50,54,55,55,97,47,119,111,114,107,47,101,110,103,105,110,101,45,108,105,110,107,47,99,114,97,116,101,115,47,112,97,118,95,97,112,112,47,115,114,99,47,103,102,120,46,114,115,10,49,51,58,112,117,98,32,115,116,114,117,99,116,32,71,102,120,32,123,10,49,52,58,32,32,32,32,112,117,98,32,119,105,110,100,111,119,58,32,65,114,99,60,87,105,110,100,111,119,62,44,10,50,48,58,32,32,32,32,1