{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_250","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-3af290ee-487d-48f1-b4fc-4f5c7d748c86-108","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224015__x42677a/work/engine-link/crates/pav_app/src/platform.rs","offset":40,"limit":30}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1764,"output_tokens":80,"cache_read_input_tokens":139136,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa38-de6f-7dc0-ae0d-e0f717ed75f2","uuid":"e807edad-ae0c-4a7e-831a-de45970127c4"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-3af290ee-487d-48f1-b4fc-4f5c7d748c86-108","content":"{\"type\":\"ReadFile\",\"FileContent\":{\"content\":\"40→\\n#[cfg(not(windows))]\\npub fn attach_console() {}\\n\\n/// Whether this is a phone or tablet: the browser says its main pointer is a finger.\\n#[cfg(target_arch = \\\"wasm32\\\")]\\npub fn touch_screen() -> bool {\\n    web_sys::window().and_then(|w| w.match_media(\\\"(pointer: coarse)\\\").ok().flatten()).is_some_and(|m| m.matches())\\n}\\n\\n50→#[cfg(not(target_arch = \\\"wasm32\\\"))]\\npub fn touch_screen() -> bool {\\n    false\\n}\\n\\n/// Full screen on or off. In the browser the whole page goes full screen (the game's own\\n/// overlays stay on top of the canvas).\\n#[cfg(target_arch = \\\"wasm32\\\")]\\npub fn toggle_fullscreen(_window: &winit::window::Window) {\\n    let Some(doc) = web_sys::window().and_then(|w| w.document()) else { return };\\n60→    if doc.fullscreen_element().is_some() {\\n        doc.exit_fullscreen();\\n    } else if let Some(el) = doc.document_element() {\\n        let _ = el.request_fullscreen();\\n    }\\n}\\n\\n#[cfg(not(target_arch = \\\"wasm32\\\"))]\\npub fn toggle_fullscreen(window: &winit::window::Window) {\\n    let on = window.fullscreen().is_some();\",\"content_concise\":\"40→\\n#[cfg(not(windows))]\\npub fn attach_console() {}\\n\\n/// Whether this is a phone or tablet: the browser says its main pointer is a finger.\\n#[cfg(target_arch = \\\"wasm32\\\")]\\npub fn touch_screen() -> bool {\\n    web_sys::window().and_then(|w| w.match_media(\\\"(pointer: coarse)\\\").ok().flatten()).is_some_and(|m| m.matches())\\n}\\n\\n50→#[cfg(not(target_arch = \\\"wasm32\\\"))]\\npub fn touch_screen() -> bool {\\n    false\\n}\\n\\n/// Full screen on or off. In the browser the whole page goes full screen (the game's own\\n/// overlays stay on top of the canvas).\\n#[cfg(target_arch = \\\"wasm32\\\")]\\npub fn toggle_fullscreen(_window: &winit::window::Window) {\\n    let Some(doc) = web_sys::window().and_then(|w| w.document()) else { return };\\n60→    if doc.fullscreen_element().is_some() {\\n        doc.exit_fullscreen();\\n    } else if let Some(el) = doc.document_element() {\\n        let _ = el.request_fullscreen();\\n    }\\n}\\n\\n#[cfg(not(target_arch = \\\"wasm32\\\"))]\\npub fn toggle_fullscreen(window: &winit::window::Window) {\\n    let on = window.fullscreen().is_some();\",\"absolute_path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224015__x42677a/work/Hands of Harbor: Second Opinion-Trauma Center: Second Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-224015/engine/crates/pav_app/src/platform.rs\",\"offset\":40,\"limit\":30,\"raw_output\":\"\\n#[cfg(not(windows))]\\npub fn attach_console() {}\\n\\n/// Whether this is a phone or tablet: the browser says its main pointer is a finger.\\n#[cfg(target_arch = \\\"wasm32\\\")]\\npub fn touch_screen() -> bool {\\n    web_sys::window().and_then(|w| w.match_media(\\\"(pointer: coarse)\\\").ok().flatten()).is_some_and(|m| m.matches())\\n}\\n\\n#[cfg(not(target_arch = \\\"wasm32\\\"))]\\npub fn touch_screen() -> bool {\\n    false\\n}\\n\\n/// Full screen on or off. In the browser the whole page goes full screen (the game's own\\n/// overlays stay on top of the canvas).\\n#[cfg(target_arch = \\\"wasm32\\\")]\\npub fn toggle_fullscreen(_window: &winit::window::Window) {\\n    let Some(doc) = web_sys::window().and_then(|w| w.document()) else { return };\\n    if doc.fullscreen_element().is_some() {\\n        doc.exit_fullscreen();\\n    } else if let Some(el) = doc.document_element() {\\n        let _ = el.request_fullscreen();\\n    }\\n}\\n\\n#[cfg(not(target_arch = \\\"wasm32\\\"))]\\npub fn toggle_fullscreen(window: &winit::window::Window) {\\n    let on = window.fullscreen().is_some();\\n\",\"total_lines\":71}}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa38-de6f-7dc0-ae0d-e0f717ed75f2","uuid":"c916b44c-a638-430e-9f47-95ee543f5a30"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_251","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Touch-only mode activates when the pointer is coarse and no keyboard or pad has been used.\n\nDesktop Chromium with a mouse is not coarse. I will also detect touch-only mode via a `?touch=1` query parameter or by checking for only touch input.\n\nShell tests will cover the touch-only sentence. Browser tests will verify title and pad behavior. I will wire `touch_screen` to `shell.touch_only`. A mouse on a coarse device will mark the input as fine and hide the sentence.\n\nI am now writing code in batches. I need to update SurgeryCmd variants exhaustively. The frame field strain is a u8 defaulting to 255. `to_frame` copies `self.strain_phase`. `empty()` sets strain to 255. Status cursors are next.\n\nStatus JSON now includes surgeon positions, tools, and active flags. Music is formatted as a number in the status string. The `fmt_status` function adds screen name, focus state, and device type to the output.\n\nThe status JSON now includes an `xbox` flag. The `music` value is formatted to two decimal places as a string so the status string contains \"0.10\" rather than \"0.1\".\n\n`apply_cmd` is now public. A stub for `apply_mirror` will be added to simplify hub integration.\n\nThe `apply_mirror` stub is deferred to hub work. `bot_drive` is skipped because attract mode uses bots. The Shell Chart screen will be added next. Then comes `product.rs`, shell tests in `surgery/mod.rs`, and finally a compile check across the UI, view, core, and app crates.\n\nThe heavy `pav_app` compile will wait until `product.rs` compiles. `Cargo.lock` must be updated and committed because `build-web` uses `--locked`. `js-sys` will be added to the workspace and `pav_app` together so one `cargo update` handles both changes.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-ea5c8df1-64e3-4a83-8994-edb80214f3a1-109","name":"grep","input":{"pattern":"Shardfall","path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224015__x42677a/work/engine-link/crates/pav_app/src/main.rs"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-ea5c8df1-64e3-4a83-8994-edb80214f3a1-110","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224015__x42677a/work/engine-link/crates/pav_ui/src/surgery/mod.rs","offset":670,"limit":100}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":499,"output_tokens":1283,"cache_read_input_tokens":140800,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa38-de6f-7dc0-ae0d-e0f717ed75f2","uuid":"d77370e5-420d-4207-ae91-0ca2b23e5dbb"}
