8,58,71,97,109,101,66,111,120,62,44,10,50,48,51,58,32,32,32,32,32,32,32,32,32,32,32,32,32,32,32,32,112,108,97,121,58,32,78,111,110,101,44,10,60,47,119,111,114,107,115,112,97,99,101,95,114,101,115,117,108,116,62],\"stderr\":[],\"exit_code\":0,\"match_count\":3,\"file_matches\":[{\"path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224015__x42677a/work/engine-link/crates/pav_core/src/sim.rs\",\"matches\":[{\"line_number\":114,\"content\":\"    pub player: Option<EntityId>,\"},{\"line_number\":134,\"content\":\"    pub play: Option<crate::games::GameBox>,\"},{\"line_number\":203,\"content\":\"                play: None,\"}]}]}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa38-de6f-7dc0-ae0d-e0f717ed75f2","uuid":"7ffacd8f-1c86-45cb-bada-b8873303aa8e"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_256","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"sim.state.play is public. The executor can access it.\n\nSurgery and apply_cmd must be public. The executor queues commands on the simulation thread before the next ticks. frames() may lag one frame behind, which is acceptable for menus.\n\nOn wasm, input is written before exec. The command publishes the post-command state without a tick. Ticks then pump from that state. On native, exec is queued while input writes immediately in the mutex.\n\nA race between ticks and exec is acceptable for gameplay. LoadCampaign commands will be visible to the next ticks.\n\nThe executor must not leave surgery_cmd set.\n\nConfirmSim is not a SurgeryCmd. Product maps Enter to surgeon pressed CONFIRM for one tick when ConfirmSim is present. Shell story confirm also uses this path. Enter during Hud does not emit ConfirmSim, so no mapping is needed there. Keys during Hud route to the surgeon: G for gift, Tab for chart, click to use. Pause is handled by Esc or Start.\n\nBACK during pause should not cancel gestures. When paused, the host stops sending USE to the simulation. The clock checks a paused flag to freeze the operation; attract mode continues ticking.\n\nThe host will set the simulation paused flag whenever the shell screen is Pause, Dev, Settings, or Controls while paused. A public `paused()` method is needed on the shell to expose its private state. This freezes the operation when paused and leaves attract mode unaffected.\n\nRefactoring `render_track` to share note generation via a new `notes` function. Shell Chart edits will use search and replace. Tests will be added at the bottom of `surgery/mod.rs`. The egui font API will be verified by compiling and fixing errors, and whether `Area::new` takes an `Id` in egui 0.36 will be checked.\n\nThe egui API details are being verified: `Area::new` may take an `Id` directly, and `RichText::strong()` is being checked. `vertical_centered` is confirmed available. The `js-sys` and `wasm-bindgen` versions align. For the WASM hook, `web_sys::window()` will be used with `js_sys::Reflect::set` to install the game object.\n\nThe WASM game hook is being wired up. A `status` closure returns the current status string. A `step` closure increments the burst counter and immediately calls the hook's `burst` method when a hook pointer exists.\n\nSimHost::burst is public and takes &self, so the raw pointer in the WASM hook is valid. The game object is attached to the window as `__game`. On non-WASM targets the install is empty and status updates are skipped. The burst counter is consumed at frame start to handle cases where the hook is not yet set.\n\nA `do_json` function will queue raw JSON commands into a pending buffer. At the start of each frame, those commands are parsed and applied to the simulation edges. This defers execution until the next frame, which is acceptable for tests that use real input.\n\nThe cursor will be hidden during mode 3 and shown otherwise. The launch test uses real winit input, so the deferred `do()` path is acceptable. All planning is complete and I am ready to write the code.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-464a057d-f34d-45cf-b8bd-5e243e6f9a72-117","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224015__x42677a/work/engine-link/crates/pav_core/src/games/surgery/story.rs","offset":1,"limit":45}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":782,"output_tokens":1969,"cache_read_input_tokens":148224,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa38-de6f-7dc0-ae0d-e0f717ed75f2","uuid":"77975c06-f5c7-4e78-a7f2-1d9debb2078c"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-464a057d-f34d-45cf-b8bd-5e243e6f9a72-117","content":"{\"type\":\"ReadFile\",\"FileContent\":{\"content\":\"1→//! Paper-theatre lines. Indices, not copies, live in the sim.\\n\\n#[derive(Clone, Copy)]\\npub struct Line {\\n    pub who: &'static str,\\n    pub text: &'static str,\\n}\\n\\nmacro_rules! L {\\n10→    ($($who:literal, $text:literal);* $(;)?) => {\\n        &[ $(Line { who: $who, text: $text }),* ]\\n    };\\n}\\n\\npub fn block(case_id: i8, after: bool) -> &'static [Line] {\\n    match (case_id, after) {\\n        (0, false) => BEFORE_0,\\n        (0, true) => AFTER_0,\\n        (1, false) => BEFORE_1,\\n20→        (1, true) => AFTER_1,\\n        (2, false) => BEFORE_2,\\n        (2, true) => AFTER_2,\\n        (3, false) => BEFORE_3,\\n        (3, true) => AFTER_3,\\n        (4, false) => BEFORE_4,\\n        (4, true) => AFTER_4,\\n        (5, false) => BEFORE_5,\\n        (5, true) => AFTER_5,\\n        (6, false) => BEFORE_6,\\n30→        (6, true) => AFTER_6,\\n        (7, false) => BEFORE_7,\\n        (7, true) => AFTER_7,\\n        _ => AFTER_7,\\n    }\\n}\\n\\npub fn all_lines() -> Vec<Line> {\\n    let mut v = Vec::new();\\n    for case_id in 0..8 {\\n40→        v.extend_from_slice(block(case_id, false));\\n        v.extend_from_slice(block(case_id, true));\\n    }\\n    v.extend_from_slice(CALLOUTS);\\n    v\\n}\",\"content_concise\":\"1→//! Paper-theatre lines. Indices, not copies, live in the sim.\\n\\n#[derive(Clone, Copy)]\\npub struct Line {\\n    pub who: &'static str,\\n    pub text: &'static str,\\n}\\n\\nmacro_rules! L {\\n10→    ($($who:literal, $text:literal);* $(;)?) => {\\n        &[ $(Line { who: $who, text: $text }),* ]\\n    };\\n}\\n\\npub fn block(case_id: i8, after: bool) -> &'static [Line] {\\n    match (case_id, after) {\\n        (0, false) => BEFORE_0,\\n        (0, true) => AFTER_0,\\n        (1, false) => BEFORE_1,\\n20→        (1, true) => AFTER_1,\\n        (2, false) => BEFORE_2,\\n        (2, true) => AFTER_2,\\n        (3, false) => BEFORE_3,\\n        (3, true) => AFTER_3,\\n        (4, false) => BEFORE_4,\\n        (4, true) => AFTER_4,\\n        (5, false) => BEFORE_5,\\n        (5, true) => AFTER_5,\\n        (6, false) => BEFORE_6,\\n30→        (6, true) => AFTER_6,\\n        (7, false) => BEFORE_7,\\n        (7, true) => AFTER_7,\\n        _ => AFTER_7,\\n    }\\n}\\n\\npub fn all_lines() -> Vec<Line> {\\n    let mut v = Vec::new();\\n    for case_id in 0..8 {\\n40→        v.extend_from_slice(block(case_id, false));\\n        v.extend_from_slice(block(case_id, true));\\n    }\\n    v.extend_from_slice(CALLOUTS);\\n    v\\n}\",\"absolute_path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224015__x42677a/work/Hands of Harbor: Second Opinion-Trauma Center: Second Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-224015/engine/crates/pav_core/src/games/surgery/story.rs\",\"offset\":1,\"limit\":45,\"raw_output\":\"//! Paper-theatre lines. Indices, not copies, live in the sim.\\n\\n#[derive(Clone, Copy)]\\npub struct Line {\\n    pub who: &'static str,\\n    pub text: &'static str,\\n}\\n\\nmacro_rules! L {\\n    ($($who:literal, $text:literal);* $(;)?) => {\\n        &[ $(Line { who: $who, text: $text }),* ]\\n    };\\n}\\n\\npub fn block(case_id: i8, after: bool) -> &'static [Line] {\\n    match (case_id, after) {\\n        (0, false) => BEFORE_0,\\n        (0, true) => AFTER_0,\\n        (1, false) => BEFORE_1,\\n        (1, true) => AFTER_1,\\n        (2, false) => BEFORE_2,\\n        (2, true) => AFTER_2,\\n        (3, false) => BEFORE_3,\\n        (3, true) => AFTER_3,\\n        (4, false) => BEFORE_4,\\n        (4, true) => AFTER_4,\\n        (5, false) => BEFORE_5,\\n        (5, true) => AFTER_5,\\n        (6, false) => BEFORE_6,\\n        (6, true) => AFTER_6,\\n        (7, false) => BEFORE_7,\\n        (7, true) => AFTER_7,\\n        _ => AFTER_7,\\n    }\\n}\\n\\npub fn all_lines() -> Vec<Line> {\\n    let mut v = Vec::new();\\n    for case_id in 0..8 {\\n        v.extend_from_slice(block(case_id, false));\\n        v.extend_from_slice(block(case_id, true));\\n    }\\n    v.extend_from_slice(CALLOUTS);\\n    v\\n}\\n\",\"total_lines\":312}}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa38-de6f-7dc0-ae0d-e0f717ed75f2","uuid":"d3bb17e4-7601-4f72-99c7-ac276aa12a8d"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_257","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"`pub use all_lines` is sufficient to expose the function from outside the module.\n\nPublic items are not dead_code warnings even if unused internally. I will now write the remaining files and add a shell test. I also need to update render_track to call a shared function for the music phrase test.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-a2019471-6128-46c6-9efa-fb004af290e9-118","name":"grep","input":{"pattern":"view\\.fog|fn build\\(","path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224015__x42677a/work/engine-link/crates/pav_view/src/build.rs"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-a2019471-6128-46c6-9efa-fb004af290e9-119","name":"grep","input":{"pattern":"struct ViewSettings|fog:","path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224015__x42677a/work/engine-link/crates/pav_view/src/look.rs"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2393,"output_tokens":441,"cache_read_input_tokens":148992,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa38-de6f-7dc0-ae0d-e0f717ed75f2","uuid":"6cd49494-4c24-4e20-bc05-358129b5807b"}
