{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_260","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Fog starts at 48 meters. Camera distance is 19.\n\nThe plate sits inside the fog start distance, so fog won't hide it. Scene settings are configured before apply_look overwrites them. The plate is created after restyle_parts with Style::Cel, so PerObject styling won't affect it. Fog will be disabled in apply_look for cleanliness.\n\nWriting the code now. Burst will be wasm-only on SimHost. A music phrase function and shell chart paused method are next. Product.rs comes after. Tests come last. Pav_app compile is the final step.\n\nShell tests will go in surgery/mod.rs so they compile with pav_ui. The egui Area id API needs checking at compile time. draw() renders the title separately from shell.lines(). A touch-only test is being drafted for Shell.\n\nShell tests are being drafted for touch-only mode, attract screen loading, and pad-driven navigation to the menu.\n\nShell tests are being expanded to cover prompt labels for different controllers, hover detection by pointer position, and the dev menu. A slider getter is needed to verify value changes.\n\nThe dev menu test now covers focus movement and tune reset. The settings music nudge path is mapped from title to menu to settings, then rightward. The about screen flow is also defined: confirm on About, then confirm or tab to advance through Credits and Source pages.\n\nKeyboard prompts show Enter. A single test will walk every screen. Mouse clicks activate rows via pointer input. Idle exits attract after ten seconds without input. Three separate tests verify pad, mouse, and keyboard exits from attract.\n\nThe shell idle logic is confirmed: attract loads after ten seconds without input, and any input resets the timer. Next is product.rs, kept under seven hundred lines. Chart screen support requires updating draw, screen_name, and lines match arms.\n\nChart screen lines will show the operation name and a begin prompt. The draw function will add Chart next to Story. Note_mode correctly skips Menu when sim is Title or Story, so it won't reset to Title. Product.rs will handle SetBus commands immediately to keep local audio in sync with the simulation.\n\nProduct will set_buses from the simulation frame when present, otherwise falling back to shell values. This prevents the simulation from overwriting local audio after a SetTune reset. A one-frame lag on native is acceptable.\n\nBus gain is applied before note playback so scheduled notes inherit the current music level. The phrase duration is roughly two seconds, so it will be rescheduled using harbor.music_until as an Instant. Heartbeat cues are handled by play_event.\n\nThe Fog struct is public and enabled. In `apply_look`, `scene.fog.enabled` will be set to false. `App::new` will initialize the harbor field with `product::Harbor::new(touch_screen)`. A `#[path = \"product.rs\"] mod product;` declaration will be added after the existing use statements in `app.rs`.\n\nApp::frame and App::window_event will delegate to product::surgery_frame and product::surgery_event when the scene name starts with \"surgery\". The title screen will be changed in init, and fail() will use a heading. js-sys must be added to the workspace Cargo.toml and the wasm dependencies, while SimHost needs a burst method. No extra web_sys features are required because Window is already present, and wasm_bindgen Closure is already available.\n\nSurgeon input defaults to tool 255 (TOOL_KEEP) so the scalpel does not reset every frame. Tool selection will be written for one tick and then restored to KEEP.\n\nThe latched tool will be sent every tick. The simulation only updates when the input tool is not TOOL_KEEP (255), so sending the selected tool each frame keeps it active.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-b4c0880d-73c8-4811-891f-43b80dfe3397-124","name":"grep","input":{"pattern":"Right stick|keyboard|1–8|left stick","path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224015__x42677a/work/PLAN.md","head_limit":40}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1454,"output_tokens":2652,"cache_read_input_tokens":153088,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa38-de6f-7dc0-ae0d-e0f717ed75f2","uuid":"d5bc8f41-d6d7-4bd1-a2c1-fc714f2db136"}
