01,44,32,50,32,83,113,117,97,114,101,44,32,51,32,84,114,105,97,110,103,108,101,44,32,52,32,76,49,44,32,53,32,82,49,44,32,54,32,76,50,44,32,55,32,82,50,44,32,56,32,67,114,101,97,116,101,44,32,57,32,79,112,116,105,111,110,115,44,32,49,48,32,76,51,44,32,49,49,32,82,51,44,32,49,50,226,128,147,49,53,32,68,45,112,97,100,44,32,49,54,32,80,83,59,32,97,120,101,115,32,48,226,128,147,49,32,108,101,102,116,32,115,116,105,99,107,44,32,50,226,128,147,51,32,114,105,103,104,116,46,32,83,101,116,32,96,118,97,108,117,101,96,32,97,115,32,119,101,108,108,32,97,115,32,96,112,114,101,115,115,101,100,96,32,102,111,114,32,116,114,105,103,103,101,114,115,46,32,65,100,100,32,97,32,115,101,99,111,110,100,32,112,97,100,32,97,116,32,105,110,100,101,120,32,49,32,102,111,114,32,99,111,45,111,112,46,10,60,47,119,111,114,107,115,112,97,99,101,95,114,101,115,117,108,116,62],\"stderr\":[],\"exit_code\":0,\"match_count\":11,\"file_matches\":[{\"path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224015__x42677a/work/PLAN.md\",\"matches\":[{\"line_number\":145,\"content\":\"| Action | DualSense | Mouse + keyboard |\"},{\"line_number\":147,\"content\":\"| Move cursor | Right stick (`v = 15 u/s · s^2.2`) | Mouse (absolute); WASD or arrows also move it for keyboard-only play |\"},{\"line_number\":149,\"content\":\"| Pick tool | Left stick flick, 8 directions, instant (or L1/R1 to cycle) | 1–8, wheel, or click the instrument on the tray |\"},{\"line_number\":150,\"content\":\"| Precision | Hold L2 (×0.35) | Hold Shift (keyboard cursor only; the mouse is already precise) |\"},{\"line_number\":160,\"content\":\"**Aim assist (pad and keyboard cursor only; slider in Settings and dev mode).** Within 1.2 u of a valid\"},{\"line_number\":342,\"content\":\"Title shows **\\\"Controller or keyboard required\\\"** and a Settings button that a tap can use. Attract still\"},{\"line_number\":349,\"content\":\"  shows flick directions on pad or digits on keyboard, via `prompt`. Gift meter beside it, pulsing with its\"},{\"line_number\":631,\"content\":\"- Shell: pad, keyboard and mouse navigation through every screen, hover moves focus, prompts follow last device, Xbox setting, attract\"},{\"line_number\":686,\"content\":\"interview shape exactly and check it parses. Suggested catalogue values (name and tagline are yours): type `Game`; genre `Simulation`; source as your TASK.md's; series `Trauma Center`; players `1–4`; controls such as \\\"Right stick or mouse aims, R2 or left click operates, left stick or 1–8 picks tools\\\"; tags from `3d, story, co-op,\"},{\"line_number\":711,\"content\":\"| 10-foot, DualSense first; native mouse and keyboard; prompts follow input; Xbox glyph setting; no dense screens | §3.2, §5 |\"},{\"line_number\":798,\"content\":\"Standard mapping: 0 Cross, 1 Circle, 2 Square, 3 Triangle, 4 L1, 5 R1, 6 L2, 7 R2, 8 Create, 9 Options, 10 L3, 11 R3, 12–15 D-pad, 16 PS; axes 0–1 left stick, 2–3 right. Set `value` as well as `pressed` for triggers. Add a second pad at index 1 for co-op.\"}]}]}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa38-de6f-7dc0-ae0d-e0f717ed75f2","uuid":"c700b265-ba07-4dab-92cd-bddc71896ed5"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_261","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"WASD and arrow keys move the cursor for keyboard-only input.\n\nWheel and L1/R1 buttons will cycle tools. Clicking near the tool tray selects a tool if the ground point is within 0.4 units. Digits and minus keys will also be mapped. Mouse input will use absolute positioning. Precision mode activates when shift is held with the keyboard cursor.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-61ea3fae-5453-4ff2-a99f-b6d1528e797d-125","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224015__x42677a/work/PLAN.md","offset":140,"limit":40}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":3266,"output_tokens":354,"cache_read_input_tokens":154496,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa38-de6f-7dc0-ae0d-e0f717ed75f2","uuid":"4e073954-9900-46be-b9a6-44edff83f9a4"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-61ea3fae-5453-4ff2-a99f-b6d1528e797d-125","content":"{\"type\":\"ReadFile\",\"FileContent\":{\"content\":\"140→Field space: x ∈ [-11, 11], z ∈ [-6.3, 6.3] (1 unit ≈ 80 px at 1080p). Keep gameplay inside x ∈ [-9, 9],\\nz ∈ [-4, 4.2], clear of the HUD. All game logic is 2D in this plane, with no physics.\\n\\n**Controls**\\n\\n| Action | DualSense | Mouse + keyboard |\\n|---|---|---|\\n| Move cursor | Right stick (`v = 15 u/s · s^2.2`) | Mouse (absolute); WASD or arrows also move it for keyboard-only play |\\n| Use tool | R2, analog (or hold Cross) | Left button (or hold E) |\\n| Pick tool | Left stick flick, 8 directions, instant (or L1/R1 to cycle) | 1–8, wheel, or click the instrument on the tray |\\n150→| Precision | Hold L2 (×0.35) | Hold Shift (keyboard cursor only; the mouse is already precise) |\\n| Cancel, let go | Circle | Right button or Q |\\n| Gift | Triangle | Space |\\n| Chart overlay | Square | Tab |\\n| Rotate held bone | L1/R1 while holding | Wheel while holding |\\n| Defibrillate | L2 + R2 | Both mouse buttons |\\n| Pause | Options (ignored while Create is held: that combination is the hub's) | Esc |\\n\\nThe stick flick is the signature: it must switch tools with no menu and no slowdown.\\n\\n160→**Aim assist (pad and keyboard cursor only; slider in Settings and dev mode).** Within 1.2 u of a valid\\ntarget for the current tool, speed falls by up to 50% and the cursor is pulled toward it at up to\\n3 u/s, only while the stick is moving. While the Scalpel is engaged, sideways error is damped (rail\\nassist). While suturing, the needle creeps along the wound by itself, so the stick only flicks across\\nit. The mouse gets none of this, since it needs none.\\n\\n### 3.3 The instruments\\n\\nThe ring has 8 fixed directions, data-driven per case. Up: Scalpel. Up-right: Forceps. Right: Suture.\\nDown-right: Suction. Down: Laser (Cryoprobe in Case 6). Down-left: Gel. Left: Scanner (Cryoprobe in\\n170→Case 7, where the nodules stay visible). Up-left: IV Push.\\n\\n| Tool | Gesture | Rated on | Misuse |\\n|---|---|---|---|\\n| **Scalpel** | Hold, follow the dashed line in one stroke | Sideways deviation (≤0.25 u is Immaculate) | Cutting healthy tissue makes a small laceration and costs vitals |\\n| **Forceps** | Hold to grab, pull along the object's axis about 1 u, it drops on the tray | Angle error of the pull | Yanking off-axis tears a laceration |\\n| **Suture** | Hold, zigzag across the wound. Each crossing near the advancing needle is a stitch; about 1 per 0.5 u | Evenness of spacing and pace | Sloppy spacing leaves a slow bleed |\\n| **Suction** | Hold over a pool. Analog: harder drains faster, and gurgles louder | None (always Good) | Safe everywhere |\\n| **Laser** | Hold on a target, the heat ring fills in about 1.2 s, release at 80–100% | Release timing | Overheating makes a burn |\\n| **Gel** | Hold and paint until the coverage ring is full. The flow meter refills in seconds | Overspray | Wasted gel |\",\"content_concise\":\"140→Field space: x ∈ [-11, 11], z ∈ [-6.3, 6.3] (1 unit ≈ 80 px at 1080p). Keep gameplay inside x ∈ [-9, 9],\\nz ∈ [-4, 4.2], clear of the HUD. All game logic is 2D in this plane, with no physics.\\n\\n**Controls**\\n\\n| Action | DualSense | Mouse + keyboard |\\n|---|---|---|\\n| Move cursor | Right stick (`v = 15 u/s · s^2.2`) | Mouse (absolute); WASD or arrows also move it for keyboard-only play |\\n| Use tool | R2, analog (or hold Cross) | Left button (or hold E) |\\n| Pick tool | Left stick flick, 8 directions, instant (or L1/R1 to cycle) | 1–8, wheel, or click the instrument on the tray |\\n150→| Precision | Hold L2 (×0.35) | Hold Shift (keyboard cursor only; the mouse is already precise) |\\n| Cancel, let go | Circle | Right button or Q |\\n| Gift | Triangle | Space |\\n| Chart overlay | Square | Tab |\\n| Rotate held bone | L1/R1 while holding | Wheel while holding |\\n| Defibrillate | L2 + R2 | Both mouse buttons |\\n| Pause | Options (ignored while Create is held: that combination is the hub's) | Esc |\\n\\nThe stick flick is the signature: it must switch tools with no menu and no slowdown.\\n\\n160→**Aim assist (pad and keyboard cursor only; slider in Settings and dev mode).** Within 1.2 u of a valid\\ntarget for the current tool, speed falls by up to 50% and the cursor is pulled toward it at up to\\n3 u/s, only while the stick is moving. While the Scalpel is engaged, sideways error is damped (rail\\nassist). While suturing, the needle creeps along the wound by itself, so the stick only flicks across\\nit. The mouse gets none of this, since it needs none.\\n\\n### 3.3 The instruments\\n\\nThe ring has 8 fixed directions, data-driven per case. Up: Scalpel. Up-right: Forceps. Right: Suture.\\nDown-right: Suction. Down: Laser (Cryoprobe in Case 6). Down-left: Gel. Left: Scanner (Cryoprobe in\\n170→Case 7, where the nodules stay visible). Up-left: IV Push.\\n\\n| Tool | Gesture | Rated on | Misuse |\\n|---|---|---|---|\\n| **Scalpel** | Hold, follow the dashed line in one stroke | Sideways deviation (≤0.25 u is Immaculate) | Cutting healthy tissue makes a small laceration and costs vitals |\\n| **Forceps** | Hold to grab, pull along the object's axis about 1 u, it drops on the tray | Angle error of the pull | Yanking off-axis tears a laceration |\\n| **Suture** | Hold, zigzag across the wound. Each crossing near the advancing needle is a stitch; about 1 per 0.5 u | Evenness of spacing and pace | Sloppy spacing leaves a slow bleed |\\n| **Suction** | Hold over a pool. Analog: harder drains faster, and gurgles louder | None (always Good) | Safe everywhere |\\n| **Laser** | Hold on a target, the heat ring fills in about 1.2 s, release at 80–100% | Release timing | Overheating makes a burn |\\n| **Gel** | Hold and paint until the coverage ring is full. The flow meter refills in seconds | Overspray | Wasted gel |\",\"absolute_path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224015__x42677a/work/PLAN.md\",\"offset\":140,\"limit\":40,\"raw_output\":\"Field space: x ∈ [-11, 11], z ∈ [-6.3, 6.3] (1 unit ≈ 80 px at 1080p). Keep gameplay inside x ∈ [-9, 9],\\nz ∈ [-4, 4.2], clear of the HUD. All game logic is 2D in this plane, with no physics.\\n\\n**Controls**\\n\\n| Action | DualSense | Mouse + keyboard |\\n|---|---|---|\\n| Move cursor | Right stick (`v = 15 u/s · s^2.2`) | Mouse (absolute); WASD or arrows also move it for keyboard-only play |\\n| Use tool | R2, analog (or hold Cross) | Left button (or hold E) |\\n| Pick tool | Left stick flick, 8 directions, instant (or L1/R1 to cycle) | 1–8, wheel, or click the instrument on the tray |\\n| Precision | Hold L2 (×0.35) | Hold Shift (keyboard cursor only; the mouse is already precise) |\\n| Cancel, let go | Circle | Right button or Q |\\n| Gift | Triangle | Space |\\n| Chart overlay | Square | Tab |\\n| Rotate held bone | L1/R1 while holding | Wheel while holding |\\n| Defibrillate | L2 + R2 | Both mouse buttons |\\n| Pause | Options (ignored while Create is held: that combination is the hub's) | Esc |\\n\\nThe stick flick is the signature: it must switch tools with no menu and no slowdown.\\n\\n**Aim assist (pad and keyboard cursor only; slider in Settings and dev mode).** Within 1.2 u of a valid\\ntarget for the current tool, speed falls by up to 50% and the cursor is pulled toward it at up to\\n3 u/s, only while the stick is moving. While the Scalpel is engaged, sideways error is damped (rail\\nassist). While suturing, the needle creeps along the wound by itself, so the stick only flicks across\\nit. The mouse gets none of this, since it needs none.\\n\\n### 3.3 The instruments\\n\\nThe ring has 8 fixed directions, data-driven per case. Up: Scalpel. Up-right: Forceps. Right: Suture.\\nDown-right: Suction. Down: Laser (Cryoprobe in Case 6). Down-left: Gel. Left: Scanner (Cryoprobe in\\nCase 7, where the nodules stay visible). Up-left: IV Push.\\n\\n| Tool | Gesture | Rated on | Misuse |\\n|---|---|---|---|\\n| **Scalpel** | Hold, follow the dashed line in one stroke | Sideways deviation (≤0.25 u is Immaculate) | Cutting healthy tissue makes a small laceration and costs vitals |\\n| **Forceps** | Hold to grab, pull along the object's axis about 1 u, it drops on the tray | Angle error of the pull | Yanking off-axis tears a laceration |\\n| **Suture** | Hold, zigzag across the wound. Each crossing near the advancing needle is a stitch; about 1 per 0.5 u | Evenness of spacing and pace | Sloppy spacing leaves a slow bleed |\\n| **Suction** | Hold over a pool. Analog: harder drains faster, and gurgles louder | None (always Good) | Safe everywhere |\\n| **Laser** | Hold on a target, the heat ring fills in about 1.2 s, release at 80–100% | Release timing | Overheating makes a burn |\\n| **Gel** | Hold and paint until the coverage ring is full. The flow meter refills in seconds | Overspray | Wasted gel |\\n\",\"total_lines\":811}}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa38-de6f-7dc0-ae0d-e0f717ed75f2","uuid":"ae89c8ff-f438-40bd-95d7-b89ef3e641c3"}
