{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-a8ddd041-2291-4e3d-aa63-1a56fbc9e96c-160","content":"{\"type\":\"GrepSearch\",\"stdout\":[60,119,111,114,107,115,112,97,99,101,95,114,101,115,117,108,116,32,119,111,114,107,115,112,97,99,101,95,112,97,116,104,61,34,47,104,111,109,101,47,109,105,99,104,97,47,100,101,118,47,99,99,45,109,97,116,114,105,120,47,114,117,110,115,47,103,114,111,107,45,120,104,105,103,104,46,98,117,105,108,100,45,118,50,95,95,50,48,50,54,49,49,48,52,45,50,50,52,48,49,53,95,95,120,52,50,54,55,55,97,47,119,111,114,107,34,62,10,70,111,117,110,100,32,49,32,109,97,116,99,104,105,110,103,32,108,105,110,101,115,10,47,104,111,109,101,47,109,105,99,104,97,47,100,101,118,47,99,99,45,109,97,116,114,105,120,47,114,117,110,115,47,103,114,111,107,45,120,104,105,103,104,46,98,117,105,108,100,45,118,50,95,95,50,48,50,54,49,49,48,52,45,50,50,52,48,49,53,95,95,120,52,50,54,55,55,97,47,119,111,114,107,47,101,110,103,105,110,101,45,108,105,110,107,47,99,114,97,116,101,115,47,112,97,118,95,99,111,114,101,47,115,114,99,47,108,105,98,46,114,115,10,54,51,58,112,117,98,32,117,115,101,32,105,110,112,117,116,58,58,73,110,112,117,116,70,114,97,109,101,59,10,60,47,119,111,114,107,115,112,97,99,101,95,114,101,115,117,108,116,62],\"stderr\":[],\"exit_code\":0,\"match_count\":1,\"file_matches\":[{\"path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224015__x42677a/work/engine-link/crates/pav_core/src/lib.rs\",\"matches\":[{\"line_number\":63,\"content\":\"pub use input::InputFrame;\"}]}]}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa38-de6f-7dc0-ae0d-e0f717ed75f2","uuid":"897f716e-2926-49a1-8ce4-d759edf32a1c"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_274","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"SurgeryCmd is located in the pav_core::input module.\n\nSurgeonInput is in the same module. TOOL_KEEP is in pav_core::games::surgery. I am writing product.rs and mapping shell commands to SurgeryCmd.\n\nRetry, SetTune, ResetTune, SetBus, and Dev map directly to SurgeryCmd variants. ConfirmSim is omitted from the shell-to-sim mapping because the title screen ignores it; it is only emitted from story, results, card, and chart states.\n\nConfirm on the HUD does nothing in the shell. The pad's Cross button is both use and confirm, so passing confirm during HUD is a no-op. Circle opens pause, but I am unsure if CANCEL should also be sent.\n\nCANCEL will only be sent when opening pause is not the current action. A stray cancel tick before pausing is acceptable. During pause, USE input is suppressed. Keyboard aim is disabled outside HUD states to prevent arrow keys from moving the cursor.\n\nMouse hover maps to the shell pointer. During HUD states, only back is sent to the shell; up and down are suppressed to avoid conflicting with cursor navigation.\n\nConfirm and pointer input are suppressed during the op screen. Mouse clicks there map to USE instead of shell click.\n\nDevice type is determined by pad activity first, then keyboard or mouse. The any input flag covers key presses, mouse movement, and pad events to exit attract mode.\n\nTouch input is recorded in surgery_event. Gamepad events are drained directly from gilrs to prevent Start from opening the engine menu.\n\nThe `poll_pads` method drains all gilrs events and resets the pad count. It then reads up to four gamepads, mapping left and right stick axes, buttons, and triggers into the `PadHand` struct.\n\nButton states will be stored as a small struct of booleans. The left stick deadzone is set to 0.18. Eight tool octants map to the left stick: up, up-right, right, down-right, down, down-left, left, and up-left. atan2 with y-up and x-right is being calculated to assign each direction to its tool index.\n\nThe left stick angle is computed with `stick.x.atan2(stick.y)` and mapped to tool octants by dividing by `FRAC_PI_4`, rounding, and taking modulo 8. Up maps to tool 0, up-right to tool 1, right to tool 2, and down-right to tool 3.\n\nDown-left maps to tool 5 (gel), left to tool 6 (scanner), and up-left to tool 7 (IV). The octant is only selected when the stick magnitude exceeds 0.55 and differs from the previous frame. L1 and R1 are mapped to gilrs LeftTrigger and RightTrigger; holding use sets ROT, while pressing cycles tools. Digits 1–8 select tools 0–7, 9 selects cryo, and 0 selects dressing.\n\nMinus selects defib tool 10. The mouse wheel selects tools when USE is held, otherwise it rotates. Both mouse buttons and L2/R2 analog pressure hold DEFIB. Cross and South are USE. E and left mouse press USE. Q and right mouse press CANCEL. Space and North press GIFT. Tab and West press CHART. Shift and L2 press PRECISION. Options, Start, and Esc trigger pause. Dpad and South/East handle menu navigation outside op. Dpad may also navigate during op.\n\nDpad will be reserved for menus only. Enter confirms and Esc exits menus; arrows navigate menus while WASD aims during operation. Mouse ground point requires setting rig parameters before calling snap. I am checking whether assigning CameraParams updates the rig's internal state.\n\nKeyboard aim is built from WASD or arrow keys into a normalized vector, then shaped and inverted for world space. Mouse movement overrides keyboard aim. The right stick on each pad maps to its corresponding slot.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-a3051d1e-6d84-47c3-9c16-05b15c12d4c3-161","name":"grep","input":{"pattern":"pressure","path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224015__x42677a/work/engine-link/crates/pav_core/src/games/surgery/hazard.rs"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":445,"output_tokens":2632,"cache_read_input_tokens":175232,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa38-de6f-7dc0-ae0d-e0f717ed75f2","uuid":"057ba56d-646f-4e88-bdfc-68661b5eb783"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-a3051d1e-6d84-47c3-9c16-05b15c12d4c3-161","content":"{\"type\":\"GrepSearch\",\"stdout\":[60,119,111,114,107,115,112,97,99,101,95,114,101,115,117,108,116,32,119,111,114,107,115,112,97,99,101,95,112,97,116,104,61,34,47,104,111,109,101,47,109,105,99,104,97,47,100,101,118,47,99,99,45,109,97,116,114,105,120,47,114,117,110,115,47,103,114,111,107,45,120,104,105,103,104,46,98,117,105,108,100,45,118,50,95,95,50,48,50,54,49,49,48,52,45,50,50,52,48,49,53,95,95,120,52,50,54,55,55,97,47,119,111,114,107,34,62,10,70,111,117,110,100,32,50,32,109,97,116,99,104,105,110,103,32,108,105,110,101,115,10,47,104,111,109,101,47,109,105,99,104,97,47,100,101,118,47,99,99,45,109,97,116,114,105,120,47,114,117,110,115,47,103,114,111,107,45,120,104,105,103,104,46,98,117,105,108,100,45,118,50,95,95,50,48,50,54,49,49,48,52,45,50,50,52,48,49,53,95,95,120,52,50,54,55,55,97,47,119,111,114,107,47,101,110,103,105,110,101,45,108,105,110,107,47,99,114,97,116,101,115,47,112,97,118,95,99,111,114,101,47,115,114,99,47,103,97,109,101,115,47,115,117,114,103,101,114,121,47,104,97,122,97,114,100,46,114,115,10,50,56,55,58,32,32,32,32,112,114,101,115,115,117,114,101,58,32,102,51,50,44,10,51,48,48,58,32,32,32,32,108,101,116,32,112,32,61,32,112,114,101,115,115,117,114,101,46,99,108,97,109,112,40,48,46,49,53,44,32,49,46,48,41,32,42,32,112,111,119,101,114,46,109,97,120,40,48,46,50,41,59,10,60,47,119,111,114,107,115,112,97,99,101,95,114,101,115,117,108,116,62],\"stderr\":[],\"exit_code\":0,\"match_count\":2,\"file_matches\":[{\"path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224015__x42677a/work/engine-link/crates/pav_core/src/games/surgery/hazard.rs\",\"matches\":[{\"line_number\":287,\"content\":\"    pressure: f32,\"},{\"line_number\":300,\"content\":\"    let p = pressure.clamp(0.15, 1.0) * power.max(0.2);\"}]}]}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa38-de6f-7dc0-ae0d-e0f717ed75f2","uuid":"88978d76-2827-4b31-aab2-caaa864da0ad"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_275","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Pressure is clamped to a minimum of 0.15 during the gesture.\n\nPressure values will be clamped to 0.15 for digital input and passed through as-is for analog input. Next steps include writing product.rs, appending shell tests to surgery/mod.rs, wiring the application, adding js-sys dependencies, verifying gilrs availability, using winit 0.30's set_cursor_visible, and adjusting egui run_ui output handling.\n\nZoom is calculated from window height and native scale factor. The font is installed once. Drawing happens inside run_ui without boot visuals. Platform output, tessellation, and rendering follow. Cursor visibility depends on mode. Audio events are handled. Music phrases reschedule when the track changes. Old notes continue until finished. Server skip logic is deferred.\n\nThe builder plate will always be drawn for now. The hub is next.\n\nA `publish_status` function is being drafted to send a JSON status update over the shell. It includes screen name, focus state, device type, Xbox mode, formatted music level, and the game title.\n\nThe status string will also include cursor data from the operation. A `window.__game.status()` hook is installed on the first surgery frame for WASM launch tests. Window attributes are set before creation to prevent winit from overwriting the title. Scene names starting with \"surgery\" are handled correctly. The file is ready to be written.\n\nThe `surgery_frame` function is being structured to avoid borrow checker issues. It checks that both `gfx` and `host` are present, calculates a capped delta time, polls gamepads through the harbor, drives the simulation, and updates the host's paused state.\n\nThe `surgery_frame` function is being restructured to avoid holding borrows on the app during the simulation step. The harbor will return commands and surgeon inputs through a `build_frame` method, which are then applied to the host control block.\n\nCommands are applied to the simulation state via `host.exec`. Surgeon inputs are updated from the harbor results, with confirmation toggled when requested. The host is then pumped.\n\nThe `build_frame` method needs mouse position and key state from the harbor. Ground point calculation requires the rig, so a closure that borrows both `app.rig` and `app.harbor` is impossible. The code will instead update rig parameters and snap the target first, then compute the aim separately.\n\nThe `compose` method will use the stored mouse aim and key state from the harbor. The `surgery_event` handler updates the harbor, egui, and window state for resize, redraw, and close. Closing exits the loop without saving a shardfall save. Redraw triggers `surgery_frame`. Touch events are mapped to a touch-only flag and click detection.\n\nTouch-only mode is gated by `ever_fine`, which only becomes true for keyboard, pad, or mouse input. This prevents a laptop with a touchscreen from getting stuck in touch-only mode when the mouse is used first. The `touch_only` flag is set exclusively from Touch events and initialized at Harbor creation.\n\nAudio will be resumed on WASM when the first key, mouse, or pad event arrives. The font is installed once inside `surgery_frame`. I am checking whether egui 0.36 supports `set_zoom_factor` or requires `set_pixels_per_point` instead. I will write the file, append shell tests, add `js-sys` to Cargo.toml, edit `app.rs`, and verify `session.rs` dependencies.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-b3439f6d-ce15-4728-86c7-d1febf46ce31-162","name":"grep","input":{"pattern":"^use |glam","path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224015__x42677a/work/engine-link/crates/pav_tools/src/session.rs","head_limit":20}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-b3439f6d-ce15-4728-86c7-d1febf46ce31-163","name":"grep","input":{"pattern":"fn step\\(","path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224015__x42677a/work/engine-link/crates/pav_core/src/sim.rs"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2850,"output_tokens":2003,"cache_read_input_tokens":175616,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa38-de6f-7dc0-ae0d-e0f717ed75f2","uuid":"30fbc0b2-db29-485d-8550-62ce8d04dacd"}
