101,110,100,101,114,70,114,97,109,101,32,123,10,60,47,119,111,114,107,115,112,97,99,101,95,114,101,115,117,108,116,62],\"stderr\":[],\"exit_code\":0,\"match_count\":1,\"file_matches\":[{\"path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224015__x42677a/work/engine-link/crates/pav_core/src/sim.rs\",\"matches\":[{\"line_number\":941,\"content\":\"    pub fn frame(&mut self) -> RenderFrame {\"}]}]}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa38-de6f-7dc0-ae0d-e0f717ed75f2","uuid":"af1b5753-e44e-43ce-afdd-8f536f5d8208"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_278","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Removing play_status from RenderFrame and using op fields only.\n\nFixing status_json. Wiring app.rs with product module, harbor field, new(), early frame and window_event handling, title, and fail. Adding js-sys dependency.\n\nFixing edge detection for pad buttons. Adding previous button states to Harbor so held inputs don't repeat every frame.\n\nAdding `prev_menu` to Harbor for pad 0. Fixing compose so pad up, south, and start act as edges instead of held inputs. `tools_from_hands` already handles its first-frame prev state correctly.\n\nConfirmed the tray click fires before compose clears it. Removing the unused `pressed` variable in hand logic and the unused `edge_pad` function. Fixing the play_status compile error and simplifying status_json to drop the RenderFrame parameter.\n\njs-sys is now an optional wasm-only dependency. Confirmed shell device and note_mode are public. Found a bug in input ordering: shell step runs before tools_from_hands, so navigation keys are consumed after the shell step.\n\nConfirmed digit and arrow key handling is correct. Space and Enter work properly on menus. Found an operator precedence bug in the confirm expression: `ate(Space) && !op` binds incorrectly within the OR chain.\n\nConfirmed that Space is consumed from the key buffer even when op is active, but gift still sees it via key(). The held start button will be fixed with edge detection. Verified that RenderFrame exposes surgery.\n\nConfirmed `builder.add_events` exists on `ViewBuilder`. Ignoring the `gfx.draw` return value is fine. `set_cursor_visible` may need a boolean argument in winit 0.30. A borrow checker issue appeared in `surgery_frame`: `poll_pads` requires mutable access to both `app.harbor` and `app.input.gilrs`, which Rust forbids as split borrows. The fix will extract `gilrs` out of `app.input` before calling `poll_pads`.\n\nThe split borrow is resolved by extracting pad data into a free function `read_pads` before mutating `app.harbor`. This lets `aim_rig` and `compose` borrow the app sequentially without overlapping mutable borrows.\n\nRestructuring host access into scoped blocks so the borrow ends before app is used again.\n\nBorrowing `frames()` returns owned `Arc`s, so the host borrow ends immediately. Audio and harbor access must be split: notes are computed from op and harbor first, then applied to audio only after that borrow is released.\n\nZoom factor must be set on the egui context before the graphics borrow begins. The `take` call on `egui_state` still conflicts with the gfx borrow because both require mutable access to `app`.\n\nRust 2021 allows split mutable borrows of different fields. `app.gfx` and `app.egui_state` are separate fields, so the `take` call can borrow both without scoping. The same applies to `harbor` and `input`, so the earlier concern about overlapping mutable borrows was mistaken.\n\nReconsidering the split borrow assumption. A method call like `app.harbor.poll_pads(app.input.gilrs.as_mut())` may not actually be allowed as a split borrow, because the compiler sees the receiver and argument as overlapping mutable borrows of the same struct. The earlier conclusion that Rust 2021 allows this pattern across method calls was likely wrong.\n\nConfirmed that `harbor.poll_pads` with a separate `gilrs` borrow is valid Rust and will keep the current code. The audio borrow conflict will be avoided by computing music timing before accessing audio. All menu pad buttons, including down, will be switched to edge detection.\n\nDeriving `Copy` and `Clone` on `PadHand` so it can be stored as a previous-state field. Adding `menu_was` to `Harbor` to track pad 0's prior state for edge detection. Removing the `edge_pad` helper and the `pav_core::RenderFrame` reference.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-d2b87e1e-bce3-4c94-9162-65316812d23c-167","name":"grep","input":{"pattern":"fn add_events|pub now","path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224015__x42677a/work/engine-link/crates/pav_view/src/build.rs"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-d2b87e1e-bce3-4c94-9162-65316812d23c-168","name":"grep","input":{"pattern":"pub surgery","path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224015__x42677a/work/engine-link/crates/pav_core/src/frame.rs"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":426,"output_tokens":2705,"cache_read_input_tokens":188288,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa38-de6f-7dc0-ae0d-e0f717ed75f2","uuid":"d200ae7f-e1ae-4e6f-9b66-40a733fd8ce1"}
