{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_282","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Another issue has appeared after the shell.\n\nConfirmed mouse ownership stays active during hand construction and tool creation. Menu interactions correctly skip hand calls. Now wiring app.rs. Need to check a potential borrow conflict between surgery_frame and host.\n\nChecking the function now and will fix it if compilation fails. The frame order is correct: shell sets the story first, then exec boots the campaign, then note_mode applies mode changes. Menu mode correctly skips title resets.\n\nFound a bug in the mode skip list. Title is not included, so when a user exits attract mode and the shell sets Title, note_mode would immediately overwrite it back to Attract before the simulation updates.\n\nWASM handles the mode transition correctly because exec runs synchronously before note_mode. On native, exec is asynchronous, so note_mode may briefly see the old attract mode and snap the screen back to Attract. Because Attract is in the skip list, the screen then stays stuck on Attract forever.\n\nThe simplest fix is to skip note_mode when the shell screen is Title, Menu, or Settings. This prevents the simulation from snapping back to Attract before exec applies the new mode.\n\nThe fix is to call note_mode only when the shell screen is driven by the simulation, such as op, story, chart, results, dead, card, attract, or title. Menu and other non-driven screens are skipped. This prevents the simulation from snapping back to Attract before exec applies the new mode.\n\nThe skip-list fix alone still fails on native because note_mode can fire while the shell is already on Title but the simulation mode is still Attract. The plan is to add an explicit guard: if the shell screen is Title and the operation mode is attract, skip note_mode so the title transition can land before the simulation snaps back.\n\nLoadCampaign sets the shell to Story, but on native note_mode still sees title mode and snaps the screen back to Title before exec applies. The fix is to restrict note_mode to simulation modes that represent a result of play, and never override the shell when the shell is already ahead.\n\nThe guard is being refined to a match on the operation mode. When the simulation mode is title, note_mode will only run if the shell screen is attract or title. This prevents the simulation from snapping back to title before exec applies the new mode.\n\nThe final rule is to skip note_mode entirely when the shell is on a menu screen. Otherwise it applies the operation mode directly.\n\nOn native, LoadCampaign briefly flashes Title before the simulation mode catches up and corrects it. This one-frame glitch is acceptable.\n\nThe packed game is built for WASM, so the native race condition is less critical. Removing Attract from the skip list would let note_mode reset the idle timer every frame while attract mode is active.\n\nThe skip list will remain unchanged. Removing Attract from it would let note_mode reset the shell's title transition on native before exec applies the new mode, even though WASM order prevents this. A comment will be added to explain the dependency on WASM execution order.\n\nThe fix is being applied directly inside `note_mode`. When the shell screen is Attract and the simulation mode is still 6, the function will skip resetting. This prevents the simulation from snapping back to Attract before exec applies the new mode. When the mode changes to title, the reset proceeds normally.\n\nThe `leaving_attract` check is insufficient because the shell screen is already Title. The fix is to return early from `note_mode` when the shell is on Title and the simulation mode is still Attract. This prevents the simulation from snapping back to Attract while the exit command is in flight. On native, the shell stays on Title until the next frame when the mode finally updates to 0. On WASM, the mode is already correct so the title transition lands immediately.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-3e6cb3ee-81ac-4de5-a71f-8a3b5b3bf32c-184","name":"search_replace","input":{"file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224015__x42677a/work/engine-link/crates/pav_ui/src/surgery/mod.rs","old_string":"    pub fn note_mode(&mut self, mode: u8) {\n        self.sim_mode = mode;\n        if self.paused","new_string":"    pub fn note_mode(&mut self, mode: u8) {\n        self.sim_mode = mode;\n        // A load or a return to the title can land a frame before the sim does.\n        if self.screen == Screen::Title && mode == 6 {\n            return;\n        }\n        if matches!(self.screen, Screen::Story | Screen::Hud | Screen::Chart) && mode == 0 {\n            return;\n        }\n        if self.paused"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-3e6cb3ee-81ac-4de5-a71f-8a3b5b3bf32c-185","name":"search_replace","input":{"file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224015__x42677a/work/engine-link/crates/pav_app/src/app.rs","old_string":"use crate::ui::{self, MenuAction};\nuse crate::uiinput::UiInput;","new_string":"use crate::ui::{self, MenuAction};\nuse crate::uiinput::UiInput;\n\n#[path = \"product.rs\"]\nmod product;"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-3e6cb3ee-81ac-4de5-a71f-8a3b5b3bf32c-186","name":"search_replace","input":{"file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224015__x42677a/work/engine-link/crates/pav_app/src/app.rs","old_string":"    init_started: bool,\n    pub fatal: Option<String>,\n}","new_string":"    init_started: bool,\n    harbor: product::Harbor,\n    pub fatal: Option<String>,\n}"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-3e6cb3ee-81ac-4de5-a71f-8a3b5b3bf32c-187","name":"search_replace","input":{"file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224015__x42677a/work/engine-link/crates/pav_app/src/app.rs","old_string":"            init_started: false,\n            fatal: None,\n            settings,\n        };","new_string":"            init_started: false,\n            harbor: product::Harbor::new(touch_screen),\n            fatal: None,\n            settings,\n        };"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-3e6cb3ee-81ac-4de5-a71f-8a3b5b3bf32c-188","name":"search_replace","input":{"file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224015__x42677a/work/engine-link/crates/pav_app/src/app.rs","old_string":"            let mut attrs = Window::default_attributes().with_title(\"Shardfall\");","new_string":"            let title = if s.scene.starts_with(\"surgery\") { pav_core::games::surgery::TITLE } else { \"Shardfall\" };\n            let mut attrs = Window::default_attributes().with_title(title);"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-3e6cb3ee-81ac-4de5-a71f-8a3b5b3bf32c-189","name":"search_replace","input":{"file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224015__x42677a/work/engine-link/crates/pav_app/src/app.rs","old_string":"    fn frame(&mut self) {\n        if self.gfx.is_none() || self.host.is_none() {\n            return;\n        }","new_string":"    fn frame(&mut self) {\n        if self.scene_name.starts_with(\"surgery\") {\n            product::surgery_frame(self);\n            return;\n        }\n        if self.gfx.is_none() || self.host.is_none() {\n            return;\n        }"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-3e6cb3ee-81ac-4de5-a71f-8a3b5b3bf32c-190","name":"search_replace","input":{"file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224015__x42677a/work/engine-link/crates/pav_app/src/app.rs","old_string":"        let msg = format!(\"{e:#}\");\n        #[cfg(target_arch = \"wasm32\")]\n        crate::platform::error_box(\"Shardfall could not start\", &msg);","new_string":"        let msg = format!(\"{e:#}\");\n        let heading = if self.scene_name.starts_with(\"surgery\") {\n            format!(\"{} could not start\", pav_core::games::surgery::TITLE)\n        } else {\n            \"Shardfall could not start\".to_string()\n        };\n        #[cfg(target_arch = \"wasm32\")]\n        crate::platform::error_box(&heading, &msg);"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-3e6cb3ee-81ac-4de5-a71f-8a3b5b3bf32c-191","name":"search_replace","input":{"file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224015__x42677a/work/engine-link/crates/pav_app/src/app.rs","old_string":"    fn window_event(&mut self, el: &ActiveEventLoop, _id: WindowId, event: WindowEvent) {\n        if let WindowEvent::Touch(t) = &event {","new_string":"    fn window_event(&mut self, el: &ActiveEventLoop, id: WindowId, event: WindowEvent) {\n        if self.scene_name.starts_with(\"surgery\") {\n            product::surgery_event(self, el, id, event);\n            return;\n        }\n        if let WindowEvent::Touch(t) = &event {"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-3e6cb3ee-81ac-4de5-a71f-8a3b5b3bf32c-192","name":"search_replace","input":{"file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224015__x42677a/work/engine-link/Cargo.toml","old_string":"wasm-bindgen = \"0.2\"","new_string":"wasm-bindgen = \"0.2\"\njs-sys = \"0.3\""}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-3e6cb3ee-81ac-4de5-a71f-8a3b5b3bf32c-193","name":"search_replace","input":{"file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224015__x42677a/work/engine-link/crates/pav_app/Cargo.toml","old_string":"wasm-bindgen.workspace = true\nwasm-bindgen-futures.workspace = true","new_string":"wasm-bindgen.workspace = true\nwasm-bindgen-futures.workspace = true\njs-sys.workspace = true"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":806,"output_tokens":3575,"cache_read_input_tokens":197376,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa38-de6f-7dc0-ae0d-e0f717ed75f2","uuid":"137964d6-8a83-47ae-aeeb-45fab02eaa88"}
