{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-2fa4da2f-ec21-4337-8fa3-9155f0b541bd-45","content":"{\"type\":\"ReadFile\",\"FileContent\":{\"content\":\"150→    }\\n\\n    pub fn paused(&self) -> bool {\\n        self.paused\\n    }\\n\\n    pub fn note_mode(&mut self, mode: u8) {\\n        self.sim_mode = mode;\\n        // A load or a return to the title can land a frame before the sim does.\\n        if self.screen == Screen::Title && mode == 6 {\\n160→            return;\\n        }\\n        if matches!(self.screen, Screen::Story | Screen::Hud | Screen::Chart) && mode == 0 {\\n            return;\\n        }\\n        if self.paused\\n            || matches!(\\n                self.screen,\\n                Screen::Menu\\n                    | Screen::Difficulty\\n170→                    | Screen::Files\\n                    | Screen::Settings\\n                    | Screen::About\\n                    | Screen::Controls\\n                    | Screen::Pause\\n                    | Screen::Dev\\n                    | Screen::Attract\\n            )\\n        {\\n            return;\\n180→        }\\n        self.screen = match mode {\\n            1 => Screen::Story,\\n            2 => Screen::Chart,\\n            3 => Screen::Hud,\\n            4 => Screen::Results,\\n            5 => Screen::Dead,\\n            6 => Screen::Attract,\\n            7 => Screen::Card,\\n            _ => Screen::Title,\\n190→        };\\n    }\\n\\n    pub fn prompt(&self, action: &str) -> &'static str {\\n        let pad = self.device == DeviceKind::Gamepad;\\n        match action {\\n            \\\"confirm\\\" => {\\n                if !pad {\\n                    \\\"Enter\\\"\\n                } else if self.xbox {\\n200→                    \\\"A\\\"\\n                } else {\\n                    \\\"Cross\\\"\\n                }\\n            }\\n            \\\"back\\\" => {\\n                if !pad {\\n                    \\\"Esc\\\"\\n                } else if self.xbox {\\n                    \\\"B\\\"\\n210→                } else {\\n                    \\\"Circle\\\"\\n                }\\n            }\\n            \\\"use\\\" => {\\n                if !pad {\\n                    \\\"LMB\\\"\\n                } else if self.xbox {\\n                    \\\"RT\\\"\\n                } else {\\n220→                    \\\"R2\\\"\\n                }\\n            }\\n            \\\"gift\\\" => {\\n                if !pad {\\n                    \\\"G\\\"\\n                } else if self.xbox {\\n                    \\\"Y\\\"\\n                } else {\\n                    \\\"Triangle\\\"\\n230→                }\\n            }\\n            \\\"chart\\\" => {\\n                if !pad {\\n                    \\\"Tab\\\"\\n                } else if self.xbox {\\n                    \\\"X\\\"\\n                } else {\\n                    \\\"Square\\\"\\n                }\\n240→            }\\n            \\\"pause\\\" => {\\n                if pad {\\n                    \\\"Options\\\"\\n                } else {\\n                    \\\"Esc\\\"\\n                }\\n            }\\n            _ => \\\" \\\",\\n        }\\n250→    }\\n\\n    pub fn lines(&self) -> Vec<String> {\\n        let mut v = Vec::new();\\n        v.push(TITLE.to_string());\\n        match self.screen {\\n            Screen::Title => {\\n                v.push(\\\"Mercy Harbor General  ·  Night Ward\\\".into());\\n                v.push(format!(\\\"Press {} \\\", self.prompt(\\\"confirm\\\")));\\n                if self.touch_only && !self.ever_fine {\\n260→                    v.push(\\\"Controller or keyboard required\\\".into());\\n                    v.push(\\\"Settings\\\".into());\\n                }\\n            }\\n            Screen::Menu => {\\n                for (i, item) in [\\\"Continue\\\", \\\"New Game\\\", \\\"Case Files\\\", \\\"Code Blue\\\", \\\"Settings\\\", \\\"About\\\"].iter().enumerate() {\\n                    v.push(self.row(i, item));\\n                }\\n            }\\n            Screen::Difficulty => {\\n270→                for (i, item) in [\\\"Resident\\\", \\\"Attending\\\", \\\"Chief\\\"].iter().enumerate() {\\n                    v.push(self.row(i, item));\\n                }\\n            }\\n            Screen::Files => {\\n                for i in 0..8 {\\n                    let rank = [\\\"\\\", \\\"C\\\", \\\"B\\\", \\\"A\\\", \\\"S\\\", \\\"ENCORE\\\"][self.best[i] as usize];\\n                    v.push(self.row(i, &format!(\\\"Case {}  {rank}\\\", i + 1)));\\n                }\\n            }\\n280→            Screen::Settings => {\\n                v.push(format!(\\\"Page {}\\\", self.settings_page + 1));\\n                match self.settings_page {\\n                    0 => {\\n                        v.push(self.row(0, &format!(\\\"Music  {:.2}  default 0.10\\\", self.music)));\\n                        v.push(self.row(1, &format!(\\\"Effects  {:.2}  default 0.80\\\", self.effects)));\\n                        v.push(self.row(2, &format!(\\\"Voices  {:.2}  default 0.70\\\", self.voices)));\\n                    }\\n                    1 => {\\n                        v.push(self.row(0, if self.xbox { \\\"Prompts  Xbox\\\" } else { \\\"Prompts  PlayStation\\\" }));\\n290→                        v.push(self.row(1, &format!(\\\"Cursor speed  {:.0}\\\", self.sliders[8])));\\n                        v.push(self.row(2, \\\"Rumble\\\"));\\n                    }\\n                    _ => {\\n                        v.push(self.row(0, \\\"Field  Anatomical\\\"));\\n                        v.push(self.row(1, \\\"Fullscreen\\\"));\\n                    }\\n                }\\n            }\\n            Screen::About => {\\n300→                v.push(about_page_title(self.about_page).into());\\n                v.extend(about_lines(self.about_page));\\n            }\\n            Screen::Controls => {\\n                v.push(format!(\\\"Aim   right stick or mouse   {}\\\", self.prompt(\\\"use\\\")));\\n                v.push(\\\"Tools   left stick or 1-8\\\".into());\\n                v.push(format!(\\\"Operate   {}\\\", self.prompt(\\\"use\\\")));\\n                v.push(format!(\\\"Gift   {}\\\", self.prompt(\\\"gift\\\")));\\n                v.push(format!(\\\"Chart   {}\\\", self.prompt(\\\"chart\\\")));\\n            }\\n310→            Screen::Pause => {\\n                for (i, item) in [\\\"Resume\\\", \\\"Restart\\\", \\\"Controls\\\", \\\"Settings\\\", \\\"Dev Mode\\\", \\\"Quit to Title\\\"].iter().enumerate() {\\n                    v.push(self.row(i, item));\\n                }\\n            }\\n            Screen::Dev => {\\n                v.push(self.row(0, if self.live { \\\"Live  on\\\" } else { \\\"Live  off\\\" }));\\n                v.push(self.row(1, if self.bot_plays { \\\"Bot plays  on\\\" } else { \\\"Bot plays  off\\\" }));\\n                let start = self.dev_page as usize * 6;\\n                for i in 0..6 {\\n320→                    let id = start + i;\\n                    if id >= Tune::FIELDS.len() {\\n                        break;\\n                    }\\n                    let (name, def, _, _) = Tune::FIELDS[id];\\n                    v.push(self.row(i + 2, &format!(\\\"{name}  {:.2}  default {def:.2}\\\", self.sliders[id])));\\n                }\\n                v.push(self.row(8, \\\"Reset All\\\"));\\n            }\\n            Screen::Attract => {\\n330→                v.push(\\\"DEMO\\\".into());\\n                v.push(format!(\\\"Press {}\\\", self.prompt(\\\"confirm\\\")));\\n            }\\n            Screen::Hud => {\\n                v.push(\\\"OPERATION\\\".into());\\n            }\\n            Screen::Story => v.push(\\\"Advance\\\".into()),\\n            Screen::Results => v.push(\\\"Results\\\".into()),\\n            Screen::Dead => v.push(self.row(0, \\\"Retry\\\")),\\n            Screen::Card => {\\n340→                v.push(\\\"Pre-op\\\".into());\\n                v.push(\\\"Keep the patient alive\\\".into());\\n                v.push(format!(\\\"{} ready\\\", self.prompt(\\\"confirm\\\")));\\n            }\\n            Screen::Chart => {\\n                v.push(\\\"Chart\\\".into());\\n                v.push(\\\"Begin the operation\\\".into());\\n                v.push(format!(\\\"{} begin\\\", self.prompt(\\\"confirm\\\")));\\n            }\\n        }\\n350→        v\\n    }\\n\\n    fn row(&self, i: usize, label: &str) -> String {\\n        if i == self.focus {\\n            format!(\\\"> {label}\\\")\\n        } else {\\n            label.to_string()\\n        }\\n    }\\n360→\\n    pub fn step(&mut self, input: Input) -> Vec<Cmd> {\\n        if let Some(d) = input.device {\\n            self.device = d;\\n            if d == DeviceKind::KeyboardMouse || d == DeviceKind::Gamepad {\\n                self.ever_fine = true;\\n            }\\n        }\\n        let mut cmds = Vec::new();\\n        if self.screen == Screen::Attract {\\n370→            if input.any {\\n                self.screen = Screen::Title;\\n                self.paused = false;\\n                self.idle = 0.0;\\n                self.focus = 0;\\n                cmds.push(Cmd::ToTitle);\\n            }\\n            return cmds;\\n        }\\n        let menuish = matches!(\\n380→            self.screen,\\n            Screen::Title | Screen::Menu | Screen::Difficulty | Screen::Files | Screen::Settings | Screen::About | Screen::Controls\\n        );\\n        if menuish && !input.any {\\n            self.idle += input.dt;\\n            if self.idle >= 10.0 {\\n                self.screen = Screen::Attract;\\n                self.idle = 0.0;\\n                cmds.push(Cmd::LoadAttract);\\n                return cmds;\\n390→            }\\n        } else if input.any {\\n            self.idle = 0.0;\\n        }\\n        if self.touch_only && !self.ever_fine && self.screen == Screen::Title {\\n            if input.confirm || input.click {\\n                self.screen = Screen::Settings;\\n                self.focus = 0;\\n            }\\n            return cmds;\\n400→        }\\n        let n = self.count();\\n        if let Some(p) = input.pointer {\\n            if let Some(hit) = self.hit(p) {\\n                self.focus = hit;\\n                self.device = DeviceKind::KeyboardMouse;\\n            }\\n        }\\n        if input.up {\\n            self.focus = self.focus.saturating_sub(1);\\n410→        }\\n        if input.down && n > 0 {\\n            self.focus = (self.focus + 1).min(n - 1);\\n        }\\n        if input.tab_l {\\n            self.page(-1);\\n        }\\n        if input.tab_r {\\n            self.page(1);\\n        }\\n420→        if input.left || input.right {\\n            let dir = if input.right { 1.0 } else { -1.0 };\\n            self.nudge(dir, &mut cmds);\\n        }\\n        if input.back {\\n            self.back();\\n        }\\n        if input.confirm || input.click {\\n            self.activate(&mut cmds);\\n        }\\n430→        if self.screen == Screen::Hud && input.back {\\n            self.paused = true;\\n            self.screen = Screen::Pause;\\n            self.focus = 0;\\n        }\\n        cmds\\n    }\\n\\n    fn count(&self) -> usize {\\n        match self.screen {\\n440→            Screen::Menu | Screen::Pause => 6,\\n            Screen::Difficulty => 3,\\n            Screen::Files => 8,\\n            Screen::Settings => 3,\\n            Screen::Dev => 9,\\n            Screen::Dead => 1,\\n            Screen::Title => {\\n                if self.touch_only && !self.ever_fine {\\n                    1\\n                } else {\\n450→                    1\\n                }\\n            }\\n            _ => 1,\\n        }\\n    }\\n\\n    fn hit(&self, p: [f32; 2]) -> Option<usize> {\\n        let n = self.count();\\n        for i in 0..n {\\n460→            let y = 280.0 + i as f32 * 72.0;\\n            if p[0] >= 180.0 && p[0] <= 1100.0 && p[1] >= y && p[1] <= y + 60.0 {\\n                return Some(i);\\n            }\\n        }\\n        None\\n    }\\n\\n    fn page(&mut self, d: i8) {\\n        match self.screen {\\n470→            Screen::Settings => self.settings_page = (self.settings_page as i8 + d).rem_euclid(3) as u8,\\n            Screen::About => self.about_page = (self.about_page as i8 + d).rem_euclid(5) as u8,\\n            Screen::Dev => self.dev_page = (self.dev_page as i8 + d).rem_euclid(4) as u8,\\n            _ => {}\\n        }\\n        self.focus = 0;\\n    }\\n\\n    fn nudge(&mut self, dir: f32, cmds: &mut Vec<Cmd>) {\\n        if self.screen == Screen::Settings && self.settings_page == 0 {\\n480→            let slot = match self.focus {\\n                0 => &mut self.music,\\n                1 => &mut self.effects,\\n                2 => &mut self.voices,\\n                _ => return,\\n            };\\n            *slot = (*slot + dir * 0.05).clamp(0.0, 1.0);\\n            cmds.push(Cmd::SetBus { which: self.focus as u8, value: *slot });\\n        }\\n        if self.screen == Screen::Dev && (2..8).contains(&self.focus) {\\n490→            let id = self.dev_page as usize * 6 + (self.focus - 2);\\n            if id < Tune::FIELDS.len() {\\n                let (_, _, lo, hi) = Tune::FIELDS[id];\\n                let step = (hi - lo) / 20.0;\\n                self.sliders[id] = (self.sliders[id] + dir * step).clamp(lo, hi);\\n                cmds.push(Cmd::SetTune { id: id as u8, value: self.sliders[id] });\\n            }\\n        }\\n    }\\n\\n500→    fn back(&mut self) {\\n        match self.screen {\\n            Screen::Menu | Screen::Attract => self.screen = Screen::Title,\\n            Screen::Difficulty | Screen::Files | Screen::Settings | Screen::About | Screen::Controls => {\\n                self.screen = if self.paused { Screen::Pause } else { Screen::Menu };\\n            }\\n            Screen::Pause => {\\n                self.paused = false;\\n                self.screen = Screen::Hud;\\n            }\\n510→            Screen::Dev => self.screen = Screen::Pause,\\n            Screen::Hud => {\\n                self.paused = true;\\n                self.screen = Screen::Pause;\\n                self.focus = 0;\\n            }\\n            _ => {}\\n        }\\n        self.focus = 0;\\n    }\\n520→\\n    fn activate(&mut self, cmds: &mut Vec<Cmd>) {\\n        match self.screen {\\n            Screen::Title => {\\n                self.screen = Screen::Menu;\\n                self.focus = 0;\\n            }\\n            Screen::Menu => match self.focus {\\n                0 => {\\n                    self.paused = false;\\n530→                    cmds.push(Cmd::LoadCampaign);\\n                    self.screen = Screen::Story;\\n                }\\n                1 => {\\n                    self.screen = Screen::Difficulty;\\n                    self.focus = self.difficulty as usize;\\n                }\\n                2 => {\\n                    self.screen = Screen::Files;\\n                    self.focus = 0;\\n540→                }\\n                3 => {\\n                    self.paused = false;\\n                    cmds.push(Cmd::LoadCode);\\n                    self.screen = Screen::Hud;\\n                }\\n                4 => {\\n                    self.screen = Screen::Settings;\\n                    self.focus = 0;\\n                }\\n550→                _ => {\\n                    self.screen = Screen::About;\\n                    self.focus = 0;\\n                }\\n            },\\n            Screen::Difficulty => {\\n                self.difficulty = self.focus.min(2) as u8;\\n                cmds.push(Cmd::SetDifficulty(self.difficulty));\\n                cmds.push(Cmd::LoadCampaign);\\n                self.paused = false;\\n560→                self.screen = Screen::Story;\\n            }\\n            Screen::Files => {\\n                let n = self.focus.min(7) as u8;\\n                cmds.push(Cmd::LoadCase(n));\\n                self.paused = false;\\n                self.screen = Screen::Hud;\\n            }\\n            Screen::Pause => match self.focus {\\n                0 => {\\n570→                    self.paused = false;\\n                    self.screen = Screen::Hud;\\n                }\\n                1 => cmds.push(Cmd::Retry),\\n                2 => self.screen = Screen::Controls,\\n                3 => self.screen = Screen::Settings,\\n                4 => {\\n                    self.screen = Screen::Dev;\\n                    self.focus = 0;\\n                }\\n580→                _ => {\\n                    self.paused = false;\\n                    self.screen = Screen::Title;\\n                    cmds.push(Cmd::ToTitle);\\n                }\\n            },\\n            Screen::Dev => {\\n                if self.focus == 0 {\\n                    self.live = !self.live;\\n                } else if self.focus == 1 {\\n590→                    self.bot_plays = !self.bot_plays;\\n                } else if self.focus >= 8 {\\n                    cmds.push(self.reset_sliders());\\n                }\\n            }\\n            Screen::Settings if self.settings_page == 1 && self.focus == 0 => self.xbox = !self.xbox,\\n            Screen::Dead => cmds.push(Cmd::Retry),\\n            Screen::Story | Screen::Results | Screen::Card | Screen::Chart => cmds.push(Cmd::ConfirmSim),\\n            Screen::About => self.about_page = (self.about_page + 1) % 5,\\n            _ => {}\\n600→        }\\n    }\\n\\n    pub fn reset_sliders(&mut self) -> Cmd {\\n        for (i, (_, v, _, _)) in Tune::FIELDS.iter().enumerate() {\\n            self.sliders[i] = *v;\\n        }\\n        self.music = 0.10;\\n        self.effects = 0.80;\\n        self.voices = 0.70;\\n610→        Cmd::ResetTune\\n    }\\n\\n    pub fn mark_rank(&mut self, case_id: i8, rank: u8) {\\n        if (0..8).contains(&case_id) {\\n            let i = case_id as usize;\\n            if rank > self.best[i] {\\n                self.best[i] = rank;\\n            }\\n        }\\n620→    }\\n\\n    pub fn open_dev_for_test(&mut self) {\\n        self.paused = true;\\n        self.screen = Screen::Dev;\\n        self.focus = 2;\\n        self.dev_page = 0;\\n    }\\n}\\n\",\"content_concise\":\"150→    }\\n\\n    pub fn paused(&self) -> bool {\\n        self.paused\\n    }\\n\\n    pub fn note_mode(&mut self, mode: u8) {\\n        self.sim_mode = mode;\\n        // A load or a return to the title can land a frame before the sim does.\\n        if self.screen == Screen::Title && mode == 6 {\\n160→            return;\\n        }\\n        if matches!(self.screen, Screen::Story | Screen::Hud | Screen::Chart) && mode == 0 {\\n            return;\\n        }\\n        if self.paused\\n            || matches!(\\n                self.screen,\\n                Screen::Menu\\n                    | Screen::Difficulty\\n170→                    | Screen::Files\\n                    | Screen::Settings\\n                    | Screen::About\\n                    | Screen::Controls\\n                    | Screen::Pause\\n                    | Screen::Dev\\n                    | Screen::Attract\\n            )\\n        {\\n            return;\\n180→        }\\n        self.screen = match mode {\\n            1 => Screen::Story,\\n            2 => Screen::Chart,\\n            3 => Screen::Hud,\\n            4 => Screen::Results,\\n            5 => Screen::Dead,\\n            6 => Screen::Attract,\\n            7 => Screen::Card,\\n            _ => Screen::Title,\\n190→        };\\n    }\\n\\n    pub fn prompt(&self, action: &str) -> &'static str {\\n        let pad = self.device == DeviceKind::Gamepad;\\n        match action {\\n            \\\"confirm\\\" => {\\n                if !pad {\\n                    \\\"Enter\\\"\\n                } else if self.xbox {\\n200→                    \\\"A\\\"\\n                } else {\\n                    \\\"Cross\\\"\\n                }\\n            }\\n            \\\"back\\\" => {\\n                if !pad {\\n                    \\\"Esc\\\"\\n                } else if self.xbox {\\n                    \\\"B\\\"\\n210→                } else {\\n                    \\\"Circle\\\"\\n                }\\n            }\\n            \\\"use\\\" => {\\n                if !pad {\\n                    \\\"LMB\\\"\\n                } else if self.xbox {\\n                    \\\"RT\\\"\\n                } else {\\n220→                    \\\"R2\\\"\\n                }\\n            }\\n            \\\"gift\\\" => {\\n                if !pad {\\n                    \\\"G\\\"\\n                } else if self.xbox {\\n                    \\\"Y\\\"\\n                } else {\\n                    \\\"Triangle\\\"\\n230→                }\\n            }\\n            \\\"chart\\\" => {\\n                if !pad {\\n                    \\\"Tab\\\"\\n                } else if self.xbox {\\n                    \\\"X\\\"\\n                } else {\\n                    \\\"Square\\\"\\n                }\\n240→            }\\n            \\\"pause\\\" => {\\n                if pad {\\n                    \\\"Options\\\"\\n                } else {\\n                    \\\"Esc\\\"\\n                }\\n            }\\n            _ => \\\" \\\",\\n        }\\n250→    }\\n\\n    pub fn lines(&self) -> Vec<String> {\\n        let mut v = Vec::new();\\n        v.push(TITLE.to_string());\\n        match self.screen {\\n            Screen::Title => {\\n                v.push(\\\"Mercy Harbor General  ·  Night Ward\\\".into());\\n                v.push(format!(\\\"Press {} \\\", self.prompt(\\\"confirm\\\")));\\n                if self.touch_only && !self.ever_fine {\\n260→                    v.push(\\\"Controller or keyboard required\\\".into());\\n                    v.push(\\\"Settings\\\".into());\\n                }\\n            }\\n            Screen::Menu => {\\n                for (i, item) in [\\\"Continue\\\", \\\"New Game\\\", \\\"Case Files\\\", \\\"Code Blue\\\", \\\"Settings\\\", \\\"About\\\"].iter().enumerate() {\\n                    v.push(self.row(i, item));\\n                }\\n            }\\n            Screen::Difficulty => {\\n270→                for (i, item) in [\\\"Resident\\\", \\\"Attending\\\", \\\"Chief\\\"].iter().enumerate() {\\n                    v.push(self.row(i, item));\\n                }\\n            }\\n            Screen::Files => {\\n                for i in 0..8 {\\n                    let rank = [\\\"\\\", \\\"C\\\", \\\"B\\\", \\\"A\\\", \\\"S\\\", \\\"ENCORE\\\"][self.best[i] as usize];\\n                    v.push(self.row(i, &format!(\\\"Case {}  {rank}\\\", i + 1)));\\n                }\\n            }\\n280→            Screen::Settings => {\\n                v.push(format!(\\\"Page {}\\\", self.settings_page + 1));\\n                match self.settings_page {\\n                    0 => {\\n                        v.push(self.row(0, &format!(\\\"Music  {:.2}  default 0.10\\\", self.music)));\\n                        v.push(self.row(1, &format!(\\\"Effects  {:.2}  default 0.80\\\", self.effects)));\\n                        v.push(self.row(2, &format!(\\\"Voices  {:.2}  default 0.70\\\", self.voices)));\\n                    }\\n                    1 => {\\n                        v.push(self.row(0, if self.xbox { \\\"Prompts  Xbox\\\" } else { \\\"Prompts  PlayStation\\\" }));\\n290→                        v.push(self.row(1, &format!(\\\"Cursor speed  {:.0}\\\", self.sliders[8])));\\n                        v.push(self.row(2, \\\"Rumble\\\"));\\n                    }\\n                    _ => {\\n                        v.push(self.row(0, \\\"Field  Anatomical\\\"));\\n                        v.push(self.row(1, \\\"Fullscreen\\\"));\\n                    }\\n                }\\n            }\\n            Screen::About => {\\n300→                v.push(about_page_title(self.about_page).into());\\n                v.extend(about_lines(self.about_page));\\n            }\\n            Screen::Controls => {\\n                v.push(format!(\\\"Aim   right stick or mouse   {}\\\", self.prompt(\\\"use\\\")));\\n                v.push(\\\"Tools   left stick or 1-8\\\".into());\\n                v.push(format!(\\\"Operate   {}\\\", self.prompt(\\\"use\\\")));\\n                v.push(format!(\\\"Gift   {}\\\", self.prompt(\\\"gift\\\")));\\n                v.push(format!(\\\"Chart   {}\\\", self.prompt(\\\"chart\\\")));\\n            }\\n310→            Screen::Pause => {\\n                for (i, item) in [\\\"Resume\\\", \\\"Restart\\\", \\\"Controls\\\", \\\"Settings\\\", \\\"Dev Mode\\\", \\\"Quit to Title\\\"].iter().enumerate() {\\n                    v.push(self.row(i, item));\\n                }\\n            }\\n            Screen::Dev => {\\n                v.push(self.row(0, if self.live { \\\"Live  on\\\" } else { \\\"Live  off\\\" }));\\n                v.push(self.row(1, if self.bot_plays { \\\"Bot plays  on\\\" } else { \\\"Bot plays  off\\\" }));\\n                let start = self.dev_page as usize * 6;\\n                for i in 0..6 {\\n320→                    let id = start + i;\\n                    if id >= Tune::FIELDS.len() {\\n                        break;\\n                    }\\n                    let (name, def, _, _) = Tune::FIELDS[id];\\n                    v.push(self.row(i + 2, &format!(\\\"{name}  {:.2}  default {def:.2}\\\", self.sliders[id])));\\n                }\\n                v.push(self.row(8, \\\"Reset All\\\"));\\n            }\\n            Screen::Attract => {\\n330→                v.push(\\\"DEMO\\\".into());\\n                v.push(format!(\\\"Press {}\\\", self.prompt(\\\"confirm\\\")));\\n            }\\n            Screen::Hud => {\\n                v.push(\\\"OPERATION\\\".into());\\n            }\\n            Screen::Story => v.push(\\\"Advance\\\".into()),\\n            Screen::Results => v.push(\\\"Results\\\".into()),\\n            Screen::Dead => v.push(self.row(0, \\\"Retry\\\")),\\n            Screen::Card => {\\n340→                v.push(\\\"Pre-op\\\".into());\\n                v.push(\\\"Keep the patient alive\\\".into());\\n                v.push(format!(\\\"{} ready\\\", self.prompt(\\\"confirm\\\")));\\n            }\\n            Screen::Chart => {\\n                v.push(\\\"Chart\\\".into());\\n                v.push(\\\"Begin the operation\\\".into());\\n                v.push(format!(\\\"{} begin\\\", self.prompt(\\\"confirm\\\")));\\n            }\\n        }\\n350→        v\\n    }\\n\\n    fn row(&self, i: usize, label: &str) -> String {\\n        if i == self.focus {\\n            format!(\\\"> {label}\\\")\\n        } else {\\n            label.to_string()\\n        }\\n    }\\n360→\\n    pub fn step(&mut self, input: Input) -> Vec<Cmd> {\\n        if let Some(d) = input.device {\\n            self.device = d;\\n            if d == DeviceKind::KeyboardMouse || d == DeviceKind::Gamepad {\\n                self.ever_fine = true;\\n            }\\n        }\\n        let mut cmds = Vec::new();\\n        if self.screen == Screen::Attract {\\n370→            if input.any {\\n                self.screen = Screen::Title;\\n                self.paused = false;\\n                self.idle = 0.0;\\n                self.focus = 0;\\n                cmds.push(Cmd::ToTitle);\\n            }\\n            return cmds;\\n        }\\n        let menuish = matches!(\\n380→            self.screen,\\n            Screen::Title | Screen::Menu | Screen::Difficulty | Screen::Files | Screen::Settings | Screen::About | Screen::Controls\\n        );\\n        if menuish && !input.any {\\n            self.idle += input.dt;\\n            if self.idle >= 10.0 {\\n                self.screen = Screen::Attract;\\n                self.idle = 0.0;\\n                cmds.push(Cmd::LoadAttract);\\n                return cmds;\\n390→            }\\n        } else if input.any {\\n            self.idle = 0.0;\\n        }\\n        if self.touch_only && !self.ever_fine && self.screen == Screen::Title {\\n            if input.confirm || input.click {\\n                self.screen = Screen::Settings;\\n                self.focus = 0;\\n            }\\n            return cmds;\\n400→        }\\n        let n = self.count();\\n        if let Some(p) = input.pointer {\\n            if let Some(hit) = self.hit(p) {\\n                self.focus = hit;\\n                self.device = DeviceKind::KeyboardMouse;\\n            }\\n        }\\n        if input.up {\\n            self.focus = self.focus.saturating_sub(1);\\n410→        }\\n        if input.down && n > 0 {\\n            self.focus = (self.focus + 1).min(n - 1);\\n        }\\n        if input.tab_l {\\n            self.page(-1);\\n        }\\n        if input.tab_r {\\n            self.page(1);\\n        }\\n420→        if input.left || input.right {\\n            let dir = if input.right { 1.0 } else { -1.0 };\\n            self.nudge(dir, &mut cmds);\\n        }\\n        if input.back {\\n            self.back();\\n        }\\n        if input.confirm || input.click {\\n            self.activate(&mut cmds);\\n        }\\n430→        if self.screen == Screen::Hud && input.back {\\n            self.paused = true;\\n            self.screen = Screen::Pause;\\n            self.focus = 0;\\n        }\\n        cmds\\n    }\\n\\n    fn count(&self) -> usize {\\n        match self.screen {\\n440→            Screen::Menu | Screen::Pause => 6,\\n            Screen::Difficulty => 3,\\n            Screen::Files => 8,\\n            Screen::Settings => 3,\\n            Screen::Dev => 9,\\n            Screen::Dead => 1,\\n            Screen::Title => {\\n                if self.touch_only && !self.ever_fine {\\n                    1\\n                } else {\\n450→                    1\\n                }\\n            }\\n            _ => 1,\\n        }\\n    }\\n\\n    fn hit(&self, p: [f32; 2]) -> Option<usize> {\\n        let n = self.count();\\n        for i in 0..n {\\n460→            let y = 280.0 + i as f32 * 72.0;\\n            if p[0] >= 180.0 && p[0] <= 1100.0 && p[1] >= y && p[1] <= y + 60.0 {\\n                return Some(i);\\n            }\\n        }\\n        None\\n    }\\n\\n    fn page(&mut self, d: i8) {\\n        match self.screen {\\n470→            Screen::Settings => self.settings_page = (self.settings_page as i8 + d).rem_euclid(3) as u8,\\n            Screen::About => self.about_page = (self.about_page as i8 + d).rem_euclid(5) as u8,\\n            Screen::Dev => self.dev_page = (self.dev_page as i8 + d).rem_euclid(4) as u8,\\n            _ => {}\\n        }\\n        self.focus = 0;\\n    }\\n\\n    fn nudge(&mut self, dir: f32, cmds: &mut Vec<Cmd>) {\\n        if self.screen == Screen::Settings && self.settings_page == 0 {\\n480→            let slot = match self.focus {\\n                0 => &mut self.music,\\n                1 => &mut self.effects,\\n                2 => &mut self.voices,\\n                _ => return,\\n            };\\n            *slot = (*slot + dir * 0.05).clamp(0.0, 1.0);\\n            cmds.push(Cmd::SetBus { which: self.focus as u8, value: *slot });\\n        }\\n        if self.screen == Screen::Dev && (2..8).contains(&self.focus) {\\n490→            let id = self.dev_page as usize * 6 + (self.focus - 2);\\n            if id < Tune::FIELDS.len() {\\n                let (_, _, lo, hi) = Tune::FIELDS[id];\\n                let step = (hi - lo) / 20.0;\\n                self.sliders[id] = (self.sliders[id] + dir * step).clamp(lo, hi);\\n                cmds.push(Cmd::SetTune { id: id as u8, value: self.sliders[id] });\\n            }\\n        }\\n    }\\n\\n500→    fn back(&mut self) {\\n        match self.screen {\\n            Screen::Menu | Screen::Attract => self.screen = Screen::Title,\\n            Screen::Difficulty | Screen::Files | Screen::Settings | Screen::About | Screen::Controls => {\\n                self.screen = if self.paused { Screen::Pause } else { Screen::Menu };\\n            }\\n            Screen::Pause => {\\n                self.paused = false;\\n                self.screen = Screen::Hud;\\n            }\\n510→            Screen::Dev => self.screen = Screen::Pause,\\n            Screen::Hud => {\\n                self.paused = true;\\n                self.screen = Screen::Pause;\\n                self.focus = 0;\\n            }\\n            _ => {}\\n        }\\n        self.focus = 0;\\n    }\\n520→\\n    fn activate(&mut self, cmds: &mut Vec<Cmd>) {\\n        match self.screen {\\n            Screen::Title => {\\n                self.screen = Screen::Menu;\\n                self.focus = 0;\\n            }\\n            Screen::Menu => match self.focus {\\n                0 => {\\n                    self.paused = false;\\n530→                    cmds.push(Cmd::LoadCampaign);\\n                    self.screen = Screen::Story;\\n                }\\n                1 => {\\n                    self.screen = Screen::Difficulty;\\n                    self.focus = self.difficulty as usize;\\n                }\\n                2 => {\\n                    self.screen = Screen::Files;\\n                    self.focus = 0;\\n540→                }\\n                3 => {\\n                    self.paused = false;\\n                    cmds.push(Cmd::LoadCode);\\n                    self.screen = Screen::Hud;\\n                }\\n                4 => {\\n                    self.screen = Screen::Settings;\\n                    self.focus = 0;\\n                }\\n550→                _ => {\\n                    self.screen = Screen::About;\\n                    self.focus = 0;\\n                }\\n            },\\n            Screen::Difficulty => {\\n                self.difficulty = self.focus.min(2) as u8;\\n                cmds.push(Cmd::SetDifficulty(self.difficulty));\\n                cmds.push(Cmd::LoadCampaign);\\n                self.paused = false;\\n560→                self.screen = Screen::Story;\\n            }\\n            Screen::Files => {\\n                let n = self.focus.min(7) as u8;\\n                cmds.push(Cmd::LoadCase(n));\\n                self.paused = false;\\n                self.screen = Screen::Hud;\\n            }\\n            Screen::Pause => match self.focus {\\n                0 => {\\n570→                    self.paused = false;\\n                    self.screen = Screen::Hud;\\n                }\\n                1 => cmds.push(Cmd::Retry),\\n                2 => self.screen = Screen::Controls,\\n                3 => self.screen = Screen::Settings,\\n                4 => {\\n                    self.screen = Screen::Dev;\\n                    self.focus = 0;\\n                }\\n580→                _ => {\\n                    self.paused = false;\\n                    self.screen = Screen::Title;\\n                    cmds.push(Cmd::ToTitle);\\n                }\\n            },\\n            Screen::Dev => {\\n                if self.focus == 0 {\\n                    self.live = !self.live;\\n                } else if self.focus == 1 {\\n590→                    self.bot_plays = !self.bot_plays;\\n                } else if self.focus >= 8 {\\n                    cmds.push(self.reset_sliders());\\n                }\\n            }\\n            Screen::Settings if self.settings_page == 1 && self.focus == 0 => self.xbox = !self.xbox,\\n            Screen::Dead => cmds.push(Cmd::Retry),\\n            Screen::Story | Screen::Results | Screen::Card | Screen::Chart => cmds.push(Cmd::ConfirmSim),\\n            Screen::About => self.about_page = (self.about_page + 1) % 5,\\n            _ => {}\\n600→        }\\n    }\\n\\n    pub fn reset_sliders(&mut self) -> Cmd {\\n        for (i, (_, v, _, _)) in Tune::FIELDS.iter().enumerate() {\\n            self.sliders[i] = *v;\\n        }\\n        self.music = 0.10;\\n        self.effects = 0.80;\\n        self.voices = 0.70;\\n610→        Cmd::ResetTune\\n    }\\n\\n    pub fn mark_rank(&mut self, case_id: i8, rank: u8) {\\n        if (0..8).contains(&case_id) {\\n            let i = case_id as usize;\\n            if rank > self.best[i] {\\n                self.best[i] = rank;\\n            }\\n        }\\n620→    }\\n\\n    pub fn open_dev_for_test(&mut self) {\\n        self.paused = true;\\n        self.screen = Screen::Dev;\\n        self.focus = 2;\\n        self.dev_page = 0;\\n    }\\n}\\n\",\"absolute_path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224015__x42677a/work/Hands of Harbor: Second Opinion-Trauma Center: Second Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-224015/engine/crates/pav_ui/src/surgery/mod.rs\",\"offset\":150,\"limit\":480,\"raw_output\":\"    }\\n\\n    pub fn paused(&self) -> bool {\\n        self.paused\\n    }\\n\\n    pub fn note_mode(&mut self, mode: u8) {\\n        self.sim_mode = mode;\\n        // A load or a return to the title can land a frame before the sim does.\\n        if self.screen == Screen::Title && mode == 6 {\\n            return;\\n        }\\n        if matches!(self.screen, Screen::Story | Screen::Hud | Screen::Chart) && mode == 0 {\\n            return;\\n        }\\n        if self.paused\\n            || matches!(\\n                self.screen,\\n                Screen::Menu\\n                    | Screen::Difficulty\\n                    | Screen::Files\\n                    | Screen::Settings\\n                    | Screen::About\\n                    | Screen::Controls\\n                    | Screen::Pause\\n                    | Screen::Dev\\n                    | Screen::Attract\\n            )\\n        {\\n            return;\\n        }\\n        self.screen = match mode {\\n            1 => Screen::Story,\\n            2 => Screen::Chart,\\n            3 => Screen::Hud,\\n            4 => Screen::Results,\\n            5 => Screen::Dead,\\n            6 => Screen::Attract,\\n            7 => Screen::Card,\\n            _ => Screen::Title,\\n        };\\n    }\\n\\n    pub fn prompt(&self, action: &str) -> &'static str {\\n        let pad = self.device == DeviceKind::Gamepad;\\n        match action {\\n            \\\"confirm\\\" => {\\n                if !pad {\\n                    \\\"Enter\\\"\\n                } else if self.xbox {\\n                    \\\"A\\\"\\n                } else {\\n                    \\\"Cross\\\"\\n                }\\n            }\\n            \\\"back\\\" => {\\n                if !pad {\\n                    \\\"Esc\\\"\\n                } else if self.xbox {\\n                    \\\"B\\\"\\n                } else {\\n                    \\\"Circle\\\"\\n                }\\n            }\\n            \\\"use\\\" => {\\n                if !pad {\\n                    \\\"LMB\\\"\\n                } else if self.xbox {\\n                    \\\"RT\\\"\\n                } else {\\n                    \\\"R2\\\"\\n                }\\n            }\\n            \\\"gift\\\" => {\\n                if !pad {\\n                    \\\"G\\\"\\n                } else if self.xbox {\\n                    \\\"Y\\\"\\n                } else {\\n                    \\\"Triangle\\\"\\n                }\\n            }\\n            \\\"chart\\\" => {\\n                if !pad {\\n                    \\\"Tab\\\"\\n                } else if self.xbox {\\n                    \\\"X\\\"\\n                } else {\\n                    \\\"Square\\\"\\n                }\\n            }\\n            \\\"pause\\\" => {\\n                if pad {\\n                    \\\"Options\\\"\\n                } else {\\n                    \\\"Esc\\\"\\n                }\\n            }\\n            _ => \\\" \\\",\\n        }\\n    }\\n\\n    pub fn lines(&self) -> Vec<String> {\\n        let mut v = Vec::new();\\n        v.push(TITLE.to_string());\\n        match self.screen {\\n            Screen::Title => {\\n                v.push(\\\"Mercy Harbor General  ·  Night Ward\\\".into());\\n                v.push(format!(\\\"Press {} \\\", self.prompt(\\\"confirm\\\")));\\n                if self.touch_only && !self.ever_fine {\\n                    v.push(\\\"Controller or keyboard required\\\".into());\\n                    v.push(\\\"Settings\\\".into());\\n                }\\n            }\\n            Screen::Menu => {\\n                for (i, item) in [\\\"Continue\\\", \\\"New Game\\\", \\\"Case Files\\\", \\\"Code Blue\\\", \\\"Settings\\\", \\\"About\\\"].iter().enumerate() {\\n                    v.push(self.row(i, item));\\n                }\\n            }\\n            Screen::Difficulty => {\\n                for (i, item) in [\\\"Resident\\\", \\\"Attending\\\", \\\"Chief\\\"].iter().enumerate() {\\n                    v.push(self.row(i, item));\\n                }\\n            }\\n            Screen::Files => {\\n                for i in 0..8 {\\n                    let rank = [\\\"\\\", \\\"C\\\", \\\"B\\\", \\\"A\\\", \\\"S\\\", \\\"ENCORE\\\"][self.best[i] as usize];\\n                    v.push(self.row(i, &format!(\\\"Case {}  {rank}\\\", i + 1)));\\n                }\\n            }\\n            Screen::Settings => {\\n                v.push(format!(\\\"Page {}\\\", self.settings_page + 1));\\n                match self.settings_page {\\n                    0 => {\\n                        v.push(self.row(0, &format!(\\\"Music  {:.2}  default 0.10\\\", self.music)));\\n                        v.push(self.row(1, &format!(\\\"Effects  {:.2}  default 0.80\\\", self.effects)));\\n                        v.push(self.row(2, &format!(\\\"Voices  {:.2}  default 0.70\\\", self.voices)));\\n                    }\\n                    1 => {\\n                        v.push(self.row(0, if self.xbox { \\\"Prompts  Xbox\\\" } else { \\\"Prompts  PlayStation\\\" }));\\n                        v.push(self.row(1, &format!(\\\"Cursor speed  {:.0}\\\", self.sliders[8])));\\n                        v.push(self.row(2, \\\"Rumble\\\"));\\n                    }\\n                    _ => {\\n                        v.push(self.row(0, \\\"Field  Anatomical\\\"));\\n                        v.push(self.row(1, \\\"Fullscreen\\\"));\\n                    }\\n                }\\n            }\\n            Screen::About => {\\n                v.push(about_page_title(self.about_page).into());\\n                v.extend(about_lines(self.about_page));\\n            }\\n            Screen::Controls => {\\n                v.push(format!(\\\"Aim   right stick or mouse   {}\\\", self.prompt(\\\"use\\\")));\\n                v.push(\\\"Tools   left stick or 1-8\\\".into());\\n                v.push(format!(\\\"Operate   {}\\\", self.prompt(\\\"use\\\")));\\n                v.push(format!(\\\"Gift   {}\\\", self.prompt(\\\"gift\\\")));\\n                v.push(format!(\\\"Chart   {}\\\", self.prompt(\\\"chart\\\")));\\n            }\\n            Screen::Pause => {\\n                for (i, item) in [\\\"Resume\\\", \\\"Restart\\\", \\\"Controls\\\", \\\"Settings\\\", \\\"Dev Mode\\\", \\\"Quit to Title\\\"].iter().enumerate() {\\n                    v.push(self.row(i, item));\\n                }\\n            }\\n            Screen::Dev => {\\n                v.push(self.row(0, if self.live { \\\"Live  on\\\" } else { \\\"Live  off\\\" }));\\n                v.push(self.row(1, if self.bot_plays { \\\"Bot plays  on\\\" } else { \\\"Bot plays  off\\\" }));\\n                let start = self.dev_page as usize * 6;\\n                for i in 0..6 {\\n                    let id = start + i;\\n                    if id >= Tune::FIELDS.len() {\\n                        break;\\n                    }\\n                    let (name, def, _, _) = Tune::FIELDS[id];\\n                    v.push(self.row(i + 2, &format!(\\\"{name}  {:.2}  default {def:.2}\\\", self.sliders[id])));\\n                }\\n                v.push(self.row(8, \\\"Reset All\\\"));\\n            }\\n            Screen::Attract => {\\n                v.push(\\\"DEMO\\\".into());\\n                v.push(format!(\\\"Press {}\\\", self.prompt(\\\"confirm\\\")));\\n            }\\n            Screen::Hud => {\\n                v.push(\\\"OPERATION\\\".into());\\n            }\\n            Screen::Story => v.push(\\\"Advance\\\".into()),\\n            Screen::Results => v.push(\\\"Results\\\".into()),\\n            Screen::Dead => v.push(self.row(0, \\\"Retry\\\")),\\n            Screen::Card => {\\n                v.push(\\\"Pre-op\\\".into());\\n                v.push(\\\"Keep the patient alive\\\".into());\\n                v.push(format!(\\\"{} ready\\\", self.prompt(\\\"confirm\\\")));\\n            }\\n            Screen::Chart => {\\n                v.push(\\\"Chart\\\".into());\\n                v.push(\\\"Begin the operation\\\".into());\\n                v.push(format!(\\\"{} begin\\\", self.prompt(\\\"confirm\\\")));\\n            }\\n        }\\n        v\\n    }\\n\\n    fn row(&self, i: usize, label: &str) -> String {\\n        if i == self.focus {\\n            format!(\\\"> {label}\\\")\\n        } else {\\n            label.to_string()\\n        }\\n    }\\n\\n    pub fn step(&mut self, input: Input) -> Vec<Cmd> {\\n        if let Some(d) = input.device {\\n            self.device = d;\\n            if d == DeviceKind::KeyboardMouse || d == DeviceKind::Gamepad {\\n                self.ever_fine = true;\\n            }\\n        }\\n        let mut cmds = Vec::new();\\n        if self.screen == Screen::Attract {\\n            if input.any {\\n                self.screen = Screen::Title;\\n                self.paused = false;\\n                self.idle = 0.0;\\n                self.focus = 0;\\n                cmds.push(Cmd::ToTitle);\\n            }\\n            return cmds;\\n        }\\n        let menuish = matches!(\\n            self.screen,\\n            Screen::Title | Screen::Menu | Screen::Difficulty | Screen::Files | Screen::Settings | Screen::About | Screen::Controls\\n        );\\n        if menuish && !input.any {\\n            self.idle += input.dt;\\n            if self.idle >= 10.0 {\\n                self.screen = Screen::Attract;\\n                self.idle = 0.0;\\n                cmds.push(Cmd::LoadAttract);\\n                return cmds;\\n            }\\n        } else if input.any {\\n            self.idle = 0.0;\\n        }\\n        if self.touch_only && !self.ever_fine && self.screen == Screen::Title {\\n            if input.confirm || input.click {\\n                self.screen = Screen::Settings;\\n                self.focus = 0;\\n            }\\n            return cmds;\\n        }\\n        let n = self.count();\\n        if let Some(p) = input.pointer {\\n            if let Some(hit) = self.hit(p) {\\n                self.focus = hit;\\n                self.device = DeviceKind::KeyboardMouse;\\n            }\\n        }\\n        if input.up {\\n            self.focus = self.focus.saturating_sub(1);\\n        }\\n        if input.down && n > 0 {\\n            self.focus = (self.focus + 1).min(n - 1);\\n        }\\n        if input.tab_l {\\n            self.page(-1);\\n        }\\n        if input.tab_r {\\n            self.page(1);\\n        }\\n        if input.left || input.right {\\n            let dir = if input.right { 1.0 } else { -1.0 };\\n            self.nudge(dir, &mut cmds);\\n        }\\n        if input.back {\\n            self.back();\\n        }\\n        if input.confirm || input.click {\\n            self.activate(&mut cmds);\\n        }\\n        if self.screen == Screen::Hud && input.back {\\n            self.paused = true;\\n            self.screen = Screen::Pause;\\n            self.focus = 0;\\n        }\\n        cmds\\n    }\\n\\n    fn count(&self) -> usize {\\n        match self.screen {\\n            Screen::Menu | Screen::Pause => 6,\\n            Screen::Difficulty => 3,\\n            Screen::Files => 8,\\n            Screen::Settings => 3,\\n            Screen::Dev => 9,\\n            Screen::Dead => 1,\\n            Screen::Title => {\\n                if self.touch_only && !self.ever_fine {\\n                    1\\n                } else {\\n                    1\\n                }\\n            }\\n            _ => 1,\\n        }\\n    }\\n\\n    fn hit(&self, p: [f32; 2]) -> Option<usize> {\\n        let n = self.count();\\n        for i in 0..n {\\n            let y = 280.0 + i as f32 * 72.0;\\n            if p[0] >= 180.0 && p[0] <= 1100.0 && p[1] >= y && p[1] <= y + 60.0 {\\n                return Some(i);\\n            }\\n        }\\n        None\\n    }\\n\\n    fn page(&mut self, d: i8) {\\n        match self.screen {\\n            Screen::Settings => self.settings_page = (self.settings_page as i8 + d).rem_euclid(3) as u8,\\n            Screen::About => self.about_page = (self.about_page as i8 + d).rem_euclid(5) as u8,\\n            Screen::Dev => self.dev_page = (self.dev_page as i8 + d).rem_euclid(4) as u8,\\n            _ => {}\\n        }\\n        self.focus = 0;\\n    }\\n\\n    fn nudge(&mut self, dir: f32, cmds: &mut Vec<Cmd>) {\\n        if self.screen == Screen::Settings && self.settings_page == 0 {\\n            let slot = match self.focus {\\n                0 => &mut self.music,\\n                1 => &mut self.effects,\\n                2 => &mut self.voices,\\n                _ => return,\\n            };\\n            *slot = (*slot + dir * 0.05).clamp(0.0, 1.0);\\n            cmds.push(Cmd::SetBus { which: self.focus as u8, value: *slot });\\n        }\\n        if self.screen == Screen::Dev && (2..8).contains(&self.focus) {\\n            let id = self.dev_page as usize * 6 + (self.focus - 2);\\n            if id < Tune::FIELDS.len() {\\n                let (_, _, lo, hi) = Tune::FIELDS[id];\\n                let step = (hi - lo) / 20.0;\\n                self.sliders[id] = (self.sliders[id] + dir * step).clamp(lo, hi);\\n                cmds.push(Cmd::SetTune { id: id as u8, value: self.sliders[id] });\\n            }\\n        }\\n    }\\n\\n    fn back(&mut self) {\\n        match self.screen {\\n            Screen::Menu | Screen::Attract => self.screen = Screen::Title,\\n            Screen::Difficulty | Screen::Files | Screen::Settings | Screen::About | Screen::Controls => {\\n                self.screen = if self.paused { Screen::Pause } else { Screen::Menu };\\n            }\\n            Screen::Pause => {\\n                self.paused = false;\\n                self.screen = Screen::Hud;\\n            }\\n            Screen::Dev => self.screen = Screen::Pause,\\n            Screen::Hud => {\\n                self.paused = true;\\n                self.screen = Screen::Pause;\\n                self.focus = 0;\\n            }\\n            _ => {}\\n        }\\n        self.focus = 0;\\n    }\\n\\n    fn activate(&mut self, cmds: &mut Vec<Cmd>) {\\n        match self.screen {\\n            Screen::Title => {\\n                self.screen = Screen::Menu;\\n                self.focus = 0;\\n            }\\n            Screen::Menu => match self.focus {\\n                0 => {\\n                    self.paused = false;\\n                    cmds.push(Cmd::LoadCampaign);\\n                    self.screen = Screen::Story;\\n                }\\n                1 => {\\n                    self.screen = Screen::Difficulty;\\n                    self.focus = self.difficulty as usize;\\n                }\\n                2 => {\\n                    self.screen = Screen::Files;\\n                    self.focus = 0;\\n                }\\n                3 => {\\n                    self.paused = false;\\n                    cmds.push(Cmd::LoadCode);\\n                    self.screen = Screen::Hud;\\n                }\\n                4 => {\\n                    self.screen = Screen::Settings;\\n                    self.focus = 0;\\n                }\\n                _ => {\\n                    self.screen = Screen::About;\\n                    self.focus = 0;\\n                }\\n            },\\n            Screen::Difficulty => {\\n                self.difficulty = self.focus.min(2) as u8;\\n                cmds.push(Cmd::SetDifficulty(self.difficulty));\\n                cmds.push(Cmd::LoadCampaign);\\n                self.paused = false;\\n                self.screen = Screen::Story;\\n            }\\n            Screen::Files => {\\n                let n = self.focus.min(7) as u8;\\n                cmds.push(Cmd::LoadCase(n));\\n                self.paused = false;\\n                self.screen = Screen::Hud;\\n            }\\n            Screen::Pause => match self.focus {\\n                0 => {\\n                    self.paused = false;\\n                    self.screen = Screen::Hud;\\n                }\\n                1 => cmds.push(Cmd::Retry),\\n                2 => self.screen = Screen::Controls,\\n                3 => self.screen = Screen::Settings,\\n                4 => {\\n                    self.screen = Screen::Dev;\\n                    self.focus = 0;\\n                }\\n                _ => {\\n                    self.paused = false;\\n                    self.screen = Screen::Title;\\n                    cmds.push(Cmd::ToTitle);\\n                }\\n            },\\n            Screen::Dev => {\\n                if self.focus == 0 {\\n                    self.live = !self.live;\\n                } else if self.focus == 1 {\\n                    self.bot_plays = !self.bot_plays;\\n                } else if self.focus >= 8 {\\n                    cmds.push(self.reset_sliders());\\n                }\\n            }\\n            Screen::Settings if self.settings_page == 1 && self.focus == 0 => self.xbox = !self.xbox,\\n            Screen::Dead => cmds.push(Cmd::Retry),\\n            Screen::Story | Screen::Results | Screen::Card | Screen::Chart => cmds.push(Cmd::ConfirmSim),\\n            Screen::About => self.about_page = (self.about_page + 1) % 5,\\n            _ => {}\\n        }\\n    }\\n\\n    pub fn reset_sliders(&mut self) -> Cmd {\\n        for (i, (_, v, _, _)) in Tune::FIELDS.iter().enumerate() {\\n            self.sliders[i] = *v;\\n        }\\n        self.music = 0.10;\\n        self.effects = 0.80;\\n        self.voices = 0.70;\\n        Cmd::ResetTune\\n    }\\n\\n    pub fn mark_rank(&mut self, case_id: i8, rank: u8) {\\n        if (0..8).contains(&case_id) {\\n            let i = case_id as usize;\\n            if rank > self.best[i] {\\n                self.best[i] = rank;\\n            }\\n        }\\n    }\\n\\n    pub fn open_dev_for_test(&mut self) {\\n        self.paused = true;\\n        self.screen = Screen::Dev;\\n        self.focus = 2;\\n        self.dev_page = 0;\\n    }\\n}\\n\\n\",\"total_lines\":939}}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa38-de6f-7dc0-ae0d-e0f717ed75f2","uuid":"03af2deb-e95b-48f8-a389-8971bf040b60"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_304","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"A potential test bug was identified in the walk test hover. The menu count is 6 and hit works.\n\nThe pointer focus chain from menu to Case Files and back is correct. Difficulty selection loads the campaign and story. Returning from the story screen lands on Hud because note_mode(3) triggers a screen change.\n\nThe back-from-Hud path is correct. The paused flag is set by back(), so the extra Pause check does not run.\n\nA bug was found in note_mode(5). The Dev screen is in the skip list, so the function returns early and never changes to Dead. This will cause a test failure.\n\nThe test expects note_mode(5) to reach Dead even after pause is cleared. The skip list currently blocks this for Dev and Pause screens. Two fixes are under consideration: either allow Dev and Pause to be overwritten when paused is false, or change the test to return to Hud first.\n\nThe skip list should only block note_mode when paused is true. When paused is false, note_mode must follow the simulation state and can overwrite Dev or Pause. The skip list already prevents unwanted jumps to Settings.\n\nThe test is artificial. Leaving the Dev overlay while paused is false still leaves the screen on Dev.\n\nA simple fix that only checks the paused flag would break Settings. When paused is false and the simulation is in title mode, note_mode(0) must still return to Title to exit Settings.\n\nThe skip list exists independently of the paused flag. The test should be fixed by returning to Hud before calling note_mode(5). Another option is to restrict skip-list behavior so only title and attract modes are protected while paused, letting story, results, dead, and card modes override Dev or Pause once paused is cleared.\n\nThe test will be adjusted to match real behavior. The sequence will return from Dev to Pause, resume to Hud, then call note_mode(5) to reach Dead.\n\nA simpler fix is to change note_mode so it only skips menu screens when the simulation is in title or attract mode, or when paused. If paused is false and the user is on Dev, mode 5 would no longer be blocked and the test would pass without extra navigation.\n\nThe proposed skip-list change was validated against edge cases. Settings during title mode still returns correctly. Story switching to chart works. Menu switching to Hud when a case is loaded is acceptable. About screen remains protected from title mode while attract mode is handled by step().\n\nThe Attract screen skip-list behavior was checked. step() sets Title before note_mode runs, so the skip-list does not block the transition.\n\nThe proposed skip-list change was validated. Attract mode 0 would not block the transition because step() already returns to Title on input before note_mode runs. Dev screen with mode 5 is confirmed to switch correctly to Dead when paused is false.\n\nThe change is confirmed. note_mode(4) on Dev while paused stays on Dev. note_mode(5) after unpausing reaches Dead. Story-to-chart transitions are also correctly blocked while paused.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-44da0a50-dd14-4517-93e9-c65508ceeed8-46","name":"grep","input":{"pattern":"fn about_page_title|enum Cmd|struct Input|sliders:|Derive|PartialEq","path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224015__x42677a/work/engine-link/crates/pav_ui/src/surgery/mod.rs"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-44da0a50-dd14-4517-93e9-c65508ceeed8-47","name":"grep","input":{"pattern":"FIELDS|pub sliders|struct Tune","path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224015__x42677a/work/engine-link/crates/pav_core/src/games/surgery/tune.rs"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":4370,"output_tokens":2240,"cache_read_input_tokens":72576,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa38-de6f-7dc0-ae0d-e0f717ed75f2","uuid":"a992d42b-8c6c-4263-96db-50de4aa4d4bf"}
