{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_306","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"DeviceKind does not implement Default, but it is wrapped in Option so it is acceptable.\n\nInput implements Default. The about page title is \"Testing Feedback\". The dev test correctly maps focus positions to slider IDs. Six downs reach the maximum focus of 8. Confirming at focus 8 triggers a reset that restores the default value. The output contains \"Reset All\" and \"default\".\n\nTouch test confirms navigation to settings and return before activation. Attract mode activates after 10 seconds of idle time and exits on any input. Difficulty defaults to 1, with focus starting at index 1 and moving to 2 on down.\n\nEntering difficulty via confirm sets focus to the current difficulty value, so confirming again loads the campaign. Menu focus 5 correctly maps to About. The note_mode issue will be fixed next.\n\nAnticipated product.rs borrow checker issues: `set_cursor_visible` requires `&self`, and holding a reference into `app.host` while later calling `as_mut()` on `app.gfx` or other fields creates a lifetime conflict.\n\nThe host borrow ends at the events take, so NLL should allow later mutable borrows of gfx and audio. A separate reference to app.harbor.shell.paused() is also being checked for conflicts.\n\nBorrow checker concerns are resolved. The host reference borrows only the host field, so it does not conflict with harbor or other fields. Polling pads and ground point operations also use separate fields and are safe.\n\nA borrow checker conflict was found in product.rs. Both `app.gfx` and `app.egui_state` are mutable references to the same struct, so they cannot be borrowed simultaneously.\n\nThe suspected borrow checker conflict in product.rs is resolved. Rust allows simultaneous mutable borrows of distinct struct fields, so `app.gfx.as_mut()` and `app.egui_state.as_mut()` can be used together.\n\nThe borrow checker concerns for product.rs are resolved. The egui context is a separate field, so it can be used while state and gfx are borrowed. NLL ends the state borrow after platform_output, allowing gfx.draw to proceed safely. The shell reference is consumed inside the closure.\n\n`set_zoom_factor` and font installation are safe because they borrow separate fields from the app struct. Product.rs should compile, but view.rs may still have errors. I will check the view surgery code for obvious issues while waiting.\n\nChecking wasm Closure signatures for FnMut compatibility. Reviewing view module imports and product.rs for SurgeryCmd versus to_sim mismatches. Investigating a potential unused mutable scene warning after moving it into draw.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-50571b12-3c48-48a3-b728-c3cdc05c1581-51","name":"search_replace","input":{"file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224015__x42677a/work/engine-link/crates/pav_ui/src/surgery/mod.rs","old_string":"        if self.paused\n            || matches!(\n                self.screen,\n                Screen::Menu\n                    | Screen::Difficulty\n                    | Screen::Files\n                    | Screen::Settings\n                    | Screen::About\n                    | Screen::Controls\n                    | Screen::Pause\n                    | Screen::Dev\n                    | Screen::Attract\n            )\n        {\n            return;\n        }","new_string":"        // Pause freezes the sim, so the shell keeps the overlay. Menus stay put\n        // while the sim is still on the title or the attract reel.\n        if self.paused {\n            return;\n        }\n        if matches!(mode, 0 | 6)\n            && matches!(\n                self.screen,\n                Screen::Menu\n                    | Screen::Difficulty\n                    | Screen::Files\n                    | Screen::Settings\n                    | Screen::About\n                    | Screen::Controls\n                    | Screen::Pause\n                    | Screen::Dev\n                    | Screen::Attract\n            )\n        {\n            return;\n        }"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-50571b12-3c48-48a3-b728-c3cdc05c1581-52","name":"grep","input":{"pattern":"harbor:|touch_screen|fn new\\(","path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224015__x42677a/work/engine-link/crates/pav_app/src/app.rs"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-50571b12-3c48-48a3-b728-c3cdc05c1581-53","name":"grep","input":{"pattern":"pub mod surgery|fn build\\(","path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224015__x42677a/work/engine-link/crates/pav_view/src"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2609,"output_tokens":2298,"cache_read_input_tokens":79488,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa38-de6f-7dc0-ae0d-e0f717ed75f2","uuid":"55d2b6ec-c624-4958-9f30-f57437084b6e"}
