{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_315","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The surgery build resets history_seconds to zero on every scene rebuild. The test can set the config after Sim::new.\n\nNeed to check if history.enabled defaults to true. SurgeryCmd injection happens through InputFrame.surgery_cmd, and I need to see how step applies it. The SLOPPY task requires spawning a K_POLYP hazard and holding the laser past aux 1.08. K_POLYP maps to LASER, likely tool index 4.\n\nHeat accumulates while the laser is held near a hazard. The first K_POLYP spawns at (1.2, 0). Aim at it with absolute snapping, hold the laser for about three seconds, and pressure must be one. Need defaults to -1. Checkpoint retry requires stepping the bot, sending a Dev command to kill, and Retry to restore. I need to verify how command() handles these inputs and whether Retry works after death.\n\nThe random tool player cycles through tools 0–10, holds USE, and wanders its aim. The idle test uses 90 seconds for case 0, but the plan caps simulation at roughly 400 seconds so timer expiry kills the bot; vitals may drain faster. Case 7 has a 280-second timer. The seed 1 campaign took about 92 seconds of simulation time.\n\nThe test suite should compile quickly after edits. The campaign is the only slow step, but ten campaigns still finish in about one second. A rank of S or better means rank_n must be at least four. The plan requires the bot to win every case and the campaign across all ten seeds.\n\nContent lint requires no empty lines, TODOs, or banned names. The music test already exists in pav_audio. I need to check heart.rs for public API methods and checkpoint fields to drive the heartbeat window. Banned names include Hope Hospital, Caduceus, Stiles, GUILT, Healing Touch, COOL, and XS; I will search story and UI strings for them.\n\nThe plan requires using shipped sim functions for rank, chain, and beat window rather than re-implementing them. Rank should be computed with the shipped `rank_of` function and verified against a finished case. Chain should use the shipped `chain_mul` function or be driven by the sim itself. Beat window logic must also come from the shipped implementation.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-fb9b5f71-5432-4a96-ae45-515c00cc9289-73","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224015__x42677a/work/engine-link/crates/pav_core/src/games/surgery/heart.rs","limit":120}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-fb9b5f71-5432-4a96-ae45-515c00cc9289-74","name":"grep","input":{"pattern":"fn command|surgery_cmd|fn all_lines|pub fn ghost_on_beat|fn on_beat|beat_window","path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224015__x42677a/work/engine-link/crates/pav_core/src/games/surgery","glob":"**/*.rs"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-fb9b5f71-5432-4a96-ae45-515c00cc9289-75","name":"grep","input":{"pattern":"fn step\\(","path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224015__x42677a/work/engine-link/crates/pav_core/src/sim.rs"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2520,"output_tokens":1289,"cache_read_input_tokens":97152,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa38-de6f-7dc0-ae0d-e0f717ed75f2","uuid":"9bf6f52f-3062-4d5f-ac72-6d9505079465"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-fb9b5f71-5432-4a96-ae45-515c00cc9289-73","content":"{\"type\":\"ReadFile\",\"FileContent\":{\"content\":\"1→//! One heartbeat clock. Vitals, the ECG, strain steps and on-beat all read it.\\n\\nuse serde::{Deserialize, Serialize};\\n\\n#[derive(Clone, Debug, Serialize, Deserialize)]\\npub struct Heart {\\n    pub vitals: f32,\\n    pub phase: f32,\\n    pub bpm: f32,\\n10→    pub since_r: f32,\\n    pub period: f32,\\n    pub beats: u32,\\n    pub flat: bool,\\n    pub ghost: f32,\\n}\\n\\nimpl Heart {\\n    pub fn new(vitals: f32) -> Self {\\n        let mut h = Self { vitals, phase: 0.0, bpm: 80.0, since_r: 1.0, period: 0.75, beats: 0, flat: false, ghost: 0.0 };\\n20→        h.recompute(1.0);\\n        h\\n    }\\n\\n    pub fn recompute(&mut self, coupling: f32) {\\n        let t = (1.0 - self.vitals.clamp(0.0, 100.0) / 100.0).clamp(0.0, 1.0);\\n        let c = coupling.clamp(0.25, 2.0);\\n        self.bpm = (72.0 + (148.0 - 72.0) * t) * c;\\n        self.period = 60.0 / self.bpm.max(40.0);\\n    }\\n30→\\n    /// Advances the clock. Returns true on an R-wave (world time; a flatline has none).\\n    pub fn tick(&mut self, dt: f32, coupling: f32) -> bool {\\n        self.recompute(coupling);\\n        self.vitals = self.vitals.clamp(0.0, 100.0);\\n        if self.flat {\\n            self.ghost = (self.ghost + dt / self.period).fract();\\n            self.since_r += dt;\\n            return false;\\n        }\\n40→        self.phase += dt / self.period;\\n        if self.phase >= 1.0 {\\n            self.phase = self.phase.fract();\\n            self.since_r = self.phase * self.period;\\n            self.beats = self.beats.wrapping_add(1);\\n            self.ghost = self.phase;\\n            true\\n        } else {\\n            self.since_r += dt;\\n            self.ghost = self.phase;\\n50→            false\\n        }\\n    }\\n\\n    pub fn on_beat(&self, window_ms: f32) -> bool {\\n        let w = (window_ms / 1000.0).clamp(0.02, 0.4);\\n        self.since_r <= w || (self.period - self.since_r) <= w\\n    }\\n\\n    /// Diastole: the quiet half, when a tendril can be pulled.\\n60→    pub fn diastole(&self) -> bool {\\n        self.phase > 0.28 && self.phase < 0.72\\n    }\\n\\n    /// The ghost QRS during a flatline. `ghost` is the phase in 0..1.\\n    pub fn ghost_on_beat(&self, window_ms: f32) -> bool {\\n        let w = (window_ms / 1000.0).clamp(0.02, 0.4);\\n        let g = self.ghost.rem_euclid(1.0);\\n        let since = g * self.period;\\n        let until = (1.0 - g) * self.period;\\n70→        since <= w || until <= w\\n    }\\n}\\n\",\"content_concise\":\"1→//! One heartbeat clock. Vitals, the ECG, strain steps and on-beat all read it.\\n\\nuse serde::{Deserialize, Serialize};\\n\\n#[derive(Clone, Debug, Serialize, Deserialize)]\\npub struct Heart {\\n    pub vitals: f32,\\n    pub phase: f32,\\n    pub bpm: f32,\\n10→    pub since_r: f32,\\n    pub period: f32,\\n    pub beats: u32,\\n    pub flat: bool,\\n    pub ghost: f32,\\n}\\n\\nimpl Heart {\\n    pub fn new(vitals: f32) -> Self {\\n        let mut h = Self { vitals, phase: 0.0, bpm: 80.0, since_r: 1.0, period: 0.75, beats: 0, flat: false, ghost: 0.0 };\\n20→        h.recompute(1.0);\\n        h\\n    }\\n\\n    pub fn recompute(&mut self, coupling: f32) {\\n        let t = (1.0 - self.vitals.clamp(0.0, 100.0) / 100.0).clamp(0.0, 1.0);\\n        let c = coupling.clamp(0.25, 2.0);\\n        self.bpm = (72.0 + (148.0 - 72.0) * t) * c;\\n        self.period = 60.0 / self.bpm.max(40.0);\\n    }\\n30→\\n    /// Advances the clock. Returns true on an R-wave (world time; a flatline has none).\\n    pub fn tick(&mut self, dt: f32, coupling: f32) -> bool {\\n        self.recompute(coupling);\\n        self.vitals = self.vitals.clamp(0.0, 100.0);\\n        if self.flat {\\n            self.ghost = (self.ghost + dt / self.period).fract();\\n            self.since_r += dt;\\n            return false;\\n        }\\n40→        self.phase += dt / self.period;\\n        if self.phase >= 1.0 {\\n            self.phase = self.phase.fract();\\n            self.since_r = self.phase * self.period;\\n            self.beats = self.beats.wrapping_add(1);\\n            self.ghost = self.phase;\\n            true\\n        } else {\\n            self.since_r += dt;\\n            self.ghost = self.phase;\\n50→            false\\n        }\\n    }\\n\\n    pub fn on_beat(&self, window_ms: f32) -> bool {\\n        let w = (window_ms / 1000.0).clamp(0.02, 0.4);\\n        self.since_r <= w || (self.period - self.since_r) <= w\\n    }\\n\\n    /// Diastole: the quiet half, when a tendril can be pulled.\\n60→    pub fn diastole(&self) -> bool {\\n        self.phase > 0.28 && self.phase < 0.72\\n    }\\n\\n    /// The ghost QRS during a flatline. `ghost` is the phase in 0..1.\\n    pub fn ghost_on_beat(&self, window_ms: f32) -> bool {\\n        let w = (window_ms / 1000.0).clamp(0.02, 0.4);\\n        let g = self.ghost.rem_euclid(1.0);\\n        let since = g * self.period;\\n        let until = (1.0 - g) * self.period;\\n70→        since <= w || until <= w\\n    }\\n}\\n\",\"absolute_path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224015__x42677a/work/Hands of Harbor: Second Opinion-Trauma Center: Second Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-224015/engine/crates/pav_core/src/games/surgery/heart.rs\",\"offset\":null,\"limit\":120,\"raw_output\":\"//! One heartbeat clock. Vitals, the ECG, strain steps and on-beat all read it.\\n\\nuse serde::{Deserialize, Serialize};\\n\\n#[derive(Clone, Debug, Serialize, Deserialize)]\\npub struct Heart {\\n    pub vitals: f32,\\n    pub phase: f32,\\n    pub bpm: f32,\\n    pub since_r: f32,\\n    pub period: f32,\\n    pub beats: u32,\\n    pub flat: bool,\\n    pub ghost: f32,\\n}\\n\\nimpl Heart {\\n    pub fn new(vitals: f32) -> Self {\\n        let mut h = Self { vitals, phase: 0.0, bpm: 80.0, since_r: 1.0, period: 0.75, beats: 0, flat: false, ghost: 0.0 };\\n        h.recompute(1.0);\\n        h\\n    }\\n\\n    pub fn recompute(&mut self, coupling: f32) {\\n        let t = (1.0 - self.vitals.clamp(0.0, 100.0) / 100.0).clamp(0.0, 1.0);\\n        let c = coupling.clamp(0.25, 2.0);\\n        self.bpm = (72.0 + (148.0 - 72.0) * t) * c;\\n        self.period = 60.0 / self.bpm.max(40.0);\\n    }\\n\\n    /// Advances the clock. Returns true on an R-wave (world time; a flatline has none).\\n    pub fn tick(&mut self, dt: f32, coupling: f32) -> bool {\\n        self.recompute(coupling);\\n        self.vitals = self.vitals.clamp(0.0, 100.0);\\n        if self.flat {\\n            self.ghost = (self.ghost + dt / self.period).fract();\\n            self.since_r += dt;\\n            return false;\\n        }\\n        self.phase += dt / self.period;\\n        if self.phase >= 1.0 {\\n            self.phase = self.phase.fract();\\n            self.since_r = self.phase * self.period;\\n            self.beats = self.beats.wrapping_add(1);\\n            self.ghost = self.phase;\\n            true\\n        } else {\\n            self.since_r += dt;\\n            self.ghost = self.phase;\\n            false\\n        }\\n    }\\n\\n    pub fn on_beat(&self, window_ms: f32) -> bool {\\n        let w = (window_ms / 1000.0).clamp(0.02, 0.4);\\n        self.since_r <= w || (self.period - self.since_r) <= w\\n    }\\n\\n    /// Diastole: the quiet half, when a tendril can be pulled.\\n    pub fn diastole(&self) -> bool {\\n        self.phase > 0.28 && self.phase < 0.72\\n    }\\n\\n    /// The ghost QRS during a flatline. `ghost` is the phase in 0..1.\\n    pub fn ghost_on_beat(&self, window_ms: f32) -> bool {\\n        let w = (window_ms / 1000.0).clamp(0.02, 0.4);\\n        let g = self.ghost.rem_euclid(1.0);\\n        let since = g * self.period;\\n        let until = (1.0 - g) * self.period;\\n        since <= w || until <= w\\n    }\\n}\\n\",\"total_lines\":72}}","is_error":fa