nput, dt: f32, speed: f32) {\"},{\"line_number\":736,\"content\":\"    let abs = inp.held & surg::AIM_ABSOLUTE != 0;\"},{\"line_number\":737,\"content\":\"    let snap = inp.held & surg::SNAP != 0;\"}]}]}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa38-de6f-7dc0-ae0d-e0f717ed75f2","uuid":"aabc0195-7b8c-4f9a-ae1c-60fb1d57f10a"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_325","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"A code failure was found: Dev what 4 begins scripted code without decrementing codes_left.\n\nScripted code dies when the 5-second window expires. The beat window test will step a fresh case for ~2 seconds, record heart.on_beat each tick, and assert both true and false occur while checking BPM against the vitals formula. Chain tests will verify best_chain exceeds zero after skill-1 case 0, plus unit-check chain_mul. A won case with best_chain >= 5 and score using chain will satisfy the plan.\n\nRank will be checked after a win to ensure rank_of(score, par) is at least 4. Campaign coverage tests will verify gifts, tools, hazards, strains, and code are all greater than zero. The test structure is being drafted.\n\nThe test plan now has eight specific cases. Skill1 wins every case and the campaign across ten seeds. Idle and random tool lose every case. Snapshot rewind and replay match. Overheat reaches sloppy. Ranks chains and beat window are checked. Code window expires and checkpoint retries are tested. Campaign coverage checks tools hazards strains gifts and code. Content lint checks for empty lines todos banned names and music defaults. Music defaults to 0.10 on a fresh sim. Story line count is also being verified.\n\nStory line count will be checked later if tests fail, since the plan allows 150 to 250 lines. The test file is being written now. A random tool lose helper is being drafted.\n\nThe random-tool lose helper risks accidentally winning if it holds USE while cycling through tools. A worse strategy—retargeting and using wrong positions every tick—should fail sutures and pulls instead. Case 0 is short, so tool changes alone probably will not clear it. Idle play for all cases is also planned.\n\nCode Blue idle will cap at 400 ticks. Bleeder vitals drain quickly, so the patient dies before the timer expires. Cases 0 through 7 and Code Blue will be tested for idle loss. Campaign idle would take roughly 108,000 ticks, but death still yields a Lost outcome.\n\nIdle and random-tool tests will run on seeds 1 and 2 to avoid lucky seeds hiding wins. Bot skill-1 tests will use ten seeds.\n\nThe full test suite should finish in about 0.3 seconds, so one seed may be enough if the bot is deterministic. Rank assertions will pass for any seed that reaches S or ENCORE. History rewind will use eight seconds of history before stepping.\n\nSnapshot replay will record 240 steps, rewind 90 ticks, and verify the hash matches a fresh run. Surgery state serializes correctly because GameBox derives Serialize. Checkpoint tests will step a case for 30 ticks with bot inputs, then assert the mode is M_OP.\n\nThe checkpoint test will issue a Dev kill command to end the case, then retry and assert the outcome is Playing. Restored vitals should approximate the checkpoint value rather than zero, since the checkpoint was saved at phase entry before vitals decayed.\n\nThe checkpoint retry test will assert the mode is OP, outcome is Playing, and vitals remain above 40. The code window test will enter the case, trigger Dev what 4, idle for six seconds, and confirm the result is Lost. The beat window test will initialize the heart, compute the expected BPM from vitals and coupling, verify it matches within 0.01, then step for 180 ticks to ensure both on_beat states appear.\n\nHelper functions `game` and `game_mut` will provide mutable access to the Surgery state. The sloppy test will spawn a K_POLYP hazard after entering the case.\n\nThe sloppy test will locate the spawned K_POLYP hazard and attack it with the LASER for 240 ticks, asserting that the sloppy rating exceeds zero. The content lint check will scan every line for empty lines, TODO markers, and banned names including Hope Hospital, Caduceus, Stiles, GUILT, and Healing Touch.\n\nThe content lint will use case-sensitive whole-word matching for banned names, so \"cool\" and \"XS\" are allowed as substrings. UI strings live in the shell, not `all_lines`, so the test must check `ABOUT` and shell lines separately.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-ed9cd405-8421-4c9e-bbc1-f8f4de7bc4bb-101","name":"grep","input":{"pattern":"The First Movement|Hope|Caduceus|Stiles|GUILT|Healing|COOL|\\\"XS\\\"","path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224015__x42677a/work/engine-link/crates","glob":"**/*.{rs,json}"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-ed9cd405-8421-4c9e-bbc1-f8f4de7bc4bb-102","name":"grep","input":{"pattern":"fn run_bot|fn bot_input|fn outcome|fn play\\(","path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224015__x42677a/work/engine-link/crates/pav_core/src/sim.rs"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1215,"output_tokens":2683,"cache_read_input_tokens":118016,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa38-de6f-7dc0-ae0d-e0f717ed75f2","uuid":"b8000f6d-5084-4e9a-aaa4-3e63a535f331"}
