{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_334","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Now writing the comprehensive test.\n\nDrafting helper functions for the test. `surg` fetches the Surgery component from the simulation. `cmd` and `hand` build `InputFrame` structs with absolute aiming, snapping, and optional use flags.\n\nThe `hand` helper now populates the first surgeon's input fields with absolute aim, held flags, tool selection, and full pressure. The remaining three surgeons are left as defaults. The idle cap is estimated at roughly 432,000 steps across all scenes and players.\n\nRevised step estimates put total runtime at roughly 450,000 steps. That is about a few seconds at 100,000 steps per second. A rank check inside the win loop will only slow things down by the cost of an assertion.\n\nDrafted the `assert_won` helper to run a bot and assert victory. It checks that non-campaign scenes reach rank 4 or better and that `rank` matches `rank_of(total_score(), par)`. A concern arose that `total_score()` might still change after the win if vitals continue draining.\n\nConfirmed that the bot stops on victory and the results mode freezes the score, so `total_score()` matches `shown_score` and the stored rank. Campaign scenes will also require rank 4 or better. The test caps are set to 420 seconds for cases, 260 for code, and 2200 for campaign.\n\nIdle mode should not lose code blue because vitals drain too slowly. Random tool selection might accidentally win a case, so the test will aim far from wounds and cycle tools to ensure failure.\n\nThe random-tool player will aim in a circle radius 3 that crosses the field. If it wins, the aim radius will be tightened. Tool 10 is valid because the simulation checks the held DEFIB bit rather than the tool value itself. Sending a new tool every tick will cycle tools correctly. Now writing the test file.\n\nAdding a banned-strings check to the test. A list of forbidden names will be checked against tool names, case names, and surgeon names. A word-boundary helper will prevent accidental substring matches.\n\nThe banned-strings check now uses a word-boundary split to catch \"COOL\" and \"XS\" as whole words. A concern arose that the story might use \"cool\" as temperature, which would match the uppercase check. No matches were found in the surgery files.\n\nConfirmed no forbidden strings appear in the source files. The test will require at least 150 lines of story text, allowing more but not failing on underlength. Now writing the tests and checking compilation.\n\nThe checkpoint test will verify that after 30 bot ticks the phase is entered and saved, and a dev kill followed by retry restores vitals. Entering phase 1 during those ticks is acceptable because vitals remain above zero. The code window starts in OP mode, requires one step to enter, then sets flat vitals and a 360-tick timer.\n\nConfirmed the code window expires after 300 ticks at 1/60 per tick. A 320-tick delay should guarantee death. The scripted code path still dies when flat vitals reach zero. Dev kills will be separated from other steps to avoid overlap.\n\nConfirmed the code window logic: the command sets flat vitals and a 360-tick timer before the tick loop begins. The beat window test will use only three seconds of idle ticks to verify that `on_beat` triggers within the 110 ms window near the R wave. The heart rate formula was checked against the default coupling of 1.0 and the initial vitals of 76, yielding an expected period of roughly 0.665 seconds.\n\nThe beat window spans 0.22 seconds, so roughly one-third of ticks should trigger `on_beat`. Two seconds of idle ticks should be enough to see a true beat. The heart's `since_r` counter starts at 1.0 and only resets on an R wave, meaning the first beat may not fire immediately. History rewind was also verified: a 480-tick window with 240 steps and a 90-tick rewind should succeed if snapshots exist.\n\nThe snapshot API is consistent with the starter pattern. Surgery state must be serializable because prior tests already compiled it. Rewind was never tested for serialization, so a skipped field could still match the hash. The replay logic will record inputs into a frame buffer, then replay them from the start after rewinding to the same tick.\n\nConfirmed that rewind does not truncate the recording buffer. The starter replay test steps a fresh simulation through the full recorded history, so the test replay will use the same approach.\n\nThe test will use case 0 with an 8-second history window. History is disabled during the build but re-enabled before stepping. If rewind fails because snapshots omit game state, the test will fail and be fixed. Input recording order and tick increments are acceptable. The file is ready to be written, and get_command status will be checked while writing.\n\nThe chain test will assert the full hazard list if pool suction fails to complete. A continuous hold on one pool until death should increment the chain five times, since `since_chain` resets on success and the 8-second window allows recovery. The sloppy test is kept separate so it does not interfere with the chain count. Overheat mistakes are intentional. The first spawn hazard appears at coordinates (1.2, 0).","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-28714157-4eab-41e9-878e-7184134f0f6d-117","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224015__x42677a/work/engine-link/crates/pav_core/src/games/surgery/content.rs","offset":1,"limit":40}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":620,"output_tokens":3139,"cache_read_input_tokens":129536,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa38-de6f-7dc0-ae0d-e0f717ed75f2","uuid":"6722b428-1d6c-4e28-8588-31d4650174a2"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-28714157-4eab-41e9-878e-7184134f0f6d-117","content":"{\"type\":\"ReadFile\",\"FileContent\":{\"content\":\"1→//! Case tables. One source: the sim reads these, not a second handwritten copy.\\n\\nuse super::kinds::*;\\n\\npub const G_HUSH: u8 = 1;\\npub const G_ECHO: u8 = 2;\\npub const G_DUET: u8 = 4;\\npub const NO_STRAIN: u8 = 255;\\npub const KEEP_PLATE: u8 = 255;\\n10→\\n#[derive(Clone, Copy)]\\npub struct SpawnDef {\\n    pub kind: u8,\\n    pub x: f32,\\n    pub z: f32,\\n    pub hidden: bool,\\n    pub drain: f32,\\n    pub axis: f32,\\n}\\n20→\\n#[derive(Clone, Copy)]\\npub struct PhaseDef {\\n    pub spawns: &'static [SpawnDef],\\n    pub checkpoint: bool,\\n    pub strain: u8,\\n    pub plate: u8,\\n    pub callout: u8,\\n    pub script_code: u8,\\n    pub unlock: u8,\\n30→    pub heat: bool,\\n}\\n\\npub struct CaseDef {\\n    pub name: &'static str,\\n    pub patient: &'static str,\\n    pub plate: u8,\\n    pub timer: f32,\\n    pub par: i32,\\n    pub vitals: f32,\\n40→    pub phases: &'static [PhaseDef],\",\"content_concise\":\"1→//! Case tables. One source: the sim reads these, not a second handwritten copy.\\n\\nuse super::kinds::*;\\n\\npub const G_HUSH: u8 = 1;\\npub const G_ECHO: u8 = 2;\\npub const G_DUET: u8 = 4;\\npub const NO_STRAIN: u8 = 255;\\npub const KEEP_PLATE: u8 = 255;\\n10→\\n#[derive(Clone, Copy)]\\npub struct SpawnDef {\\n    pub kind: u8,\\n    pub x: f32,\\n    pub z: f32,\\n    pub hidden: bool,\\n    pub drain: f32,\\n    pub axis: f32,\\n}\\n20→\\n#[derive(Clone, Copy)]\\npub struct PhaseDef {\\n    pub spawns: &'static [SpawnDef],\\n    pub checkpoint: bool,\\n    pub strain: u8,\\n    pub plate: u8,\\n    pub callout: u8,\\n    pub script_code: u8,\\n    pub unlock: u8,\\n30→    pub heat: bool,\\n}\\n\\npub struct CaseDef {\\n    pub name: &'static str,\\n    pub patient: &'static str,\\n    pub plate: u8,\\n    pub timer: f32,\\n    pub par: i32,\\n    pub vitals: f32,\\n40→    pub phases: &'static [PhaseDef],\",\"absolute_path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224015__x42677a/work/Hands of Harbor: Second Opinion-Trauma Center: Second Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-224015/engine/crates/pav_core/src/games/surgery/content.rs\",\"offset\":1,\"limit\":40,\"raw_output\":\"//! Case tables. One source: the sim reads these, not a second handwritten copy.\\n\\nuse super::kinds::*;\\n\\npub const G_HUSH: u8 = 1;\\npub const G_ECHO: u8 = 2;\\npub const G_DUET: u8 = 4;\\npub const NO_STRAIN: u8 = 255;\\npub const KEEP_PLATE: u8 = 255;\\n\\n#[derive(Clone, Copy)]\\npub struct SpawnDef {\\n    pub kind: u8,\\n    pub x: f32,\\n    pub z: f32,\\n    pub hidden: bool,\\n    pub drain: f32,\\n    pub axis: f32,\\n}\\n\\n#[derive(Clone, Copy)]\\npub struct PhaseDef {\\n    pub spawns: &'static [SpawnDef],\\n    pub checkpoint: bool,\\n    pub strain: u8,\\n    pub plate: u8,\\n    pub callout: u8,\\n    pub script_code: u8,\\n    pub unlock: u8,\\n    pub heat: bool,\\n}\\n\\npub struct CaseDef {\\n    pub name: &'static str,\\n    pub patient: &'static str,\\n    pub plate: u8,\\n    pub timer: f32,\\n    pub par: i32,\\n    pub vitals: f32,\\n    pub phases: &'static [PhaseDef],\\n\",\"total_lines\":328}}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa38-de6f-7dc0-ae0d-e0f717ed75f2","uuid":"5db8bae9-200c-4777-8459-a7bb05515320"}
