{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_370","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Spawn does not set tags. The pool does not wander.\n\nSticky selection is ruled out because the first pool is dead. The nearest pool is the new one at distance zero. Tremor offset is too small to explain the failure. Another cause is being sought.\n\nThe focus sticky logic is the culprit. It checks if the focused hazard is alive, but it also accepts any alive hazard that accepts the tool and is within radius plus 2.6 while use is held. Because the first pool is dead, the focus stays on it. Another alive hazard can then intercept the gesture.\n\nThe next spawn step runs without the use button held. The previous release sets just_release to true. Because focus is still on the dead pool, position() fails and selection falls through to the nearest hazard.\n\nThe cursor remains at the old pool's position during the spawn tick. The new pool is slightly closer, so nearest selection should target it. The case pool might still be chosen if focus was previously set to it.\n\nThe first pool suctioned correctly. The second pool held for 120 ticks without dying. The suspicion is shifting to the `near` distance check in suction, which uses `d <= h.radius + 0.08`. The `select` function returns the nearest hazard of any kind, not necessarily one that accepts the tool.\n\nThe first pool might not actually be dead. The alive pool search could then select the original case pool instead of the newest spawn. The second pool's work might also reset when focus switches, or its drain parameter could make it too strong to die.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-3805de19-6688-408b-a9ad-4ab3114b9733-170","name":"grep","input":{"pattern":"fr.score|score:","path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224015__x42677a/work/engine-link/crates/pav_core/src/games/surgery/mod.rs"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-3805de19-6688