{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_371","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The score formula weights hands, vitals, timer, and mistakes.\n\nThe first pool cleared with a score of 2295. The second did not. The cursor is closer to the new pool than the case pool despite tremor. I am checking accepts() and Hazard::dist for hidden selection checks.\n\nThe second pool does not overlap the case laceration. I will add a temporary debug print to the test and remove it afterward, then examine the hands code after selection.\n\nI checked whether pool work requires proximity to the center, but the cursor is already there. The pool is not jittering after spawn because its tag is zero. I am now reading the start of hazard::act for a global rejection. I also verified that the second pool is not the original case pool; the spawn logic places it correctly.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-7d741198-a385-4aa8-a5e9-cc7932663985-172","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224015__x42677a/work/engine-link/crates/pav_core/src/games/surgery/hazard.rs","offset":265,"limit":50}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2004,"output_tokens":746,"cache_read_input_tokens":166912,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa38-de6f-7dc0-ae0d-e0f717ed75f2","uuid":"4b28c369-83a2-4525-b4e5-1e96e530a2a1"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-7d741198-a385-4aa8-a5e9-cc7932663985-172","content":"{\"type\":\"ReadFile\",\"FileContent\":{\"content\":\"265→        false\\n    }\\n}\\n\\nfn side_of(h: &Hazard, x: f32, z: f32) -> (f32, f32) {\\n270→    let dx = x - h.x;\\n    let dz = z - h.z;\\n    let dirx = h.axis.cos();\\n    let dirz = h.axis.sin();\\n    let along = dx * dirx + dz * dirz;\\n    let side = -dx * dirz + dz * dirx;\\n    (along, side)\\n}\\n\\n/// One tick of a tool against one hazard. `just_release` is use going up.\\n280→pub fn apply(\\n    h: &mut Hazard,\\n    x: f32,\\n    z: f32,\\n    tool: u8,\\n    use_held: bool,\\n    just_release: bool,\\n    pressure: f32,\\n    rot: i32,\\n    dt: f32,\\n290→    power: f32,\\n    diastole: bool,\\n    strict: f32,\\n) -> Hit {\\n    let mut hit = Hit::default();\\n    if !h.alive {\\n        return hit;\\n    }\\n    let d = h.dist(x, z);\\n    let near = d <= h.radius + 0.08;\\n300→    let p = pressure.clamp(0.15, 1.0) * power.max(0.2);\\n\\n    if tool == SCANNER && use_held && d < h.radius + 0.35 {\\n        hit.engaged = true;\\n        hit.cue = CUE_PING;\\n        h.revealed = 8.0;\\n        h.hidden = false;\\n        if h.kind == K_FOREIGN || h.kind == K_NODULE {\\n            return hit;\\n        }\\n310→    }\\n\\n    if h.hidden && h.revealed <= 0.0 {\\n        return hit;\\n    }\",\"content_concise\":\"265→        false\\n    }\\n}\\n\\nfn side_of(h: &Hazard, x: f32, z: f32) -> (f32, f32) {\\n270→    let dx = x - h.x;\\n    let dz = z - h.z;\\n    let dirx = h.axis.cos();\\n    let dirz = h.axis.sin();\\n    let along = dx * dirx + dz * dirz;\\n    let side = -dx * dirz + dz * dirx;\\n    (along, side)\\n}\\n\\n/// One tick of a tool against one hazard. `just_release` is use going up.\\n280→pub fn apply(\\n    h: &mut Hazard,\\n    x: f32,\\n    z: f32,\\n    tool: u8,\\n    use_held: bool,\\n    just_release: bool,\\n    pressure: f32,\\n    rot: i32,\\n    dt: f32,\\n290→    power: f32,\\n    diastole: bool,\\n    strict: f32,\\n) -> Hit {\\n    let mut hit = Hit::default();\\n    if !h.alive {\\n        return hit;\\n    }\\n    let d = h.dist(x, z);\\n    let near = d <= h.radius + 0.08;\\n300→    let p = pressure.clamp(0.15, 1.0) * power.max(0.2);\\n\\n    if tool == SCANNER && use_held && d < h.radius + 0.35 {\\n        hit.engaged = true;\\n        hit.cue = CUE_PING;\\n        h.revealed = 8.0;\\n        h.hidden = false;\\n        if h.kind == K_FOREIGN || h.kind == K_NODULE {\\n            return hit;\\n        }\\n310→    }\\n\\n    if h.hidden && h.revealed <= 0.0 {\\n        return hit;\\n    }\",\"absolute_path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224015__x42677a/work/Hands of Harbor: Second Opinion-Trauma Center: Second Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-224015/engine/crates/pav_core/src/games/surgery/hazard.rs\",\"offset\":265,\"limit\":50,\"raw_output\":\"        false\\n    }\\n}\\n\\nfn side_of(h: &Hazard, x: f32, z: f32) -> (f32, f32) {\\n    let dx = x - h.x;\\n    let dz = z - h.z;\\n    let dirx = h.axis.cos();\\n    let dirz = h.axis.sin();\\n    let along = dx * dirx + dz * dirz;\\n    let side = -dx * dirz + dz * dirx;\\n    (along, side)\\n}\\n\\n/// One tick of a tool against one hazard. `just_release` is use going up.\\npub fn apply(\\n    h: &mut Hazard,\\n    x: f32,\\n    z: f32,\\n    tool: u8,\\n    use_held: bool,\\n    just_release: bool,\\n    pressure: f32,\\n    rot: i32,\\n    dt: f32,\\n    power: f32,\\n    diastole: bool,\\n    strict: f32,\\n) -> Hit {\\n    let mut hit = Hit::default();\\n    if !h.alive {\\n        return hit;\\n    }\\n    let d = h.dist(x, z);\\n    let near = d <= h.radius + 0.08;\\n    let p = pressure.clamp(0.15, 1.0) * power.max(0.2);\\n\\n    if tool == SCANNER && use_held && d < h.radius + 0.35 {\\n        hit.engaged = true;\\n        hit.cue = CUE_PING;\\n        h.revealed = 8.0;\\n        h.hidden = false;\\n        if h.kind == K_FOREIGN || h.kind == K_NODULE {\\n            return hit;\\n        }\\n    }\\n\\n    if h.hidden && h.revealed <= 0.0 {\\n        return hit;\\n    }\\n\",\"total_lines\":642}}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa38-de6f-7dc0-ae0d-e0f717ed75f2","uuid":"a30742f5-88be-4493-9571-c5a830b17215"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_372","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The apply function returns early when the pool is hidden, so suction never runs.\n\nSpawn does not set hidden, and make() leaves it false. The chain test failed because the second pool was not cleared. I will instrument the failing test to print hazard state and pool details. A fresh test design is preferable to fighting existing wounds.\n\nI will print work, hidden status, position, and surgeon focus in the assert to diagnose the failure. I am also checking whether the old pool's sticky radius is keeping focus on it after death, which would prevent suction of the newly spawned pool.\n\nThe second pool is nearest to the cursor, so focus shifts to it on the spawn tick. Work does not increase because there is no USE command. The focus is already on the target when use is held.\n\nThe second pool should be suctioned because it is within range and the hands run after spawn. The alive count is three, so the case has not ended. I am checking whether a maximum hazard limit or replacement logic is interfering.\n\nThe alive count is confirmed at three. The second pool remains alive and the cursor is on its coordinates, so suction should be happening. I am now checking whether the DEFIB constant or the SUCTION tool constant matches the hazard tool value. I am also investigating if tremor position is interfering with distance checks.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-4bf4e8eb-fa98-4f2e-a20e-efc51ed32baf-173","name":"search_replace","input":{"file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224015__x42677a/work/engine-link/crates/pav_core/tests/surgery.rs","old_string":"        assert!(!game(&sim).hazards.iter().any(|h| h.id == id && h.alive), \"pool stayed {}\", status(&sim));","new_string":"        let stuck = game(&sim).hazards.iter().find(|h| h.id == id && h.alive).map(|h| {\n            format!(\"id {} work {:.3} need {:.3} rad {:.2} hid {} at {:.2},{:.2} focus {:?}\", h.id, h.work, h.need, h.radius, h.hidden, h.x, h.z, game(&sim).surgeons[0].focus)\n        });\n        assert!(stuck.is_none(), \"pool stayed {stuck:?} {}\", status(&sim));"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1249,"output_tokens":1100,"cache_read_input_tokens":168832,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa38-de6f-7dc0-ae0d-e0f717ed75f2","uuid":"2ef1e791-5403-4021-9c31-d25bd3ba3d6b"}
