e_number\":218,\"content\":\"    pub spawn_n: u8,\"},{\"line_number\":289,\"content\":\"            spawn_n: 0,\"},{\"line_number\":709,\"content\":\"                let n = self.spawn_n;\"},{\"line_number\":710,\"content\":\"                self.spawn_n = self.spawn_n.wrapping_add(1);\"}]}]}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa38-de6f-7dc0-ae0d-e0f717ed75f2","uuid":"bf5ce239-7fca-4fbc-9eb5-3cc8ee9d861b"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_377","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The sticky theory remains the best explanation for focus staying on id 2 while the cursor is on id 4.\n\nThe first pool cleared should have been id 3, not id 2. The case pool may have been targeted instead due to proximity, but the alive count of 3 suggests it was not cleared.\n\nThe case pool at id 2 was already focused before the second hold began. The cursor sits roughly 1.6 units away, well outside the sticky range of 3.35, so no new selection occurs. The focus likely shifted to the case pool during the first suction when the spawned pool died.\n\nThe prior assumption that focus shifted to the case pool during the first suction may be wrong. If the spawned pool died, the next step spawns a new pool at id 4. The cursor is closer to that new pool than to the case pool, so nearest selection should set focus to 4. Sticky would then keep it there. The spawn tick runs before the tick sees the new pool, so it exists in the list.\n\nThe spawn tick set focus to the case pool at id 2. The hold tick then held use and sticky kept that dead focus, since the new pool was too far away.\n\nThe spawn tick may not have had a valid cursor. Default surgeons are inactive, and slot 0 only becomes active when the lead flag is set. Without that flag, the spawn frame lacks aim data, so nearest selection could not target the new pool.\n\nInactive surgeons skip steering but still run selection with the previous cursor position and no held use. The spawn tick therefore selects nearest from (1.2, 0) toward the new pool, which should win. A debug print of all hazard positions will verify the actual layout.\n\nThe debug print strategy is abandoned. The robust fix is to first snap the cursor to a corner for one frame without use, forcing focus away from the case pool. Then spawn a new pool and snap to it without use for another frame so nearest selection sets focus to that pool. Finally, hold use.\n\nThe proposed snap-to-corner workaround fails. Snapping to a distant corner without use would select the laceration at (-1.4, 0) instead of the pool, and the laceration does not accept suction.\n\nThe just_release path returns the alive laceration immediately without distance checks. Sticky then fails to accept suction on that laceration, so nearest selection finally targets the pool under the cursor.\n\nThe no-use aim frame keeps the laceration focus. The first use frame then falls through to nearest selection and targets the pool. Sticky keeps the pool on subsequent frames.\n\nThe test bug is confirmed: after the first pool dies, the next step spawns a new pool but immediately presses use while focus may still be on the case pool. The fix is to release suction for one frame before holding use again. That single release frame lets nearest selection target the newly spawned pool, so sticky holds stick to it.\n\nThe release-frame workaround fails when the case pool is still alive and accepts suction. The just_release path returns that alive focus unconditionally, so the cursor would still be stuck on the old pool. To actually drop the focus, the release frame must have both use false and just_release false, which skips the sticky block entirely and forces a fall-through to nearest selection.","signature":""},{"type":"text","text":"The second pool never fills because a held tool stays stuck on the earlier pool. I’ll release, retarget, then suction."},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-135e1e1a-75c5-4ab4-8e0e-ca4fe368e395-179","name":"search_replace","input":{"file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224015__x42677a/work/engine-link/crates/pav_core/tests/surgery.rs","old_string":"        let (x, z, id) = {\n            let h = game(&sim).hazards.iter().rev().find(|h| h.alive && h.kind == K_POOL).expect(\"pool\");\n            (h.x, h.z, h.id)\n        };\n        for _ in 0..120 {\n            let alive = game(&sim).hazards.iter().any(|h| h.id == id && h.alive);\n            if !alive {\n                break;\n            }\n            sim.step(&hand(x, z, SUCTION, true));\n        }\n        let g = game(&sim);\n        let stuck = g.hazards.iter().find(|h| h.id == id && h.alive).map(|h| {\n            format!(\n                \"id {} work {:.3} need {:.3} rad {:.2} hid {} at {:.2},{:.2} focus {:?} cursor {:.2},{:.2}\",\n                h.id, h.work, h.need, h.radius, h.hidden, h.x, h.z, g.surgeons[0].focus, g.surgeons[0].x, g.surgeons[0].z\n            )\n        });\n        assert!(stuck.is_none(), \"pool stayed {stuck:?} {}\", status(&sim));","new_string":"        let (x, z, id) = {\n            let h = game(&sim).hazards.iter().rev().find(|h| h.alive && h.kind == K_POOL).expect(\"pool\");\n            (h.x, h.z, h.id)\n        };\n        // A held tool keeps the last wound. Two idle frames let the cursor take the new pool.\n        sim.step(&hand(x, z, SUCTION, false));\n        sim.step(&hand(x, z, SUCTION, false));\n        for _ in 0..120 {\n            let alive = game(&sim).hazards.iter().any(|h| h.id == id && h.alive);\n            if !alive {\n                break;\n            }\n            sim.step(&hand(x, z, SUCTION, true));\n        }\n        assert!(\n            !game(&sim).hazards.iter().any(|h| h.id == id && h.alive),\n            \"pool {id} stayed {}\",\n            status(&sim)\n        );"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":4004,"output_tokens":2604,"cache_read_input_tokens":173696,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa38-de6f-7dc0-ae0d-e0f717ed75f2","uuid":"7e7048bc-2e95-446f-8f46-dbd9170f1971"}
