,101,115,40,41,46,101,118,101,114,121,40,40,112,41,32,61,62,32,112,46,114,101,97,100,121,41,44,32,99,111,112,105,101,115,40,41,46,102,105,108,116,101,114,40,40,112,41,32,61,62,32,33,112,46,114,101,97,100,121,41,46,109,97,112,40,40,112,41,32,61,62,32,112,46,107,101,121,41,46,106,111,105,110,40,39,44,32,39,41,32,124,124,32,115,116,97,116,101,46,115,116,97,116,117,115,63,46,112,104,97,115,101,41,59,10,60,47,119,111,114,107,115,112,97,99,101,95,114,101,115,117,108,116,62],\"stderr\":[],\"exit_code\":0,\"match_count\":24,\"file_matches\":[{\"path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224015__x42677a/tmp/grok-goal-907ccca5ce3b/implementer/harness.html\",\"matches\":[{\"line_number\":102,\"content\":\"      session: meta('hub:session'),\"},{\"line_number\":103,\"content\":\"      players: meta('hub:session-players'),\"},{\"line_number\":104,\"content\":\"      mode: meta('hub:session-mode'),\"},{\"line_number\":105,\"content\":\"      minutes: meta('hub:session-minutes'),\"},{\"line_number\":224,\"content\":\"    const cell = { ...p, el, label, frame, endpoint, violations: [], instrumented: true, gone: false, progress: [], cardSent: '' };\"},{\"line_number\":254,\"content\":\"  // By hand, the card lifts by itself after ten seconds (more when a player asks), as in a session;\"},{\"line_number\":272,\"content\":\"/** A game's own card, as the hub drives it: the countdown and who is ready, to every copy that shows one. */\"},{\"line_number\":278,\"content\":\"    const card = { left, paused: false, starting: left === null, ready, asking: state.answers.more.size, asked: state.answers.more.has(cell.key) };\"},{\"line_number\":279,\"content\":\"    const id = JSON.stringify({ ...card, left: left === null ? null : Math.ceil(left / 1000) });\"},{\"line_number\":280,\"content\":\"    if (cell.cardSent === id) continue;\"},{\"line_number\":281,\"content\":\"    cell.cardSent = id;\"},{\"line_number\":282,\"content\":\"    cell.bridge.card(card);\"},{\"line_number\":286,\"content\":\"/** A player answered on the game's own card: Ready, or more time (+10 s; again takes it back). */\"},{\"line_number\":300,\"content\":\"  log(`${cell.key} answers ${what} on the game's card`);\"},{\"line_number\":421,\"content\":\"    check('head metas', m && m.session === '1' && modeOf(m.mode), m ? `hub:session=${m.session} mode=${m.mode}` : 'could not fetch the page');\"},{\"line_number\":424,\"content\":\"    check('hub:session-players is a range within 1–4', seats.length >= 1 && seats.length <= 2 && least >= 1 && least <= most && most <= 4, `hub:session-players=${m?.players}`);\"},{\"line_number\":425,\"content\":\"    if (m?.minutes != null) check('hub:session-minutes, when given, is a number', Number(m.minutes) > 0, `hub:session-minutes=${m.minutes}`);\"},{\"line_number\":440,\"content\":\"    // The card collects ready: every game readies up by itself once loaded, with no prompt and no key.\"},{\"line_number\":442,\"content\":\"    check('ready without a key press (the card asks the players)', loaded, copies().filter((p) => !p.ready).map((p) => p.key).join(', '));\"},{\"line_number\":443,\"content\":\"    // A game that shows its own card takes the players' answers on it: Enter is Ready.\"},{\"line_number\":444,\"content\":\"    if (caps.some((c) => c?.card)) {\"},{\"line_number\":446,\"content\":\"      const sent = await until(() => players.every((c) => c.cardSent), 2000);\"},{\"line_number\":449,\"content\":\"      check('its own card: Enter answers Ready', sent && answered, players.filter((c) => !state.answers.ready.has(c.key)).map((c) => `${c.key}${c.cardSent ? '' : ' (no card yet)'}`).join(', '));\"},{\"line_number\":453,\"content\":\"    check('the round starts when the card ends', started && copies().every((p) => p.ready), copies().filter((p) => !p.ready).map((p) => p.key).join(', ') || state.status?.phase);\"}]}]}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa38-de6f-7dc0-ae0d-e0f717ed75f2","uuid":"55c51539-be0b-43a1-a1c3-bbbc65f4b9eb"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_398","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"I need to understand what the harness checks for shared-world mode.\n\nThe conformance checklist requires head metas with hub:session=1 and a recognized mode. It requires hub:session-players to be a range within 1-4 and hub:session-minutes to be numeric if provided. Every copy must say hello, naming protocol 1 and the mode. The hello seats must cover the player count, which [1,4] satisfies for any number of players from 1 to 4. The game must call ready() once loaded without a key press.\n\nThe harness sends a synthetic Enter key each frame. The game shim listens for this JavaScript event and calls AIHub.answer('ready'). The harness sets cardSent internally, not the game. The conformance check passes only when every player cell has cardSent and the ready answer is present.\n\nThe shim adds a capture-phase keydown listener for Enter to call AIHub.answer('ready'). It only initializes when window.AIHub is already active, then connects in shared-world mode with seats [1, 4] and card: true.\n\nThe Enter listener is placed after the active check, so it only registers when the hub is already active.\n\nRounds begin once the card ends. Random arrow keys are sent during play.\n\nShared-world mode is not in SELF_REPORTED, so the traffic check requires bidirectional flow for multiplayer sessions. A single player passes automatically. Four-player host-leave scenarios must show traffic flowing both ways.\n\nIn host-leave mode, the game must not call finish when the host leaves. The coordinator should void the round instead. The shim finishes on time-up only if isHost, but host-leave removes the host before that point. It is unclear whether the hub reassigns host in this case.\n\nThe conformance check for host-leave mode requires the round status to be 'void' and the end reason to be 'host-left'. The game must not call finish if the remaining player is not the new host. Otherwise the round ends with a valid 'played' status, and the host must call finish with valid standings on time-up. Every remaining copy must receive the bridge.ended signal. There must be no protocol problems, errors, dialogs, popups, or socket issues.\n\nThe server scenario requires the world copy to have record.status 'played', record.hostId matching the server cell, and positive server traffic.\n\nPLAN.md specifies two manual checks. A two-page test verifies that client aim changes the host cursor and vitals match. A one-page test outside the session confirms the title appears and play does not depend on the hub. These are separate from harness conformance and must be implemented manually with output logged to hub.txt.\n\nThe shim calls AIHub.finish with standings formatted as an array of arrays of player IDs. Every present player must appear exactly once, and the server must be excluded. The IDs come from AIHub.players. A single group containing all present players is a valid tie.\n\nThe fallback standings format is confirmed as a valid single group. If Rust publishes H.last with proper standings, that should be used instead.\n\nI need to read round.js to identify what counts as protocol problems, such as invalid standings, finish calls from non-hosts, or messages sent before the round starts.\n\nThe ready() call must happen automatically after the first frame without any key press. The shim's connect().then block does not trigger this.\n\nRust must poll the shim and call H.ready() after the first frame. The full startup sequence is page load, session.js, shim connection, slow WASM unpack, game start, then Rust polling H.info to trigger ready. The harness allows 20 seconds for this. Packed HTML may delay unpacking enough to fail that window.\n\nThe shim emits hello before WASM loads, while ready waits for the first frame. The Enter key that answers ready is handled entirely in JavaScript by the shim, so Rust does not need to process it. The game must still draw its own card visually. ready() and answer('ready') are separate calls.\n\nThe harness waits for every copy to call ready() before it sends the card and pokes Enter. The shim should trigger ready() from Rust after the first frame, while the Enter listener handles the answer. If WASM unpacking delays too long, ready() may fail. I should also call ready() from the shim once connect resolves.\n\nI should not call ready() in the connect callback. The game must finish unpacking and reach its first frame before Rust triggers ready(). Otherwise the harness starts the round too early, and the traffic check fails because the game is not running during the play window.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-78c57845-c01e-48c1-b78d-7e96511f0876-31","name":"grep","input":{"pattern":"host-left|server|function finish|standings|issues","path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224015__x42677a/work/engine-link/web","glob":"*.js"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-78c57845-c01e-48c1-b78d-7e96511f0876-32","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224015__x42677a/work/engine-link/web/session.js","offset":180,"limit":80}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":7479,"output_tokens":2303,"cache_read_input_tokens":83456,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa38-de6f-7dc0-ae0d-e0f717ed75f2","uuid":"31187943-f1be-49fc-8835-fc65c52c310a"}
