\"line_number\":423,\"content\":\"    const [least, most = least] = seats;\"},{\"line_number\":424,\"content\":\"    check('hub:session-players is a range within 1–4', seats.length >= 1 && seats.length <= 2 && least >= 1 && least <= most && most <= 4, `hub:session-players=${m?.players}`);\"},{\"line_number\":432,\"content\":\"    const caps = state.coordinator.seats().map((s) => s.caps);\"},{\"line_number\":434,\"content\":\"    check('hello seats cover this player count', caps.every((c) => Array.isArray(c.seats) && c.seats[0] <= Math.max(2, n) && c.seats[1] >= n), JSON.stringify(caps[0]?.seats));\"},{\"line_number\":470,\"content\":\"    const own = SELF_REPORTED.includes(mode);\"},{\"line_number\":505,\"content\":\"    if (scenario === 'host-leave' && !SELF_REPORTED.includes(state.coordinator.mode)) {\"},{\"line_number\":506,\"content\":\"      check('host leaving voids the round', ended && record.status === 'void' && record.endReason === 'host-left', record ? `${record.status} (${record.reason})` : 'no end');\"}]}]}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa38-de6f-7dc0-ae0d-e0f717ed75f2","uuid":"11c054d3-5c9e-4442-b213-4fdd6bedec72"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_400","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"bridge.js and round.js are missing from the scratch directory.\n\nI will fetch bridge.js and round.js from the GitHub repository to serve the harness. I also need to copy harness.html into tests/hub.\n\nI will verify the exact hub test steps in PLAN. I need to understand Surgeon struct fields for apply_mirror. The JS shim will follow Appendix B almost verbatim.\n\nRust will poll H.poll() each frame to read JSON events. It must process card, start, time-up, message, leave, and end events. Before the shim calls finish on time-up, Rust should publish standings via H.publish. It also needs to read H.info from the hub once it is available.\n\nRust will call H.ready() once H.info is available. Non-host clients send input to the hub roughly every 15 frames. Host clients send snapshots roughly every 15 frames. Standings publish to the hub about once per second so the time-up event can read H.last.\n\nThe server runs the simulation and sends snapshots but skips local drawing and sound. It treats itself as the host.\n\nClients in mirror mode receive snapshots from the host and render SurgeryFrame directly from JSON without running an authoritative simulation.\n\nClients will run a local simulation but overwrite state from snapshots using apply_mirror. SurgeryFrame is the single source of truth for drawing. The client predicts its own cursor, tool animation, sound, and particles locally. It stores decoded snapshots in hazards, vitals, and cursors while keeping its own cursor separate.\n\nThe host runs the authoritative simulation, applies client inputs to surgeon slots, and sends snapshots. Players carry id, name, and color but no slot; the local slot should be AIHub.me when not the server. Player IDs likely match seat order. I still need to inspect the welcome message shape.\n\nSnapshot encoding will quantize hazard positions and other values to keep payloads under 1200 bytes. The example snapshot JSON includes vitals, BPM, phase, timer, code time, a hazards array with scaled coordinates, a cursors array, and the last eight cues. Client input JSON carries slot, aim coordinates, tool selection, held item, and pressure.\n\nClient input JSON also includes a sequence number for edge repeat. The host applies each input to the surgeon at the matching slot.\n\nThe host seeds the simulation from info.seed, but Surgery uses sim.state.rng, so I need to check whether that RNG supports reseeding.\n\nWhen the hub is active, the game should skip the title screen and start in card mode waiting for connection. Otherwise it runs normally.\n\nThe shim always sets window.__hub, yet returns early if H.active is false. The product must not depend on __hub existing.\n\nThe shim only defines poll, ready, and other methods when H.active is true. Rust must check H.active before calling them. session.js always injects AIHub, so the game falls back to normal title behavior when the hub is inactive.\n\nThe server will still pump the simulation and redraw frames even though it skips drawing, clears the canvas, and omits sound. It should also ignore pause keys like Esc and Options while the hub is active. A two-page Playwright test script will verify the hub integration.\n\nThe two-page test will use the harness with two players. It will drive client aim and read window.__game.status() from each iframe to compare host cursors and vitals.\n\nI will check whether the codebase already evaluates JavaScript from Rust. I also need to inspect Surgeon fields, input application logic, and shell card drawing before writing the hub shim.\n\nI will use wasm_bindgen, web_sys, and js_sys to call the hub shim from Rust. The plan is to fetch window.__hub via js_sys::Reflect, then invoke its poll method as a JavaScript function and return the result as a string.\n\nRust will read H.info separately from H.poll and stringify it. Once the hub resolves, Rust will call ready(), reseed the simulation RNG before boot_code, and switch to card mode. The operation timer must wait until AIHub.time() becomes non-negative; otherwise the game stays in card mode.\n\nThe title, attract mode, and menus will be skipped entirely. The server will run the Code Blue operation directly without a local surgeon, sending snapshots while skipping drawing and audio. I still need to check how the welcome message sets the server flag.\n\nThe server flag is probably set by round.js when it sends the welcome message. Client input will be sent at 15Hz and repeated on tool or button changes until acknowledged. The host writes each input into InputFrame.surgeons[slot] for the next ticks. The local slot maps directly to AIHub.me, but the server should not assign a local surgeon.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-cfcd2249-3003-4693-a35e-3ccd9519f0b9-36","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224015__x42677a/work/engine-link/crates/pav_ui/src/surgery/mod.rs","offset":300,"limit":120}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-cfcd2249-3003-4693-a35e-3ccd9519f0b9-37","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224015__x42677a/work/engine-link/crates/pav_ui/src/surgery/mod.rs","offset":680,"limit":200}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-cfcd2249-3003-4693-a35e-3ccd9519f0b9-38","name":"grep","input":{"pattern":"struct Rng|fn seed|pub struct Surgeon","glob":"**/pav_core/src/**/*.rs"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-cfcd2249-3003-4693-a35e-3ccd9519f0b9-39","name":"web_fetch","input":{"url":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/michaelcrosato/ai-hub/main/lib/hub/round.js"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":957,"output_tokens":2825,"cache_read_input_tokens":94080,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa38-de6f-7dc0-ae0d-e0f717ed75f2","uuid":"82475ab5-199e-4d77-97fe-a4b20dfea13b"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-cfcd2249-3003-4693-a35e-3ccd9519f0b9-36","content":"{\"type\":\"ReadFile\",\"FileContent\":{\"content\":\"300→                        v.push(self.row(1, \\\"Fullscreen\\\"));\\n                    }\\n                }\\n            }\\n            Screen::About => {\\n                v.push(about_page_title(self.about_page).into());\\n                v.extend(about_lines(self.about_page));\\n            }\\n            Screen::Controls => {\\n                v.push(format!(\\\"Aim   right stick or mouse   {}\\\", self.prompt(\\\"use\\\")));\\n310→                v.push(\\\"Tools   left stick or 1-8\\\".into());\\n                v.push(format!(\\\"Operate   {}\\\", self.prompt(\\\"use\\\")));\\n                v.push(format!(\\\"Gift   {}\\\", self.prompt(\\\"gift\\\")));\\n                v.push(format!(\\\"Chart   {}\\\", self.prompt(\\\"chart\\\")));\\n            }\\n            Screen::Pause => {\\n                for (i, item) in [\\\"Resume\\\", \\\"Restart\\\", \\\"Controls\\\", \\\"Settings\\\", \\\"Dev Mode\\\", \\\"Quit to Title\\\"].iter().enumerate() {\\n                    v.push(self.row(i, item));\\n                }\\n            }\\n320→            Screen::Dev => {\\n                v.push(self.row(0, if self.live { \\\"Live  on\\\" } else { \\\"Live  off\\\" }));\\n                v.push(self.row(1, if self.bot_plays { \\\"Bot plays  on\\\" } else { \\\"Bot plays  off\\\" }));\\n                let start = self.dev_page as usize * 6;\\n                for i in 0..6 {\\n                    let id = start + i;\\n                    if id >= Tune::FIELDS.len() {\\n                        break;\\n                    }\\n                    let (name, def, _, _) = Tune::FIELDS[id];\\n330→                    v.push(self.row(i + 2, &format!(\\\"{name}  {:.2}  default {def:.2}\\\", self.sliders[id])));\\n                }\\n                v.push(self.row(8, \\\"Reset All\\\"));\\n            }\\n            Screen::Attract => {\\n                v.push(\\\"DEMO\\\".into());\\n                v.push(format!(\\\"Press {}\\\", self.prompt(\\\"confirm\\\")));\\n            }\\n            Screen::Hud => {\\n                v.push(\\\"OPERATION\\\".into());\\n340→            }\\n            Screen::Story => v.push(\\\"Advance\\\".into()),\\n            Screen::Results => v.push(\\\"Results\\\".into()),\\n            Screen::Dead => v.push(self.row(0, \\\"Retry\\\")),\\n            Screen::Card => {\\n                v.push(\\\"Pre-op\\\".into());\\n                v.push(\\\"Keep the patient alive\\\".into());\\n                v.push(format!(\\\"{} ready\\\", self.prompt(\\\"confirm\\\")));\\n            }\\n            Screen::Chart => {\\n350→                v.push(\\\"Chart\\\".into());\\n                v.push(\\\"Begin the operation\\\".into());\\n                v.push(format!(\\\"{} begin\\\", self.prompt(\\\"confirm\\\")));\\n            }\\n        }\\n        v\\n    }\\n\\n    fn row(&self, i: usize, label: &str) -> String {\\n        if i == self.focus {\\n360→            format!(\\\"> {label}\\\")\\n        } else {\\n            label.to_string()\\n        }\\n    }\\n\\n    pub fn step(&mut self, input: Input) -> Vec<Cmd> {\\n        if let Some(d) = input.device {\\n            self.device = d;\\n            if d == DeviceKind::KeyboardMouse || d == DeviceKind::Gamepad {\\n370→                self.ever_fine = true;\\n            }\\n        }\\n        let mut cmds = Vec::new();\\n        if self.screen == Screen::Attract {\\n            if input.any {\\n                self.screen = Screen::Title;\\n                self.paused = false;\\n                self.idle = 0.0;\\n                self.focus = 0;\\n380→                cmds.push(Cmd::ToTitle);\\n            }\\n            return cmds;\\n        }\\n        let menuish = matches!(\\n            self.screen,\\n            Screen::Title | Screen::Menu | Screen::Difficulty | Screen::Files | Screen::Settings | Screen::About | Screen::Controls\\n        );\\n        if menuish && !input.any {\\n            self.idle += input.dt;\\n390→            if self.idle >= 10.0 {\\n                self.screen = Screen::Attract;\\n                self.idle = 0.0;\\n                cmds.push(Cmd::LoadAttract);\\n                return cmds;\\n            }\\n        } else if input.any {\\n            self.idle = 0.0;\\n        }\\n        if self.touch_only && !self.ever_fine && self.screen == Screen::Title {\\n400→            if input.confirm || input.click {\\n                self.screen = Screen::Settings;\\n                self.focus = 0;\\n            }\\n            return cmds;\\n        }\\n        let n = self.count();\\n        if let Some(p) = input.pointer {\\n            if let Some(hit) = self.hit(p) {\\n                self.focus = hit;\\n410→                self.device = DeviceKind::KeyboardMouse;\\n            }\\n        }\\n        if input.up {\\n            self.focus = self.focus.saturating_sub(1);\\n        }\\n        if input.down && n > 0 {\\n            self.focus = (self.focus + 1).min(n - 1);\\n        }\\n        if input.tab_l {\",\"content_concise\":\"300→                        v.push(self.row(1, \\\"Fullscreen\\\"));\\n                    }\\n                }\\n            }\\n            Screen::About => {\\n                v.push(about_page_title(self.about_page).into());\\n                v.extend(about_lines(self.about_page));\\n            }\\n            Screen::Controls => {\\n                v.push(format!(\\\"Aim   right stick or mouse   {}\\\", self.prompt(\\\"use\\\")));\\n310→                v.push(\\\"Tools   left stick or 1-8\\\".into());\\n                v.push(format!(\\\"Operate   {}\\\", self.prompt(\\\"use\\\")));\\n                v.push(format!(\\\"Gift   {}\\\", self.prompt(\\\"gift\\\")));\\n                v.push(format!(\\\"Chart   {}\\\", self.prompt(\\\"chart\\\")));\\n            }\\n            Screen::Pause => {\\n                for (i, item) in [\\\"Resume\\\", \\\"Restart\\\", \\\"Controls\\\", \\\"Settings\\\", \\\"Dev Mode\\\", \\\"Quit to Title\\\"].iter().enumerate() {\\n                    v.push(self.row(i, item));\\n                }\\n            }\\n320→            Screen::Dev => {\\n                v.push(self.row(0, if self.live { \\\"Live  on\\\" } else { \\\"Live  off\\\" }));\\n                v.push(self.row(1, if self.bot_plays { \\\"Bot plays  on\\\" } else { \\\"Bot plays  off\\\" }));\\n                let start = self.dev_page as usize * 6;\\n                for i in 0..6 {\\n                    let id = start + i;\\n                    if id >= Tune::FIELDS.len() {\\n                        break;\\n                    }\\n                    let (name, def, _, _) = Tune::FIELDS[id];\\n330→                    v.push(self.row(i + 2, &format!(\\\"{name}  {:.2}  default {def:.2}\\\", self.sliders[id])));\\n                }\\n                v.push(self.row(8, \\\"Reset All\\\"));\\n            }\\n            Screen::Attract => {\\n                v.push(\\\"DEMO\\\".into());\\n                v.push(format!(\\\"Press {}\\\", self.prompt(\\\"confirm\\\")));\\n            }\\n            Screen::Hud => {\\n                v.push(\\\"OPERATION\\\".into());\\n340→            }\\n            Screen::Story => v.push(\\\"Advance\\\".into()),\\n            Screen::Results => v.push(\\\"Results\\\".into()),\\n            Screen::Dead => v.push(self.row(0, \\\"Retry\\\")),\\n            Screen::Card => {\\n                v.push(\\\"Pre-op\\\".into());\\n                v.push(\\\"Keep the patient alive\\\".into());\\n                v.push(format!(\\\"{} ready\\\", self.prompt(\\\"confirm\\\")));\\n            }\\n            Screen::Chart => {\\n350→                v.push(\\\"Chart\\\".into());\\n                v.push(\\\"Begin the operation\\\".into());\\n                v.push(format!(\\\"{} begin\\\", self.prompt(\\\"confirm\\\")));\\n            }\\n        }\\n        v\\n    }\\n\\n    fn row(&self, i: usize, label: &str) -> String {\\n        if i == self.focus {\\n360→            format!(\\\"> {label}\\\")\\n        } else {\\n            label.to_string()\\n        }\\n    }\\n\\n    pub fn step(&mut self, input: Input) -> Vec<Cmd> {\\n        if let Some(d) = input.device {\\n            self.device = d;\\n            if d == DeviceKind::KeyboardMouse || d == DeviceKind::Gamepad {\\n370→                self.ever_fine = true;\\n            }\\n        }\\n        let mut cmds = Vec::new();\\n        if self.screen == Screen::Attract {\\n            if input.any {\\n                self.screen = Screen::Title;\\n                self.paused = false;\\n                self.idle = 0.0;\\n                self.focus = 0;\\n380→                cmds.push(Cmd::ToTitle);\\n            }\\n            return cmds;\\n        }\\n        let menuish = matches!(\\n            self.screen,\\n            Screen::Title | Screen::Menu | Screen::Difficulty | Screen::Files | Screen::Settings | Screen::About | Screen::Controls\\n        );\\n        if menuish && !input.any {\\n            self.idle += input.dt;\\n390→            if self.idle >= 10.0 {\\n                self.screen = Screen::Attract;\\n                self.idle = 0.0;\\n                cmds.push(Cmd::LoadAttract);\\n                return cmds;\\n            }\\n        } else if input.any {\\n            self.idle = 0.0;\\n        }\\n        if self.touch_only && !self.ever_fine && self.screen == Screen::Title {\\n400→            if input.confirm || input.click {\\n                self.screen = Screen::Settings;\\n                self.focus = 0;\\n            }\\n            return cmds;\\n        }\\n        let n = self.count();\\n        if let Some(p) = input.pointer {\\n            if let Some(hit) = self.hit(p) {\\n                self.focus = hit;\\n410→                self.device = DeviceKind::KeyboardMouse