{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-919b06c5-c961-4685-a601-efd26a2bb831-64","content":"{\"type\":\"ReadFile\",\"FileContent\":{\"content\":\"68→pub struct Shell {\\n    screen: Screen,\\n70→    focus: usize,\\n    pub device: DeviceKind,\\n    pub xbox: bool,\\n    pub touch_only: bool,\\n    pub ever_fine: bool,\\n    idle: f32,\\n    settings_page: u8,\\n    about_page: u8,\\n    dev_page: u8,\\n    sliders: [f32; 19],\\n80→    pub music: f32,\\n    pub effects: f32,\\n    pub voices: f32,\\n    pub difficulty: u8,\\n    best: [u8; 8],\\n    sim_mode: u8,\\n    paused: bool,\\n    live: bool,\\n    bot_plays: bool,\\n}\\n90→\\nimpl Default for Shell {\\n    fn default() -> Self {\\n        Self::new()\\n    }\\n}\\n\\nimpl Shell {\\n    pub fn new() -> Self {\\n        let mut sliders = [0.0; 19];\\n100→        for (i, (_, v, _, _)) in Tune::FIELDS.iter().enumerate() {\\n            sliders[i] = *v;\\n        }\\n        Self {\\n            screen: Screen::Title,\\n            focus: 0,\\n            device: DeviceKind::KeyboardMouse,\\n            xbox: false,\\n            touch_only: false,\\n            ever_fine: false,\\n110→            idle: 0.0,\\n            settings_page: 0,\\n            about_page: 0,\\n            dev_page: 0,\\n            sliders,\\n            music: 0.10,\\n            effects: 0.80,\\n            voices: 0.70,\\n            difficulty: 1,\\n            best: [0; 8],\\n120→            sim_mode: 0,\\n            paused: false,\\n            live: true,\\n            bot_plays: false,\\n        }\\n    }\\n\\n    pub fn screen_name(&self) -> &'static str {\\n        match self.screen {\\n            Screen::Title => \\\"title\\\",\\n130→            Screen::Menu => \\\"menu\\\",\\n            Screen::Difficulty => \\\"difficulty\\\",\\n            Screen::Files => \\\"files\\\",\\n            Screen::Settings => \\\"settings\\\",\\n            Screen::About => \\\"about\\\",\\n            Screen::Controls => \\\"controls\\\",\\n            Screen::Pause => \\\"pause\\\",\\n            Screen::Dev => \\\"dev\\\",\\n            Screen::Attract => \\\"attract\\\",\\n            Screen::Hud => \\\"op\\\",\\n140→            Screen::Story => \\\"story\\\",\\n            Screen::Results => \\\"results\\\",\\n            Screen::Dead => \\\"dead\\\",\\n            Screen::Card => \\\"card\\\",\\n            Screen::Chart => \\\"chart\\\",\\n        }\\n    }\\n\",\"content_concise\":\"68→pub struct Shell {\\n    screen: Screen,\\n70→    focus: usize,\\n    pub device: DeviceKind,\\n    pub xbox: bool,\\n    pub touch_only: bool,\\n    pub ever_fine: bool,\\n    idle: f32,\\n    settings_page: u8,\\n    about_page: u8,\\n    dev_page: u8,\\n    sliders: [f32; 19],\\n80→    pub music: f32,\\n    pub effects: f32,\\n    pub voices: f32,\\n    pub difficulty: u8,\\n    best: [u8; 8],\\n    sim_mode: u8,\\n    paused: bool,\\n    live: bool,\\n    bot_plays: bool,\\n}\\n90→\\nimpl Default for Shell {\\n    fn default() -> Self {\\n        Self::new()\\n    }\\n}\\n\\nimpl Shell {\\n    pub fn new() -> Self {\\n        let mut sliders = [0.0; 19];\\n100→        for (i, (_, v, _, _)) in Tune::FIELDS.iter().enumerate() {\\n            sliders[i] = *v;\\n        }\\n        Self {\\n            screen: Screen::Title,\\n            focus: 0,\\n            device: DeviceKind::KeyboardMouse,\\n            xbox: false,\\n            touch_only: false,\\n            ever_fine: false,\\n110→            idle: 0.0,\\n            settings_page: 0,\\n            about_page: 0,\\n            dev_page: 0,\\n            sliders,\\n            music: 0.10,\\n            effects: 0.80,\\n            voices: 0.70,\\n            difficulty: 1,\\n            best: [0; 8],\\n120→            sim_mode: 0,\\n            paused: false,\\n            live: true,\\n            bot_plays: false,\\n        }\\n    }\\n\\n    pub fn screen_name(&self) -> &'static str {\\n        match self.screen {\\n            Screen::Title => \\\"title\\\",\\n130→            Screen::Menu => \\\"menu\\\",\\n            Screen::Difficulty => \\\"difficulty\\\",\\n            Screen::Files => \\\"files\\\",\\n            Screen::Settings => \\\"settings\\\",\\n            Screen::About => \\\"about\\\",\\n            Screen::Controls => \\\"controls\\\",\\n            Screen::Pause => \\\"pause\\\",\\n            Screen::Dev => \\\"dev\\\",\\n            Screen::Attract => \\\"attract\\\",\\n            Screen::Hud => \\\"op\\\",\\n140→            Screen::Story => \\\"story\\\",\\n            Screen::Results => \\\"results\\\",\\n            Screen::Dead => \\\"dead\\\",\\n            Screen::Card => \\\"card\\\",\\n            Screen::Chart => \\\"chart\\\",\\n        }\\n    }\\n\",\"absolute_path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224015__x42677a/work/Hands of Harbor: Second Opinion-Trauma Center: Second Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-224015/engine/crates/pav_ui/src/surgery/mod.rs\",\"offset\":68,\"limit\":80,\"raw_output\":\"pub struct Shell {\\n    screen: Screen,\\n    focus: usize,\\n    pub device: DeviceKind,\\n    pub xbox: bool,\\n    pub touch_only: bool,\\n    pub ever_fine: bool,\\n    idle: f32,\\n    settings_page: u8,\\n    about_page: u8,\\n    dev_page: u8,\\n    sliders: [f32; 19],\\n    pub music: f32,\\n    pub effects: f32,\\n    pub voices: f32,\\n    pub difficulty: u8,\\n    best: [u8; 8],\\n    sim_mode: u8,\\n    paused: bool,\\n    live: bool,\\n    bot_plays: bool,\\n}\\n\\nimpl Default for Shell {\\n    fn default() -> Self {\\n        Self::new()\\n    }\\n}\\n\\nimpl Shell {\\n    pub fn new() -> Self {\\n        let mut sliders = [0.0; 19];\\n        for (i, (_, v, _, _)) in Tune::FIELDS.iter().enumerate() {\\n            sliders[i] = *v;\\n        }\\n        Self {\\n            screen: Screen::Title,\\n            focus: 0,\\n            device: DeviceKind::KeyboardMouse,\\n            xbox: false,\\n            touch_only: false,\\n            ever_fine: false,\\n            idle: 0.0,\\n            settings_page: 0,\\n            about_page: 0,\\n            dev_page: 0,\\n            sliders,\\n            music: 0.10,\\n            effects: 0.80,\\n            voices: 0.70,\\n            difficulty: 1,\\n            best: [0; 8],\\n            sim_mode: 0,\\n            paused: false,\\n            live: true,\\n            bot_plays: false,\\n        }\\n    }\\n\\n    pub fn screen_name(&self) -> &'static str {\\n        match self.screen {\\n            Screen::Title => \\\"title\\\",\\n            Screen::Menu => \\\"menu\\\",\\n            Screen::Difficulty => \\\"difficulty\\\",\\n            Screen::Files => \\\"files\\\",\\n            Screen::Settings => \\\"settings\\\",\\n            Screen::About => \\\"about\\\",\\n            Screen::Controls => \\\"controls\\\",\\n            Screen::Pause => \\\"pause\\\",\\n            Screen::Dev => \\\"dev\\\",\\n            Screen::Attract => \\\"attract\\\",\\n            Screen::Hud => \\\"op\\\",\\n            Screen::Story => \\\"story\\\",\\n            Screen::Results => \\\"results\\\",\\n            Screen::Dead => \\\"dead\\\",\\n            Screen::Card => \\\"card\\\",\\n            Screen::Chart => \\\"chart\\\",\\n        }\\n    }\\n\\n\",\"total_lines\":945}}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa38-de6f-7dc0-ae0d-e0f717ed75f2","uuid":"226a8914-9022-447b-92e8-65a85ac6c53f"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_412","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Adding a public `card_note` field to the `Shell` struct.\n\nFixing a compose borrow issue. Hub polling will live in a separate `hub_link.rs` module to keep `product.rs` clean. The JS shim must define `poll` even when inactive, and Rust will check both `active` and the existence of `poll` before calling it.\n\nWriting the `hub_active`, `hub_info_json`, and `hub_poll` Rust helpers to read hub state and poll results from JavaScript.\n\n`hub_poll` now calls the JavaScript `poll` function and deserializes its JSON string result into a vector of `serde_json::Value`.\n\nA generic `hub_call` helper will handle `ready`, `time`, `send`, and `publish`. `time()` returns an `f64` that Rust can read directly from `JsValue`.\n\nThe JavaScript shim wraps `AIHub.send` to accept a JSON string, parse it, and pass it with `{ reliable: false, to }`.\n\n`H.publish(json)` will call `AIHub.publish` directly. The JavaScript shim will track held keys in a `held` map and expose a `dom` function that reads arrow keys and WASD to compute x and y movement.\n\nThe `dom` function now returns a JSON object with x, y, use, and gift flags. It will be wired into the existing Enter-key listener rather than a separate one.\n\nRust will read `H.dom()` and apply its synthetic keyboard aim to the local slot in addition to winit input. If both sources fire, the cursor simply moves faster, which is acceptable for testing.\n\nA new JavaScript hook exposes `__game.place(x, z)` as `__game.aim`. Rust will read this value and use it for a snap-absolute aim on the local slot when present.\n\nThe `setPlace` hook will be placed on `__hub` so it is available before `__game`. The test will use this reliable hook to move the host cursor, but mouse and keyboard input will also be wired properly and used in the test to avoid relying solely on a synthetic path.\n\nPlaywright can dispatch synthetic keyboard events directly inside the iframe. If the capture listener intercepts them, `H.dom()` returns the key vector and Rust moves the local cursor. This makes the `setPlace` hook unnecessary for the test; it will remain only as a debug aid. The host applies the client's relative stick aim every tick while the key is held.\n\nThe two-page test will use zero latency to avoid packet loss. The four harness queries still include latency.\n\nVitals will be quantized to 0.1 and compared with an absolute difference of less than 1.5 to allow one snapshot of drain.\n\nA solo page test will open the game HTML without the AI hub and verify the title screen and status title.\n\nThe game HTML will include meta tags for hub session configuration, such as shared-world mode, a four-minute duration, and a required WebGPU flag. The goal and how-to descriptions are kept under sixty and eighty characters respectively. The session.js script will be injected immediately after the charset tag, and its contents must remain byte-for-byte identical.\n\nThe packer will inject an `about-data` script tag containing the JSON from `pav_ui/src/surgery/about.json`. An optional `--about` file path argument will supply this data.\n\nThe `--about` argument will be wired into `pack_single_html.py` and passed from the pack command. The `exit-interview.json` file will also be copied to the work root. The about text will be validated against TASK requirements, and its hub claims updated only after the hub passes. A new `run_all.py` script will run cargo tests from a symlinked target directory and print only failures and a summary.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-78a343c2-1dd3-4f48-a49c-091eecd2e0eb-65","name":"grep","input":{"pattern":"js-sys","glob":"**/Cargo.lock","head_limit":20}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-78a343c2-1dd3-4f48-a49c-091eecd2e0eb-66","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224015__x42677a/