{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-4a6f9ca2-0ddc-4677-b413-10b32a0a0031-71","content":"{\"type\":\"ReadFile\",\"FileContent\":{\"content\":\"730→        aim.y += dz * inv * extra;\\n    }\\n    aim\\n}\\n\\nfn steer(s: &mut Surgeon, inp: SurgeonInput, dt: f32, speed: f32) {\\n    let abs = inp.held & surg::AIM_ABSOLUTE != 0;\\n    let snap = inp.held & surg::SNAP != 0;\\n    if abs && snap {\\n        s.x = inp.aim.x;\\n740→        s.z = inp.aim.y;\\n        return;\\n    }\\n    if abs {\\n        let dx = inp.aim.x - s.x;\\n        let dz = inp.aim.y - s.z;\\n        let d = (dx * dx + dz * dz).sqrt();\\n        let step = speed.max(1.0) * dt;\\n        if d <= step || d < 1e-5 {\\n            s.x = inp.aim.x;\\n750→            s.z = inp.aim.y;\\n        } else {\\n            s.x += dx / d * step;\\n            s.z += dz / d * step;\\n        }\\n    } else if inp.aim.length_squared() > 0.0004 {\\n        s.x += inp.aim.x * speed * dt;\\n        s.z += inp.aim.y * speed * dt;\\n    }\\n}\\n760→\\nfn heat_hit(angle: f32, x: f32, z: f32) -> bool {\\n    let ang = z.atan2(x);\\n    let mut d = (ang - angle).abs();\\n    if d > std::f32::consts::PI {\\n        d = std::f32::consts::TAU - d;\\n    }\\n    let r = (x * x + z * z).sqrt();\\n    d < 0.22 && r > 0.4\\n}\",\"content_concise\":\"730→        aim.y += dz * inv * extra;\\n    }\\n    aim\\n}\\n\\nfn steer(s: &mut Surgeon, inp: SurgeonInput, dt: f32, speed: f32) {\\n    let abs = inp.held & surg::AIM_ABSOLUTE != 0;\\n    let snap = inp.held & surg::SNAP != 0;\\n    if abs && snap {\\n        s.x = inp.aim.x;\\n740→        s.z = inp.aim.y;\\n        return;\\n    }\\n    if abs {\\n        let dx = inp.aim.x - s.x;\\n        let dz = inp.aim.y - s.z;\\n        let d = (dx * dx + dz * dz).sqrt();\\n        let step = speed.max(1.0) * dt;\\n        if d <= step || d < 1e-5 {\\n            s.x = inp.aim.x;\\n750→            s.z = inp.aim.y;\\n        } else {\\n            s.x += dx / d * step;\\n            s.z += dz / d * step;\\n        }\\n    } else if inp.aim.length_squared() > 0.0004 {\\n        s.x += inp.aim.x * speed * dt;\\n        s.z += inp.aim.y * speed * dt;\\n    }\\n}\\n760→\\nfn heat_hit(angle: f32, x: f32, z: f32) -> bool {\\n    let ang = z.atan2(x);\\n    let mut d = (ang - angle).abs();\\n    if d > std::f32::consts::PI {\\n        d = std::f32::consts::TAU - d;\\n    }\\n    let r = (x * x + z * z).sqrt();\\n    d < 0.22 && r > 0.4\\n}\",\"absolute_path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224015__x42677a/work/Hands of Harbor: Second Opinion-Trauma Center: Second Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-224015/engine/crates/pav_core/src/games/surgery/ops.rs\",\"offset\":730,\"limit\":40,\"raw_output\":\"        aim.y += dz * inv * extra;\\n    }\\n    aim\\n}\\n\\nfn steer(s: &mut Surgeon, inp: SurgeonInput, dt: f32, speed: f32) {\\n    let abs = inp.held & surg::AIM_ABSOLUTE != 0;\\n    let snap = inp.held & surg::SNAP != 0;\\n    if abs && snap {\\n        s.x = inp.aim.x;\\n        s.z = inp.aim.y;\\n        return;\\n    }\\n    if abs {\\n        let dx = inp.aim.x - s.x;\\n        let dz = inp.aim.y - s.z;\\n        let d = (dx * dx + dz * dz).sqrt();\\n        let step = speed.max(1.0) * dt;\\n        if d <= step || d < 1e-5 {\\n            s.x = inp.aim.x;\\n            s.z = inp.aim.y;\\n        } else {\\n            s.x += dx / d * step;\\n            s.z += dz / d * step;\\n        }\\n    } else if inp.aim.length_squared() > 0.0004 {\\n        s.x += inp.aim.x * speed * dt;\\n        s.z += inp.aim.y * speed * dt;\\n    }\\n}\\n\\nfn heat_hit(angle: f32, x: f32, z: f32) -> bool {\\n    let ang = z.atan2(x);\\n    let mut d = (ang - angle).abs();\\n    if d > std::f32::consts::PI {\\n        d = std::f32::consts::TAU - d;\\n    }\\n    let r = (x * x + z * z).sqrt();\\n    d < 0.22 && r > 0.4\\n}\\n\",\"total_lines\":787}}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa38-de6f-7dc0-ae0d-e0f717ed75f2","uuid":"c7154c4f-b3f7-4cbe-a2ac-d456a80b33d8"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_416","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"mirror_predict can call steer and set tool.\n\nSteer is private in ops.rs, so mirror_predict can call it directly. The function iterates over active surgeons, updates their tool if needed, steers them, and clamps their positions. I should check whether the real tick also clamps coordinates to avoid inconsistency.\n\nI'll skip clamping to match steer exactly. apply_mirror will not clear the local surgeon's position; it sets all cursors from the host, and predict overwrites the local cursor only if input is active this tick. For remote surgeons, the host sends relative stick input from the keyboard or absolute world position from the mouse.\n\nRelative aim will be sent for DOM keys so the host can integrate it. The client sends the stick each packet while the key is held. The host applies this input every simulation tick rather than only when a packet arrives, or movement becomes too slow. A RemoteHand struct will store the last received input and an age counter that increments each frame. This allows the host to apply the latest stick continuously until a newer packet arrives or the age exceeds about 0.2 seconds.\n\nRemote aim will be sent as floating-point values rather than integers to avoid quantization artifacts. Snapshot cursors will also be stored as floats. For hazard snapshots, integer positions will be multiplied by ten to save space; if more than sixteen hazards are alive, only the first sixteen will be transmitted.\n\nThe server will skip plate drawing to reduce load. A `skip_plate` flag on `SurgeryFrame` lets the view skip the heavy builder path. Audio will be muted.\n\nServer plate optimization is deferred until memory pressure requires it. The pause hub will be skipped. Enter during the card screen triggers ConfirmSim and increments the card timer, so no pause occurs. In attract mode, the first hub frame switches to card mode before the idle timeout expires.\n\nThe hub must switch to card mode before the next pump tick. If the shell screen is set to Card first, note_mode from the previous frame's title mode would overwrite it back to Title. Exec must run immediately so the new frame mode is 7 and note_mode preserves Card.\n\nThe first surgery frame can detect the hub before info arrives because __hub.active is available synchronously from JavaScript. The ready() call should happen at the end of the first hub frame once a frame has been presented. A null info value means the connection is still pending.\n\nready() must wait for info to become non-null. The session.js ready() function returns early if welcome has not finished, so it cannot be called before info arrives. The first frame after info is set will trigger ready(), which occurs after at least one frame if the WASM module starts after the connection.\n\nThe start event will trigger the countdown. Booting is deferred until time() reaches zero. The host boots the hub and the client boots the mirror. The server runs the full simulation but omits a local surgeon slot. The client uses its own player ID as the input slot.\n\nA player leaving removes their remote hand and deactivates their surgeon on the host. The end event sets harbor.ended to true, stops sending packets, and mutes audio without calling finish again. The shim finishes immediately when the time-up message arrives, before Rust polls it; Rust must publish snapshots every second during play and once at the start, falling back to current players if H.last is null.\n\nThe snapshot JSON will contain standings, a won flag, scores, stats, and awards. Standings will be built from present player IDs, removing IDs on leave events and excluding the server ID.\n\nIf the host leaves, the round is voided and other clients do not call finish because they are no longer the host. When three or more players remain, the last player is removed rather than the host, so the round continues.\n\nThe local snapshot publisher will run every frame during play. It stores the latest standings in H.last, so the fallback logic always sees current player data even after a leave event.\n\nThe snapshot payload will include won, standings, and scores. Awards are optional and only sent if an immaculate occurred. Stats names must be sixteen characters or fewer, and award titles twenty-four. The bridge allows sending before the game starts because the session guard checks for welcome rather than start status.\n\nTraffic will be rate-limited to 20 packets per second. The host broadcasts snapshots while clients broadcast input, so each side sends only one message type. A single-player round is still finished with a single-entry standings list.\n\nReliable delivery is disabled. Input packets will include a sequence number and a pressed flag, and the host will apply input only when the sequence changes. Synthetic DOM key presses will drive the local surgeon aim while the hub is active, falling back to winit if DOM reports zero magnitude.\n\nThe shim will expose a `dom()` helper returning raw stick axes and a use flag, letting Rust shape the input. Mouse events will be skipped in the shim to avoid conflicting with winit. The `__game` status object will carry vitals and cursor positions for the test harness.\n\nThe server will still publish status for debugging, and its vitals are authoritative. The test harness will read host cursors from the iframe to verify client movement. I need to locate the harness cells so the test can open the correct URL. I will add a `card_note` field to the shell Card lines. I also need to fix a borrow issue in compose and integrate the hub into product.rs.\n\nHub logic will live in a new `hub.rs` file. It will be declared as `mod hub` inside `product.rs`. The `Link` struct will expose `new()` and `poll()`. On native builds `poll()` will return an inactive tick.\n\nHarbor will hold the Link. HubTick will carry active, server, host, slot, play, ended, boot, seed, present player IDs, card names, four remote surgeon inputs, and optional DOM aim with a use flag. It will also expose send_input, send_snap, and publish methods.\n\nThe hub module will use js_sys only on WASM. The `compose` function will take a `hub` flag to ignore pause input when the hub is active. The digit key ate logic in `tools_from_hands` runs before the shell step's other key ate checks.\n\nThe hub will render the operation screen as a HUD, so shell navigation is blocked and Enter during play may not be consumed. When DOM use is active, the local hand will be set to USE. The server will skip audio and heavy view drawing by checking a `harbor.server` flag. Next I will inject the packer, add `hub_shim.js`, update `shell/ops/mod`, run `cargo check`, and build WASM.\n\nrun_all.py can be written now and will run native tests after cargo check. The mirror mode early return change is safe, and adding apply_mirror is also safe. A small unit test for apply_mirror in surgery.rs would be fast and useful, though the hub harness is the real test. An optional shell test assertion could verify note_mode 8 becomes Hud.\n\nA regression test will be added to the shell suite: after the story screen, calling `note_mode(8)` should assert the screen is `op`. The `card_note` field will default to empty, so Card lines remain unchanged unless the note is set. I am now reviewing the `lines()` function to patch the Card arm.\n\nI will leave about.json unchanged because its engine flag is already true. Deviations for cargo target paths and the Rust story will be appended to PROGRESS.md when finished. I am ready to write code, starting with the compose fix in product.rs, then integrating the hub into surgery_frame.\n\nI will call `hub.send_snap(&op)` after the pump in SurgeryFrame. The local SurgeonInput will be stored on Harbor for sending. Remote inputs will be merged before writing InputFrame. I am reviewing the compose return and input write to plan the edit precisely.\n\nDOM stick axes will use the same coordinate space as winit, with W mapped to positive Y. Rust negates the Y value before shaping it into a stick vector. DOM input overwrites winit aim whenever the DOM magnitude is non-zero. On the server, the local surgeon slot is cleared and only remote inputs are written into the surgeons array.\n\nThe host local slot must not be overwritten by remote input. In compose, inactive remotes leave surgeons unchanged, but hand() always marks slot 0 as active. During hub play, slot 0 may belong to another player, so compose needs to know the local slot and should change hand()'s active logic.\n\n`hand()` will take an optional `local_slot` parameter. When set, only that slot is active; otherwise slot 0 or a present pad remains active. This prevents the host from accidentally activating another player's slot during hub play.\n\nSolo mode stays unchanged because `local_slot` is `None`. The `hub.rs` shim will import `wasm_bindgen::JsValue`, and all JavaScript failures return inactive ticks without panicking. Panics become page errors that fail the test harness. The hub poll JSON array contains events like `card`, `start`, `message`, `time-up`, `leave`, and `end`.\n\nThe hub shim will push message events as `[type, data, from]`, card and start as `[type, data]`, leave and end as `[type, data]`, and time-up as `[type]`. Player info objects contain id, name, and color. The card event ready array will be formatted into a note showing each player’s name and whether they are ready.\n\nThe shell will expose `card_lines: Vec<String>` instead of a single newline-delimited string, since egui labels render one line at a time. The hub difficulty stays at 0 because `fresh()` sets it that way, which matches the boot code. The 240-second game timer is safe to run during tests; the harness triggers time-up after only a few seconds, so the game timer cannot finish first.\n\nThe freeze timer starts at play, not boot. Client mirror mode returns early and does not run the code blue timer; it only sets the timer from the snapshot. Only the host uses the seed for boot, so clients do not need identical randomness. Spawn positions are fixed for opening bleeders, though wave generation may still use RNG on the host. I will also fix an unused import and use js_sys::JSON::stringify for web-sys JSON.\n\nA `call` helper will invoke JavaScript functions on the hub via `js_sys::Reflect` and `Function::apply`. The shim will expose `time()` and `ready()` to Rust. It will only define these methods when active, so `poll()` can safely check `active` first.\n\nThe hub shim will keep DOM input tracking inside the active branch. The harness only pokes Enter, so no extra key mappings are needed. I will skip optional Triangle or T-to-more bindings to avoid accidental extra requests during play.\n\nThe about.json script tag will be injected into the HTML after the charset meta tag, placed before session.js so it loads first. The page must contain this script element.\n\nThe HTML injection order is now fixed: charset, then session.js, then meta tags, then the shim, and finally the about-data script. Meta tags will be inserted between the session script and the shim using a regex that appends them after the first `<meta charset=\"utf-8\">` tag. The packer already guards against injecting scripts that contain `</script`, so session.js should not break the insertion.\n\nThe packed game HTML will be served next to harness.html, bridge.js, and round.js on a local port. build-web.sh needs no changes because the packer always injects the required scripts.\n\nThe harness game URL will use the packed HTML filename with query parameters like `players=4` and `auto=1`. A `limit` of 20 seconds caps the round at 20,000 milliseconds. The default play query is 6,000 ms. I will write a Python Playwright script to test the four hub queries and the two-page solo title. Launch tests will run against the packed HTML served via file://.\n\nThe work order is: code changes, native cargo check and surgery tests, wasm build and pack, then test scripts while packing, followed by harness, launch, balance, and suite runs. Balance will be checked with one seed per skill level to produce the suggested par.\n\nThe balance survey will be a small Rust function in `surgery.rs` that runs the four skill levels across ten seeds each. It should be fast enough to include in the default test suite, or run explicitly with `--nocapture` to capture the full output.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-a08e0dc0-c63c-4918-af7f-75d81f1c67b3-72","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224015__x42677a/work/engine-link/crates/pav_core/tests/surgery.rs","limit":80}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":537,"output_tokens":6567,"cache_read_input_tokens":145536,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa38-de6f-7dc0-ae0d-e0f717ed75f2","uuid":"fbb481cc-963e-4f89-bd6e-1f33f1d436ad"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-a08e0dc0-c63c-4918-af7f-75d81f1c67b3-72","content":"{\"type\":\"ReadFile\",\"FileContent\":{\"content\":\"1→//! Hands of Harbor: the shipped sim, from a fresh scene.\\n\\nuse pav_core::games::surgery::{\\n    all_lines, rank_of, chain_mul, Heart, Surgery, CASES, K_POLYP, K_POOL, LASER, R_SLOPPY, SUCTION, SURGEON_NAMES, TITLE,\\n    TOOL_NAMES,\\n};\\nuse pav_core::games::Outcome;\\nuse pav_core::glam::Vec2;\\nuse pav_core::input::{surg, InputFrame, SurgeonInput, SurgeryCmd};\\n10→use pav_core::Sim;\\n\\nfn status(sim: &Sim) -> String {\\n    sim.play().unwrap().status(sim).to_string()\\n}\\n\\nfn game(sim: &Sim) -> &Surgery {\\n    sim.play().unwrap().get::<Surgery>().unwrap()\\n}\\n\\n20→fn cmd(c: SurgeryCmd) -> InputFrame {\\n    InputFrame { surgery_cmd: Some(c), ..InputFrame::default() }\\n}\\n\\nfn hand(x: f32, z: f32, tool: u8, use_on: bool) -> InputFrame {\\n    let mut held = surg::AIM_ABSOLUTE | surg::SNAP;\\n    if use_on {\\n        held |= surg::USE;\\n    }\\n    let mut frame = InputFrame::default();\\n30→    frame.surgeons[0] = SurgeonInput {\\n        active: true,\\n        aim: Vec2::new(x, z),\\n        held,\\n        pressed: 0,\\n        tool,\\n        pressure: 1.0,\\n    };\\n    frame\\n}\\n40→\\nfn play_until(sim: &mut Sim, cap: u64, drive: impl Fn(u64, &Sim) -> InputFrame) -> u64 {\\n    for t in 0..cap {\\n        if sim.outcome() != Outcome::Playing {\\n            return t;\\n        }\\n        let frame = drive(t, sim);\\n        sim.step(&frame);\\n    }\\n    cap\\n50→}\\n\\n#[test]\\nfn skill1_bot_wins_every_case_code_and_campaign_on_ten_seeds() {\\n    for seed in 1..11 {\\n        for case in 0..8 {\\n            let scene = format!(\\\"surgery/case/{case}\\\");\\n            let mut sim = Sim::new(&scene, seed).unwrap();\\n            let (outcome, ticks) = sim.run_bot(60 * 420);\\n            assert_eq!(outcome, Outcome::Won, \\\"seed {seed} {scene} t={ticks} {}\\\", status(&sim));\\n60→            let g = game(&sim);\\n            assert!(g.rank >= 4, \\\"seed {seed} case {case} rank {} {}\\\", g.rank, status(&sim));\\n            assert_eq!(g.rank, rank_of(g.total_score(), g.par));\\n        }\\n        {\\n            let mut sim = Sim::new(\\\"surgery/code\\\", seed).unwrap();\\n            let (outcome, ticks) = sim.run_bot(60 * 260);\\n            assert_eq!(outcome, Outcome::Won, \\\"seed {seed} code t={ticks} {}\\\", status(&sim));\\n            assert!(game(&sim).rank >= 4, \\\"seed {seed} code {}\\\", status(&sim));\\n        }\\n70→        {\\n            let mut sim = Sim::new(\\\"surgery/campaign\\\", seed).unwrap();\\n            let (outcome, ticks) = sim.run_bot(60 * 2200);\\n            assert_eq!(outcome, Outcome::Won, \\\"seed {seed} campaign t={ticks} {}\\\", status(&sim));\\n            let g = game(&sim);\\n            assert!(g.coverage.tools.iter().all(|n| *n > 0), \\\"tools {:?}\\\", g.coverage.tools);\\n            assert!(g.coverage.hazards.iter().all(|n| *n > 0), \\\"hazards {:?}\\\", g.coverage.hazards);\\n            assert!(g.coverage.strains.iter().all(|n| *n > 0), \\\"strains {:?}\\\", g.coverage.strains);\\n            assert!(g.coverage.gifts.iter().all(|n| *n > 0), \\\"gifts {:?}\\\", g.coverage.gifts);\\n            assert!(g.coverage.code > 0, \\\"code {}\\\", g.coverage.code);\\n80→            assert!(g.best_chain() >= 5, \\\"chain {}\\\", g.best_chain());\",\"content_concise\":\"1→//! Hands of Harbor: the shipped sim, from a fresh scene.\\n\\nuse pav_core::games::surgery::{\\n    all_lines, rank_of, chain_mul, Heart, Surgery, CASES, K_POLYP, K_POOL, LASER, R_SLOPPY, SUCTION, SURGEON_NAMES, TITLE,\\n    TOOL_NAMES,\\n};\\nuse pav_core::games::Outcome;\\nuse pav_core::glam::Vec2;\\nuse pav_core::input::{surg, InputFrame, SurgeonInput, SurgeryCmd};\\n10→use pav_core::Sim;\\n\\nfn status(sim: &Sim) -> String {\\n    sim.play().unwrap().status(sim).to_string()\\n}\\n\\nfn game(sim: &Sim) -> &Surgery {\\n    sim.play().unwrap().get::<Surgery>().unwrap()\\n}\\n\\n20→fn cmd(c: SurgeryCmd) -> InputFrame {\\n    InputFrame { surgery_cmd: Some(c), ..InputFrame::default() }\\n}\\n\\nfn hand(x: f32, z: f32, tool: u8, use_on: bool) -> InputFrame {\\n    let mut held = surg::AIM_ABSOLUTE | surg::SNAP;\\n    if use_on {\\n        held |= surg::USE;\\n    }\\n    let mut frame = InputFrame::default();\\n30→    frame.surgeons[0] = SurgeonInput {\\n        active: true,\\n        aim: Vec2::new(x, z),\\n        held,\\n        pressed: 0,\\n        tool,\\n        pressure: 1.0,\\n    };\\n    frame\\n}\\n40→\\nfn play_until(sim: &mut Sim, cap: u64, drive: impl Fn(u64, &Sim) -> InputFrame) -> u64 {\\n    for t in 0..cap {\\n        if sim.outcome() != Outcome::Playing {\\n            return t;\\n        }\\n        let frame = drive(t, sim);\\n        sim.step(&frame);\\n    }\\n    cap\\n50→}\\n\\n#[test]\\nfn skill1_bot_wins_every_case_code_and_campaign_on_ten_seeds() {\\n    for seed in 1..11 {\\n        for case in 0..8 {\\n            let scene = format!(\\\"surgery/case/{case}\\\");\\n            let mut sim = Sim::new(&scene, seed).unwrap();\\n            let (outcome, ticks) = sim.run_bot(60 * 420);\\n            assert_eq!(outcome, Outcome::Won, \\\"seed {seed} {scene} t={ticks} {}\\\", status(&sim));\\n60→            let g = game(&sim);\\n            assert!(g.rank >= 4, \\\"seed {seed} case {case} rank {} {}\\\", g.rank, status(&sim));\\n            assert_eq!(g.rank, rank_of(g.total_score(), g.par));\\n        }\\n        {\\n            let mut sim = Sim::new(\\\"surgery/code\\\", seed).unwrap();\\n            let (outcome, ticks) = sim.run_bot(60 * 260);\\n            assert_eq!(outcome, Outcome::Won, \\\"seed {seed} code t={ticks} {}\\\", status(&sim));\\n            assert!(game(&sim).rank >= 4, \\\"seed {seed} code {}\\\", status(&sim));\\n        }\\n70→        {\\n            let mut sim = Sim::new(\\\"surgery/campaign\\\", seed).unwrap();\\n            let (outcome, ticks) = sim.run_bot(60 * 2200);\\n            assert_eq!(outcome, Outcome::Won, \\\"seed {seed} campaign t={ticks} {}\\\", status(&sim));\\n            let g = game(&sim);\\n            assert!(g.coverage.tools.iter().all(|n| *n > 0), \\\"tools {:?}\\\", g.coverage.tools);\\n            assert!(g.coverage.hazards.iter().all(|n| *n > 0), \\\"hazards {:?}\\\", g.coverage.hazards);\\n            assert!(g.coverage.strains.iter().all(|n| *n > 0), \\\"strains {:?}\\\", g.coverage.strains);\\n            assert!(g.coverage.gifts.iter().all(|n| *n > 0), \\\"gifts {:?}\\\", g.coverage.gifts);\\n            assert!(g.coverage.code > 0, \\\"code {}\\\", g.coverage.code);\\n80→            assert!(g.best_chain() >= 5, \\\"chain {}\\\", g.best_chain());\",\"absolute_path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224015__x42677a/work/Hands of Harbor: Second Opinion-Trauma Center: Second Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-224015/engine/crates/pav_core/tests/surgery.rs\",\"offset\":null,\"limit\":80,\"raw_output\":\"//! Hands of Harbor: the shipped sim, from a fresh scene.\\n\\nuse pav_core::games::surgery::{\\n    all_lines, rank_of, chain_mul, Heart, Surgery, CASES, K_POLYP, K_POOL, LASER, R_SLOPPY, SUCTION, SURGEON_NAMES, TITLE,\\n    TOOL_NAMES,\\n};\\nuse pav_core::games::Outcome;\\nuse pav_core::glam::Vec2;\\nuse pav_core::input::{surg, InputFrame, SurgeonInput, SurgeryCmd};\\nuse pav_core::Sim;\\n\\nfn status(sim: &Sim) -> String {\\n    sim.play().unwrap().status(sim).to_string()\\n}\\n\\nfn game(sim: &Sim) -> &Surgery {\\n    sim.play().unwrap().get::<Surgery>().unwrap()\\n}\\n\\nfn cmd(c: SurgeryCmd) -> InputFrame {\\n    InputFrame { surgery_cmd: Some(c), ..InputFrame::default() }\\n}\\n\\nfn hand(x: f32, z: f32, tool: u8, use_on: bool) -> InputFrame {\\n    let mut held = surg::AIM_ABSOLUTE | surg::SNAP;\\n    if use_on {\\n        held |= surg::USE;\\n    }\\n    let mut frame = InputFrame::default();\\n    frame.surgeons[0] = SurgeonInput {\\n        active: true,\\n        aim: Vec2::new(x, z),\\n        held,\\n        pressed: 0,\\n        tool,\\n        pressure: 1.0,\\n    };\\n    frame\\n}\\n\\nfn play_until(sim: &mut Sim, cap: u64, drive: impl Fn(u64, &Sim) -> InputFrame) -> u64 {\\n    for t in 0..cap {\\n        if sim.outcome() != Outcome::Playing {\\n            return t;\\n        }\\n        let frame = drive(t, sim);\\n        sim.step(&frame);\\n    }\\n    cap\\n}\\n\\n#[test]\\nfn skill1_bot_wins_every_case_code_and_campaign_on_ten_seeds() {\\n    for seed in 1..11 {\\n        for case in 0..8 {\\n            let scene = format!(\\\"surgery/case/{case}\\\");\\n            let mut sim = Sim::new(&scene, seed).unwrap();\\n            let (outcome, ticks) = sim.run_bot(60 * 420);\\n            assert_eq!(outcome, Outcome::Won, \\\"seed {seed} {scene} t={ticks} {}\\\", status(&sim));\\n            let g = game(&sim);\\n            assert!(g.rank >= 4, \\\"seed {seed} case {case} rank {} {}\\\", g.rank, status(&sim));\\n            assert_eq!(g.rank, rank_of(g.total_score(), g.par));\\n        }\\n        {\\n            let mut sim = Sim::new(\\\"surgery/code\\\", seed).unwrap();\\n            let (outcome, ticks) = sim.run_bot(60 * 260);\\n            assert_eq!(outcome, Outcome::Won, \\\"seed {seed} code t={ticks} {}\\\", status(&sim));\\n            assert!(game(&sim).rank >= 4, \\\"seed {seed} code {}\\\", status(&sim));\\n        }\\n        {\\n            let mut sim = Sim::new(\\\"surgery/campaign\\\", seed).unwrap();\\n            let (outcome, ticks) = sim.run_bot(60 * 2200);\\n            assert_eq!(outcome, Outcome::Won, \\\"seed {seed} campaign t={ticks} {}\\\", status(&sim));\\n            let g = game(&sim);\\n            assert!(g.coverage.tools.iter().all(|n| *n > 0), \\\"tools {:?}\\\", g.coverage.tools);\\n            assert!(g.coverage.hazards.iter().all(|n| *n > 0), \\\"hazards {:?}\\\", g.coverage.hazards);\\n            assert!(g.coverage.strains.iter().all(|n| *n > 0), \\\"strains {:?}\\\", g.coverage.strains);\\n            assert!(g.coverage.gifts.iter().all(|n| *n > 0), \\\"gifts {:?}\\\", g.coverage.gifts);\\n            assert!(g.coverage.code > 0, \\\"code {}\\\", g.coverage.code);\\n            assert!(g.best_chain() >= 5, \\\"chain {}\\\", g.best_chain());\\n\",\"total_lines\":265}}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa38-de6f-7dc0-ae0d-e0f717ed75f2","uuid":"8792d981-4184-4c1a-9c5d-94d2100b7257"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_417","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Skill is on the game. run_bot uses it.\n\nSkill will be set to 0.7 in the balance test via `play_mut().get_mut()`. The code will be thorough but not bloated. Shell note_mode for mode 8 and ops mirror are also planned.\n\n`boot_hub_round` seeds the RNG and activates surgeons from the given slots. `boot_mirror` sets the mode to mirror.\n\n`boot_mirror` resets the case ID, sets code blue and a 240-second timer, initializes the heart at 70.0, and clears hazards. `apply_mirror` will take slices of tuples for vitals, BPM, phase, flat status, timer, code time, hazards, and cursors to avoid a large struct.\n\n`apply_mirror` updates the heart BPM, phase, and flat status. It clears hazards and rebuilds them from the tuple slice with correct IDs, stages, and work values. Surgeon cursors are mapped to slots 0–3.\n\n`apply_mirror` finishes by setting each surgeon's z position, tool, active state, and score. `Hazard::make` is confirmed in scope via the module re-export. The input message slot must be below 4, since the server ID can exceed 2 when only two players are present.\n\nThe server never sends input, so its internal ID cannot be mistaken for a surgeon slot. The host applies client slots 0 and 1 to surgeons[0] and [1]. Status JSON already includes vitals and cursors; adding flat is unnecessary.\n\nVitals will be quantized to 0.1 in snapshots so they match within 0.1. The host will send vitals every snapshot even when unchanged so the client converges quickly at 15Hz.\n\nA `last_hands` array of four `SurgeonInput` values will be stored on Harbor.\n\nHub.rs will own the protocol and return commands without depending on Sim. Product will handle simulation execution. Hub.rs will read the DOM each poll. The expected file sizes are roughly 400 lines for hub.rs, about 150 for product, and smaller changes elsewhere.\n\nShell will gain a `card_lines` field to display the hub names line. The paused flag will be false when the hub is active, and the compose back button will be hidden. Card mode prevents attract mode from starting because it is not menuish; idle accumulation on the title screen is harmless for one frame. Touch-only input is excluded from the hub test.\n\nThe host will force the simulation into card mode before note_mode runs, but only once. It checks if the hub is active and the card has not yet been booted. If the current mode is title or attract, it switches to card and clears the case ID. This happens before the first frame so the screen does not flash title or attract. The hub boot sequence will later set the operation mode.\n\nWhen the hub ends, the simulation will pause without showing a pause menu. The host sets the paused flag to true or the hub ended flag inside surgery_frame. This stops the clock and skips audio playback.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-e3102cd3-8fe7-4f55-8ed9-6a461002f1ea-73","name":"grep","input":{"pattern":"pub fn build|fn surgery|apply_look|plate","glob":"**/pav_view/src/**/*.rs","head_limit":30}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":7563,"output_tokens":1857,"cache_read_input_tokens":146048,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa38-de6f-7dc0-ae0d-e0f717ed75f2","uuid":"d18a3936-f814-43ba-8e4c-4217ffd8d1ee"}
