{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_424","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"I can write a test that uses sim.state.\n\nA focused test can wait; the harness is the main proof. I will batch edits now. SurgeryFrame and Surgery structs get a `quiet` flag. The emit method skips quiet operations. Shell and product changes are next. Then I will write hub.rs, hub_shim.js, and edit the packer. Finally I will run cargo check.\n\nI will rewrite the shell.step section in product compose and insert hub calls into surgery_frame. The Harbor struct needs a `link` field and a `local_slot` field, and its `compose` method will accept an optional local slot.\n\nThe `hand` method now accepts an optional local slot. When a local slot is set, only that slot becomes active; all other slots return inactive input. The back button logic also respects the new `block_back` flag.\n\n`tools_from_hands` will now apply digit and wheel input to the local slot instead of always slot 0. The pad loop still updates tools per pad index. In a hub iframe, the first gamepad controls the local slot rather than pad index 0.\n\nSolo mode keeps its existing pad-to-slot mapping. In hub mode, the local surgeon's pad is read from pads[0] rather than pads[slot]. tools_from_hands will use pads[0] to update tool[me].","signature":""},{"type":"text","text":"The product crate fails on a borrow in the shell step. I’ll fix that and wire the hub so a session can skip the title, share one Code Blue, and finish cleanly."},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-748ad84d-0fbb-4c58-908f-384829d9f163-81","name":"search_replace","input":{"file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224015__x42677a/work/engine-link/crates/pav_core/src/games/surgery/ops.rs","old_string":"        M_CARD => {\n            g.card_t += dt;\n            return;\n        }\n        M_TITLE | M_MIRROR | M_DEAD => return,","new_string":"        M_CARD => {\n            g.card_t += dt;\n            return;\n        }\n        M_MIRROR => {\n            mirror_predict(g, input, dt);\n            return;\n        }\n        M_TITLE | M_DEAD => return,"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-748ad84d-0fbb-4c58-908f-384829d9f163-82","name":"search_replace","input":{"file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224015__x42677a/work/engine-link/crates/pav_core/src/games/surgery/ops.rs","old_string":"fn steer(s: &mut Surgeon, inp: SurgeonInput, dt: f32, speed: f32) {","new_string":"fn mirror_predict(g: &mut Surgery, input: &InputFrame, dt: f32) {\n    for (i, inp) in input.surgeons.iter().enumerate() {\n        if !inp.active {\n            continue;\n        }\n        let s = &mut g.surgeons[i];\n        s.active = true;\n        if inp.tool != TOOL_KEEP {\n            s.tool = inp.tool;\n        }\n        steer(s, *inp, dt, g.tune.cursor_speed);\n    }\n}\n\nfn steer(s: &mut Surgeon, inp: SurgeonInput, dt: f32, speed: f32) {"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-748ad84d-0fbb-4c58-908f-384829d9f163-83","name":"search_replace","input":{"file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224015__x42677a/work/engine-link/crates/pav_view/src/surgery/mod.rs","old_string":"pub fn emit(scene: &mut Scene, op: &SurgeryFrame) {\n    scene.dynamic.push(plate(op));","new_string":"pub fn emit(scene: &mut Scene, op: &SurgeryFrame) {\n    if op.quiet {\n        return;\n    }\n    scene.dynamic.push(plate(op));"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-748ad84d-0fbb-4c58-908f-384829d9f163-84","name":"search_replace","input":{"file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224015__x42677a/work/engine-link/crates/pav_ui/src/surgery/mod.rs","old_string":"    live: bool,\n    bot_plays: bool,\n}","new_string":"    live: bool,\n    bot_plays: bool,\n    pub card_lines: Vec<String>,\n}"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-748ad84d-0fbb-4c58-908f-384829d9f163-85","name":"search_replace","input":{"file_path