{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_440","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Effects and voices are disabled when the server is inactive or ended.\n\nSchedule is skipped when audio is quiet. Mode 8 now maps to Hud for mirror mode. Cursor hides for modes 3 and 8. snap_json and standings_json are added before status_json. SimEvent is imported via pav_core::... for cue matching.\n\n`pav_core::SimEvent` is confirmed public. The `snap_json` function is being implemented to serialize alive hazards, limited to 14 entries.\n\nHazard coordinates and work values are rounded to two decimals. Active cursors are serialized with their tool, active state, and score. The last eight cue events are extracted from the event list.\n\nThe JSON body now includes vitals, BPM, phase, flat flag, timer, code time, hazards, cursors, and cues. If the serialized string exceeds 1200 bytes, cues and extra hazards are dropped to keep it within limit.\n\nThe `standings_json` function is being implemented. It defaults to player 0 when no present IDs are given, otherwise uses the provided slice. Each ID becomes its own group, and scores are fetched from the cursor array.\n\nThe `standings_json` function now returns a JSON object with the standings list, a win flag based on vitals and flat state, and a map of player scores. A single tie group is acceptable.\n\nBorrow checker issues were resolved: `surgeons` is still owned when passed to `send_input`, `boot` was cloned before moving into `exec`, and `Boot` and `Snap` satisfy `'static` bounds for the Wasm executor.\n\nNative link implements the required poll, send_input, send_snap, and publish methods. The js_sys Array push import now includes JsCast. glam::Vec2 is available through pav_app. Parentheses will be added to fix an operator precedence bug in the owns line. During hub card mode, shell.screen still applies aim after the active check even though hands are not built from mouse; this is harmless.\n\nThe first frame after play starts runs compose while the shell is still a card. Surgeons remain inactive during that pass. The card mode executor runs on the first frame only if no card was seen yet. Boot then sets the operator state. DOM is applied to surgeons next. Input is written and the simulation pumps so hands move. Finally note_mode switches to the HUD. Boot can trigger a mode change if DOM is present. There is uncertainty about whether saw_card execution might set the card mode before boot completes in the same frame.\n\nBoot always overrides card mode when both run on the same frame, so the first frame is safe. ready() is called before play starts and does not require a key. A potential bug was noted: ready() may be marked as done even if the call fails, and it is skipped entirely if the info has not joined.\n\nThe joined flag is false until the welcome message sets H.info, so ready() only fires once the info arrives. The dom shim is defined before the connect promise resolves, meaning Rust can poll for it immediately; if the call fails, read_dom returns None. When H.send omits the to argument, the shim passes undefined, and AIHub treats that as a broadcast.\n\nThe bridge checks `msg.to === undefined` to detect broadcasts. JSON.stringify omits undefined fields, but postMessage uses structured clone so the field remains present.\n\nPublish updates `H.last` every frame during play. This is acceptable because it is local-only and Link does not rate-limit publish calls.\n\nHost sends snapshots at 15Hz over the network and publishes local state continuously.\n\nThe server sends snapshots but not input, and clears its own surgeons. The client sends input but not snapshots, and applies received snapshots.\n\nWith only one player, the host still increments sent stats even when no targets exist, while received stays zero; the check is waived for a single player, yet finish is still required.\n\nWhen the host leaves, the game does not finish. The shim only triggers finish on time-up if the local peer is the host.\n\nThe host iframe is removed before its time-up listener fires. The leave() call sets the record flag, so timeUp never runs and the round is voided. Rust panics fail the harness, while JavaScript errors are caught as Option values.\n\nThe `js_sys::Array::push` return type is acceptable. The `web_sys::window` feature is already enabled in Cargo. `js_sys::JSON.stringify` is available for JSON serialization.\n\nThe next steps are to fix the audio quiet check and add the two remaining functions. Cursor hiding for mode 8 will also be added.\n\nThe `surgeons` reference in `send_input` is safe because the variable is not used after the hub block. `hub.boot.clone()` is valid since `Boot` implements `Clone`. The executor closure receives `&mut Sim`, which matches the `boot_hub_round` signature. `get_mut` is available on `GameBox`.\n\nThe `get_mut` path for the Surgery state is confirmed. Mode literals match the public surgery constants. During quiet frames the server skips emitting snapshots but still applies camera look and skips drawing the plate. The client mirror draws the plate from snapshot hazards. The `op` variable shadowing in snap is harmless.\n\nThe standings JSON fallback is safe because the present list updates when players leave, and time-up reads from the recently published state. Scores will use string IDs as keys. Effects will be muted during quiet frames so scheduled notes remain silent. The hand() operator precedence check is left unchanged. tools_from_hands allocates a new vector every frame, which is acceptable.\n\nThe cycle_one logic handles keyboard-only local input correctly by skipping L1 updates when pad 0 is absent. Solo pads are filtered properly by checking present flags. The next step is to add the remaining JSON functions and fix the note cursor for mode 8.\n\nSurgeryFrame hazard fields and SurgeonInput imports are confirmed. Snap and Boot field access inside closures is valid. The next steps are adding the remaining functions, injecting the packer, running cargo check, and adding a unit test for apply_mirror.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-137b43f4-b08d-4b44-81be-386d5e01b309-122","name":"search_replace","input":{"file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224015__x42677a/work/engine-link/crates/pav_app/src/product.rs","old_string":"        if op.mode == 3 {","new_string":"        if op.mode == 3 || op.mode == 8 {"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-137b43f4-b08d-4b44-81be-386d5e01b309-123","name":"search_replace","input":{"file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224015__x42677a/work/engine-link/crates/pav_app/src/product.rs","old_string":"    let music = if hub.server || hub.ended { 0.0 } else { op.as_ref().map(|o| o.music).unwrap_or(0.10) };\n    let effects = op.as_ref().map(|o| o.effects).unwrap_or(0.80);\n    let voices = op.as_ref().map(|o| o.voices).unwrap_or(0.70);","new_string":"    let quiet_audio = hub.server || hub.ended;\n    let music = if quiet_audio { 0.0 } else { op.as_ref().map(|o| o.music).unwrap_or(0.10) };\n    let effects = if quiet_audio { 0.0 } else { op.as_ref().map(|o| o.effects).unwrap_or(0.80) };\n    let voices = if quiet_audio { 0.0 } else { op.as_ref().map(|o| o.voices).unwrap_or(0.70) };"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-137b43f4-b08d-4b44-81be-386d5e01b309-124","name":"search_replace","input":{"file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224015__x42677a/work/engine-link/crates/pav_app/src/product.rs","old_string":"    let schedule = if app.harbor.music_left <= 0.0 {","new_string":"    let schedule = if quiet_audio {\n        None\n    } else if app.harbor.music_left <= 0.0 {"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-137b43f4-b08d-4b44-81be-386d5e01b309-125","name":"search_replace","input":{"file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224015__x42677a/work/engine-link/crates/pav_app/src/product.rs","old_string":"fn status_json(shell: &Shell, op: Option<&SurgeryFrame>) -> String {","new_string":"fn snap_json(op: &SurgeryFrame, events: &[pav_core::SimEvent]) -> String {\n    let mut hazards = Vec::new();\n    for h in op.hazards.iter().filter(|h| h.alive).take(12) {\n        hazards.push(serde_json::json!([\n            h.id,\n            h.kind,\n            (h.x * 100.0).round() / 100.0,\n            (h.z * 100.0).round() / 100.0,\n            1,\n            h.stage,\n            (h.work * 100.0).round() / 100.0\n        ]));\n    }\n    let mut cursors = Vec::new();\n    for (i, c) in op.cursors.iter().enumerate() {\n        cursors.push(serde_json::json!([\n            i,\n            (c.x * 100.0).round() / 100.0,\n            (c.z * 100.0).round() / 100.0,\n            c.tool,\n            if c.active { 1 } else { 0 },\n            c.score\n        ]));\n    }\n    let mut cues = Vec::new();\n    for e in events.iter().rev().take(8) {\n        if let pav_core::SimEvent::Cue { id, .. } = e {\n            cues.push(*id);\n        }\n    }\n    serde_json::json!({\n        \"k\": \"s\",\n        \"v\": (op.vitals * 10.0).round() / 10.0,\n        \"b\": op.bpm.round(),\n        \"p\": (op.phase * 100.0).round() / 100.0,\n        \"f\": if op.flat { 1 } else { 0 },\n        \"tm\": (op.timer * 10.0).round() / 10.0,\n        \"cd\": (op.code_t * 10.0).round() / 10.0,\n        \"h\": hazards,\n        \"u\": cursors,\n        \"q\": cues,\n    })\n    .to_string()\n}\n\nfn standings_json(present: &[u8], op: &SurgeryFrame) -> String {\n    let ids: Vec<u8> = if present.is_empty() { vec![0] } else { present.to_vec() };\n    let mut scores = serde_json::Map::new();\n    for id in &ids {\n        let score = op.cursors.get(*id as usize).map(|c| c.score).unwrap_or(0);\n        scores.insert(id.to_string(), serde_json::json!(score));\n    }\n    serde_json::json!({\n        \"standings\": [ids],\n        \"won\": op.vitals > 0.0,\n        \"scores\": scores,\n    })\n    .to_string()\n}\n\nfn status_json(shell: &Shell, op: Option<&SurgeryFrame>) -> String {"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-137b43f4-b08d-4b44-81be-386d5e01b309-126","name":"search_replace","input":{"file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224015__x42677a/work/engine-link/scripts/pack_single_html.py","old_string":"    # A manifest is another file to load: the single page goes without one.\n    page = replace_one(page, r'[ \\t]*<link rel=\"manifest\"[^>]*>\\n', lambda m: \"\", \"manifest link\")","new_string":"    # A manifest is another file to load: the single page goes without one.\n    page = replace_one(page, r'[ \\t]*<link rel=\"manifest\"[^>]*>\\n', lambda m: \"\", \"manifest link\")\n\n    # Session client first, then the game's hub tags and shim. about-data rides with them.\n    client_path = ROOT / \"web\" / \"session.js\"\n    shim_path = ROOT / \"web\" / \"hub_shim.js\"\n    about_path = ROOT / \"crates\" / \"pav_ui\" / \"src\" / \"surgery\" / \"about.json\"\n    for label, text in (\n        (\"session.js\", client_path.read_text(encoding=\"utf-8\")),\n        (\"hub_shim.js\", shim_path.read_text(encoding=\"utf-8\")),\n    ):\n        if re.search(r\"(?i)</script|<script|<!--\", text):\n            fail(f\"{label} contains <script, </script or <!--, which can't sit inside an inline script\")\n    client = client_path.read_text(encoding=\"utf-8\")\n    shim = shim_path.read_text(encoding=\"utf-8\")\n    tags = (\n        '<meta name=\"hub:session\" content=\"1\">\\n'\n        '<meta name=\"hub:session-players\" content=\"1-4\">\\n'\n        '<meta name=\"hub:session-mode\" content=\"shared-world\">\\n'\n        '<meta name=\"hub:session-minutes\" content=\"4\">\\n'\n        '<meta name=\"hub:webgpu\" content=\"required\">\\n'\n        '<meta name=\"hub:session-goal\" content=\"Keep the patient alive\">\\n'\n        '<meta name=\"hub:session-howto\" content=\"Aim, pick a tool, operate on the beat\">\\n'\n    )\n    about = about_path.read_text(encoding=\"utf-8\") if about_path.is_file() else \"\"\n    if about and re.search(r\"(?i)</script\", about):\n        fail(\"about.json contains </script>\")\n    about_tag = f'<script type=\"application/json\" id=\"about-data\">\\n{about}</script>\\n' if about else \"\"\n    page = replace_one(\n        page,\n        r'<meta charset=\"utf-8\">\\n',\n        lambda m: m.group(0) + \"<script>\\n\" + client + \"\\n</script>\\n\" + tags + \"<script>\\n\" + shim + \"\\n</script>\\n\" + about_tag,\n        \"charset meta\",\n    )"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":879,"output_tokens":5100,"cache_read_input_tokens":189696,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa38-de6f-7dc0-ae0d-e0f717ed75f2","uuid":"790e66a6-05f1-4ece-bca5-648d2ddac476"}
