109,115,103,46,118,44,32,99,108,105,101,110,116,58,32,109,115,103,46,99,108,105,101,110,116,44,32,109,111,100,101,58,32,109,115,103,46,109,111,100,101,32,63,63,32,110,117,108,108,44,32,115,101,97,116,115,58,32,109,115,103,46,115,101,97,116,115,32,63,63,32,110,117,108,108,44,32,99,97,114,100,58,32,109,115,103,46,99,97,114,100,32,61,61,61,32,116,114,117,101,32,125,59,10,52,48,51,58,32,32,32,32,32,32,32,32,99,111,110,115,116,32,115,97,105,100,32,61,32,109,111,100,101,79,102,40,109,115,103,46,109,111,100,101,41,59,10,60,47,119,111,114,107,115,112,97,99,101,95,114,101,115,117,108,116,62],\"stderr\":[],\"exit_code\":0,\"match_count\":11,\"file_matches\":[{\"path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224015__x42677a/work/Hands of Harbor: Second Opinion-Trauma Center: Second Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-224015/tests/hub/bridge.js\",\"matches\":[{\"line_number\":17,\"content\":\" *   {k:'h', r, m}       from the coordinator: welcome, start, leave, time-up, end\"},{\"line_number\":100,\"content\":\"        return toHub({ type: 'hello', v: msg.v, client: String(msg.client || ''), mode: msg.mode ?? null, seats: msg.seats ?? null, card: ownsCard });\"},{\"line_number\":106,\"content\":\"        if (!ownsCard) return issue('answer without its own card: connect({ card: true })');\"},{\"line_number\":225,\"content\":\"      case 'time-up':\"},{\"line_number\":226,\"content\":\"        return toGame({ type: 'time-up', graceMs: m.graceMs });\"}]},{\"path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224015__x42677a/work/Hands of Harbor: Second Opinion-Trauma Center: Second Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-224015/tests/hub/round.js\",\"matches\":[{\"line_number\":38,\"content\":\"export function modeOf(word) {\"},{\"line_number\":169,\"content\":\" * @param {string|null} o.mode        parallel | ghost | shared-world, or an older tag (modeOf); null takes the first hello's\"},{\"line_number\":194,\"content\":\"  mode = modeOf(mode);\"},{\"line_number\":342,\"content\":\"    toPresent({ type: 'time-up', graceMs: t.graceMs });\"},{\"line_number\":401,\"content\":\"        seat.caps = { v: msg.v, client: msg.client, mode: msg.mode ?? null, seats: msg.seats ?? null, card: msg.card === true };\"},{\"line_number\":403,\"content\":\"        const said = modeOf(msg.mode);\"}]}]}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa38-de6f-7dc0-ae0d-e0f717ed75f2","uuid":"6a41649b-0bdf-4eea-bfba-8a30af936e38"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_459","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"A bug was found: when H.active is false, the shim returns before defining poll.\n\nThe early return is intentional. The product checks the active flag before calling poll, so inactive hubs and pages without a hub are handled safely. When a hub is active, connect is async; until info arrives, poll exists but does nothing until joined.\n\ntime() is -Infinity before start. The Enter keydown path may call AIHub.answer('ready') before welcome, though session.js likely no-ops that early. Event listeners are added inside the connect promise's then(), so a standalone connection with null info leaves them unregistered.\n\nEvent listeners are registered immediately, not inside the connect promise. If connect fails or returns null, they still fire and call AIHub.answer, which is harmless if answer no-ops. The harness sends a synthetic Enter key on the iframe body; a capture listener on the window should catch it.\n\nThe Enter key also sets held['Enter'] to true. During play, repeated AIHub.answer('ready') calls are harmless because answer no-ops after start. When time-up finishes, the hub submits a fallback standings object using the current player IDs.\n\nThe finish fallback produces a single tie group from player IDs. The server publishes its own standings every play frame and must call finish itself.\n\nThe shim must not finish on host-leave; only time-up should trigger finish. Need to check whether send_snap increments sent when targets are empty. Will read session.js send, finish, and ready next.\n\nH.send may pass `to: undefined` to AIHub.send. Need to check if that is valid or if the property should be omitted.\n\nSnap quantization rounds vitals to 0.1, not multiplied by ten. parse_snap uses raw values. Now checking parse_snap defaults.\n\nparse_snap defaults to 70.0 for vitals and 240.0 for timer, using raw values when fields exist.\n\nA potential mismatch exists between client snapshot vitals and host real vitals. The two-page test allows about a one-unit variance, which is acceptable.\n\nCursor flow: client aim changes host cursor through send_input. The host receives the remote aim, merges it into surgeons before pump, and mirror_predict only steers local hands without ticking the heart.\n\nThe host simulates cursor movement and sends snapshots containing cursor positions. The client applies these via apply_mirror to update surgeon positions.\n\nFor a two-player game, the host is player 0 and the client is player 1. The host compose logic marks slot 1 as inactive via TOOL_KEEP because local is Some(0), so remote input from the client slot is applied there. The client compose logic keeps its own slot active.\n\nA DOM override for held keys is sent via send_input. Input is rate-limited to 15 Hz unless an edge triggers it, so aim updates at that frequency. When the harness drives input through the iframe keyboard, both winit and DOM may see the keys. The product code checks if the DOM cursor position is non-zero; if so, it activates the local surgeon, sets its aim from the DOM coordinates, and clears the absolute-aim and snap flags from held.\n\nIf the DOM cursor is non-zero, it overrides winit's aim and produces a relative stick rather than an absolute one. This prevents doubled input when both sources fire.\n\nWhen only the mouse moves on the client, winit sets absolute aim while the DOM stays zero, so the host receives absolute aim. The host's steer logic must correctly handle AIM_ABSOLUTE.\n\nBefore boot, the client remains in card mode and cannot move the simulation cursor; boot occurs once time() reaches zero. After boot, the host enters operation mode and the client enters mirror mode.\n\nThe host updates its cursor during the ops tick via steer. Both client and host slots are active after boot, so remote input reaches the host correctly. Need to verify that shape_stick produces movement. The pause state is not an issue during play; note_mode(7) shows the card screen and note_mode(3) shows the HUD.\n\nsaw_card exec sets mode 7 only when the current mode is 0 or 6. If boot and saw_card both queue on the same frame, saw_card runs first and then boot runs immediately before pump. If boot is delayed, the card screen still appears first.\n\nsaw_card is a one-shot flag that runs only on the first frame. If boot occurs later, saw_card still sets mode 7 before boot switches to OP.\n\nIf the hub welcome and countdown finish before the ten-second title attract begins, the hub connects in time. Otherwise the attract mode 6 starts first, and saw_card will still queue mode 7 because mode 6 satisfies its condition.\n\nThe boot one-shot in Link::poll must fire exactly once during play. The ready() call is gated by the info field, which the shim sets when connect resolves; the next poll frame then issues it, so the wasm loop needs to be running.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-30a77868-0b57-41eb-b8e1-c91701c7c3ac-23","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224015__x42677a/work/engine-link/crates/pav_app/src/hub.rs","offset":145,"limit":60}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-30a77868-0b57-41eb-b8e1-c91701c7c3ac-24","name":"grep","input":{"pattern":"ready\\(|function send|finish\\(|this\\.time|standAlone|rate","path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224015__x42677a/work/engine-link/web/session.js"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-30a77868-0b57-41eb-b8e1-c91701c7c3ac-25","name":"grep","input":{"pattern":"dataset.complete|__hubCheck|sent > 0|host-left|answer","path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224015__x42677a/work/Hands of Harbor: Second Opinion-Trauma Center: Second Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-224015/tests/hub/harness.html"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":3008,"output_tokens":2562,"cache_read_input_tokens":57344,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa38-de6f-7dc0-ae0d-e0f717ed75f2","uuid":"8a794e33-669a-401d-b9c4-56958f35bfd2"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-30a77868-0b57-41eb-b8e1-c91701c7c3ac-23","content":"{\"type\":\"ReadFile\",\"FileContent\":{\"content\":\"145→\\n        pub fn poll(&mut self, dt: f32) -> super::View {\\n            let Some(hub) = hub_obj() else {\\n                return super::View::idle();\\n            };\\n150→            if !flag(&hub, \\\"active\\\") {\\n                return super::View::idle();\\n            }\\n            if !self.joined {\\n                if let Some(info) = json_field(&hub, \\\"info\\\") {\\n                    self.take_info(&info);\\n                }\\n            }\\n            if self.joined && !self.readied {\\n                let _ = call(&hub, \\\"ready\\\", &[]);\\n160→                self.readied = true;\\n            }\\n            if let Some(text) = call(&hub, \\\"poll\\\", &[]).and_then(|v| v.as_string()) {\\n                if let Ok(events) = serde_json::from_str::<Vec<serde_json::Value>>(&text) {\\n                    for ev in events {\\n                        self.on_event(&ev);\\n                    }\\n                }\\n            }\\n            let t = call(&hub, \\\"time\\\", &[]).and_then(|v| v.as_f64()).unwrap_or(f64::NEG_INFINITY);\\n170→            if self.joined && !self.ended && t >= 0.0 {\\n                self.play = true;\\n            }\\n            for i in 0..4 {\\n                self.remote_age[i] += dt;\\n                if self.remote_age[i] > 0.35 {\\n                    self.remote[i] = None;\\n                }\\n            }\\n            let boot = if self.play && !self.booted && self.joined {\\n180→                self.booted = true;\\n                Some(super::Boot {\\n                    seed: self.seed,\\n                    slots: self.present.clone(),\\n                    server: self.server,\\n                    mirror: !self.host,\\n                })\\n            } else {\\n                None\\n            };\\n190→            super::View {\\n                active: true,\\n                server: self.server,\\n                host: self.host,\\n                play: self.play,\\n                ended: self.ended,\\n                slot: self.slot,\\n                boot,\\n                snap: self.pending_snap.take(),\\n                remote: self.remote,\\n200→                dom: read_dom(&hub),\\n                card_lines: self.card_lines.clone(),\\n                present: self.present.clone(),\\n            }\\n        }\",\"content_concise\":\"145→\\n        pub fn poll(&mut self, dt: f32) -> super::View {\\n            let Some(hub) = hub_obj() else {\\n                return super::View::idle();\\n            };\\n150→            if !flag(&hub, \\\"active\\\") {\\n                return super::View::idle();\\n            }\\n            if !self.joined {\\n                if let Some(info) = json_field(&hub, \\\"info\\\") {\\n                    self.take_info(&info);\\n                }\\n            }\\n            if self.joined && !self.readied {\\n                let _ = call(&hub, \\\"ready\\\", &[]);\\n160→                self.readied = true;\\n            }\\n            if let Some(text) = call(&hub, \\\"poll\\\", &[]).and_then(|v| v.as_string()) {\\n                if let Ok(events) = serde_json::from_str::<Vec<serde_json::Value>>(&text) {\\n                    for ev in events {\\n                        self.on_event(&ev);\\n                    }\\n                }\\n            }\\n            let t = call(&hub, \\\"time\\\", &[]).and_then(|v| v.as_f64()).unwrap_or(f64::NEG_INFINITY);\\n170→            if self.joined && !self.ended && t >= 0.0 {\\n                self.play = true;\\n            }\\n            for i in 0..4 {\\n                self.remote_age[i] += dt;\\n                if self.remote_age[i] > 0.35 {\\n                    self.remote[i] = None;\\n                }\\n            }\\n            let boot = if self.play && !self.booted && self.joined {\\n180→                self.booted = true;\\n                Some(super::Boot {\\n                    seed: self.seed,\\n                    slots: self.present.clone(),\\n                    server: self.server,\\n                    mirror: !self.host,\\n                })\\n            } else {\\n                None\\n            };\\n190→            super::View {\\n                active: true,\\n                server: self.server,\\n                host: self.host,\\n                play: self.play,\\n                ended: self.ended,\\n                slot: self.slot,\\n                boot,\\n                snap: self.pending_snap.take(),\\n                remote: self.remote,\\n200→                dom: read_dom(&hub),\\n                card_lines: self.card_lines.clone(),\\n                present: self.present.clone(),\\n            }\\n        }\",\"absolute_path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224015__x42677a/work/Hands of Harbor: Second Opinion-Trauma Center: Second Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-224015/engine/crates/pav_app/src/hub.rs\",\"offset\":145,\"limit\":60,\"raw_output\":\"\\n        pub fn poll(&mut self, dt: f32) -> super::View {\\n            let Some(hub) = hub_obj() else {\\n                return super::View::idle();\\n            };\\n            if !flag(&hub, \\\"active\\\") {\\n                return super::View::idle();\\n            }\\n            if !self.joined {\\n                if let Some(info) = json_field(&hub, \\\"info\\\") {\\n                    self.take_info(&info);\\n                }\\n            }\\n            if self.joined && !self.readied {\\n                let _ = call(&hub, \\\"ready\\\", &[]);\\n                self.readied = true;\\n            }\\n            if let Some(text) = call(&hub, \\\"poll\\\", &[]).and_then(|v| v.as_string()) {\\n                if let Ok(events) = serde_json::from_str::<Vec<serde_json::Value>>(&text) {\\n                    for ev in events {\\n                        self.on_event(&ev);\\n                    }\\n                }\\n            }\\n            let t = call(&hub, \\\"time\\\", &[]).and_then(|v| v.as_f64()).unwrap_or(f64::NEG_INFINITY);\\n            if self.joined && !self.ended && t >= 0.0 {\\n                self.play = true;\\n            }\\n            for i in 0..4 {\\n                self.remote_age[i] += dt;\\n                if self.remote_age[i] > 0.35 {\\n                    self.remote[i] = None;\\n                }\\n            }\\n            let boot = if self.play && !self.booted && self.joined {\\n                self.booted = true;\\n                Some(super::Boot {\\n                    seed: self.seed,\\n                    slots: self.present.clone(),\\n                    server: self.server,\\n                    mirror: !self.host,\\n                })\\n            } else {\\n                None\\n            };\\n            super::View {\\n                active: true,\\n                server: self.server,\\n                host: self.host,\\n                play: self.play,\\n                ended: self.ended,\\n                slot: self.slot,\\n                boot,\\n                snap: self.pending_snap.take(),\\n                remote: self.remote,\\n                dom: read_dom(&hub),\\n                card_lines: self.card_lines.clone(),\\n                present: self.present.clone(),\\n            }\\n        }\\n\",\"total_lines\":453}}","is_error":false},{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-30a77868-0b57-41eb-b8e1-c91701c7c3ac-24","content":"{\"type\":\"GrepSearch\",\"stdout\":[60,119,111,114,107,115,112,97,99,101,95,114,101,115,117,108,116,32,119,111,114,107,115,112,97,99,101,95,112,97,116,104,61,34,47,104,111,109,101,47,109,105,99,104,97,47,100,101,118,47,99,99,45,109,97,116,114,105,120,47,114,117,110,115,47,103,114,111,107,45,120,104,105,103,104,46,98,117,105,108,100,45,118,50,95,95,50,48,50,54,49,49,48,52