{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-33e8aa92-c750-43e6-86d3-33ee3c1b6984-34","content":"{\"type\":\"ReadFile\",\"FileContent\":{\"content\":\"90→  function fromGame(msg) {\\n    if (!msg || msg.aihub !== 1) return;\\n    if (!FROM_GAME.has(msg.type)) return issue(`unknown message type ${JSON.stringify(msg.type)}`);\\n    if (msg.type === 'fullscreen') return onFullscreen(msg.on === true);\\n    if (ended && msg.type !== 'error') return;\\n    switch (msg.type) {\\n      case 'hello':\\n        if (helloSent) return;\\n        helloSent = true;\\n        ownsCard = msg.card === true;\\n100→        return toHub({ type: 'hello', v: msg.v, client: String(msg.client || ''), mode: msg.mode ?? null, seats: msg.seats ?? null, card: ownsCard });\\n      case 'ready':\\n        if (!welcomed) return issue('ready before welcome');\\n        readySent = true;\\n        return toHub({ type: 'ready' });\\n      case 'answer':\\n        if (!ownsCard) return issue('answer without its own card: connect({ card: true })');\\n        if (!welcomed || started) return;\\n        if (msg.answer !== 'ready' && msg.answer !== 'more') return issue(`answer ${JSON.stringify(msg.answer)} is not ready or more`);\\n        return onAnswer(msg.answer);\\n110→      case 'result':\\n        if (!welcomed) return issue('result before welcome');\\n        return toHub({ type: 'result', time: msg.time, score: msg.score, stats: msg.stats, awards: msg.awards });\\n      case 'finish':\\n        if (!welcomed) return issue('finish before welcome');\\n        return toHub({ type: 'finish', standings: msg.standings, scores: msg.scores, won: msg.won, stats: msg.stats, awards: msg.awards });\\n      case 'error':\\n        return toHub({ type: 'error', message: String(msg.message || '').slice(0, 500), fatal: msg.fatal === true });\\n      case 'send':\\n        return sendGame(msg);\\n120→      case 'progress':\\n        return sendProgress(msg);\\n    }\\n  }\\n\\n  /** Progress goes to this hub's scoreboard and to every other player's, never to a game. */\\n  function sendProgress(msg) {\\n    if (!welcomed) return issue('progress before welcome');\\n    const p = cleanProgress(msg);\\n    if (!p) return issue('progress needs a finite score');\\n130→    const now = clock.now();\\n    if (now - progressAt < LIMITS.progressMs) {\\n      stats.dropped++;\\n      return;\\n    }\\n    progressAt = now;\\n    onProgress(me, p);\\n    const envelope = { k: 'p', r: round, f: me, d: p };\\n    for (const target of keys.filter((k, id) => id !== me && !gone.has(id))) net.send(target, envelope, { reliable: false });\\n  }\\n140→\\n  function sendGame(msg) {\\n    if (!welcomed) return issue('send before welcome');\\n    let text;\\n    try {\\n      text = JSON.stringify(msg.data);\\n    } catch {\\n      return issue('send: data is not JSON');\\n    }\\n    if (text === undefined) return issue('send: no data');\\n150→    if (text.length > LIMITS.maxBytes) {\\n      stats.dropped++;\\n      return issue(`send: ${text.length} bytes is over the ${LIMITS.maxBytes}-byte limit`);\\n    }\\n    const now = clock.now();\\n    tokens = Math.min(LIMITS.burst, tokens + ((now - refilled) / 1000) * LIMITS.ratePerS);\\n    refilled = now;\\n    if (tokens < 1) {\\n      stats.dropped++;\\n      return issue(`send: over ${LIMITS.ratePerS} messages a second`);\\n160→    }\\n    tokens -= 1;\\n    let targets;\\n    if (msg.to === undefined || msg.to === null) {\\n      targets = keys.filter((k, id) => id !== me && !gone.has(id));\\n    } else {\\n      if (!Number.isInteger(msg.to) || msg.to < 0 || msg.to >= keys.length || msg.to === me) {\\n        return issue(`send: no player ${JSON.stringify(msg.to)} to send to`);\\n      }\\n      if (gone.has(msg.to)) return;\\n170→      targets = [keys[msg.to]];\\n    }\\n    const reliable = msg.reliable !== false;\\n    const envelope = { k: 'g', r: round, f: me, d: JSON.parse(text) };\\n    for (const target of targets) net.send(target, envelope, { reliable });\\n    stats.sent++;\\n    stats.bytesSent += text.length;\\n  }\\n\\n  function deliverGame(fromKey, env) {\\n180→    if (ended || gone.has(env.f)) return;\\n    if (keys[env.f] !== fromKey) return issue(`traffic from ${fromKey} claims to be player ${env.f}`);\\n    stats.received++;\\n    toGame({ type: 'message', from: env.f, data: env.d });\\n  }\\n\\n  function fromNet(fromKey, env) {\\n    if (!env || env.r !== round) return;\\n    if (env.k === 'p') {\\n      const p = cleanProgress(env.d);\",\"content_concise\":\"90→  function fromGame(msg) {\\n    if (!msg || msg.aihub !== 1) return;\\n    if (!FROM_GAME.has(msg.type)) return issue(`unknown message type ${JSON.stringify(msg.type)}`);\\n    if (msg.type === 'fullscreen') return onFullscreen(msg.on === true);\\n    if (ended && msg.type !== 'error') return;\\n    switch (msg.type) {\\n      case 'hello':\\n        if (helloSent) return;\\n        helloSent = true;\\n        ownsCard = msg.card === true;\\n100→        return toHub({ type: 'hello', v: msg.v, client: String(msg.client || ''), mode: msg.mode ?? null, seats: msg.seats ?? null, card: ownsCard });\\n      case 'ready':\\n        if (!welcomed) return issue('ready before welcome');\\n        readySent = true;\\n        return toHub({ type: 'ready' });\\n      case 'answer':\\n        if (!ownsCard) return issue('answer without its own card: connect({ card: true })');\\n        if (!welcomed || started) return;\\n        if (msg.answer !== 'ready' && msg.answer !== 'more') return issue(`answer ${JSON.stringify(msg.answer)} is not ready or more`);\\n        return onAnswer(msg.answer);\\n110→      case 'result':\\n        if (!welcomed) return issue('result before welcome');\\n        return toHub({ type: 'result', time: msg.time, score: msg.score, stats: msg.stats, awards: msg.awards });\\n      case 'finish':\\n        if (!welcomed) return issue('finish before welcome');\\n        return toHub({ type: 'finish', standings: msg.standings, scores: msg.scores, won: msg.won, stats: msg.stats, awards: msg.awards });\\n      case 'error':\\n        return toHub({ type: 'error', message: String(msg.message || '').slice(0, 500), fatal: msg.fatal === true });\\n      case 'send':\\n        return sendGame(msg);\\n120→      case 'progress':\\n        return sendProgress(msg);\\n    }\\n  }\\n\\n  /** Progress goes to this hub's scoreboard and to every other player's, never to a game. */\\n  function sendProgress(msg) {\\n    if (!welcomed) return issue('progress before welcome');\\n    const p = cleanProgress(msg);\\n    if (!p) return issue('progress needs a finite score');\\n130→    const now = clock.now();\\n    if (now - progressAt < LIMITS.progressMs) {\\n      stats.dropped++;\\n      return;\\n    }\\n    progressAt = now;\\n    onProgress(me, p);\\n    const envelope = { k: 'p', r: round, f: me, d: p };\\n    for (const target of keys.filter((k, id) => id !== me && !gone.has(id))) net.send(target, envelope, { reliable: false });\\n  }\\n140→\\n  function sendGame(msg) {\\n    if (!welcomed) return issue('send before welcome');\\n    let text;\\n    try {\\n      text = JSON.stringify(msg.data);\\n    } catch {\\n      return issue('send: data is not JSON');\\n    }\\n    if (text === undefined) return issue('send: no data');\\n150→    if (text.length > LIMITS.maxBytes) {\\n      stats.dropped++;\\n      return issue(`send: ${text.length} bytes is over the ${LIMITS.maxBytes}-byte limit`);\\n    }\\n    const now = clock.now();\\n    tokens = Math.min(LIMITS.burst, tokens + ((now - refilled) / 1000) * LIMITS.ratePerS);\\n    refilled = now;\\n    if (tokens < 1) {\\n      stats.dropped++;\\n      return issue(`send: over ${LIMITS.ratePerS} messages a second`);\\n160→    }\\n    tokens -= 1;\\n    let targets;\\n    if (msg.to === undefined || msg.to === null) {\\n      targets = keys.filter((k, id) => id !== me && !gone.has(id));\\n    } else {\\n      if (!Number.isInteger(msg.to) || msg.to < 0 || msg.to >= keys.length || msg.to === me) {\\n        return issue(`send: no player ${JSON.stringify(msg.to)} to send to`);\\n      }\\n      if (gone.has(msg.to)) return;\\n170→      targets = [keys[msg.to]];\\n    }\\n    const reliable = msg.reliable !== false;\\n    const envelope = { k: 'g', r: round, f: me, d: JSON.parse(text) };\\n    for (const target of targets) net.send(target, envelope, { reliable });\\n    stats.sent++;\\n    stats.bytesSent += text.length;\\n  }\\n\\n  function deliverGame(fromKey, env) {\\n180→    if (ended || gone.has(env.f)) return;\\n    if (keys[env.f] !== fromKey) return issue(`traffic from ${fromKey} claims to be player ${env.f}`);\\n    stats.received++;\\n    toGame({ type: 'message', from: env.f, data: env.d });\\n  }\\n\\n  function fromNet(fromKey, env) {\\n    if (!env || env.r !== round) return;\\n    if (env.k === 'p') {\\n      const p = cleanProgress(env.d);\",\"absolute_path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224015__x42677a/work/Hands of Harbor: Second Opinion-Trauma Center: Second Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-224015/tests/hub/bridge.js\",\"offset\":90,\"limit\":100,\"raw_output\":\"  function fromGame(msg) {\\n    if (!msg || msg.aihub !== 1) return;\\n    if (!FROM_GAME.has(msg.type)) return issue(`unknown message type ${JSON.stringify(msg.type)}`);\\n    if (msg.type === 'fullscreen') return onFullscreen(msg.on === true);\\n    if (ended && msg.type !== 'error') return;\\n    switch (msg.type) {\\n      case 'hello':\\n        if (helloSent) return;\\n        helloSent = true;\\n        ownsCard = msg.card === true;\\n        return toHub({ type: 'hello', v: msg.v, client: String(msg.client || ''), mode: msg.mode ?? null, seats: msg.seats ?? null, card: ownsCard });\\n      case 'ready':\\n        if (!welcomed) return issue('ready before welcome');\\n        readySent = true;\\n        return toHub({ type: 'ready' });\\n      case 'answer':\\n        if (!ownsCard) return issue('answer without its own card: connect({ card: true })');\\n        if (!welcomed || started) return;\\n        if (msg.answer !== 'ready' && msg.answer !== 'more') return issue(`answer ${JSON.stringify(msg.answer)} is not ready or more`);\\n        return onAnswer(msg.answer);\\n      case 'result':\\n        if (!welcomed) return issue('result before welcome');\\n        return toHub({ type: 'result', time: msg.time, score: msg.score, stats: msg.stats, awards: msg.awards });\\n      case 'finish':\\n        if (!welcomed) return issue('finish before welcome');\\n        return toHub({ type: 'finish', standings: msg.standings, scores: msg.scores, won: msg.won, stats: msg.stats, awards: msg.awards });\\n      case 'error':\\n        return toHub({ type: 'error', message: String(msg.message || '').slice(0, 500), fatal: msg.fatal === true });\\n      case 'send':\\n        return sendGame(msg);\\n      case 'progress':\\n        return sendProgress(msg);\\n    }\\n  }\\n\\n  /** Progress goes to this hub's scoreboard and to every other player's, never to a game. */\\n  function sendProgress(msg) {\\n    if (!welcomed) return issue('progress before welcome');\\n    const p = cleanProgress(msg);\\n    if (!p) return issue('progress needs a finite score');\\n    const now = clock.now();\\n    if (now - progressAt < LIMITS.progressMs) {\\n      stats.dropped++;\\n      return;\\n    }\\n    progressAt = now;\\n    onProgress(me, p);\\n    const envelope = { k: 'p', r: round, f: me, d: p };\\n    for (const target of keys.filter((k, id) => id !== me && !gone.has(id))) net.send(target, envelope, { reliable: false });\\n  }\\n\\n  function sendGame(msg) {\\n    if (!welcomed) return issue('send before welcome');\\n    let text;\\n    try {\\n      text = JSON.stringify(msg.data);\\n    } catch {\\n      return issue('send: data is not JSON');\\n    }\\n    if (text === undefined) return issue('send: no data');\\n    if (text.length > LIMITS.maxBytes) {\\n      stats.dropped++;\\n      return issue(`send: ${text.length} bytes is over the ${LIMITS.maxBytes}-byte limit`);\\n    }\\n    const now = clock.now();\\n    tokens = Math.min(LIMITS.burst, tokens + ((now - refilled) / 1000) * LIMITS.ratePerS);\\n    refilled = now;\\n    if (tokens < 1) {\\n      stats.dropped++;\\n      return issue(`send: over ${LIMITS.ratePerS} messages a second`);\\n    }\\n    tokens -= 1;\\n    let targets;\\n    if (msg.to === undefined || msg.to === null) {\\n      targets = keys.filter((k, id) => id !== me && !gone.has(id));\\n    } else {\\n      if (!Number.isInteger(msg.to) || msg.to < 0 || msg.to >= keys.length || msg.to === me) {\\n        return issue(`send: no player ${JSON.stringify(msg.to)} to send to`);\\n      }\\n      if (gone.has(msg.to)) return;\\n      targets = [keys[msg.to]];\\n    }\\n    const reliable = msg.reliable !== false;\\n    const envelope = { k: 'g', r: round, f: me, d: JSON.parse(text) };\\n    for (const target of targets) net.send(target, envelope, { reliable });\\n    stats.sent++;\\n    stats.bytesSent += text.length;\\n  }\\n\\n  function deliverGame(fromKey, env) {\\n    if (ended || gone.has(env.f)) return;\\n    if (keys[env.f] !== fromKey) return issue(`traffic from ${fromKey} claims to be player ${env.f}`);\\n    stats.received++;\\n    toGame({ type: 'message', from: env.f, data: env.d });\\n  }\\n\\n  function fromNet(fromKey, env) {\\n    if (!env || env.r !== round) return;\\n    if (env.k === 'p') {\\n      const p = cleanProgress(env.d);\\n\",\"total_lines\":339}}","is_error":false},{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-33e8aa92-c750-43e6-86d3-33ee3c1b6984-35","content":"{\"type\":\"ReadFile\",\"FileContent\":{\"content\":\"120→  const given = new Map();\\n  const out = [];\\n  for (const a of awards) {\\n    const id = self ?? a?.id;\\n    const title = String(a?.title ?? '').trim().slice(0, HIGHLIGHTS.title);\\n    if (!title || !ids.includes(id) || (given.get(id) || 0) >= HIGHLIGHTS.awards) continue;\\n    given.set(id, (given.get(id) || 0) + 1);\\n    const detail = String(a.detail ?? '').trim().slice(0, HIGHLIGHTS.detail);\\n    out.push(detail ? { id, title, detail } : { id, title });\\n  }\\n130→  return out;\\n}\\n\\n/**\\n * Check a host's standings: groups of ids, best first, every present player\\n * exactly once. Players already gone may be placed or left out; whoever is\\n * left out lands in a last group of their own.\\n */\\nexport function checkStandings(standings, presentIds, allIds) {\\n  if (!Array.isArray(standings)) return { ok: false, problem: 'standings is not an array' };\\n140→  const all = new Set(allIds);\\n  const seen = new Set();\\n  const groups = [];\\n  for (const group of standings) {\\n    const ids = Array.isArray(group) ? group : [group];\\n    const kept = [];\\n    for (const id of ids) {\\n      if (!Number.isInteger(id) || !all.has(id)) return { ok: false, problem: `unknown player id ${JSON.stringify(id)}` };\\n      if (seen.has(id)) return { ok: false, problem: `player ${id} is placed twice` };\\n      seen.add(id);\\n150→      kept.push(id);\\n    }\\n    if (kept.length) groups.push(kept);\\n  }\\n  const missing = presentIds.filter((id) => !seen.has(id));\\n  if (missing.length) return { ok: false, problem: `standings leave out player${missing.length > 1 ? 's' : ''} ${missing.join(', ')}` };\\n  const absent = allIds.filter((id) => !seen.has(id));\\n  if (absent.length) groups.push(absent);\\n  return { ok: true, standings: groups };\\n}\\n160→\\n/**\\n * @param {object} o\\n * @param {number} o.round            round number, carried on every message\\n * @param {{key:string, slot:number, name:string}[]} o.players\\n * @param {string} o.hostKey          whose game runs a shared world\\n * @param {string} [o.serverKey]      a copy with no player of its own that runs the shared world\\n *                                    instead (a server): one more copy after the players, welcomed\\n *                                    with server: true, never ranked; the round is void if it goes\\n * @param {string|null} o.mode        parallel | ghost | shared-world, or an older tag (modeOf); null takes the first hello's\",\"content_concise\":\"120→  const given = new Map();\\n  const out = [];\\n  for (const a of awards) {\\n    const id = self ?? a?.id;\\n    const title = String(a?.title ?? '').trim().slice(0, HIGHLIGHTS.title);\\n    if (!title || !ids.includes(id) || (given.get(id) || 0) >= HIGHLIGHTS.awards) continue;\\n    given.set(id, (given.get(id) || 0) + 1);\\n    const detail = String(a.detail ?? '').trim().slice(0, HIGHLIGHTS.detail);\\n    out.push(detail ? { id, title, detail } : { id, title });\\n  }\\n130→  return out;\\n}\\n\\n/**\\n * Check a host's standings: groups of ids, best first, every present player\\n * exactly once. Players already gone may be placed or left out; whoever is\\n * left out lands in a last group of their own.\\n */\\nexport function checkStandings(standings, presentIds, allIds) {\\n  if (!Array.isArray(standings)) return { ok: false, problem: 'standings is not an array' };\\n140→  const all = new Set(allIds);\\n  const seen = new Set();\\n  const groups = [];\\n  for (const group of standings) {\\n    const ids = Array.isArray(group) ? group : [group];\\n    const kept = [];\\n    for (const id of ids) {\\n      if (!Number.isInteger(id) || !all.has(id)) return { ok: false, problem: `unknown player id ${JSON.stringify(id)}` };\\n      if (seen.has(id)) return { ok: false, problem: `player ${id} is placed twice` };\\n      seen.add(id);\\n150→      kept.push(id);\\n    }\\n    if (kept.length) groups.push(kept);\\n  }\\n  const missing = presentIds.filter((id) => !seen.has(id));\\n  if (missing.length) return { ok: false, problem: `standings leave out player${missing.length > 1 ? 's' : ''} ${missing.join(', ')}` };\\n  const absent = allIds.filter((id) => !seen.has(id));\\n  if (absent.length) groups.push(absent);\\n  return { ok: true, standings: groups };\\n}\\n160→\\n/**\\n * @param {object} o\\n * @param {number} o.round            round number, carried on every message\\n * @param {{key:string, slot:number, name:string}[]} o.players\\n * @param {string} o.hostKey          whose game runs a shared world\\n * @param {string} [o.serverKey]      a copy with no player of its own that runs the shared world\\n *                                    instead (a server): one more copy after the players, welcomed\\n *                                    with server: true, never ranked; the round is void if it goes\\n * @param {string|null} o.mode        parallel | ghost | shared-world, or an older tag (modeOf); null takes the first hello's\",\"absolute_path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224015__x42677a/work/Hands of Harbor: Second Opinion-Trauma Center: Second Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-224015/tests/hub/round.js\",\"offset\":120,\"limit\":50,\"raw_output\":\"  const given = new Map();\\n  const out = [];\\n  for (const a of awards) {\\n    const id = self ?? a?.id;\\n    const title = String(a?.title ?? '').trim().slice(0, HIGHLIGHTS.title);\\n    if (!title || !ids.includes(id) || (given.get(id) || 0) >= HIGHLIGHTS.awards) continue;\\n    given.set(id, (given.get(id) || 0) + 1);\\n    const detail = String(a.detail ?? '').trim().slice(0, HIGHLIGHTS.detail);\\n    out.push(detail ? { id, title, detail } : { id, title });\\n  }\\n  return out;\\n}\\n\\n/**\\n * Check a host's standings: groups of ids, best first, every present player\\n * exactly once. Players already gone may be placed or left out; whoever is\\n * left out lands in a last group of their own.\\n */\\nexport function checkStandings(standings, presentIds, allIds) {\\n  if (!Array.isArray(standings)) return { ok: false, problem: 'standings is not an array' };\\n  const all = new Set(allIds);\\n  const seen = new Set();\\n  const groups = [];\\n  for (const group of standings) {\\n    const ids = Array.isArray(group) ? group : [group];\\n    const kept = [];\\n    for (const id of ids) {\\n      if (!Number.isInteger(id) || !all.has(id)) return { ok: false, problem: `unknown player id ${JSON.stringify(id)}` };\\n      if (seen.has(id)) return { ok: false, problem: `player ${id} is placed twice` };\\n      seen.add(id);\\n      kept.push(id);\\n    }\\n    if (kept.length) groups.push(kept);\\n  }\\n  const missing = presentIds.filter((id) => !seen.has(id));\\n  if (missing.length) return { ok: false, problem: `standings leave out player${missing.length > 1 ? 's' : ''} ${missing.join(', ')}` };\\n  const absent = allIds.filter((id) => !seen.has(id));\\n  if (absent.length) groups.push(absent);\\n  return { ok: true, standings: groups };\\n}\\n\\n/**\\n * @param {object} o\\n * @param {number} o.round            round number, carried on every message\\n * @param {{key:string, slot:number, name:string}[]} o.players\\n * @param {string} o.hostKey          whose game runs a shared world\\n * @param {string} [o.serverKey]      a copy with no player of its own that runs the shared world\\n *                                    instead (a server): one more copy after the players, welcomed\\n *                                    with server: true, never ranked; the round is void if it goes\\n * @param {string|null} o.mode        parallel | ghost | shared-world, or an older tag (modeOf); null takes the first hello's\\n\",\"total_lines\":533}}","is_error":false},{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-33e8aa92-c750-43e6-86d3-33ee3c1b6984-36","content":"{\"type\":\"ReadFile\",\"FileContent\":{\"content\":\"400→        seat.hello = true;\\n        seat.caps = { v: msg.v, client: msg.client, mode: msg.mode ?? null, seats: msg.seats ?? null, card: msg.card === true };\\n        if (msg.v !== 1) issue(seat, `hello speaks protocol ${JSON.stringify(msg.v)}, not 1`);\\n        const said = modeOf(msg.mode);\\n        if (!mode && said) mode = said;\\n        else if (msg.mode && said !== mode) issue(seat, `hello says mode ${msg.mode}, the round is ${mode}`);\\n        welcome(seat);\\n        status();\\n        return;\\n      }\\n410→      case 'ready':\\n        if (!seat.hello || seat.ready || phase !== 'loading') return;\\n        seat.ready = true;\\n        status();\\n        return settle();\\n      case 'result': {\\n        if (!selfReported()) return issue(seat, `result is for parallel and ghost; this round is ${mode}`);\\n        if (phase === 'loading') return issue(seat, 'result before start');\\n        if (seat.result) return;\\n        const time = asNumber(msg.time);\\n420→        const score = asNumber(msg.score);\\n        if (Number.isFinite(time)) seat.result = { time };\\n        else if (Number.isFinite(score)) seat.result = { score };\\n        else return issue(seat, 'result needs a finite time or score');\\n        seat.stats = cleanStats(msg.stats);\\n        seat.awards = cleanAwards(msg.awards, ids, seat.id);\\n        status();\\n        return settle();\\n      }\\n      case 'finish': {\\n430→        if (selfReported()) return issue(seat, `finish is for a shared world; ${mode} games report result`);\\n        if (seat !== host) return issue(seat, 'finish from a player who is not the host');\\n        if (phase === 'loading') return issue(seat, 'finish before start');\\n        const checked = checkStandings(msg.standings, present().map((s) => s.id), ids);\\n        if (!checked.ok) return issue(seat, `finish ignored: ${checked.problem}`);\\n        const scores = msg.scores && typeof msg.scores === 'object' ? msg.scores : undefined;\\n        const given = msg.stats && typeof msg.stats === 'object' ? msg.stats : {};\\n        const stats = Object.fromEntries(ids.map((id) => [id, cleanStats(given[id])]).filter(([, v]) => v));\\n        const awards = cleanAwards(msg.awards, ids);\\n        // won makes it a team result; a game tagged co-op that leaves it out lost, as co-op always read it.\\n440→        const won = typeof msg.won === 'boolean' ? msg.won : seat.caps?.mode === 'co-op' ? false : undefined;\\n        return finishPlayed(checked.standings, { scores, won, stats, awards });\\n      }\\n      case 'error':\\n        issue(seat, `game error: ${String(msg.message || '').slice(0, 200)}`);\\n        if (msg.fatal) {\\n          if (needsHost() && seat === host) return finishVoid('host-error');\\n          markOut(seat, 'disconnected');\\n          status();\\n          settle();\\n450→        }\\n        return;\\n      case 'vis':\\n        if (seat !== host || !needsHost()) return;\\n        if (msg.hidden && seat.hidden == null && phase !== 'loading') {\\n          seat.hidden = later(t.hiddenMs, () => finishVoid('host-hidden'));\\n        } else if (!msg.hidden) {\\n          cancel(seat.hidden);\\n          seat.hidden = null;\\n        }\",\"content_concise\":\"400→        seat.hello = true;\\n        seat.caps = { v: msg.v, client: msg.client, mode: msg.mode ?? null, seats: msg.seats ?? null, card: msg.card === true };\\n        if (msg.v !== 1) issue(seat, `hello speaks protocol ${JSON.stringify(msg.v)}, not 1`);\\n        const said = modeOf(msg.mode);\\n        if (!mode && said) mode = said;\\n        else if (msg.mode && said !== mode) issue(seat, `hello says mode ${msg.mode}, the round is ${mode}`);\\n        welcome(seat);\\n        status();\\n        return;\\n      }\\n410→      case 'ready':\\n        if (!seat.hello || seat.ready || phase !== 'loading') return;\\n        seat.ready = true;\\n        status();\\n        return settle();\\n      case 'result': {\\n        if (!selfReported()) return issue(seat, `result is for parallel and ghost; this round is ${mode}`);\\n        if (phase === 'loading') return issue(seat, 'result before start');\\n        if (seat.result) return;\\n        const time = asNumber(msg.time);\\n420→        const score = asNumber(msg.score);\\n        if (Number.isFinite(time)) seat.result = { time };\\n        else if (Number.isFinite(score)) seat.result = { score };\\n        else return issue(seat, 'result needs a finite time or score');\\n        seat.stats = cleanStats(msg.stats);\\n        seat.awards = cleanAwards(msg.awards, ids, seat.id);\\n        status();\\n        return settle();\\n      }\\n      case 'finish': {\\n430→        if (selfReported()) return issue(seat, `finish is for a shared world; ${mode} games report result`);\\n        if (seat !== host) return issue(seat, 'finish from a player who is not the host');\\n        if (phase === 'loading') return issue(seat, 'finish before start');\\n        const checked = checkStandings(msg.standings, present().map((s) => s.id), ids);\\n        if (!checked.ok) return issue(seat, `finish ignored: ${checked.problem}`);\\n        const scores = msg.scores && typeof msg.scores === 'object' ? msg.scores : undefined;\\n        const given = msg.stats && typeof msg.stats === 'object' ? msg.stats : {};\\n        const stats = Object.fromEntries(ids.map((id) => [id, cleanStats(given[id])]).filter(([, v]) => v));\\n        const awards = cleanAwards(msg.awards, ids);\\n        // won makes it a team result; a game tagged co-op that leaves it out lost, as co-op always read it.\\n440→        const won = typeof msg.won === 'boolean' ? msg.won : seat.caps?.mode === 'co-op' ? false : undefined;\\n        return finishPlayed(checked.standings, { scores, won, stats, awards });\\n      }\\n      case 'error':\\n        issue(seat, `game error: ${String(msg.message || '').slice(0, 200)}`);\\n        if (msg.fatal) {\\n          if (needsHost() && seat === host) return finishVoid('host-error');\\n          markOut(seat, 'disconnected');\\n          status();\\n          settle();\\n450→        }\\n        return;\\n      case 'vis':\\n        if (seat !== host || !needsHost()) return;\\n        if (msg.hidden && seat.hidden == null && phase !== 'loading') {\\n          seat.hidden = later(t.hiddenMs, () => finishVoid('host-hidden'));\\n        } else if (!msg.hidden) {\\n          cancel(seat.hidden);\\n          seat.hidden = null;\\n        }\",\"absolute_path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224015__x42677a/work/Hands of Harbor: Second Opinion-Trauma Center: Second Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-224015/tests/hub/round.js\",\"offset\":400,\"limit\":60,\"raw_output\":\"        seat.hello = true;\\n        seat.caps = { v: msg.v, client: msg.client, mode: msg.mode ?? null, seats: msg.seats ?? null, card: msg.card === true };\\n        if (msg.v !== 1) issue(seat, `hello speaks protocol ${JSON.stringify(msg.v)}, not 1`);\\n        const said = modeOf(msg.mode);\\n        if (!mode && said) mode = said;\\n        else if (msg.mode && said !== mode) issue(seat, `hello says mode ${msg.mode}, the round is ${mode}`);\\n        welcome(seat);\\n        status();\\n        return;\\n      }\\n      case 'ready':\\n        if (!seat.hello || seat.ready || phase !== 'loading') return;\\n        seat.ready = true;\\n        status();\\n        return settle();\\n      case 'result': {\\n        if (!selfReported()) return issue(seat, `result is for parallel and ghost; this round is ${mode}`);\\n        if (phase === 'loading') return issue(seat, 'result before start');\\n        if (seat.result) return;\\n        const time = asNumber(msg.time);\\n        const score = asNumber(msg.score);\\n        if (Number.isFinite(time)) seat.result = { time };\\n        else if (Number.isFinite(score)) seat.result = { score };\\n        else return issue(seat, 'result needs a finite time or score');\\n        seat.stats = cleanStats(msg.stats);\\n        seat.awards = cleanAwards(msg.awards, ids, seat.id);\\n        status();\\n        return settle();\\n      }\\n      case 'finish': {\\n        if (selfReported()) return issue(seat, `finish is for a shared world; ${mode} games report result`);\\n        if (seat !== host) return issue(seat, 'finish from a player who is not the host');\\n        if (phase === 'loading') return issue(seat, 'finish before start');\\n        const checked = checkStandings(msg.standings, present().map((s) => s.id), ids);\\n        if (!checked.ok) return issue(seat, `finish ignored: ${checked.problem}`);\\n        const scores = msg.scores && typeof msg.scores === 'object' ? msg.scores : undefined;\\n        const given = msg.stats && typeof msg.stats === 'object' ? msg.stats : {};\\n        const stats = Object.fromEntries(ids.map((id) => [id, cleanStats(given[id])]).filter(([, v]) => v));\\n        const awards = cleanAwards(msg.awards, ids);\\n        // won makes it a team result; a game tagged co-op that leaves it out lost, as co-op always read it.\\n        const won = typeof msg.won === 'boolean' ? msg.won : seat.caps?.mode === 'co-op' ? false : undefined;\\n        return finishPlayed(checked.standings, { scores, won, stats, awards });\\n      }\\n      case 'error':\\n        issue(seat, `game error: ${String(msg.message || '').slice(0, 200)}`);\\n        if (msg.fatal) {\\n          if (needsHost() && seat === host) return finishVoid('host-error');\\n          markOut(seat, 'disconnected');\\n          status();\\n          settle();\\n        }\\n        return;\\n      case 'vis':\\n        if (seat !== host || !needsHost()) return;\\n        if (msg.hidden && seat.hidden == null && phase !== 'loading') {\\n          seat.hidden = later(t.hiddenMs, () => finishVoid('host-hidden'));\\n        } else if (!msg.hidden) {\\n          cancel(seat.hidden);\\n          seat.hidden = null;\\n        }\\n\",\"total_lines\":533}}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa38-de6f-7dc0-ae0d-e0f717ed75f2","uuid":"2660f900-be8c-4ca5-bc88-375d4420072f"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_464","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"stats.sent increments even when targets is empty with only one player.\n\nThe host sends both snap and input. The 15Hz rate is safe against the double 20/s limits.\n\nThe host sends both input and snapshots at 15Hz each. That totals 30Hz. This exceeds the 20/s rate limit. The bridge drops messages and issues a protocol error. The fix is to have only clients send input and only the host send snapshots.\n\nThe fix is to change product.rs so the host sends only snapshots and clients send only input. The host's own cursor will still appear because snapshots include cursor data.\n\nClients apply mirrors from snapshots that contain all cursors. The host receives client inputs and simulates them before sending snapshots. This creates a clean one-way flow: clients send input, the host sends snapshots only. Rate stays under 20/s. The host does not receive its own snapshots.\n\nThe 5% packet loss is unlikely to zero out the round. The play window is long enough to absorb it.\n\nJitter and latency should keep messages within the play window.\n\nThe host snapshots the frame after pump. Client inputs are merged before pump, so the snapshot correctly includes their results.\n\nNo traffic is sent during the countdown because play is false. The first snapshot waits four frames after boot before sending, since snap_acc starts at zero and the threshold is one-fifteenth of a second. Clients boot their mirrors in the same frame but lack world state until snapshots arrive.\n\nThe harness waits for the card to be shown before pressing Enter. The game only sends card events after ready() is called, so the Enter keypress triggers the answer after the card appears.\n\nThe shim registers its card listener only after the connect promise resolves. If the card event fires before that registration, it could be missed. The session.js hub queues pending events for handlers that are not yet registered, so the event would be held until the listener attaches.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-83bc16db-2470-4890-89ad-faad9ea1d327-37","name":"grep","input":{"pattern":"function emit","path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224015__x42677a/work/engine-link/web/session.js","-A":25}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-83bc16db-2470-4890-89ad-faad9ea1d327-38","name":"grep","input":{"pattern":"cardSent|showsCard|type === 'card'","path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224015__x42677a/work/Hands of Harbor: Second Opinion-Trauma Center: Second Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-224015/tests/hub"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":3082,"output_tokens":1453,"cache_read_input_tokens":74752,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa38-de6f-7dc0-ae0d-e0f717ed75f2","uuid":"2ce3a88b-7e7a-437e-bf85-d3743a538380"}
