{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_469","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"`paused` is a direct field on `self`, not derived from the screen.\n\nThe host-only snap fix is the key change. The host simulates client input, so remote aim updates the host cursor. A relative stick input of (1, 0) yields roughly 0.25 units per frame.\n\nRemote input is applied continuously at 15Hz. The host simulates every tick using the last received remote value until a 0.35s timeout expires. A 120ms client hold therefore produces roughly one to two packets.\n\nThe host cursor moves for 0.35 seconds after the last packet, which is enough for the traffic test but not the longer two-page hold.\n\nNext I will fix the double send and check WASM status.\n\nStandings scores are string keys that pass through without validation. Player IDs serialize as JSON numbers. An empty present list defaults to vec![0], though this edge case does not apply.\n\nThe server is included in the present list and standings. If a player leaves before the game ends, the remaining players are still retained. A time-up finish uses the last published state, which already reflects any leave events.\n\nThe Rust poll loop processes leave events and updates the present list before publishing the frame. This ordering ensures H.last always reflects the current present set, so a time-up finish cannot reference a missing player.\n\nThe JS time-up handler fires asynchronously when the event arrives. It calls finish immediately using H.last. This can happen before Rust publishes the updated standings.\n\nThe fallback for a null H.last uses AIHub.players, which session.js already filters to current players on leave. This ensures the time-up finish always sees the correct present set.\n\nPublishing only happens while hub.play is true. During countdown play remains false until the timer reaches zero.\n\nThe double-send is the main bug. The host only applies input messages, so clients ignore them.\n\nThe double-send pushes traffic to 30 packets per second, which exceeds the 20-per-second rate limit. This causes bridge issues and protocol failures. Publishing does not send network traffic.\n\nThe combined snap and input traffic peaks at 30Hz, confirming the double-send issue. Client input is correctly suppressed before play begins. I will patch the send block in product.rs and check WASM compilation. Native tests pass. I also noticed a potential serde issue: if `hub_quiet` lacks a default, old serialized test data may fail bincode round-trips.\n\nTests likely snapshot in-memory via the same binary, so the new `hub_quiet` field should be present and round-trip fine. Snapshot tests compare replay hashes rather than struct schemas, so behavior changes are harmless. The `boot_hub_round` signature change does not affect tests. I still need to check whether `serde_json` snapshots of the full simulation would break if the field is not skipped.\n\nI confirmed the snapshot test uses the same binary on both sides, so the new `hub_quiet` field will round-trip correctly.\n\nI also found a server slot bug. When there are two players, the server gets ID 2. The local surgeon lookup fails because `local = None`, and remote input decoding rejects slots of 4 or higher. Since the server never sends input, this is harmless.\n\nThe host player occupies slot 0, which the boot sequence activates and the host cursor moves. Snapshot data includes this cursor so clients can render it.\n\nI still need to verify that client mirror application does not fight the host.\n\nThe quiet server mode skips its own plate, which risks running out of GPU memory with four webgpu contexts.\n\nI am verifying that packer injection places session.js first and that about-data is valid JSON. The send call passes undefined as the optional target, which is safe. I also need to check whether small harness iframes will still render the canvas correctly.\n\nThe code-blue timer and win condition are being checked for the hub. The patient must survive long enough to avoid a 240-second code-blue death, since a false win is still valid. A panic is unlikely if tests pass. WebGPU console errors will not be caught by the error event listener.\n\nWASM panics must be avoided because they surface as uncaught error events. Audio and WebSocket calls are unlikely to throw uncaught errors since audio is synthesized. I am also checking whether `op.cursors.get` or frame building could panic, and whether snapshot hazards with invalid kinds might crash `Hazard::make` during mirror prediction.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-486cef8d-9a6e-4340-a98d-98e8f2225723-49","name":"search_replace","input":{"file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224015__x42677a/work/engine-link/crates/pav_app/src/product.rs","old_string":"    if hub.active {\n        if !hub.server {\n            let me = hub.slot as usize;\n            if me < 4 {\n                app.harbor.link.send_input(&surgeons[me]);\n            }\n        }\n        if hub.host {\n            if let Some(op) = op.as_ref() {\n                app.harbor.link.send_snap(&snap_json(op, &events));\n                if hub.play {\n                    app.harbor.link.publish(&standings_json(&hub.present, op));\n                }\n            }\n        }\n    }","new_string":"    if hub.active {\n        // One stream per copy. Host and server send snapshots; clients send a hand.\n        // Sending both blows the hub's 20 messages/second cap.\n        if hub.host {\n            if let Some(op) = op.as_ref() {\n                app.harbor.link.send_snap(&snap_json(op, &events));\n                if hub.play {\n                    app.harbor.link.publish(&standings_json(&hub.present, op));\n                }\n            }\n        } else if !hub.server {\n            let me = hub.slot as usize;\n            if me < 4 {\n                app.harbor.link.send_input(&surgeons[me]);\n            }\n        }\n    }"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-486cef8d-9a6e-4340-a98d-98e8f2225723-50","name":"get_command_or_subagent_output","input":{"task_ids":["cc632eca-3a51-4676-a866-599c9503d45e"],"timeout_ms":120000}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1577,"output_tokens":2841,"cache_read_input_tokens":85248,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa38-de6f-7dc0-ae0d-e0f717ed75f2","uuid":"0a6defde-ce04-4dc0-afec-0b1121584c3a"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-486cef8d-9a6e-4340-a98d-98e8f2225723-49","content":"{\"type\":\"SearchReplace\",\"EditsApplied\":{\"old_string\":\"    if hub.active {\\n        if !hub.server {\\n            let me = hub.slot as usize;\\n            if me < 4 {\\n                app.harbor.link.send_input(&surgeons[me]);\\n            }\\n        }\\n        if hub.host {\\n            if let Some(op) = op.as_ref() {\\n                app.harbor.link.send_snap(&snap_json(op, &events));\\n                if hub.play {\\n                    app.harbor.link.publish(&standings_json(&hub.present, op));\\n                }\\n            }\\n        }\\n    }\",\"new_string\":\"    if hub.active {\\n        // One stream per copy. Host and server send snapshots; clients send a hand.\\n        // Sending both blows the hub's 20 messages/second cap.\\n        if hub.host {\\n            if let Some(op) = op.as_ref() {\\n                app.harbor.link.send_snap(&snap_json(op, &events));\\n                if hub.play {\\n                    app.harbor.link.publish(&standings_json(&hub.present, op));\\n                }\\n            }\\n        } else if !hub.server {\\n            let me = hub.slot as usize;\\n            if me < 4 {\\n                app.harbor.link.send_input(&surgeons[me]);\\n            }\\n        }\\n    }\",\"tool_output_for_prompt\":\"The file /home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224015__x42677a/work/engine-link/crates/pav_app/src/product.rs has been updated successfully.\",\"tool_output_for_prompt_concise\":\"The file /home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224015__x42677a/work/engine-link/crates/pav_app/src/product.rs has been updated.\",\"absolute_path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224015__x42677a/work/Hands of Harbor: Second Opinion-Trauma Center: Second Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-224015/engine/crates/p