{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_474","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"build-web.sh changes to the parent directory using `cd \"$(dirname \"$0\")/..\"`.\n\nBash `cd` follows logical paths by default. The script lands in the symlinked `engine-link` directory rather than its physical parent.\n\nThe colon issue is caused by rustc joining LD_LIBRARY_PATH paths that contain colons. The current directory and CARGO_TARGET_DIR must not contain colons. build-web.sh writes the wasm output to `${CARGO_TARGET_DIR:-target}/wasm32-unknown-unknown/dist/shardfall.wasm`.\n\nThe packer script resolves its own path with `resolve()`, which follows symlinks. This makes `ROOT` point to the physical engine directory containing the colon. That is fine for reading files. The output path is absolute and does not need to be inside that directory.\n\nThe generated HTML filename contains a colon from the game title. The packer preserves colons in the output path when `--out` is provided, so build-web.sh will pass an absolute path to avoid this issue. Using `python3 -I` ignores PYTHONPATH and user site packages.\n\nThe dist profile may be missing and could take 5–15 minutes on first use. Cargo.lock must match; a stale lock will cause --locked to fail fast. The packer's PAGE path and index.html meta charset need verification before starting the build.\n\nThe build will run in the background for up to ten minutes. This avoids a monitor that wakes on every cargo progress line.\n\nI will read about.json and TASK.md while the build runs. I also need to check the index.html charset and review shell tests for the UI driver. The plan requires a headless UI driver that navigates every screen with pad, keyboard, and mouse.\n\nI need to verify that the shell unit test `keyboard_pad_and_mouse_walk_the_shell` actually navigates every screen. The balance script requires a small Rust or Python driver, but no balance binary exists yet.\n\nA balance test would pollute the suite with printed output, and writing to scratch is unsafe because that directory gets deleted. I need a different approach for the balance script.\n\nA separate `cargo test` command with `--nocapture` could print the balance without polluting the main suite. Adding a new test to `run_all.py` would increase the passed count and conflict with the saved `suite.txt`, so that approach is rejected.\n\nAn ignored balance test avoids polluting the suite count. It will be run separately with `--ignored --nocapture` and write to `balance.txt`. This satisfies the plan without overriding a green suite.\n\nThe balance probe will be an ignored test in `pav_core/tests/surgery.rs` because it already has access to the simulation. I need to check how `run_bot` and `skill` are configured before writing it. Screenshots require the packed HTML and a browser, so they come after packing. I am verifying that the `send_json` fix is correct and that DOM aim during hub on host is handled properly for the host player.\n\nHost aim is generated locally by compose and winit, not through send_input. Other clients see the host cursor via snapshots.\n\nClients receive a snapshot and apply_mirror every 15 Hz. apply_mirror replaces the world state. The same frame then predicts. Pending snapshots are consumed once per update.\n\napply_mirror sets mode M_MIRROR unconditionally. This is safe because the host never applies it.\n\nA boot bug exists for both host and client mirrors. Server and host players both have host set to true.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-a6063c63-e288-4331-90de-320a83cc61bf-59","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224015__x42677a/work/Hands of Harbor: Second Opinion-Trauma Center: Second Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-224015/tests/hub/round.js","offset":180,"limit":100}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-a6063c63-e288-4331-90de-320a83cc61bf-60","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224015__x42677a/work/engine-link/web/index.html","limit":40}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-a6063c63-e288-4331-90de-320a83cc61bf-61","name":"grep","input":{"pattern":"fn run_bot|skill","path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224015__x42677a/work/engine-link/crates/pav_core/src/games/surgery","glob":"*.rs"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":3135,"output_tokens":2185,"cache_read_input_tokens":103808,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa38-de6f-7dc0-ae0d-e0f717ed75f2","uuid":"0514db10-e5ab-44bf-a80a-5b072a54a45d"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-a6063c63-e288-4331-90de-320a83cc61bf-59","content":"{\"type\":\"ReadFile\",\"FileContent\":{\"content\":\"180→  round,\\n  players,\\n  hostKey,\\n  mode = null,\\n  seed,\\n  limitMs,\\n  clock = REAL_CLOCK,\\n  deliver,\\n  onStatus = () => {},\\n  onEnd = () => {},\\n190→  timings = TIMINGS,\\n  gate = false,\\n  serverKey = null,\\n}) {\\n  mode = modeOf(mode);\\n  const t = { ...TIMINGS, ...timings };\\n  const seats = [...players]\\n    .sort((a, b) => a.slot - b.slot)\\n    .map((p, id) => ({\\n      id,\\n200→      key: p.key,\\n      slot: p.slot,\\n      name: p.name,\\n      color: SLOT_COLORS[p.slot % SLOT_COLORS.length],\\n      hello: false,\\n      ready: false,\\n      out: null,\\n      result: null,\\n      /** The last progress score the hub saw: the result of a player who never reports one. */\\n      progress: null,\\n210→      stats: null,\\n      awards: [],\\n      caps: null,\\n      hidden: null,\\n    }));\\n  const server = serverKey\\n    ? { id: seats.length, key: serverKey, slot: null, name: 'Server', color: null, hello: false, ready: false, out: null, result: null, progress: null, stats: null, awards: [], caps: null, hidden: null }\\n    : null;\\n  /** Every copy in the round: the players, then the server when there is one. */\\n  const copies = server ? [...seats, server] : seats;\\n220→  const byKey = new Map(copies.map((s) => [s.key, s]));\\n  const ids = seats.map((s) => s.id);\\n  const host = server ?? byKey.get(hostKey) ?? seats[0];\\n  const timers = new Set();\\n  const issues = [];\\n  let phase = 'loading';\\n  let goAt = null;\\n  let record = null;\\n  let released = !gate;\\n\\n230→  const later = (ms, fn) => {\\n    const handle = clock.setTimeout(() => {\\n      timers.delete(handle);\\n      fn();\\n    }, Math.max(0, ms));\\n    timers.add(handle);\\n    return handle;\\n  };\\n  const cancel = (handle) => {\\n    if (handle == null) return;\\n240→    clock.clearTimeout(handle);\\n    timers.delete(handle);\\n  };\\n\\n  /** The players still in the round. */\\n  const present = () => seats.filter((s) => !s.out);\\n  /** The copies still in the round: the players, and the server. */\\n  const presentCopies = () => copies.filter((s) => !s.out);\\n  const selfReported = () => SELF_REPORTED.includes(mode);\\n  const needsHost = () => !selfReported();\\n250→  const send = (seat, msg) => deliver(seat.key, { round, ...msg });\\n  const toPresent = (msg, except = null) => {\\n    for (const s of presentCopies()) if (s !== except && s.hello) send(s, msg);\\n  };\\n  const issue = (seat, problem) => {\\n    issues.push({ key: seat?.key ?? null, id: seat?.id ?? null, problem });\\n    status();\\n  };\\n\\n  function status() {\\n260→    onStatus({\\n      round,\\n      phase,\\n      mode,\\n      host: host.id,\\n      goAt,\\n      gate,\\n      released,\\n      players: seats.map((s) => ({\\n        id: s.id,\\n270→        key: s.key,\\n        slot: s.slot,\\n        name: s.name,\\n        color: s.color,\\n        hello: s.hello,\\n        ready: s.ready,\\n        out: s.out,\\n        result: s.result,\\n        client: s.caps?.client ?? null,\\n      })),\",\"content_concise\":\"180→  round,\\n  players,\\n  hostKey,\\n  mode = null,\\n  seed,\\n  limitMs,\\n  clock = REAL_CLOCK,\\n  deliver,\\n  onStatus = () => {},\\n  onEnd = () => {},\\n190→  timings = TIMINGS,\\n  gate = false,\\n  serverKey = null,\\n}) {\\n  mode = modeOf(mode);\\n  const t = { ...TIMINGS, ...timings };\\n  const seats = [...players]\\n    .sort((a, b) => a.slot - b.slot)\\n    .map((p, id) => ({\\n      id,\\n200→      key: p.key,\\n      slot: p.slot,\\n      name: p.name,\\n      color: SLOT_COLORS[p.slot % SLOT_COLORS.length],\\n      hello: false,\\n      ready: false,\\n      out: null,\\n      result: null,\\n      /** The last progress score the hub saw: the result of a player who never reports one. */