{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_488","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"HTML packed successfully at 11.6 MB.\n\nNext steps include verifying the packed HTML structure and hub server setup. The HTML contains a colon in its filename. I will check for banned names inside the embedded WASM binary. Remaining tasks are running hub tests, launching and screenshotting, balance, exit-interview.json, deleting target directories, and updating the plan checklist.\n\nTrauma Center is allowed as a source attribution. Banned names must not appear in the story text. I will copy the HTML into tests/hub rather than symlink it.\n\nA symlink is fine because Python http.server follows symlinks by default. The game filename must be URL-encoded for the query parameter. I will write a Python script to start the server and run Playwright hub tests with xvfb-run, using PLAYWRIGHT_HOST_PLATFORM_OVERRIDE=ubuntu24.04-x64.\n\nChromium will be launched with WebGPU arguments. Four concurrent WebGPU contexts may exhaust memory, so tests will run sequentially in one browser, closing pages between scenarios. Each scenario needs roughly ninety seconds, totaling about six minutes for all four plus the two-page and solo tests. A structural check of the HTML comes first, followed by copying the file and running the hub script. requestAnimationFrame should work inside an iframe, but a potential bug with WASM and WebGPU in an iframe still needs verification.\n\nI will symlink the packed HTML into tests/hub as harbor.html. This avoids colon characters in the URL and keeps the filename short.\n\nThe symlink will preserve the original HTML filename in tests/hub. This avoids URL encoding and matches the verifier's expected path. The relative path from tests/hub to the work root is ../../.., which I will verify with Python realpath after linking.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-9cd68792-cedb-4606-b43a-63e84abc3c50-83","name":"run_terminal_command","input":{"command":"python3 - << 'PY'\nfrom pathlib import Path\np = Path(\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224015__x42677a/work/Hands of Harbor: Second Opinion-Trauma Center: Second Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-224015.html\")\ntext = p.read_text(encoding=\"utf-8\", errors=\"replace\")\nprint(\"size\", p.stat().st_size)\nprint(\"title\", \"Hands of Harbor: Second Opinion\" in text)\ni = text.find(\"<script\")\nprint(\"first script at\", i)\nprint(text[i:i+80].replace(\"\\n\",\" \"))\nprint(\"session banner\", \"aihub-session\" in text[: text.find(\"</script>\")+20])\nprint(\"about-data\", 'id=\"about-data\"' in text)\nprint(\"hub session meta\", 'hub:session' in text)\nprint(\"shim __hub\", \"window.__hub\" in text)\n# banned in the html text outside base64? search early head only\nhead = text[:8000]\nfor w in [\"Hope Hospital\", \"Caduceus\", \"Stiles\", \"GUILT\", \"Healing Touch\"]:\n    print(w, w in head)\nprint(\"usage\", \"added on import\" in text[:20000])\nPY","description":"Check packed HTML hub injection and title"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":8973,"output_tokens":1320,"cache_read_input_tokens":138368,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa38-de6f-7dc0-ae0d-e0f717ed75f2","uuid":"67e3eaca-196c-4e1c-81e9-62692d52a6ad"}
