{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_489","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Proceeding to symlink and start hub tests.\n\nWriting a Playwright script to run the hub tests. It will use xvfb-run with the exact GPU flags from the plan. The server will start in tests/hub.\n\nThe local HTTP server will run on a random port. The test URL will be built with urllib.parse.quote to encode the game filename.\n\nThe viewport will be 800x600 to reduce GPU memory. Each scenario gets a 120-second timeout. The two-page test will run separately from conformance so one failure does not hide the other. All output goes to hub.txt.\n\nThe two-page test will use the harness with auto=0 and players=2. The two copies are the host and client iframes inside one page, not separate browser tabs. The plan is to load the page with a game set, click New round, then drive keys into the client iframe and read status from both.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-8a4a545e-64fb-4460-bbb7-727d59f24ea8-84","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224015__x42677a/work/Hands of Harbor: Second Opinion-Trauma Center: Second Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-224015/tests/hub/harness.html","offset":360,"limit":45}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1433,"output_tokens":862,"cache_read_input_tokens":147328,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa38-de6f-7dc0-ae0d-e0f717ed75f2","uuid":"49988b14-97c2-4fcb-a8e4-854587d77d66"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-8a4a545e-64fb-4460-bbb7-727d59f24ea8-84","content":"{\"type\":\"ReadFile\",\"FileContent\":{\"content\":\"360→$('restart').onclick = () => newRound();\\n$('release').onclick = () => releaseRound();\\n$('timeup').onclick = () => current?.coordinator.timeUp();\\n$('remove').onclick = () => {\\n  const cell = current?.cells.find((c) => c.key === $('who').value);\\n  if (cell) removeCell(cell);\\n};\\n$('hide').onclick = () => {\\n  if (!current) return;\\n  current.hidden = !current.hidden;\\n370→  $('hide').setAttribute('aria-pressed', String(current.hidden));\\n  (current.cells.find((c) => c.server) ?? current.cells[0])?.bridge.visibility(current.hidden);\\n  log(`host tab ${current.hidden ? 'hidden' : 'shown'}`);\\n};\\nfor (const id of ['latency', 'jitter', 'loss']) $(id).onchange = applyNet;\\n\\n/* ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\\n * ?auto=1 — the conformance run. It presses keys inside each frame with\\n * synthetic events while the round plays (the frames must be served from this\\n * page's origin). Results land in window.__hubCheck, and body[data-complete]\\n380→ * turns \\\"true\\\".\\n * ------------------------------------------------------------------------- */\\n\\nconst sleep = (ms) => new Promise((r) => setTimeout(r, ms));\\nasync function until(test, ms) {\\n  const end = performance.now() + ms;\\n  while (performance.now() < end) {\\n    if (test()) return true;\\n    await sleep(50);\\n  }\\n390→  return test();\\n}\\n\\nfunction poke(cell, key) {\\n  const doc = cell.frame.contentDocument;\\n  const win = cell.frame.contentWindow;\\n  if (!doc || !win) return false;\\n  const target = doc.activeElement && doc.activeElement !== doc.documentElement ? doc.activeElement : doc.body || doc.documentElement;\\n  const init = { key, code: key === ' ' ? 'Space' : key, bubbles: true, cancelable: true, view: win };\\n  target.dispatchEvent(new win.KeyboardEvent('keydown', init));\\n400→  setTimeout(() => target.dispatchEvent(new win.KeyboardEvent('keyup', init)), 120);\\n  return true;\\n}\\n\\nasync function conformance() {\",\"content_concise\":\"360→$('restart').onclick = () => newRound();\\n$('release').onclick = () => releaseRound();\\n$('timeup').onclick = () => current?.coordinator.timeUp();\\n$('remove').onclick = () => {\\n  const cell = current?.cells.find((c) => c.key === $('who').value);\\n  if (cell) removeCell(cell);\\n};\\n$('hide').onclick = () => {\\n  if (!current) return;\\n  current.hidden = !current.hidden;\\n370→  $('hide').setAttribute('aria-pressed', String(current.hidden));\\n  (current.cells.find((c) => c.server) ?? current.cells[0])?.bridge.visibility(current.hidden);\\n  log(`host tab ${current.hidden ? 'hidden' : 'shown'}`);\\n};\\nfor (const id of ['latency', 'jitter', 'loss']) $(id).onchange = applyNet;\\n\\n/* ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\\n * ?auto=1 — the conformance run. It presses keys inside each frame with\\n * synthetic events while the round plays (the frames must be served from this\\n * page's origin). Results land in window.__hubCheck, and body[data-complete]\\n380→ * turns \\\"true\\\".\\n * ------------------------------------------------------------------------- */\\n\\nconst sleep = (ms) => new Promise((r) => setTimeout(r, ms));\\nasync function until(test, ms) {\\n  const end = performance.now() + ms;\\n  while (performance.now() < end) {\\n    if (test()) return true;\\n    await sleep(50);\\n  }\\n390→  return test();\\n}\\n\\nfunction poke(cell, key) {\\n  const doc = cell.frame.contentDocument;\\n  const win = cell.frame.contentWindow;\\n  if (!doc || !win) return false;\\n  const target = doc.activeElement && doc.activeElement !== doc.documentElement ? doc.activeElement : doc.body || doc.documentElement;\\n  const init = { key, code: key === ' ' ? 'Space' : key, bubbles: true, cancelable