01,97,115,101,100,40,41,32,123,10,53,50,51,58,32,32,32,32,32,32,114,101,116,117,114,110,32,114,101,108,101,97,115,101,100,59,10,60,47,119,111,114,107,115,112,97,99,101,95,114,101,115,117,108,116,62],\"stderr\":[],\"exit_code\":0,\"match_count\":8,\"file_matches\":[{\"path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224015__x42677a/work/Hands of Harbor: Second Opinion-Trauma Center: Second Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-224015/tests/hub/round.js\",\"matches\":[{\"line_number\":228,\"content\":\"  let released = !gate;\"},{\"line_number\":267,\"content\":\"      released,\"},{\"line_number\":319,\"content\":\"      if (released && presentCopies().every((s) => s.ready)) begin();\"},{\"line_number\":492,\"content\":\"  function release() {\"},{\"line_number\":493,\"content\":\"    if (released || phase !== 'loading') return;\"},{\"line_number\":494,\"content\":\"    released = true;\"},{\"line_number\":522,\"content\":\"    get released() {\"},{\"line_number\":523,\"content\":\"      return released;\"}]}]}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa38-de6f-7dc0-ae0d-e0f717ed75f2","uuid":"1115b9d2-ef99-4a69-a954-d1b23e816372"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_493","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"A gate set to true means the released flag starts as false.\n\nRounds wait for release() and all players to be ready. Conformance calls releaseRound after entering answers, which sets released=true and begins settling if everyone is ready. Card answers are only needed for the conformance check, not round start. Next steps are writing the test script and starting the server. I also need to verify that instrument() wraps alerts before iframe scripts run, and check whether gilrs throws on WASM due to gamepad API issues.\n\nI'll start with players=1 to verify the game boots in the harness before scaling up. The script will use one browser with a fresh page per scenario, closing each page afterward to limit memory. A 90-second timeout should cover WASM unpacking and readiness. I'll also pipe page console output into the scratch log for easier debugging.\n\nPlaywright must launch Chromium with headless=False under xvfb-run. Headless mode may not support WebGPU correctly. The PLAYWRIGHT_HOST_PLATFORM_OVERRIDE environment variable must be set to ubuntu24.04-x64. The --disable-gpu flag should be avoided.\n\nI'll try the plan's exact Chromium flags first, adding ignore-gpu-blocklist only if WebGPU fails. The script will run all four player counts sequentially and exit immediately on the first failure.\n\nI'll run the single-player test first as a standalone command, then proceed to the remaining scenarios only if it passes. I'll copy about.json into exit-interview.json now and verify its contents against the HTML's embedded about-data. The hub symlink will point to the game's HTML file.\n\nThe server will run in the background from tests/hub with python3 -u so the port line appears immediately. A curl check will verify the game file is reachable.\n\nThe server must be fully up before the test script starts. I also need to verify that requestAnimationFrame works correctly inside an iframe, since the app loop likely uses winit. saw_card should set mode 7 immediately when the hub is active, which hides the title inside the hub. I will test the title visibility outside the session too. Page errors from history.replaceState and AudioContext initialization are additional failure modes to watch for.\n\ngilrs on WASM will only log errors if no gamepad is present, not as a window error. I verified the send_json call signature matches its shim: the body is parsed with JSON.parse and sent without an explicit recipient, so it broadcasts correctly. I also confirmed that host send_snap during play routes through client send_input.\n\nI estimated that snap payloads stay well under the 1400-byte limit. Code blue spawns roughly 600 characters, and event cues are small. I also verified that `flag(&hub, \"active\")` uses `as_bool()` correctly, and that JSON fields like `info`, `seed`, and `me` serialize properly. I still need to confirm the WASM Link is used.\n\nThe WASM Link is confirmed available through the js module. On wasm, exec runs synchronously and boot_hub_round is reached correctly. The paused simulation state during the card phase is safe because the mode switches before the frame pump begins. Play starts with the operation mode set once boot completes.\n\nI checked the attract timer timing. If WASM loads slowly, the shell's first frame occurs when wasm actually starts, not when the page loads. The idle timer begins at that first frame, and saw_card sets mode 7 immediately because H.active is true from the start.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-e6344b9b-e51c-4bfe-88bd-b05ad5414261-90","name":"grep","input":{"pattern":"attract|idle","path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224015__x42677a/work/engine-link/crates/pav_ui/src/surgery/mod.rs"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1545,"output_tokens":1952,"cache_read_input_tokens":152064,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa38-de6f-7dc0-ae0d-e0f717ed75f2","uuid":"b774cb2f-68b3-4b69-9fd2-e4685fe4985b"}
