{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_502","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The probe ended after 9 seconds because the loop only ran 18 iterations of 500ms each. Player 1 was ready at that exact moment.\n\nThe second copy's WASM took about 9 seconds to start because two WebGPU contexts were created. The single-player test finished with a traffic waiver and zero sent cards, but it is still unclear whether snaps are sent during play. A longer wait is needed for the two-player case.\n\nFour copies might exceed the 20-second ready timeout. The probe will be extended to 90 seconds to complete a full two-player test and capture sent and received data. The required four-player latency query remains outstanding.\n\nThe two-player auto test will use a 120-second timeout to verify traffic. If no cards are sent during a completed round, the sending logic needs fixing.\n\nHost status during card mode shows timer 0.0 and vitals 80. The boot code normally sets vitals to 70 and timer to 240. The zero timer likely occurs because saw_card only sets mode and case_id without invoking boot_code. This is acceptable before boot.\n\nboot_hub_round calls boot_code to set the timer and vitals once play begins. The two-player auto test will run with a 120-second timeout and print traffic numbers. The host sends snaps immediately at round start, and the client sends input. If this passes, the harder tests will follow.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-0a208830-3b0f-414e-9c94-08dcc4a64895-99","name":"search_replace","input":{"file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224015__x42677a/tmp/grok-goal-907ccca5ce3b/implementer/hub_one.py","old_string":"import json\nimport os\nfrom urllib.parse import quote","new_string":"import json\nimport os\nimport sys\nfrom urllib.parse import quote"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-0a208830-3b0f-414e-9c94-08dcc4a64895-100","name":"search_replace","inpu