{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_504","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Finish worked with the fallback OR publish.\n\nAIHub.send was never called because sent is 0. Publish requires hub.play to run, which it did not.\n\nsend_snap also requires self.play. If the message body exceeds 1400 bytes, send_snap may return early without sending while publish still runs. This would explain the real standings in H.last with sent remaining zero.\n\nI need to measure the actual snap size. I am checking SurgeryFrame hazards and to_frame for oversized data. The JSON only includes cue IDs, so the payload should be small.\n\nThe fallback standings also produce [[0,1]], so the presence of H.last does not prove publish ran. The play flags are identical, ruling out a mismatch between send_snap and publish. Since sent is zero, send() was never called.\n\nThe card status showed the game was running, yet Rust never published or sent. This points to play staying false, op being None during play, or the loop stopping before play began. The finish output of [[0,1]] with zero sends is exactly the fallback path.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-26ee54fc-57a1-4c6d-9f8e-3614852cd2d6-103","name":"search_replace","input":{"file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224015__x42677a/tmp/grok-goal-907ccca5ce3b/implementer/hub_probe.py","old_string":"        for i in range(18):\n            page.wait_for_timeout(500)","new_string":"        for i in range(40):\n            page.wait_for_timeout(500)"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2140,"output_tokens":966,"cache_read_input_tokens":173696,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa38-de6f-7dc0-ae0d-e0f717ed75f2","uuid":"979e1581-b4bf-4f66-8fac-4f7af203250a"}
