sh(serde_json::json!([\\n            i,\\n            (c.x * 100.0).round() / 100.0,\\n            (c.z * 100.0).round() / 100.0,\\n            c.tool,\\n            if c.active { 1 } else { 0 },\\n            c.score\\n        ]));\\n    }\\n    let mut cues = Vec::new();\\n    for e in events.iter().rev().take(8) {\\n        if let pav_core::SimEvent::Cue { id, .. } = e {\\n            cues.push(*id);\\n        }\\n    }\\n    serde_json::json!({\\n        \\\"k\\\": \\\"s\\\",\\n        \\\"v\\\": (op.vitals * 10.0).round() / 10.0,\\n        \\\"b\\\": op.bpm.round(),\\n        \\\"p\\\": (op.phase * 100.0).round() / 100.0,\\n        \\\"f\\\": if op.flat { 1 } else { 0 },\\n        \\\"tm\\\": (op.timer * 10.0).round() / 10.0,\\n        \\\"cd\\\": (op.code_t * 10.0).round() / 10.0,\\n        \\\"h\\\": hazards,\\n        \\\"u\\\": cursors,\\n        \\\"q\\\": cues,\\n    })\\n    .to_string()\\n}\\n\\nfn standings_json(present: &[u8], op: &SurgeryFrame) -> String {\\n    let ids: Vec<u8> = if present.is_empty() { vec![0] } else { present.to_vec() };\\n    let mut scores = serde_json::Map::new();\\n    for id in &ids {\\n        let score = op.cursors.get(*id as usize).map(|c| c.score).unwrap_or(0);\\n        scores.insert(id.to_string(), serde_json::json!(score));\\n    }\\n    serde_json::json!({\\n        \\\"standings\\\": [ids],\\n        \\\"won\\\": op.vitals > 0.0,\\n        \\\"scores\\\": scores,\\n    })\\n    .to_string()\\n}\\n\\nfn status_json(shell: &Shell, op: Option<&SurgeryFrame>) -> String {\\n    let music = op.map(|o| o.music).unwrap_or(0.10);\\n    let cursors: Vec<serde_json::Value> = op\\n        .map(|o| {\\n            o.cursors\\n                .iter()\\n                .map(|c| serde_json::json!({ \\\"x\\\": c.x, \\\"z\\\": c.z, \\\"tool\\\": c.tool, \\\"active\\\": c.active }))\\n                .collect()\\n        })\\n        .unwrap_or_default();\\n    serde_json::json!({\\n        \\\"screen\\\": shell.screen_name(),\\n        \\\"focus\\\": shell.focus(),\\n        \\\"device\\\": if shell.device == DeviceKind::Gamepad { \\\"gamepad\\\" } else { \\\"keyboard\\\" },\\n        \\\"xbox\\\": shell.xbox,\\n        \\\"music\\\": format!(\\\"{music:.2}\\\"),\\n        \\\"title\\\": TITLE,\\n        \\\"cursors\\\": cursors,\\n        \\\"vitals\\\": op.map(|o| o.vitals),\\n        \\\"bpm\\\": op.map(|o| o.bpm),\\n        \\\"timer\\\": op.map(|o| o.timer),\\n        \\\"mode\\\": op.map(|o| o.mode),\\n    })\\n    .to_string()\\n}\\n\\nfn publish_status(s: &str) {\\n    STATUS.with(|c| *c.borrow_mut() = s.to_string());\\n}\\n\\nthread_local! {\\n    static STATUS: RefCell<String> = const { RefCell::new(String::new()) };\\n    static BURST: Cell<u32> = const { Cell::new(0) };\\n    static HOOKED: Cell<bool> = const { Cell::new(false) };\\n}\\n\\n#[cfg(target_arch = \\\"wasm32\\\")]\\nfn drain_hook(app: &mut App) {\\n    let n = BURST.with(|b| b.replace(0));\\n\",\"total_lines\":883}}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa38-de6f-7dc0-ae0d-e0f717ed75f2","uuid":"a7a83560-3cba-4ed1-b978-9c48431360dc"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_524","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"A critical bug needs to be examined.\n\nsend_input does not check self.host. The host only reaches it through send_snap, so this is safe.\n\nsend_snap is safe too. It returns early if !self.play, so snaps are not sent before the game starts.\n\nSnap payloads are small enough at roughly 400–800 bytes, well under the 1400-byte limit. If hub_quiet skips the mesh, frames should continue advancing.\n\nThe two-page cursor test still needs ongoing frames to confirm the stall. The previous theory that the full operative mesh stalls the iframe after one frame is being reconsidered. Setting hub_quiet only suppresses rendering output, not the simulation itself. If the stall persists, the bottleneck likely lies in view building rather than simulation.\n\nThe egui HUD, cursor hiding, and audio startup might be stalling the loop. The quiet view path needs inspection to confirm it skips mesh building entirely. A requestAnimationFrame issue is also being considered. The prior full-plate test left the wasm loop alive but pubN remained stuck at one.\n\nThe iframe JavaScript thread was not blocked inside WASM. The frame callback returned, but subsequent frames were never scheduled. This points to either a missing requestAnimationFrame call or browser throttling because the iframe is hidden or backgrounded. The fact that about_to_wait always requests redraw makes this puzzling.\n\nThe winit event loop and about_to_wait in app.rs need inspection. ControlFlow::Poll should keep the loop spinning, but a ControlFlow::Wait state might be set without requesting redraw. Chrome may throttle Playwright iframes when they are not focused. The card frames rendered normally before switching to the operative mode, which suggests the stall is specific to that transition rather than a general iframe throttle.\n\nThe operative frame itself is now the prime suspect. The frame callback returned, so the stall likely happens after it finishes. A hidden panic or a device-lost error during the heavy draw are being considered. A cursor visibility change is unlikely.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-4e4ac967-e5c4-4a5a-9ab2-8b188da9578e-13","name":"grep","input":{"pattern":"quiet","glob":"**/pav_view/**/*.rs"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-4e4ac967-e5c4-4a5a-9ab2-8b188da9578e-14","name":"grep","input":{"pattern":"request_redraw|ControlFlow|about_to_wait","glob":"**/pav_app/src/app.rs"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":4766,"output_tokens":1301,"cache_read_input_tokens":44928,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa38-de6f-7dc0-ae0d-e0f717ed75f2","uuid":"77f58277-2676-4e74-a41d-00b8587373bc"}
