{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_537","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Reading the pump() function around line 204 and its paused logic.\n\nRealized the shell's paused flag might keep the hub paused. The first tick likely happened before set_control applied the pause, since surgery_frame sets control then pumps.\n\nThe timer discrepancy suggests a step occurred before the pause took effect. If note_mode sets shell.paused after pump, the next frame would freeze. send_snap still runs even when paused.\n\nOnly two sends occurred, so frames with real delta time are rare. The large rAF schedule count suggests callbacks may not be executing. I will add separate counters to track scheduled calls versus actual runs.\n\nI will wrap requestAnimationFrame to count scheduled calls and actual runs. If the run counter stays small while scheduling is huge, the callbacks are not executing. I also plan to monitor game status changes by periodically checking a frame counter on the page.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-5bc74825-2c98-49b0-91c5-0b89db01ba0b-39","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224015__x42677a/work/Hands of Harbor: Second Opinion-Trauma Center: Second Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-224015/engine/crates/pav_app/src/simhost.rs","offset":180,"limit":220}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-5bc74825-2c98-49b0-91c5-0b89db01ba0b-40","name":"grep","input":{"pattern":"fn paused|paused:","glob":"**/pav_ui/src/surgery/**/*.rs"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":4475,"output_tokens":846,"cache_read_input_tokens":78464,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa38-de6f-7dc0-ae0d-e0f717ed75f2","uuid":"ee1e9de3-861f-4e10-8410-e567ca6f089c"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-5bc74825-2c98-49b0-91c5-0b89db01ba0b-39","content":"{\"type\":\"ReadFile\",\"FileContent\":{\"content\":\"180→        let dt = sim.dt();\\n        publish(&mut sim, &self.shared, dt, Instant::now());\\n        Some(r)\\n    }\\n\\n    /// Runs `n` ticks immediately. The first keeps button edges; the rest see holds only.\\n    pub fn burst(&self, n: u32) {\\n        let mut sim = self.sim.borrow_mut();\\n        let mut input = *self.shared.input.lock().unwrap();\\n        for i in 0..n.min(240) {\\n190→            sim.step(&input);\\n            if i == 0 {\\n                input.pressed = 0;\\n                input.surgery_cmd = None;\\n                for s in &mut input.surgeons {\\n                    s.pressed = 0;\\n                }\\n            }\\n            let dt = sim.dt();\\n            publish(&mut sim, &self.shared, dt, Instant::now());\\n200→        }\\n    }\\n\\n    /// Runs the ticks that are due (called once per frame).\\n    pub fn pump(&self) {\\n        self.clock.borrow_mut().advance(&mut self.sim.borrow_mut(), &self.shared);\\n    }\\n}\\n\\nimpl SimHost {\\n210→    pub fn frames(&self) -> (Arc<RenderFrame>, Arc<RenderFrame>, Instant, f32) {\\n        let f = self.shared.frames.lock().unwrap();\\n        (f.prev.clone(), f.curr.clone(), f.curr_at, f.tick_wall)\\n    }\\n\\n    pub fn control(&self) -> TimeControl {\\n        *self.shared.control.lock().unwrap()\\n    }\\n\\n    pub fn set_control(&self, f: impl FnOnce(&mut TimeControl)) {\\n220→        f(&mut self.shared.control.lock().unwrap());\\n    }\\n}\\n\\n#[cfg(not(target_arch = \\\"wasm32\\\"))]\\nimpl Drop for SimHost {\\n    fn drop(&mut self) {\\n        let _ = self.tx.send(Cmd::Quit);\\n        if let Some(t) = self.thread.take() {\\n            let _ = t.join();\\n230→        }\\n    }\\n}\\n\\nfn publish(sim: &mut Sim, sh: &Shared, tick_wall: f32, at: Instant) {\\n    let events = sim.drain_events();\\n    if !events.is_empty() {\\n        let mut q = sh.events.lock().unwrap();\\n        q.extend(events);\\n        let n = q.len();\\n240→        if n > 512 {\\n            q.drain(..n - 512);\\n        }\\n    }\\n    let frame = Arc::new(sim.frame());\\n    let mut f = sh.frames.lock().unwrap();\\n    f.prev = std::mem::replace(&mut f.curr, frame);\\n    f.curr_at = at;\\n    f.tick_wall = tick_wall;\\n}\\n250→\\n/// Fixed-rate ticking with time controls (pause, single steps, speed, rewind, scrubbing).\\nstruct Clock {\\n    next: Instant,\\n    window_start: Instant,\\n    window_ticks: u32,\\n    busy: Duration,\\n    rewound: bool,\\n    studio_mode: pav_core::prop_preview::StudioMode,\\n}\\n260→\\nimpl Clock {\\n    fn new() -> Self {\\n        Self {\\n            next: Instant::now(),\\n            window_start: Instant::now(),\\n            window_ticks: 0,\\n            busy: Duration::ZERO,\\n            rewound: false,\\n            studio_mode: pav_core::prop_preview::StudioMode::World,\\n270→        }\\n    }\\n\\n    /// Runs whatever is due now; returns how long until the next tick.\\n    fn advance(&mut self, sim: &mut Sim, sh: &Shared) -> Duration {\\n        let previewing = sim.studio_active();\\n        let mode = sim.studio_mode();\\n        if self.studio_mode != mode {\\n            self.studio_mode = mode;\\n            self.next = Instant::now();\\n280→        }\\n        let ctl = *sh.control.lock().unwrap();\\n        // The animation stage has its own play, pause and speed controls. The world's time\\n        // controls stay untouched, including a paused or rewound game behind the stage.\\n        let tick_wall = if previewing { sim.dt() } else { sim.dt() / ctl.speed.clamp(0.01, 16.0) };\\n        let (busy, window_ticks) = (&mut self.busy, &mut self.window_ticks);\\n        let mut tick_once = |sim: &mut Sim, at: Instant| {\\n            let input = if previewing {\\n                InputFrame::default()\\n            } else {\\n290→                let mut i = sh.input.lock().unwrap();\\n                let mut frame = *i;\\n                i.pressed = 0;\\n                i.surgery_cmd = None;\\n                for s in &mut i.surgeons {\\n                    s.pressed = 0;\\n                }\\n                frame.cmd = sh.cmds.lock().unwrap().pop_front();\\n                frame\\n            };\\n300→            let stamp = if previewing { None } else { sh.input_stamp.lock().unwrap().take() };\\n            let t = Instant::now();\\n            sim.step(&input);\\n            *busy += t.elapsed();\\n            if let Some(s) = stamp {\\n                *sh.latency_probe.lock().unwrap() = Some((s, Instant::now(), sim.state.tick));\\n            }\\n            *window_ticks += 1;\\n            publish(sim, sh, tick_wall, at);\\n        };\\n310→\\n        let now = Instant::now();\\n        if previewing {\\n            let mut n = 0;\\n            while now >= self.next && n < 8 {\\n                self.next += Duration::from_secs_f32(tick_wall);\\n                tick_once(sim, self.next);\\n                n += 1;\\n            }\\n            if n == 8 && now > self.next {\\n320→                self.next = now;\\n            }\\n        } else if ctl.rewinding {\\n            if now >= self.next {\\n                self.next = now + Duration::from_secs_f32(sim.dt());\\n                let oldest = sim.history.oldest_tick().unwrap_or(sim.state.tick);\\n                let target = sim.state.tick.saturating_sub(ctl.rewind_speed.max(1) as u64).max(oldest);\\n                if target < sim.state.tick && sim.rewind_to(target) {\\n                    self.rewound = true;\\n                }\\n330→                let dt = sim.dt();\\n                publish(sim, sh, dt, now);\\n            }\\n        } else if let Some(t) = ctl.scrub {\\n            sh.control.lock().unwrap().scrub = None;\\n            if sim.rewind_to(t) {\\n                self.rewound = true;\\n            }\\n            let dt = sim.dt();\\n            publish(sim, sh, dt, now);\\n340→            self.next = now;\\n        } else if ctl.paused {\\n            if ctl.step_requests > 0 {\\n                sh.control.lock().unwrap().step_requests -= 1;\\n                if self.rewound {\\n                    sim.commit_rewind();\\n                    self.rewound = false;\\n                }\\n                tick_once(sim, now);\\n            }\\n350→            self.next = now;\\n        } else {\\n            if self.rewound {\\n                // Acting after a rewind starts a new timeline.\\n                sim.commit_rewind();\\n                self.rewound = false;\\n                self.next = now;\\n            }\\n            let mut n = 0;\\n            while now >= self.next && n < 8 {\\n360→                self.next += Duration::from_secs_f32(tick_wall);\\n                tick_once(sim, self.next);\\n                n += 1;\\n            }\\n            if n == 8 && now > self.next {\\n                self.next = now; // too far behind: drop time instead of spiralling\\n            }\\n        }\\n\\n        let elapsed = self.window_start.elapsed();\\n370→        if elapsed >= Duration::from_millis(500) {\\n            let mut s = sh.stats.lock().unwrap();\\n            s.tps = self.window_ticks as f32 / elapsed.as_secs_f32();\\n            s.tick_ms = if self.window_ticks > 0 { self.busy.as_secs_f32() * 1000.0 / self.window_ticks as f32 } else { 0.0 };\\n            s.tick = sim.state.tick;\\n            s.entities = sim.state.entities.len();\\n            s.oldest = sim.history.oldest_tick().unwrap_or(sim.state.tick);\\n            s.newest = sim.history.newest_tick().unwrap_or(sim.state.tick).max(sim.state.tick);\\n            s.history_mb = sim.history.approx_bytes() as f32 / 1.0e6;\\n            s.rewound = self.rewound;\\n380→            self.window_start = Instant::now();\\n            self.window_ticks = 0;\\n            self.busy = Durat