r.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/API/Window/requestIdleCallback\\n    /// [`setTimeout()`]: https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/API/setTimeout\\n    IdleCallback,\\n    /// Uses the [Prioritized Task Scheduling API] to queue the next event loop. If not available\\n    /// this will fallback to [`setTimeout()`].\\n    ///\\n    /// This strategy will run as fast as possible without disturbing users from interacting with\\n    /// the page and is not affected by browser throttling.\\n    ///\\n    /// This is the default strategy.\\n    ///\\n    /// [Prioritized Task Scheduling API]: https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/API/Prioritized_Task_Scheduling_API\\n    /// [`setTimeout()`]: https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/API/setTimeout\\n    #[default]\\n\",\"total_lines\":465}}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa38-de6f-7dc0-ae0d-e0f717ed75f2","uuid":"0e8ea747-87b2-4749-8722-0feafad281d6"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_543","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The bug is in AnimationFrameHandler::request().\n\nrequest() cancels the previous animation frame before scheduling a new one. ControlFlow::Poll also schedules a new poll on every apply_control_flow call.\n\nabout_to_wait calls request_redraw, which also cancels the previous animation frame. This creates a tight loop where each frame cancels the next.\n\nThe logs show 345,000 request() calls and only 10 actual callbacks. This indicates a synchronous loop is repeatedly cancelling the previous animation frame before the browser can run any callback.\n\nThe synchronous loop likely stems from PollStrategy running as a microtask or immediate queueMicrotask. Each poll processes events, schedules a redraw that cancels the previous animation frame, and then queues another immediate task. This creates an endless chain of cancellations before the browser can ever run a callback.\n\nThe animation frame is cancelled before the browser can paint. Poll tasks run via scheduler.postTask as fast as possible, which explains why scheduling far exceeds actual callback execution.\n\nThe card still appears to work because ready() runs on the task scheduler, not only on animation frames. However, simulation ticks rely on RedrawRequested, which is tied to the animation frame that keeps getting cancelled.\n\nThe exact failure chain is now clear. When a poll task runs, it drains any pending redraws and fires RedrawRequested synchronously inside the task. Then about_to_wait queues another redraw and schedules an animation frame. The next poll immediately cancels that animation frame before the browser can ever run it.\n\nIf postTask yields between tasks, the browser gets a chance to run. Each poll still fires surgery_frame and schedules an animation frame. Then the next poll runs before the browser can execute that frame, cancelling it and repeating the cycle.\n\nThe frozen timer during OP contradicts the theory that surgery_frame runs thousands of times per second. If it did, the operation clock would have hit zero within seconds. The timer stayed at 239.87 instead. This means surgery_frame did not keep running during OP. The card timer remaining at zero is consistent with the card mode staying locked at 7.\n\nThe scheduler kept climbing during OP, so polls continued running. This means surgery_frame was not hanging the GPU or blocking the task queue. The frozen timer instead suggests RedrawRequested is missing from the event queue, or that request_redraw sets a pending flag without actually enqueuing a redraw.\n\nThe scheduler is still climbing during OP, so polls continue and AboutToWait definitely fires. This means request_redraw runs every cycle. The next poll should process the pending redraw and call surgery_frame. The frozen timer during OP therefore cannot be explained by missing redraws or a blocked event loop.\n\nAnother possibility is that the simulation is paused. If paused, the timer freezes while status is republished with identical values. This would explain why the timer remained at 239.87 without any visible frame updates.\n\nThe snapshot count is only 2 over 5 seconds. If polls ran at 20,000 per second, send_snap would fire roughly 75 times. This proves surgery_frame is not executing at the poll rate during the play window. Either most polls do not include a redraw, or the frame delta is effectively zero.\n\nrequest_redraw likely sets a pending flag that only becomes an actual redraw event when the animation frame callback finally fires. Because the browser cancels every scheduled animation frame before it can run, that flag never flushes into the event queue. The ten recorded callbacks are therefore the rare exceptions where an animation frame actually survives. This explains why the scheduler climbs to 345,000 while only ten redraws occur.\n\nThe card works because ready() only needs to run once inside surgery_frame. The card answers via JavaScript keydown, not Rust. During play, the next surviving callback boots and ticks eight times to catch up on wall-clock time, sending one snapshot. After that it is cancelled again for seconds until another rare callback arrives.\n\nThe root cause is confirmed. ControlFlow::Poll combined with request_redraw's animation frame cancellation loop starves actual redraws, leaving the timer frozen at its first catch-up value.\n\nThe fix is to stop using ControlFlow::Poll on wasm for surgery frames. Switching to ControlFlow::Wait and requesting a redraw once per frame should allow the browser to actually paint.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-58449fc9-125f-4156-8119-1530d8902665-52","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/.cargo/registry/src/index.crates.io-1949cf8c6b5b557f/winit-0.30.13/src/platform/web.rs","offset":317,"limit":80}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-58449fc9-125f-4156-8119-1530d8902665-53","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/.cargo/registry/src/index.crates.io-1949cf8c6b5b557f/winit-0.30.13/src/platform_impl/web/web_sys/canvas.rs","offset":430,"limit":50}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-58449fc9-125f-4156-8119-1530d8902665-54","name":"grep","input":{"pattern":"enum Schedule|fn new\\(|PollStrategy|request_animation_frame|postTask|setTimeout","path":"/home/micha/.cargo/registry/src/index.crates.io-1949cf8c6b5b557f/winit-0.30.13/src/platform_impl/web"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":4082,"output_tokens":2316,"cache_read_input_tokens":93056,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa38-de6f-7dc0-ae0d-e0f717ed75f2","uuid":"ed0a9aca-9b57-4657-b152-f6e8fb788da5"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-58449fc9-125f-4156-8119-1530d8902665-52","content":"{\"type\":\"ReadFile\",\"FileContent\":{\"content\":\"317→/// Strategy used for [`ControlFlow::Poll`][crate::event_loop::ControlFlow::Poll].\\n#[derive(Clone, Copy, Debug, Default, PartialEq, Eq)]\\npub enum PollStrategy {\\n320→    /// Uses [`Window.requestIdleCallback()`] to queue the next event loop. If not available\\n    /// this will fallback to [`setTimeout()`].\\n    ///\\n    /// This strategy will wait for the browser to enter an idle period before running and might\\n    /// be affected by browser throttling.\\n    ///\\n    /// [`Window.requestIdleCallback()`]: https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/API/Window/requestIdleCallback\\n    /// [`setTimeout()`]: https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/API/setTimeout\\n    IdleCallback,\\n    /// Uses the [Prioritized Task Scheduling API] to queue the next event loop. If not available\\n330→    /// this will fallback to [`setTimeout()`].\\n    ///\\n    /// This strategy will run as fast as possible without disturbing users from interacting with\\n    /// the page and is not affected by browser throttling.\\n    ///\\n    /// This is the default strategy.\\n    ///\\n    /// [Prioritized Task Scheduling API]: https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/API/Prioritized_Task_Scheduling_API\\n    /// [`setTimeout()`]: https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/API/setTimeout\\n    #[default]\\n340→    Scheduler,\\n}\\n\\n/// Strategy used for [`ControlFlow::WaitUntil`][crate::event_loop::ControlFlow::WaitUntil].\\n#[derive(Clone, Copy, Debug, Default, PartialEq, Eq)]\\npub enum WaitUntilStrategy {\\n    /// Uses the [Prioritized Task Scheduling API] to queue the next event loop. If not available\\n    /// this will fallback to [`setTimeout()`].\\n    ///\\n    /// This strategy is commonly not affected by browser throttling unless the window is not\\n350→    /// focused.\\n    ///\\n    /// This is the default strategy.\\n    ///\\n    /// [Prioritized Task Scheduling API]: https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/API/Prioritized_Task_Scheduling_API\\n    /// [`setTimeout()`]: https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/API/setTimeout\\n    #[default]\\n    Scheduler,\\n    /// Equal to [`Scheduler`][Self::Scheduler] but wakes up the event loop from a [worker].\\n    ///\\n360→    /// This strategy is commonly not affected by browser throttling regardless of window focus.\\n    ///\\n    /// [worker]: https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/API/Web_Workers_API\\n    Worker,\\n}\\n\\npub trait CustomCursorExtWebSys {\\n    /// Returns if this cursor is an animation.\\n    fn is_animation(&self) -> bool;\\n\\n370→    /// Creates a new cursor from a URL pointing to an image.\\n    /// It uses the [url css function](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/CSS/url),\\n    /// but browser support for image formats is inconsistent. Using [PNG] is recommended.\\n    ///\\n    /// [PNG]: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/PNG\\n    fn from_url(url: String, hotspot_x: u16, hotspot_y: u16) -> CustomCursorSource;\\n\\n    /// Crates a new animated cursor from multiple [`CustomCursor`]s.\\n    /// Supplied `cursors` can't be empty or other animations.\\n    fn from_animation(\\n380→        duration: Duration,\\n        cursors: Vec<CustomCursor>,\\n    ) -> Result<CustomCursorSource, BadAnimation>;\\n}\\n\\nimpl CustomCursorExtWebSys for CustomCursor {\\n    fn is_animation(&self) -> bool {\\n        self.inner.animation\\n    }\\n\\n390→    fn from_url(url: String, hotspot_x: u16, hotspot_y: u16) -> CustomCursorSource {\\n        CustomCursorSource { inner: PlatformCustomCursorSource::Url { url, hotspot_x, hotspot_y } }\\n    }\\n\\n    fn from_animation(\\n        duration: Duration,\\n        cursors: Vec<CustomCursor>,\",\"content_concise\":\"317→/// Strategy used for [`ControlFlow::Poll`][crate::event_loop::ControlFlow::Poll].\\n#[derive(Clone, Copy, Debug, Default, PartialEq, Eq)]\\npub enum PollStrategy {\\n320→    /// Uses [`Window.requestIdleCallback()`] to queue the next event loop. If not available\\n    /// this will fallback to [`setTimeout()`].\\n    ///\\n    /// This strategy will wait for the browser to enter an idle period before running and might\\n    /// be affected by browser throttling.\\n    ///\\n    /// [`Window.requestIdleCallback()`]: https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/API/Window/requestIdleCallback\\n    /// [`setTimeout()`]: https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/API/setTimeout\\n    IdleCallback,\\n    /// Uses the [Prioritized Task Scheduling API] to queue the next event loop. If not available\\n330→    /// this will fallback to [`setTimeout()`].\\n    ///\\n    /// This strategy will run as fast as possible without disturbing users from interacting with\\n    /// the page and is not affected by browser throttling.\\n    ///\\n    /// This is the default strategy.\\n    ///\\n    /// [Prioritized Task Scheduling API]: https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/API/Prioritized_Task_Scheduling_API\\n    /// [`setTimeout()`]: https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/API/setTimeout\\n    #[default]\\n340→    Scheduler,\\n}\\n\\n/// Strategy used for [`ControlFlow::WaitUntil`][crate::event_loop::ControlFlow::WaitUntil].\\n#[derive(Clone, Copy, Debug, Default, PartialEq, Eq)]\\npub enum WaitUntilStrategy {\\n    /// Uses the [Prioritized Task Scheduling API] to queue the next event loop. If not available\\n    /// this will fallback to [`setTimeout()`].\\n    ///\\n    /// This strategy is commonly not affected by browser throttling unless the window is not\\n350→    /// focused.\\n    ///\\n    /// This is the default strategy.\\n    ///\\n    /// [Prioritized Task Scheduling API]: https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/API/Prioritized_Task_Scheduling_API\\n    /// [`setTimeout()`]: https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/API/setTimeout\\n    #[default]\\n    Scheduler,\\n    /// Equal to [`Scheduler`][Self::Scheduler] but wakes up the event loop from a [worker].\\n    ///\\n360→    /// This strategy is commonly not affected by browser throttling regardless of window focus.\\n    ///\\n    /// [worker]: https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/API/Web_Workers_API\\n    Worker,\\n}\\n\\npub trait CustomCursorExtWebSys {\\n    /// Returns if this cursor is an animation.\\n    fn is_animation(&self) -> bool;\\n\\n370→    /// Creates a new cursor from a URL pointing to an image.\\n    /// It uses the [url css function](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/CSS/url),\\n    /// but browser support for image formats is inconsistent. Using [PNG] is recommended.\\n    ///\\n    /// [PNG]: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/PNG\\n    fn from_url(url: String, hotspot_x: u16, hotspot_y: u16) -> CustomCursorSource;\\n\\n    /// Crates a new animated cursor from multiple [`CustomCursor`]s.\\n    /// Supplied `cursors` can't be empty or other animations.\\n    fn from_animation(\\n380→        duration: Duration,\\n        cursors: Vec<CustomCursor>,\\n    ) -> Result<CustomCursorSource, BadAnimation>;\\n}\\n\\nimpl CustomCursorExtWebSys for CustomCursor {\\n    fn is_animation(&self) -> bool {\\n        self.inner.animation\\n    }\\n\\n390→    fn from_url(url: String, hotspot_x: u16, hotspot_y: u16) -> CustomCursorSource {\\n        CustomCursorSource { inner: PlatformCustomCursorSource::Url { url, hotspot_x, hotspot_y } }\\n    }\\n\\n    fn from_animation(\\n        duration: Duration,\\n        cursors: Vec<CustomCursor>,\",\"absolute_path\":\"/home/micha/.cargo/registry/src/index.crates.io-1949cf8c6b5b557f/winit-0.30.13/src/platform/web.rs\",\"offset\":317,\"limit\":80,\"raw_output\":\"/// Strategy used for [`ControlFlow::Poll`][crate::event_loop::ControlFlow::Poll].\\n#[derive(Clone, Copy, Debug, Default, PartialEq, Eq)]\\npub enum PollStrategy {\\n    /// Uses [`Window.requestIdleCallb