 title: &str) {\\n        self.canvas.borrow().set_attribute(\\\"alt\\\", title)\\n    }\\n\\n    pub fn set_transparent(&self, _transparent: bool) {}\\n\\n    pub fn set_blur(&self, _blur: bool) {}\\n\\n    pub fn set_visible(&self, _visible: bool) {\\n        // Intentionally a no-op\\n    }\\n\\n    #[inline]\\n    pub fn is_visible(&self) -> Option<bool> {\\n        None\\n    }\\n\\n    pub fn request_redraw(&self) {\\n        self.canvas.borrow().request_animation_frame();\\n    }\\n\\n    pub fn pre_present_notify(&self) {}\\n\\n    pub fn outer_position(&self) -> Result<PhysicalPosition<i32>, NotSupportedError> {\\n        Ok(self.canvas.borrow().position().to_physical(self.scale_factor()))\\n    }\\n\\n    pub fn inner_position(&self) -> Result<PhysicalPosition<i32>, NotSupportedError> {\\n        // Note: the canvas element has no window decorations, so this is equal to `outer_position`.\\n        self.outer_position()\\n    }\\n\\n    pub fn set_outer_position(&self, position: Position) {\\n        let canvas = self.canvas.borrow();\\n        let position = position.to_logical::<f64>(self.scale_factor());\\n\",\"total_lines\":477}}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa38-de6f-7dc0-ae0d-e0f717ed75f2","uuid":"1be56b9c-7ae6-4411-8b29-28072abb4ad6"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_545","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The mechanism is now fully understood.\n\n`request_redraw()` cancels the previous animation frame and schedules a new one. `about_to_wait` calls it on every poll iteration. `ControlFlow::Poll` uses `scheduler.postTask` with no delay, running as fast as possible. The loop fires `poll()` through `run_until_cleared`. A queued redraw may come from the rAF callback. I need to check whether `runner.request_redraw` or `window.request_redraw` is the source.\n\nThe animation frame callback calls `runner.request_redraw`, which queues a `RedrawRequested` event. `window.request_redraw` schedules the actual animation frame. `about_to_wait` cancels any pending rAF and reschedules it.\n\n`postTask` runs before the browser paints, so `about_to_wait` cancels every pending animation frame. Polls fire thousands of times per frame and never let it through. Only a handful of frames actually tick because the scheduler occasionally yields to rendering.\n\nThe card still functions because JavaScript handles Enter and ready() on the rare animation frames that slip through. Startup run reaches 4 quickly, then stays there for most of the 18-second trace; only a handful of rAFs fire overall. The first probe ticked eight times in catch-up after one of those rare frames, sent a snap, and then starvation resumed. The second rare frame sent the second message, so traffic checks passed with an upward and downward count.\n\nCursor and vitals would fail because the simulation stops ticking. The fix is to stop calling `request_redraw()` inside `about_to_wait` on WASM. Polling runs independently of the animation frame, so removing that cancel loop should let frames actually fire.\n\nThe first animation frame must be scheduled exactly once per frame, not on every poll. Changing ControlFlow to Wait on WASM is another option. The loop would then wait for events instead of postTask-spinning. The rAF would fire without being cancelled. It would queue a RedrawRequested event to wake the loop. I need to verify whether a queued event wakes a Wait loop.\n\nI need to check how `send_event` wakes a waiting loop. If `Wait` does not schedule a timer, events must wake it directly.\n\nOption C is to switch the poll strategy to `IdleCallback`. Polls would then only run when the browser is idle, letting the animation frame fire during the frame. But `about_to_wait` would still cancel that rAF on the next idle callback, so this probably will not solve the starvation.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-0daf2cb9-840b-44f3-a30b-6a892682bfcc-58","name":"grep","input":{"pattern":"fn send_event|fn request_redraw|fn poll\\(|State::Wait","path":"/home/micha/.cargo/registry/src/index.crates.io-1949cf8c6b5b557f/winit-0.30.13/src/platform_impl/web/event_loop/runner.rs"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2439,"output_tokens":1198,"cache_read_input_tokens":102656,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa38-de6f-7dc0-ae0d-e0f717ed75f2","uuid":"d69de6c0-2826-45a1-9ca8-c9725bcfa42f"}
