{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_550","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The GPU promise fills `pending_gfx` but never wakes the event loop.\n\nSwitching to Wait mode would freeze the game because the event loop never wakes after the GPU promise resolves. The window is moved into Gfx::create, so calling request_redraw from spawn_local is not straightforward.\n\nReclaiming the window from the Result is too messy. The better approach is to keep Poll mode until the GPU finishes initializing, then switch to Wait inside about_to_wait. ActiveEventLoop can set control flow directly there.\n\nThe `about_to_wait` callback runs before `apply_control_flow`, so setting `ControlFlow::Wait` there will not take effect until the next iteration. The redraw request must therefore be issued inside the same `about_to_wait` call to ensure the animation frame is scheduled immediately.\n\nSetting `ControlFlow::Wait` inside `about_to_wait` works because `apply_control_flow` reads the updated value and switches state immediately. The animation frame scheduled during that same callback will not be cancelled by a subsequent poll. The postTask storm will keep cancelling frames until the GPU promise resolves, at which point the next poll sees the ready graphics and switches to Wait. The remaining question is whether `set_control_flow` is actually available on `ActiveEventLoop`.\n\n`ActiveEventLoop::set_control_flow` is confirmed available in winit 0.30. The first poll after initialization will switch to Wait and schedule a redraw. The remaining question is whether `request_redraw` during Poll gets cancelled by the same iteration's later code.\n\n`request_redraw` during Poll is safe because no other code cancels it before the next poll. The CPU burn during the initialization storm is acceptable. After switching to Wait, every animation frame will run immediately and reschedule itself.\n\nThe animation frame callback clears its own handle immediately upon firing, so `request_redraw` can safely schedule the next frame without cancelling a live one. This should yield roughly 60 frames per second. Each redraw will pump the event loop and advance the simulation by about one tick.\n\nThe hub sends at 15 Hz using real frame_dt, so it only transmits every four frames. Both client and host tick together, keeping snaps, cursor updates, and vitals synchronized. The hub_quiet path already skips heavy mesh uploads to keep per-frame costs low for multiple WebGPU contexts; four players may work without it. When the state is Wait and process_immediately is true, run_until_cleared is called from inside the animation frame callback, which then calls about_to_wait to schedule the next redraw. This nesting is safe.\n\nThe animation frame callback drains its own redraw request inside `run_until_cleared`, so the loop stays clean and one frame per rAF. The change will be limited to the WASM branch in `about_to_wait`, keeping the initial Poll state so GPU initialization is still observed.\n\nThe WASM `run()` comment should clarify that Poll mode is only until the canvas exists. The initialization CPU storm is brief, so leaving it as-is is fine. After editing, the wasm build must be rebuilt. Native tests cannot run in parallel with the wasm build because both share `.harbor-target`; they do not need this wasm-only change.\n\nThe next steps are to edit `about_to_wait`, rebuild the WASM binary, and verify the animation frame count and timer movement.\n\nAfter the build finishes, I will run the four harness scenarios one at a time, then the two-page cursor test, solo title, file:// launches, and balance checks. The two-page test requires DOM aim injection via H.dom() JSON {x, y, use} into a stick product. I will read the harness code to see if it already handles this before writing a custom test.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-2df170b4-3fef-4764-8ade-5b02ae8f5d33-65","name":"search_replace","input":{"file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224015__x42677a/work/Hands of Harbor: Second Opinion-Trauma Center: Second Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-224015/engine/crates/pav_app/src/app.rs","old_string":"    fn about_to_wait(&mut self, el: &ActiveEventLoop) {\n        #[cfg(target_arch = \"wasm32\")]\n        if let Some(r) = self.pending_gfx.as_ref().and_then(|slot| slot.borrow_mut().take()) {\n            self.pending_gfx = None;\n            if let Err(e) = r.and_then(|gfx| self.finish_init(gfx)) {\n                self.fail(el, e);\n            }\n        }\n        #[cfg(not(target_arch = \"wasm32\"))]\n        let _ = el;\n        if let Some(g) = &self.gfx {\n            g.window.request_redraw();\n        }\n    }","new_string":"    fn about_to_wait(&mut self, el: &ActiveEventLoop) {\n        #[cfg(target_arch = \"wasm32\")]\n        {\n            if let Some(r) = self.pending_gfx.as_ref().and_then(|slot| slot.borrow_mut().take()) {\n                self.pending_gfx = None;\n                if let Err(e) = r.and_then(|gfx| self.finish_init(gfx)) {\n                    self.fail(el, e);\n                }\n            }\n            // Poll's task scheduler runs ahead of the display and each\n            // request_redraw cancels the animation frame still waiting.\n            // The canvas only paints when a frame wins that race, so the\n            // sim freezes after a tick or two. Wait lets the frame run.\n            // Poll stays on until the canvas exists: the GPU arrives in a\n            // promise, and only a spinning loop notices it.\n            if self.gfx.is_some() {\n                el.set_control_flow(ControlFlow::Wait);\n            }\n        }\n        #[cfg(not(target_arch = \"wasm32\"))]\n        let _ = el;\n        if let Some(g) = &self.gfx {\n            g.window.request_redraw();\n        }\n    }"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-2df170b4-3fef-4764-8ade-5b02ae8f5d33-66","name":"grep","input":{"pattern":"dom|H\\.dom|function dom","path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224015__x42677a/work/Hands of Harbor: Second Opinion-Trauma Center: Second Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-224015/engine/web/hub_shim.js"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1657,"output_tokens":2454,"cache_read_input_tokens":111104,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa38-de6f-7dc0-ae0d-e0f717ed75f2","uuid":"39c3a3c5-770d-44a9-b80f-50a373ddb798"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-2df170b4-3fef-4764-8ade-5b02ae8f5d33-65","content":"{\"type\":\"SearchReplace\",\"EditsApplied\":{\"old_string\":\"    fn about_to_wait(&mut self, el: &ActiveEventLoop) {\\n        #[cfg(target_arch = \\\"wasm32\\\")]\\n        if let Some(r) = self.pending_gfx.as_ref().and_then(|slot| slot.borrow_mut().take()) {\\n            self.pending_gfx = None;\\n            if let Err(e) = r.and_then(|gfx| self.finish_init(gfx)) {\\n                self.fail(el, e);\\n            }\\n        }\\n        #[cfg(not(target_arch = \\\"wasm32\\\"))]\\n        let _ = el;\\n        if let Some(g) = &self.gfx {\\n            g.window.request_redraw();\\n        }\\n    }\",\"new_string\":\"    fn about_to_wait(&mut self, el: &ActiveEventLoop) {\\n        #[cfg(target_arch = \\\"wasm32\\\")]\\n        {\\n            if let Some(r) = self.pending_gfx.as_ref().and_then(|slot| slot.borrow_mut().take()) {\\n                self.pending_gfx = None;\\n                if let Err(e) = r.and_then(|gfx| self.finish_init(gfx)) {\\n                    self.fail(el, e);\\n                }\\n            }\\n            // Poll's task scheduler runs ahead of the display and each\\n            // request_redraw cancels the animation frame still waiting.\\n            // The canvas only paints when a frame wins that race, so the\\n            // sim freezes after a tick or two. Wait lets the frame run.\\n            // Poll stays on until the canvas exists: the GPU arrives in a\\n            // promise, and only a spinning loop notices it.\\n            if self.gfx.is_some() {\\n                el.set_control_flow(ControlFlow::Wait);\\n            }\\n        }\\n        #[cfg(not(target_arch = \\\"wasm32\\\"))]\\n        let _ = el;\\n        if let Some(g) = &self.gfx {\\n            g.window.request_redraw();\\n        }\\n    }\",\"tool_output_for_prompt\":\"The file /home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224015__x42677a/work/Hands of Harbor: Second Opinion-Trauma Center: Second Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-224015/engine/crates/pav_app/src/app.rs has been updated successfully.\",\"tool_output_for_prompt_concise\":\"The file /home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224015__x42677a/work/Hands of Harbor: Second Opinion-Trauma Center: Second Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-224015/engine/crates/pav_app/src/app.rs has been updated.\",\"absolute_path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224015__x42677a/work/Hands of Harbor: Second Opinion-Trauma Center: Second Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-224015/engine/crates/pav_app/src/app.rs\",\"edits\":{\"details\":[{\"old_string\":\"    fn about_to_wait(&mut self, el: &ActiveEventLoop) {\\n        #[cfg(target_arch = \\\"wasm32\\\")]\\n        if let Some(r) = self.pending_gfx.as_ref().and_then(|slot| slot.borrow_mut().take()) {\\n            self.pending_gfx = None;\\n            if let Err(e) = r.and_then(|gfx| self.finish_init(gfx)) {\\n                self.fail(el, e);\\n            }\\n        }\\n        #[cfg(not(target_arch = \\\"wasm32\\\"))]\\n        let _ = el;\\n        if let Some(g) = &self.gfx {\\n            g.window.request_redraw();\\n        }\\n    }\",\"old_line\":2253,\"new_string\":\"    fn about_to_wait(&mut self, el: &ActiveEventLoop) {\\n        #[cfg(target_arch = \\\"wasm32\\\")]\\n        {\\n            if let Some(r) = self.pending_gfx.as_ref().and_then(|slot| slot.borrow_mut().take()) {\\n                self.pending_gfx = None;\\n                if let Err(e) = r.and_then(|gfx| self.finish_init(gfx)) {\\n                    self.fail(el, e);\\n                }\\n            }\\n            // Poll's task scheduler runs ahead of the display and each\\n            // request_redraw cancels the animation frame still waiting.\\n            // The canvas only paints when a frame wins that race, so the\\n            // sim freezes after a tick or two. Wait lets the frame run.\\n            // Poll stays on until the canvas exists: the GPU arrives in a\\n            // promise, and only a spinning loop notices it.\\n            if self.gfx.is_some() {\\n                el.set_control_flow(ControlFlow::Wait);\\n            }\\n        }\\n        #[cfg(not(target_arch = \\\"wasm32\\\"))]\\n        let _ = el;\\n        if let Some(g) = &self.gfx {\\n            g.window.request_redraw();\\n        }\\n    }\",\"new_line\":2253,\"context_before\":\"        }\\n    }\\n\\n\",\"context_after\":\"}\\n\\nfn room_entries(sim: &Sim) -> Vec<RoomEntry> {\\n\",\"line_prefix\":\"\"}]}}}","is_error":false},{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-2df170b4-3fef-4764-8ade-5b02ae8f5d33-66","content":"{\"type\":\"GrepSearch\",\"stdout\":[60,119,111,114,107,115,112,97,99,101,95,114,101,115,117,108,116,32,119,111,114,107,115,112,97,99,101,95,112,97,116,104,61,34,47,104,111,109,101,47,109,105,99,104,97,47,100,101,118,47,99,99,45,109,97,116,114,105,120,47,114,117,110,115,47,103,114,111,107,45,120,104,105,103,104,46,98,117,105,108,100,45,118,50,95,95,50,48,50,54,49,49,48,52,45,50,50,52,48,49,53,95,95,120,52,50,54,55,55,97,47,119,111,114,107,34,62,10,70,111,117,110,100,32,49,32,109,97,116,99,104,105,110,103,32,108,105,110,101,115,10,47,104,111,109,101,47,109,105,99,104,97,47,100,101,118,47,99,99,45,109,97,116,114,105,120,47,114,117,110,115,47,103,114,111,107,45,120,104,105,103,104,46,98,117,105,108,100,45,118,50,95,95,50,48,50,54,49,49,48,52,45,50,50,52,48,49,53,95,95,120,52,50,54,55,55,97,47,119,111,114,107,47,72,97,110,100,115,32,111,102,32,72,97,114,98,111,114,58,32,83,101,99,111,110,100,32,79,112,105,110,105,111,110,45,84,114,97,117,109,97,32,67,101,110,116,101,114,58,32,83,101,99,111,110,100,32,79,112,105,110,105,111,110,45,103,114,111,107,45,52,46,55,45,120,104,105,103,104,45,50,48,50,54,49,49,48,52,45,50,50,52,48,49,53,47,101,110,103,105,110,101,47,119,101,98,47,104,117,98,95,115,104,105,109,46,106,115,10