es host cursor and vitals match\",\"current_dir\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224015__x42677a/work\",\"output_file\":\"/home/micha/.grok/sessions/%2Fhome%2Fmicha%2Fdev%2Fcc-matrix%2Fruns%2Fgrok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224015__x42677a%2Fwork/01a1aa38-de6f-7dc0-ae0d-e0f717ed75f2/terminal/call-75986106-35ea-4928-a9d0-df51c5bd8062-77.log\",\"total_bytes\":751}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa38-de6f-7dc0-ae0d-e0f717ed75f2","uuid":"024a0e89-95de-4fb2-ac47-aae36be2a3bd"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_558","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The round timer reached 1418, but the mode remained at 7 (card) for the full 20 seconds.\n\nThe simulation never booted into op mode because no redraws fired after the timer turned positive. The cursor script waited 20 seconds, but only 1.4 seconds of actual play time elapsed with no frame updates to trigger the round transition. This is flaky behavior caused by rare animation-frame callbacks. The previous probe reached mode 3, while this one did not.\n\nThe 500ms polling loop never detected mode 3 or 8, confirming the animation loop froze entirely. The final snapshot remains at mode 7 with a positive timer.\n\nThe round likely started only 1.4 seconds before the 20-second wait ended. The player was slow to ready, so the boot frame arrived just as the script stopped polling. The condition required both a positive timer and mode 3 or 8, which explains why the transition was missed.\n\nThe timer was negative for most of the 20-second wait, so the boot frame never arrived. The script will be updated to poll for mode 3 specifically and wait up to 45 seconds. The deeper issue is unreliable low FPS. Hub frames must be made cheap enough to run at the display rate.\n\nTo fix the low FPS, the plan is to disable shadows, bloom, outlines, and GI during quiet hub frames. The main target is skipping `gfx.draw` entirely for hub copies, since the harness does not screenshot them. This would let the wasm loop poll, simulate, and send data while skipping GPU work, then request the next frame at 60Hz.\n\nSkipping the draw call entirely would leave the hub iframe blank or frozen, which is a regression for human observers. The better approach is to render cheaply by disabling shadows and other expensive effects while still painting something. If frames remain too slow after that optimization, then skipping the draw for hub copies can be considered as a fallback.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-7140fd90-bd99-4593-a6fe-9071619d9d60-78","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224015__x42677a/work/Hands of Harbor: Second Opinion-Trauma Center: Second Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-224015/engine/crates/pav_view/src/build.rs","offset":1400,"limit":90}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":576,"output_tokens":1056,"cache_read_input_tokens":128256,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa38-de6f-7dc0-ae0d-e0f717ed75f2","uuid":"e5b1e1d0-6fe4-420e-b888-fc2a42c20443"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-7140fd90-bd99-4593-a6fe-9071619d9d60-78","content":"{\"type\":\"ReadFile\",\"FileContent\":{\"content\":\"1400→                            style: Style::Unlit,\\n                            flags: rs::flags::NO_SHADOW | rs::flags::NO_CUT,\\n                            group: o.id.0 + 2,\\n                            material: 0,\\n                        });\\n                    }\\n                }\\n                None => {\\n                    match &o.prop {\\n                        Some(prop) => {\\n1410→                            self.emit_prop(&mut scene, &o, prop, settings, time, dt);\\n                            live.push(o.id.0);\\n                        }\\n                        None => emit_object(&mut scene, &o, settings.style, now, 0),\\n                    }\\n                    if let Some(v) = &o.vehicle {\\n                        crate::vehicles::emit_vehicle(\\n                            &mut scene,\\n                            &o,\\n                            v,\\n1420→                            style_of(o.visual.look, settings.style),\\n                            settings.particles,\\n                        );\\n                    }\\n                }\\n            }\\n        }\\n        if let Some(creature) = crate::creatures::interpolate(prev, curr, alpha) {\\n            puppets.push(creature.id.0 + 2);\\n            if let Err(error) = crate::creatures::emit(&mut scene, &creature, style_of(Look::Lit, settings.style)) {\\n1430→                eprintln!(\\\"creature preview: {error}\\\");\\n            }\\n        }\\n        self.emit_carry.retain(|(id, _), _| live.contains(id));\\n        if let Some(g) = &curr.game {\\n            self.arpg.emit(&mut scene, curr, g, alpha, time, dt, settings.particles, cam_fwd);\\n        }\\n        // Projectiles: drawn where they are between ticks (they move in straight lines).\\n        let back = (1.0 - alpha) * curr.dt;\\n        for p in &curr.projectiles {\\n1440→            let mut sd = SdfInstance::sphere(p.pos - p.vel * back, p.radius, v3(p.color));\\n            sd.style = Style::Unlit;\\n            sd.emissive = 0.6;\\n            sd.flags = rs::flags::NO_SHADOW | rs::flags::NO_CUT;\\n            sd.group = 0x7f1;\\n            scene.sdfs.push(sd);\\n        }\\n        self.emit_effects(&mut scene);\\n        scenery.sort_unstable();\\n        mark_objects(&mut scene, env_end, &scenery);\\n1450→        if settings.style == StyleOverride::PerObject {\\n            restyle_parts(&mut scene, settings.style_objects, settings.style_environment);\\n        }\\n        if f.pixel_art > 1.0 {\\n            let hero = curr.player.map(|p| p.0 + 2);\\n            mark_pixel_art(&mut scene, |g, flags| match f.pixel_target {\\n                PixelTarget::All => true,\\n                PixelTarget::Characters => puppets.contains(&g),\\n                PixelTarget::Hero => Some(g) == hero,\\n                PixelTarget::Others => puppets.contains(&g) && Some(g) != hero,\\n1460→                PixelTarget::World => !puppets.contains(&g),\\n                PixelTarget::Entity => g == f.pixel_entity as u32 + 2,\\n                PixelTarget::Objects => flags & rs::flags::OBJECT != 0,\\n                PixelTarget::Environment => flags & rs::flags::OBJECT == 0,\\n            });\\n        }\\n        lock(&self.materials).attach(&mut scene);\\n        if let Some(op) = curr.surgery.as_deref() {\\n            crate::surgery::emit(&mut scene, op);\\n            crate::surgery::apply_look(&mut scene, rig, aspect, &op.camera);\\n1470→        }\\n        scene\\n    }\\n}\\n\\n/// Flags the characters and objects: every instance emitted after the environment (`from`:\\n/// meshes, SDFs, dynamic meshes) except fixed scenery (outline groups in `scenery`, sorted).\\nfn mark_objects(scene: &mut Scene, from: (usize, usize, usize), scenery: &[u32]) {\\n    let object = |g: u32| scenery.binary_search(&g).is_err();\\n    for m in &mut scene.meshes[from.0..] {\\n1480→        if object(m.group) {\\n            m.flags |= rs::flags::OBJECT;\\n        }\\n    }\\n    for s in &mut scene.sdfs[from.1..] {\\n        if object(s.group) {\\n            s.flags |= rs::flags::OBJECT;\\n        }\\n    }\\n    for d in &mut scene.dynamic[from.2..] {\",\"content_concise\":\"1400→                            style: Style::Unlit,\\n                            flags: rs::flags::NO_SHADOW | rs::flags::NO_CUT,\\n                            group: o.id.0 + 2,\\n                            material: 0,\\n                        });\\n                    }\\n                }\\n                None => {\\n                    match &o.prop {\\n                        Some(prop) => {\\n1410→                            self.emit_prop(&mut scene, &o, prop, settings, time, dt);\\n                            live.push(o.id.0);\\n                        }\\n                        None => emit_object(&mut scene, &o, settings.style, now, 0),\\n                    }\\n                    if let Some(v) = &o.vehicle {\\n                        crate::vehicles::emit_vehicle(\\n                            &mut scene,\\n                            &o,\\n                            v,\\n1420→                            style_of(o.visual.look, settings.style),\\n                            settings.particles,\\n                        );\\n                    }\\n                }\\n            }\\n        }\\n        if let Some(creature) = crate::creatures::interpolate(prev, curr, alpha) {\\n            puppets.push(creature.id.0 + 2);\\n            if let Err(error) = crate::creatures::emit(&mut scene, &creature, style_of(Look::Lit, settings.style)) {\\n1430→                eprintln!(\\\"creature preview: {error}\\\");\\n            }\\n        }\\n        self.emit_carry.retain(|(id, _), _| live.contains(id));\\n        if let Some(g) = &curr.game {\\n            