{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_559","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The surgery scene likely contains a full room of world meshes. The plate is added afterward, or skipped if quiet. Then apply_look enables shadows on everything.\n\nShadowing the entire room on SwiftShader is extremely expensive. Card mode still builds the full 420×240 plate mesh plus shadows before hub_quiet activates, which explains the 2fps and boot delay.\n\nThe fix is to set hub_quiet immediately when a hub session begins, not just at boot. This prevents card frames from building the full plate. Shadows and post-processing should also be disabled during quiet mode. The first surgery frame or the existing mode=7 card transition are the likely spots to trigger this.\n\nThe concrete fix is to set `hub_quiet = true` inside the mode=7 card transition block. `boot_hub_round` already handles this at boot.\n\n`apply_look` must also disable shadows when quiet, because even an empty room can still shadow on SwiftShader.\n\nThe real CPU bottleneck is building 100,000 vertices in WASM for the plate mesh. An empty room with shadows might still take over 100 ms.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-77ed68db-6bbf-4b94-85a7-59b7539f8459-79","name":"grep","input":{"pattern":"fn exec","glob":"**/pav_app/src/simhost.rs"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2127,"output_tokens":603,"cache_read_input_tokens":128768,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa38-de6f-7dc0-ae0d-e0f717ed75f2","uuid":"7026656a-de62-48d6-9ef3-b15364a5280a"}
