{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_567","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The four-player test passed. Traffic metrics for players 0 through 2 are now recorded.\n\nPlayer 3 also passed, so the detail was likely truncated. The 38-message rate is healthy at roughly 2.5 Hz. The remaining three scenarios will be run sequentially in one shell script.\n\nThe remaining three scenarios are host-leave, server, and players=1. Each may take up to 150 seconds, so the combined runtime could reach three to four minutes. I will run them sequentially in one script with a generous timeout. After that, I will handle solo title and file launches. Cargo will not be run in parallel to keep the machine free for the browser tests.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-5d62e6fb-0261-437d-88b6-597ff3da18d4-92","name":"run_terminal_command","input":{"command":"export TMPDIR=/tmp/hbr-pw PLAYWRIGHT_HOST_PLATFORM_OVERRIDE=ubuntu24.04-x64\nSCRATCH=\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224015__x42677a/tmp/grok-goal-907ccca5ce3b/implementer\"\nPY=\"$SCRATCH/hub_one.py\"\nrun() {\n  local name=\"$1\" q=\"$2\"\n  echo \"===== $name =====\"\n  xvfb-run -a python3 \"$PY\" \"$q\" > \"$SCRATCH/hub-$name.txt\" 2>&1\n  echo \"exit:$?\"\n  python3 - \"$SCRATCH/hub-$name.txt\" << 'PY'\nimport json,sys\nfrom pathlib import Path\nt = Path(sys.argv[1]).read_text(errors=\"replace\")\ni = t.find(\"{\")\n# report json starts after REPORT\nr = t.find(\"REPORT\")\nblob = t[r:]\n# first json object\na = blob.find(\"{\")\ndepth=0\nend=None\nfor n,ch in enumerate(blob[a:], a):\n    if ch==\"{\": depth+=1\n    elif ch==\"}\":\n        depth-=1\n        if depth==0:\n            end=n+1\n            break\ntry:\n    rep=json.loads(blob[a:end])\nexcept Exception as e:\n    print(\"parse\", e)\n    print(t[-1500:])\n    sys.exit(0)\nfails=[c for c in rep.get(\"checks\",[]) if not c.get(\"pass\")]\nprint(\"pass\", rep.get(\"pass\"), \"players\", rep.get(\"players\"), \"scenario\", rep.get(\"scenario\"))\ntraffic=next((c for c in rep.get(\"checks\",[]) if \"traffic\" in c[\"name\"]), None)\nif traffic: print(\"traffic\", traffic.get(\"detail\"))\nendc=next((c for c in rep.get(\"checks\",[]) if c[\"name\"].startswith(\"the round ends\")), None)\nif endc: print(\"end\", endc.get(\"detail\"))\nif fails:\n    for c in fails:\n        print(\"FAIL\", c[\"name\"], c.get(\"detail\"))\nelse:\n    print(\"all checks passed\", len(rep.get(\"checks\",[])))\nPY\n}\nrun leave 'players=4&latency=150&jitter=50&loss=5&auto=1&limit=20&scenario=host-leave'\nrun server 'players=2&scenario=server&auto=1&limit=20'\nrun one 'players=1&auto=1&limit=20'\necho DONE","description":"Run host-leave, server, and solo hub harnesses","block_until_ms":360000}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":3087,"output_tokens":1053,"cache_read_input_tokens":137728,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa38-de6f-7dc0-ae0d-e0f717ed75f2","uuid":"e0f4db0f-175e-41b9-a928-d430034f5010"}
