{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_587","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The skill can be set via get_mut after Sim::new.\n\nThe skill field needs to be public. The exact get_mut path is being weighed against play_mut(). A full test with 20 seeds and four skills would take many minutes, so an ignored test is likely. The summary requires balance output for skills 1.0, 0.7, 0.4, and 0.\n\nThe plan calls for 20 seeds. I will run those but skip the full campaign for lower skills and only test it at skill 1.0.\n\nSuggested par will be the mean skill-1.0 score so rank S is achieved. Time will be ticks divided by sixty and vitals will be the final health count. The ignored test will run with a long timeout.\n\nThe launch script and ignored balance test will be written first. Cargo will run next, but the browser script may start earlier to avoid earlyoom conflicts between CPU and GPU load.\n\nThe browser script will run before cargo. Playwright must press Enter on the canvas to focus it, then navigate through the title, about, and story screens. Escape does not exit the story screen because its back() handler ignores that key.\n\nThe browser script will use four separate Playwright flows on one page. One flow captures the title screen. Another enters the menu, selects About, and returns to the menu. A third exits the story by pressing Enter repeatedly until reaching the operation screen, then screenshots both the story and operation views. The fourth pauses from the operation screen, navigates to Dev Mode, and takes a screenshot.\n\nA fifth browser flow for the results screen is impossible. The story-to-case transition never wins, so the operation screen cannot be reached. The draw function will be checked to see if a missed key triggers Dev Mode. If not, no results screenshot will be added.\n\nA hidden key for the unbound dev command was considered but rejected. The operation screen will be captured. The dead screen is not the results view. Screenshots require the GPU page, so a native bot test cannot replace them. Attract mode plays a short immortal case and still does not reach results. Five screenshots will be taken. A short bot run might reveal the results screen.\n\nThe operation screen is the target screenshot after the story ends. The browser viewport will be 1920 by 1080 pixels. A gamepad stub will be injected to press button zero and advance the timestamp, then the status focus and screen will be compared across both launches. If the stubbed pad fails, keyboard Enter will be used instead.\n\nStatus will be recorded before and after pressing Enter to confirm the menu screen and focus zero match across launches. Console errors will be checked, but 404s are expected from file:// favicon requests and will be ignored; only page errors and WASM errors will fail the run. The status text will include music volume \"0.10\". To verify the canvas is actually painted, a screenshot will be captured and checked for non-zero variance using either Pillow or a simple PNG parser.\n\nA solo test will open the game directly at http://127.0.0.1:39337/GAME.html to verify the title without the harness. The screenshot script must click the canvas before pressing keyboard keys.\n\nThe script will wait for `window.__game.status` to exist, pause 1.5 seconds for a frame to paint, and read the status object via `page.evaluate`. File URLs with spaces and colons will be encoded using `pathlib.as_uri()`. Two browsers will run sequentially in one script. Screenshots may be kept separate from launches so a shot failure does not hide launch results.\n\nA single script is sufficient if it prints clearly and saves files even when later steps fail. The operation screen can be reached by loading case zero from the menu, then pausing, selecting Dev Mode, and entering it. The story path starts by pressing Continue twice. The title screenshot will also be saved as shots/title.png. After the operation screenshot, the mode will be checked to see if the results screen is reachable.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-029fa5e9-e056-4268-8c6e-c3842c023ac2-122","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224015__x42677a/work/Hands of Harbor: Second Opinion-Trauma Center: Second Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-224015/engine/crates/pav_ui/src/surgery/about.json"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1261,"output_tokens":2090,"cache_read_input_tokens":161536,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa38-de6f-7dc0-ae0d-e0f717ed75f2","uuid":"5b291bce-01e8-4b24-8e76-6a679b8f2405"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-029fa5e9-e056-4268-8c6e-c3842c023ac2-122","content":"{\"type\":\"ReadFile\",\"FileContent\":{\"content\":\"1→{\\n  \\\"sourceInformation\\\": {\\n    \\\"date\\\": \\\"2026-11-04 22:40:15\\\",\\n    \\\"source\\\": \\\"Trauma Center: Second Opinion\\\",\\n    \\\"plan\\\": \\\"PLAN.md\\\",\\n    \\\"genre\\\": \\\"Simulation\\\",\\n    \\\"perspective\\\": \\\"Fixed overhead view of the operative field\\\",\\n    \\\"tech\\\": \\\"Pavilion engine (Shardfall commit 49ef2ba), Rust 1.98.1, wgpu/WebGPU, wasm-bindgen 0.2.129, egui 0.36.2\\\",\\n    \\\"artDirection\\\": \\\"Cel-shaded overhead operative field painted per vertex, with layered paper-theatre cards for story\\\",\\n10→    \\\"animation\\\": \\\"Simulation-driven tissue, instruments, heartbeat, and paper-card motion\\\",\\n    \\\"audio\\\": \\\"Synthesized music, effects, and short gibberish voices. No audio files. Music bus defaults to 0.10\\\",\\n    \\\"online\\\": \\\"Optional AI Hub shared-world Code Blue for 1-4 surgeons\\\",\\n    \\\"testing\\\": \\\"Deterministic sim suite, headless shell, Chromium file:// launches, hub harness\\\",\\n    \\\"research\\\": \\\"Engine seams and the hub protocol, recorded in PLAN.md\\\",\\n    \\\"environment\\\": \\\"Grok CLI (headless); Linux\\\",\\n    \\\"model\\\": \\\"xAI, grok-4.7, reasoning effort xhigh\\\",\\n    \\\"usage\\\": \\\"added on import\\\"\\n  },\\n  \\\"testingFeedback\\\": [\\n20→    \\\"Testing caught three rule bugs: a Rust or-pattern guard skipped stage-0 sutures, nearest-hazard selection stole forceps pulls, and a sac's swell shared the laser charge meter.\\\",\\n    \\\"3\\\",\\n    \\\"The most helpful test was a skill-1.0 bot playing every case, Code Blue, and the campaign from a fresh scene.\\\",\\n    \\\"The least helpful test was a temporary print probe that only dumped stuck hazards and was removed once the selection bug was fixed.\\\"\\n  ],\\n  \\\"engineFeedback\\\": [\\n    \\\"The Game hook, recorded input, RenderFrame, headless egui, and the single-file packer.\\\",\\n    \\\"Yes. A colon in the project path makes rustc fail joining LD_LIBRARY_PATH, and the demo frame path captures the camera, pause menu, and touch layer unless a game returns first.\\\",\\n    \\\"The operative rules, the plate mesh, the ten-foot shell, the cue and music buses, and the hub shim.\\\",\\n    \\\"Keeping a surgery scene off the demo boot panel, stats, guide, toasts, and the engine pause menu.\\\",\\n30→    \\\"Added the surgery frame, surgeon input, and cue event; a view emit and camera shot; a product frame branch; audio buses and formants; session.js injection in the packer; and js-sys. The hook alone cannot draw, play cues, or join a hub.\\\",\\n    \\\"A first-class per-game frame path, so a new game does not have to outrun the demo loop.\\\"\\n  ],\\n  \\\"promptFeedback\\\": [\\n    \\\"The tested camera, light, and palette numbers, and a hub shim that the harness had already accepted.\\\",\\n    \\\"The deliverable folder name must contain a colon, which Cargo cannot use as its working directory.\\\",\\n    \\\"Shipping one packed page that is the full game, a hub client, and a file:// WebGPU build.\\\",\\n    \\\"Say at the start that the Cargo target directory cannot contain a colon.\\\"\\n  ],\\n  \\\"aiHub\\\": {\\n40→    \\\"name\\\": \\\"Hands of Harbor: Second Opinion\\\",\\n    \\\"tagline\\\": \\\"Night Ward. Keep the beat. Keep them alive.\\\",\\n    \\\"description\\\": \\\"Overhead surgical melodrama for one to four surgeons at Mercy Harbor General in Port Verity.\\\",\\n    \\\"type\\\": \\\"Game\\\",\\n    \\\"genre\\\": \\\"Simulation\\\",\\n    \\\"source\\\": \\\"Trauma Center: Second Opinion\\\",\\n    \\\"series\\\": \\\"Trauma Center\\\",\\n    \\\"players\\\": \\\"1–4\\\",\\n    \\\"controls\\\": \\\"Right stick or mouse aims, R2 or left click operates, left stick or 1–8 picks tools\\\",\\n    \\\"tags\\\": [\\\"3d\\\", \\\"story\\\", \\\"co-op\\\", \\\"arcade\\\", \\\"boss fights\\\"]\\n50→  }\\n}\\n\",\"content_concise\":\"1→{\\n  \\\"sourceInformation\\\": {\\n    \\\"date\\\": \\\"2026-11-04 22:40:15\\\",\\n    \\\"source\\\": \\\"Trauma Center: Second Opinion\\\",\\n    \\\"plan\\\": \\\"PLAN.md\\\",\\n    \\\"genre\\\": \\\"Simulation\\\",\\n    \\\"perspective\\\": \\\"Fixed overhead view of the operative field\\\",\\n    \\\"tech\\\": \\\"Pavilion engine (Shardfall commit 49ef2ba), Rust 1.98.1, wgpu/WebGPU, wasm-bindgen 0.2.129, egui 0.36.2\\\",\\n    \\\"artDirection\\\": \\\"Cel-shaded overhead operative field painted per vertex, with layered paper-theatre cards for story\\\",\\n10→    \\\"animation\\\": \\\"Simulation-driven tissue, instruments, heartbeat, and paper-card motion\\\",\\n    \\\"audio\\\": \\\"Synthesized music, effects, and short gibberish voices. No audio files. Music bus defaults to 0.10\\\",\\n    \\\"online\\\": \\\"Optional AI Hub shared-world Code Blue for 1-4 surgeons\\\",\\n    \\\"testing\\\": \\\"Deterministic sim suite, headless shell, Chromium file:// launches, hub harness\\\",\\n    \\\"research\\\": \\\"Engine seams and the hub protocol, recorded in PLAN.md\\\",\\n    \\\"environment\\\": \\\"Grok CLI (headless); Linux\\\",\\n    \\\"model\\\": \\\"xAI, grok-4.7, reasoning effort xhigh\\\",\\n    \\\"usage\\\": \\\"added on import\\\"\\n  },\\n  \\\"testingFeedback\\\": [\\n20→    \\\"Testing caught three rule bugs: a Rust or-pattern guard skipped stage-0 sutures, nearest-hazard selection stole forceps pulls, and a sac's swell shared the laser charge meter.\\\",\\n    \\\"3\\\",\\n    \\\"The most helpful test was a skill-1.0 bot playing every case, Code Blue, and the campaign from a fresh scene.\\\",\\n    \\\"The least helpful test was a temporary print probe that only dumped stuck hazards and was removed once the selection bug was fixed.\\\"\\n  ],\\n  \\\"engineFeedback\\\": [\\n    \\\"The Game hook, recorded input, RenderFrame, headless egui, and the single-file packer.\\\",\\n    \\\"Yes. A colon in the project path makes rustc fail joining LD_LIBRARY_PATH, and the demo frame path captures the camera, pause menu, and touch layer unless a game returns first.\\\",\\n    \\\"The operative rules, the plate mesh, the ten-foot shell, the cue and music buses, and the hub shim.\\\",\\n    \\\"Keeping a surgery scene off the demo boot panel, stats, guide, toasts, and the engine pause menu.\\\",\\n30→    \\\"Added the surgery frame, surgeon input, and cue event; a view emit and camera shot; a product frame branch; audio buses and formants; session.js injection in the packer; and js-sys. The hook alone cannot draw, play cues, or join a hub.\\\",\\n    \\\"A first-class per-game frame path, so a new game does not have to outrun the demo loop.\\\"\\n  ],\\n  \\\"promptFeedback\\\": [\\n    \\\"The tested camera, light, and palette numbers, and a hub shim that the harness had already accepted.\\\",\\n    \\\"The deliverable folder name must contain a colon, which Cargo cannot use as its working directory.\\\",\\n    \\\"Shipping one packed page that is the full game, a hub client, and a file:// WebGPU build.\\\",\\n    \\\"Say at the start that the Cargo target directory cannot contain a colon.\\\"\\n  ],\\n  \\\"aiHub\\\": {\\n40→    \\\"name\\\": \\\"Hands of Harbor: Second Opinion\\\",\\n    \\\"tagline\\\": \\\"Night Ward. Keep the beat. Keep them alive.\\\",\\n    \\\"description\\\": \\\"Overhead surgical melodrama for one to four surgeons at Mercy Harbor General in Port Verity.\\\",\\n    \\\"type\\\": \\\"Game\\\",\\n    \\\"genre\\\": \\\"Simulation\\\",\\n    \\\"source\\\": \\\"Trauma Center: Second Opinion\\\",\\n    \\\"series\\\": \\\"Trauma Center\\\",\\n    \\\"players\\\": \\\"1–4\\\",\\n    \\\"controls\\\": \\\"Right stick or mouse aims, R2 or left click operates, left stick or 1–8 picks tools\\\",\\n    \\\"tags\\\": [\\\"3d\\\", \\\"story\\\", \\\"co-op\\\", \\\"arcade\\\", \\\"boss fights\\\"]\\n50→  }\\n}\\n\",\"absolute_path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224015__x42677a/work/Hands of Harbor: Second Opinion-Trauma Center: Second Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-224015/engine/crates/pav_ui/src/surgery/about.json\",\"offset\":null,\"raw_output\":\"{\\n  \\\"sourceInformation\\\": {\\n    \\\"date\\\": \\\"2026-11-04 22:40:15\\\",\\n    \\\"source\\\": \\\"Trauma Center: Second Opinion\\\",\\n    \\\"plan\\\": \\\"PLAN.md\\\",\\n    \\\"genre\\\": \\\"Simulation\\\",\\n    \\\"perspective\\\": \\\"Fixed overhead view of the operative field\\\",\\n    \\\"tech\\\": \\\"Pavilion engine (Shardfall commit 49ef2ba), Rust 1.98.1, wgpu/WebGPU, wasm-bindgen 0.2.129, egui 0.36.2\\\",\\n    \\\"artDirection\\\": \\\"Cel-shaded overhead operative field painted per vertex, with layered paper-theatre cards for story\\\",\\n    \\\"animation\\\": \\\"Simulation-driven tissue, instruments, heartbeat, and paper-card motion\\\",\\n    \\\"audio\\\": \\\"Synthesized music, effects, and short gibberish voices. No audio files. Music bus defaults to 0.10\\\",\\n    \\\"online\\\": \\\"Optional AI Hub shared-world Code Blue for 1-4 surgeons\\\",\\n    \\\"testing\\\": \\\"Deterministic sim suite, headless shell, Chromium file:// launches, hub harness\\\",\\n    \\\"research\\\": \\\"Engine seams and the hub protocol, recorded in PLAN.md\\\",\\n    \\\"environment\\\": \\\"Grok CLI (headless); Linux\\\",\\n    \\\"model\\\": \\\"xAI, grok-4.7, reasoning effort xhigh\\\",\\n    \\\"usage\\\": \\\"added on import\\\"\\n  },\\n  \\\"testingFeedback\\\": [\\n    \\\"Testing caught three rule bugs: a Rust or-pattern guard skipped stage-0 sutures, nearest-hazard selection stole forceps pulls, and a sac's swell shared the laser charge meter.\\\",\\n    \\\"3\\\",\\n    \\\"The most helpful test was a skill-1.0 bot playing every case, Code Blue, and the campaign from a fresh scene.\\\",\\n    \\\"The least helpful test was a temporary print probe that only dumped stuck hazards and was removed once the selection bug was fixed.\\\"\\n  ],\\n  \\\"engineFeedback\\\": [\\n    \\\"The Game hook, recorded input, RenderFrame, headless egui, and the single-file packer.\\\",\\n    \\\"Yes. A colon in the project path makes rustc fail joining LD_LIBRARY_PATH, and the demo frame path captures the camera, pause menu, and touch layer unless a game returns first.\\\",\\n    \\\"The operative rules, the plate mesh, the ten-foot shell, the cue and music buses, and the hub shim.\\\",\\n    \\\"Keeping a surgery scene off the demo boot panel, stats, guide, toasts, and the engine pause menu.\\\",\\n    \\\"Added the surgery frame, surgeon input, and cue event; a view emit and camera shot; a product frame branch; audio buses and formants; session.js injection in the packer; and js-sys. The hook alone cannot draw, play cues, or join a hub.\\\",\\n    \\\"A first-class per-game frame path, so a new game does not have to outrun the demo loop.\\\"\\n  ],\\n  \\\"promptFeedback\\\": [\\n    \\\"The tested camera, light, and palette numbers, and a hub shim that the harness had already accepted.\\\",\\n    \\\"The deliverable folder name must contain a colon, which Cargo cannot use as its working directory.\\\",\\n    \\\"Shipping one packed page that is the full game, a hub client, and a file:// WebGPU build.\\\",\\n    \\\"Say at the start that the Cargo target directory cannot contain a colon.\\\"\\n  ],\\n  \\\"aiHub\\\": {\\n    \\\"name\\\": \\\"Hands of Harbor: Second Opinion\\\",\\n    \\\"tagline\\\": \\\"Night Ward. Keep the beat. Keep them alive.\\\",\\n    \\\"description\\\": \\\"Overhead surgical melodrama for one to four surgeons at Mercy Harbor General in Port Verity.\\\",\\n    \\\"type\\\": \\\"Game\\\",\\n    \\\"genre\\\": \\\"Simulation\\\",\\n    \\\"source\\\": \\\"Trauma Center: Second Opinion\\\",\\n    \\\"series\\\": \\\"Trauma Center\\\",\\n    \\\"players\\\": \\\"1–4\\\",\\n