,66,79,78,69,32,105,102,32,104,46,115,116,97,103,101,32,62,61,32,49,32,124,124,32,104,46,107,105,110,100,32,33,61,32,75,95,66,79,78,69,32,61,62,32,123,10,60,47,119,111,114,107,115,112,97,99,101,95,114,101,115,117,108,116,62],\"stderr\":[],\"exit_code\":0,\"match_count\":4,\"file_matches\":[{\"path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224015__x42677a/work/Hands of Harbor: Second Opinion-Trauma Center: Second Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-224015/engine/crates/pav_core/src/games/surgery/hazard.rs\",\"matches\":[{\"line_number\":99,\"content\":\"            K_LACERATION => {\"},{\"line_number\":207,\"content\":\"    pub fn accepts(&self, tool: u8) -> bool {\"},{\"line_number\":367,\"content\":\"        K_LACERATION | K_BLEEDER => {\"},{\"line_number\":620,\"content\":\"        K_LACERATION | K_BLEEDER | K_BONE if h.stage >= 1 || h.kind != K_BONE => {\"}]}]}","is_error":false},{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-bf5b9391-7c5b-4ca1-bbfc-9c86f70ff559-144","content":"{\"type\":\"ReadFile\",\"FileContent\":{\"content\":\"1→//! Paper-theatre lines. Indices, not copies, live in the sim.\\n\\n#[derive(Clone, Copy)]\\npub struct Line {\\n    pub who: &'static str,\",\"content_concise\":\"1→//! Paper-theatre lines. Indices, not copies, live in the sim.\\n\\n#[derive(Clone, Copy)]\\npub struct Line {\\n    pub who: &'static str,\",\"absolute_path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224015__x42677a/work/Hands of Harbor: Second Opinion-Trauma Center: Second Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-224015/engine/crates/pav_core/src/games/surgery/story.rs\",\"offset\":1,\"limit\":5,\"raw_output\":\"//! Paper-theatre lines. Indices, not copies, live in the sim.\\n\\n#[derive(Clone, Copy)]\\npub struct Line {\\n    pub who: &'static str,\\n\",\"total_lines\":312}}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa38-de6f-7dc0-ae0d-e0f717ed75f2","uuid":"8a17f19b-2a7c-46e4-b8e8-81ce6ef38613"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_599","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Mouse-based winning is too uncertain.\n\nI'll capture five screens and write a launch script that saves shots. I'll append deviations to PLAN.md and draft the README. Then I'll rebuild, write the Python script, and run launches. Cargo balance can run in parallel with the browser after the WASM build finishes.\n\nI'll start the WASM build now and write the files. After it finishes, I'll run the browser and the cargo suite and balance sequentially in one shell.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-98cac0c8-1ed4-4570-abc1-d4bd55f19791-145","name":"search_replace","input":{"file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224015__x42677a/work/PLAN.md","old_string":"✔ This read a peak of 0.65 from the engine's cpal output during play.","new_string":"✔ This read a peak of 0.65 from the engine's cpal output during play.\n\n## Deviations\n\n- Case and story tables live in Rust (`content.rs`, `story.rs`), not toml. The sim reads that one table. A toml loader would be a second copy of the same data.\n- Cargo cannot put the target directory on a path that contains a colon. The dev folder name has one, so web and test builds set `CARGO_TARGET_DIR` to `work/.harbor-target` and run from the `engine-link` symlink. That directory is deleted after the final pack."}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-98cac0c8-1ed4-4570-abc1-d4bd55f19791-146","name":"write","input":{"file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224015__x42677a/work/Hands of Harbor: Second Opinion-Trauma Center: Second Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-224015/content/README.md","content":"# Adding a Night Ward case\n\nCases, lines, and strains are Rust tables the sim reads directly. Edit them and run `tests/run_all.py`. A bad speaker, an empty line, or a banned source name fails `story_lines_are_filled_and_music_defaults_quiet`.\n\n## A case\n\n`engine/crates/pav_core/src/games/surgery/content.rs` holds `CASES`. Each `CaseDef` is a name, a patient, a starting plate, a timer, a par score, opening vitals, and phases.\n\nA phase is a `PhaseDef`: a spawn list, whether it saves a checkpoint, a strain id (`NO_STRAIN` if none), a plate (`KEEP_PLATE` to keep the current one), a callout id, a scripted Code count, a gift bit (`G_HUSH`, `G_ECHO`, `G_DUET`), and the heat flag.\n\nA spawn is `s(kind, x, z, hidden, drain, axis)`. Kinds are the `K_` constants in `kinds.rs` (laceration, pool, bleeder, and the rest of the tray). `x` and `z` are on the plate, about −3 to 3. Hidden spawns stay down until a scanner pass. Drain is how fast an open hazard pulls vitals.\n\nWire the new case into `CASES` and give it a scene name `surgery/case/N` in `mod.rs` if it should boot on its own. Par is the S-rank line (100%). Ranks sit at 50, 70, 85, 100, and 115 percent of par.\n\n## A strain\n\nStrains are phases inside a case, not a separate file. Set `strain` on the phase to the strain id from `kinds.rs`. The strain runs when that phase becomes current. Parameters that used to be a toml block (length, intensity) are the fields already on `PhaseDef` and the tune sliders in `tune.rs`.\n\n## A line\n\n`story.rs` stores paper-theatre lines as `Line { who, text }`. `block(case_id, after)` returns the lines before a case and the lines after it. Add the strings to the matching `BEFORE_N` or `AFTER_N` list. `who` must be a cast name already used in the file (Mara Quill, Pet Nwosu, Bashir Haddad, Teddy Lark, Ottoline Voss, Cordelia Vane). Keep the text in the Night Ward voice. Do not use Hope Hospital, Caduceus, Stiles, GUILT, or Healing Touch.\n\n## A character\n\nSpeaking parts are the `who` strings above. A new speaker is a new name used consistently in `story.rs`, plus a paper rig if they should stand on stage. Rigs are the card builders in the surgery view. Seat colours for the four surgeons are `SEAT_COLOR` in `content.rs`.\n\n## Check\n\nFrom the dev folder, `python3 tests/run_all.py` prints only failures and `N passed, M failed`. The ignored balance sheet is separate:\n\n`cargo test -p pav_core --test surgery -- --ignored --nocapture balance_sheet`\n"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-98cac0c8-1ed4-4570-abc1-d4bd55f19791-147","name":"write","input":{"file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224015__x42677a/tmp/grok-goal-907ccca5ce3b/implementer/launch.py","content":"\"\"\"Two file:// launches, then shots of title, story, operation, dev, and about.\"\"\"\nimport json\nimport os\nimport traceback\nfrom pathlib import Path\n\nfrom playwright.sync_api import sync_playwright\n\nHTML = Path(\n    \"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224015__x42677a/work/\"\n    \"Hands of Harbor: Second Opinion-Trauma Center: Second Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-224015.html\"\n)\nSCRATCH = Path(\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224015__x42677a/tmp/grok-goal-907ccca5ce3b/implementer\")\nARGS = [\n    \"--enable-unsafe-webgpu\",\n    \"--enable-features=Vulkan\",\n    \"--use-webgpu-adapter=swiftshader\",\n    \"--use-vulkan=swiftshader\",\n    \"--use-angle=swiftshader\",\n]\nPAD = \"\"\"\n(() => { const buttons = Array.from({length: 17}, () => ({pressed: false, touched: false, value: 0}));\n  const pad = {id: 'DualSense Wireless Controller (STANDARD GAMEPAD)', index: 0, connected: true,\n               mapping: 'standard', timestamp: 0, axes: [0,0,0,0], buttons};\n  window.__pad = pad; navigator.getGamepads = () => [pad, null, null, null]; })();\n\"\"\"\n\n\ndef status(page):\n    return json.loads(page.evaluate(\"() => window.__game.status()\"))\n\n\ndef boot(page, url):\n    page.goto(url, wait_until=\"domcontentloaded\", timeout=60000)\n    page.wait_for_function(\"() => window.__game && window.__game.status\", timeout=45000)\n    page.wait_for_timeout(1200)\n    canvas = page.locator(\"canvas\")\n    if canvas.count():\n        canvas.first.click(position={\"x\": 200, \"y\": 200})\n\n\ndef press(page, key, n=1):\n    for _ in range(n):\n        page.keyboard.press(key)\n        page.wait_for_timeout(180)\n\n\ndef wait_screen(page, name, tries=40):\n    last = None\n    for _ in range(tries):\n        last = status(page)\n        if last.get(\"screen\") == name:\n            return last\n        page.wait_for_timeout(250)\n    return last\n\n\ndef shot(page, path):\n    path.parent.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)\n    page.screenshot(path=str(path))\n\n\ndef one_launch(p, n, url):\n    dest = SCRATCH / f\"launch-{n}\"\n    dest.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)\n    logs = []\n    browser = p.chromium.launch(headless=False, args=ARGS)\n    context = browser.new_context(viewport={\"width\": 1920, \"height\": 1080})\n    context.add_init_script(PAD)\n    page = context.new_page()\n    page.on(\"console\", lambda m: logs.append(f\"{m.type}: {m.text[:240]}\") if m.type == \"error\" else None)\n    page.on(\"pageerror\", lambda e: logs.append(f\"pageerror: {e}\"))\n    boot(page, url)\n    st = status(page)\n    box = page.evaluate(\n        \"\"\"() => {\n          const c = document.querySelector('canvas');\n          if (!c) return null;\n          return {w: c.width, h: c.height, cw: c.clientWidth, ch: c.clientHeight};\n        }\"\"\"\n    )\n    shot(page, dest / \"title.png\")\n    # Same input both launches: confirm on the title.\n    press(page, \"Enter\")\n    page.wait_for_timeout(400)\n    after = status(page)\n    (dest / \"status.json\").write_text(json.dumps({\"before\": st, \"after\": after, \"canvas\": box, \"console\": logs}, indent=2))\n    print(f\"LAUNCH {n} before\", st.get(\"screen\"), st.get(\"title\"), st.get(\"music\"), \"canvas\", box)\n    print(f\"LAUNCH {n} after\", after.get(\"screen\"), after.get(\"focus\"))\n    print(f\"LAUNCH {n} console\", logs[:8])\n    browser.close()\n    return st, after, box, logs\n\n\ndef shoot(p, url):\n    out = SCRATCH / \"shots\"\n    out.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)\n    browser = p.chromium.launch(headless=False, args=ARGS)\n    context = browser.new_context(viewport={\"width\": 1920, \"height\": 1080})\n    context.add_init_script(PAD)\n    page = context.new_page()\n    notes = {}\n\n    def grab(name, screen):\n        st = wait_screen(page, screen)\n        shot(page, out / f\"{name}.png\")\n        notes[name] = st.get(\"screen\") if st else None\n        print(\"SHOT\", name, notes[name])\n\n    boot(page, url)\n    grab(\"title\", \"title\")\n\n    press(page, \"Enter\")\n    press(page, \"ArrowDown\", 5)\n    press(page, \"Enter\")\n    grab(\"about\", \"about\")\n\n    boot(page, url)\n    press(page, \"Enter\")\n    press(page, \"Enter\")\n    grab(\"story\", \"story\")\n\n    boot(page, url)\n    press(page, \"Enter\")\n    press(page, \"ArrowDown\", 2)\n    press(page, \"Enter\")\n    press(page, \"Enter\")\n    grab(\"op\", \"op\")\n\n    press(page, \"Escape\")\n    press(page, \"ArrowDown\", 4)\n    press(page, \"Enter\")\n    grab(\"dev\", \"dev\")\n\n    (out / \"notes.json\").write_text(json.dumps(notes, indent=2))\n    browser.close()\n\n\ndef main():\n    os.environ.setdefault(\"PLAYWRIGHT_HOST_PLATFORM_OVERRIDE\", \"ubuntu24.04-x64\")\n    url = HTML.as_uri()\n    with sync_playwright() as p:\n        one_launch(p, 1, url)\n        one_launch(p, 2, url)\n        shoot(p, url)\n    print(\"DONE\")\n\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    try:\n        main()\n    except Exception:\n        traceback.print_exc()\n        raise\n"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-98cac0c8-1ed4-4570-abc1-d4bd55f19791-148","name":"run_terminal_command","input":{"command":"cd /home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224015__x42677a/work/engine-link && CARGO_TARGET_DIR=/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224015__x42677a/work/.harbor-target CARGO_BUILD_JOBS=6 bash scripts/build-web.sh --single-file --scene surgery/title --title \"Hands of Harbor: Second Opinion\" --description \"Night Ward. Keep the beat. Keep them alive.\" --theme-color \"#10282c\" --out \"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224015__x42677a/work/Hands of Harbor: Second Opinion-Trauma Center: Second Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-224015.html\"","description":"Repack HTML with final About interview text","block_until_ms":0}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1095,"output_tokens":3129,"cache_read_input_tokens":175232,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa38-de6f-7dc0-ae0d-e0f717ed75f2","uuid":"2f6c9bf0-205e-4aa7-a4f5-e302b690d6d8"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-98cac0c8-1ed4-4570-abc1-d4bd55f19791-145","content":"{\"type\":\"SearchReplace\",\"EditsApplied\":{\"old_string\":\"✔ This read a peak of 0.65 from the engine's cpal output during play.\",\"new_string\":\"✔ This read a peak of 0.65 from the engine's cpal output during play.\\n\\n## Deviations\\n\\n- Case and story tables live in Rust (`content.rs`, `story.rs`), not toml. The sim reads that one table. A toml loader would be a second copy of the same data.\\n- Cargo cannot put the target directory on a path that contains a colon. The dev folder name has one, so web and test builds set `CARGO_TARGET_DIR` to `work/.harbor-target` and run from the `engine-link` symlink. That directory is deleted after the final pack.\",\"tool_output_for_prompt\":\"The file /home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224015__x42677a/work/PLAN.md has been updated successfully.\",\"tool_output_for_prompt_concise\":\"The file /home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224015__x42677a/work/PLAN.md has been updated.\",\"absolute_path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224015__x42677a/work/PLAN.md\",\"edits\":{\"details\":[{\"old_string\":\"✔ This read a peak of 0.65 from the engine's cpal output during play.\",\"old_line\":811,\"new_string\":\"✔ This read a peak of 0.65 from the engine's cpal output during play.\\n\\n## Deviations\\n\\n- Case and story tables live in Rust (`content.rs`, `story.rs`), not toml. The sim reads that one table. A toml loader would be a second copy of the same data.\\n- Cargo cannot put the target directory on a path that contains a colon. The dev folder name has one, so web and test builds set `CARGO_TARGET_DIR` to `work/.harbor-target` and run from the `engine-link` symlink. That directory is deleted after the final pack.\",\"new_line\":811,\"context_before\":\"    a.getFloatTimeDomainData(b); for (const v of b) m = Math.max(m, Math.abs(v)); } return m; }; })();\\n\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n```\\n\",\"context_after\":\"\",\"line_prefix\":\"\"}]}}}","is_error":false},{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-98cac0c8-1ed4-4570-abc1-d4bd55f19791-146","content":"{\"type\":\"SearchReplace\",\"EditsApplied\":{\"old_string\":\"\",\"new_string\":\"# Adding a Night Ward case\\n\\nCases, lines, and strains are Rust tables the sim reads directly. Edit them and run `tests/run_all.py`. A bad speaker, an empty line, or a banned source name fails `story_lines_are_filled_and_music_defaults_quiet`.\\n\\n## A case\\n\\n`engine/crates/pav_core/src/games/surgery/content.rs` holds `CASES`. Each `CaseDef` is a name, a patient, a starting plate, a timer, a par score, opening vitals, and phases.\\n\\nA phase is a `PhaseDef`: a spawn list, whether it saves a checkpoint, a strain id (`NO_STRAIN` if none), a plate (`KEEP_PLATE` to keep the current one), a callout id, a scripted Code count, a gift bit (`G_HUSH`, `G_ECHO`, `G_DUET`), and the heat flag.\\n\\nA spawn is `s(kind, x, z, hidden, drain, axis)`. Kinds are the `K_` constants in `kinds.rs` (laceration, pool, bleeder, and the rest of the tray). `x` and `z` are on the plate, about −3 to 3. Hidden spawns stay down until a scanner pass. Drain is how fast an open hazard pulls vitals.\\n\\nWire the new case into `CASES` and give it a scene name `surgery/case/N` in `mod.rs` if it should boot on its own. Par is the S-rank line (100%). Ranks sit at 50, 70, 85, 100, and 115 percent of par.\\n\\n## A strain\\n\\nStrains are phases inside a case, not a separate file. Set `strain` on the phase to the strain id from `kinds.rs`. The strain runs when that phase becomes current. Parameters that used to be a toml block (length, intensity) are the fields already on `PhaseDef` and the tune sliders in `tune.rs`.\\n\\n## A line\\n\\n`story.rs` stores paper-theatre lines as `Line { who, text }`. `block(case_id, after)` returns the lines before a case and the lines after it. Add the strings to the matching `BEFORE_N` or `AFTER_N` list. `who` must be a cast name already used in the file (Mara Quill, Pet Nwosu, Bashir Haddad, Teddy Lark, Ottoline Voss, Cordelia Vane). Keep the text in the Night Ward voice. Do not use Hope Hospital, Caduceus, Stiles, GUILT, or Healing Touch.\\n\\n## A character\\n\\nSpeaking parts are the `who` strings above. A new speaker is a new name used consistently in `story.rs`, plus a paper rig if they should stand on stage. Rigs are the card builders in the surgery view. Seat colours for the four surgeons are `SEAT_COLOR` in `content.rs`.\\n\\n## Check\\n\\nFrom the dev folder, `python3 tests/run_all.py` prints only failures and `N passed, M failed`. The ignored balance sheet is separate:\\n\\n`cargo test -p pav_core --test surgery -- --ignored --nocapture balance_sheet`\\n\",\"tool_output_for_prompt\":\"The file /home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224015__x42677a/work/Hands of Harbor: Second Opinion-Trauma Center: Second Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-224015/content/README.md has been created.\",\"tool_output_for_prompt_concise\":\"The file /home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224015__x42677a/work/Hands of Harbor: Second Opinion-Trauma Center: Second Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-224015/content/README.md has been created.\",\"absolute_path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224015__x42677a/work/Hands of Harbor: Second Opinion-Trauma Center: Second Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-224015/content/README.md\",\"edits\":{\"details\":[{\"old_string\":\"\",\"old_line\":1,\"new_string\":\"# Adding a Night Ward case\\n\\nCases, lines, and strains are Rust tables the sim reads directly. Edit them and run `tests/run_all.py`. A bad speaker, an empty line, or a banned source name fails `story_lines_are_filled_and_music_defaults_quiet`.\\n\\n## A case\\n\\n`engine/crates/pav_core/src/games/surgery/content.rs` holds `CASES`. Each `CaseDef` is a name, a patient, a starting plate, a timer, a par score, opening vitals, and phases.\\n\\nA phase is a `PhaseDef`: a spawn list, whether it saves a checkpoint, a strain id (`NO_STRAIN` if none), a plate (`KEEP_PLATE` to keep the current one), a callout id, a scripted Code count, a gift bit (`G_HUSH`, `G_ECHO`, `G_DUET`), and the heat flag.\\n\\nA spawn is `s(kind, x, z, hidden, drain, axis)`. Kinds are the `K_` constants in `kinds.rs` (laceration, pool, bleeder, and the rest of the tray). `x` and `z` are on the plate, about −3 to 3. Hidden spawns stay down until a scanner pass. Drain is how fast an open hazard pulls vitals.\\n\\nWire the new case into `CASES` and give it a scene name `surgery/case/N` in `mod.rs` if it should boot on its own. Par is the S-rank line (100%). Ranks sit at 50, 70, 85, 100, and 115 percent of par.\\n\\n## A strain\\n\\nStrains are phases inside a case, not a separate file. Set `strain` on the phase to the strain id from `kinds.rs`. The strain runs when that phase becomes current. Parameters that used to be a toml block (length, intensity) are the fields already on `PhaseDef` and the tune sliders in `tune.rs`.\\n\\n## A line\\n\\n`story.rs` stores paper-theatre lines as `Line { who, text }`. `block(case_id, after)` returns the lines before a case and the lines after it. Add the strings to the matching `BEFORE_N` or `AFTER_N` list. `who` must be a cast name already used in the file (Mara Quill, Pet Nwosu, Bashir Haddad, Teddy Lark, Ottoline Voss, Cordelia Vane). Keep the text in the Night Ward voice. Do not use Hope Hospital, Caduceus, Stiles, GUILT, or Healing Touch.\\n\\n## A character\\n\\nSpeaking parts are the `who` strings above. A new speaker is a new name used consistently in `story.rs`, plus a paper rig if they should stand on stage. Rigs are the card builders in the surgery view. Seat colours for the four surgeons are `SEAT_COLOR` in `content.rs`.\\n\\n## Check\\n\\nFrom the dev folder, `python3 tests/run_all.py` prints only failures and `N passed, M failed`. The ignored balance sheet is separate:\\n\\n`cargo test -p pav_core --test surgery -- --ignored --nocapture balance_sheet`\\n\",\"new_line\":1,\"context_before\":\"\",\"context_after\":\"\",\"line_prefix\":\"\"}]}}}","is_error":false},{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-98cac0c8-1ed4-4570-abc1-d4bd55f19791-147","content":"{\"type\":\"SearchReplace\",\"EditsApplied\":{\"old_string\":\"\",\"new_string\":\"\\\"\\\"\\\"Two file:// launches, then shots of title, story, operation, dev, and about.\\\"\\\"\\\"\\nimport json\\nimport os\\nimport traceback\\nfrom pathlib import Path\\n\\nfrom playwright.sync_api import sync_playwright\\n\\nHTML = Path(\\n    \\\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224015__x42677a/work/\\\"\\n    \\\"Hands of Harbor: Second Opinion-Trauma Center: Second Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-224015.html\\\"\\n)\\nSCRATCH = Path(\\\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224015__x42677a/tmp/grok-goal-907ccca5ce3b/implementer\\\")\\nARGS = [\\n    \\\"--enable-unsafe-webgpu\\\",\\n    \\\"--enable-features=Vulkan\\\",\\n    \\\"--use-webgpu-adapter=swiftshader\\\",\\n    \\\"--use-vulkan=swiftshader\\\",\\n    \\\"--use-angle=swiftshader\\\",\\n]\\nPAD = \\\"\\\"\\\"\\n(() => { const buttons = Array.from({length: 17}, () => ({pressed: false, touched: false, value: 0}));\\n  const pad = {id: 'DualSense Wireless Controller (STANDARD GAMEPAD)', index: 0, connected: true,\\n               mapping: 'standard', timestamp: 0, axes: [0,0,0,0], buttons};\\n  window.__pad = pad; navigator.getGamepads = () => [pad, null, null, null]; })();\\n\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n\\n\\ndef status(page):\\n    return json.loads(page.evaluate(\\\"() => window.__game.status()\\\"))\\n\\n\\ndef boot(page, url):\\n    page.goto(url, wait_until=\\\"domcontentloaded\\\", timeout=60000)\\n    page.wait_for_function(\\\"() => window.__game && window.__game.status\\\", timeout=45000)\\n    page.wait_for_timeout(1200)\\n    canvas = page.locator(\\\"canvas\\\")\\n    if canvas.count():\\n        canvas.first.click(position={\\\"x\\\": 200, \\\"y\\\": 200})\\n\\n\\ndef press(page, key, n=1):\\n    for _ in range(n):\\n        page.keyboard.press(key)\\n        page.wait_for_timeout(180)\\n\\n\\ndef wait_screen(page, name, tries=40):\\n    last = None\\n    for _ in range(tries):\\n        last = status(page)\\n        if last.get(\\\"screen\\\") == name:\\n            return last\\n        page.wait_for_timeout(250)\\n    return last\\n\\n\\ndef shot(page, path):\\n    path.parent.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)\\n    page.screenshot(path=str(path))\\n\\n\\ndef one_launch(p, n, url):\\n    dest = SCRATCH / f\\\"launch-{n}\\\"\\n    dest.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)\\n    logs = []\\n    browser = p.chromium.launch(headless=False, args=ARGS)\\n    context = browser.new_context(viewport={\\\"width\\\": 1920, \\\"height\\\": 1080})\\n    context.add_init_script(PAD)\\n    page = context.new_page()\\n    page.on(\\\"console\\\", lambda m: logs.append(f\\\"{m.type}: {m.text[:240]}\\\") if m.type == \\\"error\\\" else None)\\n    page.on(\\\"pageerror\\\", lambda e: logs.append(f\\\"pageerror: {e}\\\"))\\n    boot(page, url)\\n    st = status(page)\\n    box = page.evaluate(\\n        \\\"\\\"\\\"() => {\\n          const c = document.querySelector('canvas');\\n          if (!c) return null;\\n          return {w: c.width, h: c.height, cw: c.clientWidth, ch: c.clientHeight};\\n        }\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n    )\\n    shot(page, dest / \\\"title.png\\\")\\n    # Same input both launches: confirm on the title.\\n    press(page, \\\"Enter\\\")\\n    page.wait_for_timeout(400)\\n    after = status(page)\\n    (dest / \\\"status.json\\\").write_text(json.dumps({\\\"before\\\": st, \\\"after\\\": after, \\\"canvas\\\": box, \\\"console\\\": logs}, indent=2))\\n    print(f\\\"LAUNCH {n} before\\\", st.get(\\\"screen\\\"), st.get(\\\"title\\\"), st.get(\\\"music\\\"), \\\"canvas\\\", box)\\n    print(f\\\"LAUNCH {n} after\\\", after.get(\\\"screen\\\"), after.get(\\\"focus\\\"))\\n    print(f\\\"LAUNCH {n} console\\\", logs[:8])\\n    browser.close()\\n    return st, after, box, logs\\n\\n\\ndef shoot(p, url):\\n    out = SCRATCH / \\\"shots\\\"\\n    out.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)\\n    browser = p.chromium.launch(headless=False, args=ARGS)\\n    context = browser.new_context(viewport={\\\"width\\\": 1920, \\\"height\\\": 1080})\\n    context.add_init_script(PAD)\\n    page = context.new_page()\\n    notes = {}\\n\\n    def grab(name, screen):\\n        st = wait_screen(page, screen)\\n        shot(page, out / f\\\"{name}.png\\\")\\n        notes[name] = st.get(\\\"screen\\\") if st else None\\n        print(\\\"SHOT\\\", name, notes[name])\\n\\n    boot(page, url)\\n    grab(\\\"title\\\", \\\"title\\\")\\n\\n    press(page, \\\"Enter\\\")\\n    press(page, \\\"ArrowDown\\\", 5)\\n    press(page, \\\"Enter\\\")\\n    grab(\\\"about\\\", \\\"about\\\")\\n\\n    boot(page, url)\\n    press(page, \\\"Enter\\\")\\n    press(page, \\\"Enter\\\")\\n    grab(\\\"story\\\", \\\"story\\\")\\n\\n    boot(page, url)\\n    press(page, \\\"Enter\\\")\\n    press(page, \\\"ArrowDown\\\", 2)\\n    press(page, \\\"Enter\\\")\\n    press(page, \\\"Enter\\\")\\n    grab(\\\"op\\\", \\\"op\\\")\\n\\n    press(page, \\\"Escape\\\")\\n    press(page, \\\"ArrowDown\\\", 4)\\n    press(page, \\\"Enter\\\")\\n    grab(\\\"dev\\\", \\\"dev\\\")\\n\\n    (out / \\\"notes.json\\\").write_text(json.dumps(notes, indent=2))\\n    browser.close()\\n\\n\\ndef main():\\n    os.environ.setdefault(\\\"PLAYWRIGHT_HOST_PLATFORM_OVERRIDE\\\", \\\"ubuntu24.04-x64\\\")\\n    url = HTML.as_uri()\\n    with sync_playwright() as p:\\n        one_launch(p, 1, url)\\n        one_launch(p, 2, url)\\n        shoot(p, url)\\n    print(\\\"DONE\\\")\\n\\n\\nif __name__ == \\\"__main__\\\":\\n    try:\\n        main()\\n    except Exception:\\n        traceback.print_exc()\\n        raise\