reenshot: Timeout 20000ms exceeded.\\nCall log:\\n  - taking page screenshot\\n    - disabled all CSS animations\\n  - waiting for fonts to load...\\n  - fonts loaded\\n\\n\",\"exit_code\":0,\"command\":\"export TMPDIR=/tmp/hbr-pw PLAYWRIGHT_HOST_PLATFORM_OVERRIDE=ubuntu24.04-x64\\nSCRATCH=\\\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224015__x42677a/tmp/grok-goal-907ccca5ce3b/implementer\\\"\\n# don't clobber a running suite log\\nwc -c \\\"$SCRATCH/suite.txt\\\" 2>/dev/null || true\\ntail -c 400 \\\"$SCRATCH/suite.txt\\\" 2>/dev/null || true\\necho\\nxvfb-run -a python3 \\\"$SCRATCH/launch.py\\\" > \\\"$SCRATCH/launch.txt\\\" 2>&1\\necho EXIT:$?\\ntail -c 2500 \\\"$SCRATCH/launch.txt\\\"\",\"truncated\":false,\"signal\":null,\"timed_out\":false,\"description\":\"Rerun file launches with screenshots that do not wait on animation\",\"current_dir\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224015__x42677a/work\",\"output_file\":\"/home/micha/.grok/sessions/%2Fhome%2Fmicha%2Fdev%2Fcc-matrix%2Fruns%2Fgrok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224015__x42677a%2Fwork/01a1aa38-de6f-7dc0-ae0d-e0f717ed75f2/terminal/call-61fb13a9-52b8-4007-9f89-e0e43ae573e6-157.log\",\"total_bytes\":2636}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa38-de6f-7dc0-ae0d-e0f717ed75f2","uuid":"d0b63bca-6884-48eb-823a-a2abb0b1e33d"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_605","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Status is working correctly. The title reads \"Hands of Harbor: Second Opinion\" and music is set to 0.\n\nScreenshot capture still times out after fonts load. The game loop appears to block the compositor, likely because Swiftshader is continuously redrawing a large mesh and keeping the GPU busy. I am considering alternatives: reading pixels directly from the canvas inside the page, or using Chrome's `Page.captureScreenshot` with `fromSurface: true`.\n\nPlaywright does not expose the needed capture method. A smaller viewport would still hang because the browser waits for the same GPU bitmap. The timeout occurs after fonts load, confirming the browser's GPU process is saturated and blocking capture. Stopping the game loop from JavaScript is not feasible. Hiding the canvas or using `document.documentElement` with `caret: \"hide\"` would not solve the underlying issue.\n\nI ruled out `chrome.debugger` and canvas-specific Playwright screenshot options. I am now testing a direct CDP session with `Page.captureScreenshot`, but I am unsure whether `fromSurface: false` captures the GPU surface or just the layout view.\n\nThe root cause is now clear: Swiftshader cannot composite the WebGPU canvas to the screenshot bitmap while the GPU is busy, and the game loop never idles because it calls requestAnimationFrame every frame.\n\nThe fix is to replace requestAnimationFrame with a no-op from JavaScript immediately before capturing. This stops the game loop and allows the browser to present the final frame, making the screenshot possible.\n\nThe plan is to inject the requestAnimationFrame replacement directly into the shot() function before capture. The canvas should retain the last presented frame once the loop stops, though double-buffered WebGPU canvases might clear it. suite.txt remains empty after 70 seconds, likely due to silent Cargo compilation. Status JSON will be saved even if screenshot capture fails.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-72c85b30-ce9c-4725-96e7-b730eaf24289-158","name":"search_replace","input":{"file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224015__x42677a/tmp/grok-goal-907ccca5ce3b/implementer/launch.py","old_string":"def shot(page, path):\n    path.parent.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)\n    page.screenshot(path=str(path), animations=\"disabled\", timeout=20000)","new_string":"def shot(page, path):\n    path.parent.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)\n    # The operation redraws forever. A capture waits on that paint unless the\n    # next animation frame is not requested.\n    page.evaluate(\n        \"\"\"() => {\n          window.requestAnimationFrame = () => 0;\n        }\"\"\"\n    )\n    page.wait_for_timeout(300)\n    page.screenshot(path=str(path), animations=\"disabled\", timeout=15000)"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1244,"output_tokens":846,"cache_read_input_tokens":187264,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa38-de6f-7dc0-ae0d-e0f717ed75f2","uuid":"c89125f6-a965-4a09-801b-e69ab3bd3278"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-72c85b30-ce9c-4725-96e7-b730eaf24289-158","content":"{\"type\":\"SearchReplace\",\"EditsApplied\":{\"old_string\":\"def shot(page, path):\\n    path.parent.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)\\n    page.screenshot(path=str(path), animations=\\\"disabled\\\", timeout=20000)\",\"new_string\":\"def shot(page, path):\\n    path.parent.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)\\n    # The operation redraws forever. A capture waits on that paint unless the\\n    # next animation frame is not requested.\\n    page.evaluate(\\n        \\\"\\\"\\\"() => {\\n          window.requestAnimationFrame = () => 0;\\n        }\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n    )\\n    page.wait_for_timeout(300)\\n    page.screenshot(path=str(path), animations=\\\"disabled\\\", timeout=15000)\",\"tool_output_for_prompt\":\"The file /home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224015__x42677a/tmp/grok-goal-907ccca5ce3b/implementer/launch.py has been updated successfully.\",\"tool_output_for_prompt_concise\":\"The file /home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224015__x42677a/tmp/grok-goal-907ccca5ce3b/implementer/launch.py has been updated.\",\"absolute_path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224015__x42677a/tmp/grok-goal-907ccca5ce3b/implementer/launch.py\",\"edits\":{\"details\":[{\"old_string\":\"def shot(page, path):\\n    path.parent.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)\\n    page.screenshot(path=str(path), animations=\\\"disabled\\\", timeout=20000)\",\"old_line\":58,\"new_string\":\"def shot(page, path):\\n    path.parent.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)\\n    # The operation redraws forever. A capture waits on that paint unless the\\n    # next animation frame is not requested.\\n    page.evaluate(\\n        \\\"\\\"\\\"() => {\\n          window.requestAnimationFrame = () => 0;\\n        }\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n    )\\n    page.wait_for_timeout(300)\\n    page.screenshot(path=str(path), animations=\\\"disabled\\\", timeout=15000)\",\"new_line\":58,\"context_before\":\"    return last\\n\\n\\n\",\"context_after\":\"\\n\\ndef one_launch(p, n, url):\\n\",\"line_prefix\":\"\"}]}}}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa38-de6f-7dc0-ae0d-e0f717ed75f2","uuid":"36d08cac-500d-4bb7-87be-0f65781c59eb"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_606","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Stopping the animation frame request may not stop winit if it captured the original function.\n\nReplacing requestAnimationFrame should work for subsequent calls. The thread yields between frames, so evaluate can run in between. Screenshot comes next. But killing the animation frame will freeze the game loop, so one_launch cannot continue pressing Enter.\n\nReordering one_launch to capture the title screen before killing the animation frame loop. The plan is: boot, status, press Enter, then status after. This proves input works while the loop is alive.\n\nThe title screen must be painted, so the title screenshot should come before pressing Enter. The menu screenshot can follow after the loop stops. The status JSON is the key evidence of the state change, not the image itself.\n\nA still title screenshot is acceptable. The launch proof requires matching status JSON across two runs plus a painted screenshot. The menu screenshot confirms the game rendered. The title shot must capture the last presented frame before Enter is pressed.\n\nThe launch sequence is now: record status, press Enter, wait, record status again, then screenshot the menu. The title screenshot will be taken separately via shoot() on a fresh boot. If the screenshot still hangs, CDP will be tried instead.\n\nThe suite output is empty because cargo buffers output when redirected. The launch suite is still running, so CPU contention may slow the screenshot. The real bug could be CPU starvation: if cargo compilation blocks the browser thread, the browser never yields to the screenshot protocol.\n\nThe screenshot likely failed because cargo test saturated the CPU and starved the browser thread. I will check if the suite is still running, and wait for it to finish before relaunching the browser.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-3a5a0ec7-ec90-4a35-89bf-