{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_611","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The screenshot still hangs after replacing requestAnimationFrame.\n\nThe hang is a GPU compositor issue with the WebGPU surface, not the rAF loop. I will try alternative capture methods like CDP without fromSurface, Playwright body screenshot, or xvfb ffmpeg.\n\nI will try capturing the X display directly with ImageMagick's `import`, `scrot`, or `xwd` while Chrome runs under xvfb. This bypasses Chrome's screenshot protocol entirely.\n\nI will check which capture tools are installed before updating the script. The xvfb-run DISPLAY environment variable will be passed to subprocess calls. I plan to use `import -window root` as the primary capture method, with `xwd` as a fallback.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-470379f5-d5fa-4005-bbd6-31a0685dd960-164","name":"run_terminal_command","input":{"command":"command -v import; command -v scrot; command -v xwd; command -v convert; command -v gnome-screenshot; python3 -c \"import PIL; print('pil', PIL.__version__)\"","description":"Find a framebuffer capture tool that skips Chrome's screenshot path"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1244,"output_tokens":612,"cache_read_input_tokens":196992,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa38-de6f-7dc0-ae0d-e0f717ed75f2","uuid":"bd31dc41-3ef3-41da-b8b3-48cc08faacd4"}
