{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_629","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The surgery path returns early from window_event and does not call handle_key.\n\nF3 does not toggle engine overlays. A full slow-frame case run risks the patient dying and showing a dead screen instead of results. The screenshots are evidence, not gating. I will try to reach results through an honest short path.\n\nNo JavaScript API exists to inject SurgeryCmd. Perfect mouse-driven surgery is too hard to script without field coordinates. I will capture the reachable screens honestly and study case 0's wounds and aim mapping to attempt a scripted suture.\n\nI will inspect the existing PNGs and read the title image. I will extract traffic lines from hub logs for hub.txt. I will check PROGRESS.md and locate the checklist. I will review about.json for the final reply. If scripted surgery is too complex, I will document that results were not reached due to missing cheats and incomplete full-frame execution.\n\nThe plan requires pad or mouse input to change focus, screen, or cursor. Keyboard Enter may be rejected by an adversarial verifier. I will try a mouse click or pad button instead. The previous boot click failed to advance the screen within the observation window. I need to determine why it was ignored.\n\nThe boot script clicks the canvas at 200,200 after waiting 1200 ms. The status is read immediately afterward and still shows title. The click was likely ignored.\n\nThe boot click likely failed because the frame had not yet processed it. If so, waiting after the click should advance the screen to menu. The launch test can simply be that click followed by a wait, since both launches use identical input and should reach the same screen. The current script already captures the title before pressing Enter.\n\nAny left mouse click on the title screen activates it and advances to the menu. The title screenshot must therefore be taken before that click. The click itself serves as the required state change for the launch test. Keyboard input will be reserved for navigating to other screens after the initial menu transition.\n\nThe stubbed pad is initialized before page scripts, so gilrs will see it. If the South button is pressed, it can confirm the launch test alongside the mouse click.\n\nI will poll the status every 250 ms for up to 25 seconds, since no timestamp is present. I will read title.png to verify it was painted. Case 0 might be reachable if it is a simple laceration and frames are fast enough; otherwise the solo plate is too slow.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-d021b6cb-0cb7-4437-8143-b5958e14fd71-32","name":"grep","input":{"pattern":"^PASS|^FAIL|pass.: true|traffic|↑|complete|errors","path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224015__x42677a/tmp/grok-goal-907ccca5ce3b/implementer","glob":"hub-*.txt"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-d021b6cb-0cb7-4437-8143-b5958e14fd71-33","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224015__x42677a/tmp/grok-goal-907ccca5ce3b/implementer/launch-1/title.png"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-d021b6cb-0cb7-4437-8143-b5958e14fd71-34","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224015__x42677a/tmp/grok-goal-907ccca5ce3b/implementer/shots/title.png"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-d021b6cb-0cb7-4437-8143-b5958e14fd71-35","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224015__x42677a/work/PROGRESS.md","limit":80}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":4666,"output_tokens":1765,"cache_read_input_tokens":63232,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa38-de6f-7dc0-ae0d-e0f717ed75f2","uuid":"ee989ebe-fbd1-4415-a5d1-42fbda5bbb98"}
