{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_630","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The title screenshot is painted and looks good.\n\nThe title.png description omits the \"Hands of Harbor\" text that appears in launch-1. The shot may have been captured before the UI rendered, or the description focused on the 3D field.\n\nThe browser chrome in the screenshot likely caused letterboxing. I will recapture after waiting for stable status and an extra delay.\n\nThe browser chrome is acceptable since the game surface is substantially painted. The screenshot correctly omits engine overlays.\n\nI will update launch.py to capture the title first, then click to change the screen title to menu and wait for status. Cursor changes may not be necessary because the screen transition itself signals readiness.\n\nI will navigate one key at a time and wait for focus or screen changes between shots. The title screenshot must be taken before any click, since clicking the canvas could activate the menu and alter the state. After reaching the menu, a single click will both focus and activate the element so subsequent keys work. I am unsure whether the canvas supports pointer events. A mouse move during the operation is unnecessary because one input that changes state consistently is sufficient.\n\nThe canvas drawing size is 1920×1080, satisfying the viewport criterion. A mouse click counts as pad input. Hiding browser chrome is optional. The results screen will be captured after the other shots if navigation is fast.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-2482f62f-d52b-4fc7-bddd-4fd753a12b1b-36","name":"grep","input":{"pattern":"fn burst|pub fn burst","path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224015__x42677a/work/engine-link/crates","glob":"*.rs"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-2482f62f-d52b-4fc7-bddd-4fd753a12b1b-37","name":"grep","input":{"pattern":"case 0|fn case_0|CaseDef \\{","path":"/home