{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-b0eb3d0f-4ae1-4cbc-a394-2f2b8bd427fa-53","content":"{\"type\":\"ReadFile\",\"FileContent\":{\"content\":\"1→//! Paper-theatre lines. Indices, not copies, live in the sim.\\n\\n#[derive(Clone, Copy)]\\npub struct Line {\\n    pub who: &'static str,\\n    pub text: &'static str,\\n}\\n\\nmacro_rules! L {\\n10→    ($($who:literal, $text:literal);* $(;)?) => {\\n        &[ $(Line { who: $who, text: $text }),* ]\\n    };\\n}\\n\\npub fn block(case_id: i8, after: bool) -> &'static [Line] {\\n    match (case_id, after) {\\n        (0, false) => BEFORE_0,\\n        (0, true) => AFTER_0,\\n        (1, false) => BEFORE_1,\\n20→        (1, true) => AFTER_1,\\n        (2, false) => BEFORE_2,\\n        (2, true) => AFTER_2,\\n        (3, false) => BEFORE_3,\\n        (3, true) => AFTER_3,\\n        (4, false) => BEFORE_4,\\n        (4, true) => AFTER_4,\\n        (5, false) => BEFORE_5,\\n        (5, true) => AFTER_5,\\n        (6, false) => BEFORE_6,\\n30→        (6, true) => AFTER_6,\\n        (7, false) => BEFORE_7,\\n        (7, true) => AFTER_7,\\n        _ => AFTER_7,\\n    }\\n}\\n\\npub fn all_lines() -> Vec<Line> {\\n    let mut v = Vec::new();\\n    for case_id in 0..8 {\\n40→        v.extend_from_slice(block(case_id, false));\\n        v.extend_from_slice(block(case_id, true));\\n    }\\n    v.extend_from_slice(CALLOUTS);\\n    v\\n}\\n\\nconst BEFORE_0: &[Line] = L![\\n    \\\"Ottoline Voss\\\", \\\"Night Ward, Mercy Harbor General. Port Verity is under a storm and the ferry is late.\\\";\\n    \\\"Ottoline Voss\\\", \\\"Mara Quill, you lead tonight. I will be in the gallery, not in your light.\\\";\\n50→    \\\"Mara Quill\\\", \\\"Understood, Chief. Who is on the table?\\\";\\n    \\\"Bashir Haddad\\\", \\\"Anton Deverell, crane crew at the west dock. A cable walked off the drum and took the forearm.\\\";\\n    \\\"Pet Nwosu\\\", \\\"I have the field set. My hands are noisy tonight. Say if you want them off the retractors.\\\";\\n    \\\"Mara Quill\\\", \\\"Stay. I trust the work more than the tremor.\\\";\\n    \\\"Teddy Lark\\\", \\\"I labeled the suction twice, because last time I labeled it once and Bashir looked at me like weather.\\\";\\n    \\\"Bashir Haddad\\\", \\\"The look stands. Pressure is soft. He lost blood on the ramp.\\\";\\n    \\\"Cordelia Vane\\\", \\\"Nothing in the smear but rope fiber and seawater. No strain. A plain wound, if any wound is plain.\\\";\\n    \\\"Mara Quill\\\", \\\"Then we do a plain thing well. Pet, count me in.\\\";\\n    \\\"Pet Nwosu\\\", \\\"On your word. Scalpel, then the bleed, then we close what the cable opened.\\\";\\n    \\\"Anton Deverell\\\", \\\"Don't let them take the arm. I still have a shift on Thursday.\\\";\\n60→];\\n\\nconst AFTER_0: &[Line] = L![\\n    \\\"Bashir Haddad\\\", \\\"Pulse is a working pulse. He will keep the arm.\\\";\\n    \\\"Pet Nwosu\\\", \\\"The last stitch sat down clean. I felt the tremor go quiet for it.\\\";\\n    \\\"Teddy Lark\\\", \\\"I have decided surgery is just sewing, if sewing could file a complaint.\\\";\\n    \\\"Mara Quill\\\", \\\"Write the chart. Cable injury, forearm, closure sound. No poetry.\\\";\\n    \\\"Ottoline Voss\\\", \\\"Poetry is how this ward gets careless. Good work, Doctor Quill.\\\";\\n    \\\"Cordelia Vane\\\", \\\"I kept the fiber. The harbor puts strange gifts in a wound. This one was only rope.\\\";\\n    \\\"Mara Quill\\\", \\\"Only rope is enough for one night.\\\";\\n70→    \\\"Bashir Haddad\\\", \\\"He asked for Thursday. I told him Thursday is a rumor until the dressing comes off.\\\";\\n    \\\"Pet Nwosu\\\", \\\"I'll sit with the monitor. Go wash. Your shoulders are up by your ears.\\\";\\n    \\\"Teddy Lark\\\", \\\"I will fetch coffee that tastes like a bandage. It is all the machine knows.\\\";\\n    \\\"Ottoline Voss\\\", \\\"Drink it standing. The board wants the ward's numbers by dawn.\\\";\\n    \\\"Mara Quill\\\", \\\"The ward's numbers are a man with a Thursday. They can wait until he wakes.\\\";\\n];\\n\\nconst BEFORE_1: &[Line] = L![\\n    \\\"Bashir Haddad\\\", \\\"Briony Pell, navigator on the evening ferry. Belly pain since the bar, then a faint on the stairs.\\\";\\n    \\\"Mara Quill\\\", \\\"Any fever?\\\";\\n80→    \\\"Bashir Haddad\\\", \\\"Low. She is guarding the right side. I do not like the silence in there.\\\";\",\"content_concise\":\"1→//! Paper-theatre lines. Indices, not copies, live in the sim.\\n\\n#[derive(Clone, Copy)]\\npub struct Line {\\n    pub who: &'static str,\\n    pub text: &'static str,\\n}\\n\\nmacro_rules! L {\\n10→    ($($who:literal, $text:literal);* $(;)?) => {\\n        &[ $(Line { who: $who, text: $text }),* ]\\n    };\\n}\\n\\npub fn block(case_id: i8, after: bool) -> &'static [Line] {\\n    match (case_id, after) {\\n        (0, false) => BEFORE_0,\\n        (0, true) => AFTER_0,\\n        (1, false) => BEFORE_1,\\n20→        (1, true) => AFTER_1,\\n        (2, false) => BEFORE_2,\\n        (2, true) => AFTER_2,\\n        (3, false) => BEFORE_3,\\n        (3, true) => AFTER_3,\\n        (4, false) => BEFORE_4,\\n        (4, true) => AFTER_4,\\n        (5, false) => BEFORE_5,\\n        (5, true) => AFTER_5,\\n        (6, false) => BEFORE_6,\\n30→        (6, true) => AFTER_6,\\n        (7, false) => BEFORE_7,\\n        (7, true) => AFTER_7,\\n        _ => AFTER_7,\\n    }\\n}\\n\\npub fn all_lines() -> Vec<Line> {\\n    let mut v = Vec::new();\\n    for case_id in 0..8 {\\n40→        v.extend_from_slice(block(case_id, false));\\n        v.extend_from_slice(block(case_id, true));\\n    }\\n    v.extend_from_slice(CALLOUTS);\\n    v\\n}\\n\\nconst BEFORE_0: &[Line] = L![\\n    \\\"Ottoline Voss\\\", \\\"Night Ward, Mercy Harbor General. Port Verity is under a storm and the ferry is late.\\\";\\n    \\\"Ottoline Voss\\\", \\\"Mara Quill, you lead tonight. I will be in the gallery, not in your light.\\\";\\n50→    \\\"Mara Quill\\\", \\\"Understood, Chief. Who is on the table?\\\";\\n    \\\"Bashir Haddad\\\", \\\"Anton Deverell, crane crew at the west dock. A cable walked off the drum and took the forearm.\\\";\\n    \\\"Pet Nwosu\\\", \\\"I have the field set. My hands are noisy tonight. Say if you want them off the retractors.\\\";\\n    \\\"Mara Quill\\\", \\\"Stay. I trust the work more than the tremor.\\\";\\n    \\\"Teddy Lark\\\", \\\"I labeled the suction twice, because last time I labeled it once and Bashir looked at me like weather.\\\";\\n    \\\"Bashir Haddad\\\", \\\"The look stands. Pressure is soft. He lost blood on the ramp.\\\";\\n    \\\"Cordelia Vane\\\", \\\"Nothing in the smear but rope fiber and seawater. No strain. A plain wound, if any wound is plain.\\\";\\n    \\\"Mara Quill\\\", \\\"Then we do a plain thing well. Pet, count me in.\\\";\\n    \\\"Pet Nwosu\\\", \\\"On your word. Scalpel, then the bleed, then we close what the cable opened.\\\";\\n    \\\"Anton Deverell\\\", \\\"Don't let them take the arm. I still have a shift on Thursday.\\\";\\n60→];\\n\\nconst AFTER_0: &[Line] = L![\\n    \\\"Bashir Haddad\\\", \\\"Pulse is a working pulse. He will keep the arm.\\\";\\n    \\\"Pet Nwosu\\\", \\\"The last stitch sat down clean. I felt the tremor go quiet for it.\\\";\\n    \\\"Teddy Lark\\\", \\\"I have decided surgery is just sewing, if sewing could file a complaint.\\\";\\n    \\\"Mara Quill\\\", \\\"Write the chart. Cable injury, forearm, closure sound. No poetry.\\\";\\n    \\\"Ottoline Voss\\\", \\\"Poetry is how this ward gets careless. Good work, Doctor Quill.\\\";\\n    \\\"Cordelia Vane\\\", \\\"I kept the fiber. The harbor puts strange gifts in a wound. This one was only rope.\\\";\\n    \\\"Mara Quill\\\", \\\"Only rope is enough for one night.\\\";\\n70→    \\\"Bashir Haddad\\\", \\\"He asked for Thursday. I told him Thursday is a rumor until the dressing comes off.\\\";\\n    \\\"Pet Nwosu\\\", \\\"I'll sit with the monitor. Go wash. Your shoulders are up by your ears.\\\";\\n    \\\"Teddy Lark\\\", \\\"I will fetch coffee that tastes like a bandage. It is all the machine knows.\\\";\\n    \\\"Ottoline Voss\\\", \\\"Drink it standing. The board wants the ward's numbers by dawn.\\\";\\n    \\\"Mara Quill\\\", \\\"The ward's numbers are a man with a Thursday. They can wait until he wakes.\\\";\\n];\\n\\nconst BEFORE_1: &[Line] = L![\\n    \\\"Bashir Haddad\\\", \\\"Briony Pell, navigator on the evening ferry. Belly pain since the bar, then a faint on the stairs.\\\";\\n    \\\"Mara Quill\\\", \\\"Any fever?\\\";\\n80→    \\\"Bashir Haddad\\\", \\\"Low. She is guarding the right side. I do not like the silence in there.\\\";\",\"absolute_path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224015__x42677a/work/Hands of Harbor: Second Opinion-Trauma Center: Second Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-224015/engine/crates/pav_core/src/games/surgery/story.rs\",\"offset\":null,\"limit\":80,\"raw_output\":\"//! Paper-theatre lines. Indices, not copies, live in the sim.\\n\\n#[derive(Clone, Copy)]\\npub struct Line {\\n    pub who: &'static str,\\n    pub text: &'static str,\\n}\\n\\nmacro_rules! L {\\n    ($($who:literal, $text:literal);* $(;)?) => {\\n        &[ $(Line { who: $who, text: $text }),* ]\\n    };\\n}\\n\\npub fn block(case_id: i8, after: bool) -> &'static [Line] {\\n    match (case_id, after) {\\n        (0, false) => BEFORE_0,\\n        (0, true) => AFTER_0,\\n        (1, false) => BEFORE_1,\\n        (1, true) => AFTER_1,\\n        (2, false) => BEFORE_2,\\n        (2, true) => AFTER_2,\\n        (3, false) => BEFORE_3,\\n        (3, true) => AFTER_3,\\n        (4, false) => BEFORE_4,\\n        (4, true) => AFTER_4,\\n        (5, false) => BEFORE_5,\\n        (5, true) => AFTER_5,\\n        (6, false) => BEFORE_6,\\n        (6, true) => AFTER_6,\\n        (7, false) => BEFORE_7,\\n        (7, true) => AFTER_7,\\n        _ => AFTER_7,\\n    }\\n}\\n\\npub fn all_lines() -> Vec<Line> {\\n    let mut v = Vec::new();\\n    for case_id in 0..8 {\\n        v.extend_from_slice(block(case_id, false));\\n        v.extend_from_slice(block(case_id, true));\\n    }\\n    v.extend_from_slice(CALLOUTS);\\n    v\\n}\\n\\nconst BEFORE_0: &[Line] = L![\\n    \\\"Ottoline Voss\\\", \\\"Night Ward, Mercy Harbor General. Port Verity is under a storm and the ferry is late.\\\";\\n    \\\"Ottoline Voss\\\", \\\"Mara Quill, you lead tonight. I will be in the gallery, not in your light.\\\";\\n    \\\"Mara Quill\\\", \\\"Understood, Chief. Who is on the table?\\\";\\n    \\\"Bashir Haddad\\\", \\\"Anton Deverell, crane crew at the west dock. A cable walked off the drum and took the forearm.\\\";\\n    \\\"Pet Nwosu\\\", \\\"I have the field set. My hands are noisy tonight. Say if you want them off the retractors.\\\";\\n    \\\"Mara Quill\\\", \\\"Stay. I trust the work more than the tremor.\\\";\\n    \\\"Teddy Lark\\\", \\\"I labeled the suction twice, because last time I labeled it once and Bashir looked at me like weather.\\\";\\n    \\\"Bashir Haddad\\\", \\\"The look stands. Pressure is soft. He lost blood on the ramp.\\\";\\n    \\\"Cordelia Vane\\\", \\\"Nothing in the smear but rope fiber and seawater. No strain. A plain wound, if any wound is plain.\\\";\\n    \\\"Mara Quill\\\", \\\"Then we do a plain thing well. Pet, count me in.\\\";\\n    \\\"Pet Nwosu\\\", \\\"On your word. Scalpel, then the bleed, then we close what the cable opened.\\\";\\n    \\\"Anton Deverell\\\", \\\"Don't let them take the arm. I still have a shift on Thursday.\\\";\\n];\\n\\nconst AFTER_0: &[Line] = L![\\n    \\\"Bashir Haddad\\\", \\\"Pulse is a working pulse. He will keep the arm.\\\";\\n    \\\"Pet Nwosu\\\", \\\"The last stitch sat down clean. I felt the tremor go quiet for it.\\\";\\n    \\\"Teddy Lark\\\", \\\"I have decided surgery is just sewing, if sewing could file a complaint.\\\";\\n    \\\"Mara Quill\\\", \\\"Write the chart. Cable injury, forearm, closure sound. No poetry.\\\";\\n    \\\"Ottoline Voss\\\", \\\"Poetry is how this ward gets careless. Good work, Doctor Quill.\\\";\\n    \\\"Cordelia Vane\\\", \\\"I kept the fiber. The harbor puts strange gifts in a wound. This one was only rope.\\\";\\n    \\\"Mara Quill\\\", \\\"Only rope is enough for one night.\\\";\\n    \\\"Bashir Haddad\\\", \\\"He asked for Thursday. I told him Thursday is a rumor until the dressing comes off.\\\";\\n    \\\"Pet Nwosu\\\", \\\"I'll sit with the monitor. Go wash. Your shoulders are up by your ears.\\\";\\n    \\\"Teddy Lark\\\", \\\"I will fetch coffee that tastes like a bandage. It is all the machine knows.\\\";\\n    \\\"Ottoline Voss\\\", \\\"Drink it standing. The board wants the ward's numbers by dawn.\\\";\\n    \\\"Mara Quill\\\", \\\"The ward's numbers are a man with a Thursday. They can wait until he wakes.\\\";\\n];\\n\\nconst BEFORE_1: &[Line] = L![\\n    \\\"Bashir Haddad\\\", \\\"Briony Pell, navigator on the evening ferry. Belly pain since the bar, then a faint on the stairs.\\\";\\n    \\\"Mara Quill\\\", \\\"Any fever?\\\";\\n    \\\"Bashir Haddad\\\", \\\"Low. She is guarding the right side. I do not like the silence in there.\\\";\\n\",\"total_lines\":312}}","is_error":false},{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-b0eb3d0f-4ae1-4cbc-a394-2f2b8bd427fa-54","content":"{\"type\":\"ReadFile\",\"FileContent\":{\"content\":\"1→//! One tick of the operation. Gameplay happens here, where the input is.\\n\\nuse glam::Vec3;\\n\\nuse super::content::{self, case_def, G_DUET, G_ECHO, G_HUSH};\\nuse super::hazard::{self, Hit};\\nuse super::kinds::*;\\nuse super::*;\\nuse super::{bot, story};\\n10→use crate::games::Outcome;\\nuse crate::frame::SimEvent;\\nuse crate::input::{surg, InputFrame, SurgeonInput};\\nuse crate::sim::Sim;\\n\\npub fn tick(g: &mut Surgery, sim: &mut Sim, input: &InputFrame, dt: f32, events: &mut Vec<SimEvent>, had_cmd: bool) {\\n    if g.outcome == Outcome::Lost && g.mode == M_DEAD {\\n        return;\\n    }\\n    let dt = dt.max(0.0);\\n20→    match g.mode {\\n        M_STORY if !had_cmd => {\\n            if confirmed(input) {\\n                let lines = story::block(g.case_id, g.story_after);\\n                if (g.story_i as usize) + 1 >= lines.len() {\\n                    g.end_story();\\n                } else {\\n                    g.story_i = g.story_i.saturating_add(1);\\n                    cue(events, CUE_VOICE, 0.0, 0.0, 0.7, 0.9 + (g.story_i as f32 % 5.0) * 0.04);\\n                }\\n30→            }\\n            return;\\n        }\\n        M_CHART if !had_cmd => {\\n            if confirmed(input) {\\n                g.mode = M_OP;\\n                g.phase_ready = false;\\n                cue(events, CUE_OK, 0.0, 0.0, 0.6, 1.0);\\n            }\\n            return;\\n40→        }\\n        M_RESULTS if !had_cmd => {\\n            if confirmed(input) && g.campaign && g.outcome == Outcome::Playing {\\n                g.mode = M_STORY;\\n                g.story_after = true;\\n                g.story_i = 0;\\n            }\\n            return;\\n        }\\n        M_CARD => {\\n50→            g.card_t += dt;\\n            return;\\n        }\\n        M_MIRROR => {\\n            mirror_predict(g, input, dt);\\n            return;\\n        }\\n        M_TITLE | M_DEAD => return,\\n        M_OP | M_ATTRACT => {}\\n        _ => return,\\n60→    }\",\"content_concise\":\"1→//! One tick of the operation. Gameplay happens here, where the input is.\\n\\nuse glam::Vec3;\\n\\nuse super::content::{self, case_def, G_DUET, G_ECHO, G_HUSH};\\nuse super::hazard::{self, Hit};\\nuse super::kinds::*;\\nuse super::*;\\nuse super::{bot, story};\\n10→use crate::games::Outcome;\\nuse crate::frame::SimEvent;\\nuse crate::input::{surg, InputFrame, SurgeonInput};\\nuse crate::sim::Sim;\\n\\npub fn tick(g: &mut Surgery, sim: &mut Sim, input: &InputFrame, dt: f32, events: &mut Vec<SimEvent>, had_cmd: bool) {\\n    if g.outcome == Outcome::Lost && g.mode == M_DEAD {\\n        return;\\n    }\\n    let dt = dt.max(0.0);\\n20→    match g.mode {\\n        M_STORY if !had_cmd => {\\n            if confirmed(input) {\\n                let lines = story::block(g.case_id, g.story_after);\\n                if (g.story_i as usize) + 1 >= lines.len() {\\n                    g.end_story();\\n                } else {\\n                    g.story_i = g.story_i.saturating_add(1);\\n                    cue(events, CUE_VOICE, 0.0, 0.0, 0.7, 0.9 + (g.story_i as f32 % 5.0) * 0.04);\\n                }\\n30→            }\\n            return;\\n        }\\n        M_CHART if !had_cmd => {\\n            if confirmed(input) {\\n                g.mode = M_OP;\\n                g.phase_ready = false;\\n                cue(events, CUE_OK, 0.0, 0.0, 0.6, 1.0);\\n            }\\n            return;\\n40→        }\\n        M_RESULTS if !had_cmd => {\\n            if confirmed(input) && g.campaign && g.outcome == Outcome::Playing {\\n                g.mode = M_STORY;\\n                g.story_after = true;\\n                g.story_i = 0;\\n            }\\n            return;\\n        }\\n        M_CARD => {\\n50→            g.card_t += dt;\\n            return;\\n        }\\n        M_MIRROR => {\\n            mirror_predict(g, input, dt);\\n            return;\\n        }\\n        M_TITLE | M_DEAD => return,\\n        M_OP | M_ATTRACT => {}\\n        _ => return,\\n60→    }\",\"absolute_path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224015__x42677a/work/Hands of Harbor: Second Opinion-Trauma Center: Second Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-224015/engine/crates/pav_core/src/games/surgery/ops.rs\",\"offset\":1,\"limit\":60,\"raw_output\":\"//! One tick of the operation. Gameplay happens here, where the input is.\\n\\nuse glam::Vec3;\\n\\nuse super::content::{self, case_def, G_DUET, G_ECHO, G_HUSH};\\nuse super::hazard::{self, Hit};\\nuse super::kinds::*;\\nuse super::*;\\nuse super::{bot, story};\\nuse crate::games::Outcome;\\nuse crate::frame::SimEvent;\\nuse crate::input::{surg, InputFrame, SurgeonInput};\\nuse crate::sim::Sim;\\n\\npub fn tick(g: &mut Surgery, sim: &mut Sim, input: &InputFrame, dt: f32, events: &mut Vec<SimEvent>, had_cmd: bool) {\\n    if g.outcome == Outcome::Lost && g.mode == M_DEAD {\\n        return;\\n    }\\n    let dt = dt.max(0.0);\\n    match g.mode {\\n        M_STORY if !had_cmd => {\\n            if confirmed(input) {\\n                let lines = story::block(g.case_id, g.story_after);\\n                if (g.story_i as usize) + 1 >= lines.len() {\\n                    g.end_story();\\n                } else {\\n                    g.story_i = g.story_i.saturating_add(1);\\n                    cue(events, CUE_VOICE, 0.0, 0.0, 0.7, 0.9 + (g.story_i as f32 % 5.0) * 0.04);\\n                }\\n            }\\n            return;\\n        }\\n        M_CHART if !had_cmd => {\\n            if confirmed(input) {\\n                g.mode = M_OP;\\n                g.phase_ready = false;\\n                cue(events, CUE_OK, 0.0, 0.0, 0.6, 1.0);\\n            }\\n            return;\\n        }\\n        M_RESULTS if !had_cmd => {\\n            if confirmed(input) && g.campaign && g.outcome == Outcome::Playing {\\n                g.mode = M_STORY;\\n                g.story_after = true;\\n                g.story_i = 0;\\n            }\\n            return;\\n        }\\n        M_CARD => {\\n            g.card_t += dt;\\n            return;\\n        }\\n        M_MIRROR => {\\n            mirror_predict(g, input, dt);\\n            return;\\n        }\\n        M_TITLE | M_DEAD => return,\\n        M_OP | M_ATTRACT => {}\\n        _ => return,\\n    }\\n\",\"total_lines\":805}}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa38-de6f-7dc0-ae0d-e0f717ed75f2","uuid":"978b27c1-db0a-4b06-8d43-6eb14b690104"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_639","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"BEFORE_0 contains 12 lines.\n\nTwelve confirms are needed to advance through the story. The shell screen remains \"story\" until the mode switches to \"chart\" and then \"op\". This sequence takes roughly 15 to 40 seconds.\n\nThe plan is to loop Enter until the screen becomes \"chart\", then shoot the story, then continue until \"op\". The about menu requires five downs and one Enter. The preferred approach uses separate boots for each screen to avoid the long story. Boot 1 handles title and input twice. Boot 3 covers title, shot, menu, and about. Boot 4 covers menu, continue, and a shorter story shot. Boot 5 covers case files, op, escape, and dev. The case files path is much shorter than the full twelve-line story.\n\nThe case files path moves two downs to Case Files, enters to files, then enters to op. It shots op, escapes to pause, moves four downs to Dev Mode, enters to dev, and shots dev. Story is a separate short boot: title, menu, continue, wait for story, shot. About is title, menu, five downs, enter, shot. Reloading the same browser is faster than launching new ones for shots, but fresh browsers are cleaner for the two launches.\n\nA mouse click on the title activates the menu. The pointer hit-test logic sets focus to the hovered element every frame. This conflicts with ArrowDown navigation in the menu. The pointer must be cleared before keyboard input.\n\nThe mouse will be held at (200, 200) throughout the sequence. That position sits above all menu rows, so pointer hit-tests will not interfere with keyboard navigation.\n\nThe pad south button is edge-triggered, so pressing it once produces a single confirm and does not need to be held. The device mode will switch to gamepad when only the pad is active, since no mouse movement or click occurs.\n\nBoth launches will show the same status change: screen title to menu and device keyboard to gamepad. The Gilrs high-level API updates button state correctly when events are drained, so is_pressed works as expected. The first next_event call connects the gamepad.\n\nThe event drain loop processes every event each frame, including the initial connection. If the gamepad button is already pressed when the pad is first discovered, the initial state copy captures it. The edge trigger then fires on the first frame because was.south is false.\n\nThe boot script will not click during setup. It polls for the title screen, takes a screenshot, and pulses the pad button to trigger the launch. If the screen does not change within twenty seconds, it falls back to a mouse click at (200, 200). Both launches will try the pad first; if that fails, they will record the failure and attempt the mouse fallback so the second launch can learn from the first.\n\nThe boot script will use a `drive` helper that takes a method argument. It evaluates JavaScript to press the pad button or clicks the canvas at (200, 200). If the first launch fails with the pad, the second launch will use the same mouse fallback.\n\nThe drive helper now waits up to twenty seconds for any change in screen, focus, or device state. It then releases the pad button. If the pad fails to advance the game, the script records that failure and falls back to a mouse click. Two full launches are expensive, so probing with a quick test is not practical.\n\nThe pad timeout is now eight seconds instead of twenty. Both launches will follow the exact same sequence: try pad first, fall back to mouse if the screen does not change, and record which method succeeded. If pad fails on both runs but mouse succeeds on both, the after states will match. If pad is flaky and only works once, the two launches will diverge and need fixing. The canvas does not need to be focused before clicking; `page.bring_to_front()` and a click are sufficient for the mouse path.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-10a