{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_640","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"gamepad.mapping() must return GamepadMappingType::Standard.\n\nThe web_sys mapping pattern should correctly convert the \"standard\" string to GamepadMappingType::Standard. Buttons, axes, and id return the expected types. The stub implementation looks viable.\n\nWriting launch.py and hub.txt next. Then running the browser test and checking suite.txt for 13 passed tests. Results may be added if time allows. No keyboard shortcut was found for dev commands.\n\nAim mapping could allow clicking wounds directly, but that may take too long if launches are slow. Launches and menu shots come first. hub.txt is being written now so item 7 can complete while launches run. The goal plan checklist will be updated after launch evidence exists.\n\nThe full checklist section must be read before editing. PROGRESS.md will be updated at the end. The server can stop after hub.txt is written because file:// launches do not need it. The .harbor-target file should only be deleted after launches finish and no cargo remains, since the bot change does not require a rebuild.\n\nThe server will stay running until the end so hub verification can be re-run if needed. The p4 traffic detail was truncated, so the exact file will be quoted. The hub-leave check passed with \"void (host-left)\". I will also verify suite.txt ends with 13 passed tests and check about.json to confirm feedback text is in the packed HTML.\n\nI will verify the screenshot dimensions later. The launch-1 title image includes browser chrome, so the game canvas is not fullscreen.\n\nThe 1920x1080 screenshots include browser chrome, but the canvas buffer is substantially painted and meets the viewport size requirement. Using `--start-fullscreen` or `--kiosk` could hide chrome if needed.\n\nThe canvas element is 1920 CSS pixels wide, matching the window and xvfb display. Browser chrome extends beyond that visible area, so the screenshot includes chrome while the layout viewport stays at 1920x1080.\n\nNo special chrome-less launch mode is needed. The script will use `--disable-infobars` and `--hide-scrollbars`. A check for monochrome screenshots will be added via ffmpeg or identify. The launch script is being written now. Keyboard input may fail if the canvas is not focused.\n\nPlaywright keyboard input targets the focused element. If winit listens on the canvas, un-focused keys are lost. The script must ensure the canvas receives focus before pressing keys.\n\nThe previous shoot() confirmed Enter reached the game after a canvas click. The new script will click at (200,200) to focus the canvas before keyboard input, and call canvas.focus() via JavaScript if needed.\n\nClicking the canvas to focus it would accidentally activate the menu item under the cursor. The script will instead set `tabIndex = 0` on the canvas element via JavaScript to gain focus without triggering a click.\n\nA `wait_pred` helper polls page status until a predicate matches, with a 22-second timeout. A `tap` helper presses a key and then waits for the expected state. If `canvas.focus()` is insufficient, window-level key events should still reach winit.\n\nA `down_to` helper will press ArrowDown until the focus and screen match the target. Each step will be logged. Story, op, dev, and about shots are planned. Results will be checked after the op screen appears.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-6d68aa1d-064d-4838-b283-8734bc82639d-56","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224015__x42677a/work/engine-link/crates/pav_core/src/games/surgery/content.rs","offset":100,"limit":70}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-6d68aa1d-064d-4838-b283-8734bc82639d-57","name":"grep","input":{"pattern":"fn aim|mouse.*field|screen_to|unproject|aim_hit","path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224015__x426