46,10,54,53,56,58,102,110,32,97,105,109,95,114,105,103,40,97,112,112,58,32,38,109,117,116,32,65,112,112,41,32,123,10,60,47,119,111,114,107,115,112,97,99,101,95,114,101,115,117,108,116,62],\"stderr\":[],\"exit_code\":0,\"match_count\":2,\"file_matches\":[{\"path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224015__x42677a/work/engine-link/crates/pav_app/src/product.rs\",\"matches\":[{\"line_number\":169,\"content\":\"    /// Shell step plus one frame of surgeon hands. `aim` is the mouse on the field, if it hit.\"},{\"line_number\":658,\"content\":\"fn aim_rig(app: &mut App) {\"}]}]}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa38-de6f-7dc0-ae0d-e0f717ed75f2","uuid":"62934ca0-6b5d-43be-af3d-ffc83162a4e6"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_641","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Case 0 spawns are earlier in the file.\n\nI will not spend more time on the operation. The results screen cannot be opened without finishing the operation, so I will record this in shots/notes.json and ship the required gating checks.\n\nI will write files and run. I noted the image reader works despite missing PIL. I will record console errors in the launch script. The pad pulse must hold for 500ms so the next frame registers it, since a longer frame interval could otherwise release the button before the game sees it.\n\nThe pad pulse will hold until the screen changes, then release. This ensures the first frame sees the edge. Keyboard keys are instantaneous and may be missed if pressed before the frame loop processes them.\n\nKeyboard presses are actually safe. The event loop queues keydown and processes it before the next redraw, so a quick press during a long frame still registers for the following frame. The earlier failure happened because keys were pressed without waiting between effects, causing extras to be cleared.\n\nA 400ms wait was too short for the frame interval, so the status had not updated. Pressing Enter once and polling for up to 20 seconds might work without the pad. The criterion requires pad or mouse input, so the pad button will be held until the screen changes. If the pad is not detected, a single held mouse click will serve as fallback; queued clicks are processed on the next event turn and consumed by the redraw.\n\nI will apply the same deterministic input sequence to both launches. Each launch holds pad south until the screen changes or 12 seconds pass, then falls back to a single mouse click if still on the title screen. This guarantees identical behavior whether the pad works or not. I will record the device field as gamepad if the pad registers. If south does not map to button 0, I can try buttons[0] instead.\n\nI will write hub.txt and launch.py, then run xvfb. I will check suite.txt to confirm the suite is green. The script timeout should be about seven minutes to cover both launches and shots.\n\nI will start the browser job in the background with block_until_ms set to 0. While it runs, I will write hub.txt, read suite.txt, and draft PROGRESS content. The hub server can remain active during this time.\n\nBrowsers will run sequentially, not in parallel. The hub server is small and safe alongside them. TMPDIR=/tmp/hbr-pw is required for Chrome sockets and must not be scratch.","signature":""},{"type":"text","text":"The title is painted, but keys were batched into one frame, so Enter never left the title. I’ll hold one pad button until the status changes, then retake the shots."},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-5a15c029-9f7f-49bd-ba43-28f8c437366e-58","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224015__x42677a/tmp/grok-goal-907ccca5ce3b/implementer/suite.txt","offset":1,"limit":30}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-5a15c029-9f7f-49bd-ba43-28f8c437366e-59","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/.grok/sessions/%2Fhome%2Fmicha%2Fdev%2Fcc-matrix%2Fruns%2Fgrok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224015__x42677a%2Fwork/01a1aa38-de6f-7dc0-ae0d-e0f717ed75f2/goal/plan.md","offset":30,"limit":20}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":4144,"output_tokens":1566,"cache_read_input_tokens":92032,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa38-de6f-7dc0-ae0d-e0f717ed75f2","uuid":"bd4dfe9c-d08a-4e74-afee-cf14c6235d45"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-5a15c029-9f7f-49bd-ba43-28f8c437366e-58","content":"{\"type\":\"ReadFile\",\"FileContent\":{\"content\":\"1→13 passed, 0 failed\\n\",\"content_concise\":\"1→13 passed, 0 failed\\n\",\"absolute_path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224015__x42677a/tmp/grok-goal-907ccca5ce3b/implementer/suite.txt\",\"offset\":1,\"limit\":30,\"raw_output\":\"13 passed, 0 failed\\n\",\"total_lines\":1}}","is_error":false},{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-5a15c029-9f7f-49bd-ba43-28f8c437366e-59","content":"{\"type\":\"ReadFile\",\"FileContent\":{\"content\":\"30→Work root only. New dev subfolder; clone `https://github.com/michaelcrosato/shardfall` at or after `49ef2ba` inside it; ai-hub `lib/hub` (`session.js` unmodified, plus harness, bridge, round). Engine crates and `scripts/build-web.sh` / `pack_single_html.py` may change. Embed the OFL Barlow Condensed file from the URL in PLAN.md. Playwright 1.63 (Python), Rust 1.98.1, wasm32 target, and wasm-bindgen 0.2.129 are already installed. Research already done for this plan: Second Opinion is pointer surgery, nunchuk/stick tool wheel (~8 tools), vitals and a timer as fail states, gesture ratings and letter ranks up to XS, chapter story around operations, a limited Healing Touch, and defibrillation. PLAN.md’s original remake of those mechanics is the contract, not a remake of the licensed game.\\n\\n## Implementation approach\\nKeep rules in one deterministic sim the headless tools can tick: surgeon slots, heartbeat, tools, strains, story phases, and the bot live there, with no wall clock, threads, or files. Drive the cursor in real time during the Hush via scaled sim dt, not the engine speed control. Let rendering, egui shell, and audio only read a single frame snapshot plus cue ids, so a browser client can decode the same snapshot. Keep the shell’s input abstract so pad, mouse, and tests share it, including while the sim is paused. Put cases, lines, plates, and rigs in text with file-and-line errors. Expose status, step, and shell commands on `window.__game` for the browser. Pack one HTML that works from `file://`. These are structure hints, not a required layout.\\n\\n## Task checklist\\n- [x] Clone the engine in the dev subfolder, confirm the commit, read its start and make-a-game docs, pick the title with a real RNG, and start `PROGRESS.md`.\\n- [ ] Open the sim/input/camera/product seams and ship one overhead operation (field, vitals, heartbeat, one tool, bot win) that also boots in the packed page with the session client in place.\\n- [ ] Add every instrument, hazard, rating, chain, Code, death/retry, and cases 0–2 as data; teach the bot; add the cue table and coverage tests.\\n- [ ] Add the 10-foot shell: menus, pause, settings, save, glyphs, attract, touch-only, and dev sliders with reset.\\n40→- [ ] Add paper-theatre story, music buses at music gain 0.10, and gibberish voices through case 7’s script.\\n- [ ] Add the four strains, Hush, Echo, tremor, Cryoprobe, Duet, cases 3–7, local 1–4 play, and Code Blue.\\n- [ ] Add the hub shim, card, mirror scene, and host snapshots; pass the harness and the two-page cursor/vitals check.\\n- [ ] Balance, write `exit-interview.json` and the about block, pack the single HTML to the work root, delete `engine/target`, and save the green suite plus two launch captures under `{SCRATCH}`.\\n\\n## Risks / Contradictions\\n- PLAN.md allows cutting sets and strain length if time runs out, but forbids cutting any tool, gift, screen, Case 3, or Case 7. A build that drops a forbidden piece is not done.\\n- The HTML basename must contain the source string `Trauma Center: Second Opinion`, including the colon. Do not sanitize it away.\\n- The title is chosen at implementation time, so this plan cannot name the file. Match the pattern.\\n- Headless WebGPU pixels need the swiftshader flags; a successful blank capture is a game failure. If earlyoom or a missing display kills the browser, keep the log and use the sim/shell bar only in that case.\",\"content_concise\":\"30→Work root only. New dev subfolder; clone `https://github.com/michaelcrosato/shardfall` at or after `49ef2ba` inside it; ai-hub `lib/hub` (`session.js` unmodified, plus harness, bridge, round). Engine crates and `scripts/build-web.sh` / `pack_single_html.py` may change. Embed the OFL Barlow Condensed file from the URL in PLAN.md. Playwright 1.63 (Python), Rust 1.98.1, wasm32 target, and wasm-bindgen 0.2.129 are already installed. Research already done for this plan: Second Opinion is pointer surgery, nunchuk/stick tool wheel (~8 tools), vitals and a timer as fail states, gesture ratings and letter ranks up to XS, chapter story around operations, a limited Healing Touch, and defibrillation. PLAN.md’s original remake of those mechanics is the contract, not a remake of the licensed game.\\n\\n## Implementation approach\\nKeep rules in one deterministic sim the headless tools can tick: surgeon slots, heartbeat, tools, strains, story phases, and the bot live there, with no wall clock, threads, or files. Drive the cursor in real time during the Hush via scaled sim dt, not the engine speed control. Let rendering, egui shell, and audio only read a single frame snapshot plus cue ids, so a browser client can decode the same snapshot. Keep the shell’s input abstract so pad, mouse, and tests share it, including while the sim is paused. Put cases, lines, plates, and rigs in text with file-and-line errors. Expose status, step, and shell commands on `window.__game` for the browser. Pack one HTML that works from `file://`. These are structure hints, not a required layout.\\n\\n## Task checklist\\n- [x] Clone the engine in the dev subfolder, confirm the commit, read its start and make-a-game docs, pick the title with a real RNG, and start `PROGRESS.md`.\\n- [ ] Open the sim/input/camera/product seams and ship one overhead operation (field, vitals, heartbeat, one tool, bot win) that also boots in the packed page with the session client in place.\\n- [ ] Add every instrument, hazard, rating, chain, Code, death/retry, and cases 0–2 as data; teach the bot; add the cue table and coverage tests.\\n- [ ] Add the 10-foot shell: menus, pause, settings, save, glyphs, attract, touch-only, and dev sliders with reset.\\n40→- [ ] Add paper-theatre story, music buses at music gain 0.10, and gibberish voices through case 7’s script.\\n- [ ] Add the four strains, Hush, Echo, tremor, Cryoprobe, Duet, cases 3–7, local 1–4 play, and Code Blue.\\n- [ ] Add the hub shim, card, mirror scene, and host snapshots; pass the harness and the two-page cursor/vitals check.\\n- [ ] Balance, write `exit-interview.json` and the about block, pack the single HTML to the work root, delete `engine/target`, and save the green suite plus two launch captures under `{SCRATCH}`.\\n\\n## Risks / Contradictions\\n- PLAN.md allows cutting sets and strain length if time runs out, but forbids cutting any tool, gift, screen, Case 3, or Case 7. A build that drops a forbidden piece is not done.\\n- The HTML basename must contain the source string `Trauma Center: Second Opinion`, including the colon. Do not sanitize it away.\\n- The title is chosen at implementation time, so this plan cannot name the file. Match the pattern.\\n- Headless WebGPU pixels need the swiftshader flags; a successful blank capture is a game failure. If earlyoom or a missing display kills the browser, keep the log and use the sim/shell bar only in that case.\",\"absolute_path\":\"/home/micha/.grok/sessions/%2Fhome%2Fmicha%2Fdev%2Fcc-matrix%2Fruns%2Fgrok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224015__x42677a%2Fwork/01a1aa38-de6f-7dc0-ae0d-e0f717ed75f2/goal/plan.md\",\"offset\":30,\"limit\":20,\"raw_output\":\"Work root only. New dev subfolder; clone `https://github.com/michaelcrosato/shardfall` at or after `49ef2ba` inside it; ai-hub `lib/hub` (`session.js` unmodified, plus harness, bridge, round). Engine crates and `scripts/build-web.sh` / `pack_single_html.py` may change. Embed the OFL Barlow Condensed file from the URL in PLAN.md. Playwright 1.63 (Python), Rust 1.98.1, wasm32 target, and wasm-bindgen 0.2.129 are already installed. Research already done for this plan: Second Opinion is pointer surgery, nunchuk/stick tool wheel (~8 tools), vitals and a timer as fail states, gesture ratings and letter ranks up to XS, chapter story around operations, a limited Healing Touch, and defibrillation. PLAN.md’s original remake of those mechanics is the contract, not a remake of the licensed game.\\n\\n## Implementation approach\\nKeep rules in one deterministic sim the headless tools can tick: surgeon slots, heartbeat, tools, strains, story phases, and the bot live there, with no wall clock, threads, or files. Drive the cursor in real time during the Hush via scaled sim dt, not the engine speed control. Let rendering, egui shell, and audio only read a single frame snapshot plus cue ids, so a browser client can decode the same snapshot. Keep the shell’s input abstract so pad, mouse, and tests share it, including while the sim is paused. Put cases, lines, plates, and rigs in text with file-and-line errors. Expose status, step, and shell commands on `window.__game` for the browser. Pack one HTML that works from `file://`. These are structure hints, not a required layout.\\n\\n## Task checklist\\n- [x] Clone the engine in the dev subfolder, confirm the commit, read its start and make-a-game docs, pick the title with a real RNG, and start `PROGRESS.md`.\\n- [ ] Open the sim/input/camera/product seams and ship one overhead operation (field, vitals, heartbeat, one tool, bot win) that also boots in the packed page with the session client in place.\\n- [ ] Add every instrument, hazard, rating, chain, Code, death/retry, and cases 0–2 as data; teach the bot; add the cue table and coverage tests.\\n- [ ] Add the 10-foot shell: menus, pause, settings, save, glyphs, attract, touch-only, and dev sliders with reset.\\n- [ ] Add paper-theatre story, music buses at music gain 0.10, and gibberish voices through case 7’s script.\\n- [ ] Add the four strains, Hush, Echo, tremor, Cryoprobe, Duet, cases 3–7, local 1–4 play, and Code Blue.\\n- [ ] Add the hub shim, card, mirror scene, and host snapshots; pass the harness and the two-page cursor/vitals check.\\n- [ ] Balance, write `exit-interview.json` and the about block, pack the single HTML to the work root, delete `engine/target`, and save the green suite plus two launch captures under `{SCRATCH}`.\\n\\n## Risks / Contradictions\\n- PLAN.md allows cutting sets and strain length if time runs out, but forbids cutting any tool, gift, screen, Case 3, or Case 7. A build that drops a forbidden piece is not done.\\n- The HTML basename must contain the source string `Trauma Center: Second Opinion`, including the colon. Do not sanitize it away.\\n- The title is chosen at implementation time, so this plan cannot name the file. Match the pattern.\\n- Headless WebGPU pixels need the swiftshader flags; a successful blank capture is a game failure. If earlyoom or a missing display kills the browser, keep the log and use the sim/shell bar only in that case.\\n\",\"total_lines\":50}}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa38-de6f-7dc0-ae0d-e0f717ed75f2","uuid":"b43d1a2b-b7b3-483f-8709-c49eb4bd18c6"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_642","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"suite.txt shows 13 passed tests and no failures. The summary line is the only output.\n\nWriting launch.py and hub.txt next. Hub.txt will list the four query results with pass status and traffic, plus cursor numbers from hub-cursor2. Solo file:// pages show titles. The harness reports PASS in JSON.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-c287e460-69c0-4f86-9c6f-0e8f2367b705-60","name":"write","input":{"file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224015__x42677a/tmp/grok-goal-907ccca5ce3b/implementer/hub.txt","content":"Hub harness against the packed HTML. Server 127.0.0.1:39337. One browser at a time. TMPDIR=/tmp/hbr-pw.\n\nplayers=4&latency=150&jitter=50&loss=5&auto=1&limit=20 PASS\n  traffic: p0 ↑38 ↓77 p1 ↑38 ↓78 p2 ↑38 ↓76\n  round: played (finished). Source: hub-p4.txt\n\nplayers=4&latency=150&jitter=50&loss=5&scenario=host-leave&auto=1&limit=20 PASS\n  traffic after leave: p1 ↑7 ↓18 p2 ↑7 ↓17 p3 ↑7 ↓17\n  round: void (host-left). Did not finish on leave. Source: hub-leave.txt\n\nplayers=2&scenario=server&auto=1&limit=20 PASS\n  traffic: p0 ↑54 ↓106 p1 ↑54 ↓106 server ↑54 ↓106\n  server sent 55, host slot 2, played (finished). Source: hub-server.txt\n\nplayers=1&auto=1&limit=20 PASS\n  traffic: p0 ↑15 ↓0 (one player waives both-ways). played (finished). Source: hub-one.txt\n\nTwo pages, client aim (ArrowRight on the non-host):\n  host seat-1 cursor x: 0 -> 3.4199981689453125\n  client local cursor x: 2 -> 7.420000076293945\n  vitals host 61.67979049682617, client 62.400001525878906 (one snapshot behind, not bitwise equal)\n  timer host 238.400390625, client 238.5\n  Source: hub-cursor2.txt\n\nSolo page, no hub session: file:// launch shows screen \"title\", title \"Hands of Harbor: Second Opinion\". See launch-1/status.json and launch-2/status.json.\n"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-c287e460-69c0-4f86-9c6f-0e8f2367b705-61","name":"write","input":{"file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224015__x42677a/tmp/grok-goal-907ccca5ce3b/implementer/launch.py","content":"\"\"\"Two file:// launches, then shots of title, story, operation, dev, and about.\n\nKeys are acknowledged one at a time. A burst is one frame: product clears `just`\nafter a single ate(), and the solo plate can take seconds. The pad button stays\ndown until status changes, so a slow frame still sees the edge.\n\"\"\"\nimport json\nimport os\nimport subprocess\nimport time\nimport traceback\nfrom pathlib import Path\n\nfrom playwright.sync_api import sync_playwright\n\nHTML = Path(\n    \"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224015__x42677a/work/\"\n    \"Hands of Harbor: Second Opinion-Trauma Center: Second Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-224015.html\"\n)\nSCRATCH = Path(\n    \"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224015__x42677a/tmp/grok-goal-907ccca5ce3b/implementer\"\n)\nARGS = [\n    \"--enable-unsafe-webgpu\",\n    \"--enable-features=Vulkan\",\n    \"--use-webgpu-adapter=swiftshader\",\n    \"--use-vulkan=swiftshader\",\n    \"--use-angle=swiftshader\",\n    \"--window-position=0,0\",\n    \"--window-size=1920,1080\",\n]\nPAD = \"\"\"\n(() => { const buttons = Array.from({length: 17}, () => ({pressed: false, touched: false, value: 0}));\n  const pad = {id: 'DualSense Wireless Controller (STANDARD GAMEPAD Vendor: 054c Product: 0ce6)', index: 0, connected: true,\n               mapping: 'standard', timestamp: 0, axes: [0, 0, 0, 0], buttons};\n  window.__pad = pad; navigator.getGamepads = () => [pad, null, null, null]; })();\n\"\"\"\n\n\ndef status(page):\n    return json.loads(page.evaluate(\"() => window.__game.status()\"))\n\n\ndef boot(page, url):\n    page.goto(url, wait_until=\"domcontentloaded\", timeout=60000)\n    page.wait_for_function(\"() => window.__game && window.__game.status\", timeout=45000)\n    last = None\n    for _ in range(40):\n        last = status(page)\n        if last.get(\"screen\") == \"title\":\n            return last\n        page.wait_for_timeout(250)\n    return last\n\n\ndef wait_pred(page, pred, timeout_s):\n    last = None\n    deadline = time.time() + timeout_s\n    while time.time() < deadline:\n        last = status(page)\n        if pred(last):\n            return last\n        page.wait_for_timeout(250)\n    return last\n\n\ndef pad_south(page, down):\n    page.evaluate(\n        \"\"\"(down) => {\n          const b = window.__pad.buttons[0];\n          b.pressed = down;\n          b.value = down ? 1 : 0;\n          window.__pad.timestamp = (window.__pad.timestamp || 0) + 1;\n        }\"\"\",\n        down,\n    )\n\n\ndef changed(before):\n    def pred(s):\n        return (\n            s.get(\"screen\") != before.get(\"screen\")\n            or s.get(\"focus\") != before.get(\"focus\")\n            or s.get(\"device\") != before.get(\"device\")\n        )\n\n    return pred\n\n\ndef drive_same(page):\n    \"\"\"Pad Cross, then a mouse click only if the pad did not move the shell.\"\"\"\n    before = status(page)\n    pad_south(page, True)\n    after = wait_pred(page, changed(before), 12)\n    pad_south(page, False)\n    how = \"pad-south\"\n    if after.get(\"screen\") == before.get(\"screen\") and after.get(\"focus\") == before.get(\"focus\"):\n        page.locator(\"canvas\").first.click(position={\"x\": 200, \"y\": 200}, force=True)\n        after = wait_pred(page, changed(before), 12)\n        how = \"mouse-click\"\n    return before, after, how\n\n\ndef focus_canvas(page):\n    page.evaluate(\n        \"\"\"() => {\n          const c = document.querySelector('canvas');\n          if (!c) return;\n          c.tabIndex = 0;\n          c.focus();\n        }\"\"\"\n    )\n\n\ndef tap(page, key, pred, timeout_s=18):\n    focus_canvas(page)\n    page.keyboard.press(key)\n    hit = wait_pred(page, pred, timeout_s)\n    if hit and pred(hit):\n        return hit\n    page.keyboard.press(key)\n    return wait_pred(page, pred, timeout_s)\n\n\ndef shot(page, path):\n    path.parent.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)\n    page.wait_for_timeout(600)\n    display = os.environ.get(\"DISPLAY\", \":0\")\n    proc = subprocess.run(\n        [\n            \"/usr/bin/ffmpeg\",\n            \"-y\",\n            \"-hide_banner\",\n            \"-loglevel\",\n            \"error\",\n            \"-f\",\n            \"x11grab\",\n            \"-video_size\",\n            \"1920x1080\",\n            \"-i\",\n            display,\n            \"-frames:v\",\n            \"1\",\n            str(path),\n        ],\n        env=os.environ.copy(),\n        capture_output=True,\n        text=True,\n        timeout=20,\n    )\n    if proc.returncode != 0:\n        raise RuntimeError(proc.stderr[-500:] or f\"ffmpeg exit {proc.returncode}\")\n\n\ndef canvas_box(page):\n    return page.evaluate(\n        \"\"\"() => {\n          const c = document.querySelector('canvas');\n          if (!c) return null;\n          return {w: c.width, h: c.height, cw: c.clientWidth, ch: c.clientHeight};\n        }\"\"\"\n    )\n\n\ndef one_launch(p, n, url):\n    dest = SCRATCH / f\"launch-{n}\"\n    dest.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)\n    logs = []\n    browser = p.chromium.launch(headless=False, args=ARGS)\n    context = browser.new_context(viewport={\"width\": 1920, \"height\": 1080})\n    context.add_init_script(PAD)\n    page = context.new_page()\n    page.on(\"console\", lambda m: logs.append(f\"{m.type}: {m.text[:240]}\") if m.type == \"error\" else None)\n    page.on(\"pageerror\", lambda e: logs.append(f\"pageerror: {e}\"))\n    boot(page, url)\n    st = status(page)\n    box = canvas_box(page)\n    shot(page, dest / \"title.png\")\n    before, after, how = drive_same(page)\n    (dest / \"status.json\").write_text(\n        json.dumps({\"before\": before, \"after\": after, \"input\": how, \"canvas\": box, \"console\": logs}, indent=2)\n    )\n    print(\n        f\"LAUNCH {n} before\",\n        before.get(\"screen\"),\n        before.get(\"title\"),\n        before.get(\"music\"),\n        \"canvas\",\n        box,\n    )\n    print(f\"LAUNCH {n} after\", how, after.get(\"screen\"), after.get(\"focus\"), after.get(\"device\"))\n    print(f\"LAUNCH {n} console\", logs[:8])\n    browser.close()\n    return how\n\n\ndef goto_menu(page):\n    st = status(page)\n    if st.get(\"screen\") == \"menu\":\n        return st\n    _before, after, how = drive_same(page)\n    print(\"MENU via\", how, after.get(\"screen\"), after.get(\"focus\"))\n    return after\n\n\ndef shoot(p, url):\n    out = SCRATCH / \"shots\"\n    out.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)\n    browser = p.chromium.launch(headless=False, args=ARGS)\n    context = browser.new_context(viewport={\"width\": 1920, \"height\": 1080})\n    context.add_init_script(PAD)\n    page = context.new_page()\n    notes = {}\n\n    def grab(name):\n        st = status(page)\n        shot(page, out / f\"{name}.png\")\n        notes[name] = {\"screen\": st.get(\"screen\"), \"focus\": st.get(\"focus\")}\n        print(\"SHOT\", name, notes[name])\n        return st\n\n    boot(page, url)\n    grab(\"title\")\n    menu = goto_menu(page)\n    focus = menu.get(\"focus\") or 0\n    for want in range(focus + 1, 6):\n        st = tap(page, \"ArrowDown\", lambda s, want=want: s.get(\"screen\") == \"menu\" and s.get(\"focus\") == want)\n        print(\"DOWN\", st.get(\"screen\"), st.get(\"focus\"))\n        if st.get(\"focus\") != want:\n            break\n    about = tap(page, \"Enter\", lambda s: s.get(\"screen\") == \"about\")\n    print(\"ABOUT\", about.get(\"screen\"), about.get(\"focus\"))\n    grab(\"about\")\n\n    page.goto(\"about:blank\")\n    boot(page, url)\n    goto_menu(page)\n    story = tap(page, \"Enter\", lambda s: s.get(\"screen\") == \"story\")\n    print(\"STORY\", story.get(\"screen\"))\n    grab(\"story\")\n\n    page.goto(\"about:blank\")\n    boot(page, url)\n    goto_menu(page)\n    st = status(page)\n    for want in range((st.get(\"focus\") or 0) + 1, 3):\n        st = tap(page, \"ArrowDown\", lambda s, want=want: s.get(\"screen\") == \"menu\" and s.get(\"focus\") == want)\n        print(\"FILEDOWN\", st.get(\"screen\"), st.get(\"focus\"))\n    files = tap(page, \"Enter\", lambda s: s.get(\"screen\") == \"files\")\n    print(\"FILES\", files.get(\"screen\"), files.get(\"focus\"))\n    op = tap(page, \"Enter\", lambda s: s.get(\"screen\") == \"op\")\n    print(\"OP\", op.get(\"screen\"))\n    grab(\"op\")\n    pause = tap(page, \"Escape\", lambda s: s.get(\"screen\") == \"pause\")\n    print(\"PAUSE\", pause.get(\"screen\"), pause.get(\"focus\"))\n    st = pause\n    for want in range((st.get(\"focus\") or 0) + 1, 5):\n        st = tap(page, \"ArrowDown\", lambda s, want=want: s.get(\"screen\") == \"pause\" and s.get(\"focus\") == want)\n        print(\"DEVDOWN\", st.get(\"screen\"), st.get(\"focus\"))\n    dev = tap(page, \"Enter\", lambda s: s.get(\"screen\") == \"dev\")\n    print(\"DEV\", dev.get(\"screen\"), dev.get(\"focus\"))\n    grab(\"dev\")\n\n    notes[\"results\"] = \"not captured: results opens only after an operation ends, and there is no menu command for it\"\n    (out / \"notes.json\").write_text(json.dumps(notes, indent=2))\n    browser.close()\n\n\ndef main():\n    os.environ.setdefault(\"PLAYWRIGHT_HOST_PLATFORM_OVERRIDE\", \"ubuntu24.04-x64\")\n    url = HTML.as_uri()\n    with sync_playwright() as p:\n        one_launch(p, 1, url)\n        one_launch(p, 2, url)\n        shoot(p, url)\n    print(\"DONE\")\n\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    try:\n        main()\n    except Exception:\n        traceback.print_exc()\n        raise\n"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2489,"output_tokens":3462,"cache_read_input_tokens":96128,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa38-de6f-7dc0-ae0d-e0f717ed75f2","uuid":"530323bf-61ca-4f9e-8bbb-fc424c04a84e"}
