{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-c02fd047-a7d9-4870-9e30-2c7e8cd0ff11-64","content":"{\"type\":\"BackgroundTaskStarted\",\"task_id\":\"38b4355b-41d9-4521-8791-927e6d92566d\",\"task_type\":\"bash\",\"output_file\":\"/home/micha/.grok/sessions/%2Fhome%2Fmicha%2Fdev%2Fcc-matrix%2Fruns%2Fgrok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224015__x42677a%2Fwork/01a1aa38-de6f-7dc0-ae0d-e0f717ed75f2/terminal/call-c02fd047-a7d9-4870-9e30-2c7e8cd0ff11-64.log\",\"status\":\"running\",\"command\":\"mkdir -p /tmp/hbr-pw && export TMPDIR=/tmp/hbr-pw PLAYWRIGHT_HOST_PLATFORM_OVERRIDE=ubuntu24.04-x64 && SCRATCH=\\\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224015__x42677a/tmp/grok-goal-907ccca5ce3b/implementer\\\" && xvfb-run -a -s \\\"-screen 0 1920x1080x24\\\" python3 \\\"$SCRATCH/launch.py\\\" > \\\"$SCRATCH/launch.txt\\\" 2>&1; echo EXIT:$? >> \\\"$SCRATCH/launch.txt\\\"; echo EXIT:$?\",\"summary\":\"Background task 38b4355b-41d9-4521-8791-927e6d92566d started\",\"retrieval_hint\":\"Use get_command_or_subagent_output with task_ids=[\\\"38b4355b-41d9-4521-8791-927e6d92566d\\\"] when you need the output.\",\"pid\":294374}","is_error":false},{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-c02fd047-a7d9-4870-9e30-2c7e8cd0ff11-65","content":"{\"type\":\"ReadFile\",\"FileContent\":{\"content\":\"1→{\\n  \\\"sourceInformation\\\": {\\n    \\\"date\\\": \\\"2026-11-04 22:40:15\\\",\\n    \\\"source\\\": \\\"Trauma Center: Second Opinion\\\",\\n    \\\"plan\\\": \\\"PLAN.md\\\",\\n    \\\"genre\\\": \\\"Simulation\\\",\\n    \\\"perspective\\\": \\\"Fixed overhead view of the operative field\\\",\\n    \\\"tech\\\": \\\"Pavilion engine (Shardfall commit 49ef2ba), Rust 1.98.1, wgpu/WebGPU, wasm-bindgen 0.2.129, egui 0.36.2\\\",\\n    \\\"artDirection\\\": \\\"Cel-shaded overhead operative field painted per vertex, with layered paper-theatre cards for story\\\",\\n10→    \\\"animation\\\": \\\"Simulation-driven tissue, instruments, heartbeat, and paper-card motion\\\",\\n    \\\"audio\\\": \\\"Synthesized music, effects, and short gibberish voices. No audio files. Music bus defaults to 0.10\\\",\\n    \\\"online\\\": \\\"Optional AI Hub shared-world Code Blue for 1-4 surgeons\\\",\\n    \\\"testing\\\": \\\"Deterministic sim suite, headless shell, Chromium file:// launches, hub harness\\\",\\n    \\\"research\\\": \\\"Engine seams and the hub protocol, recorded in PLAN.md\\\",\\n    \\\"environment\\\": \\\"Grok CLI (headless); Linux\\\",\\n    \\\"model\\\": \\\"xAI, grok-4.7, reasoning effort xhigh\\\",\\n    \\\"usage\\\": \\\"added on import\\\"\\n  },\\n  \\\"testingFeedback\\\": [\\n20→    \\\"Testing caught five issues: a Rust or-pattern guard skipped stage-0 sutures, nearest-hazard selection stole forceps pulls, a sac's swell shared the laser charge meter, hub snapshots waited on a 60 Hz accumulator that never fired in an iframe, and ControlFlow::Poll cancelled the pending animation frame so an operation froze after one tick.\\\",\\n    \\\"5\\\",\\n    \\\"The most helpful checks were a skill-1.0 bot on every case from a fresh scene, and the hub harness traffic counters once the frame loop actually ticked.\\\",\\n    \\\"The least helpful test was a temporary print probe that only dumped stuck hazards and was removed once the selection bug was fixed.\\\"\\n  ],\\n  \\\"engineFeedback\\\": [\\n    \\\"The Game hook, recorded input, RenderFrame, headless egui, and the single-file packer.\\\",\\n    \\\"Yes. A colon in the project path makes rustc fail joining LD_LIBRARY_PATH, and the demo frame path captures the camera, pause menu, and touch layer unless a game returns first.\\\",\\n    \\\"The operative rules, the plate mesh, the ten-foot shell, the cue and music buses, and the hub shim.\\\",\\n    \\\"Keeping a surgery scene off the demo boot panel, stats, guide, toasts, and the engine pause menu.\\\",\\n30→    \\\"Added the surgery frame, surgeon input, and cue event; a view emit and camera shot; a product frame branch; audio buses and formants; session.js injection in the packer; and js-sys. On the web the surgery loop waits for animation frames, because Poll cancelled the pending frame. The hook alone cannot draw, play cues, or join a hub.\\\",\\n    \\\"A first-class per-game frame path, so a new game does not have to outrun the demo loop.\\\"\\n  ],\\n  \\\"promptFeedback\\\": [\\n    \\\"The tested camera, light, and palette numbers, and a hub shim that the harness had already accepted.\\\",\\n    \\\"The deliverable folder name must contain a colon, which Cargo cannot use as its working directory.\\\",\\n    \\\"Shipping one packed page that is the full game, a hub client, and a file:// WebGPU build.\\\",\\n    \\\"Say at the start that the Cargo target directory cannot contain a colon.\\\"\\n  ],\\n  \\\"aiHub\\\": {\\n40→    \\\"name\\\": \\\"Hands of Harbor: Second Opinion\\\",\\n    \\\"tagline\\\": \\\"Night Ward. Keep the beat. Keep them alive.\\\",\\n    \\\"description\\\": \\\"Overhead surgical melodrama for one to four surgeons at Mercy Harbor General in Port Verity.\\\",\\n    \\\"type\\\": \\\"Game\\\",\\n    \\\"genre\\\": \\\"Simulation\\\",\\n    \\\"source\\\": \\\"Trauma Center: Second Opinion\\\",\\n    \\\"series\\\": \\\"Trauma Center\\\",\\n    \\\"players\\\": \\\"1–4\\\",\\n    \\\"controls\\\": \\\"Right stick or mouse aims, R2 or left click operates, left stick or 1–8 picks tools\\\",\\n    \\\"tags\\\": [\\\"3d\\\", \\\"story\\\", \\\"co-op\\\", \\\"arcade\\\", \\\"boss fights\\\"]\\n50→  }\\n}\\n\",\"content_concise\":\"1→{\\n  \\\"sourceInformation\\\": {\\n    \\\"date\\\": \\\"2026-11-04 22:40:15\\\",\\n    \\\"source\\\": \\\"Trauma Center: Second Opinion\\\",\\n    \\\"plan\\\": \\\"PLAN.md\\\",\\n    \\\"genre\\\": \\\"Simulation\\\",\\n    \\\"perspective\\\": \\\"Fixed overhead view of the operative field\\\",\\n    \\\"tech\\\": \\\"Pavilion engine (Shardfall commit 49ef2ba), Rust 1.98.1, wgpu/WebGPU, wasm-bindgen 0.2.129, egui 0.36.2\\\",\\n    \\\"artDirection\\\": \\\"Cel-shaded overhead operative field painted per vertex, with layered paper-theatre cards for story\\\",\\n10→    \\\"animation\\\": \\\"Simulation-driven tissue, instruments, heartbeat, and paper-card motion\\\",\\n    \\\"audio\\\": \\\"Synthesized music, effects, and short gibberish voices. No audio files. Music bus defaults to 0.10\\\",\\n    \\\"online\\\": \\\"Optional AI Hub shared-world Code Blue for 1-4 surgeons\\\",\\n    \\\"testing\\\": \\\"Deterministic sim suite, headless shell, Chromium file:// launches, hub harness\\\",\\n    \\\"research\\\": \\\"Engine seams and the hub protocol, recorded in PLAN.md\\\",\\n    \\\"environment\\\": \\\"Grok CLI (headless); Linux\\\",\\n    \\\"model\\\": \\\"xAI, grok-4.7, reasoning effort xhigh\\\",\\n    \\\"usage\\\": \\\"added on import\\\"\\n  },\\n  \\\"testingFeedback\\\": [\\n20→    \\\"Testing caught five issues: a Rust or-pattern guard skipped stage-0 sutures, nearest-hazard selection stole forceps pulls, a sac's swell shared the laser charge meter, hub snapshots waited on a 60 Hz accumulator that never fired in an iframe, and ControlFlow::Poll cancelled the pending animation frame so an operation froze after one tick.\\\",\\n    \\\"5\\\",\\n    \\\"The most helpful checks were a skill-1.0 bot on every case from a fresh scene, and the hub harness traffic counters once the frame loop actually ticked.\\\",\\n    \\\"The least helpful test was a temporary print probe that only dumped stuck hazards and was removed once the selection bug was fixed.\\\"\\n  ],\\n  \\\"engineFeedback\\\": [\\n    \\\"The Game hook, recorded input, RenderFrame, headless egui, and the single-file packer.\\\",\\n    \\\"Yes. A colon in the project path makes rustc fail joining LD_LIBRARY_PATH, and the demo frame path captures the camera, pause menu, and touch layer unless a game returns first.\\\",\\n    \\\"The operative rules, the plate mesh, the ten-foot shell, the cue and music buses, and the hub shim.\\\",\\n    \\\"Keeping a surgery scene off the demo boot panel, stats, guide, toasts, and the engine pause menu.\\\",\\n30→    \\\"Added the surgery frame, surgeon input, and cue event; a view emit and camera shot; a product frame branch; audio buses and formants; session.js injection in the packer; and js-sys. On the web the surgery loop waits for animation frames, because Poll cancelled the pending frame. The hook alone cannot draw, play cues, or join a hub.\\\",\\n    \\\"A first-class per-game frame path, so a new game does not have to outrun the demo loop.\\\"\\n  ],\\n  \\\"promptFeedback\\\": [\\n    \\\"The tested camera, light, and palette numbers, and a hub shim that the harness had already accepted.\\\",\\n    \\\"The deliverable folder name must contain a colon, which Cargo cannot use as its working directory.\\\",\\n    \\\"Shipping one packed page that is the full game, a hub client, and a file:// WebGPU build.\\\",\\n    \\\"Say at the start that the Cargo target directory cannot contain a colon.\\\"\\n  ],\\n  \\\"aiHub\\\": {\\n40→    \\\"name\\\": \\\"Hands of Harbor: Second Opinion\\\",\\n    \\\"tagline\\\": \\\"Night Ward. Keep the beat. Keep them alive.\\\",\\n    \\\"description\\\": \\\"Overhead surgical melodrama for one to four surgeons at Mercy Harbor General in Port Verity.\\\",\\n    \\\"type\\\": \\\"Game\\\",\\n    \\\"genre\\\": \\\"Simulation\\\",\\n    \\\"source\\\": \\\"Trauma Center: Second Opinion\\\",\\n    \\\"series\\\": \\\"Trauma Center\\\",\\n    \\\"players\\\": \\\"1–4\\\",\\n    \\\"controls\\\": \\\"Right stick or mouse aims, R2 or left click operates, left stick or 1–8 picks tools\\\",\\n    \\\"tags\\\": [\\\"3d\\\", \\\"story\\\", \\\"co-op\\\", \\\"arcade\\\", \\\"boss fights\\\"]\\n50→  }\\n}\\n\",\"absolute_path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224015__x42677a/work/Hands of Harbor: Second Opinion-Trauma Center: Second Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-224015/engine/crates/pav_ui/src/surgery/about.json\",\"offset\":null,\"limit\":80,\"raw_output\":\"{\\n  \\\"sourceInformation\\\": {\\n    \\\"date\\\": \\\"2026-11-04 22:40:15\\\",\\n    \\\"source\\\": \\\"Trauma Center: Second Opinion\\\",\\n    \\\"plan\\\": \\\"PLAN.md\\\",\\n    \\\"genre\\\": \\\"Simulation\\\",\\n    \\\"perspective\\\": \\\"Fixed overhead view of the operative field\\\",\\n    \\\"tech\\\": \\\"Pavilion engine (Shardfall commit 49ef2ba), Rust 1.98.1, wgpu/WebGPU, wasm-bindgen 0.2.129, egui 0.36.2\\\",\\n    \\\"artDirection\\\": \\\"Cel-shaded overhead operative field painted per vertex, with layered paper-theatre cards for story\\\",\\n    \\\"animation\\\": \\\"Simulation-driven tissue, instruments, heartbeat, and paper-card motion\\\",\\n    \\\"audio\\\": \\\"Synthesized music, effects, and short gibberish voices. No audio files. Music bus defaults to 0.10\\\",\\n    \\\"online\\\": \\\"Optional AI Hub shared-world Code Blue for 1-4 surgeons\\\",\\n    \\\"testing\\\": \\\"Deterministic sim suite, headless shell, Chromium file:// launches, hub harness\\\",\\n    \\\"research\\\": \\\"Engine seams and the hub protocol, recorded in PLAN.md\\\",\\n    \\\"environment\\\": \\\"Grok CLI (headless); Linux\\\",\\n    \\\"model\\\": \\\"xAI, grok-4.7, reasoning effort xhigh\\\",\\n    \\\"usage\\\": \\\"added on import\\\"\\n  },\\n  \\\"testingFeedback\\\": [\\n    \\\"Testing caught five issues: a Rust or-pattern guard skipped stage-0 sutures, nearest-hazard selection stole forceps pulls, a sac's swell shared the laser charge meter, hub snapshots waited on a 60 Hz accumulator that never fired in an iframe, and ControlFlow::Poll cancelled the pending animation frame so an operation froze after one tick.\\\",\\n    \\\"5\\\",\\n    \\\"The most helpful checks were a skill-1.0 bot on every case from a fresh scene, and the hub harness traffic counters once the frame loop actually ticked.\\\",\\n    \\\"The least helpful test was a temporary print probe that only dumped stuck hazards and was removed once the selection bug was fixed.\\\"\\n  ],\\n  \\\"engineFeedback\\\": [\\n    \\\"The Game hook, recorded input, RenderFrame, headless egui, and the single-file packer.\\\",\\n    \\\"Yes. A colon in the project path makes rustc fail joining LD_LIBRARY_PATH, and the demo frame path captures the camera, pause menu, and touch layer unless a game returns first.\\\",\\n    \\\"The operative rules, the plate mesh, the ten-foot shell, the cue and music buses, and the hub shim.\\\",\\n    \\\"Keeping a surgery scene off the demo boot panel, stats, guide, toasts, and the engine pause menu.\\\",\\n    \\\"Added the surgery frame, surgeon input, and cue event; a view emit and camera shot; a product frame branch; audio buses and formants; session.js injection in the packer; and js-sys. On the web the surgery loop waits for animation frames, because Poll cancelled the pending frame. The hook alone cannot draw, play cues, or join a hub.\\\",\\n    \\\"A first-class per-game frame path, so a new game does not have to outrun the demo loop.\\\"\\n  ],\\n  \\\"promptFeedback\\\": [\\n    \\\"The tested camera, light, and palette numbers, and a hub shim that the harness had already accepted.\\\",\\n    \\\"The deliverable folder name must contain a colon, which Cargo cannot use as its working directory.\\\",\\n    \\\"Shipping one packed page that is the full game, a hub client, and a file:// WebGPU build.\\\",\\n    \\\"Say at the start that the Cargo target directory cannot contain a colon.\\\"\\n  ],\\n  \\\"aiHub\\\": {\\n    \\\"name\\\": \\\"Hands of Harbor: Second Opinion\\\",\\n    \\\"tagline\\\": \\\"Night Ward. Keep the beat. Keep them alive.\\\",\\n    \\\"description\\\": \\\"Overhead surgical melodrama for one to four surgeons at Mercy Harbor General in Port Verity.\\\",\\n    \\\"type\\\": \\\"Game\\\",\\n    \\\"genre\\\": \\\"Simulation\\\",\\n    \\\"source\\\": \\\"Trauma Center: Second Opinion\\\",\\n    \\\"series\\\": \\\"Trauma Center\\\",\\n    \\\"players\\\": \\\"1–4\\\",\\n    \\\"controls\\\": \\\"Right stick or mouse aims, R2 or left click operates, left stick or 1–8 picks tools\\\",\\n    \\\"tags\\\": [\\\"3d\\\", \\\"story\\\", \\\"co-op\\\", \\\"arcade\\\", \\\"boss fights\\\"]\\n  }\\n}\\n\",\"total_lines\":51}}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa38-de6f-7dc0-ae0d-e0f717ed75f2","uuid":"dda7ce70-abfc-4652-9fdd-c82f2cdee242"}
