{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_657","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The screenshots are consistently behind the logical state.\n\nThe about, op, and dev screenshots each lag by roughly three steps. The about image shows focus 3 while the menu is at focus 5. The op image shows focus 1 after two down presses. The dev image shows focus 2 after four down presses.\n\nThe story screenshot lags by two steps rather than three. The about, op, and dev screenshots each lag by three steps.\n\nThe lag appears to be a three-frame swapchain or compositor delay. Waiting four extra frames after the screen settles should let the display catch up. The timestamps show each screenshot was captured about one second apart.\n\nThe roughly one-minute gap between the title and about screenshots suggests each transition takes about eight seconds. If key presses return quickly, frames are fast. That would make the three-frame lag equal to one to three seconds.\n\nThe title screenshot was black because it was captured on the first status before the mesh painted. The plan is to update shot() so it waits until the same screen remains stable for four seconds of polling, then grabs the image.\n\nThe title screenshot must be painted before any pad input. The capture order is: boot to title, wait four seconds while the title remains stable, shot the title, record the before status, then press pad and wait for the menu. A dark luma check will trigger a regrab if the frame is too dim.\n\nThe required screenshot is the painted title. A second menu.png will be saved as extra proof of the input change, but it is not mandatory.\n\nThe four-second wait may be too short if frames are slow. On the title screen, the status shows no frame counter and the timer never changes between polls, so there is no way to measure actual frame time. A harmless mouse wiggle could help detect when a new frame arrives, or the script could simply time how long the pad press takes to change the screen.\n\nThe pad press likely takes about one frame. The total run time of 197 seconds suggests frames are only 0.3 to 1 second long, so the three-frame lag is roughly three seconds. The wait will be five seconds after the screen stabilizes, and at least four status polls will pass before capturing.\n\nA canvas-independent frame counter will replace the polling wait. The script will hook requestAnimationFrame to count frames, then wait until that counter increases by four after the screen stabilizes.\n\nThe frame counter will be injected via an init script so it runs from the very start. After the screen stabilizes, the script records the current frame number and waits until that count reaches five more than that baseline. This guarantees four extra presented frames after the screen settles, letting the three-frame lag catch up.\n\nThe extra requestAnimationFrame loop will not interfere with winit's redraw callback. A `settle` helper is being drafted to wait until the screen matches and the frame counter has advanced by at least five.\n\nThe `settle` helper will be called before each screenshot to ensure the frame counter has advanced. Five frames of waiting after the title screen appears should let the mesh paint, since the earlier successful title capture already worked with a short delay. The plan is to update `launch.py`, rerun the script, and delete the temporary crop images afterward.\n\nThe extra requestAnimationFrame loop might alter Chrome's frame pacing, but that is acceptable. The script must be rerun because the existing files are incorrect; a full honest capture is required rather than reshooting individual frames. The hub.txt solo line remains valid.","signature":""},{"type":"text","text":"The grabs are a few frames behind the sim: the title shots are black, and the later ones still show the previous menu. I’ll wait for several presented frames before each capture."},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-db7e0ed9-2a19-46f2-a79d-cc455863da65-89","name":"search_replace","input":{"file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224015__x42677a/tmp/grok-goal-907ccca5ce3b/implementer/launch.py","old_string":"PAD = \"\"\"\n(() => { const buttons = Array.from({length: 17}, () => ({pressed: false, touched: false, value: 0}));\n  const pad = {id: 'DualSense Wireless Controller (STANDARD GAMEPAD Vendor: 054c Product: 0ce6)', index: 0, connected: true,\n               mapping: 'standard', timestamp: 0, axes: [0, 0, 0, 0], buttons};\n  window.__pad = pad; navigator.getGamepads = () => [pad, null, null, null]; })();\n\"\"\"","new_string":"PAD = \"\"\"\n(() => { const buttons = Array.from({length: 17}, () => ({pressed: false, touched: false, value: 0}));\n  const pad = {id: 'DualSense Wireless Controller (STANDARD GAMEPAD Vendor: 054c Product: 0ce6)', index: 0, connected: true,\n               mapping: 'standard', timestamp: 0, axes: [0, 0, 0, 0], buttons};\n  window.__pad = pad; navigator.getGamepads = () => [pad, null, null, null];\n  let n = 0;\n  const loop = () => { window.__frames = ++n; requestAnimationFrame(loop); };\n  requestAnimationFrame(loop);\n})();\n\"\"\""}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-db7e0ed9-2a19-46f2-a79d-cc455863da65-90","name":"search_replace","input":{"file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224015__x42677a/tmp/grok-goal-907ccca5ce3b/implementer/launch.py","old_string":"def shot(page, path):\n    path.parent.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)\n    page.wait_for_timeout(600)\n    display = os.environ.get(\"DISPLAY\", \":0\")\n    proc = subprocess.run(","new_string":"def frames(page):\n    return page.evaluate(\"() => window.__frames || 0\")\n\n\ndef settle(page, screen, extra=6):\n    \"\"\"The X grab lags the sim by a few presents. Wait until this screen has been drawn again.\"\"\"\n    start = frames(page)\n    last = None\n    deadline = time.time() + 25\n    while time.time() < deadline:\n        last = status(page)\n        if last.get(\"screen\") == screen and frames(page) >= start + extra:\n            return last\n        page.wait_for_timeout(200)\n    return last\n\n\ndef luma(path):\n    proc = subprocess.run(\n        [\"ffmpeg\", \"-v\", \"error\", \"-i\", str(path), \"-f\", \"rawvideo\", \"-pix_fmt\", \"gray\", \"-\"],\n        capture_output=True,\n    )\n    data = proc.stdout\n    if not data:\n        return 0.0\n    return sum(data) / len(data)\n\n\ndef shot(page, path, screen):\n    path.parent.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)\n    settle(page, screen)\n    display = os.environ.get(\"DISPLAY\", \":0\")\n    for _ in range(3):\n        proc = subprocess.run("}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":3293,"output_tokens":2898,"cache_read_input_tokens":127104,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa38-de6f-7dc0-ae0d-e0f717ed75f2","uuid":"91c7faca-b8f6-4fa8-b59d-fcab285b98c4"}
