{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_687","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The attract mode already runs the bot inside the simulation.\n\nAttract mode reboots after the bot finishes instead of showing results. The existing Dev command \"what: 6\" forces results mode, which is the simplest path.\n\nThe forced results mode does not satisfy the evaluator's requirement to drive a skill-1.0 bot through an actual finished operation. The correct approach is to route the bot into slot 0 during M_OP when the shell flag is active, then let the normal finish_op path display results. A SurgeryCmd::Dev toggle on a `bot_drive` field is being considered as a lightweight way to pass this flag into the simulation.\n\nThe shell already toggles `bot_plays` locally without sending a command. The existing Dev command enum has eight slots, so adding a toggle there would be magic-numbery. A dedicated named command is cleaner but requires more files. The next step is to inspect the SurgeryCmd and Cmd definitions in the shell.\n\nThe simulation overwrites slot 0 after receiving input, so the bot can run inside the sim without blocking product input. The shell will set a `bot_drive` flag during pause, then unpause to let the bot play. The screenshot flow starts by booting the game and navigating to case 0.\n\nThe exact pause-and-resume flow is now mapped: pause, navigate to Dev Mode, toggle \"Bot plays,\" then resume. The shell clears its paused flag on resume, so the simulation stays active. The skill level is already 1.0 by default. Case 0 requires roughly 23 frames at real-time capped dt, which may be slow in a web environment.\n\nA burst step of 240 ticks can finish case 0 in a single frame. The simulation overwrites slot 0 with the bot during that burst, so the operation ends instantly. The shell then detects mode 4 and switches to results.\n\nThe shell's note_mode returns early while paused, so the Dev screen stays visible during the burst. The simulation switches to results mode immediately after the burst ends.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-c25b1e34-c2ed-4f69-af1e-d56e60df8f3e-147","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224015__x42677a/work/engine-link/crates/pav_ui/src/surgery/mod.rs","offset":700,"limit":50}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-c25b1e34-c2ed-4f69-af1e-d56e60df8f3e-148","name":"grep","input":{"pattern":"enum Cmd|enum SurgeryCmd|bot_drive|struct Surgery","path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224015__x42677a/work/engine-link/crates","glob":"*.rs"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1341,"output_tokens":1355,"cache_read_input_tokens":168960,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa38-de6f-7dc0-ae0d-e0f717ed75f2","uuid":"091e018d-21aa-430e-96a7-cf7a7fa7ea64"}
