{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_689","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Surgery derives Serialize and Deserialize.\n\nAdding `#[serde(default)]` to the new `bot_drive` field prevents old save files from breaking. It defaults to `false`. The `fresh()` function also needs this field added.\n\nDev toggle 8 now sets `bot_drive` from the `extra` value instead of toggling it. The attract and operator modes will check this flag to control bot behavior.\n\nThe bot will run in attract and operator modes when `bot_drive` is enabled. Pause freezes the simulation, so the bot stops during the dev menu and resumes afterward. The screenshot script will burst 200 ticks to finish case 0.\n\nThe screenshot script will load case 0 and burst 240 ticks to finish it. A new `results.py` script automates the full sequence: boot, pad to menu, navigate to case files, enter operator mode, pause, enter dev menu, toggle bot focus 1, resume, then step the simulation.\n\nThe `__game.step` function is confirmed available for the screenshot script. Pausing quickly after entering the dev menu limits idle damage to vitals, since case 0 is resolved in about 2.3 seconds.\n\nThe screenshot script will pause immediately upon entering operator mode. This prevents the patient from bleeding for several seconds before the bot takes over. The extra frame of simulation time before pausing is negligible.\n\nDev mode is only reachable from the pause menu, so entering an operator case first is unavoidable. The screenshot script will pause immediately upon entry. There is a concern that burst() calls sim.step directly and may ignore the paused flag.\n\nBursting while paused is safe. The simulation still advances, but the shell remains frozen because note_mode exits early when paused. Resuming afterward lets the screen switch to results normally. This prevents the patient from bleeding during menu navigation.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use",