{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_699","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Confirmed that `slots` is used later. Proceeding with the edit.\n\nVerified that `finish_op` sets mode before outcome. Will implement the fix, then run the single native test first for faster feedback, followed by the full suite, balance, and wasm.\n\nWasm and native builds will run sequentially to avoid Cargo lock conflicts. Checking build-web.sh and HTML output paths. The results script will be self-contained since launch.py is not a module.\n\nScreenshot settling will use `__frames` like launch.py. Will update notes.json after results. Target will be deleted again at the end, after the suite, balance, wasm pack, and screenshot. The new pack requires re-deleting target. Surgery serde tests likely won't break compilation. Cmd::Dev is already mapped in product to_sim.\n\nNo product change is needed if the shell emits the command. The browser path works once the shell pushes it and the simulation honors it.\n\nWhen paused on dev, the command still executes via host.exec in the frame. Burst steps the simulation, but the frame pump may be paused. The burst drains at the start of the next surgery_frame.\n\nThe bot plays sequence is now fully traced. The frame drains the burst and finishes the case. If paused, note_mode keeps the screen on dev even though mode is results. Escape to pause then Enter to resume fixes this by setting mode 4. The fix is to make note_mode return early when paused.","signature":""},{"type":"text","text":"Dev Mode’s “Bot plays” switch never reached the sim. I’ll connect it, then let a skill-1.0 bot finish a case and capture the results screen."},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-a88253e9-d607-4a86-862a-c704ab4a8b54-166","name":"search_replace","input":{"file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224015__x42677a/work/engine-link/crates/pav_core/src/games/surgery/mod.rs","old_strin