e 7. A build that drops a forbidden piece is not done.\\n- The HTML basename must contain the source string `Trauma Center: Second Opinion`, including the colon. Do not sanitize it away.\\n- The title is chosen at implementation time, so this plan cannot name the file. Match the pattern.\\n- Headless WebGPU pixels need the swiftshader flags; a successful blank capture is a game failure. If earlyoom or a missing display kills the browser, keep the log and use the sim/shell bar only in that case.\\n50→- Other agents share this machine. Do not `pkill`, `killall`, or kill a port you did not bind; stop only PIDs this work started. Keep files inside the work folder.\\n\",\"absolute_path\":\"/home/micha/.grok/sessions/%2Fhome%2Fmicha%2Fdev%2Fcc-matrix%2Fruns%2Fgrok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224015__x42677a%2Fwork/01a1aa38-de6f-7dc0-ae0d-e0f717ed75f2/goal/plan.md\",\"offset\":null,\"raw_output\":\"# Plan: Build the original surgical-action drama in workspace PLAN.md and hand in the TASK.md package\\n\\n## Goal kind\\ncode-change\\n\\n## Acceptance criteria\\n1. The work folder contains `PROGRESS.md`, a dev subfolder, and beside it one self-contained HTML file whose basename is `{GameTitle}-Trauma Center: Second Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-224015` (the same name as the dev subfolder). `{GameTitle}` is one playful riff on the source name, chosen with a real RNG and stored so the title screen, page title, hub card, and About screen match. `exit-interview.json` in that same root parses as one object in TASK.md’s exact shape: `usage` is exactly `added on import`; feedback arrays follow the question order; `aiHub` is filled. The page embeds those answers in `<script type=\\\"application/json\\\" id=\\\"about-data\\\">` and the About screen shows Source Information, Testing Feedback, Engine Feedback, and Prompt Feedback. Shipped game content has no TODOs, placeholders, or stubbed features, and does not use the source’s world (Hope Hospital, Caduceus, Stiles, GUILT, Healing Touc