{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_719","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The work is complete. I will now write a completion reply that includes the four about sections verbatim.","signature":""},{"type":"text","text":"Hands of Harbor: Second Opinion is packed and the computer-side plan is done. The work folder holds the dev tree, the single HTML file, `exit-interview.json`, and `PROGRESS.md`.\n\nThe page title is Hands of Harbor: Second Opinion. `exit-interview.json` matches the page `about-data` block, usage is `added on import`, and `session.js` is the first script. The suite log is `14 passed, 0 failed`. Skill 1.0 wins every case and Code Blue; skill 0 loses all of them. Balance for skills 1.0, 0.7, 0.4, and 0 is in the scratch `balance.txt`. Two `file://` launches show the title, music `0.10`, a 1920×1080 canvas, and the same pad-south step into the menu, with an empty console. The results shot is Anton Deverell, The First Movement, score 3616, rank ENCORE, after Dev Mode “Bot plays” finished the operation. Hub harness queries passed. On the two-page aim check the client moved the host cursor; vitals were one snapshot apart (61.68 on the host, 62.40 on the client).\n\n## Source Information\n\n- Date: 2026-11-04 22:40:15\n- Source: Trauma Center: Second Opinion\n- Plan: PLAN.md\n- Genre: Simulation\n- Perspective: Fixed overhead view of the operative field\n- Tech: Pavilion engine (Shardfall commit 49ef2ba), Rust 1.98.1, wgpu/WebGPU, wasm-bindgen 0.2.129, egui 0.36.2\n- Art Direction: Cel-shaded overhead operative field painted per vertex, with layered paper-theatre cards for story\n- Animation: Simulation-driven tissue, instruments, heartbeat, and paper-card motion\n- Audio: Synthesized music, effects, and short gibberish voices. No audio files. Music bus defaults to 0.10\n- Online: Optional AI Hub shared-world Code Blue for 1-4 surgeons\n- Testing: Deterministic sim suite, headless shell, Chromium file:// launches, hub harness\n- Research: Engine seams and the hub protocol, recorded in PLAN.md\n- Environment: Grok CLI (headless); Linux\n- Model: xAI, grok-4.7, reasoning effort xhigh\n- Usage: added on import\n\n## Testing Feedback\n\n- Testing caught five issues: a Rust or-pattern guard skipped stage-0 sutures, nearest-hazard selection stole forceps pulls, a sac's swell shared the laser charge meter, hub snapshots waited on a 60 Hz accumulator that never fired in an iframe, and ControlFlow::Poll cancelled the pending animation frame so an operation froze after one tick.\n- 5\n- The most helpful checks were a skill-1.0 bot on every case from a fresh scene, and the hub harness traffic counters once the frame loop actually ticked.\n- The least helpful test was a temporary print probe that only dumped stuck hazards and was removed once the selection bug was fixed.\n\n## Engine Feedback\n\n- The Game hook, recorded input, RenderFrame, headless egui, and the single-file packer.\n- Yes. A colon in the project path makes rustc fail joining LD_LIBRARY_PATH, and the demo frame path captures the camera, pause menu, and touch layer unless a game returns first.\n- The operative rules, the plate mesh, the ten-foot shell, the cue and music buses, and the hub shim.\n- Keeping a surgery scene off the demo boot panel, stats, guide, toasts, and the engine pause menu.\n- Added the surgery frame, surgeon input, and cue event; a view emit and camera shot; a product frame branch; audio buses and formants; session.js injection in the packer; and js-sys. On the web the surgery loop waits for animation frames, because Poll cancelled the pending frame. The hook alone cannot draw, play cues, or join a hub.\n- A first-class per-game frame path, so a new game does not have to outrun the demo loop.\n\n## Prompt Feedback\n\n- The tested camera, light, and palette numbers, and a hub shim that the harness had already accepted.\n- The deliverable folder name must contain a colon, which Cargo cannot use as its working directory.\n- Shipping one packed page that is the full game, a hub client, and a file:// WebGPU build.\n- Say at the start that the Cargo target directory cannot contain a colon."}],"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1203,"output_tokens":1216,"cache_read_input_tokens":49536,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa38-de6f-7dc0-ae0d-e0f717ed75f2","uuid":"828dd6f5-1841-4557-8127-168b407433cb"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_720","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Reading STAGE.md to continue the goal.\n\nThe hub multiplayer vitals check shows a one-snapshot timing gap between host and client. I need to fix the snapshot alignment so both sides report identical values, then overwrite hub.txt with the passing evidence.\n\nThe hub protocol sends snapshots from the host and inputs from clients. The shim only finishes on time-up when isHost is true. This timing gap causes the one-snapshot vitals mismatch.\n\nThe server slot must never be written into surgeons[slot]. The DOM aim shim sends JSON {x,y,use} and the product converts it to a stick Vec2. Snap keys round vitals, timer, and code_t to 0.1 using a \"s\" key. The one-snapshot gap likely occurs because the client has not yet applied the latest snapshot when the comparison happens.\n\nThe host advances the simulation between snapshots, so live vitals diverge from published ones. The test should compare the last published snapshot on the host against the client's applied snapshot. I will fix the test to wait until both sides share the same snapshot before comparing.\n\nThe evaluator's wording suggests a product bug rather than a test timing issue. I will examine the snapshot and two-page test code carefully before making any changes.\n\nI will keep a running todo. I am reading the hub cursor test and related code now.\n\nBuild constraints are strict. No retuning of suture, sticky select, or sac aux2 is allowed. No subagents, no pkill, and no HOME or CARGO_HOME changes. Chromium must use TMPDIR=/tmp/hbr-pw. Targets were deleted and must be recreated for pack. Cargo must not overlap. The server was stopped. A colon in path issue exists.\n\nThe vitals mismatch is 61.67979049682617 on the host versus 62.400001525878906 on the client.\n\nThe host reports live unrounded vitals while the client shows a rounded snapshot. The 0.7 gap confirms the client is genuinely one snapshot behind, not merely a rounding artifact. Both sides must be compared against the same snapshot generation.","signature":""},{"type":"text","text":"The two-page hub check still shows the client one snapshot behind the host. I’ll find where vitals are published and applied, then make that comparison report the same numbers."},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-439b19ca-d59a-4088-8499-861613b9fd9b-13","name":"todo_write","input":{"todos":[{"id":"9","content":"Fix hub snapshot timing so host and client vitals match, re-run the two-page check, overwrite hub.txt","status":"in_progress"}],"merge":true}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-439b19ca-d59a-4088-8499-861613b9fd9b-14","name":"grep","input":{"pattern":"vitals|snapshot|hub_quiet|k:\\\"s\\\"|publish","glob":"**/*hub*","path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224015__x42677a/work/Hands of Harbor: Second Opinion-Trauma Center: Second Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-224015"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-439b19ca-d59a-4088-8499-861613b9fd9b-15","name":"grep","input":{"pattern":"fn status|vitals|snapshot|Snap","glob":"**/*.{rs,js}","path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224015__x42677a/work/Hands of Harbor: Second Opinion-Trauma Center: Second Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-224015/engine","head_limit":80}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":37163,"output_tokens":1429,"cache_read_input_tokens":14848,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa38-de6f-7dc0-ae0d-e0f717ed75f2","uuid":"14776a12-dfc6-46ab-bf2d-05c9ce8ba37b"}
