": self.skill,\\n            \\\"players\\\": self.players,\\n            \\\"title\\\": TITLE,\",\"absolute_path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224015__x42677a/work/Hands of Harbor: Second Opinion-Trauma Center: Second Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-224015/engine/crates/pav_core/src/games/surgery/mod.rs\",\"offset\":1000,\"limit\":90,\"raw_output\":\"    let mut g = Surgery::fresh();\\n    match rest.unwrap_or(\\\"title\\\") {\\n        \\\"campaign\\\" => g.boot_campaign(),\\n        \\\"codeblue\\\" | \\\"code\\\" => g.boot_code(),\\n        \\\"attract\\\" => g.boot_attract(),\\n        \\\"card\\\" => {\\n            g.mode = M_CARD;\\n            g.case_id = -1;\\n            g.boot_code();\\n            g.mode = M_CARD;\\n            g.outcome = Outcome::Playing;\\n            g.hazards.clear();\\n        }\\n        \\\"mirror\\\" => g.mode = M_MIRROR,\\n        s if s.starts_with(\\\"case/\\\") => {\\n            let n: u8 = s[5..].parse().unwrap_or(0);\\n            g.boot_single(n.min(7));\\n        }\\n        _ => g.mode = M_TITLE,\\n    }\\n    sim.state.play = Some(GameBox::new(g));\\n    Ok(())\\n}\\n\\nimpl Game for Surgery {\\n    const KEY: &'static str = \\\"surgery\\\";\\n\\n    fn pre(&mut self, sim: &mut Sim, input: &InputFrame, dt: f32, events: &mut Vec<SimEvent>) -> std::collections::BTreeMap<crate::entity::EntityId, InputFrame> {\\n        let cmd = input.surgery_cmd;\\n        if let Some(cmd) = cmd {\\n            self.command(cmd);\\n        }\\n        ops::tick(self, sim, input, dt, events, cmd.is_some());\\n        std::collections::BTreeMap::new()\\n    }\\n\\n    fn hud(&self, _sim: &Sim) -> Vec<String> {\\n        Vec::new()\\n    }\\n\\n    fn status(&self, _sim: &Sim) -> serde_json::Value {\\n        let fr = self.to_frame();\\n        let cursors: Vec<_> = self\\n            .surgeons\\n            .iter()\\n            .map(|s| json!({ \\\"x\\\": s.x, \\\"z\\\": s.z, \\\"tool\\\": s.tool, \\\"active\\\": s.active }))\\n            .collect();\\n        json!({\\n            \\\"mode\\\": self.mode_name(),\\n            \\\"case\\\": self.case_id,\\n            \\\"op\\\": fr.op_name,\\n            \\\"patient\\\": fr.patient,\\n            \\\"vitals\\\": self.heart.vitals,\\n            \\\"bpm\\\": self.heart.bpm,\\n            \\\"on_beat\\\": fr.on_beat,\\n            \\\"timer\\\": self.timer,\\n            \\\"score\\\": fr.score,\\n            \\\"par\\\": self.par,\\n            \\\"rank\\\": rank_name(self.rank),\\n            \\\"rank_n\\\": self.rank,\\n            \\\"chain\\\": self.best_chain(),\\n            \\\"mistakes\\\": self.mistakes,\\n            \\\"phase\\\": self.phase_i,\\n            \\\"strain\\\": self.strain_phase,\\n            \\\"alive\\\": self.hazards.iter().filter(|h| h.alive && h.kind != K_HEAT).count(),\\n            \\\"flat\\\": self.heart.flat,\\n            \\\"code\\\": self.code_t,\\n            \\\"codes_left\\\": self.codes_left,\\n            \\\"music\\\": self.tune.music,\\n            \\\"effects\\\": self.tune.effects,\\n            \\\"voices\\\": self.tune.voices,\\n            \\\"gifts\\\": self.gifts_unlocked,\\n            \\\"gifts_used\\\": self.gifts_used,\\n            \\\"tools\\\": self.coverage.tools,\\n            \\\"hazards\\\": self.coverage.hazards,\\n            \\\"strains\\\": self.coverage.strains,\\n            \\\"gift_counts\\\": self.coverage.gifts,\\n            \\\"code_count\\\": self.coverage.code,\\n            \\\"ratings\\\": self.coverage.ratings,\\n            \\\"outcome\\\": match self.outcome {\\n                Outcome::Playing => \\\"playing\\\",\\n                Outcome::Won => \\\"won\\\",\\n                Outcome::Lost => \\\"lost\\\",\\n            },\\n            \\\"story_i\\\": self.story_i,\\n            \\\"story\\\": fr.story_line,\\n            \\\"callout\\\": fr.callout,\\n            \\\"skill\\\": self.skill,\\n            \\\"players\\\": self.players,\\n            \\\"title\\\": TITLE,\\n\",\"total_lines\":1117}}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa38-de6f-7dc0-ae0d-e0f717ed75f2","uuid":"09215364-dcb5-4006-b023-0815f5c655ad"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_724","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Snapshots round vitals to zero.\n\nThe host reports live vitals while the client displays a delayed snapshot. This timing gap causes mismatched values at comparison points. The fix requires aligning the host's live output with the client's snapshot.\n\nOption A would freeze the host's vitals to the last published snapshot until the next update. The host currently keeps simulating after sending, so its live value drifts away from the snapshot.\n\nThe host must report its last-sent rounded vitals instead of live values. The client will still lag until it applies the snapshot. The test needs to poll until both sides match. The evaluator requires both fixing snapshot timing and re-running the hub cursor/vitals check.\n\nThe host status and the snapshot it just sent are identical except for rounding. The client status reflects the previous snapshot. This means the host is already reporting the last published state, so the mismatch is purely a rounding difference.\n\nThe host status already includes `snap_v`, the sequence number of its last sent snapshot. The client status includes `snap_v` for the snapshot it just applied. Comparing these fields would reveal the one-snapshot lag directly. The test should compare both `vitals` values and both `snap_v` values to confirm they match.\n\nThe host simulates every frame at 15Hz while the client only updates at snapshot intervals. This creates a one-frame race window where the two sides can align. Pausing both systems until the client applies the matching snapshot would eliminate the timing mismatch.\n\nThe 500ms poll is too short to catch the one-frame alignment window. Even when it does, rounding still creates a mismatch. The robust fix is to make snapshots the authoritative source of truth. Both sides should report the last snapshot's rounded vitals. The test should wait until a snapshot fully propagates, either by comparing sequence IDs or by polling until two consecutive samples match after input settles.\n\nThe timer gap of 0.1 is exactly one rounding quantum and one snapshot interval. This confirms the vitals mismatch is a direct result of the one-snapshot lag.\n\nThe timer gap is 0.1 seconds, which equals roughly one to two snapshots at 15Hz. The client snapshot is therefore about one to two snapshots older than the host. This explains why vitals differ by more than a single rounding quantum.\n\nThe heart drain formula confirms vitals drop quickly during code blue. Even after rounding is fixed, the host and client will still differ because the host keeps simulating while the client waits. Pausing both systems from outside is difficult without a command, so the practical fix is to make snapshots carry a sequence number and have the host report its last sent vitals.\n\nThe host keeps sending newer snapshots at 15Hz, so the client always lags behind. Comparing sequence numbers would not work because the host is always ahead. The better approach is to freeze snapshot generation during comparison: send one final snapshot and then stop advancing the reported state.\n\nA test-specific freeze is too narrow. The real bug may be step ordering: the host builds snapshots before simulating, while the client applies snapshots and then ticks vitals locally. If the client drains vitals after applying, its status would read lower than the snapshot, not higher. The host order would produce the opposite divergence.\n\nThe client is behind the host, not ahead. Its vitals are higher because it is displaying a stale snapshot while the host keeps simulating live. Rounding both sides to the same 0.1 interval would still leave them unequal, since vitals drain at roughly 7 points per second. The two values drift apart faster than one snapshot can freeze them.\n\nThe evaluator likely wants snapshots sampled from the pre-step state, with both sides reporting that same snapshot. The host should record its last sent vitals and sequence number at send time, while the client stores its applied sequence and vitals. The test must wait for the in-flight snapshot to land before comparing.\n\nThe host should return its last-sent snapshot vitals instead of live heart.vitals. The client already reports rounded applied vitals. A synchronous read in evaluate() would see the client still on the previous sequence, so the test must poll until both sides match.\n\nA single synchronous read cannot align the two sides because the host keeps sending newer snapshots while the client lags behind. The host must either pause snapshot advancement during comparison, or the test must accept a momentary match when vitals are stable and rounded values do not change across snapshots.\n\nPausing both systems via the shell would freeze vitals. The host could still send snapshots of that frozen state, so the client would apply a matching snapshot and both sides would report identical values after one round trip. The key question is whether pause actually stops the simulation.\n\nPausing the host would freeze snapshots and let the client catch up, but Plan.md forbids pause inside a hub session. The mirror client may also fail to sync. A proper fix using snapshot timestamps and sequence numbers is too complex.\n\nA cleaner model would have the host publish snapshots and report those exact values as its own status, rather than reading live state after publishing. Both sides would then share the same published snapshot, but the race condition remains.\n\nThe host must stop advancing its reported state until the snapshot matches what status displays. The test should hold input for 2.5 seconds, release it, and then poll both sides in a loop until vitals and cursor position align. Live host status and snapshot-based client status will never match by chance, so the host must return its last-sent rounded vitals as its own status.\n\nA polling loop that waits for client frames to process is flawed because the host keeps sending new snapshots during that wait, so the host vitals keep changing. The snapshot values themselves are not stable across frames, which makes it impossible to align the two sides by waiting for a quiet period.\n\nThe host must keep its displayed vitals locked to the confirmed snapshot until the client acknowledges it, but this conflicts with showing live simulation to the player. The evaluator specifically asked to fix snapshot timing, so I will check git history for clues about a 60Hz accumulator bug.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-cd0c025e-1b65-439f-9f16-e9adddafdad0-25","name":"grep","input":{"pattern":"vitals match|same vitals|snapshot","path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224015__x42677a/work/PLAN.md","head_limit":40}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-cd0c025e-1b65-439f-9f16-e9adddafdad0-26","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224015__x42677a/work/Hands of Harbor: Second Opinion-Trauma Center: Second Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-224015/engine/crates/pav_core/src/games/surgery/ops.rs","offset":1,"limit":80}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-cd0c025e-1b65-439f-9f16-e9adddafdad0-27","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224015__x42677a/work/Hands of Harbor: Second Opinion-Trauma Center: Second Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-224015/engine/crates/pav_core/src/games/surgery/ops.rs","offset":700,"limit":80}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-cd0c025e-1b65-439f-9f16-e9adddafdad0-28","name":"grep","input":{"pattern":"fn pump|paused","glob":"**/simhost.rs"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":8976,"output_tokens":3253,"cache_read_input_tokens":73472,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa38-de6f-7dc0-ae0d-e0f717ed75f2","uuid":"866a2b89-0e77-4882-8409-5bc05838676f"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-cd0c025e-1b65-439f-9f16-e9adddafdad0-25","content":"{\"type\":\"GrepSearch\",\"stdout\":[60,119,111,114,107,115,112,97,99,101,95,114,101,115,117,108,116,32,119,111,114,107,115,112,97,99,101,95,112,97,116,104,61,34,47,104,111,109,101,47,109,105,99,104,97,47,100,101,118,47,99,99,45,109,97,116,114,105,120,47,114,117,110,115,47,103,114,111,107,45,120,104,105,103,104,46,98,117,105,108,100,45,118,50,95,95,50,48,50,54,49,49,48,52,45,50,50,52,48,49,53,95,95,120,52,50,54,55,55,97,47,119,111,114,107,34,62,10,70,111,117,110,100,32,51,32,109,97,116,99,104,105,110,103,32,108,105,110,101,115,10,47,104,111,109,101,47,109,105,99,104,97,47,100,101,118,47,99,99,45,109,97,116,114,105,120,47,114,117,110,115,47,103,114,111,107,45,120,104,105,103,104,46,98,117,105,108,100,45,118,50,95,95,50,48,50,54,49,49,48,52,45,50,50,52,48,49,53,95,95,120,52,50,54,55,55,97,47,119,111,114,107,47,80,76,65,78,46,109,100,10,51,54,55,58,32,32,40,104,105,116,32,114,97,100,105,105,44,32,116,97,114,103,101,116,115,44,32,98,101,97,116,32,119,105,110,100,111,119,44,32,97,115,115,105,115,116,32,114,97,100,105,117,115,41,44,32,70,80,83,32,97,110,100,32,116,105,99,107,32,115,116,97,116,115,44,32,114,101,119,105,110,100,32,53,32,115,32,97,110,100,32,115,110,97,112,115,104,111,116,32,115,97,118,101,47,108,111,97,100,32,40,116,104,101,10,52,57,56,58,32,32,101,100,103,101,115,32,114,101,112,101,97,116,101,100,32,117,110,116,105,108,32,115,101,101,110,46,32,84,104,101,32,104,111,115,116,32,115,101,110,100,115,32,111,110,101,32,115,110,97,112,115,104,111,116,32,97,116,32,97,98,111,117,116,32,49,53,32,72,122,32,40,96,114,101,108,105,97,98,108,101,58,32,102,97,108,115,101,96,41,58,32,118,105,116,97,108,115,44,32,98,101,97,116,32,112,104,97,115,101,44,32,66,80,77,44,10,54,50,53,58,45,32,68,101,116,101,114,109,105,110,105,115,109,58,32,115,110,97,112,115,104,111,116,44,32,114,101,119,105,110,100,32,97,110,100,32,114,101,112,108,97,121,32,104,97,115,104,101,115,32,97,114,101,32,101,120,97,99,116,32,40,99,111,112,121,32,96,101,110,103,105,110,101,47,99,114,97,116,101,115,47,112,97,118,95,99,111,114,101,47,116,101,115,116,115,47,103,97,109,101,115,46,114,115,96,41,46,10,60,47,119,111,114,107,115,112,97,99,101,95,114,101,115,117,108,116,62],\"stderr\":[],\"exit_code\":0,\"match_count\":3,\"file_matches\":[{\"path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224015__x42677a/work/PLAN.md\",\"matches\":[{\"line_number\":367,\"content\":\"  (hit radii, targets, beat window, assist radius), FPS and tick stats, rewind 5 s and snapshot save/load (the\"},{\"line_number\":498,\"content\":\"  edges repeated until seen. The host sends one snapshot at about 15 Hz (`reliable: false`): vitals, beat phase, BPM,\"},{\"line_number\":625,\"content\":\"- Determinism: snapshot, rewind and replay hashes are exact (copy `engine/crates/pav_core/tests/games.rs`).\"}]}]}","is_error":false},{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-cd0c025e-1b65-439f-9f16-e9adddafdad0-26","content":"{\"type\":\"ReadFile\",\"FileContent\":{\"content\":\"1→//! One tick of the operation. Gameplay happens here, where the input is.\\n\\nuse glam::Vec3;\\n\\nuse super::content::{self, case_def, G_DUET, G_ECHO, G_HUSH};\\nuse super::hazard::{self, Hit};\\nuse super::kinds::*;\\nuse super::*;\\nuse super::{bot, story};\\n10→use crate::games::Outcome;\\nuse crate::frame::SimEvent;\\nuse crate::input::{surg, InputFrame, SurgeonInput};\\nuse crate::sim::Sim;\\n\\npub fn tick(g: &mut Surgery, sim: &mut Sim, input: &InputFrame, dt: f32, events: &mut Vec<SimEvent>, had_cmd: bool) {\\n    if g.outcome == Outcome::Lost && g.mode == M_DEAD {\\n        return;\\n    }\\n    let dt = dt.max(0.0);\\n20→    match g.mode {\\n        M_STORY if !had_cmd => {\\n            if confirmed(input) {\\n                let lines = story::block(g.case_id, g.story_after);\\n                if (g.story_i as usize) + 1 >= lines.len() {\\n                    g.end_story();\\n                } else {\\n                    g.story_i = g.story_i.saturating_add(1);\\n                    cue(events, CUE_VOICE, 0.0, 0.0, 0.7, 0.9 + (g.story_i as f32 % 5.0) * 0.04);\\n                }\\n30→            }\\n            return;\\n        }\\n        M_CHART if !had_cmd => {\\n            if confirmed(input) {\\n                g.mode = M_OP;\\n                g.phase_ready = false;\\n                cue(events, CUE_OK, 0.0, 0.0, 0.6, 1.0);\\n            }\\n            return;\\n40→        }\\n        M_RESULTS if !had_cmd => {\\n            if confirmed(input) && g.campaign && g.outcome == Outcome::Playing {\\n                g.mode = M_STORY;\\n                g.story_after = true;\\n                g.story_i = 0;\\n            }\\n            return;\\n        }\\n        M_CARD => {\\n50→            g.card_t += dt;\\n            return;\\n        }\\n        M_MIRROR => {\\n            mirror_predict(g, input, dt);\\n            return;\\n        }\\n        M_TITLE | M_DEAD => return,\\n        M_OP | M_ATTRACT => {}\\n        _ => return,\\n60→    }\\n    if g.outcome != Outcome::Playing {\\n        return;\\n    }\\n\\n    let mut slots = input.surgeons;\\n    if g.mode == M_ATTRACT || (g.mode == M_OP && g.bot_drive) {\\n        slots[0] = bot::decide(g, sim.state.tick, 0);\\n        slots[0].active = true;\\n    }\\n70→    if g.case_id == 7 && !slots[1].active {\\n        slots[1] = bot::decide(g, sim.state.tick, 1);\\n    }\\n    let joined = slots.iter().filter(|s| s.active).count().max(1) as u8;\\n    g.players = g.players.max(joined);\\n\\n    let rules = if g.hush_beats > 0 { dt * g.tune.hush_scale.clamp(0.05, 1.0) } else { dt };\\n    let wave = g.heart.tick(rules, g.tune.heart_coupling);\\n    if wave {\\n        cue(events, CUE_LUB, 0.0, 0.0, 0.35, (g.heart.bpm / 80.0).clamp(0.7, 1.6));\\n80→        if g.hush_beats > 0 {\",\"content_concise\":\"1→//! One tick of the operation. Gameplay happens here, where the input is.\\n\\nuse glam::Vec3;\\n\\nuse super::content::{self, case_def, G_DUET, G_ECHO, G_HUSH};\\nuse super::hazard::{self, Hit};\\nuse super::kinds::*;\\nuse super::*;\\nuse super::{bot, story};\\n10→use crate::games::Outcome;\\nuse crate::frame::SimEvent;\\nuse crate::input::{surg, InputFrame, SurgeonInput};\\nuse crate::sim::Sim;\\n\\npub fn tick(g: &mut Surgery, sim: &mut Sim, input: &InputFrame, dt: f32, events: &mut Vec<SimEvent>, had_cmd: bool) {\\n    if g.outcome == Outcome::Lost && g.mode == M_DEAD {\\n        return;\\n    }\\n    let dt = dt.max(0.0);\\n20→    match g.mode {\\n        M_STORY if !had_cmd => {\\n            if confirmed(input) {\\n                let lines = story::block(g.case_id, g.story_after);\\n                if (g.story_i as usize) + 1 >= lines.len() {\\n                    g.end_story();\\n                } else {\\n                    g.story_i = g.story_i.saturating_add(1);\\n                    cue(events, CUE_VOICE, 0.0, 0.0, 0.7, 0.9 + (g.story_i as f32 % 5.0) * 0.04);\\n                }\\n30→            }\\n            return;\\n        }\\n        M_CHART if !had_cmd => {\\n            if confirmed(input) {\\n                g.mode = M_OP;\\n                g.phase_ready = false;\\n                cue(events, CUE_OK, 0.0, 0.0, 0.6, 1.0);\\n            }\\n            return;\\n40→        }\\n        M_RESULTS if !had_cmd => {\\n            if confirmed(input) && g.campaign && g.outcome == Outcome::Playing {\\n                g.mode = M_STORY;\\n                g.story_after = true;\\n                g.story_i = 0;\\n            }\\n            return;\\n        }\\n        M_CARD => {\\n50→            g.card_t += dt;\\n            return;\\n        }\\n        M_MIRROR => {\\n            mirror_predict(g, input, dt);\\n            return;\\n        }\\n        M_TITLE | M_DEAD => return,\\n        M_OP | M_ATTRACT => {}\\n        _ => return,\\n60→    }\\n    if g.outcome != Outcome::Playing {\\n        return;\\n    }\\n\\n    let mut slots = input.surgeons;\\n    if g.mode == M_ATTRACT || (g.mode == M_OP && g.bot_drive) {\\n        slots[0] = bot::decide(g, sim.state.tick, 0);\\n        slots[0].active = true;\\n    }\\n70→    if g.case_id == 7 && !slots[1].active {\\n        slots[1] = bot::decide(g, sim.state.tick, 1);\\n    }\\n    let joined = slots.iter().filter(|s| s.active).count().max(1) as u8;\\n    g.players = g.players.max(joined);\\n\\n    let rules = if g.hush_beats > 0 { dt * g.tune.hush_scale.clamp(0.05, 1.0) } else { dt };\\n    let wave = g.heart.tick(rules, g.tune.heart_coupling);\\n    if wave {\\n        cue(events, CUE_LUB, 0.0, 0.0, 0.35, (g.heart.bpm / 80.0).clamp(0.7, 1.6));\\n80→        if g.hush_beats > 0 {\",\"absolute_path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224015__x42677a/work/Hands of Harbor: Second Opinion-Trauma Center: Second Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-224015/engine/crates/pav_core/src/games/surgery/ops.rs\",\"offset\":1,\"limit\":80,\"raw_output\":\"//! One tick of the operation. Gameplay happens here, where the input is.\\n\\nuse glam::Vec3;\\n\\nuse super::content::{self, case_def, G_DUET, G_ECHO, G_HUSH};\\nuse super::hazard::{self, Hit};\\nuse super::kinds::*;\\nuse super::*;\\nuse super::{bot, story};\\nuse crate::games::Outcome;\\nuse crate::frame::SimEvent;\\nuse crate::input::{surg, InputFrame, SurgeonInput};\\nuse crate::sim::Sim;\\n\\npub fn tick(g: &mut Surgery, sim: &mut Sim, input: &InputFrame, dt: f32, events: &mut Vec<SimEvent>, had_cmd: bool) {\\n    if g.outcome == Outcome::Lost && g.mode == M_DEAD {\\n        return;\\n    }\\n    let dt = dt.max(0.0);\\n    match g.mode {\\n        M_STORY if !had_cmd => {\\n            if confirmed(input) {\\n                let lines = story::block(g.case_id, g.story_after);\\n                if (g.story_i as usize) + 1 >= lines.len() {\\n                    g.end_story();\\n                } else {\\n                    g.story_i = g.story_i.saturating_add(1);\\n                    cue(events, CUE_VOICE, 0.0, 0.0, 0.7, 0.9 + (g.story_i as f32 % 5.0) * 0.04);\\n                }\\n            }\\n            return;\\n        }\\n        M_CHART if !had_cmd => {\\n            if confirmed(input) {\\n                g.mode = M_OP;\\n                g.phase_ready = false;\\n                cue(events, CUE_OK, 0.0, 0.0, 0.6, 1.0);\\n            }\\n            return;\\n        }\\n        M_RESULTS if !had_cmd => {\\n            if confirmed(input) && g.campaign && g.outcome == Outcome::Playing {\\n                g.mode = M_STORY;\\n                g.story_after = true;\\n                g.story_i = 0;\\n            }\\n            return;\\n        }\\n        M_CARD => {\\n            g.card_t += dt;\\n            return;\\n        }\\n        M_MIRROR => {\\n            mirror_predict(g, input, dt);\\n            return;\\n        }\\n        M_TITLE | M_DEAD => return,\\n        M_OP | M_ATTRACT => {}\\n        _ => return,\\n    }\\n    if g.outcome != Outcome::Playing {\\n        return;\\n    }\\n\\n    let mut slots = input.surgeons;\\n    if g.mode == M_ATTRACT || (g.mode == M_OP && g.bot_drive) {\\n        slots[0] = bot::decide(g, sim.state.tick, 0);\\n        slots[0].active = true;\\n    }\\n    if g.case_id == 7 && !slots[1].active {\\n        slots[1] = bot::decide(g, sim.state.tick, 1);\\n    }\\n    let joined = slots.iter().filter(|s| s.active).count().max(1) as u8;\\n    g.players = g.players.max(joined);\\n\\n    let rules = if g.hush_beats > 0 { dt * g.tune.hush_scale.clamp(0.05, 1.0) } else { dt };\\n    let wave = g.heart.tick(rules, g.tune.heart_coupling);\\n    if wave {\\n        cue(events, CUE_LUB, 0.0, 0.0, 0.35, (g.heart.bpm / 80.0).clamp(0.7, 1.6));\\n        if g.hush_beats > 0 {\\n\",\"total_lines\":805}}","is_error":false},{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-cd0c025e-1b65-439f-9f16-e9adddafdad0-27","content":"{\"type\":\"ReadFile\",\"FileContent\":{\"content\":\"700→        let d = h.dist(x, z);\\n        if d <= h.radius + 0.12 && d < best_d {\\n            best_d = d;\\n            best = Some(i);\\n        }\\n    }\\n    best\\n}\\n\\nfn assist_aim(g: &Surgery, x: f32, z: f32, tool: u8, aim: glam::Vec2, dt: f32) -> glam::Vec2 {\\n710→    let scale = g.tune.aim_assist.clamp(0.0, 2.0);\\n    if scale <= 0.0 || aim.length_squared() < 0.0004 {\\n        return aim;\\n    }\\n    let mut best: Option<(f32, f32, f32)> = None;\\n    for h in &g.hazards {\\n        if !h.alive || h.kind == K_HEAT || !h.accepts(tool) {\\n            continue;\\n        }\\n        let dx = h.x - x;\\n720→        let dz = h.z - z;\\n        let d = (dx * dx + dz * dz).sqrt();\\n        if d < 1.2 && best.map(|(bd, _, _)| d < bd).unwrap_or(true) {\\n            best = Some((d, dx, dz));\\n        }\\n    }\\n    let Some((d, dx, dz)) = best else { return aim };\\n    let closeness = (1.0 - d / 1.2).clamp(0.0, 1.0) * scale.min(1.0);\\n    let mut aim = aim * (1.0 - 0.5 * closeness);\\n    if d > 0.02 {\\n730→        let inv = 1.0 / d;\\n        let pull = 3.0 * dt * closeness;\\n        let extra = pull / (g.tune.cursor_speed.max(1.0) * dt.max(1e-4));\\n        aim.x += dx * inv * extra;\\n        aim.y += dz * inv * extra;\\n    }\\n    aim\\n}\\n\\nfn mirror_predict(g: &mut Surgery, input: &InputFrame, dt: f32) {\\n740→    for (i, inp) in input.surgeons.iter().enumerate() {\\n        if !inp.active {\\n            continue;\\n        }\\n        let s = &mut g.surgeons[i];\\n        s.active = true;\\n        if inp.tool != TOOL_KEEP {\\n            s.tool = inp.tool;\\n        }\\n        steer(s, *inp, dt, g.tune.cursor_speed);\\n750→    }\\n}\\n\\nfn steer(s: &mut Surgeon, inp: SurgeonInput, dt: f32, speed: f32) {\\n    let abs = inp.held & surg::AIM_ABSOLUTE != 0;\\n    let snap = inp.held & surg::SNAP != 0;\\n    if abs && snap {\\n        s.x = inp.aim.x;\\n        s.z = inp.aim.y;\\n        return;\\n760→    }\\n    if abs {\\n        let dx = inp.aim.x - s.x;\\n        let dz = inp.aim.y - s.z;\\n        let d = (dx * dx + dz * dz).sqrt();\\n        let step = speed.max(1.0) * dt;\\n        if d <= step || d < 1e-5 {\\n            s.x = inp.aim.x;\\n            s.z = inp.aim.y;\\n        } else {\\n770→            s.x += dx / d * step;\\n            s.z += dz / d * step;\\n        }\\n    } else if inp.aim.length_squared() > 0.0004 {\\n        s.x += inp.aim.x * speed * dt;\\n        s.z += inp.aim.y * speed * dt;\\n    }\\n}\\n\\nfn heat_hit(angle: f32, x: f32, z: f32) -> bool {\",\"content_concise\":\"700→        let d = h.dist(x, z);\\n        if d <= h.radius + 0.12 && d < best_d {\\n            best_d = d;\\n            best = Some(i);\\n        }\\n    }\\n    best\\n}\\n\\nfn assist_aim(g: &Surgery, x: f32, z: f32, tool: u8, aim: glam::Vec2, dt: f32) -> glam::Vec2 {\\n710→    let scale = g.tune.aim_assist.clamp(0.0, 2.0);\\n    if scale <= 0.0 || aim.length_squared() < 0.0004 {\\n        return aim;\\n    }\\n    let mut best: Option<(f32, f32, f32)> = None;\\n    for h in &g.hazards {\\n        if !h.alive || h.kind == K_HEAT || !h.accepts(tool) {\\n            continue;\\n        }\\n        let dx = h.x - x;\\n720→        let dz = h.z - z;\\n        let d = (dx * dx + dz * dz).sqrt();\\n        if d < 1.2 && best.map(|(bd, _, _)| d < bd).unwrap_or(true) {\\n            best = Some((d, dx, dz));\\n        }\\n    }\\n    let Some((d, dx, dz)) = best else { return aim };\\n    let closeness = (1.0 - d / 1.2).clamp(0.0, 1.0) * scale.min(1.0);\\n    let mut aim = aim * (1.0 - 0.5 * closeness);\\n    if d > 0.02 {\\n730→        let inv = 1.0 / d;\\n        let pull = 3.0 * dt * closeness;\\n        let extra = pull / (g.tune.cursor_speed.max(1.0) * dt.max(1e-4));\\n        aim.x += dx * inv * extra;\\n        aim.y += dz * inv * extra;\\n    }\\n    aim\\n}\\n\\nfn mirror_predict(g: &mut Surgery, input: &InputFrame, dt: f32) {\\n740→    for (i, inp) in input.surgeons.iter().enumerate() {\\n        if !inp.active {\\n            continue;\\n        }\\n        let s = &mut g.surgeons[i];\\n        s.active = true;\\n        if inp.tool != TOOL_KEEP {\\n            s.tool = inp.tool;\\n        }\\n        steer(s, *inp, dt, g.tune.cursor_speed);\\n750→    }\\n}\\n\\nfn steer(s: &mut Surgeon, inp: SurgeonInput, dt: f32, speed: f32) {\\n    let abs = inp.held & surg::AIM_ABSOLUTE != 0;\\n    let snap = inp.held & surg::SNAP != 0;\\n    if abs && snap {\\n        s.x = inp.aim.x;\\n        s.z = inp.aim.y;\\n        return;\\n760→    }\\n    if abs {\\n        let dx = inp.aim.x - s.x;\\n        let dz = inp.aim.y - s.z;\\n        let d = (dx * dx + dz * dz).sqrt();\\n        let step = speed.max(1.0) * dt;\\n        if d <= step || d < 1e-5 {\\n            s.x = inp.aim.x;\\n            s.z = inp.aim.y;\\n        } else {\\n770→            s.x += dx / d * step;\\n            s.z += dz / d * step;\\n        }\\n    } else if inp.aim.length_squared() > 0.0004 {\\n        s.x += inp.aim.x * speed * dt;\\n        s.z += inp.aim.y * speed * dt;\\n    }\\n}\\n\\nfn heat_hit(angle: f32, x: f32, z: f32) -> bool {\",\"absolute_path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224015__x42677a/work/Hands of Harbor: Second Opinion-Trauma Center: Second Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-224015/engine/crates/pav_core/src/games/surgery/ops.rs\",\"offset\":700,\"limit\":80,\"raw_output\":\"        let d = h.dist(x, z);\\n        if d <= h.radius + 0.12 && d < best_d {\\n            best_d = d;\\n            best = Some(i);\\n        }\\n    }\\n    best\\n}\\n\\nfn assist_aim(g: &Surgery, x: f32, z: f32, tool: u8, aim: glam::Vec2, dt: f32) -> glam::Vec2 {\\n    let scale = g.tune.aim_assist.clamp(0.0, 2.0);\\n    if scale <= 0.0 || aim.length_squared() < 0.0004 {\\n        return aim;\\n    }\\n    let mut best: Option<(f32, f32, f32)> = None;\\n    for h in &g.hazards {\\n        if !h.alive || h.kind == K_HEAT || !h.accepts(tool) {\\n            continue;\\n        }\\n        let dx = h.x - x;\\n        let dz = h.z - z;\\n        let d = (dx * dx + dz * dz).sqrt();\\n        if d < 1.2 && best.map(|(bd, _, _)| d < bd).unwrap_or(true) {\\n            best = Some((d, dx, dz));\\n        }\\n    }\\n    let Some((d, dx, dz)) = best else { return aim };\\n    let closeness = (1.0 - d / 1.2).clamp(0.0, 1.0) * scale.min(1.0);\\n    let mut aim = aim * (1.0 - 0.5 * closeness);\\n    if d > 0.02 {\\n        let inv = 1.0 / d;\\n        let pull = 3.0 * dt * closeness;\\n        let extra = pull / (g.tune.cursor_speed.max(1.0) * dt.max(1e-4));\\n        aim.x += dx * inv * extra;\\n        aim.y += dz * inv * extra;\\n    }\\n    aim\\n}\\n\\nfn mirror_predict(g: &mut Surgery, input: &InputFrame, dt: f32) {\\n    for (i, inp) in input.surgeons.iter().enumerate() {\\n        if !inp.active {\\n            continue;\\n        }\\n        let s = &mut g.surgeons[i];\\n        s.active = true;\\n        if inp.tool != TOOL_KEEP {\\n            s.tool = inp.tool;\\n        }\\n        steer(s, *inp, dt, g.tune.cursor_speed);\\n    }\\n}\\n\\nfn steer(s: &mut Surgeon, inp: SurgeonInput, dt: f32, speed: f32) {\\n    let abs = inp.held & surg::AIM_ABSOLUTE != 0;\\n    let snap = inp.held & surg::SNAP != 0;\\n    if abs && snap {\\n        s.x = inp.aim.x;\\n        s.z = inp.aim.y;\\n        return;\\n    }\\n    if abs {\\n        let dx = inp.aim.x - s.x;\\n        let dz = inp.aim.y - s.z;\\n        let d = (dx * dx + dz * dz).sqrt();\\n        let step = speed.max(1.0) * dt;\\n        if d <= step || d < 1e-5 {\\n            s.x = inp.aim.x;\\n            s.z = inp.aim.y;\\n        } else {\\n            s.x += dx / d * step;\\n            s.z += dz / d * step;\\n        }\\n    } else if inp.aim.length_squared() > 0.0004 {\\n        s.x += inp.aim.x * speed * dt;\\n        s.z += inp.aim.y * speed * dt;\\n    }\\n}\\n\\nfn heat_hit(angle: f32, x: f32, z: f32) -> bool {\\n\",\"total_lines\":805}}","is_error":false},{"type":"tool_result","tool_