t_b: bool,\\n    lt: f32,\\n    rt: f32,\\n}\\n\\nimpl Default for PadHand {\\n    fn default() -> Self {\\n        Self {\\n            present: false,\\n            left: Vec2::ZERO,\\n            right: Vec2::ZERO,\\n            south: false,\\n            east: false,\\n            north: false,\\n            west: false,\\n            l1: false,\\n            r1: false,\\n            start: false,\\n            up: false,\\n            down: false,\\n            left_b: false,\\n            right_b: false,\\n            lt: 0.0,\\n            rt: 0.0,\\n        }\\n    }\\n}\\n\\n\",\"total_lines\":886}}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa38-de6f-7dc0-ae0d-e0f717ed75f2","uuid":"c9a0d6c6-bddd-40b2-8830-5e42edf09d7f"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_734","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Beginning implementation. Also considering a subtle bug.\n\nConfirmed host and client vitals match across the 500ms bucket. Cursor updates correctly because each snap applies fully. apply_mirror replaces all state including vitals, but the values are identical.\n\nAlso noted two edge cases. A dropped snap due to size is acceptable since the host already latched the value. If send_snap hits a rate limit, the host updates its latch but the client misses the packet; this shrinks the equal window by up to 66ms, which remains safe within the 500ms bucket.\n\nUpdating the latch before send_snap is risky. If the send fails, the host shows new vitals while the client stays stale until the next successful packet. Changing send_snap to return a bool will let the host update the latch only after a successful send.\n\nThe native `send_snap` is currently a no-op, so changing its signature to return a bool would require updates in both backends. Computing the latch before building the body and reverting it on send failure was considered but rejected as too messy. Instead, the host will keep the old latch in status and the next packet while rate limiting.\n\nThe host now computes the snap body before sending. It latches vitals and timer only when the 500ms bucket changes, then passes those values into `snap_json`. This ensures the packet always carries the correct latched data.\n\nThe host now commits the latched vitals only after a successful send. If the packet drops, the status keeps the previous latch and the next frame recomputes from live data. This guarantees the client receives matching values once the packet arrives.\n\nDuring rate-limit frames, host and client remain equal because both keep the old latch. The only inequality window is during packet transit, lasting roughly 16 to 100 milliseconds. The test will now require equality on two consecutive polls spaced 100 milliseconds apart to avoid one-frame drift coincidences.\n\nThe cursor check will read the host seat-1 cursor and vitals together at the comparison point. The test script will wait until both modes are active, mirror mode is ready, and time exceeds 200 milliseconds. It will record the initial cursor position, hold ArrowRight on the client, then poll for up to four seconds.\n\nThe test will wait 150 milliseconds after confirming the cursor moved and vitals matched, then verify both values remain equal. It will release the key and print a BEFORE/AFTER comparison. The test must also exclude boot-default matches so the equality is not just a coincidence at startup.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-eefd6962-0cbe-494f-aed5-93f99b94f12a-47","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224015__x42677a/work/Hands of Harbor: Second Opinion-Trauma Center: Second Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-224015/engine/crates/pav_core/src/games/surgery/mod.rs","offset":450,"limit":55}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":4017,"output_tokens":1473,"cache_read_input_tokens":117504,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa38-de6f-7dc0-ae0d-e0f717ed75f2","uuid":"71b78f8c-9274-4d94-b71c-66b591c80798"}
