{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_735","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Two bleeders with drain 2.6 each total 5.\n\nVital drops align with the 500ms bucket latch. Initial 70.0 matches client boot before any snapshot. reset_hands activates slot 0 first, then boot_hub_round activates present slots.\n\nFixing send_snap return values and checking native and wasm signatures. Client applied_bucket uses >= to preserve cursor-only updates when skipping old snaps. Host net_bucket initializes to -1, setting bucket 0 on the first valid send. Adding time_ms to View. Confirmed product.rs hub can be mutably borrowed from app.harbor without conflicts.\n\nThe client will apply snapshots only for fresh buckets, dropping stale ones. The 500ms latch is a timing fix rather than a behavior change, so no deviation needs to be added.\n\nA one-sentence deviation will be added to the Deviations section. It explains that hub vitals and the timer in a snapshot stay locked to the start of a 500 ms clock bucket, so the host status reports that same value and clients show matching numbers.\n\nCursors still update on every snapshot. PROGRESS.md will be updated after success. Gameplay will not be retuned. The pack command is ready.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-20a8888b-f8ae-4a6f-8940-6dc073932dcb-48","name":"grep","input":{"pattern":"send_snap\\(","glob":"**/*.rs"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2104,"output_tokens":904,"cache_read_input_tokens":121472,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa38-de6f-7dc0-ae0d-e0f717ed75f2","uuid":"ce5a2446-2cea-439c-89c5-18fa102b7e88"}
