{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_738","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The work directory will be served so both the root HTML and the dev harness are accessible.\n\nThe harness URL needs a relative path from `tests/hub/` to `GAME.html`. The correct path is `../../GAME.html`.\n\nThe harness will explicitly set `latency=0` to bypass the 60ms default. Symlinking the game file into the dev folder was considered but rejected in favor of the cleaner relative path approach.\n\nThe check will use the default 60ms latency to match the previous failing scenario. The 500ms buckets create a wide enough equality window.\n\nThe test harness will use `play=14000` and a 30-second limit so the round does not end during the check. The script waits up to 35 seconds for the game to start.\n\nBoth native and Wasm `send_snap` will return `bool`. Wasm early returns will return `false`, and success returns `true`.\n\nA bug was spotted in the Rust `send_snap` logic: `did_snap` and `snap_acc` are zeroed before the body length check.\n\nThe `send_snap` logic is being re-examined. Returning `false` for oversized bodies consumes the rate slot but does not latch, so the next frame waits the 1/15s interval before retrying. Rate-limited early returns remain unchanged. The latch will only trigger on a successful `true` return.\n\nThe host status before the first send uses live vitals. The client's 70.0 value is unlikely to match by accident because cursor movement takes seconds and the latch already exists by then.\n\nWhen send returns true, the latch updates immediately and the status uses new vitals in the same frame. The client has not received this yet, so the test samples later.\n\nA bucket change will be added to the snap even when fallback vitals are used before time is valid. No bucket change occurs if time is negative.\n\nA short comment and a one-line deviation note will be added. The long-running skill will be read in parallel with the code edits. The pack command will use a long block_until_ms because the browser test depends on its result.","signature":""},{"type":"text","text":"The host was reporting live vitals while the client showed the last snapshot, so a single read never matched. I’ll publish one latched value and have both pages report that."},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-955bc81c-4ffe-479e-a681-f6d67edce859-52","name":"search_replace","input":{"file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224015__x42677a/work/Hands of Harbor: Second Opinion-Trauma Center: Second Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-224015/engine/crates/pav_app/src/hub.rs","old_string":"    pub card_lines: Vec<String>,\n    pub present: Vec<u8>,\n}","new_string":"    pub card_lines: Vec<String>,\n    pub present: Vec<u8>,\n    /// `AIHub.time()` in milliseconds. Negative before the round clock starts.\n    pub time_ms: f32,\n    /// Snapshot clock bucket. The client ignores an older one.\n    pub snap_bucket: i32,\n}"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-955bc81c-4ffe-479e-a681-f6d67edce859-53","name":"search_replace","input":{"file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224015__x42677a/work/Hands of Harbor: Second Opinion-Trauma Center: Second Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-224015/engine/crates/pav_app/src/hub.rs","old_string":"    pub hazards: Vec<(u32, u8, f32, f32, bool, u8, f32)>,\n    pub cursors: Vec<(u8, f32, f32, u8, bool, i32)>,\n}","new_string":"    pub hazards: Vec<(u32, u8, f32, f32, bool, u8, f32)>,\n    pub cursors: Vec<(u8, f32, f32, u8, bool, i32)>,\n    pub bucket: i32,\n}"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-955bc81c-4ffe-479e-a681-f6d67edce859-54","name":"search_replace","input":{"file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224015__x42677a/work/Hands of Harbor: Second Opinion-Trauma Center: Second Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-224015/engine/crates/pav_app/src/hub.rs","old_string":"            card_lines: V