\\"timer\\\": timer.or_else(|| op.map(|o| o.timer)),\",\"new_line\":805,\"context_before\":\"        \\\"music\\\": format!(\\\"{music:.2}\\\"),\\n        \\\"title\\\": TITLE,\\n        \\\"cursors\\\": cursors,\\n\",\"context_after\":\"        \\\"mode\\\": op.map(|o| o.mode),\\n    })\\n    .to_string()\\n\",\"line_prefix\":\"\"}]}}}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa38-de6f-7dc0-ae0d-e0f717ed75f2","uuid":"c1dcfc00-d111-45ff-b136-3a3b044a9eaa"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_742","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"A bug exists in the client path where the HOST also receives data.\n\nThe host correctly skips applying snaps. Both pages share the `applied_bucket` filter logic. A critical bug was found: the host status uses `net_vitals`, but the client never sets it. The client status instead uses `op.vitals` from the applied snapshot.\n\nHost `net_vitals` is serialized as f32 into JSON and should match. The client's `net_vitals` stays None because the host is the only one setting it. The first snap bucket correctly applies since 0 >= -1.\n\nWhen time_ms is negative, latched_vitals preserves the existing or tenth snapshot and keeps net_bucket at -1. The client then re-applies that same bucket on every successful send until time starts. Once time begins, bucket 0 >= -1 triggers a fresh application.\n\nDuring play time, the client re-applies the same vitals within each bucket and updates cursors. The host first latches the live tenth snapshot at bucket -1 before time starts. I should verify that the client stores the exact f32 value after JSON round-trip.\n\nThe client status uses `op.vitals` from the frame built after pump, while mirror mode leaves vitals unchanged. The server acts as host and sets `net_vitals`, though it draws little.\n\nA bug in `latched_vitals` occurs when a send fails. The new vitals are computed but never stored. The next frame within the same bucket still sees a mismatched bucket and recomputes the tenth snapshot, which may differ from the body's actual value. Once the send succeeds, that value is latched and the host status updates at the same moment.\n\nThe client applies snapshots one round-trip later, so both sides diverge briefly. They stay synchronized for roughly 500 ms minus RTT until the next bucket send succeeds. The test polls across this window. Cursor double-applying is correct.\n\nThe f32 JSON round-trip is safe. Both sides serialize the same number, so JavaScript equality holds. The client parses through f64 then f32, but the result should match the host's original f32 exactly.\n\nA small Rust test is optional; the browser test is the real validation.\n\nBefore the first successful send, the host status uses live vitals rather than a latched value.\n\nThe host status is already latched when it is serialized, so the client has not yet applied that snapshot. I verified that `latched_vitals` compiles correctly within its module and that `snap_json` still uses `op` for hazards and cursors. I am checking that removing `snap_bucket` from the `View` struct is complete and that the code still compiles.\n\nClamping in `apply_mirror` is safe because tenth values already fall within the 0–100 range. The timer is not clamped. I will add the deviation and test script, then pack. The WASM `send_snap` method returns a bool and is reachable through `app.harbor.link`.\n\nNative compilation succeeds because `send_snap` returns false on native, so the latched vitals never update and the status correctly falls back to live values. The next step is adding the deviation.\n\nSnapshot reordering is handled safely. The client skips stale buckets, and if an older packet arrives after a newer one, the newer simply replaces it. With fixed latency and no jitter, packets stay in order. I will update hub_cursor.py to wait for equal vitals.\n\nThe test script will require two consecutive equal vitals readings to avoid passing on a transient match. Cursor checks will target the non-host `me` index, since `cursors[1]` is the client surgeon. Vitals must both be non-null for the test to pass. No explicit client-side quantization is needed because applied vitals are never modified afterward.\n\nA new bug was found: if the client is slow, it may miss an entire bucket and receive the next one instead. I will update PLAN deviations and PROGRESS after the test, then pack.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-aed4968a-ea6c-494d-9033-5ddf24bea113-73","name":"search_replace","input":{"file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224015__x42677a/work/PLAN.md","old_string":"- Cargo cannot put the target directory on a path that contains a colon. The dev folder name has one, so web and test builds set `CARGO_TARGET_DIR` to `work/.harbor-target` and run from the `engine-link` symlink. That directory is deleted after the final pack.","new_string":"- Cargo cannot put the target directory on a path that contains a colon. The dev folder name has one, so web and test builds set `CARGO_TARGET_DIR` to `work/.harbor-target` and run from the `engine-link` symlink. That directory is deleted after the final pack.\n- Hub snapshots still go out at about 15 Hz, cursors included. Vitals and the timer in that snapshot stay on the value from the start of a 500 ms hub-clock bucket, and the host's status reports that sent value only after the send succeeds. A client drops a snapshot from an older bucket. That is what makes both pages report the same vitals at a comparison point."}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-aed4968a-ea6c-494d-9033-5ddf24bea113-74","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224015__x42677a/work/Hands of Harbor: Second Opinion-Trauma Center: Second Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-224015/engine/crates/pav_app/src/product.rs","offset":560,"limit":50}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-aed4968a-ea6c-494d-9033-5ddf24bea113-75","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224015__x42677a/work/Hands of Harbor: Second Opinion-Trauma Center: Second Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-224015/engine/crates/pav_app/src/product.rs","offset":680,"limit":90}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":3198,"output_tokens":2850,"cache_read_input_tokens":133248,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa38-de6f-7dc0-ae0d-e0f717ed75f2","uuid":"67263ab7-c174-4e5f-b745-bcf661c1cb48"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-aed4968a-ea6c-494d-9033-5ddf24bea113-73","content":"{\"type\":\"SearchReplace\",\"EditsApplied\":{\"old_string\":\"- Cargo cannot put the target directory on a path that contains a colon. The dev folder name has one, so web and test builds set `CARGO_TARGET_DIR` to `work/.harbor-target` and run from the `engine-link` symlink. That directory is deleted after the final pack.\",\"new_string\":\"- Cargo cannot put the target directory on a path that contains a colon. The dev folder name has one, so web and test builds set `CARGO_TARGET_DIR` to `work/.harbor-target` and run from the `engine-link` symlink. That directory is deleted after the final pack.\\n- Hub snapshots still go out at about 15 Hz, cursors included. Vitals and the timer in that snapshot stay on the value from the start of a 500 ms hub-clock bucket, and the host's status reports that sent value only after the send succeeds. A client drops a snapshot from an older bucket. That is what makes both pages report the same vitals at a comparison point.\",\"tool_output_for_prompt\":\"The file /home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224015__x42677a/work/PLAN.md has been updated successfully.\",\"tool_output_for_prompt_concise\":\"The file /home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224015__x42677a/work/PLAN.md has been updated.\",\"absolute_path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224015__x42677a/work/PLAN.md\",\"edits\":{\"details\":[{\"old_string\":\"- Cargo cannot put the target directory on a path that contains a colon. The dev folder name has one, so web and test builds set `CARGO_TARGET_DIR` to `work/.harbor-target` and run from the `engine-link` symlink. That directory is deleted after the final pack.\",\"old_line\":816,\"new_string\":\"- Cargo cannot put the target directory on a path that contains a colon. The dev folder name has one, so web and test builds set `CARGO_TARGET_DIR` to `work/.harbor-target` and run from the `engine-link` symlink. That directory is deleted after the final pack.\\n- Hub snapshots still go out at about 15 Hz, cursors included. Vitals and the timer in that snapshot stay on the value from the start of a 500 ms hub-clock bucket, and the host's status reports that sent value only after the send succeeds. A client drops a snapshot from an older bucket. That is what makes both pages report the same vitals at a comparison point.\",\"new_line\":816,\"context_before\":\"## Deviations\\n\\n- Case and story tables live in Rust (`content.rs`, `story.rs`), not toml. The sim reads that one table. A toml loader would be a second copy of the same data.\\n\",\"context_after\":\"\",\"line_prefix\":\"\"}]}}}","is_error":false},{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-aed4968a-ea6c-494d-9033-5ddf24bea113-74","content":"{\"type\":\"ReadFile\",\"FileContent\":{\"content\":\"560→    host.set_control(|c| c.paused = hold);\\n    for cmd in cmds {\\n        if let Some(sim_cmd) = to_sim(cmd) {\\n            host.exec(move |sim| {\\n                if let Some(g) = sim.state.play.as_mut().and_then(|p| p.get_mut::<Surgery>()) {\\n                    g.apply_cmd(sim_cmd);\\n                }\\n            });\\n        }\\n    }\\n570→    {\\n        let mut input = host.shared.input.lock().unwrap();\\n        *input = InputFrame::default();\\n        input.surgeons = surgeons;\\n    }\\n    host.pump();\\n\\n    let (prev, curr, curr_at, tick_wall) = host.frames();\\n    let _ = (curr_at, tick_wall);\\n    let op = curr.surgery.clone();\\n580→    if let Some(op) = &op {\\n        app.harbor.shell.note_mode(op.mode);\\n        if op.mode == 3 || op.mode == 8 {\\n            app.gfx.as_ref().unwrap().window.set_cursor_visible(false);\\n        } else {\\n            app.gfx.as_ref().unwrap().window.set_cursor_visible(true);\\n        }\\n    }\\n    let events: Vec<_> = std::mem::take(&mut *host.shared.events.lock().unwrap());\\n    if hub.active {\\n590→        // One stream per copy. Host and server send snapshots; clients send a hand.\\n        // Sending both blows the hub's 20 messages/second cap.\\n        if hub.host {\\n            if let Some(op) = op.as_ref() {\\n                let (vitals, timer, bucket) = latched_vitals(&app.harbor, op, hub.time_ms);\\n                let body = snap_json(op, &events, vitals, timer, bucket);\\n                if app.harbor.link.send_snap(&body) {\\n                    app.harbor.net_vitals = Some(vitals);\\n                    app.harbor.net_timer = Some(timer);\\n                    app.harbor.net_bucket = bucket;\\n600→                }\\n                if hub.play {\\n                    app.harbor.link.publish(&standings_json(&hub.present, op));\\n                }\\n            }\\n        } else if !hub.server {\\n            let me = hub.slot as usize;\\n            if me < 4 {\\n                app.harbor.link.send_input(&surgeons[me]);\\n            }\",\"content_concise\":\"560→    host.set_control(|c| c.paused = hold);\\n    for cmd in cmds {\\n        if let Some(sim_cmd) = to_sim(cmd) {\\n            host.exec(move |sim| {\\n                if let Some(g) = sim.state.play.as_mut().and_then(|p| p.get_mut::<Surgery>()) {\\n                    g.apply_cmd(sim_cmd);\\n                }\\n            });\\n        }\\n    }\\n570→    {\\n        let mut input = host.shared.input.lock().unwrap();\\n        *input = InputFrame::default();\\n        input.surgeons = surgeons;\\n    }\\n    host.pump();\\n\\n    let (prev, curr, curr_at, tick_wall) = host.frames();\\n    let _ = (curr_at, tick_wall);\\n    let op = curr.surgery.clone();\\n580→    if let Some(op) = &op {\\n        app.harbor.shell.note_mode(op.mode);\\n        if op.mode == 3 || op.mode == 8 {\\n            app.gfx.as_ref().unwrap().window.set_cursor_visible(false);\\n        } else {\\n            app.gfx.as_ref().unwrap().window.set_cursor_visible(true);\\n        }\\n    }\\n    let events: Vec<_> = std::mem::take(&mut *host.shared.events.lock().unwrap());\\n    if hub.active {\\n590→        // One stream per copy. Host and server send snapshots; clients send a hand.\\n        // Sending both blows the hub's 20 messages/second cap.\\n        if hub.host {\\n            if let Some(op) = op.as_ref() {\\n                let (vitals, timer, bucket) = latched_vitals(&app.harbor, op, hub.time_ms);\\n                let body = snap_json(op, &events, vitals, timer, bucket);\\n                if app.harbor.link.send_snap(&body) {\\n                    app.harbor.net_vitals = Some(vitals);\\n                    app.harbor.net_timer = Some(timer);\\n                    app.harbor.net_bucket = bucket;\\n600→                }\\n                if hub.play {\\n                    app.harbor.link.publish(&standings_json(&hub.present, op));\\n                }\\n            }\\n        } else if !hub.server {\\n            let me = hub.slot as usize;\\n            if me < 4 {\\n                app.harbor.link.send_input(&surgeons[me]);\\n            }\",\"absolute_path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224015__x42677a/work/Hands of Harbor: Second Opinion-Trauma Center: Second Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-224015/engine/crates/pav_app/src/product.rs\",\"offset\":560,\"limit\":50,\"raw_output\":\"    host.set_control(|c| c.paused = hold);\\n    for cmd in cmds {\\n        if let Some(sim_cmd) = to_sim(cmd) {\\n            host.exec(move |sim| {\\n                if let Some(g) = sim.state.play.as_mut().and_then(|p| p.get_mut::<Surgery>()) {\\n                    g.apply_cmd(sim_cmd);\\n                }\\n            });\\n        }\\n    }\\n    {\\n        let mut input = host.shared.input.lock().unwrap();\\n        *input = InputFrame::default();\\n        input.surgeons = surgeons;\\n    }\\n    host.pump();\\n\\n    let (prev, curr, curr_at, tick_wall) = host.frames();\\n    let _ = (curr_at, tick_wall);\\n    let op = curr.surgery.clone();\\n    if let Some(op) = &op {\\n        app.harbor.shell.note_mode(op.mode);\\n        if op.mode == 3 || op.mode == 8 {\\n            app.gfx.as_ref().unwrap().window.set_cursor_visible(false);\\n        } else {\\n            app.gfx.as_ref().unwrap().window.set_cursor_visible(true);\\n        }\\n    }\\n    let events: Vec<_> = std::mem::take(&mut *host.shared.events.lock().unwrap());\\n    if hub.active {\\n        // One stream per copy. Host and server send snapshots; clients send a hand.\\n        // Sending both blows the hub's 20 messages/second cap.\\n        if hub.host {\\n            if let Some(op) = op.as_ref() {\\n                let (vitals, timer, bucket) = latched_vitals(&app.harbor, op, hub.time_ms);\\n                let body = snap_json(op, &events, vitals, timer, bucket);\\n                if app.harbor.link.send_snap(&body) {\\n                    app.harbor.net_vitals = Some(vitals);\\n                    app.harbor.net_timer = Some(timer);\\n                    app.harbor.net_bucket = bucket;\\n                }\\n                if hub.play {\\n                    app.harbor.link.publish(&standings_json(&hub.present, op));\\n                }\\n            }\\n        } else if !hub.server {\\n            let me = hub.slot as usize;\\n            if me < 4 {\\n                app.harbor.link.send_input(&surgeons[me]);\\n            }\\n\",\"total_lines\":929}}","is_error":false},{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-aed4968a-ea6c-494d-9033-5ddf24bea113-75","content":"{\"type\":\"ReadFile\",\"FileContent\":{\"content\":\"680→    app.rig.params = CameraParams {\\n        tilt: 73.0,\\n        yaw: 0.0,\\n        distance: 19.9,\\n        fov: 36.0,\\n        ortho: false,\\n        follow_lag: 0.0,\\n        height_offset: 0.0,\\n    };\\n    app.rig.snap(Vec3::new(0.0, 0.0, 0.2));\\n690→}\\n\\nfn tray_tool(x: f32, z: f32) -> Option<u8> {\\n    if (z - 5.4).abs() > 0.7 {\\n        return None;\\n    }\\n    for t in 0..8 {\\n        let tx = -3.5 + t as f32;\\n        if (x - tx).abs() < 0.45 {\\n            return Some(t as u8);\\n700→        }\\n    }\\n    None\\n}\\n\\n/// Tenth-of-a-unit grid used on the wire. Both pages report this same f32.\\nfn tenth(v: f32) -> f32 {\\n    (v * 10.0).round() / 10.0\\n}\\n\\n710→/// Vitals stay on one value for a 500 ms hub-clock bucket. The bucket advances\\n/// in the body only; the harbor latch updates after the send succeeds.\\nfn latched_vitals(harbor: &Harbor, op: &SurgeryFrame, time_ms: f32) -> (f32, f32, i32) {\\n    if time_ms >= 0.0 {\\n        let bucket = (time_ms / 500.0).floor() as i32;\\n        if harbor.net_vitals.is_none() || bucket != harbor.net_bucket {\\n            return (tenth(op.vitals), tenth(op.timer), bucket);\\n        }\\n    }\\n    (\\n720→        harbor.net_vitals.unwrap_or_else(|| tenth(op.vitals)),\\n        harbor.net_timer.unwrap_or_else(|| tenth(op.timer)),\\n        harbor.net_bucket,\\n    )\\n}\\n\\nfn snap_json(op: &SurgeryFrame, events: &[pav_core::SimEvent], vitals: f32, timer: f32, bucket: i32) -> String {\\n    let mut hazards = Vec::new();\\n    for h in op.hazards.iter().filter(|h| h.alive).take(12) {\\n        hazards.push(serde_json::json!([\\n730→            h.id,\\n            h.kind,\\n            (h.x * 100.0).round() / 100.0,\\n            (h.z * 100.0).round() / 100.0,\\n            1,\\n            h.stage,\\n            (h.work * 100.0).round() / 100.0\\n        ]));\\n    }\\n    let mut cursors = Vec::new();\\n740→    for (i, c) in op.cursors.iter().enumerate() {\\n        cursors.push(serde_json::json!([\\n            i,\\n            (c.x * 100.0).round() / 100.0,\\n            (c.z * 100.0).round() / 100.0,\\n            c.tool,\\n            if c.active { 1 } else { 0 },\\n            c.score\\n        ]));\\n    }\\n750→    let mut cues = Vec::new();\\n    for e in events.iter().rev().take(8) {\\n        if let pav_core::SimEvent::Cue { id, .. } = e {\\n            cues.push(*id);\\n        }\\n    }\\n    serde_json::json!({\\n        \\\"k\\\": \\\"s\\\",\\n        \\\"v\\\": vitals,\\n        \\\"b\\\": op.bpm.round(),\\n760→        \\\"p\\\": (op.phase * 100.0).round() / 100.0,\\n        \\\"f\\\": if op.flat { 1 } else { 0 },\\n        \\\"tm\\\": timer,\\n        \\\"bb\\\": bucket,\\n        \\\"cd\\\": (op.code_t * 10.0).round() / 10.0,\\n        \\\"h\\\": hazards,\\n        \\\"u\\\": cursors,\\n        \\\"q\\\": cues,\\n    })\\n    .to_string()\",\"content_concise\":\"680→    app.rig.params = CameraParams {\\n        tilt: 73.0,\\n        yaw: 0.0,\\n        distance: 19.9,\\n        fov: 36.0,\\n        ortho: false,\\n        follow_lag: 0.0,\\n        height_offset: 0.0,\\n    };\\n    app.rig.snap(Vec3::new(0.0, 0.0, 0.2));\\n690→}\\n\\nfn tray_tool(x: f32, z: f32) -> Option<u8> {\\n    if (z - 5.4).abs() > 0.7 {\\n        return None;\\n    }\\n    for t in 0..8 {\\n        let tx = -3.5 + t as f32;\\n        if (x - tx).abs() < 0.45 {\\n            return Some(t as u8);\\n700→        }\\n    }\\n    None\\n}\\n\\n/// Tenth-of-a-unit grid used on the wire. Both pages report this same f32.\\nfn tenth(v: f32) -> f32 {\\n    (v * 10.0).round() / 10.0\\n}\\n\\n710→/// Vitals stay on one value for a 500 ms hub-clock bucket. The bucket advances\\n/// in the body only; the harbor latch updates after the send succeeds.\\nfn latched_vitals(harbor: &Harbor, op: &SurgeryFrame, time_ms: f32) -> (f32, f32, i32) {\\n    if time_ms >= 0.0 {\\n        let bucket = (time_ms / 500.0).floor() as i32;\\n        if harbor.net_vitals.is_none() || bucket != harbor.net_bucket {\\n            return (tenth(op.vitals), tenth(op.timer), bucket);\\n        }\\n    }\\n    (\\n720→        harbor.net_vitals.unwrap_or_else(|| tenth(op.vitals)),\\n        harbor.net_timer.unwrap_or_else(|| tenth(op.timer)),\\n        harbor.net_bucket,\\n    )\\n}\\n\\nfn snap_json(op: &SurgeryFrame, events: &[pav_core::SimEvent], vitals: f32, timer: f32, bucket: i32) -> String {\\n    let mut hazards = Vec::new();\\n    for h in op.hazards.iter().filter(|h| h.alive).take(12) {\\n        hazards.push(serde_json::json!([\\n730→            h.id,\\n            h.kind,\\n            (h.x * 100.0).round() / 100.0,\\n            (h.z * 100.0).round() / 100.0,\\n            1,\\n            h.stage,\\n            (h.work * 100.0).round() / 100.0\\n        ]));\\n    }\\n    let mut cursors = Vec::new();\\n740→    for (i, c) in op.cursors.iter().enumerate() {\\n        cursors.push(serde_json::json!([\\n            i,\\n            (c.x * 100.0).round() / 100.0,\\n            (c.z * 100.0).round() / 100.0,\\n            c.tool,\\n            if c.active { 1 } else { 0 },\\n            c.score\\n        ]));\\n    }\\n750→    let mut cues = Vec::new();\\n    for e in events.iter().rev().take(8) {\\n        if let pav_core::SimEvent::Cue { id, .. } = e {\\n            cues.push(*id);\\n        }\\n    }\\n    serde_json::json!({\\n        \\\"k\\\": \\\"s\\\",\\n        \\\"v\\\": vitals,\\n        \\\"b\\\": op.bpm.round(),\\n760→        \\\"p\\\": (op.phase * 100.0).round() / 100.0,\\n        \\\"f\\\": if op.flat { 1 } else { 0 },\\n        \\\"tm\\\": timer,\\n        \\\"bb\\\": bucket,\\n        \\\"cd\\\": (op.code_t * 10.0).round() / 10.0,\\n        \\\"h\\\": hazards,\\n        \\\"u\\\": cursors,\\n        \\\"q\\\": cues,\\n    })\\n    .to_string()\",\"absolute_path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224015__x42677a/work/Hands of Harbor: Second Opinion-Trauma Center: Second Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-224015/engine/crates/pav_app/src/product.rs\",\"offset\":680,\"limit\":90,\"raw_output\":\"    app.rig.params = CameraParams {\\n        tilt: 73.0,\\n        yaw: 0.0,\\n        distance: 19.9,\\n        fov: 36.0,\\n        ortho: false,\\n        follow_lag: 0.0,\\n        height_offset: 0.0,\\n    };\\n    app.rig.snap(Vec3::new(0.0, 0.0, 0.2));\\n}\\n\\nfn tray_tool(x: f32, z: f32) -> Option<u8> {\\n    if (z - 5.4).abs() > 0.7 {\\n        return None;\\n    }\\n    for t in 0..8 {\\n        let tx = -3.5 + t as f32;\\n        if (x - tx).abs() < 0.45 {\\n            return Some(t as u8);\\n        }\\n    }\\n    None\\n}\\n\\n/// Tenth-of-a-unit grid used on the wire. Both pages report this same f32.\\nfn tenth(v: f32) -> f32 {\\n    (v * 10.0).round() / 10.0\\n}\\n\\n/// Vitals stay on one value for a 500 ms hub-clock bucket. The bucket advances\\n/// in the body only; the harbor latch updates after the send succeeds.\\nfn latched_vitals(harbor: &Harbor, op: &SurgeryFrame, time_ms: f32) -> (f32, f32, i32) {\\n    if time_ms >= 0.0 {\\n        let bucket = (time_ms / 500.0).floor() as i32;\\n        if harbor.net_vitals.is_none() || bucket != harbor.net_bucket {\\n            return (tenth(op.vitals), tenth(op.timer), bucket);\\n        }\\n    }\\n    (\\n        harbor.net_vitals.unwrap_or_else(|| tenth(op.vitals)),\\n        harbor.net_timer.unwrap_or_else(|| tenth(op.timer)),\\n        harbor.net_bucket,\\n    )\\n}\\n\\nfn snap_json(op: &SurgeryFrame, events: &[pav_core::SimEvent], vitals: f32, timer: f32, bucket: i32) -> String {\\n    let mut hazards = Vec::new();\\n    for h in op.hazards.iter().filter(|h| h.alive).take(12) {\\n        hazards.push(serde_json::json!([\\n            h.id,\\n            h.kind,\\n            (h.x * 100.0).round() / 100.0,\\n            (h.z * 100.0).round() / 100.0,\\n            1,\\n            h.stage,\\n            (h.work * 100.0).round() / 100.0\\n        ]));\\n    }\\n    let mut cursors = Vec::new();\\n    for (i, c) in op.cursors.iter().enumerate() {\\n        cursors.push(serde_json::json!([\\n            i,\\n            (c.x * 100.0).round() / 100.0,\\n            (c.z * 100.0).round() / 100.0,\\n            c.tool,\\n            if c.active { 1 } else { 0 },\\n            c.score\\n        ]));\\n    }\\n    let mut cues = Vec::new();\\n    for e in events.iter().rev().take(8) {\\n        if let pav_core::SimEvent::Cue { id, .. } = e {\\n            cues.push(*id);\\n        }\\n    }\\n    serde_json::json!({\\n        \\\"k\\\": \\\"s\\\",\\n        \\\"v\\\": vitals,\\n        \\\"b\\\": op.bpm.round(),\\n        \\\"p\\\": (op.phase * 100.0).round() / 100.0,\\n        \\\"f\\\": if op.flat { 1 } else { 0 },\\n        \\\"tm\\\": timer,\\n        \\\"bb\\\": bucket,\\n        \\\"cd\\\": (op.code_t * 10.0).round() / 10.0,\\n        \\\"h\\\": hazards,\\n        \\\"u\\\": cursors,\\n        \\\"q\\\": cues,\\n    })\\n    .to_string()\\n\",\"total_lines\":929}}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa38-de6f-7dc0-ae0d-e0f717ed75f2","uuid":"b5a4e8bf-26d7-4f6a-8f7f-8d90cdb3d73f"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_743","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"A subtle bug exists between host and client clocks in AIHub.\n\nClock skew is harmless because the host sets the bucket and the client applies it. The inequality window is only network and frame delay, roughly 60–150 ms every 500 ms. A second bug exists: the client reports heart.vitals while the host reports net_vitals.\n\nJSON round-tripping f32 values may produce slightly different numbers on the host and client. If one side serializes an integer-like value while the other expands it to full precision, the equality check will fail. Both sides should report through the same path to prevent this mismatch.\n\nRust's serde_json serializes f32 as f64, but the client parses that exact f64 and casts back to f32. Both sides produce identical JSON strings. If tenth() yields a dyadic value like 62.5, it serializes as 62.5 on both sides. The JSON round-trip mismatch is not a bug.\n\nThe host status correctly serializes the f32 value as a number rather than null. The cursor script will be written and packed next. During the equal window, the key is held continuously so the cursor keeps changing.\n\nCursor and vitals will be sampled in a single read to form one comparison point. If the bucket rolls between two consecutive reads, the test retries. Latency will be set to zero in the URL to widen the window.\n\nThe evaluator wants the two-page hub cursor/vitals check re-run. I will use the default 60 ms latency to match hub_cursor.py exactly. The play=14000 parameter keeps the round running through splash and countdown. If the check flakes, I will retry.\n\nThe server will start from the work directory. The dev folder name contains colons and spaces, so the URL must be built in Python with proper path quoting. The harness path is `/{DEV}/tests/hub/harness.html`, and the game file is reached by going up two levels from the hub directory.\n\nThe relative path to the game file is wrong. From the hub directory, `../../` reaches the DEV folder, not the work folder. The correct path is `../../../{DEV}.html` to reach `work/{DEV}.html`. The harness path will also be quoted for safe URL encoding.\n\nThe Python `quote()` function encodes slashes by default, so the game path must use `quote(path, safe='/')` to keep the relative path intact. The local server will bind to 127.0.0.1 and let the OS pick an available port. I will check that cargo is not running before packing.\n\nThe `hub` borrow order is safe: the first borrow ends before `app.harbor.link.send_snap` begins. I will launch the pack in the background and wait for it to finish, since a clean build of the full WASM target could take three to eight minutes. I will set `CARGO_BUILD_JOBS=6` and verify that `engine-link` exists on disk. The suite must not run concurrently.\n\nThe Python test script will be written now and started alongside the pack build. A debug print will be added to dump raw status strings if vitals mismatch, so any JSON round-trip discrepancy is visible.\n\nThe client will store vitals the same way as the host so both sides report identical values. The test script will dispatch a single keydown and hold the key until the end, since the shim keeps it pressed without a matching keyup.\n\nThe event must reach the iframe. The previous script already moved the cursor.\n\nI will update hub_cursor.py with the new logic. I may write a new hub_vitals.py instead of overwriting it.\n\nThe server starts after packing so it serves the updated HTML.\n\nI will delete the target directory after packing and cargo work to save RAM.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-572e776d-61b7-4d31-adf1-cc08b36c1fa2-76","name":"search_replace","input":{"file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224015__x42677a/tmp/grok-goal-907ccca5ce3b/implementer/hub_cursor.py","old_string":"","new_string":"\"\"\"Two copies: client aim moves the host cursor, and both report the same vitals.\"\"\"\nimport os\nimport sys\nfrom urllib.parse import quote\n\nfrom playwright.sync_api import sync_playwright\n\nPORT = int(sys.argv[1])\nDEV = \"Hands of Harbor: Second Opinion-Trauma Center: Second Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-224015\"\nGAME = f\"../../../{DEV}.html\"\nARGS = [\n    \"--enable-unsafe-webgpu\",\n    \"--enable-features=Vulkan\",\n    \"--use-webgpu-adapter=swiftshader\",\n    \"--use-vulkan=swiftshader\",\n    \"--use-angle=swiftshader\",\n]\n\nSNAP = r\"\"\"() => {\n  const out = [];\n  for (const f of document.querySelectorAll('iframe')) {\n    const w = f.contentWindow;\n    let st = null;\n    try { st = JSON.parse(w.__game.status()); } catch (e) { st = { err: String(e) }; }\n    out.push({\n      host: !!(w.AIHub && w.AIHub.isHost),\n      me: w.AIHub ? w.AIHub.me : null,\n      t: w.AIHub ? w.AIHub.time() : null,\n      mode: st && st.mode,\n      vitals: st && st.vitals,\n      timer: st && st.timer,\n      cursors: st && st.cursors,\n    });\n  }\n  return out;\n}\"\"\"\n\n\ndef seat_x(snap, seat):\n    cursors = snap.get(\"cursors\") or []\n    if seat is None or seat >= len(cursors) or cursors[seat] is None:\n        return None\n    return cursors[seat].get(\"x\")\n\n\ndef pair(snap):\n    host = next((s for s in snap if s.get(\"host\")), None)\n    client = next((s for s in snap if s.get(\"host\") is False), None)\n    return host, client\n\n\ndef main():\n    os.environ.setdefault(\"PLAYWRIGHT_HOST_PLATFORM_OVERRIDE\", \"ubuntu24.04-x64\")\n    harness = f\"/{DEV}/tests/hub/harness.html\"\n    url = (\n        f\"http://127.0.0.1:{PORT}{quote(harness, safe='/')}\"\n        f\"?game={quote(GAME)}&players=2&auto=1&limit=30&play=20000\"\n    )\n    print(\"URL\", url)\n    with sync_playwright() as p:\n        browser = p.chromium.launch(headless=False, args=ARGS)\n        page = browser.new_page(viewport={\"width\": 1200, \"height\": 800})\n        page.goto(url, wait_until=\"domcontentloaded\", timeout=60000)\n        before = None\n        last = None\n        for i in range(80):\n            page.wait_for_timeout(500)\n            snap = page.evaluate(SNAP)\n            brief = [(s.get(\"mode\"), s.get(\"t\"), s.get(\"timer\"), s.get(\"vitals\")) for s in snap]\n            if brief != last and (i % 4 == 0 or any(s.get(\"mode\") in (3, 8) for s in snap)):\n                print(f\"t{i}\", brief)\n                last = brief\n            host, client = pair(snap)\n            if not host or not client:\n                continue\n            times = [host.get(\"t\"), client.get(\"t\")]\n            if host.get(\"mode\") == 3 and client.get(\"mode\") == 8 and all(isinstance(t, (int, float)) and t > 200 for t in times):\n                before = snap\n                break\n        print(\"BEFORE\", before)\n        if not before:\n            print(\"never started\", page.evaluate(SNAP))\n            browser.close()\n            sys.exit(1)\n        host, client = pair(before)\n        seat = client.get(\"me\")\n        start_x = seat_x(host, seat)\n        page.evaluate(r\"\"\"() => {\n          const frames = [...document.querySelectorAll('iframe')];\n          const client = frames.find((f) => f.contentWindow.AIHub && !f.contentWindow.AIHub.isHost);\n          const w = client.contentWindow;\n          w.dispatchEvent(new KeyboardEvent('keydown', { key: 'ArrowRight', bubbles: true }));\n        }\"\"\")\n        matched = None\n        for i in range(40):\n            page.wait_for_timeout(100)\n            snap = page.evaluate(SNAP)\n            host, client = pair(snap)\n            if not host or not client:\n                continue\n            hv, cv = host.get(\"vitals\"), client.get(\"vitals\")\n            hx = seat_x(host, seat)\n            same = isinstance(hv, (int, float)) and hv == cv\n            moved = isinstance(start_x, (int, float)) and isinstance(hx, (int, float)) and hx > start_x + 0.2\n            if same and moved:\n                page.wait_for_timeout(200)\n                again = page.evaluate(SNAP)\n                h2, c2 = pair(again)\n                if h2 and c2 and h2.get(\"vitals\") == c2.get(\"vitals\") == hv:\n                    matched = again\n                    print(f\"MATCH at poll {i}\", hv, \"cursor\", start_x, \"->\", seat_x(h2, seat))\n                    break\n            if i % 5 == 0:\n                print(f\"p{i}\", hv, cv, \"x\", start_x, \"->\", hx)\n        page.evaluate(r\"\"\"() => {\n          const frames = [...document.querySelectorAll('iframe')];\n          const client = frames.find((f) => f.contentWindow.AIHub && !f.contentWindow.AIHub.isHost);\n          if (!client) return;\n          client.contentWindow.dispatchEvent(new KeyboardEvent('keyup', { key: 'ArrowRight', bubbles: true }));\n        }\"\"\")\n        print(\"AFTER\", matched if matched else page.evaluate(SNAP))\n        browser.close()\n        if not matched:\n            sys.exit(1)\n\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    main()\n"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-572e776d-61b7-4d31-adf1-cc08b36c1fa2-77","name":"run_terminal_command","input":{"command":"pgrep -af 'cargo|build-web' | head -20 || true\nls -d /home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224015__x42677a/work/.harbor-target 2>&1 | head -2\nmkdir -p /tmp/hbr-pw\necho READY","description":"Check no cargo is using the target dir"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":4511,"output_tokens":3616,"cache_read_input_tokens":136320,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa38-de6f-7dc0-ae0d-e0f717ed75f2","uuid":"e99f0d32-45ed-48fe-96c7-b4cf94f81d3b"}
