{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_760","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Writing the runner and starting the server.\n\nRunning four scenarios sequentially in one browser process. Verifying the HTML pack changed by checking file sizes. Writing fresh reports to overwrite old logs: hub-p4.txt, hub-leave.txt, hub-server.txt, hub-one.txt, and hub.txt.\n\nAll four scenarios will run together with a long timeout. Each failure will be reported individually. Memory issues will halt the run. The harness will verify the game HTML size matches the new pack. Starting to write hub_four.py.\n\nDefining the four scenario parameters in hub_four.py. Each scenario has its own query string with specific player counts and network settings.\n\nThe runner script launches a visible Chromium browser, loads the harness URL with the game and scenario parameters, waits up to three minutes for the completion flag to appear in the page body, and then extracts the final report data.\n\nThe runner script now extracts the browser log and closes the page after each scenario. The main loop iterates through all four queries, prints completion status, and checks whether the report shows a pass.\n\nThe runner now prints individual failing checks and traffic-related results. It writes each scenario's output to a dedicated file and records failures.\n\nThe runner now exits with the total failure count. Traffic statistics are preserved in check details even when a test passes, so the log will include complete traffic numbers. The full checks list will be written to hub.txt for an accurate summary.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-6dab08f8-aa2e-4f8b-b2f9-ee5d384dcf31-99","name":"search_replace","input":{"file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224015__x42677a/tmp/grok-goal-907ccca5ce3b/implementer/hub_four.py","old_string":"","new_string":"\"\"\"Four hub harness queries against the packed page. One browser at a time.\"\"\"\nimport json\nimport os\nimport sys\nfrom pathlib import Path\nfrom urllib.parse import quote\n\nfrom playwright.sync_api import sync_playwright\n\nPORT = int(sys.argv[1])\nDEV = \"Hands of Harbor: Second Opinion-Trauma Center: Second Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-224015\"\nGAME = f\"../../../{DEV}.html\"\nHARNESS = f\"/{DEV}/tests/hub/harness.html\"\nOUT = Path(__file__).resolve().parent\nARGS = [\n    \"--enable-unsafe-webgpu\",\n    \"--enable-features=Vulkan\",\n    \"--use-webgpu-adapter=swiftshader\",\n    \"--use-vulkan=swiftshader\",\n    \"--use-angle=swiftshader\",\n]\nQUERIES = [\n    (\"p4\", \"players=4&latency=150&jitter=50&loss=5&auto=1&limit=20\"),\n    (\"leave\", \"players=4&latency=150&jitter=50&loss=5&scenario=host-leave&auto=1&limit=20\"),\n    (\"server\", \"players=2&scenario=server&auto=1&limit=20\"),\n    (\"one\", \"players=1&auto=1&limit=20\"),\n]\n\n\ndef run_one(playwright, name, query):\n    url = f\"http://127.0.0.1:{PORT}{quote(HARNESS, safe='/')}?game={quote(GAME)}&{query}\"\n    print(\"URL\", url, flush=True)\n    browser = playwright.chromium.launch(headless=False, args=ARGS)\n    page = browser.new_page(viewport={\"width\": 1100, \"height\": 700})\n    page.goto(url, wait_until=\"domcontentloaded\", timeout=60000)\n    try:\n        page.wait_for_function(\"document.body.dataset.complete === 'true'\", timeout=180000)\n    except Exception as exc:\n        print(name, \"WAIT\", exc, flush=True)\n    complete = page.evaluate(\"() => document.body.dataset.complete || ''\")\n    report = page.evaluate(\"() => window.__hubCheck || null\")\n    log = page.locator(\"#log\").inner_text()\n    browser.close()\n    return complete, report, log\n\n\ndef main():\n    os.environ.setdefault(\"PLAYWRIGHT_HOST_PLATFORM_OVERRIDE\", \"ubuntu24.04-x64\")\n    failed = 0\n    with sync_playwright() as playwright:\n        for name, query in QUERIES:\n            print(\"RUN\", name, query, flush=True)\n            complete, report, log = run_one(playwright, name, query)\n            passed = complete == \"true\" and bool(report) and report.get(\"pass\") is True\n            print(name, \"complete\", complete, \"pass\", None if not report else report.get(\"pass\"), flush=True)\n            lines = [f\"query {query}\", f\"dataset.complete {complete}\", f\"__hubCheck.pass {None if not report else report.get('pass')}\"]\n            if report:\n                for check in report.get(\"checks\") or []:\n                    mark = \"PASS\" if check.get(\"pass\") else \"FAIL\"\n                    lines.append(f\"  {mark} {check.get('name')} {check.get('detail') or ''}\".rstrip())\n                    if not check.get(\"pass\"):\n                        print(\" FAIL\", check.get(\"name\"), check.get(\"detail\"), flush=True)\n            lines.append(\"\")\n            lines.append(log)\n            (OUT / f\"hub-{name}.txt\").write_text(\"\\n\".join(lines) + \"\\n\")\n            print(name, \"PASS\" if passed else \"FAIL\", flush=True)\n            if not passed:\n                failed += 1\n    print(f\"HUB {failed} failed\", flush=True)\n    return failed\n\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    sys.exit(main())\n"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-6dab08f8-aa2e-4f8b-b2f9-ee5d384dcf31-100","name":"run_terminal_command","input":{"command":"ss -ltnp 2>/dev/null | awk '/41171|python3 -u -m http.server/ {print}' || netstat -ltnp 2>/dev/null | awk '/41171/ {print}'\ncd /home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224015__x42677a/work\npython3 -u -m http.server 0 --bind 127.0.0.1","description":"Serve packed game on an OS-picked port","block_until_ms":0}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":882,"output_tokens":2232,"cache_read_input_tokens":163840,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa38-de6f-7dc0-ae0d-e0f717ed75f2","uuid":"61511b60-c7fb-48a0-9f79-9da5b3cad0df"}
