{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_780","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The screenshots look substantially painted.\n\nBalance sheet analysis shows skill 1.0 always wins but scores far above par, giving an S rank. Skill 0.7 wins almost everything except case 5. Skill 0.4 wins most cases including 3 and 7, and only case 5 loses. The plan targets skill 1.0 at S or above, 0.7 as the main winner, 0.4 in later cases, and 0.0 losing.\n\nSkill 0.4 wins cases 3, 4, 6, and 7. This misses the PLAN.md section 11.2 balance target. Balance targets are not gating criteria. The acceptance criteria only require cases 0–7 and Code Blue to lose to an idle or random-tool player at skill 1.0.\n\nCase 0 finishes in 2.3 seconds, which is extremely fast. The bot may be skipping content or the simulation timestep is too large. This could undermine the feature-complete demo goal.\n\nCase 3 takes 18.5 seconds and case 5 takes 29.6 seconds, while Code Blue runs exactly 240 seconds. Case 0 finishing in 2.3 seconds suggests it may contain almost no content or the bot is clearing instantly. The next step is to inspect the case definitions and bot logic to verify coverage. The rank calculation is correct: a score of 3624 against a par of 900 yields an ENCORE rank.\n\nI will read surgery mod.rs to inspect the step loop, bot logic, cases, and tools. I also need to verify HTML about-data, banned names in the story, session.js, hub tags, local 1-4, engine/target deletion, title RNG recording, and whether COOL/XS is banned. Criterion 1 forbids using the source world's proper names, but the test only bans Hope Hospital, Caduceus, Stiles, GUILT, and Healing Touch.","signature":""},{"type":"text","text":"Screenshots show a painted title and field. Next I’ll check whether the bot, cases, and coverage actually exercise the sim rather than skip it."},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-75e63601-45d5-47e9-8909-dcf19f3e1bb3-27","name":"grep","in