 self.heart.phase = 0.0;\"},{\"line_number\":699,\"content\":\"    pub(crate) fn activate_gift(&mut self, bit: u8) {\"},{\"line_number\":709,\"content\":\"        if self.gifts_used & bit == 0 {\"},{\"line_number\":710,\"content\":\"            self.coverage.gifts[idx] = self.coverage.gifts[idx].saturating_add(1);\"},{\"line_number\":712,\"content\":\"        self.gifts_used |= bit;\"},{\"line_number\":717,\"content\":\"                self.hush_beats = ((6.0 * self.tune.gift_duration).round() as u8).max(1);\"},{\"line_number\":721,\"content\":\"                self.echo_left = self.tune.echo_duration * self.tune.gift_duration;\"},{\"line_number\":726,\"content\":\"                self.duet_left = 8.0 * self.tune.gift_duration;\"},{\"line_number\":764,\"content\":\"                    self.gifts_unlocked |= content::G_HUSH | content::G_ECHO | content::G_DUET;\"},{\"line_number\":784,\"content\":\"                    self.phase_i = self.phase_i.saturating_add(1);\"},{\"line_number\":785,\"content\":\"                    self.phase_ready = false;\"},{\"line_number\":825,\"content\":\"                self.mode = if self.mode == M_ATTRACT { M_ATTRACT } else { M_OP };\"},{\"line_number\":826,\"content\":\"                self.phase_ready = false;\"},{\"line_number\":874,\"content\":\"        fr.phase = self.heart.phase;\"},{\"line_number\":877,\"content\":\"            self.heart.ghost_on_beat(self.tune.beat_window_ms)\"},{\"line_number\":879,\"content\":\"            self.heart.on_beat(self.tune.beat_window_ms)\"},{\"line_number\":895,\"content\":\"        fr.strain = self.strain_phase;\"},{\"line_number\":896,\"content\":\"        fr.gift_hush = if self.hush_beats > 0 { self.hush_beats as f32 } else { 0.0 };\"},{\"line_number\":897,\"content\":\"        fr.gift_echo = self.echo_left;\"},{\"line_number\":898,\"content\":\"        fr.gift_duet = self.duet_left;\"},{\"line_number\":899,\"content\":\"        fr.gifts_unlocked = self.gifts_unlocked;\"},{\"line_number\":905,\"content\":\"        if self.strain_phase != 255 {\"},{\"line_number\":906,\"content\":\"            fr.banner = STRAIN_PHASES.get(self.strain_phase as usize).copied().unwrap_or(\\\"\\\").to_string();\"},{\"line_number\":965,\"content\":\"        fr.coverage_strains = self.coverage.strains;\"},{\"line_number\":966,\"content\":\"        fr.coverage_gifts = self.coverage.gifts;\"},{\"line_number\":979,\"content\":\"            M_OP => \\\"op\\\",\"},{\"line_number\":1062,\"content\":\"            \\\"phase\\\": self.phase_i,\"},{\"line_number\":1063,\"content\":\"            \\\"strain\\\": self.strain_phase,\"},{\"line_number\":1071,\"content\":\"            \\\"gifts\\\": self.gifts_unlocked,\"},{\"line_number\":1072,\"content\":\"            \\\"gifts_used\\\": self.gifts_used,\"},{\"line_number\":1075,\"content\":\"            \\\"strains\\\": self.coverage.strains,\"},{\"line_number\":1076,\"content\":\"            \\\"gift_counts\\\": self.coverage.gifts,\"}]}]}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa38-de6f-7dc0-ae0d-e0f717ed75f2","uuid":"ba4bbd3c-6ae0-4166-b3a2-5be984f053ee"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_783","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Case names don't match PLAN.md.\n\nCase 0 lists laceration, pool, incision, and inflam. PLAN.md lists Gel, Forceps, Suction, Suture, and Dressing. Forceps and dressing are missing from case 0 but appear later.\n\nThe acceptance criterion confirms the required case names. Case 0 is The First Movement, Case 3 is Introit, and Case 4 is Lacrimosa.\n\nCase 5 is Dies Irae. PLAN.md assigns Echo and bone to case 5, but the acceptance criterion only requires four strains across cases 0–7 without specific numbering. PLAN.md is the authoritative design document. Divergences from the implementation approach are not grounds for refutation.\n\nPLAN.md is the immutable contract. STAGE.md explicitly names it as the build target, and verifier instructions treat named artifacts as unchangeable. This makes PLAN.md the authoritative source for case names and structure.\n\nPLAN.md is the immutable contract. The implementation maps Dies Irae to Case 5, but PLAN.md assigns it to Case 6. PLAN.md explicitly forbids cutting Case 3 or Case 7. This structural mismatch could constitute a forbidden cut.\n\nCase 6 is \"Margin of the Map\" with tumor, laceration, pool, burn, and bleeder. It does not contain the Cryoprobe mechanic that PLAN.md assigns to Case 6.\n\nEcho unlocks during Lacrimosa in Case 4. PLAN.md assigns Echo to Pet's gift in Case 5.\n\nBone reassembly appears in Case 2 rather than Case 5.\n\nCryoprobe mechanics are present via embers in Case 5. The tools themselves exist throughout the campaign.\n\nAll 18 strain phases are accounted for across cases 3, 4, 5, and 7. The acceptance criteria explicitly require the Hush, Echo, and Duet gifts. It is unclear whether the tremor mechanic, partner presence in case 7, or Code Blue waves are actually implemented.\n\nThe verifier instructions explicitly forbid refuting for missing edge cases or extensions the plan did not require. PLAN.md is the immutable contract, and its non-goals explicitly exclude a campaign longer than cases 0–7 plus Code Blue. This means the implementation is bound by the specific case structure and mechanics defined in PLAN.md, and any divergence from that design document could constitute a forbidden cut.\n\nThe verifier instructions allow shorter campaigns if every tool, gift, screen, Case 3, and Case 7 remain intact. This means the case numbering mismatch may not be a forbidden cut. The focus should shift to finding actual bugs that break gameplay rather than missing fidelity.\n\nops.rs will be inspected for logic bugs in tool gestures, defibrillation, and Hush. Coverage might increment before an action truly completes. The case 5 versus case 6 swap is being weighed as a core intent deviation.\n\nThe acceptance criterion's parenthetical wording likely means case 0 is titled The First Movement and the four listed strains belong to it, rather than requiring every PLAN case name to match exactly. The goal plan was written as the acceptance contract after research.\n\nA direct contradiction exists between the OBJECTIVE and the verifier instructions. The OBJECTIVE demands completing every detail in PLAN.md that can be done on this computer, while the verifier forbids refuting for missing edge cases or extensions the plan did not require. This tension suggests the goal plan's acceptance criteria were deliberately written to operationalize the broad OBJECTIVE.\n\nThe verifier instructions explicitly direct me to judge each acceptance criterion as met or unmet, but to refute any objective requirement the plan or implementation omits. I should verify whether the implementation omits core PLAN.md requirements that the goal plan captured, or if the goal plan narrowed away any essential elements. The goal plan criteria are comprehensive and align with PLAN.md's testing section.\n\nI will inspect ops.rs for concrete bugs in tool handling and the surgery step. I will also review HTML, session.js, and the hub. I am checking specific PLAN requirements against the acceptance criteria: eight-way tool selection, gestures and ratings for each tool, rising BPM as vitals fall, timed defibrillation, chains and ranks, gifts, bot wins versus idle losses, campaign coverage, retry checkpoints, and rewind or replay.\n\nI am hunting for bugs in screens, attract, touch, dev, music 0.10, hub, file:// launch, exit interview, banned names, and TODOs.\n\nCase 2 contains a scripted code phase with no spawns. I need to verify whether the player must defibrillate during that phase.\n\nI am also auditing campaign coverage against all 19 hazard types. I have mapped which cases spawn each kind. I still need to confirm every type appears at least once.\n\nK_HEAT may be a heat ring rather than a spawned hazard. If it never increments, campaign coverage would fail. The test passed, so the increment path must exist. All eleven tools are confirmed present in the campaign.\n\nGift coverage increments in activate_gift. The bot triggers gifts when the meter reaches 100 and skill is at least 0.55. The test suite only reports \"14 passed, 0 failed\" with no details. I should verify these results by running the tests directly, since the instructions permit cheap re-runs.\n\nThe full surgery suite should take roughly 10 to 60 seconds. Each run averages about 6 milliseconds based on the balance sheet timing. The single-line suite.txt output matches the runner's exact print format, so the log is likely genuine. I will also check whether the .harbor-target directory still exists, since the plan calls for deleting engine/target after completion.\n\nThe non-goal to delete engine/target is a verification requirement, so its absence is correct. I will now read ops.rs and mod.rs in chunks to hunt for real logic bugs in tool application and the step function. I will also search the game code for TODOs, banned names, and HTML about-data issues, and inspect the hub implementation for missed bugs.\n\nHub evidence appears detailed. I will spot-check hub_shim and confirm session.js is unmodified and first. I will also inspect launch.py to verify the painted-pixel check was genuine rather than a canvas-size proxy. The verification plan requires canvas dimensions and painted coverage, yet status.json only records size fields. The screenshots visually confirm substantial painting. Music 0.10 is present in status.json.\n\nInput focus and screen transitions match across both runs. The console shows zero page errors, and the screenshots are clean with no overlays. The device correctly shifts from keyboard to gamepad when pad-south is pressed. I will now inspect the simulation for deeper bugs.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-d5a7c882-d9f6-411b-8f3e-3810bd25725d-35","name":"grep","input":{"pattern":"todo!|unimplemented!|TODO|FIXME|stub|placeholder","path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224015__x42677a/work/Hands of Harbor: Second Opinion-Trauma Center: Second Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-224015/engine/crates/pav_core/src/games/surgery","glob":"*.rs"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-d5a7c882-d9f6-411b-8f3e-3810bd25725d-36","name":"grep","input":{"pattern":"Hope Hospital|Caduceus|Stiles|GUILT|Healing Touch|COOL|Derek Stiles|Angie|Naomi Kimishima|Delphi|Kyriaki|Triti|Paraskevi","path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224015__x42677a/work/Hands of Harbor: Second Opinion-Trauma Center: Second Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-224015/engine/crates","glob":"*.{rs,js,html,toml}"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-d5a7c882-d9f6-411b-8f3e-3810bd25725d-37","name":"grep","input":{"pattern":"about-data|aihub-session|hub:session","path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224015__x42677a/work/Hands of Harbor: Second Opinion-Trauma Center: Second Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-224015.html","head_limit":30}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":