            g.hub_quiet = true;\\n                }\\n            });\\n        }\\n        if let Some(boot) = hub.boot.clone() {\\n            let host = app.host.as_ref().unwrap();\\n            host.exec(move |sim| {\\n                if boot.mirror {\\n                    if let Some(g) = sim.state.play.as_mut().and_then(|p| p.get_mut::<Surgery>()) {\\n                        g.boot_mirror();\\n                    }\\n                } else {\\n                    Surgery::boot_hub_round(sim, boot.seed as u64, &boot.slots, true);\\n                }\\n            });\\n        }\\n        if let Some(snap) = hub.snap.clone() {\\n            if snap.bucket >= app.harbor.applied_bucket {\\n                app.harbor.applied_bucket = snap.bucket;\\n                let host = app.host.as_ref().unwrap();\\n                host.exec(move |sim| {\\n                    if let Some(g) = sim.state.play.as_mut().and_then(|p| p.get_mut::<Surgery>()) {\\n                        g.apply_mirror(snap.vitals, snap.bpm, snap.phase, snap.flat, snap.timer, snap.code_t, &snap.hazards, &snap.cursors);\\n                    }\\n                });\\n            }\\n        }\\n        if !hub.server {\\n            let me = hub.slot as usize;\\n            if me < 4 {\\n                if let Some(dom) = hub.dom {\\n                    if dom.x != 0.0 || dom.y != 0.0 {\\n                        surgeons[me].active = true;\\n                        surgeons[me].aim = shape_stick(Vec2::new(dom.x, -dom.y));\\n                        surgeons[me].held &= !(surg::AIM_ABSOLUTE | surg::SNAP);\\n                    }\\n                    if dom.use_on {\\n                        surgeons[me].held |= surg::USE;\\n\",\"total_lines\":929}}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa38-de6f-7dc0-ae0d-e0f717ed75f2","uuid":"0ea5ed6a-738d-447c-a23b-7c0a5757c632"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_796","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"`emit` returns immediately when the operation condition is met.\n\n`emit` suppresses the entire operative field during hub sessions. The plate, instruments, and hazards are all omitted, leaving only camera and lights. Criterion 4 states that hub sessions are shared-world Code Blue client mirrors.\n\nThe protocol harness passed, so the underlying code is correct. The empty 3D view during hub play is an intentional design choice. Players cannot see their cursor or the patient in the operative field.\n\nThe host hub also boots with quiet mode enabled, so the operative field is hidden for the host as well. The harness passed because it validates JavaScript state rather than rendered pixels. PLAN.md section 9 should clarify what the client mirror must display.\n\nThe empty operative field is a real bug for the online multiplayer feature. TASK.md requires online play through ai-hub, so playing a surgery without seeing it fails that requirement. The HUD probably still shows vitals and timer, but not the operative field itself. The code in `pav_view/src/surgery/mod.rs` and `product.rs` confirms that `boot_hub_round` sets `hub_quiet` to true at session start.\n\nThe empty hub view is a documented workaround to prevent iframe stalls. The acceptance criteria require a client mirror of the operation, but the verification plan only gates on protocol-level observations such as cursor position and vitals. The visual field is not explicitly included in those gating checks.\n\nThe mirror state is computed correctly. The view layer drops it during quiet mode. This is a feature wired to nothing visually. It is a demonstrable bug from source.\n\nThe hub view would render as a blank dark teal background with no organ, tools, or wounds. I will also examine local play for a clearer dressing bug.\n\nDressing auto-select is the stronger solo-campaign bug. The blank hub field is an online-only issue.\n\nI will verify session.js loads first and remains unmodified. I will also spot-check about-data against the exit interview.\n\nEngine target deletion is extra guidance, not a required contract.\n\nThe `#[ignore]` on `balance_sheet` was run separately and passed. I will not cite it as a strict failure, since removing the ignore would print the balance table and violate the single-pass line requirement.\n\nTremor is always active for player 0 by default, so Mara's hands shake too. PLAN.md says it should be Pet's and off during Echo via a setting. This is a design miss rather than a wrong-result bug.\n\nCase 2 scripted code works correctly. The phase has empty spawns and script_code 1, so pending_script triggers begin_code and the bot defibrillates.\n\nHeat coverage is verified. The heat ring notes K_HEAT when the sweep completes.\n\nGift coverage is verified. The meter sets to 100 on unlock and the bot consumes the gift. All three campaign gifts unlock correctly.\n\nScanner behavior is confirmed. Foreign tools remain hidden in case 1.\n\nThe cryo/dressing input bug is the strongest player-facing issue.\n\nA tool mismatch case was also confirmed. When the player holds LASER and the ember holds CRYO, accepts() returns false. The wrong-tool penalty fires and the ember never progresses. This case cannot complete.\n\nCase 2 is unwinnable with the pad or mouse ring. The ring cannot select tool 9 (Dressing), which the phase requires. Case 0 and 1 avoid this because they use only tools 0 through 5. Cases 5 and 7 are blocked by embers. Keyboard digits 0 and 9 can still select those tools.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-9fb62479-5448-4835-98fe-b7d7626aac7b-62","name":"grep","input":{"pattern":"Cryoprobe|Dressing|Digit9|tool 8|contextual","path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224015__x42677a/work/Hands of Harbor: Second Opinion-Trauma Center: Second Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104