{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_799","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"A potential SAC bug was spotted: when an SAC bursts, note_kind increments coverage and marks the SAC dead.\n\nThe SAC burst timing checks out: 14 seconds to burst versus 12.4 seconds in case 4 is feasible with fast laser attacks. The SAC bug theory is being refuted. Introit wander logic is also clarified: only the first phase wanders, while later phases remain static nodules.\n\nHub quiet mode suppresses all 3D rendering during hub rounds. The emit function exits early when the quiet flag is set, and that flag remains true throughout the entire hub session. Only the egui HUD may still display vitals.\n\nWounds are invisible to players. The cursor is also hidden because instruments() is skipped during quiet hub rounds. Tests validate cursor positions in JSON status rather than rendered output, so the client mirror is purely a data layer. Both issues will be reported. A test gap exists: no test exercises the real input path through Harbor::tools_from_hands, octant, and tray, then simulates selecting cryoprobe or dressing to clear an ember or dressing.\n\nThe implementer should wire contextual selection and add a test that exercises the player input mapping. The octant and tray_tool functions are callable but cannot return tool IDs 8 or 9 because of missing contextual remapping. Surgery tests pass tool IDs directly, so they never catch unreachable tools.\n\nThe hub's 3D suppression may be a necessary workaround. A full operative mesh stalls the iframe after one frame, and shadows or post-processing on a software GPU can freeze rendering entirely. Requiring the full plate to draw would likely break hub tests again.\n\nThe emit function exits before shadows are reduced, so even a lightweight quiet mesh would be suppressed. A low-resolution plate could still render during hub rounds without breaking the harness. A blank field is a real bug.\n\nThe SAC note_kind double count is not a bug. The silent hub field is an application bug, not an environment limitation.\n\nCase 6 is named \"Margin of the Map\" rather than Dies Irae, and cryoprobe appears in case 5 instead of replacing a ring. The reachability bug remains the only issue if all mechanics are still reachable.\n\nPar is not tuned to the bot's runs. At skill 1.0 the score reaches roughly 3600 while par is only 900, so every clear becomes an ENCORE. PLAN 3.6 requires setting par from the bot's runs.\n\nThe balance sheet computed par but never wrote it back. Because every win yields an ENCORE, the C/B/A/S rank tiers are unreachable and the ranking system is non-functional.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-c4b3d730-c4ae-493c-a35f-65cd4a945337-68","name":"grep","input":{"pattern":"hazard|cursor|quiet","path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224015__x42677a/work/Hands of Harbor: Second Opinion-Trauma Center: Second Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-224015/engine/crates/pav_ui/src/surgery/mod.rs"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-c4b3d730-c4ae-493c-a35f-65cd4a945337-69","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224015__x42677a/work/Hands of Harbor: Second Opinion-Trauma Center: Second Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-224015/engine/crates/pav_view/src/build.rs","offset":1455,"limit":30}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2433,"output_tokens":2396,"cache_read_input_tokens":131968,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa38-de6f-7dc0-ae0d-e0f717ed75f2","uuid":"2aacb0c7-9a67-4b5f-9266-493696f80223"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-c4b3d730-c4ae-493c-a35f-65cd4a945337-68","content":"{\"type\":\"GrepSearch\",\"stdout\":[60,119,111,114,107,115,112,97,99,101,95,114,101,115,117,108,116,32,119,111,114,107,115,112,97,99,101,95,112,97,116,104,61,34,47,104,111,109,101,47,109,105,99,104,97,47,100,101,118,47,99,99,45,109,97,116,114,105,120,47,114,117,110,115,47,103,114,111,107,45,120,104,105,103,104,46,98,117,105,108,100,45,118,50,95,95,50,48,50,54,49,49,48,52,45,50,50,52,48,49,53,95,95,120,52,50,54,55,55,97,47,119,111,114,107,34,62,10,78,111,32,109,97,116,99,104,101,115,32,102,111,117,110,100,10,60,47,119,111,114,107,115,112,97,99,101,95,114,101,115,117,108,116,62],\"stderr\":[],\"exit_code\":1,\"match_count\":0,\"file_matches\":[]}","is_error":false},{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-c4b3d730-c4ae-493c-a35f-65cd4a945337-69","content":"{\"type\":\"ReadFile\",\"FileContent\":{\"content\":\"1455→            mark_pixel_art(&mut scene, |g, flags| match f.pixel_target {\\n                PixelTarget::All => true,\\n                PixelTarget::Characters => puppets.contains(&g),\\n                PixelTarget::Hero => Some(g) == hero,\\n                PixelTarget::Others => puppets.contains(&g) && Some(g) != hero,\\n1460→                PixelTarget::World => !puppets.contains(&g),\\n                PixelTarget::Entity => g == f.pixel_entity as u32 + 2,\\n                PixelTarget::Objects => flags & rs::flags::OBJECT != 0,\\n                PixelTarget::Environment => flags & rs::flags::OBJECT == 0,\\n            });\\n        }\\n        lock(&self.materials).attach(&mut scene);\\n        if let Some(op) = curr.surgery.as_deref() {\\n            crate::surgery::emit(&mut scene, op);\\n            crate::surgery::apply_look(&mut scene, rig, aspect, &op.camera, op.quiet);\\n1470→        }\\n        scene\\n    }\\n}\\n\\n/// Flags the characters and objects: every instance emitted after the environment (`from`:\\n/// meshes, SDFs, dynamic meshes) except fixed scenery (outline groups in `scenery`, sorted).\\nfn mark_objects(scene: &mut Scene, from: (usize, usize, usize), scenery: &[u32]) {\\n    let object = |g: u32| scenery.binary_search(&g).is_err();\\n    for m in &mut scene.meshes[from.0..] {\\n1480→        if object(m.group) {\\n            m.flags |= rs::flags::OBJECT;\\n        }\\n    }\\n    for s in &mut scene.sdfs[from.1..] {\",\"content_concise\":\"1455→            mark_pixel_art(&mut scene, |g, flags| match f.pixel_target {\\n                PixelTarget::All => true,\\n                PixelTarget::Characters => puppets.contains(&g),\\n                PixelTarget::Hero => Some(g) == hero,\\n                PixelTarget::Others => puppets.contains(&g) && Some(g) != hero,\\n1460→                PixelTarget::World => !puppets.contains(&g),\\n                PixelTarget::Entity => g == f.pixel_entity as u32 + 2,\\n                PixelTarget::Objects => flags & rs::flags::OBJECT != 0,\\n                PixelTarget::Environment => flags & rs::flags::OBJECT == 0,\\n            });\\n        }\\n        lock(&self.materials).attach(&mut scene);\\n        if let Some(op) = curr.surgery.as_deref() {\\n            crate::surgery::emit(&mut scene, op);\\n            crate::surgery::apply_look(&mut scene, rig, aspect, &op.camera, op.quiet);\\n1470→        }\\n        scene\\n    }\\n}\\n\\n/// Flags the characters and objects: every instance emitted after the environment (`from`:\\n/// meshes, SDFs, dynamic meshes) except fixed scenery (outline groups in `scenery`, sorted).\\nfn mark_objects(scene: &mut Scene, from: (usize, usize, usize), scenery: &[u32]) {\\n    let object = |g: u32| scenery.binary_search(&g).is_err();\\n    for m in &mut scene.meshes[from.0..] {\\n1480→        if object(m.group) {\\n            m.flags |= rs::flags::OBJECT;\\n        }\\n    }\\n    for s in &mut scene.sdfs[from.1..] {\",\"absolute_path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224015__x42677a/work/Hands of Harbor: Second Opinion-Trauma Center: Second Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-224015/engine/crates/pav_view/src/build.rs\",\"offset\":1455,\"limit\":30,\"raw_output\":\"            mark_pixel_art(&mut scene, |g, flags| match f.pixel_target {\\n                PixelTarget::All => true,\\n                PixelTarget::Characters => puppets.contains(&g),\\n                PixelTarget::Hero => Some(g) == hero,\\n                PixelTarget::Others => puppets.contains(&g) && Some(g) != hero,\\n                PixelTarget::World => !puppets.contains(&g),\\n                PixelTarget::Entity => g == f.pixel_entity as u32 + 2,\\n                PixelTarget::Objects => flags & rs::flags::OBJECT != 0,\\n                PixelTarget::Environment => flags & rs::flags::OBJECT == 0,\\n            });\\n        }\\n        lock(&self.materials).attach(&mut scene);\\n        if let Some(op) = curr.surgery.as_deref() {\\n            crate::surgery::emit(&mut scene, op);\\n            crate::surgery::apply_look(&mut scene, rig, aspect, &op.camera, op.quiet);\\n        }\\n        scene\\n    }\\n}\\n\\n/// Flags the characters and objects: every instance emitted after the environment (`from`:\\n/// meshes, SDFs, dynamic meshes) except fixed scenery (outline groups in `scenery`, sorted).\\nfn mark_objects(scene: &mut Scene, from: (usize, usize, usize), scenery: &[u32]) {\\n    let object = |g: u32| scenery.binary_search(&g).is_err();\\n    for m in &mut scene.meshes[from.0..] {\\n        if object(m.group) {\\n            m.flags |= rs::flags::OBJECT;\\n        }\\n    }\\n    for s in &mut scene.sdfs[from.1..] {\\n\",\"total_lines\":2409}}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa38-de6f-7dc0-ae0d-e0f717ed75f2","uuid":"53a7a1a4-6dbd-456d-bf68-0818f75c648a"}
