{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-1a8c5f62-84e8-46db-b10d-9022ee2b4c55-122","content":"{\"type\":\"ReadFile\",\"FileContent\":{\"content\":\"140→Field space: x ∈ [-11, 11], z ∈ [-6.3, 6.3] (1 unit ≈ 80 px at 1080p). Keep gameplay inside x ∈ [-9, 9],\\nz ∈ [-4, 4.2], clear of the HUD. All game logic is 2D in this plane, with no physics.\\n\\n**Controls**\\n\\n| Action | DualSense | Mouse + keyboard |\\n|---|---|---|\\n| Move cursor | Right stick (`v = 15 u/s · s^2.2`) | Mouse (absolute); WASD or arrows also move it for keyboard-only play |\\n| Use tool | R2, analog (or hold Cross) | Left button (or hold E) |\\n| Pick tool | Left stick flick, 8 directions, instant (or L1/R1 to cycle) | 1–8, wheel, or click the instrument on the tray |\\n150→| Precision | Hold L2 (×0.35) | Hold Shift (keyboard cursor only; the mouse is already precise) |\\n| Cancel, let go | Circle | Right button or Q |\\n| Gift | Triangle | Space |\\n| Chart overlay | Square | Tab |\\n| Rotate held bone | L1/R1 while holding | Wheel while holding |\\n| Defibrillate | L2 + R2 | Both mouse buttons |\\n| Pause | Options (ignored while Create is held: that combination is the hub's) | Esc |\\n\\nThe stick flick is the signature: it must switch tools with no menu and no slowdown.\\n\\n160→**Aim assist (pad and keyboard cursor only; slider in Settings and dev mode).** Within 1.2 u of a valid\\ntarget for the current tool, speed falls by up to 50% and the cursor is pulled toward it at up to\\n3 u/s, only while the stick is moving. While the Scalpel is engaged, sideways error is damped (rail\\nassist). While suturing, the needle creeps along the wound by itself, so the stick only flicks across\\nit. The mouse gets none of this, since it needs none.\\n\\n### 3.3 The instruments\\n\\nThe ring has 8 fixed directions, data-driven per case. Up: Scalpel. Up-right: Forceps. Right: Suture.\\nDown-right: Suction. Down: Laser (Cryoprobe in Case 6). Down-left: Gel. Left: Scanner (Cryoprobe in\\n170→Case 7, where the nodules stay visible). Up-left: IV Push.\\n\\n| Tool | Gesture | Rated on | Misuse |\\n|---|---|---|---|\\n| **Scalpel** | Hold, follow the dashed line in one stroke | Sideways deviation (≤0.25 u is Immaculate) | Cutting healthy tissue makes a small laceration and costs vitals |\\n| **Forceps** | Hold to grab, pull along the object's axis about 1 u, it drops on the tray | Angle error of the pull | Yanking off-axis tears a laceration |\\n| **Suture** | Hold, zigzag across the wound. Each crossing near the advancing needle is a stitch; about 1 per 0.5 u | Evenness of spacing and pace | Sloppy spacing leaves a slow bleed |\\n| **Suction** | Hold over a pool. Analog: harder drains faster, and gurgles louder | None (always Good) | Safe everywhere |\\n| **Laser** | Hold on a target, the heat ring fills in about 1.2 s, release at 80–100% | Release timing | Overheating makes a burn |\\n| **Gel** | Hold and paint until the coverage ring is full. The flow meter refills in seconds | Overspray | Wasted gel |\\n180→| **Scanner** | Hold and sweep. Sonar pings reveal hidden things for 8 s | None | Safe everywhere |\\n| **IV Push** | Auto-moves to the IV port. Hold; vitals rise; release in the green band (+18 at a full dose, 4 s cooldown) | Release timing | Overdose: a spike, then −8 |\\n| **Cryoprobe** (Case 6 on) | Hold on a node until the frost ring closes (1 s), which makes it brittle | Release timing | Frostbite |\\n| **Dressing** (context, auto-selected) | Final close: hold and draw along the closure | Coverage | None |\\n| **Defibrillator** (context) | Code only: hold L2 + R2 to charge (1.2 s), release as the ghost beat crosses centre | Timing | Failure: no recovery |\\n\\nWrong tool on a target: a clink, Bashir's callout, a chain reset, no effect. Every tool must have its\\nown 3D model, motion, sound and particles, and the tray shows its state.\\n\\n### 3.4 Hazards (what tasks are made of)\\n190→\\nEach is a data-spawned object with position, progress and a vitals drain per second.\\n\\n| Hazard | Tool(s) | Drain/s | Notes |\\n|---|---|---|---|\",\"content_concise\":\"140→Field space: x ∈ [-11, 11], z ∈ [-6.3, 6.3] (1 unit ≈ 80 px at 1080p). Keep gameplay inside x ∈ [-9, 9],\\nz ∈ [-4, 4.2], clear of the HUD. All game logic is 2D in this plane, with no physics.\\n\\n**Controls**\\n\\n| Action | DualSense | Mouse + keyboard |\\n|---|---|---|\\n| Move cursor | Right stick (`v = 15 u/s · s^2.2`) | Mouse (absolute); WASD or arrows also move it for keyboard-only play |\\n| Use tool | R2, analog (or hold Cross) | Left button (or hold E) |\\n| Pick tool | Left stick flick, 8 directions, instant (or L1/R1 to cycle) | 1–8, wheel, or click the instrument on the tray |\\n150→| Precision | Hold L2 (×0.35) | Hold Shift (keyboard cursor only; the mouse is already precise) |\\n| Cancel, let go | Circle | Right button or Q |\\n| Gift | Triangle | Space |\\n| Chart overlay | Square | Tab |\\n| Rotate held bone | L1/R1 while holding | Wheel while holding |\\n| Defibrillate | L2 + R2 | Both mouse buttons |\\n| Pause | Options (ignored while Create is held: that combination is the hub's) | Esc |\\n\\nThe stick flick is the signature: it must switch tools with no menu and no slowdown.\\n\\n160→**Aim assist (pad and keyboard cursor only; slider in Settings and dev mode).** Within 1.2 u of a valid\\ntarget for the current tool, speed falls by up to 50% and the cursor is pulled toward it at up to\\n3 u/s, only while the stick is moving. While the Scalpel is engaged, sideways error is damped (rail\\nassist). While suturing, the needle creeps along the wound by itself, so the stick only flicks across\\nit. The mouse gets none of this, since it needs none.\\n\\n### 3.3 The instruments\\n\\nThe ring has 8 fixed directions, data-driven per case. Up: Scalpel. Up-right: Forceps. Right: Suture.\\nDown-right: Suction. Down: Laser (Cryoprobe in Case 6). Down-left: Gel. Left: Scanner (Cryoprobe in\\n170→Case 7, where the nodules stay visible). Up-left: IV Push.\\n\\n| Tool | Gesture | Rated on | Misuse |\\n|---|---|---|---|\\n| **Scalpel** | Hold, follow the dashed line in one stroke | Sideways deviation (≤0.25 u is Immaculate) | Cutting healthy tissue makes a small laceration and costs vitals |\\n| **Forceps** | Hold to grab, pull along the object's axis about 1 u, it drops on the tray | Angle error of the pull | Yanking off-axis tears a laceration |\\n| **Suture** | Hold, zigzag across the wound. Each crossing near the advancing needle is a stitch; about 1 per 0.5 u | Evenness of spacing and pace | Sloppy spacing leaves a slow bleed |\\n| **Suction** | Hold over a pool. Analog: harder drains faster, and gurgles louder | None (always Good) | Safe everywhere |\\n| **Laser** | Hold on a target, the heat ring fills in about 1.2 s, release at 80–100% | Release timing | Overheating makes a burn |\\n| **Gel** | Hold and paint until the coverage ring is full. The flow meter refills in seconds | Overspray | Wasted gel |\\n180→| **Scanner** | Hold and sweep. Sonar pings reveal hidden things for 8 s | None | Safe everywhere |\\n| **IV Push** | Auto-moves to the IV port. Hold; vitals rise; release in the green band (+18 at a full dose, 4 s cooldown) | Release timing | Overdose: a spike, then −8 |\\n| **Cryoprobe** (Case 6 on) | Hold on a node until the frost ring closes (1 s), which makes it brittle | Release timing | Frostbite |\\n| **Dressing** (context, auto-selected) | Final close: hold and draw along the closure | Coverage | None |\\n| **Defibrillator** (context) | Code only: hold L2 + R2 to charge (1.2 s), release as the ghost beat crosses centre | Timing | Failure: no recovery |\\n\\nWrong tool on a target: a clink, Bashir's callout, a chain reset, no effect. Every tool must have its\\nown 3D model, motion, sound and particles, and the tray shows its state.\\n\\n### 3.4 Hazards (what tasks are made of)\\n190→\\nEach is a data-spawned object with position, progress and a vitals drain per second.\\n\\n| Hazard | Tool(s) | Drain/s | Notes |\\n|---|---|---|---|\",\"absolute_path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224015__x42677a/work/PLAN.md\",\"offset\":140,\"limit\":55,\"raw_output\":\"Field space: x ∈ [-11, 11], z ∈ [-6.3, 6.3] (1 unit ≈ 80 px at 1080p). Keep gameplay inside x ∈ [-9, 9],\\nz ∈ [-4, 4.2], clear of the HUD. All game logic is 2D in this plane, with no physics.\\n\\n**Controls**\\n\\n| Action | DualSense | Mouse + keyboard |\\n|---|---|---|\\n| Move cursor | Right stick (`v = 15 u/s · s^2.2`) | Mouse (absolute); WASD or arrows also move it for keyboard-only play |\\n| Use tool | R2, analog (or hold Cross) | Left button (or hold E) |\\n| Pick tool | Left stick flick, 8 directions, instant (or L1/R1 to cycle) | 1–8, wheel, or click the instrument on the tray |\\n| Precision | Hold L2 (×0.35) | Hold Shift (keyboard cursor only; the mouse is already precise) |\\n| Cancel, let go | Circle | Right button or Q |\\n| Gift | Triangle | Space |\\n| Chart overlay | Square | Tab |\\n| Rotate held bone | L1/R1 while holding | Wheel while holding |\\n| Defibrillate | L2 + R2 | Both mouse buttons |\\n| Pause | Options (ignored while Create is held: that combination is the hub's) | Esc |\\n\\nThe stick flick is the signature: it must switch tools with no menu and no slowdown.\\n\\n**Aim assist (pad and keyboard cursor only; slider in Settings and dev mode).** Within 1.2 u of a valid\\ntarget for the current tool, speed falls by up to 50% and the cursor is pulled toward it at up to\\n3 u/s, only while the stick is moving. While the Scalpel is engaged, sideways error is damped (rail\\nassist). While suturing, the needle creeps along the wound by itself, so the stick only flicks across\\nit. The mouse gets none of this, since it needs none.\\n\\n### 3.3 The instruments\\n\\nThe ring has 8 fixed directions, data-driven per case. Up: Scalpel. Up-right: Forceps. Right: Suture.\\nDown-right: Suction. Down: Laser (Cryoprobe in Case 6). Down-left: Gel. Left: Scanner (Cryoprobe in\\nCase 7, where the nodules stay visible). Up-left: IV Push.\\n\\n| Tool | Gesture | Rated on | Misuse |\\n|---|---|---|---|\\n| **Scalpel** | Hold, follow the dashed line in one stroke | Sideways deviation (≤0.25 u is Immaculate) | Cutting healthy tissue makes a small laceration and costs vitals |\\n| **Forceps** | Hold to grab, pull along the object's axis about 1 u, it drops on the tray | Angle error of the pull | Yanking off-axis tears a laceration |\\n| **Suture** | Hold, zigzag across the wound. Each crossing near the advancing needle is a stitch; about 1 per 0.5 u | Evenness of spacing and pace | Sloppy spacing leaves a slow bleed |\\n| **Suction** | Hold over a pool. Analog: harder drains faster, and gurgles louder | None (always Good) | Safe everywhere |\\n| **Laser** | Hold on a target, the heat ring fills in about 1.2 s, release at 80–100% | Release timing | Overheating makes a burn |\\n| **Gel** | Hold and paint until the coverage ring is full. The flow meter refills in seconds | Overspray | Wasted gel |\\n| **Scanner** | Hold and sweep. Sonar pings reveal hidden things for 8 s | None | Safe everywhere |\\n| **IV Push** | Auto-moves to the IV port. Hold; vitals rise; release in the green band (+18 at a full dose, 4 s cooldown) | Release timing | Overdose: a spike, then −8 |\\n| **Cryoprobe** (Case 6 on) | Hold on a node until the frost ring closes (1 s), which makes it brittle | Release timing | Frostbite |\\n| **Dressing** (context, auto-selected) | Final close: hold and draw along the closure | Coverage | None |\\n| **Defibrillator** (context) | Code only: hold L2 + R2 to charge (1.2 s), release as the ghost beat crosses centre | Timing | Failure: no recovery |\\n\\nWrong tool on a target: a clink, Bashir's callout, a chain reset, no effect. Every tool must have its\\nown 3D model, motion, sound and particles, and the tray shows its state.\\n\\n### 3.4 Hazards (what tasks are made of)\\n\\nEach is a data-spawned object with position, progress and a vitals drain per second.\\n\\n| Hazard | Tool(s) | Drain/s | Notes |\\n|---|---|---|---|\\n\",\"total_lines\":817}}","is_error":false},{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-1a8c5f62-84e8-46db-b10d-9022ee2b4c55-123","content":"{\"type\":\"ReadFile\",\"FileContent\":{\"content\":\"220→            right: !op && right,\\n            confirm: !op && confirm,\\n            back,\\n            tab_l,\\n            tab_r,\\n            pointer,\\n            click,\\n            any,\\n            dt,\\n            device,\\n230→        });\\n        let confirm_sim = cmds.iter().any(|c| matches!(c, Cmd::ConfirmSim));\\n        self.tools_from_hands(op, local);\\n        let mut surgeons = [SurgeonInput { tool: TOOL_KEEP, ..SurgeonInput::default() }; 4];\\n        if op {\\n            for i in 0..4 {\\n                let owns = local.is_none() && i == 0 && self.mouse_owns || local == Some(i as u8) && self.mouse_owns;\\n                surgeons[i] = self.hand(i, aim, owns, local);\\n            }\\n        } else if confirm_sim {\\n240→            surgeons[0].active = true;\\n            surgeons[0].tool = TOOL_KEEP;\\n            surgeons[0].held |= surg::CONFIRM;\\n            surgeons[0].pressed |= surg::CONFIRM;\\n        }\\n        self.mouse_click = false;\\n        self.mouse_moved = false;\\n        self.touch_click = false;\\n        self.wheel = 0.0;\\n        self.just.clear();\\n250→        (cmds, surgeons, confirm_sim)\\n    }\\n\\n    fn tools_from_hands(&mut self, op: bool, local: Option<u8>) {\\n        if !op {\\n            return;\\n        }\\n        let pairs: Vec<(usize, usize)> = if let Some(me) = local {\\n            vec![(0, me as usize)]\\n        } else {\\n260→            (0..4).filter(|i| self.pads[*i].present).map(|i| (i, i)).collect()\\n        };\\n        for (pad_i, tool_i) in pairs {\\n            let pad = self.pads[pad_i];\\n            if !pad.present && local.is_none() {\\n                continue;\\n            }\\n            let using = pad.rt > 0.2 || pad.south;\\n            if pad.present && pad.l1 && !self.prev_l1[pad_i] && !using {\\n                self.tool[tool_i] = (self.tool[tool_i] + 7) % 8;\\n270→            }\\n            if pad.present && pad.r1 && !self.prev_r1[pad_i] && !using {\\n                self.tool[tool_i] = (self.tool[tool_i] + 1) % 8;\\n            }\\n            if pad.present {\\n                self.prev_l1[pad_i] = pad.l1;\\n                self.prev_r1[pad_i] = pad.r1;\\n                let oct = octant(pad.left);\\n                if let Some(t) = oct {\\n                    if self.prev_oct[pad_i] != Some(t) {\\n280→                        self.tool[tool_i] = t;\\n                    }\\n                }\\n                self.prev_oct[pad_i] = oct;\\n            }\\n        }\\n        let me = local.unwrap_or(0) as usize;\\n        if self.wheel.abs() > 0.01 && !self.mouse_left {\\n            let dir = if self.wheel > 0.0 { 1 } else { 7 };\\n            self.tool[me] = (self.tool[me] + dir) % 8;\\n290→        }\\n        for (code, tool) in DIGITS {\\n            if self.ate(code) {\\n                self.tool[me] = tool;\\n            }\\n        }\\n    }\\n\\n    fn hand(&self, slot: usize, mouse_aim: Option<[f32; 2]>, mouse_owns: bool, local: Option<u8>) -> SurgeonInput {\\n        if let Some(me) = local {\\n300→            if slot as u8 != me {\\n                return SurgeonInput { tool: TOOL_KEEP, ..SurgeonInput::default() };\\n            }\\n        }\\n        let pad = if local.is_some() { &self.pads[0] } else { &self.pads[slot] };\\n        let mine = local.is_some() || slot == 0;\\n        let mut held = 0;\\n        let mut aim = Vec2::ZERO;\\n        let mut pressure = 0.85;\\n        if mine && mouse_owns {\\n310→            if let Some(p) = mouse_aim {\\n                aim = Vec2::new(p[0], p[1]);\\n                held |= surg::AIM_ABSOLUTE | surg::SNAP;\\n            }\\n        } else if pad.present && pad.right.length() > 0.12 {\\n            aim = shape_stick(Vec2::new(pad.right.x, -pad.right.y));\\n        } else if mine && !mouse_owns {\\n            let mut v = Vec2::ZERO;\\n            if self.key(KeyCode::KeyW) || self.key(KeyCode::ArrowUp) {\\n                v.y += 1.0;\\n320→            }\\n            if self.key(KeyCode::KeyS) || self.key(KeyCode::ArrowDown) {\\n                v.y -= 1.0;\\n            }\\n            if self.key(KeyCode::KeyD) || self.key(KeyCode::ArrowRight) {\\n                v.x += 1.0;\\n            }\\n            if self.key(KeyCode::KeyA) || self.key(KeyCode::ArrowLeft) {\\n                v.x -= 1.0;\\n            }\\n330→            if v.length_squared() > 0.0 {\\n                aim = shape_stick(Vec2::new(v.x, -v.y));\\n            }\\n        }\\n        let use_key = mine && (self.mouse_left || self.key(KeyCode::KeyE));\\n        let use_pad = pad.present && (pad.rt > 0.08 || pad.south);\\n        if use_key || use_pad {\\n            held |= surg::USE;\\n            pressure = if pad.rt > 0.08 { pad.rt.max(0.15) } else { 1.0 };\\n        }\\n340→        let precise = (mine && self.key(KeyCode::ShiftLeft) && !mouse_owns) || pad.lt > 0.35;\\n        if precise {\\n            held |= surg::PRECISION;\\n        }\\n        if mine && (self.mouse_right || self.key(KeyCode::KeyQ)) || pad.east {\\n            held |= surg::CANCEL;\\n        }\\n        if mine && self.key(KeyCode::Space) || pad.north {\\n            held |= surg::GIFT;\\n        }\\n350→        if mine && self.key(KeyCode::Tab) || pad.west {\\n            held |= surg::CHART;\\n        }\\n        let both_mouse = mine && self.mouse_left && self.mouse_right;\\n        let both_trig = pad.lt > 0.45 && pad.rt > 0.45;\\n        if both_mouse || both_trig || self.tool[slot] == 10 && (use_key || use_pad) {\\n            held |= surg::DEFIB;\\n        }\\n        let using = held & surg::USE != 0;\\n        if using && pad.l1 {\\n360→            held |= surg::ROT_L;\\n        }\\n        if using && pad.r1 {\\n            held |= surg::ROT_R;\\n        }\\n        if mine && using && self.wheel > 0.1 {\\n            held |= surg::ROT_R;\\n        }\\n        if mine && using && self.wheel < -0.1 {\\n            held |= surg::ROT_L;\\n370→        }\\n        let active = local.is_some() || slot == 0 || pad.present;\\n        SurgeonInput { active, aim, held, pressed: 0, tool: self.tool[slot], pressure }\\n    }\\n}\\n\\nconst DIGITS: [(KeyCode, u8); 11] = [\\n    (KeyCode::Digit1, 0),\\n    (KeyCode::Digit2, 1),\\n    (KeyCode::Digit3, 2),\\n380→    (KeyCode::Digit4, 3),\\n    (KeyCode::Digit5, 4),\\n    (KeyCode::Digit6, 5),\\n    (KeyCode::Digit7, 6),\\n    (KeyCode::Digit8, 7),\\n    (KeyCode::Digit9, 8),\\n    (KeyCode::Digit0, 9),\\n    (KeyCode::Minus, 10),\\n];\\n\\n390→fn dead(v: Vec2) -> Vec2 {\\n    if v.length() < 0.18 { Vec2::ZERO } else { v.clamp_length_max(1.0) }\\n}\\n\\nfn shape_stick(v: Vec2) -> Vec2 {\\n    let mag = v.length().min(1.0);\\n    if mag < 0.001 {\\n        return Vec2::ZERO;\\n    }\\n    v.normalize() * mag.powf(2.2)\\n400→}\\n\\nfn octant(stick: Vec2) -> Option<u8> {\\n    if stick.length() < 0.55 {\\n        return None;\\n    }\\n    let ang = stick.x.atan2(stick.y);\\n    Some((ang / std::f32::consts::FRAC_PI_4).round() as i32).map(|i| i.rem_euclid(8) as u8)\\n}\\n\\n410→fn to_sim(c: Cmd) -> Option<SurgeryCmd> {\\n    Some(match c {\\n        Cmd::LoadCampaign => SurgeryCmd::LoadCampaign,\\n        Cmd::LoadCase(n) => SurgeryCmd::LoadCase(n),\\n        Cmd::LoadCode => SurgeryCmd::LoadCode,\\n        Cmd::LoadAttract => SurgeryCmd::LoadAttract,\\n        Cmd::ToTitle => SurgeryCmd::ToTitle,\\n        Cmd::SetDifficulty(d) => SurgeryCmd::SetDifficulty(d),\\n        Cmd::Retry => SurgeryCmd::Retry,\\n        Cmd::SetTune { id, value } => SurgeryCmd::SetTune { id, value },\\n420→        Cmd::ResetTune => SurgeryCmd::ResetTune,\\n        Cmd::SetBus { which, value } => SurgeryCmd::SetBus { which, value },\\n        Cmd::Dev { what, extra } => SurgeryCmd::Dev { what, extra },\\n        Cmd::ConfirmSim => return None,\\n    })\\n}\\n\\nfn track_name(op: &SurgeryFrame) -> &'static str {\\n    if op.gift_hush > 0.0 {\\n        return \\\"hush\\\";\\n430→    }\\n    if op.flat || op.code_t >= 0.0 {\\n        return \\\"code\\\";\\n    }\\n    match op.mode {\\n        1 => {\\n            if op.case_id % 2 == 0 {\\n                \\\"story_ward\\\"\\n            } else {\\n                \\\"story_night\\\"\\n440→            }\\n        }\\n        3 | 6 => match op.strain {\\n            0..=3 => \\\"introit\\\",\\n            4..=7 => \\\"lacrimosa\\\",\\n            8..=10 => \\\"dies\\\",\\n            11..=17 => \\\"libera\\\",\\n            _ => {\\n                if op.case_id < 0 {\\n                    \\\"code\\\"\\n450→                } else {\\n                    \\\"or\\\"\\n                }\\n            }\\n        },\\n        4 => \\\"results\\\",\\n        5 => \\\"crisis\\\",\\n        7 => \\\"code\\\",\\n        _ => \\\"title\\\",\\n    }\\n460→}\\n\\npub fn surgery_frame(app: &mut App) {\\n    if app.gfx.is_none() || app.host.is_none() {\\n        return;\\n    }\\n    let now = web_time::Instant::now();\\n    let dt = (now - app.last).as_secs_f32().min(0.1);\\n    app.last = now;\\n\\n470→    #[cfg(target_arch = \\\"wasm32\\\")]\\n    drain_hook(app);\\n\\n    app.harbor.poll_pads(app.input.gilrs.as_mut());\\n    let hub = app.harbor.link.poll(dt);\\n    aim_rig(app);\\n    let (w, h) = app.gfx.as_ref().unwrap().size();\\n    let size = Vec2::new(w as f32, h as f32);\\n    let hit = app.rig.ground_point(app.harbor.mouse, size, 0.0).map(|p| [p.x, p.z]);\\n    if app.harbor.mouse_click {\\n480→        if let Some(p) = hit {\\n            if let Some(tool) = tray_tool(p[0], p[1]) {\\n                let me = if hub.active { hub.slot as usize } else { 0 };\\n                app.harbor.tool[me.min(3)]