.tool.min(DEFIB);\"},{\"line_number\":746,\"content\":\"        if inp.tool != TOOL_KEEP {\"},{\"line_number\":747,\"content\":\"            s.tool = inp.tool;\"}]}]}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa38-de6f-7dc0-ae0d-e0f717ed75f2","uuid":"4d46368c-ac05-4fab-9ce5-dbf0acdd3109"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_810","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The player tool mapping will be placed in pav_core so the shell and tests can share it.\n\nContextual swap happens when resolving the ring tool against the live field. Eight directions remain 0-7. Narrative case numbers may differ from array indices. The skeptic's references to cases 2, 5, and 7 align with content case IDs C2_B, C5_A, and C7.\n\nThe contextual swap depends on the cursor position and the nearest hazard, not just case ID 6. Cryoprobe resolves to CRYO when the player selects LASER or the plan's case-specific slot and the nearest CRYO-compatible hazard is an ember in stage 0. The plan maps down to Laser (Cryoprobe in Case 6) and left to Scanner (Cryoprobe in Case 7). The skeptic notes that a pad cannot clear case 5's embers.\n\nThe contextual swap must apply to case 5, not only case 6. The rule is broadened: if LASER or SCANNER is selected and any alive ember wants CRYO, swap to CRYO. This fixes cases 5 and 7 while loosely matching the down-stick laser mapping.\n\nThe contextual swap should live inside the simulation's hands() method. The shell can keep sending tool 4, and the sim upgrades it to CRYO when the cursor is near an ember. This lets the player path work without the shell ever emitting tool 8.\n\nThe test will call the same swap function. The skeptic confirms that cryoprobe and dressing are never selected, and nothing auto-swaps them in. The fix is auto-swap, not adding digits 9 and 0 to the pad. The swap should happen in the shipped shell mapping before the tool is sent, or inside the simulation when it receives a ring tool.\n\n`resolve_tool` will live in `pav_core::games::surgery`, likely in a new `select.rs` or `kinds.rs`. It will be called from `product.rs` and from the simulation tick. The test will call the same function before stepping the sim.\n\nThe `pav_core::games::surgery::select` module will expose `octant`, `cycle`, `tray_tool`, and `contextual_tool`. The contextual resolver takes the ring tool, case ID, aim coordinates, and live hazard list. Cycle stays modulo 8. The test can reuse these same helpers to drive the shipped mapping.\n\nThe swap rule is refined: if the ring tool is LASER or SCANNER and any alive hazard requires CRYO, return CRYO. This covers cases 5 and 7 while leaving case 6 unchanged when no embers are present. A conflict emerges in case 7, where nodules need LASER in stage 0 and embers need CRYO later.\n\nA blanket swap from LASER to CRYO whenever any ember wants it would break case 7, where nodules and embers phase sequentially. The safer rule is to swap only when the cursor is near a hazard that accepts CRYO and the ring tool is LASER or SCANNER. When aiming at an ember, laser becomes cryo; elsewhere, laser stays laser. Dressing is auto-selected based on context.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-052798ed-3692-40b5-83a1-91d33fe851e3-138","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224015__x42677a/work/Hands of Harbor: Second Opinion-Trauma Center: Second Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-224015/engine/crates/pav_core/src/games/surgery/hazard.rs","offset":140,"limit":35}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-052798ed-3692-40b5-83a1-91d33fe851e3-139","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224015__x42677a/work/Hands of Harbor: Second Opinion-Trauma Center: Second Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-224015/engine/crates/pav_core/src/games/surgery/ops.rs","offset":600,"limit":50}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-052798ed-3692-40b5-83a1-91d33fe851e3-140","name":"grep","input":{"pattern":"surgery::emit|op.quiet|hub_quiet","glob":"**/*.rs"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1653,"output_tokens":2791,"cache_read_input_tokens":201472,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa38-de6f-7dc0-ae0d-e0f717ed75f2","uuid":"aa095086-977f-47d7-bf3a-c43d78d40b1c"}
