-20261104-224015/engine/crates/pav_core/src/games/surgery/frame.rs\",\"matches\":[{\"line_number\":33,\"content\":\"pub struct HazardView {\"}]},{\"path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224015__x42677a/work/Hands of Harbor: Second Opinion-Trauma Center: Second Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-224015/engine/crates/pav_core/src/room.rs\",\"matches\":[{\"line_number\":246,\"content\":\"    pub uses: Vec<String>,\"}]},{\"path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224015__x42677a/work/Hands of Harbor: Second Opinion-Trauma Center: Second Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-224015/engine/crates/pav_core/src/games/mod.rs\",\"matches\":[{\"line_number\":23,\"content\":\"pub mod surgery;\"}]}]}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa38-de6f-7dc0-ae0d-e0f717ed75f2","uuid":"c7fb61f0-807a-4424-820d-a659adbf106a"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_815","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"I need to understand how bone stage 1 works. I need to understand suture after forceps and tether with a scalpel. I need to understand how phases advance.\n\nI need to check instruments() for cursor drawing and PLAN controls. The mapping design will go in hands.rs, kinds.rs, or a new map.rs. The player path selects an octant, cycles L1/R1 and wheel modulo 8, returns a tray tool index, then calls contextual_tool with ring, aim_x, aim_z, and hazards to get CRYO or DRESSING. I need to find where the contextual swap happens so pads can clear hazards. If only tests call contextual_tool, the skeptic's bug remains.\n\nHarbor::compose cannot perform the contextual swap because it lacks the current aim and hazards. The swap must happen when building SurgeonInput instead. The compose function runs before the pump, so it cannot access the previous frame's SurgeryFrame either.\n\nThe previous frame's SurgeryFrame is available before compose if host.frames() is read earlier. The swap can then use the current aim and prior hazards to decide on contextual tools. No prior frame exists on the first frame, but that is acceptable.\n\nThe swap should live inside the simulation in hands(). The shell would keep sending only 0-7 ring tools. The simulation would resolve contextual swaps at use time. This avoids depending on the shell having prior frame hazards. It also keeps the control table clean and lets a tool like CRYO activate when the cursor is over an ember.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-c769c682-a789-4787-9810-c45d3605e53b-15","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224015__x42677a/work/PLAN.md","offset":140,"limit":50}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-c769c682-a789-4787-9810-c45d3605e53b-16","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224015__x42677a/work/Hands of Harbor: Second Opinion-Trauma Center: Second Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-224015/engine/crates/pav_view/src/surgery/mod.rs","offset":200,"limit":180}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-c769c682-a789-4787-9810-c45d3605e53b-17","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224015__x42677a/work/Hands of Harbor: Second Opinion-Trauma Center: Second Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-224015/engine/crates/pav_core/src/games/surgery/hazard.rs","offset":1,"limit":140}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-c769c682-a789-4787-9810-c45d3605e53b-18","name":"grep","input":{"pattern":"fn advance|phase_i|next_phase|alive","glob":"**/games/surgery/ops.rs"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":49839,"output_tokens":957,"cache_read_input_tokens":10112,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa38-de6f-7dc0-ae0d-e0f717ed75f2","uuid":"44c15174-7182-404a-9f8a-5b97ae38dbb8"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-c769c682-a789-4787-9810-c45d3605e53b-15","content":"{\"type\":\"ReadFile\",\"FileContent\":{\"content\":\"140→Field space: x ∈ [-11, 11], z ∈ [-6.3, 6.3] (1 unit ≈ 80 px at 1080p). Keep gameplay inside x ∈ [-9, 9],\\nz ∈ [-4, 4.2], clear of the HUD. All game logic is 2D in this plane, with no physics.\\n\\n**Controls**\\n\\n| Action | DualSense | Mouse + keyboard |\\n|---|---|---|\\n| Move cursor | Right stick (`v = 15 u/s · s^2.2`) | Mouse (absolute); WASD or arrows also move it for keyboard-only play |\\n| Use tool | R2, analog (or hold Cross) | Left button (or hold E) |\\n| Pick tool | Left stick flick, 8 directions, instant (or L1/R1 to cycle) | 1–8, wheel, or click the instrument on the tray |\\n150→| Precision | Hold L2 (×0.35) | Hold Shift (keyboard cursor only; the mouse is already precise) |\\n| Cancel, let go | Circle | Right button or Q |\\n| Gift | Triangle | Space |\\n| Chart overlay | Square | Tab |\\n| Rotate held bone | L1/R1 while holding | Wheel while holding |\\n| Defibrillate | L2 + R2 | Both mouse buttons |\\n| Pause | Options (ignored while Create is held: that combination is the hub's) | Esc |\\n\\nThe stick flick is the signature: it must switch tools with no menu and no slowdown.\\n\\n160→**Aim assist (pad and keyboard cursor only; slider in Settings and dev mode).** Within 1.2 u of a valid\\ntarget for the current tool, speed falls by up to 50% and the cursor is pulled toward it at up to\\n3 u/s, only while the stick is moving. While the Scalpel is engaged, sideways error is damped (rail\\nassist). While suturing, the needle creeps along the wound by itself, so the stick only flicks across\\nit. The mouse gets none of this, since it needs none.\\n\\n### 3.3 The instruments\\n\\nThe ring has 8 fixed directions, data-driven per case. Up: Scalpel. Up-right: Forceps. Right: Suture.\\nDown-right: Suction. Down: Laser (Cryoprobe in Case 6). Down-left: Gel. Left: Scanner (Cryoprobe in\\n170→Case 7, where the nodules stay visible). Up-left: IV Push.\\n\\n| Tool | Gesture | Rated on | Misuse |\\n|---|---|---|---|\\n| **Scalpel** | Hold, follow the dashed line in one stroke | Sideways deviation (≤0.25 u is Immaculate) | Cutting healthy tissue makes a small laceration and costs vitals |\\n| **Forceps** | Hold to grab, pull along the object's axis about 1 u, it drops on the tray | Angle error of the pull | Yanking off-axis tears a laceration |\\n| **Suture** | Hold, zigzag across the wound. Each crossing near the advancing needle is a stitch; about 1 per 0.5 u | Evenness of spacing and pace | Sloppy spacing leaves a slow bleed |\\n| **Suction** | Hold over a pool. Analog: harder drains faster, and gurgles louder | None (always Good) | Safe everywhere |\\n| **Laser** | Hold on a target, the heat ring fills in about 1.2 s, release at 80–100% | Release timing | Overheating makes a burn |\\n| **Gel** | Hold and paint until the coverage ring is full. The flow meter refills in seconds | Overspray | Wasted gel |\\n180→| **Scanner** | Hold and sweep. Sonar pings reveal hidden things for 8 s | None | Safe everywhere |\\n| **IV Push** | Auto-moves to the IV port. Hold; vitals rise; release in the green band (+18 at a full dose, 4 s cooldown) | Release timing | Overdose: a spike, then −8 |\\n| **Cryoprobe** (Case 6 on) | Hold on a node until the frost ring closes (1 s), which makes it brittle | Release timing | Frostbite |\\n| **Dressing** (context, auto-selected) | Final close: hold and draw along the closure | Coverage | None |\\n| **Defibrillator** (context) | Code only: hold L2 + R2 to charge (1.2 s), release as the ghost beat crosses centre | Timing | Failure: no recovery |\\n\\nWrong tool on a target: a clink, Bashir's callout, a chain reset, no effect. Every tool must have its\\nown 3D model, motion, sound and particles, and the tray shows its state.\\n\\n### 3.4 Hazards (what tasks are made of)\",\"content_concise\":\"140→Field space: x ∈ [-11, 11], z ∈ [-6.3, 6.3] (1 unit ≈ 80 px at 1080p). Keep gameplay inside x ∈ [-9, 9],\\nz ∈ [-4, 4.2], clear of the HUD. All game logic is 2D in this plane, with no physics.\\n\\n**Controls**\\n\\n| Action | DualSense | Mouse + keyboard |\\n|---|---|---|\\n| Move cursor | Right stick (`v = 15 u/s · s^2.2`) | Mouse (absolute); WASD or arrows also move it for keyboard-only play |\\n| Use tool | R2, analog (or hold Cross) | Left button (or hold E) |\\n| Pick tool | Left stick flick, 8 directions, instant (or L1/R1 to cycle) | 1–8, wheel, or click the instrument on the tray |\\n150→| Precision | Hold L2 (×0.35) | Hold Shift (keyboard cursor only; the mouse is already precise) |\\n| Cancel, let go | Circle | Right button or Q |\\n| Gift | Triangle | Space |\\n| Chart overlay | Square | Tab |\\n| Rotate held bone | L1/R1 while holding | Wheel while holding |\\n| Defibrillate | L2 + R2 | Both mouse buttons |\\n| Pause | Options (ignored while Create is held: that combination is the hub's) | Esc |\\n\\nThe stick flick is the signature: it must switch tools with no menu and no slowdown.\\n\\n160→**Aim assist (pad and keyboard cursor only; slider in Settings and dev mode).** Within 1.2 u of a valid\\ntarget for the current tool, speed falls by up to 50% and the cursor is pulled toward it at up to\\n3 u/s, only while the stick is moving. While the Scalpel is engaged, sideways error is damped (rail\\nassist). While suturing, the needle creeps along the wound by itself, so the stick only flicks across\\nit. The mouse gets none of this, since it needs none.\\n\\n### 3.3 The instruments\\n\\nThe ring has 8 fixed directions, data-driven per case. Up: Scalpel. Up-right: Forceps. Right: Suture.\\nDown-right: Suction. Down: Laser (Cryoprobe in Case 6). Down-left: Gel. Left: Scanner (Cryoprobe in\\n170→Case 7, where the nodules stay visible). Up-left: IV Push.\\n\\n| Tool | Gesture | Rated on | Misuse |\\n|---|---|---|---|\\n| **Scalpel** | Hold, follow the dashed line in one stroke | Sideways deviation (≤0.25 u is Immaculate) | Cutting healthy tissue makes a small laceration and costs vitals |\\n| **Forceps** | Hold to grab, pull along the object's axis about 1 u, it drops on the tray | Angle error of the pull | Yanking off-axis tears a laceration |\\n| **Suture** | Hold, zigzag across the wound. Each crossing near the advancing needle is a stitch; about 1 per 0.5 u | Evenness of spacing and pace | Sloppy spacing leaves a slow bleed |\\n| **Suction** | Hold over a pool. Analog: harder drains faster, and gurgles louder | None (always Good) | Safe everywhere |\\n| **Laser** | Hold on a target, the heat ring fills in about 1.2 s, release at 80–100% | Release timing | Overheating makes a burn |\\n| **Gel** | Hold and paint until the coverage ring is full. The flow meter refills in seconds | Overspray | Wasted gel |\\n180→| **Scanner** | Hold and sweep. Sonar pings reveal hidden things for 8 s | None | Safe everywhere |\\n| **IV Push** | Auto-moves to the IV port. Hold; vitals rise; release in the green band (+18 at a full dose, 4 s cooldown) | Release timing | Overdose: a spike, then −8 |\\n| **Cryoprobe** (Case 6 on) | Hold on a node until the frost ring closes (1 s), which makes it brittle | Release timing | Frostbite |\\n| **Dressing** (context, auto-selected) | Final close: hold and draw along the closure | Coverage | None |\\n| **Defibrillator** (context) | Code only: hold L2 + R2 to charge (1.2 s), release as the ghost beat crosses centre | Timing | Failure: no recovery |\\n\\nWrong tool on a target: a clink, Bashir's callout, a chain reset, no effect. Every tool must have its\\nown 3D model, motion, sound and particles, and the tray shows its state.\\n\\n### 3.4 Hazards (what tasks are made of)\",\"absolute_path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224015__x42677a/work/PLAN.md\",\"offset\":140,\"limit\":50,\"raw_output\":\"Field space: x ∈ [-11, 11], z ∈ [-6.3, 6.3] (1 unit ≈ 80 px at 1080p). Keep gameplay inside x ∈ [-9, 9],\\nz ∈ [-4, 4.2], clear of the HUD. All game logic is 2D in this plane, with no physics.\\n\\n**Controls**\\n\\n| Action | DualSense | Mouse + keyboard |\\n|---|---|---|\\n| Move cursor | Right stick (`v = 15 u/s · s^2.2`) | Mouse (absolute); WASD or arrows also move it for keyboard-only play |\\n| Use tool | R2, analog (or hold Cross) | Left button (or hold E) |\\n| Pick tool | Left stick flick, 8 directions, instant (or L1/R1 to cycle) | 1–8, wheel, or click the instrument on the tray |\\n| Precision | Hold L2 (×0.35) | Hold Shift (keyboard cursor only; the mouse is already precise) |\\n| Cancel, let go | Circle | Right button or Q |\\n| Gift | Triangle | Space |\\n| Chart overlay | Square | Tab |\\n| Rotate held bone | L1/R1 while holding | Wheel while holding |\\n| Defibrillate | L2 + R2 | Both mouse buttons |\\n| Pause | Options (ignored while Create is held: that combination is the hub's) | Esc |\\n\\nThe stick flick is the signature: it must switch tools with no menu and no slowdown.\\n\\n**Aim assist (pad and keyboard cursor only; slider in Settings and dev mode).** Within 1.2 u of a valid\\ntarget for the current tool, speed falls by up to 50% and the cursor is pulled toward it at up to\\n3 u/s, only while the stick is moving. While the Scalpel is engaged, sideways error is damped (rail\\nassist). While suturing, the needle creeps along the wound by itself, so the stick only flicks across\\nit. The mouse gets none of this, since it needs none.\\n\\n### 3.3 The instruments\\n\\nThe ring has 8 fixed directions, data-driven per case. Up: Scalpel. Up-right: Forceps. Right: Suture.\\nDown-right: Suction. Down: Laser (Cryoprobe in Case 6). Down-left: Gel. Left: Scanner (Cryoprobe in\\nCase 7, where the nodules stay visible). Up-left: IV Push.\\n\\n| Tool | Gesture | Rated on | Misuse |\\n|---|---|---|---|\\n| **Scalpel** | Hold, follow the dashed line in one stroke | Sideways deviation (≤0.25 u is Immaculate) | Cutting healthy tissue makes a small laceration and costs vitals |\\n| **Forceps** | Hold to grab, pull along the object's axis about 1 u, it drops on the tray | Angle error of the pull | Yanking off-axis tears a laceration |\\n| **Suture** | Hold, zigzag across the wound. Each crossing near the advancing needle is a stitch; about 1 per 0.5 u | Evenness of spacing and pace | Sloppy spacing leaves a slow bleed |\\n| **Suction** | Hold over a pool. Analog: harder drains faster, and gurgles louder | None (always Good) | Safe everywhere |\\n| **Laser** | Hold on a target, the heat ring fills in about 1.2 s, release at 80–100% | Release timing | Overheating makes a burn |\\n| **Gel** | Hold and paint until the coverage ring is full. The flow meter refills in seconds | Overspray | Wasted gel |\\n| **Scanner** | Hold and sweep. Sonar pings reveal hidden things for 8 s | None | Safe everywhere |\\n| **IV Push** | Auto-moves to the IV port. Hold; vitals rise; release in the green band (+18 at a full dose, 4 s cooldown) | Release timing | Overdose: a spike, then −8 |\\n| **Cryoprobe** (Case 6 on) | Hold on a node until the frost ring closes (1 s), which makes it brittle | Release timing | Frostbite |\\n| **Dressing** (context, auto-selected) | Final close: hold and draw along the closure | Coverage | None |\\n| **Defibrillator** (context) | Code only: hold L2 + R2 to charge (1.2 s), release as the ghost beat crosses centre | Timing | Failure: no recovery |\\n\\nWrong tool on a target: a clink, Bashir's callout, a chain reset, no effect. Every tool must have its\\nown 3D model, motion, sound and particles, and the tray shows its state.\\n\\n### 3.4 Hazards (what tasks are made of)\\n\",\"total_lines\":817}}","is_error":false},{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-c769c682-a789-4787-9810-c45d3605e53b-16","content":"{\"type\":\"ReadFile\",\"FileContent\":{\"content\":\"200→    n = (n ^ (n >> 13)).wrapping_mul(1274126177);\\n    (n as u32 & 0xffff) as f32 / 65535.0\\n}\\n\\nfn instruments(scene: &mut Scene, op: &SurgeryFrame) {\\n    let steel = rs::srgb(186, 196, 204);\\n    let grip = rs::srgb(40, 78, 86);\\n    for (i, c) in op.cursors.iter().enumerate() {\\n        if !c.active && op.mode == 3 && i > 0 {\\n            continue;\\n210→        }\\n        if op.mode != 3 && op.mode != 6 && op.mode != 8 && i > 0 {\\n            continue;\\n        }\\n        let show = c.active || i == 0;\\n        if !show && op.mode != 0 {\\n            continue;\\n        }\\n        if op.mode == 0 {\\n            break;\\n220→        }\\n        let y = 0.55 + if c.tool == op.cursors[0].tool { 0.12 } else { 0.0 };\\n        let origin = Vec3::new(c.x, y, c.z);\\n        let tint = Vec3::new(c.color[0], c.color[1], c.color[2]);\\n        tool_mesh(scene, c.tool, origin, steel.lerp(tint, 0.25), grip, 40 + i as u32);\\n    }\\n    if op.mode == 3 || op.mode == 0 || op.mode == 6 {\\n        for t in 0..8 {\\n            let x = -3.5 + t as f32 * 1.0;\\n            let z = 5.4;\\n230→            let lift = op.cursors.first().map(|c| c.tool == t as u8).unwrap_or(false);\\n            let y = if lift { 0.42 } else { 0.22 };\\n            tool_mesh(scene, t as u8, Vec3::new(x, y, z), steel, grip, 20 + t as u32);\\n        }\\n    }\\n}\\n\\nfn tool_mesh(scene: &mut Scene, tool: u8, at: Vec3, steel: Vec3, grip: Vec3, group: u32) {\\n    let tip = match tool {\\n        FORCEPS => Vec3::new(0.18, 0.05, 0.34),\\n240→        LASER | CRYO => Vec3::new(0.0, 0.08, 0.42),\\n        DEFIB => Vec3::new(0.22, 0.02, 0.1),\\n        _ => Vec3::new(0.0, 0.02, 0.38),\\n    };\\n    let mut a = SdfInstance::capsule(at, at + tip, 0.035, steel);\\n    a.style = Style::Lit;\\n    a.group = group;\\n    scene.sdfs.push(a);\\n    let mut b = SdfInstance::capsule(at, at + Vec3::new(-0.05, 0.02, -0.28), 0.045, grip);\\n    b.style = Style::Lit;\\n250→    b.group = group;\\n    scene.sdfs.push(b);\\n    if tool == DEFIB {\\n        let mut pad = SdfInstance::capsule(at + Vec3::new(0.16, 0.04, 0.12), at + Vec3::new(-0.16, 0.04, 0.12), 0.06, steel);\\n        pad.style = Style::Lit;\\n        pad.group = group;\\n        scene.sdfs.push(pad);\\n    }\\n}\\n\\n260→fn hazards(scene: &mut Scene, op: &SurgeryFrame) {\\n    let parasite = rs::srgb(58, 26, 96);\\n    let core = rs::srgb(36, 18, 66);\\n    let eye = rs::srgb(255, 210, 70);\\n    let sac = rs::srgb(120, 255, 170);\\n    let ember = rs::srgb(255, 120, 40);\\n    for h in &op.hazards {\\n        if !h.alive || h.hidden && h.kind != K_FOREIGN {\\n            continue;\\n        }\\n270→        let p = Vec3::new(h.x, 0.35 + h.work * 0.05, h.z);\\n        match h.kind {\\n            K_SAC => {\\n                let mut s = SdfInstance::sphere(p, h.radius.max(0.18) * (0.7 + h.aux.min(1.2) * 0.4), sac);\\n                s.emissive = 0.75;\\n                s.style = Style::Unlit;\\n                s.group = 80 + (h.id % 40);\\n                scene.sdfs.push(s);\\n            }\\n            K_EYE => {\\n280→                let mut s = SdfInstance::sphere(p + Vec3::Y * 0.1, 0.16, eye);\\n                s.emissive = 1.6;\\n                s.style = Style::Unlit;\\n                s.group = 120;\\n                scene.sdfs.push(s);\\n                let mut body = SdfInstance::sphere(p, 0.28, parasite);\\n                body.style = Style::Cel;\\n                body.group = 121;\\n                scene.sdfs.push(body);\\n            }\\n290→            K_POLYP | K_NODULE | K_TUMOR | K_TENDRIL => {\\n                let mut s = SdfInstance::sphere(p, h.radius.max(0.16), parasite);\\n                s.style = Style::Cel;\\n                s.group = 140 + (h.id % 30);\\n                scene.sdfs.push(s);\\n                let mut c = SdfInstance::sphere(p + Vec3::Y * 0.08, 0.07, core);\\n                c.emissive = 0.4;\\n                c.style = Style::Unlit;\\n                c.group = 170;\\n                scene.sdfs.push(c);\\n300→            }\\n            K_EMBER => {\\n                let mut s = Sd