7-b9e9-4ff2-bafd-0e2849448a30"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_817","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The actual game content does not match the PLAN case table exactly.\n\nCases 2, 5, and 7 require dressing and embers. PLAN table numbering conflicts with content.rs indices.\n\nContent.rs indices 0 through 7 map to First Movement, Salt, Held Note, nodules, sacs, embers, tumor, and libera. The skeptic's references to cases 2, 5, and 7 align with these content IDs.\n\nThe fix targets content case IDs rather than PLAN narrative numbers. PLAN controls map to content cases 5 and 7. The safer approach is a nearest-hazard swap: when the cursor nears an alive hazard requiring CRYO, resolve LASER or SCANNER to CRYO.\n\nA blanket replacement of Laser with Cryo for an entire case would break nodules in case 7, since those require LASER while embers require CRYO. The nearest-hazard swap is therefore necessary.\n\nThe auto-resolve rule for dressings also needs implementation: when the cursor nears a dressing or only dressings remain as alive non-heat work, the tool should resolve to DRESSING.\n\nI will add a `contextual_tool` function in `pav_core` and call it from `product.rs` when assigning the tool into `SurgeonInput`. I may also invoke it inside `ops.rs` hands() so the simulation swaps any incoming laser or scanner command.\n\nThe contextual tool resolver must be idempotent. If the shell already sends CRYO or DRESSING, the simulation should return that tool unchanged rather than double-swapping.\n\nThis matters because tests drive mapping functions and then step the simulator. If the simulation auto-resolves inside hands(), a test could pass even when it sets LASER near an ember.\n\nThe skeptic explicitly requires the shell to call `contextual_tool` and emit tool 8 or 9 directly. The simulation may auto-swap internally, but the shell must perform the swap itself. I am now drafting a public `octant` helper in the surgery map module.\n\nI am defining three helper functions: `cycle` for ring rotation, `tray_tool` for cursor position mapping, and `contextual_tool` for the main resolver. The resolver will pass through DEFIB unchanged, accept CRYO and DRESSING directly, and scan alive hazards near the cursor to determine the correct tool.\n\nThe reach radius for the contextual resolver is set to each hazard's own radius plus a small margin. Any alive non-heat hazard within that distance counts as \"near.\" If a dressing is present, the tool must resolve to DRESSING regardless of which ring tool the player holds. This means any ring tool near a dressing should auto-resolve to DRESSING.\n\nAuto-resolving every tool to DRESSING whenever the cursor is near a dressing would prevent using other tools on nearby hazards like IVs. The rule should instead apply only when the cursor is within the dressing's own radius.\n\nA global auto-resolve to DRESSING whenever only dressings remain would steal the tool before the player aims. Case 2_B still contains an alive IV, so the resolver must not blanket-switch to dressing in that phase.\n\nThe contextual resolver will use the nearest alive hazard within a selection radius. If that hazard requires CRYO and the ring tool is LASER or SCANNER, it returns CRYO. If the nearest hazard requires DRESSING, it returns DRESSING. The selection radius is 1.2 units to match the aim assist.\n\nThe resolver will use each hazard's own radius for the near test. A dressing at radius 1.1 and an ember at 0.5 are both covered. When only dressings remain as alive non-heat work, the tool auto-resolves to DRESSING even if the cursor is not yet on a dressing. This equips the tool before the player reaches it. The implementation of `contextual_tool` is now being drafted.\n\nThe implementation clamps the ring index to 7 when it is not already CRYO, DRESSING, or DEFIB. It then gathers all alive non-heat hazards and checks whether every remaining work item is a dressing; if so, the tool resolves to DRESSING. Otherwise it iterates through those hazards and selects the nearest one within a reach radius of its own radius plus 0.2 units.\n\nThe resolver now returns the nearest hazard's tool when it is DRESSING. If the nearest hazard requires CRYO and the ring tool is LASER, SCANNER, or CRYO, it returns CRYO. Explicitly selected tools—CRYO, DRESSING, or DEFIB—pass through unchanged. All other ring values are clamped to 7.\n\nThe resolver correctly leaves laser unchanged when the cursor is not near an ember. It swaps to cryo only when the nearest alive hazard still requires cryo, such as a stage 0 ember. Once that ember advances to stage 1 and becomes scalpel, the tool stays laser because nodules require laser, and the test must switch the ring to scalpel via octant. PLAN specifies scanner direction for case 7 and laser direction for case 6.\n\nThe shell lacks hazard positions. It only receives a SurgeryFrame from the previous pump. I must check whether that frame exposes tool, position, radius, alive status, and kind for each hazard.\n\nI cannot rely on internal auto-swapping in ops.rs. The skeptic requires product.rs to emit raw ring values 0 through 7 without any simulation-side tool conversion.\n\nThe simulation's `hands()` must call the shared contextual resolver so it can emit tool 8 or 9. Otherwise `product.rs` would still store raw ring values 0 through 7 and emit them unchanged.\n\nThe shell cannot access simulation hazards directly. The cleanest fix is to read the previous frame's hazard list after compose and post-process each surgeon's tool with contextual_tool. However, stick aim is a velocity vector, not a world position, so it cannot be used as the cursor coordinate for the near-hazard test.\n\nThe shell cannot know the cursor world position for stick input at compose time, so the authoritative contextual swap must happen in ops.rs hands() where surgeon coordinates, ring tool, and hazards are all available. The shell can still handle mouse absolute aims because hit is a world point. Tests using AIM_ABSOLUTE set x and z directly.\n\nThe test should drive the same ring-selection functions the shell uses, then call `contextual_tool` directly to obtain the final tool before stepping. This lets the simulation swap inside `hands()` while keeping the test’s own assertions on the resolved tool.\n\nproduct.rs should also call contextual_tool when it knows the aim point so the UI status shows Cryoprobe. Otherwise tools_from_hands still writes only raw ring values 0 through 7 into self.tool.\n\nThe helper functions will be moved into pav_core and exported. product.rs will use cycle() and octant() for ring selection, tray_tool() for tray clicks, and contextual_tool() when the aim is absolute. ops.rs hands() will always run contextual_tool on the world cursor position before applying the tool.\n\nThe shell will also emit the resolved tool directly, not just raw ring values. Pad input cannot supply a world cursor position at compose time, so the simulation must handle that swap internally. I will add clear comments explaining this split.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-712bb174-9ad2-4523-9bf8-e730a6dc85ea-23","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224015__x42677a/work/Hands of Harbor: Second Opinion-Trauma Center: Second Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-224015/engine/crates/pav_core/src/games/surgery/frame.rs","limit":120}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-712bb174-9ad2-4523-9bf8-e730a6dc85ea-24","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224015__x42677a/work/Hands of Harbor: Second Opinion-Trauma Center: Second Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-224015/engine/crates/pav_core/src/games/surgery/hazard.rs","offset":300,"limit":80}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-712bb174-9ad2-4523-9bf8-e730a6dc85ea-25","name":"grep","input":{"pattern":"pav_core::games::surgery","glob":"**/pav_app/**/*.rs"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-712bb174-9ad2-4523-9bf8-e730a6dc85ea-26","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224015__x42677a/work/Hands of Harbor: Second Opinion-Trauma Center: Second Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-224015/engine/crates/pav_core/src/games/surgery/mod.rs","offset":900,"limit":90}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":4391,"output_tokens":3837,"cache_read_input_tokens":66176,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa38-de6f-7dc0-ae0d-e0f717ed75f2","uuid":"54791595-4706-4ada-8957-6425cde3e9eb"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-712bb174-9ad2-4523-9bf8-e730a6dc85ea-23","content":"{\"type\":\"ReadFile\",\"FileContent\":{\"content\":\"1→//! What one draw of the operation needs. Built fresh each frame; not part of the saved state.\\n\\nuse glam::Vec3;\\n\\nuse super::kinds::TITLE;\\n\\n#[derive(Clone, Copy, Debug)]\\npub struct CameraShot {\\n    pub tilt: f32,\\n10→    pub yaw: f32,\\n    pub distance: f32,\\n    pub fov_deg: f32,\\n    pub target: Vec3,\\n    pub follow_lag: f32,\\n    pub height_offset: f32,\\n}\\n\\nimpl Default for CameraShot {\\n    fn default() -> Self {\\n20→        Self {\\n            tilt: 73.0,\\n            yaw: 0.0,\\n            distance: 19.9,\\n            fov_deg: 36.0,\\n            target: Vec3::new(0.0, 0.0, 0.2),\\n            follow_lag: 0.0,\\n            height_offset: 0.0,\\n        }\\n    }\\n30→}\\n\\n#[derive(Clone, Copy, Debug)]\\npub struct HazardView {\\n    pub id: u32,\\n    pub kind: u8,\\n    pub x: f32,\\n    pub z: f32,\\n    pub radius: f32,\\n    pub work: f32,\\n40→    pub need: f32,\\n    pub alive: bool,\\n    pub hidden: bool,\\n    pub stage: u8,\\n    pub stages: u8,\\n    pub axis: f32,\\n    pub aux: f32,\\n    pub bits: u8,\\n    pub tool: u8,\\n    pub grabbed: bool,\\n50→}\\n\\n#[derive(Clone, Copy, Debug)]\\npub struct CursorView {\\n    pub active: bool,\\n    pub x: f32,\\n    pub z: f32,\\n    pub tool: u8,\\n    pub score: i32,\\n    pub chain: u32,\\n60→    pub meter: f32,\\n    pub color: [f32; 3],\\n}\\n\\n#[derive(Clone, Copy, Debug)]\\npub struct PopupView {\\n    pub rating: u8,\\n    pub life: f32,\\n    pub x: f32,\\n    pub z: f32,\\n70→}\\n\\n/// Draw-only snapshot. The view reads this and does not consult the sim.\\n#[derive(Clone, Debug)]\\npub struct SurgeryFrame {\\n    pub title: &'static str,\\n    pub mode: u8,\\n    pub case_id: i8,\\n    pub op_name: String,\\n    pub patient: String,\\n80→    pub plate: u8,\\n    pub plate_next: u8,\\n    pub plate_blend: f32,\\n    pub vitals: f32,\\n    pub bpm: f32,\\n    pub phase: f32,\\n    pub flat: bool,\\n    pub on_beat: bool,\\n    pub timer: f32,\\n    pub elapsed: f32,\\n90→    pub score: i32,\\n    pub par: i32,\\n    pub rank: u8,\\n    pub chain: u32,\\n    pub mistakes: u32,\\n    pub code_t: f32,\\n    pub codes_left: u8,\\n    pub shocks_done: u8,\\n    pub shocks_need: u8,\\n    pub fever: f32,\\n100→    pub heat_on: bool,\\n    pub heat_angle: f32,\\n    pub strain: u8,\\n    pub gift_hush: f32,\\n    pub gift_echo: f32,\\n    pub gift_duet: f32,\\n    pub gifts_unlocked: u8,\\n    pub banner: String,\\n    pub callout: String,\\n    pub story_who: String,\\n110→    pub story_line: String,\\n    pub difficulty: u8,\\n    pub players: u8,\\n    pub music: f32,\\n    pub effects: f32,\\n    pub voices: f32,\\n    pub camera: CameraShot,\\n    pub hazards: Vec<HazardView>,\\n    pub cursors: [CursorView; 4],\\n    pub echo_x: f32,\\n120→    pub echo_z: f32,\",\"content_concise\":\"1→//! What one draw of the operation needs. Built fresh each frame; not part of the saved state.\\n\\nuse glam::Vec3;\\n\\nuse super::kinds::TITLE;\\n\\n#[derive(Clone, Copy, Debug)]\\npub struct CameraShot {\\n    pub tilt: f32,\\n10→    pub yaw: f32,\\n    pub distance: f32,\\n    pub fov_deg: f32,\\n    pub target: Vec3,\\n    pub follow_lag: f32,\\n    pub height_offset: f32,\\n}\\n\\nimpl Default for CameraShot {\\n    fn default() -> Self {\\n20→        Self {\\n            tilt: 73.0,\\n            yaw: 0.0,\\n            distance: 19.9,\\n            fov_deg: 36.0,\\n            target: Vec3::new(0.0, 0.0, 0.2),\\n            follow_lag: 0.0,\\n            height_offset: 0.0,\\n        }\\n    }\\n30→}\\n\\n#[derive(Clone, Copy, Debug)]\\npub struct HazardView {\\n    pub id: u32,\\n    pub kind: u8,\\n    pub x: f32,\\n    pub z: f32,\\n    pub radius: f32,\\n    pub work: f32,\\n40→    pub need: f32,\\n    pub alive: bool,\\n    pub hidden: bool,\\n    pub stage: u8,\\n    pub stages: u8,\\n    pub axis: f32,\\n    pub aux: f32,\\n    pub bits: u8,\\n    pub tool: u8,\\n    pub grabbed: bool,\\n50→}\\n\\n#[derive(Clone, Copy, Debug)]\\npub struct CursorView {\\n    pub active: bool,\\n    pub x: f32,\\n    pub z: f32,\\n    pub tool: u8,\\n    pub score: i32,\\n    pub chain: u32,\\n60→    pub meter: f32,\\n    pub color: [f32; 3],\\n}\\n\\n#[derive(Clone, Copy, Debug)]\\npub struct PopupView {\\n    pub rating: u8,\\n    pub life: f32,\\n    pub x: f32,\\n    pub z: f32,\\n70→}\\n\\n/// Draw-only snapshot. The view reads this and does not consult the sim.\\n#[derive(Clone, Debug)]\\npub struct SurgeryFrame {\\n    pub title: &'static str,\\n    pub mode: u8,\\n    pub case_id: i8,\\n    pub op_name: String,\\n    pub patient: String,\\n80→    pub plate: u8,\\n    pub plate_next: u8,\\n    pub plate_blend: f32,\\n    pub vitals: f32,\\n    pub bpm: f32,\\n    pub phase: f32,\\n    pub flat: bool,\\n    pub on_beat: bool,\\n    pub timer: f32,\\n    pub elapsed: f32,\\n90→    pub score: i32,\\n    pub par: i32,\\n    pub rank: u8,\\n    pub chain: u32,\\n    pub mistakes: u32,\\n    pub code_t: f32,\\n    pub codes_left: u8,\\n    pub shocks_done: u8,\\n    pub shocks_need: u8,\\n    pub fever: f32,\\n100→    pub heat_on: bool,\\n    pub heat_angle: f32,\\n    pub strain: u8,\\n    pub gift_hush: f32,\\n    pub gift_echo: f32,\\n    pub gift_duet: f32,\\n    pub gifts_unlocked: u8,\\n    pub banner: String,\\n    pub callout: String,\\n    pub story_who: String,\\n110→    pub story_line: String,\\n    pub difficulty: u8,\\n    pub players: u8,\\n    pub music: f32,\\n    pub effects: f32,\\n    pub voices: f32,\\n    pub camera: CameraShot,\\n    pub hazards: Vec<HazardView>,\\n    pub cursors: [CursorView; 4],\\n    pub echo_x: f32,\\n120→    pub echo_z: f32,\",\"absolute_path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224015__x42677a/work/Hands of Harbor: Second Opinion-Trauma Center: Second Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-224015/engine/crates/pav_core/src/games/surgery/frame.rs\",\"offset\":null,\"limit\":120,\"raw_output\":\"//! What one draw of the operation needs. Built fresh each frame; not part of the saved state.\\n\\nuse glam::Vec3;\\n\\nuse super::kinds::TITLE;\\n\\n#[derive(Clone, Copy, Debug)]\\npub struct CameraShot {\\n    pub tilt: f32,\\n    pub yaw: f32,\\n    pub distance: f32,\\n    pub fov_deg: f32,\\n    pub target: Vec3,\\n    pub follow_lag: f32,\\n    pub height_offset: f32,\\n}\\n\\nimpl Default for CameraShot {\\n    fn default() -> Self {\\n        Self {\\n            tilt: 73.0,\\n            yaw: 0.0,\\n            distance: 19.9,\\n            fov_deg: 36.0,\\n            target: Vec3::new(0.0, 0.0, 0.2),\\n            follow_lag: 0.0,\\n            height_offset: 0.0,\\n        }\\n    }\\n}\\n\\n#[derive(Clone, Copy, Debug)]\\npub struct HazardView {\\n    pub id: u32,\\n    pub kind: u8,\\n    pub x: f32,\\n    pub z: f32,\\n    pub radius: f32,\\n    pub work: f32,\\n    pub need: f32,\\n    pub alive: bool,\\n    pub hidden: bool,\\n    pub stage: u8,\\n    pub stages: u8,\\n    pub axis: f32,\\n    pub aux: f32,\\n    pub bits: u8,\\n    pub tool: u8,\\n    pub grabbed: bool,\\n}\\n\\n#[derive(Clone, Copy, Debug)]\\npub struct CursorView {\\n    pub active: bool,\\n    pub x: f32,\\n    pub z: f32,\\n    pub tool: u8,\\n    pub score: i32,\\n    pub chain: u32,\\n    pub meter: f32,\\n    pub color: [f32; 3],\\n}\\n\\n#[derive(Clone, Copy, Debug)]\\npub struct PopupView {\\n    pub rating: u8,\\n    pub life: f32,\\n    pub x: f32,\\n    pub z: f32,\\n}\\n\\n/// Draw-only snapshot. The view reads this and does not consult the sim.\\n#[derive(Clone, Debug)]\\npub struct SurgeryFrame {\\n    pub title: &'static str,\\n    pub mode: u8,\\n    pub case_id: i8,\\n    pub op_name: String,\\n    pub patient: String,\\n    pub plate: u8,\\n    pub plate_next: u8,\\n    pub plate_blend: f32,\\n    pub vitals: f32,\\n    pub bpm: f32,\\n    pub phase: f32,\\n    pub flat: bool,\\n    pub on_beat: bool,\\n    pub timer: f32,\\n    pub elapsed: f32,\\n    pub score: i32,\\n    pub par: i32,\\n    pub rank: u8,\\n    pub chain: u32,\\n    pub mistakes: u32,\\n    pub code_t: f32,\\n    pub codes_left: u8,\\n    pub shocks_done: u8,\\n    pub shocks_need: u8,\\n    pub fever: f32,\\n    pub heat_on: bool,\\n    pub heat_angle: f32,\\n    pub strain: u8,\\n    pub gift_hush: f32,\\n    pub gift_echo: f32,\\n    pub gift_duet: f32,\\n    pub gifts_unlocked: u8,\\n    pub banner: String,\\n    pub callout: String,\\n    pub story_who: String,\\n    pub story_line: String,\\n    pub difficulty: u8,\\n    pub players: u8,\\n    pub music: f32,\\n    pub effects: f32,\\n    pub voices: f32,\\n    pub camera: CameraShot,\\n    pub hazards: Vec<HazardView>,\\n    pub cursors: [CursorView; 4],\\n    pub echo_x: f32,\\n    pub echo_z: f32,\\n\",\"total_lines\":206}}","is_error":false},{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-712bb174-9ad2-4523-9bf8-e730a6dc85ea-24","content":"{\"type\":\"ReadFile\",\"FileContent\":{\"content\":\"300→    let p = pressure.clamp(0.15, 1.0) * power.max(0.2);\\n\\n    if tool == SCANNER && use_held && d < h.radius + 0.35 {\\n        hit.engaged = true;\\n        hit.cue = CUE_PING;\\n        h.revealed = 8.0;\\n        h.hidden = false;\\n        if h.kind == K_FOREIGN || h.kind == K_NODULE {\\n            return hit;\\n        }\\n310→    }\\n\\n    if h.hidden && h.revealed <= 0.0 {\\n        return hit;\\n    }\\n\\n    match h.kind {\\n        K_INCISION | K_TETHER => {\\n            if tool != SCALPEL || !use_held {\\n                return hit;\\n320→            }\\n            let (along, side) = side_of(h, x, z);\\n            if side.abs() < 0.5 && along >= h.work - 0.15 && along <= h.work + 0.55 {\\n                hit.engaged = true;\\n                hit.cue = CUE_SLICE;\\n                h.quality += side.abs() * dt;\\n                h.work = h.work.max(along);\\n                if side.abs() > 0.62 {\\n                    hit.misuse = 1;\\n                }\\n330→            }\\n            if h.work >= h.need {\\n                finish(h, &mut hit, h.quality / h.need.max(0.3), strict);\\n            }\\n        }\\n        K_TUMOR if h.stage == 0 => {\\n            if tool != SCALPEL || !use_held {\\n                return hit;\\n            }\\n            let ang = h.work;\\n340→            let px = h.x + ang.cos() * (h.radius * 0.75);\\n            let pz = h.z + ang.sin() * (h.radius * 0.75);\\n            let dd = ((x - px).powi(2) + (z - pz).powi(2)).sqrt();\\n            if dd < 0.48 {\\n                hit.engaged = true;\\n                hit.cue = CUE_SLICE;\\n                h.work += dt * 2.4 * p;\\n                h.quality += dd * dt;\\n            }\\n            if h.work >= std::f32::consts::TAU {\\n350→                finish(h, &mut hit, h.quality / 2.0, strict);\\n            }\\n        }\\n        K_FOREIGN | K_TENDRIL | K_TUMOR if h.tool == FORCEPS => {\\n            forceps(h, x, z, tool, use_held, dt, &mut hit, strict, diastole);\\n        }\\n        K_NODULE if h.stage >= 1 => {\\n            forceps(h, x, z, tool, use_held, dt, &mut hit, strict, true);\\n        }\\n        K_EYE if h.stage >= 2 => {\\n360→            forceps(h, x, z, tool, use_held, dt, &mut hit, strict, true);\\n        }\\n        K_EMBER if h.stage >= 2 => {\\n            forceps(h, x, z, tool, use_held, dt, &mut hit, strict, true);\\n        }\\n        // The guard binds the whole or-pattern, so a stage check cannot share this arm\\n        // with wounds that suture on stage 0.\\n        K_LACERATION | K_BLEEDER => {\\n            suture(h, x, z, tool, use_held, dt, &mut hit, strict);\\n        }\\n370→        K_BONE if h.stage >= 1 => {\\n            suture(h, x, z, tool, use_held, dt, &mut hit, strict);\\n        }\\n        K_EYE if h.stage < 2 => {\\n            if tool == SCALPEL && use_held 