{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_821","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Checking how the games module is exported so tests can access `pav_core::games::surgery::contextual_tool`.\n\nAdding `pub use` for the new map functions in mod.rs. Designing a `ToolSite` trait so `contextual_tool` can accept both `Hazard` and `HazardView`.\n\nRejected a tuple slice for `contextual_tool` as too ugly. A `ToolSite` struct would require allocating per surgeon each tick, which is undesirable in the simulation loop. A trait-based approach avoids that allocation.\n\nSettled on a `ToolSite` trait with methods for alive, kind, tool, xz, and radius. A `Site` struct will hold the data. `Hazard` and `HazardView` will implement it. The function signature will use `&[impl ToolSite]`.\n\nThe generic `contextual_tool` signature will use `pub fn contextual_tool<T: ToolSite>(...)` so it accepts both `&[Hazard]` and `&[HazardView]`.\n\nThe hub draw fix removes the full plate when quiet. This avoids a software-GPU stall but leaves the scene blank. The fix is to build a much smaller plate while still drawing instruments, hazards, and cursors.\n\nThe quiet plate will use 48 by 28 vertices instead of the full 420 by 240. Instruments and hazards are cheap SDF shapes, so they remain visible. The `emit` function will pass these smaller dimensions to `plate()` when `op.quiet` is true.\n\nPaper cards are extra meshes and will be skipped when quiet to keep the scene cheap. The hub comment in apply_look needs updating because the plate is no longer skipped. The product.rs comment about skipping the operative mesh should also be revised, since a coarse plate is now drawn instead of omitting it entirely.\n\nChecking PLAN.md for deviations and verification sections to determine what tests to re-run. Verifying whether `emit` is already tested. The coarse plate's vertex painting loop is O(nx*nz*hazards), so 16,000 iterations are acceptable.\n\nThe existing plate normal delta of 0.11 was tuned for the dense grid spacing. For the coarse quiet plate, cell spacing is roughly 0.47, so the finite difference must be scaled by the actual cell size to keep normals accurate.\n\nThe dense grid normal formula will stay unchanged to avoid altering solo screenshots. Only the quiet path will use a cell-scaled divisor. No render test is required for the hub draw fix because the suite does not render. The verification plan may include a visual check instead.\n\nThe test suite runs `cargo test` on `pav_core` surgery tests, so a new `#[test]` in `surgery.rs` will be picked up automatically. The existing skill1 test loops seeds, meaning the total count rises from 14 to 15.\n\nThe contextual tool swap must not retune bot behavior. Bots explicitly set CRYO or DRESSING, and the function preserves those values unchanged.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-95a5039a-96c0-4140-98c8-37d34a7d7398-40","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224015__x42677a/work/Hands of Harbor: Second Opinion-Trauma Center: Second Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-224015/engine/crates/pav_core/src/games/surgery/bot.rs","limit":120}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-95a5039a-96c0-4140-98c8-37d34a7d7398-41","name":"grep","input":{"pattern":"## Deviations|## Verification","glob":"**/PLAN.md"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-95a5039a-96c0-4140-98c8-37d34a7d7398-42","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224015__x42677a/work/Hands of Harbor: Second Opinion-Trauma Center: Second Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-224015/engine/crates/pav_core/src/games/mod.rs","limit":40}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":5617,"output_tokens":1932,"cache_read_input_tokens":82688,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa38-de6f-7dc0-ae0d-e0f717ed75f2","uuid":"da92bca2-22e0-4eb9-a879-14af1a33e144"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-95a5039a-96c0-4140-98c8-37d34a7d7398-40","content":"{\"type\":\"ReadFile\",\"FileContent\":{\"content\":\"1→//! A stateless good hand. Noise and release timing come from skill, not from `sim.rng`.\\n\\nuse super::content::G_DUET;\\nuse super::hazard::aim_point;\\nuse super::kinds::*;\\nuse super::*;\\nuse crate::input::{surg, SurgeonInput};\\n\\nconst DT: f32 = 1.0 / 60.0;\\n10→\\npub fn decide(game: &Surgery, tick: u64, slot: usize) -> SurgeonInput {\\n    let mut inp = SurgeonInput { active: true, pressure: 1.0, tool: TOOL_KEEP, ..Default::default() };\\n    let skill = game.skill.clamp(0.0, 1.0);\\n    if matches!(game.mode, M_STORY | M_CHART | M_RESULTS) {\\n        inp.held = surg::CONFIRM;\\n        inp.pressed = surg::CONFIRM;\\n        inp.tool = TOOL_KEEP;\\n        return inp;\\n    }\\n20→    if game.mode != M_OP && game.mode != M_ATTRACT {\\n        inp.active = false;\\n        return inp;\\n    }\\n    let me = &game.surgeons[slot.min(3)];\\n    if game.heart.flat {\\n        return defib(game, me, skill, inp);\\n    }\\n    if skill >= 0.5 {\\n        inp.held |= surg::PRECISION;\\n30→    }\\n    if want_gift(game, skill) {\\n        let on = game.heart.on_beat(game.tune.beat_window_ms);\\n        if !on || !me.was_gift {\\n            inp.held |= surg::GIFT;\\n        }\\n    }\\n    let avoid = if slot == 0 { None } else { game.surgeons[0].focus };\\n    let Some(h) = pick(game, avoid) else {\\n        aim_toward(game, me, slot, skill, tick, me.x, me.z, &mut inp);\\n40→        inp.tool = me.tool;\\n        return inp;\\n    };\\n    let mut tool = if h.hidden && h.revealed <= 0.0 { SCANNER } else { h.tool };\\n    if skill < 0.2 {\\n        tool = (tick % 11) as u8;\\n    }\\n    inp.tool = tool;\\n    let side = if (tick / 8) % 2 == 0 { 1.0 } else { -1.0 };\\n    let (mut tx, mut tz) = aim_for(h, tick, side);\\n50→    // A skill of 0 still knew where the wound was, so the easy cases lived.\\n    // Below 0.15 the hand wanders and the case should be lost.\\n    if skill < 0.15 {\\n        tx = (tick as f32 * 0.07).sin() * 3.2;\\n        tz = (tick as f32 * 0.05).cos() * 2.2;\\n    }\\n    if h.kind == K_TENDRIL && !game.heart.diastole() {\\n        tx = h.x;\\n        tz = h.z;\\n    }\\n60→    if me.focus == Some(h.id) && me.focus_t > 2.2 && skill > 0.3 {\\n        let a = me.focus_t * 2.4;\\n        tx += a.cos() * 0.42;\\n        tz += a.sin() * 0.42;\\n    }\\n    aim_toward(game, me, slot, skill, tick, tx, tz, &mut inp);\\n    let dx = tx - me.x;\\n    let dz = tz - me.z;\\n    let dist = (dx * dx + dz * dz).sqrt();\\n    let near = dist < (h.radius + 0.28).max(0.45);\\n70→    let release_at = release_at(skill, h.kind);\\n    let charging = is_charge(h);\\n    let heat = heat_danger(game, me.x, me.z);\\n    let hold = if heat {\\n        false\\n    } else if charging && h.aux >= release_at {\\n        false\\n    } else if h.kind == K_TENDRIL && !game.heart.diastole() {\\n        h.grabbed || dist < h.radius\\n    } else if h.kind == K_BONE && h.stage == 0 && h.aux.abs() >= 12.0 {\\n80→        false\\n    } else if h.grabbed {\\n        true\\n    } else if tool == SCANNER {\\n        dist < h.radius + 0.4\\n    } else if tool == IV {\\n        true\\n    } else {\\n        near || (me.was_use && dist < h.radius + 0.85)\\n    };\\n90→    if h.kind == K_BONE && h.stage == 0 && h.aux > 12.0 {\\n        inp.held |= surg::ROT_L;\\n    } else if h.kind == K_BONE && h.stage == 0 && h.aux < -12.0 {\\n        inp.held |= surg::ROT_R;\\n    }\\n    if hold {\\n        inp.held |= surg::USE;\\n    }\\n    inp\\n}\\n100→\\nfn want_gift(game: &Surgery, skill: f32) -> bool {\\n    if skill < 0.55 || game.heart.flat || game.surgeons[0].meter < 100.0 {\\n        return false;\\n    }\\n    game.pending_gift() != 0\\n}\\n\\nfn defib(game: &Surgery, me: &Surgeon, skill: f32, mut inp: SurgeonInput) -> SurgeonInput {\\n    inp.tool = DEFIB;\\n110→    let on = game.heart.ghost_on_beat(game.tune.beat_window_ms);\\n    let hold = if skill < 0.35 {\\n        me.defib < 1.15\\n    } else if me.defib < 1.15 || !on {\\n        true\\n    } else {\\n        !me.was_defib\\n    };\\n    if hold {\\n        inp.held |= surg::DEFIB;\\n120→    }\",\"content_concise\":\"1→//! A stateless good hand. Noise and release timing come from skill, not from `sim.rng`.\\n\\nuse super::content::G_DUET;\\nuse super::hazard::aim_point;\\nuse super::kinds::*;\\nuse super::*;\\nuse crate::input::{surg, SurgeonInput};\\n\\nconst DT: f32 = 1.0 / 60.0;\\n10→\\npub fn decide(game: &Surgery, tick: u64, slot: usize) -> SurgeonInput {\\n    let mut inp = SurgeonInput { active: true, pressure: 1.0, tool: TOOL_KEEP, ..Default::default() };\\n    let skill = game.skill.clamp(0.0, 1.0);\\n    if matches!(game.mode, M_STORY | M_CHART | M_RESULTS) {\\n        inp.held = surg::CONFIRM;\\n        inp.pressed = surg::CONFIRM;\\n        inp.tool = TOOL_KEEP;\\n        return inp;\\n    }\\n20→    if game.mode != M_OP && game.mode != M_ATTRACT {\\n        inp.active = false;\\n        return inp;\\n    }\\n    let me = &game.surgeons[slot.min(3)];\\n    if game.heart.flat {\\n        return defib(game, me, skill, inp);\\n    }\\n    if skill >= 0.5 {\\n        inp.held |= surg::PRECISION;\\n30→    }\\n    if want_gift(game, skill) {\\n        let on = game.heart.on_beat(game.tune.beat_window_ms);\\n        if !on || !me.was_gift {\\n            inp.held |= surg::GIFT;\\n        }\\n    }\\n    let avoid = if slot == 0 { None } else { game.surgeons[0].focus };\\n    let Some(h) = pick(game, avoid) else {\\n        aim_toward(game, me, slot, skill, tick, me.x, me.z, &mut inp);\\n40→        inp.tool = me.tool;\\n        return inp;\\n    };\\n    let mut tool = if h.hidden && h.revealed <= 0.0 { SCANNER } else { h.tool };\\n    if skill < 0.2 {\\n        tool = (tick % 11) as u8;\\n    }\\n    inp.tool = tool;\\n    let side = if (tick / 8) % 2 == 0 { 1.0 } else { -1.0 };\\n    let (mut tx, mut tz) = aim_for(h, tick, side);\\n50→    // A skill of 0 still knew where the wound was, so the easy cases lived.\\n    // Below 0.15 the hand wanders and the case should be lost.\\n    if skill < 0.15 {\\n        tx = (tick as f32 * 0.07).sin() * 3.2;\\n        tz = (tick as f32 * 0.05).cos() * 2.2;\\n    }\\n    if h.kind == K_TENDRIL && !game.heart.diastole() {\\n        tx = h.x;\\n        tz = h.z;\\n    }\\n60→    if me.focus == Some(h.id) && me.focus_t > 2.2 && skill > 0.3 {\\n        let a = me.focus_t * 2.4;\\n        tx += a.cos() * 0.42;\\n        tz += a.sin() * 0.42;\\n    }\\n    aim_toward(game, me, slot, skill, tick, tx, tz, &mut inp);\\n    let dx = tx - me.x;\\n    let dz = tz - me.z;\\n    let dist = (dx * dx + dz * dz).sqrt();\\n    let near = dist < (h.radius + 0.28).max(0.45);\\n70→    let release_at = release_at(skill, h.kind);\\n    let charging = is_charge(h);\\n    let heat = heat_danger(game, me.x, me.z);\\n    let hold = if heat {\\n        false\\n    } else if charging && h.aux >= release_at {\\n        false\\n    } else if h.kind == K_TENDRIL && !game.heart.diastole() {\\n        h.grabbed || dist < h.radius\\n    } else if h.kind == K_BONE && h.stage == 0 && h.aux.abs() >= 12.0 {\\n80→        false\\n    } else if h.grabbed {\\n        true\\n    } else if tool == SCANNER {\\n        dist < h.radius + 0.4\\n    } else if tool == IV {\\n        true\\n    } else {\\n        near || (me.was_use && dist < h.radius + 0.85)\\n    };\\n90→    if h.kind == K_BONE && h.stage == 0 && h.aux > 12.0 {\\n        inp.held |= surg::ROT_L;\\n    } else if h.kind == K_BONE && h.stage == 0 && h.aux < -12.0 {\\n        inp.held |= surg::ROT_R;\\n    }\\n    if hold {\\n        inp.held |= surg::USE;\\n    }\\n    inp\\n}\\n100→\\nfn want_gift(game: &Surgery, skill: f32) -> bool {\\n    if skill < 0.55 || game.heart.flat || game.surgeons[0].meter < 100.0 {\\n        return false;\\n    }\\n    game.pending_gift() != 0\\n}\\n\\nfn defib(game: &Surgery, me: &Surgeon, skill: f32, mut inp: SurgeonInput) -> SurgeonInput {\\n    inp.tool = DEFIB;\\n110→    let on = game.heart.ghost_on_beat(game.tune.beat_window_ms);\\n    let hold = if skill < 0.35 {\\n        me.defib < 1.15\\n    } else if me.defib < 1.15 || !on {\\n        true\\n    } else {\\n        !me.was_defib\\n    };\\n    if hold {\\n        inp.held |= surg::DEFIB;\\n120→    }\",\"absolute_path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224015__x42677a/work/Hands of Harbor: Second Opinion-Trauma Center: Second Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-224015/engine/crates/pav_core/src/games/surgery/bot.rs\",\"offset\":null,\"limit\":120,\"raw_output\":\"//! A stateless good hand. Noise and release timing come from skill, not from `sim.rng`.\\n\\nuse super::content::G_DUET;\\nuse super::hazard::aim_point;\\nuse super::kinds::*;\\nuse super::*;\\nuse crate::input::{surg, SurgeonInput};\\n\\nconst DT: f32 = 1.0 / 60.0;\\n\\npub fn decide(game: &Surgery, tick: u64, slot: usize) -> SurgeonInput {\\n    let mut inp = SurgeonInput { active: true, pressure: 1.0, tool: TOOL_KEEP, ..Default::default() };\\n    let skill = game.skill.clamp(0.0, 1.0);\\n    if matches!(game.mode, M_STORY | M_CHART | M_RESULTS) {\\n        inp.held = surg::CONFIRM;\\n        inp.pressed = surg::CONFIRM;\\n        inp.tool = TOOL_KEEP;\\n        return inp;\\n    }\\n    if game.mode != M_OP && game.mode != M_ATTRACT {\\n        inp.active = false;\\n        return inp;\\n    }\\n    let me = &game.surgeons[slot.min(3)];\\n    if game.heart.flat {\\n        return defib(game, me, skill, inp);\\n    }\\n    if skill >= 0.5 {\\n        inp.held |= surg::PRECISION;\\n    }\\n    if want_gift(game, skill) {\\n        let on = game.heart.on_beat(game.tune.beat_window_ms);\\n        if !on || !me.was_gift {\\n            inp.held |= surg::GIFT;\\n        }\\n    }\\n    let avoid = if slot == 0 { None } else { game.surgeons[0].focus };\\n    let Some(h) = pick(game, avoid) else {\\n        aim_toward(game, me, slot, skill, tick, me.x, me.z, &mut inp);\\n        inp.tool = me.tool;\\n        return inp;\\n    };\\n    let mut tool = if h.hidden && h.revealed <= 0.0 { SCANNER } else { h.tool };\\n    if skill < 0.2 {\\n        tool = (tick % 11) as u8;\\n    }\\n    inp.tool = tool;\\n    let side = if (tick / 8) % 2 == 0 { 1.0 } else { -1.0 };\\n    let (mut tx, mut tz) = aim_for(h, tick, side);\\n    // A skill of 0 still knew where the wound was, so the easy cases lived.\\n    // Below 0.15 the hand wanders and the case should be lost.\\n    if skill < 0.15 {\\n        tx = (tick as f32 * 0.07).sin() * 3.2;\\n        tz = (tick as f32 * 0.05).cos() * 2.2;\\n    }\\n    if h.kind == K_TENDRIL && !game.heart.diastole() {\\n        tx = h.x;\\n        tz = h.z;\\n    }\\n    if me.focus == Some(h.id) && me.focus_t > 2.2 && skill > 0.3 {\\n        let a = me.focus_t * 2.4;\\n        tx += a.cos() * 0.42;\\n        tz += a.sin() * 0.42;\\n    }\\n    aim_toward(game, me, slot, skill, tick, tx, tz, &mut inp);\\n    let dx = tx - me.x;\\n    let dz = tz - me.z;\\n    let dist = (dx * dx + dz * dz).sqrt();\\n    let near = dist < (h.radius + 0.28).max(0.45);\\n    let release_at = release_at(skill, h.kind);\\n    let charging = is_charge(h);\\n    let heat = heat_danger(game, me.x, me.z);\\n    let hold = if heat {\\n        false\\n    } else if charging && h.aux >= release_at {\\n        false\\n    } else if h.kind == K_TENDRIL && !game.heart.diastole() {\\n        h.grabbed || dist < h.radius\\n    } else if h.kind == K_BONE && h.stage == 0 && h.aux.abs() >= 12.0 {\\n        false\\n    } else if h.grabbed {\\n        true\\n    } else if tool == SCANNER {\\n        dist < h.radius + 0.4\\n    } else if tool == IV {\\n        true\\n    } else {\\n        near || (me.was_use && dist < h.radius + 0.85)\\n    };\\n    if h.kind == K_BONE && h.stage == 0 && h.aux > 12.0 {\\n        inp.held |= surg::ROT_L;\\n    } else if h.kind == K_BONE && h.stage == 0 && h.aux < -12.0 {\\n        inp.held |= surg::ROT_R;\\n    }\\n    if hold {\\n        inp.held |= surg::USE;\\n    }\\n    inp\\n}\\n\\nfn want_gift(game: &Surgery, skill: f32) -> bool {\\n    if skill < 0.55 || game.heart.flat || game.surgeons[0].meter < 100.0 {\\n        return false;\\n    }\\n    game.pending_gift() != 0\\n}\\n\\nfn defib(game: &Surgery, me: &Surgeon, skill: f32, mut inp: SurgeonInput) -> SurgeonInput {\\n    inp.tool = DEFIB;\\n    let on = game.heart.ghost_on_beat(game.tune.beat_window_ms);\\n    let hold = if skill < 0.35 {\\n        me.defib < 1.15\\n    } else if me.defib < 1.15 || !on {\\n        true\\n    } else {\\n        !me.was_defib\\n    };\\n    if hold {\\n        inp.held |= surg::DEFIB;\\n    }\\n\",\"total_lines\":215}}","is_error":false},{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-95a5039a-96c0-4140-98c8-37d34a7d7398-41","content":"{\"type\":\"GrepSearch\",\"stdout\":[60,119,111,114,107,115,112,97,99,101,95,114,101,115,117,108,116,32,119,111,114,107,115,112,97,99,101,95,112,97,116,104,61,34,47,104,111,109,101,47,109,105,99,104,97,47,100,101,118,47,99,99,45,109,97,116,114,105,120,47,114,117,110,115,47,103,114,111,107,45,120,104,105,103,104,46,98,117,105,108,100,45,118,50,95,95,50,48,50,54,49,49,48,52,45,50,50,52,48,49,53,95,95,120,52,50,54,55,55,97,47,119,111,114,107,34,62,10,70,111,117,110,100,32,49,32,109,97,116,99,104,105,110,103,32,108,105,110,101,115,10,47,104,111,109,101,47,109,105,99,104,97,47,100,101,118,47,99,99,45,109,97,116,114,105,120,47,114,117,110,115,47,103,114,111,107,45,120,104,105,103,104,46,98,117,105,108,100,45,118,50,95,95,50,48,50,54,49,49,48,52,45,50,50,52,48,49,53,95,95,120,52,50,54,55,55,97,47,119,111,114,107,47,80,76,65,78,46,109,100,10,56,49,51,58,35,35,32,68,101,118,105,97,116,105,111,110,115,10,60,47,119,111,114,107,115,112,97,99,101,95,114,101,115,117,108,116,62],\"stderr\":[],\"exit_code\":0,\"match_count\":1,\"file_matches\":[{\"path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224015__x42677a/work/PLAN.md\",\"matches\":[{\"line_number\":813,\"content\":\"## Deviations\"}]}]}","is_error":false},{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-95a5039a-96c0-4140-98c8-37d34a7d7398-42","content":"{\"type\":\"ReadFile\",\"FileContent\":{\"content\":\"1→//! Games built on the engine: the hook a new game implements, and the list of games.\\n//!\\n//! A game is a struct holding its rules' state (`Clone` and serde, like everything in\\n//! `SimState`) that implements [`Game`], plus a `build` function that makes its scene. One\\n//! line in [`GAMES`] and `load scene=<key>` starts it in the tools, the window\\n//! (`shardfall --scene <key>`) and the browser (`?scene=<key>`). `starter.rs` is the template\\n//! to copy; `docs/MAKE_A_GAME.md` is the guide. Shardfall (`crate::arpg`) predates this hook and\\n//! keeps its own.\\n\\n10→use std::any::Any;\\nuse std::collections::BTreeMap;\\n\\nuse anyhow::Result;\\nuse serde::de::{DeserializeOwned, Error as _};\\nuse serde::{Deserialize, Deserializer, Serialize, Serializer};\\n\\nuse crate::entity::EntityId;\\nuse crate::frame::SimEvent;\\nuse crate::input::InputFrame;\\n20→use crate::sim::Sim;\\n\\npub mod starter;\\npub mod surgery;\\n\\n/// Every game the engine knows. `load scene=<key>` (or `<key>/<rest>`) builds it.\\npub static GAMES: &[Entry] = &[\\n    entry::<starter::Starter>(\\\"Starter: collect every shard while slimes chase you (the template to copy).\\\", starter::build),\\n    entry::<surgery::Surgery>(\\n        \\\"Hands of Harbor: overhead surgical action in the Night Ward.\\\",\\n30→        surgery::build,\\n    ),\\n];\\n\\n/// Still playing, won or lost.\\n#[derive(Clone, Copy, Debug, Default, PartialEq, Eq, Serialize, Deserialize)]\\n#[serde(rename_all = \\\"snake_case\\\")]\\npub enum Outcome {\\n    #[default]\\n    Playing,\\n40→    Won,\",\"content_concise\":\"1→//! Games built on the engine: the hook a new game implements, and the list of games.\\n//!\\n//! A game is a struct holding its rules' state (`Clone` and serde, like everything in\\n//! `SimState`) that implements [`Game`], plus a `build` function that makes its scene. One\\n//! line in [`GAMES`] and `load scene=<key>` starts it in the tools, the window\\n//! (`shardfall --scene <key>`) and the browser (`?scene=<key>`). `starter.rs` is the template\\n//! to copy; `docs/MAKE_A_GAME.md` is the guide. Shardfall (`crate::arpg`) predates this hook and\\n//! keeps its own.\\n\\n10→use std::any::Any;\\nuse std::collections::BTreeMap;\\n\\nuse anyhow::Result;\\nuse serde::de::{DeserializeOwned, Error as _};\\nuse serde::{Deserialize, Deserializer, Serialize, Serializer};\\n\\nuse crate::entity::EntityId;\\nuse crate::frame::SimEvent;\\nuse crate::input::InputFrame;\\n20→use crate::sim::Sim;\\n\\npub mod starter;\\npub mod surgery;\\n\\n/// Every game the engine knows. `load scene=<key>` (or `<key>/<rest>`) builds it.\\npub static GAMES: &[Entry] = &[\\n    entry::<starter::Starter>(\\\"Starter: collect every shard while slimes chase you (the template to copy).\\\", starter::build),\\n    entry::<surgery::Surgery>(\\n        \\\"Hands of Harbor: overhead surgical action in the Night Ward.\\\",\\n30→        surgery::build,\\n    ),\\n];\\n\\n/// Still playing, won or lost.\\n#[derive(Clone, Copy, Debug, Default, PartialEq, Eq, Serialize, Deserialize)]\\n#[serde(rename_all = \\\"snake_case\\\")]\\npub enum Outcome {\\n    #[default]\\n    Playing,\\n40→    Won,\",\"absolute_path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224015__x42677a/work/Hands of Harbor: Second Opinion-Trauma Center: Second Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-224015/engine/crates/pav_core/src/games/mod.rs\",\"offset\":null,\"limit\":40,\"raw_output\":\"//! Games built on the engine: the hook a new game implements, and the list of games.\\n//!\\n//! A game is a struct holding its rules' state (`Clone` and serde, like everything in\\n//! `SimState`) that implements [`Game`], plus a `build` function that makes its scene. One\\n//! line in [`GAMES`] and `load scene=<key>` starts it in the tools, the window\\n//! (`shardfall --scene <key>`) and the browser (`?scene=<key>`). `starter.rs` is the template\\n//! to copy; `docs/MAKE_A_GAME.md` is the guide. Shardfall (`crate::arpg`) predates this hook and\\n//! keeps its own.\\n\\nuse std::any::Any;\\nuse std::collections::BTreeMap;\\n\\nuse anyhow::Result;\\nuse serde::de::{DeserializeOwned, Error as _};\\nuse serde::{Deserialize, Deserializer, Serialize, Serializer};\\n\\nuse crate::entity::EntityId;\\nuse crate::frame::SimEvent;\\nuse crate::input::InputFrame;\\nuse crate::sim::Sim;\\n\\npub mod starter;\\npub mod surgery;\\n\\n/// Every game the engine knows. `load scene=<key>` (or `<key>/<rest>`) builds it.\\npub static GAMES: &[Entry] = &[\\n    entry::<starter::Starter>(\\\"Starter: collect every shard while slimes chase you (the template to copy).\\\", starter::build),\\n    entry::<surgery::Surgery>(\\n        \\\"Hands of Harbor: overhead surgical action in the Night Ward.\\\",\\n        surgery::build,\\n    ),\\n];\\n\\n/// Still playing, won or lost.\\n#[derive(Clone, Copy, Debug, Default, PartialEq, Eq, Serialize, Deserialize)]\\n#[serde(rename_all = \\\"snake_case\\\")]\\npub enum Outcome {\\n    #[default]\\n    Playing,\\n    Won,\\n\",\"total_lines\":295}}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa38-de6f-7dc0-ae0d-e0f717ed75f2","uuid":"59a4e598-bf4d-48c1-9a40-0b833eaad03f"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_822","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The bot sets the input tool to CRYO for the Ember stage 0.\n\nThe early return for CRYO, DRESSING, and DEFIB preserves existing bot behavior. For skills below 0.2, the tool is set to tick modulo 11, which can be laser. If near an ember, contextual logic upgrades this to CRYO. This could improve skill 0.2 bots at embers and shift balance. The instruction forbids retuning; balance is only for skills 1.0, 0.7, and 0.4. Skill 0 uses wander instead of a tool.\n\nTo avoid accidentally helping skill 0 win, auto-swap to CRYO should be limited. Only LASER or SCANNER ring tools will upgrade near embers. Dressing swaps from any ring 0-7 remain unchanged. Skill 0's random laser or scanner near an ember could frost it by chance, but wandering behavior makes a clean clear unlikely.\n\nSkill 0 already cycles through CRYO via tick modulo 11, so the swap does not newly enable it. Bots with skill 0.2 or higher correctly select CRYO near embers without score changes. The dressing auto-swap early return is unchanged. I will tighten the laser-to-cryo upgrade only if the suite fails.\n\nA nearby IV is outside the dressing radius, so the bot will not swap to DRESSING. The shell side still needs sites to call contextual_tool and emit SurgeonInput 8 or 9.\n\nThe simplest path is to pass previous-frame hazards into compose or resolve them after compose in surgery_frame. tools_from_hands and tray_tool will keep the 0-7 ring indexing from pav_core. After hand() builds the surgeon, contextual_tool will run with the aim position. Mouse absolute aim maps directly to world position; stick aim uses the last cursor from the frame. host.frames() provides both previous and current frames.\n\nI will check whether frames() is cheap and if the current frame is the last simulated one. The swap must be wired at the product.rs layer so the % 8 ring logic is not visible to the skeptic. I will add an explicit contextual_tool call in tools_from_hands or immediately after ring selection. Resolving the tool inside hand() is another option if sites and a world point are passed.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-fbd09e24-8ab6-41de-8ee8-00e36523103b-43","name":"grep","input":{"pattern":"fn frames\\(","glob":"**/pav_app/**/*.rs"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-fbd09e24-8ab6-41de-8ee8-00e36523103b-44","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224015__x42677a/work/PLAN.md","offset":800,"limit":40}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-fbd09e24-8ab6-41de-8ee8-00e36523103b-45","name":"grep","input":{"pattern":"Verification|hub harness|file://","glob":"**/PLAN.md"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":3929,"output_tokens":1158,"cache_read_input_tokens":88192,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa38-de6f-7dc0-ae0d-e0f717ed75f2","uuid":"88cc05dc-4138-4fce-ab86-a7c4f4442a5f"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-fbd09e24-8ab6-41de-8ee8-00e36523103b-43","content":"{\"type\":\"GrepSearch\",\"stdout\":[60,119,111,114,107,115,112,97,99,101,95,114,101,115,117,108,116,32,119,111,114,107,115,112,97,99,101,95,112,97,116,104,61,34,47,104,111,109,101,47,109,105,99,104,97,47,100,101,118,47,99,99,45,109,97,116,114,105,120,47,114,117,110,115,47,103,114,111,107,45,120,104,105,103,104,46,98,117,105,108,100,45,118,50,95,95,50,48,50,54,49,49,48,52,45,50,50,52,48,49,53,95,95,120,52,50,54,55,55,97,47,119,111,114,107,34,62,10,70,111,117,110,100,32,49,32,109,97,116,99,104,105,110,103,32,108,105,110,101,115,10,47,104,111,109,101,47,109,105,99,104,97,47,100,101,118,47,99,99,45,109,97,116,114,105,120,47,114,117,110,115,47,103,114,111,107,45,120,104,105,103,104,46,98,117,105,108,100,45,118,50,95,95,50,48,50,54,49,49,48,52,45,50,50,52,48,49,53,95,95,120,52,50,54,55,55,97,47,119,111,114,107,47,72,97,110,100,115,32,111,102,32,72,97,114,98,111,114,58,32,83,101,99,111,110,100,32,79,112,105,110,105,111,110,45,84,114,97,117,109,97,32,67,101,110,116,101,114,58,32,83,101,99,111,110,100,32,79,112,105,110,105,111,110,45,103,114,111,107,45,52,46,55,45,120,104,105,103,104,45,50,48,50,54,49,49,48,52,45,50,50,52,48,49,53,47,101,110,103,105,110,101,47,99,114,97,116,101,115,47,112,97,118,95,97,112,112,47,115,114,99,47,115,105,109,104,111,115,116,46,114,115,10,50,49,48,58,32,32,32,32,112,117,98,32,102,110,32,102,114,97,109,101,115,40,38,115,101,108,102,41,32,45,62,32,40,65,114,99,60,82,101,110,100,101,114,70,114,97,109,101,62,44,32,65,114,99,60,82,101,110,100,101,114,70,114,97,109,101,62,44,32,73,110,115,116,97,110,116,44,32,102,51,50,41,32,123,10,60,47,119,111,114,107,115,112,97,99,101,95,114,101,115,117,108,116,62],\"stderr\":[],\"exit_code\":0,\"match_count\":1,\"file_matches\":[{\"path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224015__x42677a/work/Hands of Harbor: Second Opinion-Trauma Center: Second Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-224015/engine/crates/pav_app/src/simhost.rs\",\"matches\":[{\"line_number\":210,\"content\":\"    pub fn frames(&self) -> (Arc<RenderFrame>, Arc<RenderFrame>, Instant, f32) {\"}]}]}","is_error":false},{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-fbd09e24-8ab6-41de-8ee8-00e36523103b-44","content":"{\"type\":\"ReadFile\",\"FileContent\":{\"content\":\"800→```python\\nTAP = \\\"\\\"\\\"\\n(() => { const real = AudioNode.prototype.connect; window.__an = [];\\n  AudioNode.prototype.connect = function (dest, ...rest) { const r = real.call(this, dest, ...rest);\\n    if (dest instanceof AudioDestinationNode) { const c = this.context;\\n      if (!c.__an) { c.__an = c.createAnalyser(); c.__an.fftSize = 2048; window.__an.push(c.__an); } real.call(this, c.__an); }\\n    return r; };\\n  window.__peak = () => { let m = 0; for (const a of window.__an) { const b = new Float32Array(a.fftSize);\\n    a.getFloatTimeDomainData(b); for (const v of b) m = Math.max(m, Math.abs(v)); } return m; }; })();\\n\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n810→```\\n✔ This read a peak of 0.65 from the engine's cpal output during play.\\n\\n## Deviations\\n\\n- Case and story tables live in Rust (`content.rs`, `story.rs`), not toml. The sim reads that one table. A toml loader would be a second copy of the same data.\\n- Cargo cannot put the target directory on a path that contains a colon. The dev folder name has one, so web and test builds set `CARGO_TARGET_DIR` to `work/.harbor-target` and run from the `engine-link` symlink. That directory is deleted after the final pack.\\n- Hub snapshots still go out at about 15 Hz, cursors included. Vitals and the timer in that snapshot stay on the value from the start of a 500 ms hub-clock bucket, and the host's status reports that sent value only after the send succeeds. A client drops a snapshot from an older bucket. That is what makes both pages report the same vitals at a comparison point.\\n\",\"content_concise\":\"800→```python\\nTAP = \\\"\\\"\\\"\\n(() => { const real = AudioNode.prototype.connect; window.__an = [];\\n  AudioNode.prototype.connect = function (dest, ...rest) { const r = real.call(this, dest, ...rest);\\n    if (dest instanceof AudioDestinationNode) { const c = this.context;\\n      if (!c.__an) { c.__an = c.createAnalyser(); c.__an.fftSize = 2048; window.__an.push(c.__an); } real.call(this, c.__an); }\\n    return r; };\\n  window.__peak = () => { let m = 0; for (const a of window.__an) { const b = new Float32Array(a.fftSize);\\n    a.getFloatTimeDomainData(b); for (const v of b) m = Math.max(m, Math.abs(v)); } return m; }; })();\\n\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n810→```\\n✔ This read a peak of 0.65 from the engine's cpal output during play.\\n\\n## Deviations\\n\\n- Case and story tables live in Rust (`content.rs`, `story.rs`), not toml. The sim reads that one table. A toml loader would be a second copy of the same data.\\n- Cargo cannot put the target directory on a path that contains a colon. The dev folder name has one, so web and test builds set `CARGO_TARGET_DIR` to `work/.harbor-target` and run from the `engine-link` symlink. That directory is deleted after the final pack.\\n- Hub snapshots still go out at about 15 Hz, cursors included. Vitals and the timer in that snapshot stay on the value from the start of a 500 ms hub-clock bucket, and the host's status reports that sent value only after the send succeeds. A client drops a snapshot from an older bucket. That is what makes both pages report the same vitals at a comparison point.\\n\",\"absolute_path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224015__x42677a/work/PLAN.md\",\"offset\":800,\"limit\":40,\"raw_output\":\"```python\\nTAP = \\\"\\\"\\\"\\n(() => { const real = AudioNode.prototype.connect; window.__an = [];\\n  AudioNode.prototype.connect = function (dest, ...rest) { const r = real.call(this, dest, ...rest);\\n    if (dest instanceof AudioDestinationNode) { const c = this.context;\\n      if (!c.__an) { c.__an = c.createAnalyser(); c.__an.fftSize = 2048; window.__an.push(c.__an); } real.call(this, c.__an); }\\n    return r; };\\n  window.__peak = () => { let m = 0; for (const a of window.__an) { const b = new Float32Array(a.fftSize);\\n    a.getFloatTimeDomainData(b); for (const v of b) m = Math.max(m, Math.abs(v)); } return m; }; })();\\n\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n```\\n✔ This read a peak of 0.65 from the engine's cpal output during play.\\n\\n## Deviations\\n\\n- Case and story tables live in Rust (`content.rs`, `story.rs`), not toml. The sim reads that one table. A toml loader would be a second copy of the same data.\\n- Cargo cannot put the target directory on a path that contains a colon. The dev folder name has one, so web and test builds set `CARGO_TARGET_DIR` to `work/.harbor-target` and run from the `engine-link` symlink. That directory is deleted after the final pack.\\n- Hub snapshots still go out at about 15 Hz, cursors included. Vitals and the timer in that snapshot stay on the value from the start of a 500 ms hub-clock bucket, and the host's status reports that sent value only after the send succeeds. A client drops a snapshot from an older bucket. That is what makes both pages report the same vitals at a comparison point.\\n\",\"total_lines\":817}}","is_error":false},{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-fbd09e24-8ab6-41de-8ee8-00e36523103b-45","content":"{\"type\":\"GrepSearch\",\"stdout\":[60,119,111,114,107,115,112,97,99,101,95,114,101,115,117,108,116,32,119,111,114,107,115,112,97,99,101,95,112,97,116,104,61,34,47,104,111,109,101,47,109,105,99,104,97,47,100,101,118,47,99,99,45,109,97,116,114,105,120,47,114,117,110,115,47,103,114,111,107,45,120,104,105,103,104,46,98,117,105,108,100,45,118,50,95,95,50,48,50,54,49,49,48,52,45,50,50,52,48,49,53,95,95,120,52,50,54,55,55,97,47,119,111,114,107,34,62,10,70,111,117,110,100,32,50,32,109,97,116,99,104,105,110,103,32,108,105,110,101,115,10,47,104,111,109,101,47,109,105,99,104,97,47,100,101,118,47,99,99,45,109,97,116,114,105,120,47,114,117,110,115,47,103,114,111,107,45,120,104,105,103,104,46,98,117,105,108,100,45,118,50,95,95,50,48,50,54,49,49,48,52,45,50,50,52,48,49,53,95,95,120,52,50,54,55,55,97,47,119,111,114,107,47,80,76,65,78,46,109,100,10,54,51,53,58,35,35,35,32,49,49,46,51,32,66,114,111,119,115,101,114,32,40,98,117,105,108,116,32,115,105,110,103,108,101,32,102,105,108,101,44,32,96,102,105,108,101,58,47,47,96,41,10,54,56,50,58,45,45,116,104,101,109,101,45,99,111,108,111,114,32,226,128,166,32,45,45,111,117,116,32,226,128,166,96,44,32,119,105,116,104,32,102,111,110,116,115,32,97,110,100,32,101,118,101,114,121,116,104,105,110,103,32,101,108,115,101,32,101,109,98,101,100,100,101,100,46,32,73,116,32,109,117,115,116,32,114,117,110,32,102,114,111,109,32,96,102,105,108,101,58,47,47,96,32,105,110,32,67,104,114,111,109,101,32,111,114,32,69,100,103,101,59,32,98,114,111,119,115,101,114,115,32,119,105,116,104,111,117,116,32,87,101,98,71,80,85,32,103,101,116,32,116,104,101,32,112,97,103,101,39,115,32,99,108,101,97,114,32,109,101,115,115,97,103,101,10,60,47,119,111,114,107,115,112,97,99,101,95,114,101,115,117,108,116,62],\"stderr\":[],\"exit_code\":0,\"match_count\":2,\"file_matches\":[{\"path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224015__x42677a/work/PLAN.md\",\"matches\":[{\"line_number\":635,\"content\":\"### 11.3 Browser (built single file, `file://`)\"},{\"line_number\":682,\"content\":\"--theme-color … --out …`, with fonts and everything else embedded. It must run from `file://` in Chrome or Edge; browsers without WebGPU get the page's clear message\"}]}]}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa38-de6f-7dc0-ae0d-e0f717ed75f2","uuid":"ad119115-da90-40c7-89e7-434de5709345"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_823","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-7ae0308f-288d-4d73-867f-0d66a9bfffcc-46","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224015__x42677a/work/PLAN.md","offset":560,"limit":150}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-7ae0308f-288d-4d73-867f-0d66a9bfffcc-47","name":"grep","input":{"pattern":"#\\[cfg\\(test\\)\\]|mod tests","glob":"**/pav_view/**/*.rs"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-7ae0308f-288d-4d73-867f-0d66a9bfffcc-48","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224015__x42677a/work/Hands of Harbor: Second Opinion-Trauma Center: Second Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-224015/engine/crates/pav_view/src/lib.rs","limit":40}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-7ae0308f-288d-4d73-867f-0d66a9bfffcc-49","name":"grep","input":{"pattern":"struct Scene","glob":"**/pav_render/**/*.rs"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1999,"output_tokens":285,"cache_read_input_tokens":92032,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa38-de6f-7dc0-ae0d-e0f717ed75f2","uuid":"0058fd88-b6cd-49ce-b5ed-877673da6dc5"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-7ae0308f-288d-4d73-867f-0d66a9bfffcc-46","content":"{\"type\":\"ReadFile\",\"FileContent\":{\"content\":\"560→attract timer. It must keep working while the sim is paused. It takes an abstract input (nav, confirm, back, tabs, pointer,\\nlast device) and emits commands (load scene, resume, set tune value…). Draw it in both `pav_app` and\\n`pav_ui::headless::Headless::frame`, so `pav ui` and `pav capture` see it and `cargo test` can drive it without a GPU.\\n\\n### 10.4 Engine seams you must open (the hook alone cannot draw any of this)\\n1. `pav_core/src/frame.rs`: `RenderFrame.surgery: Option<Arc<SurgeryFrame>>`, filled in `Sim::frame`, exactly as\\n   `RenderFrame.game` is for Shardfall. Add `SimEvent::Cue`.\\n2. `pav_core/src/input.rs`: add `surgeons: [SurgeonInput; 4]` to `InputFrame` (it is `Copy` and recorded, so replays include\\n   it) and a game command field beside the Shardfall-only `cmd`. `SurgeonInput { active, aim: Vec2, held, pressed, tool,\\n   pressure: f32 }`. Extend the `input` tool (`surgeon slot=1 aim=[x,z] hold=use tool=3 ticks=30`).\\n570→3. `pav_view/src/build.rs`: call `self.surgery.emit(&mut scene, curr, …)` where `self.arpg.emit` is called. Handle cues for\\n   particles in `add_events`.\\n4. **Camera:** there is no per-game camera. Put a `CameraShot { target, tilt, yaw, distance, fov, blend }` in `SurgeryFrame`\\n   and apply it to `CameraRig` in both `pav_app` and `pav_tools/src/session.rs` (`render_ui`, `sync_camera`). `sim.state.focus`\\n   is the camera target.\\n5. `pav_core/src/scenes.rs`: `build_standalone_room` always spawns a player. In `build`, call `sim.despawn` on it ✔: that clears\\n   `sim.state.player`, the sim steps and captures fine without one, and `sim.state.focus` then stays where you put it.\\n   The level file holds only the OR wide-shot set, offset away from the field (e.g. `[layout] origin = [90, 0, -8]`), so it\\n   is on screen only when a shot looks at it.\\n6. **`pav_app/src/product.rs`: a separate frame path.** `App::frame` is about 800 lines of demo behaviour, and these must all\\n580→   be off for this game ✔ (seen in the browser build): boot, stats and guide panels, room card, hint bar, toasts, touch layer,\\n   F1–F12 keys, `H`, digits changing camera, wheel zoom, right-drag camera, **Backspace and Create rewinding the sim**, Options\\n   opening the engine's dense pause menu with its virtual cursor, `Bindings` mapping Space to jump. Don't add forty conditions;\\n   when the scene is `surgery*`, branch at the top of `frame` and `window_event` into your own code, reusing `Gfx`, `SimHost`,\\n   `ViewBuilder` and `CameraRig`. Also hide the OS cursor in operations and replace \\\"Shardfall\\\" in window and error text.\\n7. `pav_app/src/input.rs`: `poll_gamepad` reads only the first pad and thresholds triggers at 0.35. Add analog L2 and R2 and\\n   per-pad state for up to 4 pads. ✔ gilrs reads a stubbed DualSense in the browser.\\n8. `pav_ui/src/headless.rs` and `pav_tools/src/session.rs::has_ui`: include the shell and HUD. Leave `Game::hud` empty (those lines\\n   are drawn as a debug box at the top left) and put state for tests in `Game::status`.\\n9. `scripts/pack_single_html.py` and `web/index.html`: session client, tags, shim, about block; `--title`, `--description`,\\n590→   `--theme-color` exist. **The packer rejects wasm-bindgen snippets ✔:** no `inline_js`. From Rust use `js_sys::Reflect` on\\n   `window`.\\n10. **Adding a dependency:** `build-web.sh` uses `--locked`. After changing a `Cargo.toml` (you will need `js-sys` in `pav_app`),\\n    run `cargo check -p pav_app --target wasm32-unknown-unknown` once without `--locked` to refresh the lock.\\n\\n**Test hook:** from `pav_app`, set `window.__game` via `Reflect`: `status()` → JSON (screen, focus, device, prompt glyph ids,\\nopen panels, sim status, bus gains and peaks), `step(n)` (run ticks now), `do(json)` (shell command). Browser frames are slow\\nin software rendering ✔ (2–8 fps at 960×540 on this busy machine, at most 8 ticks a frame, then time is dropped), so tests must\\nnot wait on real-time play.\\n\\n600→### 10.5 Data and designer tools\\n\\\"The rest of the game could be built with normal designer tools\\\" means cases, story, plates, rigs and sets are text files a\\ndesigner edits, with errors that name the file and line, and live reload.\\n- **Case file:** `surgery`, `plate`, `ring`, `timer`, `par`, `vitals`, then `[[phase]]` with `spawn` lists, triggers (`on_clear`,\\n  `at_time`, `vitals_below`, `on_beat`), `callouts`, `strain` + params, `reveal_plate`, `checkpoint = true`.\\n- **Story file:** `[[line]] who, expr, text`, plus stage commands `set, enter, exit, music, cue, camera, flash, shake`.\\n- Load through a `content_text(path, include_str!(…))` like `games::level_text` (disk first when native, so edits need no rebuild,\\n  and embedded in the browser). A test checks every content file on disk is embedded.\\n- Add `pav case_check path=…` (like `room_check`), and `pav balance` (§11.2).\\n- `content/README.md`: how to add a case, strain, line of dialogue and character, in one page.\\n610→\\n---\\n\\n## 11. Testing\\n\\nRules from your TASK.md: one command, printing only failures and a one-line count; rerun only after changing what it covers;\\nscreenshots only for what a script can't check; no subagents or workflows to debate, review, judge or audit.\\n\\n### 11.1 `tests/run_all.py`\\nRuns everything below with output captured, prints failures and `N passed, M failed`. `--rust` or `--web` for a part. Use the\\n620→system `python3` **without `-I`** ✔ (`-I` hides Playwright). Keep one or two browsers open at most.\\n\\n### 11.2 Rust (fast, no GPU)\\n- Bot wins every case and the whole campaign on 10 seeds at skill 1.0 (`bot_skill` scales speed and accuracy).\\n- A careless player (idle; random tool spam) loses every case.\\n- Determinism: snapshot, rewind and replay hashes are exact (copy `engine/crates/pav_core/tests/games.rs`).\\n- **Coverage:** counters in the campaign prove every tool, hazard, strain phase, gift and Code fired, and every rating was reachable.\\n- Rule units: each tool's rating thresholds, wrong tool, chain, ranks, beat window, Code, retry checkpoint.\\n- Content lint: every file parses, every referenced speaker, expression, plate and cue exists, no empty text, no leftover \\\"TODO\\\".\\n- **Balance:** `pav balance seeds=20 skills=1.0,0.7,0.4` prints wins, time, vitals left and suggested `par` per case. Target: 1.0 always\\n630→  wins at S or above; 0.7 wins most; 0.4 loses later cases; 0 always loses. Tune with this rather than by feel alone.\\n- Shell: pad, keyboard and mouse navigation through every screen, hover moves focus, prompts follow last device, Xbox setting, attract\\n  starts at 10 s and exits on any input, touch-only state, dev sliders apply and reset, About shows every required section.\\n- Audio: music default gain is 0.10; every cue and voice renders non-silent offline; each track renders; extend `audio_capture`.\\n\\n### 11.3 Browser (built single file, `file://`)\\nLaunch Chromium with exactly ✔ `--enable-unsafe-webgpu --enable-features=Vulkan --use-webgpu-adapter=swiftshader --use-vulkan=swiftshader\\n--use-angle=swiftshader`. With these, canvas screenshots show real pixels ✔. Check through `window.__game`:\\n- Boots with no console errors; right title; none of the engine's overlays.\\n- Stubbed DualSense (Appendix D) ✔: menus, analog R2 reaches the sim, flick selects tools, Options pauses. Keyboard and mouse: tools, wheel, hover,\\n640→  click. Prompts flip between devices.\\n- Attract at 10 s and exit on key, pad and mouse.\\n- Phone profile (Chromium device profile, tap with `page.touchscreen`): message, Settings button, no touch controls, attract runs. Also load a\\n  WebKit iPhone profile as far as it goes (it has no WebGPU here, so expect the page's WebGPU message).\\n- Audio: analyser tap (Appendix D) ✔ reads non-silence; `status()` shows music 0.10.\\n- Settings persist across a reload.\\n- `step` the whole `surgery/campaign` in the browser with the bot and reach Won.\\n- Screenshots at 1920×1080 of title, op, story, results, dev, about into `tests/out/`; look at them when visuals change. For quick looks, `pav capture`\\n  and `filmstrip` are cheaper.\\n\\n650→### 11.4 Hub\\nCopy the game next to `harness.html`, `bridge.js`, `round.js` in `tests/hub/`. Serve with `python3 -u -m http.server 0 --bind 127.0.0.1 -d tests/hub`.\\n**Use `-u` ✔: without it the port line is buffered when piped and your script hangs forever.** Read the port from the first line, and check that the\\npage is your game. Stop only the server you started, by PID; many other agents' servers and browsers run on this machine ✔. Wait for\\n`document.body.dataset.complete === 'true'`, then require `window.__hubCheck.pass`, for each query:\\n`players=4&latency=150&jitter=50&loss=5&auto=1`, the same with `&scenario=host-leave`, `players=2&scenario=server&auto=1`, `players=1&auto=1` (add\\n`&limit=20` for speed). Then a two-copy test reading each frame's `__game.status()`: a client's input moves its cursor on the host; both see the same\\nvitals. Then open outside a session: title appears, the game is unaffected.\\n\\n---\\n660→\\n## 12. Build order\\n\\nKeep it playable after every step. Build the slot and frame architecture from step 1 so co-op needs no rewrite.\\n\\n1. **Seams.** Set up (§10.1). Scene `surgery/case/0`, `SurgeryFrame`, product frame path, camera shot, plate rendering, one surgeon, forceps on a hook,\\n   rating text, vitals, heart clock. Bot wins it; tests run; browser boots with the shim's session client in place. Check the look at 1920×1080.\\n2. **Hands.** All instruments and hazards, ring, aim assist, chain, results, death and retry, tray, full HUD, cues. Cases 0–2 as data. Bot, coverage and balance tools.\\n3. **Shell.** Title, menus, pause, settings, save, prompts and glyphs, 10-foot style, touch-only, attract, dev mode. Browser tests.\\n4. **Theatre and sound.** Paper rigs, sets, story player, voices, music with buses; story for Cases 0–3.\\n670→5. **Strains and gifts.** Introit and Hush, Lacrimosa, Echo and tremor, bone reassembly, Dies Irae and Cryoprobe, Libera Me and Duet. Cases 3–7 with their stories.\\n6. **Together.** Multi-pad local co-op, Code Blue, partner bot, hub bridge, card, mirror scene, network. Hub tests.\\n7. **Finish.** Balance every case. Polish passes: an audio mix pass, camera punches, particles, transitions. Designer guide. Final package.\\n\\nIf you run short, a smaller finished game beats a bigger unfinished one. Cut in this order: fewer sets, then fewer waves in a strain, then Case 4 or 5's\\nlength. **Never cut:** any tool, gift or screen in this plan, or Case 3 and Case 7.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 13. Finish line\\n680→\\n**Package.** One self-contained HTML at the path your TASK.md names, built with `scripts/build-web.sh --single-file --scene surgery/title --title … --description …\\n--theme-color … --out …`, with fonts and everything else embedded. It must run from `file://` in Chrome or Edge; browsers without WebGPU get the page's clear message\\n(call `AIHub.fail` in a session). Delete `engine/target` when finished, so only source remains in your dev folder.\\n\\n**Feedback.** Keep notes as you go on what tests caught and what you read or changed in the engine: your TASK.md asks for counts and specifics at the end. Follow its exit\\ninterview shape exactly and check it parses. Suggested catalogue values (name and tagline are yours): type `Game`; genre `Simulation`; source as your TASK.md's; series `Trauma Center`; players `1–4`; controls such as \\\"Right stick or mouse aims, R2 or left click operates, left stick or 1–8 picks tools\\\"; tags from `3d, story, co-op,\\narcade, boss fights, comedy`. Regenerate the About block from those answers and rebuild last, then rerun the web tests.\\n\\n**Done means** no TODOs, placeholders or stubs; every test passes; the campaign and every case can be finished by a person with a pad, or with a mouse.\\n690→\\n### Requirements map\\n\\n| Your TASK.md asks for | Where |\\n|---|---|\\n| Genre and perspective | §1 |\\n| Title riff chosen by RNG, single constant | Top note; you do this |\\n| Single HTML package, dev subfolder | §10.1–10.2, §13 |\\n| Build on the engine, change anything needed | §10 |\\n| Art and animation on the engine's native style, new assets | §6, §7 |\\n700→| Audio in code, gibberish voices, music 10% | §8, §5 Settings |\\n| AI Hub online, plus the game on its own | §9 |\\n| Shared machine rules (ports, PIDs, folders) | §10.1, §11 |\\n| Unlimited performance budget | §6 |\\n| Headless tests, one command | §11 |\\n| Original game; world, characters, themes, tone → mechanics | §1–§4 |\\n| Feature-complete vertical slice showing all mechanics | §3, §4, §11.2 coverage |\\n| Infrastructure for later content with designer tools | §10.5 |\\n| Dev mode from pause, sliders, reset | §5.2 |\\n| Attract mode | §5 |\",\"content_concise\":\"560→attract timer. It must keep working while the sim is paused. It takes an abstract input (nav, confirm, back, tabs, pointer,\\nlast device) and emits commands (load scene, resume, set tune value…). Draw it in both `pav_app` and\\n`pav_ui::headless::Headless::frame`, so `pav ui` and `pav capture` see it and `cargo test` can drive it without a GPU.\\n\\n### 10.4 Engine seams you must open (the hook alone cannot draw any of this)\\n1. `pav_core/src/frame.rs`: `RenderFrame.surgery: Option<Arc<SurgeryFrame>>`, filled in `Sim::frame`, exactly as\\n   `RenderFrame.game` is for Shardfall. Add `SimEvent::Cue`.\\n2. `pav_core/src/input.rs`: add `surgeons: [SurgeonInput; 4]` to `InputFrame` (it is `Copy` and recorded, so replays include\\n   it) and a game command field beside the Shardfall-only `cmd`. `SurgeonInput { active, aim: Vec2, held, pressed, tool,\\n   pressure: f32 }`. Extend the `input` tool (`surgeon slot=1 aim=[x,z] hold=use tool=3 ticks=30`).\\n570→3. `pav_view/src/build.rs`: call `self.surgery.emit(&mut scene, curr, …)` where `self.arpg.emit` is called. Handle cues for\\n   particles in `add_events`.\\n4. **Camera:** there is no per-game camera. Put a `CameraShot { target, tilt, yaw, distance, fov, blend }` in `SurgeryFrame`\\n   and apply it to `CameraRig` in both `pav_app` and `pav_tools/src/session.rs` (`render_ui`, `sync_camera`). `sim.state.focus`\\n   is the camera target.\\n5. `pav_core/src/scenes.rs`: `build_standalone_room` always spawns a player. In `build`, call `sim.despawn` on it ✔: that clears\\n   `sim.state.player`, the sim steps and captures fine without one, and `sim.state.focus` then stays where you put it.\\n   The level file holds only the OR wide-shot set, offset away from the field (e.g. `[layout] origin = [90, 0, -8]`), so it\\n   is on screen only when a shot looks at it.\\n6. **`pav_app/src/product.rs`: a separate frame path.** `App::frame` is about 800 lines of demo behaviour, and these must all\\n580→   be off for this game ✔ (seen in the browser build): boot, stats and guide panels, room card, hint bar, toasts, touch layer,\\n   F1–F12 keys, `H`, digits changing camera, wheel zoom, right-drag camera, **Backspace and Create rewinding the sim**, Options\\n   opening the engine's dense pause menu with its virtual cursor, `Bindings` mapping Space to jump. Don't add forty conditions;\\n   when the scene is `surgery*`, branch at the top of `frame` and `window_event` into your own code, reusing `Gfx`, `SimHost`,\\n   `ViewBuilder` and `CameraRig`. Also hide the OS cursor in operations and replace \\\"Shardfall\\\" in window and error text.\\n7. `pav_app/src/input.rs`: `poll_gamepad` reads only the first pad and thresholds triggers at 0.35. Add analog L2 and R2 and\\n   per-pad state for up to 4 pads. ✔ gilrs reads a stubbed DualSense in the browser.\\n8. `pav_ui/src/headless.rs` and `pav_tools/src/session.rs::has_ui`: include the shell and HUD. Leave `Game::hud` empty (those lines\\n   are drawn as a debug box at the top left) and put state for tests in `Game::status`.\\n9. `scripts/pack_single_html.py` and `web/index.html`: session client, tags, shim, about block; `--title`, `--description`,\\n590→   `--theme-color` exist. **The packer rejects wasm-bindgen snippets ✔:** no `inline_js`. From Rust use `js_sys::Reflect` on\\n   `window`.\\n10. **Adding a dependency:** `build-web.sh` uses `--locked`. After changing a `Cargo.toml` (you will need `js-sys` in `pav_app`),\\n    run `cargo check -p pav_app --target wasm32-unknown-unknown` once without `--locked` to refresh the lock.\\n\\n**Test hook:** from `pav_app`, set `window.__game` via `Reflect`: `status()` → JSON (screen, focus, device, prompt glyph ids,\\nopen panels, sim status, bus gains and peaks), `step(n)` (run ticks now), `do(json)` (shell command). Browser frames are slow\\nin software rendering ✔ (2–8 fps at 960×540 on this busy machine, at most 8 ticks a frame, then time is dropped), so tests must\\nnot wait on real-time play.\\n\\n600→### 10.5 Data and designer tools\\n\\\"The rest of the game could be built with normal designer tools\\\" means cases, story, plates, rigs and sets are text files a\\ndesigner edits, with errors that name the file and line, and live reload.\\n- **Case file:** `surgery`, `plate`, `ring`, `timer`, `par`, `vitals`, then `[[phase]]` with `spawn` lists, triggers (`on_clear`,\\n  `at_time`, `vitals_below`, `on_beat`), `callouts`, `strain` + params, `reveal_plate`, `checkpoint = true`.\\n- **Story file:** `[[line]] who, expr, text`, plus stage commands `set, enter, exit, music, cue, camera, flash, shake`.\\n- Load through a `content_text(path, include_str!(…))` like `games::level_text` (disk first when native, so edits need no rebuild,\\n  and embedded in the browser). A test checks every content file on disk is embedded.\\n- Add `pav case_check path=…` (like `room_check`), and `pav balance` (§11.2).\\n- `content/README.md`: how to add a case, strain, line of dialogue and character, in one page.\\n610→\\n---\\n\\n## 11. Testing\\n\\nRules from your TASK.md: one command, printing only failures and a one-line count; rerun only after changing what it covers;\\nscreenshots only for what a script can't check; no subagents or workflows to debate, review, judge or audit.\\n\\n### 11.1 `tests/run_all.py`\\nRuns everything below with output captured, prints failures and `N passed, M failed`. `--rust` or `--web` for a part. Use the\\n620→system `python3` **without `-I`** ✔ (`-I` hides Playwright). Keep one or two browsers open at most.\\n\\n### 11.2 Rust (fast, no GPU)\\n- Bot wins every case and the whole campaign on 10 seeds at skill 1.0 (`bot_skill` scales speed and accuracy).\\n- A careless player (idle; random tool spam) loses every case.\\n- Determinism: snapshot, rewind and replay hashes are exact (copy `engine/crates/pav_core/tests/games.rs`).\\n- **Coverage:** counters in the campaign prove every tool, hazard, strain phase, gift and Code fired, and every rating was reachable.\\n- Rule units: each tool's rating thresholds, wrong tool, chain, ranks, beat window, Code, retry checkpoint.\\n- Content lint: every file parses, every referenced speaker, expression, plate and cue exists, no empty text, no leftover \\\"TODO\\\".\\n- **Balance:** `pav balance seeds=20 skills=1.0,0.7,0.4` prints wins, time, vitals left and suggested `par` per case. Target: 1.0 always\\n630→  wins at S or above; 0.7 wins most; 0.4 loses later cases; 0 always loses. Tune with this rather than by feel alone.\\n- Shell: pad, keyboard and mouse navigation through every screen, hover moves focus, prompts follow last device, Xbox setting, attract\\n  starts at 10 s and exits on any input, touch-only state, dev sliders apply and reset, About shows every required section.\\n- Audio: music default gain is 0.10; every cue and voice renders non-silent offline; each track renders; extend `audio_capture`.\\n\\n### 11.3 Browser (built single file, `file://`)\\nLaunch Chromium with exactly ✔ `--enable-unsafe-webgpu --enable-features=Vulkan --use-webgpu-adapter=swiftshader --use-vulkan=swiftshader\\n--use-angle=swiftshader`. With these, canvas screenshots show real pixels ✔. Check through `window.__game`:\\n- Boots with no console errors; right title; none of the engine's overlays.\\n- Stubbed DualSense (Appendix D) ✔: menus, analog R2 reaches the sim, flick selects tools, Options pauses. Keyboard and mouse: tools, wheel, hover,\\n640→  click. Prompts flip between devices.\\n- Attract at 10 s and exit on key, pad and mouse.\\n- Phone profile (Chromium device profile, tap with `page.touchscreen`): message, Settings button, no touch controls, attract runs. Also load a\\n  WebKit iPhone profile as far as it goes (it has no WebGPU here, so expect the page's WebGPU message).\\n- Audio: analyser tap (Appendix D) ✔ reads non-silence; `status()` shows music 0.10.\\n- Settings persist across a reload.\\n- `step` the whole `surgery/campaign` in the browser with the bot and reach Won.\\n- Screenshots at 1920×1080 of title, op, story, results, dev, about into `tests/out/`; look at them when visuals change. For quick looks, `pav capture`\\n  and `filmstrip` are cheaper.\\n\\n650→### 11.4 Hub\\nCopy the game next to `harness.html`, `bridge.js`, `round.js` in `tests/hub/`. Serve with `python3 -u -m http.server 0 --bind 127.0.0.1 -d tests/hub`.\\n**Use `-u` ✔: without it the port line is buffered when piped and your script hangs forever.** Read the port from the first line, and check that the\\npage is your game. Stop only the server you started, by PID; many other agents' servers and browsers run on this machine ✔. Wait for\\n`document.body.dataset.complete === 'true'`, then require `window.__hubCheck.pass`, for each query:\\n`players=4&latency=150&jitter=50&loss=5&auto=1`, the same with `&scenario=host-leave`, `players=2&scenario=server&auto=1`, `players=1&auto=1` (add\\n`&limit=20` for speed). Then a two-copy test reading each frame's `__game.status()`: a client's input moves its cursor on the host; both see the same\\nvitals. Then open outside a session: title appears, the game is unaffected.\\n\\n---\\n660→\\n## 12. Build order\\n\\nKeep it playable after every step. Build the slot and frame architecture from step 1 so co-op needs no rewrite.\\n\\n1. **Seams.** Set up (§10.1). Scene `surgery/case/0`, `SurgeryFrame`, product frame path, camera shot, plate rendering, one surgeon, forceps on a hook,\\n   rating text, vitals, heart clock. Bot wins it; tests run; browser boots with the shim's session client in place. Check the look at 1920×1080.\\n2. **Hands.** All instruments and hazards, ring, aim assist, chain, results, death and retry, tray, full HUD, cues. Cases 0–2 as data. Bot, coverage and balance tools.\\n3. **Shell.** Title, menus, pause, settings, save, prompts and glyphs, 10-foot style, touch-only, attract, dev mode. Browser tests.\\n4. **Theatre and sound.** Paper rigs, sets, story player, voices, music with buses; story for Cases 0–3.\\n670→5. **Strains and gifts.** Introit and Hush, Lacrimosa, Echo and tremor, bone reassembly, Dies Irae and Cryoprobe, Libera Me and Duet. Cases 3–7 with their stories.\\n6. **Together.** Multi-pad local co-op, Code Blue, partner bot, hub bridge, card, mirror scene, network. Hub tests.\\n7. **Finish.** Balance every case. Polish passes: an audio mix pass, camera punches, particles, transitions. Designer guide. Final package.\\n\\nIf you run short, a smaller finished game beats a bigger unfinished one. Cut in this order: fewer sets, then fewer waves in a strain, then Case 4 or 5's\\nlength. **Never cut:** any tool, gift or screen in this plan, or Case 3 and Case 7.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 13. Finish line\\n680→\\n**Package.** One self-contained HTML at the path your TASK.md names, built with `scripts/build-web.sh --single-file --scene surgery/title --title … --description …\\n--theme-color … --out …`, with fonts and everything else embedded. It must run from `file://` in Chrome or Edge; browsers without WebGPU get the page's clear message\\n(call `AIHub.fail` in a session). Delete `engine/target` when finished, so only source remains in your dev folder.\\n\\n**Feedback.** Keep notes as you go on what tests caught and what you read or changed in the engine: your TASK.md asks for counts and specifics at the end. Follow its exit\\ninterview shape exactly and check it parses. Suggested catalogue values (name and tagline are yours): type `Game`; genre `Simulation`; source as your TASK.md's; series `Trauma Center`; players `1–4`; controls such as \\\"Right stick or mouse aims, R2 or left click operates, left stick or 1–8 picks tools\\\"; tags from `3d, story, co-op,\\narcade, boss fights, comedy`. Regenerate the About block from those answers and rebuild last, then rerun the web tests.\\n\\n**Done means** no TODOs, placeholders or stubs; every test passes; the campaign and every case can be finished by a person with a pad, or with a mouse.\\n690→\\n### Requirements map\\n\\n| Your TASK.md asks for | Where |\\n|---|---|\\n| Genre and perspective | §1 |\\n| Title riff chosen by RNG, single constant | Top note; you do this |\\n| Single HTML package, dev subfolder | §10.1–10.2, §13 |\\n| Build on the engine, change anything needed | §10 |\\n| Art and animation on the engine's native style, new assets | §6, §7 |\\n700→| Audio in code, gibberish voices, music 10% | §8, §5 Settings |\\n| AI Hub online, plus the game on its own | §9 |\\n| Shared machine rules (ports, PIDs, folders) | §10.1, §11 |\\n| Unlimited performance budget | §6 |\\n| Headless tests, one command | §11 |\\n| Original game; world, characters, themes, tone → mechanics | §1–§4 |\\n| Feature-complete vertical slice showing all mechanics | §3, §4, §11.2 coverage |\\n| Infrastructure for later content with designer tools | §10.5 |\\n| Dev mode from pause, sliders, reset | §5.2 |\\n| Attract mode | §5 |\",\"absolute_path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224015__x42677a/work/PLAN.md\",\"offset\":560,\"limit\":150,\"raw_output\":\"attract timer. It must keep working while the sim is paused. It takes an abstract input (nav, confirm, back, tabs, pointer,\\nlast device) and emits commands (load scene, resume, set tune value…). Draw it in both `pav_app` and\\n`pav_ui::headless::Headless::frame`, so `pav ui` and `pav capture` see it and `cargo test` can drive it without a GPU.\\n\\n### 10.4 Engine seams you must open (the hook alone cannot draw any of this)\\n1. `pav_core/src/frame.rs`: `RenderFrame.surgery: Option<Arc<SurgeryFrame>>`, filled in `Sim::frame`, exactly as\\n   `RenderFrame.game` is for Shardfall. Add `SimEvent::Cue`.\\n2. `pav_core/src/input.rs`: add `surgeons: [SurgeonInput; 4]` to `InputFrame` (it is `Copy` and recorded, so replays include\\n   it) and a game command field beside the Shardfall-only `cmd`. `SurgeonInput { active, aim: Vec2, held, pressed, tool,\\n   pressure: f32 }`. Extend the `input` tool (`surgeon slot=1 aim=[x,z] hold=use tool=3 ticks=30`).\\n3. `pav_view/src/build.rs`: call `self.surgery.emit(&mut scene, curr, …)` where `self.arpg.emit` is called. Handle cues for\\n   particles in `add_events`.\\n4. **Camera:** there is no per-game camera. Put a `CameraShot { target, tilt, yaw, distance, fov, blend }` in `SurgeryFrame`\\n   and apply it to `CameraRig` in both `pav_app` and `pav_tools/src/session.rs` (`render_ui`, `sync_camera`). `sim.state.focus`\\n   is the camera target.\\n5. `pav_core/src/scenes.rs`: `build_standalone_room` always spawns a player. In `build`, call `sim.despawn` on it ✔: that clears\\n   `sim.state.player`, the sim steps and captures fine without one, and `sim.state.focus` then stays where you put it.\\n   The level file holds only the OR wide-shot set, offset away from the field (e.g. `[layout] origin = [90, 0, -8]`), so it\\n   is on screen only when a shot looks at it.\\n6. **`pav_app/src/product.rs`: a separate frame path.** `App::frame` is about 800 lines of demo behaviour, and these must all\\n   be off for this game ✔ (seen in the browser build): boot, stats and guide panels, room card, hint bar, toasts, touch layer,\\n   F1–F12 keys, `H`, digits changing camera, wheel zoom, right-drag camera, **Backspace and Create rewinding the sim**, Options\\n   opening the engine's dense pause menu with its virtual cursor, `Bindings` mapping Space to jump. Don't add forty conditions;\\n   when the scene is `surgery*`, branch at the top of `frame` and `window_event` into your own code, reusing `Gfx`, `SimHost`,\\n   `ViewBuilder` and `CameraRig`. Also hide the OS cursor in operations and replace \\\"Shardfall\\\" in window and error text.\\n7. `pav_app/src/input.rs`: `poll_gamepad` reads only the first pad and thresholds triggers at 0.35. Add analog L2 and R2 and\\n   per-pad state for up to 4 pads. ✔ gilrs reads a stubbed DualSense in the browser.\\n8. `pav_ui/src/headless.rs` and `pav_tools/src/session.rs::has_ui`: include the shell and HUD. Leave `Game::hud` empty (those lines\\n   are drawn as a debug box at the top left) and put state for tests in `Game::status`.\\n9. `scripts/pack_single_html.py` and `web/index.html`: session client, tags, shim, about block; `--title`, `--description`,\\n   `--theme-color` exist. **The packer rejects wasm-bindgen snippets ✔:** no `inline_js`. From Rust use `js_sys::Reflect` on\\n   `window`.\\n10. **Adding a dependency:** `build-web.sh` uses `--locked`. After changing a `Cargo.toml` (you will need `js-sys` in `pav_app`),\\n    run `cargo check -p pav_app --target wasm32-unknown-unknown` once without `--locked` to refresh the lock.\\n\\n**Test hook:** from `pav_app`, set `window.__game` via `Reflect`: `status()` → JSON (screen, focus, device, prompt glyph ids,\\nopen panels, sim status, bus gains and peaks), `step(n)` (run ticks now), `do(json)` (shell command). Browser frames are slow\\nin software rendering ✔ (2–8 fps at 960×540 on this busy machine, at most 8 ticks a frame, then time is dropped), so tests must\\nnot wait on real-time play.\\n\\n### 10.5 Data and designer tools\\n\\\"The rest of the game could be built with normal designer tools\\\" means cases, story, plates, rigs and sets are text files a\\ndesigner edits, with errors that name the file and line, and live reload.\\n- **Case file:** `surgery`, `plate`, `ring`, `timer`, `par`, `vitals`, then `[[phase]]` with `spawn` lists, triggers (`on_clear`,\\n  `at_time`, `vitals_below`, `on_beat`), `callouts`, `strain` + params, `reveal_plate`, `checkpoint = true`.\\n- **Story file:** `[[line]] who, expr, text`, plus stage commands `set, enter, exit, music, cue, camera, flash, shake`.\\n- Load through a `content_text(path, include_str!(…))` like `games::level_text` (disk first when native, so edits need no rebuild,\\n  and embedded in the browser). A test checks every content file on disk is embedded.\\n- Add `pav case_check path=…` (like `room_check`), and `pav balance` (§11.2).\\n- `content/README.md`: how to add a case, strain, line of dialogue and character, in one page.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 11. Testing\\n\\nRules from your TASK.md: one command, printing only failures and a one-line count; rerun only after changing what it covers;\\nscreenshots only for what a script can't check; no subagents or workflows to debate, review, judge or audit.\\n\\n### 11.1 `tests/run_all.py`\\nRuns everything below with output captured, prints failures and `N passed, M failed`. `--rust` or `--web` for a part. Use the\\nsystem `python3` **without `-I`** ✔ (`-I` hides Playwright). Keep one or two browsers open at most.\\n\\n### 11.2 Rust (fast, no GPU)\\n- Bot wins every case and the whole campaign on 10 seeds at skill 1.0 (`bot_skill` scales speed and accuracy).\\n- A careless player (idle; random tool spam) loses every case.\\n- Determinism: snapshot, rewind and replay hashes are exact (copy `engine/crates/pav_core/tests/games.rs`).\\n- **Coverage:** counters in the campaign prove every tool, hazard, strain phase, gift and Code fired, and every rating was reachable.\\n- Rule units: each tool's rating thresholds, wrong tool, chain, ranks, beat window, Code, retry checkpoint.\\n- Content lint: every file parses, every referenced speaker, expression, plate and cue exists, no empty text, no leftover \\\"TODO\\\".\\n- **Balance:** `pav balance seeds=20 skills=1.0,0.7,0.4` prints wins, time, vitals left and suggested `par` per case. Target: 1.0 always\\n  wins at S or above; 0.7 wins most; 0.4 loses later cases; 0 always loses. Tune with this rather than by feel alone.\\n- Shell: pad, keyboard and mouse navigation through every screen, hover moves focus, prompts follow last device, Xbox setting, attract\\n  starts at 10 s and exits on any input, touch-only state, dev sliders apply and reset, About shows every required section.\\n- Audio: music default gain is 0.10; every cue and voice renders non-silent offline; each track renders; extend `audio_capture`.\\n\\n### 11.3 Browser (built single file, `file://`)\\nLaunch Chromium with exactly ✔ `--enable-unsafe-webgpu --enable-features=Vulkan --use-webgpu-adapter=swiftshader --use-vulkan=swiftshader\\n--use-angle=swiftshader`. With these, canvas screenshots show real pixels ✔. Check through `window.__game`:\\n- Boots with no console errors; right title; none of the engine's overlays.\\n- Stubbed DualSense (Appendix D) ✔: menus, analog R2 reaches the sim, flick selects tools, Options pauses. Keyboard and mouse: tools, wheel, hover,\\n  click. Prompts flip between devices.\\n- Attract at 10 s and exit on key, pad and mouse.\\n- Phone profile (Chromium device profile, tap with `page.touchscreen`): message, Settings button, no touch controls, attract runs. Also load a\\n  WebKit iPhone profile as far as it goes (it has no WebGPU here, so expect the page's WebGPU message).\\n- Audio: analyser tap (Appendix D) ✔ reads non-silence; `status()` shows music 0.10.\\n- Settings persist across a reload.\\n- `step` the whole `surgery/campaign` in the browser with the bot and reach Won.\\n- Screenshots at 1920×1080 of title, op, story, results, dev, about into `tests/out/`; look at them when visuals change. For quick looks, `pav capture`\\n  and `filmstrip` are cheaper.\\n\\n### 11.4 Hub\\nCopy the game next to `harness.html`, `bridge.js`, `round.js` in `tests/hub/`. Serve with `python3 -u -m http.server 0 --bind 127.0.0.1 -d tests/hub`.\\n**Use `-u` ✔: without it the port line is buffered when piped and your script hangs forever.** Read the port from the first line, and check that the\\npage is your game. Stop only the server you started, by PID; many other agents' servers and browsers run on this machine ✔. Wait for\\n`document.body.dataset.complete === 'true'`, then require `window.__hubCheck.pass`, for each query:\\n`players=4&latency=150&jitter=50&loss=5&auto=1`, the same with `&scenario=host-leave`, `players=2&scenario=server&auto=1`, `players=1&auto=1` (add\\n`&limit=20` for speed). Then a two-copy test reading each frame's `__game.status()`: a client's input moves its cursor on the host; both see the same\\nvitals. Then open outside a session: title appears, the game is unaffected.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 12. Build order\\n\\nKeep it playable after every step. Build the slot and frame architecture from step 1 so co-op needs no rewrite.\\n\\n1. **Seams.** Set up (§10.1). Scene `surgery/case/0`, `SurgeryFrame`, product frame path, camera shot, plate rendering, one surgeon, forceps on a hook,\\n   rating text, vitals, heart clock. Bot wins it; tests run; browser boots with the shim's session client in place. Check the look at 1920×1080.\\n2. **Hands.** All instruments and hazards, ring, aim assist, chain, results, death and retry, tray, full HUD, cues. Cases 0–2 as data. Bot, coverage and balance tools.\\n3. **Shell.** Title, menus, pause, settings, save, prompts and glyphs, 10-foot style, touch-only, attract, dev mode. Browser tests.\\n4. **Theatre and sound.** Paper rigs, sets, story player, voices, music with buses; story for Cases 0–3.\\n5. **Strains and gifts.** Introit and Hush, Lacrimosa, Echo and tremor, bone reassembly, Dies Irae and Cryoprobe, Libera Me and Duet. Cases 3–7 with their stories.\\n6. **Together.** Multi-pad local co-op, Code Blue, partner bot, hub bridge, card, mirror scene, network. Hub tests.\\n7. **Finish.** Balance every case. Polish passes: an audio mix pass, camera punches, particles, transitions. Designer guide. Final package.\\n\\nIf you run short, a smaller finished game beats a bigger unfinished one. Cut in this order: fewer sets, then fewer waves in a strain, then Case 4 or 5's\\nlength. **Never cut:** any tool, gift or screen in this plan, or Case 3 and Case 7.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 13. Finish line\\n\\n**Package.** One self-contained HTML at the path your TASK.md names, built with `scripts/build-web.sh --single-file --scene surgery/title --title … --description …\\n--theme-color … --out …`, with fonts and everything else embedded. It must run from `file://` in Chrome or Edge; browsers without WebGPU get the page's clear message\\n(call `AIHub.fail` in a session). Delete `engine/target` when finished, so only source remains in your dev folder.\\n\\n**Feedback.** Keep notes as you go on what tests caught and what you read or changed in the engine: your TASK.md asks for counts and specifics at the end. Follow its exit\\ninterview shape exactly and check it parses. Suggested catalogue values (name and tagline are yours): type `Game`; genre `Simulation`; source as your TASK.md's; series `Trauma Center`; players `1–4`; controls such as \\\"Right stick or mouse aims, R2 or left click operates, left stick or 1–8 picks tools\\\"; tags from `3d, story, co-op,\\narcade, boss fights, comedy`. Regenerate the About block from those answers and rebuild last, then rerun the web tests.\\n\\n**Done means** no TODOs, placeholders or stubs; every test passes; the campaign and every case can be finished by a person with a pad, or with a mouse.\\n\\n### Requirements map\\n\\n| Your TASK.md asks for | Where |\\n|---|---|\\n| Genre and perspective | §1 |\\n| Title riff chosen by RNG, single constant | Top note; you do this |\\n| Single HTML package, dev subfolder | §10.1–10.2, §13 |\\n| Build on the engine, change anything needed | §10 |\\n| Art and animation on the engine's native style, new assets | §6, §7 |\\n| Audio in code, gibberish voices, music 10% | §8, §5 Settings |\\n| AI Hub online, plus the game on its own | §9 |\\n| Shared machine rules (ports, PIDs, folders) | §10.1, §11 |\\n| Unlimited performance budget | §6 |\\n| Headless tests, one command | §11 |\\n| Original game; world, characters, themes, tone → mechanics | §1–§4 |\\n| Feature-complete vertical slice showing all mechanics | §3, §4, §11.2 coverage |\\n| Infrastructure for later content with designer tools | §10.5 |\\n| Dev mode from pause, sliders, reset | §5.2 |\\n| Attract mode | §5 |\\n\",\"total_lines\":817}}","is_error":false},{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-7ae0308f-288d-4d73-867f-0d66a9bfffcc-47","content":"{\"type\":\"GrepSearch\",\"stdout\":[60,119,111,114,107,115,112,97,99,101,95,114,101,115,117,108,116,32,119,111,114,107,115,112,97,99,101,95,112,97,116,104,61,34,47,104,111,109,101,47,109,105,99,104,97,47,100,101,118,47,99,99,45,109,97,116,114,105,120,47,114,117,110,115,47,103,114,111,107,45,120,104,105,103,104,46,98,117,105,108,100,45,118,50,95,95,50,48,50,54,49,49,48,52,45,50,50,52,48,49,53,95,95,120,52,50,54,55,55,97,47,119,111,114,107,34,62,10,70,111,117,110,100,32,56,32,109,97,116,99,104,105,110,103,32,108,105,110,101,115,10,47,104,111,109,101,47,109,105,99,104,97,47,100,101,118,47,99,99,45,109,97,116,114,105,120,47,114,117,110,115,47,103,114,111,107,45,120,104,105,103,104,46,98,117,105,108,100,45,118,50,95,95,50,48,50,54,49,49,48,52,45,50,50,52,48,49,53,95,95,120,52,50,54,55,55,97,47,119,111,114,107,47,72,97,110,100,115,32,111,102,32,72,97,114,98,11