{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_831","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Case 5 begins with heat enabled on the phase.\n\nHeat rings fire every 5 beats. At 72 BPM, a charge overlaps one ring. Vitals drop about 8 per hit. One ember can be cleared without killing the patient. The other embers keep draining vitals. Vitals will not reach zero in five seconds.\n\nHeat damage during the ember charge resets the chain but does not interrupt it. The charge fills to 0.912 over about 52 ticks, landing inside the target band. A single release tick follows.\n\nThe release frame must follow a hold frame. The scalpel stage fills work over 60 ticks at the center. The forceps stage grabs at the center and drags along a 0.2 rad axis for 0.75 distance. Work equals the distance dragged.\n\nA snap jump in the first tick of the forceps stage pulls the ember to the target point immediately. The grab stores the current position, and the tool context correctly identifies the forceps.\n\nThe test must exercise all three input mappers. The octant mapper routes the up vector to the laser, then to cryo via contextual. The cycle mapper shifts from laser through suction and scalpel. The tray tool mapper selects forceps. Cycle must be used as an active tool source, not merely discarded.\n\nThe dressing stage will use the octant gel mapper and contextual swap to reach dressing. This completes the path for all four input mappers.\n\nCase 2 phase A uses the bone hazard at (0.15, 0.15) with aux 38 and radius 0.6. The octant up-right vector selects forceps. Contextual returns forceps for this bone. The cursor is held at the center while rotating left to drain aux.\n\nThe bone stage splits into two phases. First about 29 ticks of rotation drain aux below 12. Then work accumulates until it exceeds 0.25 and the hazard finishes.\n\nThe bone stage finishes on tick 44. The test will loop until the stage changes or the patient dies, reading the current hazard each tick. This avoids hardcoded timing and still follows the shipped mapping path.\n\nThe bone suture stage needs two samples across a 1.2 span. The needle starts at -0.3 and ends at 0.3. The logic requires the cursor to cross one side first so aux2 is set, then cross the opposite side to count the sample.\n\nThe suture cursor will hold at (-0.3, +0.45) to set aux2, then move to (-0.3, -0.45) to flip the sign and count the first sample. After reading samples, it moves to (+0.3, ±0.45) for the second sample. The octant right vector or a forward cycle from forceps selects the suture tool.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-c1628153-56c2-4e0e-9166-98e178af3ed8-69","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224015__x42677a/work/Hands of Harbor: Second Opinion-Trauma Center: Second Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-224015/engine/crates/pav_core/src/games/surgery/ops.rs","offset":145,"limit":140}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1622,"output_tokens":2460,"cache_read_input_tokens":109056,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa38-de6f-7dc0-ae0d-e0f717ed75f2","uuid":"d99e9c4f-3bb2-44b6-b001-0272c5016dc7"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-c1628153-56c2-4e0e-9166-98e178af3ed8-69","content":"{\"type\":\"ReadFile\",\"FileContent\":{\"content\":\"145→\\n    g.heart.vitals = g.heart.vitals.clamp(0.0, 100.0);\\n    if g.immortal && g.heart.vitals < 20.0 {\\n        g.heart.vitals = 55.0;\\n        g.heart.flat = false;\\n150→        g.code_t = -1.0;\\n    }\\n    if g.heart.vitals < 40.0 && !g.warned_40 && !g.heart.flat {\\n        g.warned_40 = true;\\n        g.callout_i = 2;\\n        g.callout_t = 2.2;\\n    }\\n    if g.pending_script && !g.heart.flat && g.mode != M_DEAD {\\n        g.pending_script = false;\\n        g.begin_code(true);\\n160→    } else if g.heart.vitals <= 0.0 && !g.heart.flat && g.mode != M_DEAD {\\n        g.begin_code(false);\\n    }\\n\\n    if g.mode != M_OP && g.mode != M_ATTRACT {\\n        return;\\n    }\\n    if !g.freeze && !g.heart.flat {\\n        let speed = 1.0 / g.tune.timer.max(0.2);\\n        if g.code_blue {\\n170→            g.timer -= dt * speed;\\n        } else {\\n            g.timer -= rules * speed;\\n        }\\n    }\\n    g.elapsed += dt;\\n\\n    if !g.code_blue && !g.heart.flat && phase_clear(g) {\\n        g.phase_i = g.phase_i.saturating_add(1);\\n        g.phase_ready = false;\\n180→        g.heat_on = false;\\n        if case_def(g.case_id.max(0) as u8).is_some_and(|c| g.phase_i as usize >= c.phases.len()) {\\n            g.finish_op();\\n            return;\\n        }\\n    }\\n\\n    if g.code_blue && g.mode == M_OP {\\n        tick_blue(g, sim, dt);\\n    }\\n190→    if g.timer <= 0.0 && (g.mode == M_OP || g.mode == M_ATTRACT) {\\n        if g.code_blue && g.heart.vitals > 0.0 && !g.heart.flat {\\n            g.finish_op();\\n        } else if !g.code_blue {\\n            g.die();\\n        } else if g.heart.flat || g.heart.vitals <= 0.0 {\\n            g.die();\\n        }\\n    }\\n}\\n200→\\nfn enter_phase(g: &mut Surgery, sim: &mut Sim, events: &mut Vec<SimEvent>) {\\n    let Some(def) = case_def(g.case_id.max(0) as u8) else {\\n        g.finish_op();\\n        return;\\n    };\\n    if g.phase_i as usize >= def.phases.len() {\\n        g.finish_op();\\n        return;\\n    }\\n210→    let phase = def.phases[g.phase_i as usize];\\n    g.hazards.clear();\\n    g.heat_phase = phase.heat;\\n    g.heat_on = false;\\n    for spawn in phase.spawns {\\n        let mut h = Hazard::make(spawn.kind, spawn.x, spawn.z);\\n        if spawn.drain >= 0.0 {\\n            h.drain = spawn.drain;\\n        }\\n        if spawn.axis < 90.0 {\\n220→            h.axis = spawn.axis;\\n        }\\n        h.hidden = spawn.hidden;\\n        h.need *= g.tune.strain_tough.clamp(0.2, 3.0);\\n        let jx = sim.state.rng.range(-0.05, 0.05);\\n        let jz = sim.state.rng.range(-0.05, 0.05);\\n        h.x = (h.x + jx).clamp(-8.2, 8.2);\\n        h.z = (h.z + jz).clamp(-3.6, 3.6);\\n        if phase.strain == 0 {\\n            h.tag = 1;\\n230→        }\\n        h.id = g.next_id;\\n        g.next_id = g.next_id.wrapping_add(1);\\n        g.hazards.push(h);\\n    }\\n    if phase.strain != NO_STRAIN_SENTINEL {\\n        let i = phase.strain as usize;\\n        if i < g.coverage.strains.len() {\\n            g.coverage.strains[i] = g.coverage.strains[i].saturating_add(1);\\n            g.strain_phase = phase.strain;\\n240→            g.banner_t = 2.4;\\n            cue(events, CUE_BANNER, 0.0, 0.0, 0.55, 1.0);\\n        }\\n    }\\n    if phase.unlock != 0 {\\n        g.gifts_unlocked |= phase.unlock;\\n        g.recent_unlock = phase.unlock;\\n        g.surgeons[0].meter = 100.0;\\n        g.callout_i = match phase.unlock {\\n            G_HUSH => 7,\\n250→            G_ECHO => 8,\\n            G_DUET => 9,\\n            _ => phase.callout,\\n        };\\n        g.callout_t = 2.6;\\n    } else if phase.callout > 0 {\\n        g.callout_i = phase.callout;\\n        g.callout_t = 2.4;\\n    }\\n    g.shocks_need = phase.script_code;\\n260→    g.shocks_done = 0;\\n    g.pending_script = phase.script_code > 0;\\n    g.phase_ready = true;\\n    if phase.checkpoint || g.phase_i == 0 {\\n        g.save_checkpoint();\\n    }\\n}\\n\\nconst NO_STRAIN_SENTINEL: u8 = 255;\\n\\n270→fn phase_clear(g: &Surgery) -> bool {\\n    if g.pending_script || (g.shocks_need > 0 && g.shocks_done < g.shocks_need) {\\n        return false;\\n    }\\n    !g.hazards.iter().any(|h| h.alive && h.kind != K_HEAT)\\n}\\n\\nfn swell_and_wander(g: &mut Surgery, rules: f32, events: &mut Vec<SimEvent>) {\\n    let mut bursts: Vec<(f32, f32)> = Vec::new();\\n    for h in &mut g.hazards {\\n280→        if !h.alive {\\n            continue;\\n        }\\n        if h.kind == K_SAC {\\n            // aux is the laser charge. Swell uses aux2 so a ripe sac can still be lased.\",\"content_concise\":\"145→\\n    g.heart.vitals = g.heart.vitals.clamp(0.0, 100.0);\\n    if g.immortal && g.heart.vitals < 20.0 {\\n        g.heart.vitals = 55.0;\\n        g.heart.flat = false;\\n150→        g.code_t = -1.0;\\n    }\\n    if g.heart.vitals < 40.0 && !g.warned_40 && !g.heart.flat {\\n        g.warned_40 = true;\\n        g.callout_i = 2;\\n        g.callout_t = 2.2;\\n    }\\n    if g.pending_script && !g.heart.flat && g.mode != M_DEAD {\\n        g.pending_script = false;\\n        g.begin_code(true);\\n160→    } else if g.heart.vitals <= 0.0 && !g.heart.flat && g.mode != M_DEAD {\\n        g.begin_code(false);\\n    }\\n\\n    if g.mode != M_OP && g.mode != M_ATTRACT {\\n        return;\\n    }\\n    if !g.freeze && !g.heart.flat {\\n        let speed = 1.0 / g.tune.timer.max(0.2);\\n        if g.code_blue {\\n170→            g.timer -= dt * speed;\\n        } else {\\n            g.timer -= rules * speed;\\n        }\\n    }\\n    g.elapsed += dt;\\n\\n    if !g.code_blue && !g.heart.flat && phase_clear(g) {\\n        g.phase_i = g.phase_i.saturating_add(1);\\n        g.phase_ready = false;\\n180→        g.heat_on = false;\\n        if case_def(g.case_id.max(0) as u8).is_some_and(|c| g.phase_i as usize >= c.phases.len()) {\\n            g.finish_op();\\n            return;\\n        }\\n    }\\n\\n    if g.code_blue && g.mode == M_OP {\\n        tick_blue(g, sim, dt);\\n    }\\n190→    if g.timer <= 0.0 && (g.mode == M_OP || g.mode == M_ATTRACT) {\\n        if g.code_blue && g.heart.vitals > 0.0 && !g.heart.flat {\\n            g.finish_op();\\n        } else if !g.code_blue {\\n            g.die();\\n        } else if g.heart.flat || g.heart.vitals <= 0.0 {\\n            g.die();\\n        }\\n    }\\n}\\n200→\\nfn enter_phase(g: &mut Surgery, sim: &mut Sim, events: &mut Vec<SimEvent>) {\\n    let Some(def) = case_def(g.case_id.max(0) as u8) else {\\n        g.finish_op();\\n        return;\\n    };\\n    if g.phase_i as usize >= def.phases.len() {\\n        g.finish_op();\\n        return;\\n    }\\n210→    let phase = def.phases[g.phase_i as usize];\\n    g.hazards.clear();\\n    g.heat_phase = phase.heat;\\n    g.heat_on = false;\\n    for spawn in phase.spawns {\\n        let mut h = Hazard::make(spawn.kind, spawn.x, spawn.z);\\n        if spawn.drain >= 0.0 {\\n            h.drain = spawn.drain;\\n        }\\n        if spawn.axis < 90.0 {\\n220→            h.axis = spawn.axis;\\n        }\\n        h.hidden = spawn.hidden;\\n        h.need *= g.tune.strain_tough.clamp(0.2, 3.0);\\n        let jx = sim.state.rng.range(-0.05, 0.05);\\n        let jz = sim.state.rng.range(-0.05, 0.05);\\n        h.x = (h.x + jx).clamp(-8.2, 8.2);\\n        h.z = (h.z + jz).clamp(-3.6, 3.6);\\n        if phase.strain == 0 {\\n            h.tag = 1;\\n230→        }\\n        h.id = g.next_id;\\n        g.next_id = g.next_id.wrapping_add(1);\\n        g.hazards.push(h);\\n    }\\n    if phase.strain != NO_STRAIN_SENTINEL {\\n        let i = phase.strain as usize;\\n        if i < g.coverage.strains.len() {\\n            g.coverage.strains[i] = g.coverage.strains[i].saturating_add(1);\\n            g.strain_phase = phase.strain;\\n240→            g.banner_t = 2.4;\\n            cue(events, CUE_BANNER, 0.0, 0.0, 0.55, 1.0);\\n        }\\n    }\\n    if phase.unlock != 0 {\\n        g.gifts_unlocked |= phase.unlock;\\n        g.recent_unlock = phase.unlock;\\n        g.surgeons[0].meter = 100.0;\\n        g.callout_i = match phase.unlock {\\n            G_HUSH => 7,\\n250→            G_ECHO => 8,\\n            G_DUET => 9,\\n            _ => phase.callout,\\n        };\\n        g.callout_t = 2.6;\\n    } else if phase.callout > 0 {\\n        g.callout_i = phase.callout;\\n        g.callout_t = 2.4;\\n    }\\n    g.shocks_need = phase.script_code;\\n260→    g.shocks_done = 0;\\n    g.pending_script = phase.script_code > 0;\\n    g.phase_ready = true;\\n    if phase.checkpoint || g.phase_i == 0 {\\n        g.save_checkpoint();\\n    }\\n}\\n\\nconst NO_STRAIN_SENTINEL: u8 = 255;\\n\\n270→fn phase_clear(g: &Surgery) -> bool {\\n    if g.pending_script || (g.shocks_need > 0 && g.shocks_done < g.shocks_need) {\\n        return false;\\n    }\\n    !g.hazards.iter().any(|h| h.alive && h.kind != K_HEAT)\\n}\\n\\nfn swell_and_wander(g: &mut Surgery, rules: f32, events: &mut Vec<SimEvent>) {\\n    let mut bursts: Vec<(f32, f32)> = Vec::new();\\n    for h in &mut g.hazards {\\n280→        if !h.alive {\\n            continue;\\n        }\\n        if h.kind == K_SAC {\\n            // aux is the laser charge. Swell uses aux2 so a ripe sac can still be lased.\",\"absolute_path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224015__x42677a/work/Hands of Harbor: Second Opinion-Trauma Center: Second Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-224015/engine/crates/pav_core/src/games/surgery/ops.rs\",\"offset\":145,\"limit\":140,\"raw_output\":\"\\n    g.heart.vitals = g.heart.vitals.clamp(0.0, 100.0);\\n    if g.immortal && g.heart.vitals < 20.0 {\\n        g.heart.vitals = 55.0;\\n        g.heart.flat = false;\\n        g.code_t = -1.0;\\n    }\\n    if g.heart.vitals < 40.0 && !g.warned_40 && !g.heart.flat {\\n        g.warned_40 = true;\\n        g.callout_i = 2;\\n        g.callout_t = 2.2;\\n    }\\n    if g.pending_script && !g.heart.flat && g.mode != M_DEAD {\\n        g.pending_script = false;\\n        g.begin_code(true);\\n    } else if g.heart.vitals <= 0.0 && !g.heart.flat && g.mode != M_DEAD {\\n        g.begin_code(false);\\n    }\\n\\n    if g.mode != M_OP && g.mode != M_ATTRACT {\\n        return;\\n    }\\n    if !g.freeze && !g.heart.flat {\\n        let speed = 1.0 / g.tune.timer.max(0.2);\\n        if g.code_blue {\\n            g.timer -= dt * speed;\\n        } else {\\n            g.timer -= rules * speed;\\n        }\\n    }\\n    g.elapsed += dt;\\n\\n    if !g.code_blue && !g.heart.flat && phase_clear(g) {\\n        g.phase_i = g.phase_i.saturating_add(1);\\n        g.phase_ready = false;\\n        g.heat_on = false;\\n        if case_def(g.case_id.max(0) as u8).is_some_and(|c| g.phase_i as usize >= c.phases.len()) {\\n            g.finish_op();\\n            return;\\n        }\\n    }\\n\\n    if g.code_blue && g.mode == M_OP {\\n        tick_blue(g, sim, dt);\\n    }\\n    if g.timer <= 0.0 && (g.mode == M_OP || g.mode == M_ATTRACT) {\\n        if g.code_blue && g.heart.vitals > 0.0 && !g.heart.flat {\\n            g.finish_op();\\n        } else if !g.code_blue {\\n            g.die();\\n        } else if g.heart.flat || g.heart.vitals <= 0.0 {\\n            g.die();\\n        }\\n    }\\n}\\n\\nfn enter_phase(g: &mut Surgery, sim: &mut Sim, events: &mut Vec<SimEvent>) {\\n    let Some(def) = case_def(g.case_id.max(0) as u8) else {\\n        g.finish_op();\\n        return;\\n    };\\n    if g.phase_i as usize >= def.phases.len() {\\n        g.finish_op();\\n        return;\\n    }\\n    let phase = def.phases[g.phase_i as usize];\\n    g.hazards.clear();\\n    g.heat_phase = phase.heat;\\n    g.heat_on = false;\\n    for spawn in phase.spawns {\\n        let mut h = Hazard::make(spawn.kind, spawn.x, spawn.z);\\n        if spawn.drain >= 0.0 {\\n            h.drain = spawn.drain;\\n        }\\n        if spawn.axis < 90.0 {\\n            h.axis = spawn.axis;\\n        }\\n        h.hidden = spawn.hidden;\\n        h.need *= g.tune.strain_tough.clamp(0.2, 3.0);\\n        let jx = sim.state.rng.range(-0.05, 0.05);\\n        let jz = sim.state.rng.range(-0.05, 0.05);\\n        h.x = (h.x + jx).clamp(-8.2, 8.2);\\n        h.z = (h.z + jz).clamp(-3.6, 3.6);\\n        if phase.strain == 0 {\\n            h.tag = 1;\\n        }\\n        h.id = g.next_id;\\n        g.next_id = g.next_id.wrapping_add(1);\\n        g.hazards.push(h);\\n    }\\n    if phase.strain != NO_STRAIN_SENTINEL {\\n        let i = phase.strain as usize;\\n        if i < g.coverage.strains.len() {\\n            g.coverage.strains[i] = g.coverage.strains[i].saturating_add(1);\\n            g.strain_phase = phase.strain;\\n            g.banner_t = 2.4;\\n            cue(events, CUE_BANNER, 0.0, 0.0, 0.55, 1.0);\\n        }\\n    }\\n    if phase.unlock != 0 {\\n        g.gifts_unlocked |= phase.unlock;\\n        g.recent_unlock = phase.unlock;\\n        g.surgeons[0].meter = 100.0;\\n        g.callout_i = match phase.unlock {\\n            G_HUSH => 7,\\n            G_ECHO => 8,\\n            G_DUET => 9,\\n            _ => phase.callout,\\n        };\\n        g.callout_t = 2.6;\\n    } else if phase.callout > 0 {\\n        g.callout_i = phase.callout;\\n        g.callout_t = 2.4;\\n    }\\n    g.shocks_need = phase.script_code;\\n    g.shocks_done = 0;\\n    g.pending_script = phase.script_code > 0;\\n    g.phase_ready = true;\\n    if phase.checkpoint || g.phase_i == 0 {\\n        g.save_checkpoint();\\n    }\\n}\\n\\nconst NO_STRAIN_SENTINEL: u8 = 255;\\n\\nfn phase_clear(g: &Surgery) -> bool {\\n    if g.pending_script || (g.shocks_need > 0 && g.shocks_done < g.shocks_need) {\\n        return false;\\n    }\\n    !g.hazards.iter().any(|h| h.alive && h.kind != K_HEAT)\\n}\\n\\nfn swell_and_wander(g: &mut Surgery, rules: f32, events: &mut Vec<SimEvent>) {\\n    let mut bursts: Vec<(f32, f32)> = Vec::new();\\n    for h in &mut g.hazards {\\n        if !h.alive {\\n            continue;\\n        }\\n        if h.kind == K_SAC {\\n            // aux is the laser charge. Swell uses aux2 so a ripe sac can still be lased.\\n\",\"total_lines\":805}}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa38-de6f-7dc0-ae0d-e0f717ed75f2","uuid":"9a4e3165-2623-438f-8545-3b0063b6481a"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_832","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Spawn positions are jittered by random number generation.\n\nHazard coordinates must be read from the simulation rather than hardcoded. Phase C is a scripted NONE_SPAWN phase with script code 1, while phase B handles dressing and IV. Only the dressing needs to die to trigger the script; leaving the IV alive prevents phase advancement.\n\nDressing paint quadrants are visited in four directions around the hazard at radius 0.5 using atan2. Each quadrant requires roughly 29 ticks of work before the phase completes.\n\nThe test will use 40 ticks per quadrant for dressing paint. It will verify that contextual targeting returns DRESSING on the dressing octant and CRYO on an ember octant. Without contextual targeting, octant, cycle, and tray values stay within 0-7. The test will also cover scanner direction for clearing case 7 embers.\n\nContextual targeting treats LASER and SCANNER identically near cryo. The test will assert that both tools return CRYO on an ember before playing case 7. This resolves the second ring slot without needing to clear the embers.\n\nThe test will clear stage 0 using SCANNER via the left octant to prove the scanner-to-cryo ring path. It will also assert that LASER contextual targeting returns CRYO on an ember before the hold.\n\nStage 1 will use SCANNER as the base tool. Cycling forward twice from SCANNER reaches scalpel. Stage 2 will use forceps from the tray at (-3.5 + 1.0, 5.4). The dressing case 2 logic is next.\n\nBone stage 0 uses the up-right octant for forceps. Stage 1 cycles forward to suture. The tether uses the up octant for scalpel. The dressing uses the down-left octant for gel, then contextual targeting resolves it as dressing. All four ring functions appear on this path. Phase C script code is unreachable. The IV auto-selects when selected directly, but contextual targeting avoids that.\n\nhands() resolves contextual targeting after applying the input tool. If the test passes a resolved CRYO, hands() keeps it because it returns early when the cursor is not near an ember. This prevents a miss from reverting the tool to LASER.\n\nSkill 0 generates tool indices from 0 to 10, so it can produce ring values 8, 9, and 10.\n\nSkill 0 may now swap tool 4 to CRYO when the cursor wanders onto an ember, but the test uses 60×400 ticks and the skill wanders aim, so a lucky clear is unlikely. The change will be left as-is. When only dressings remain, any ring resolves to dressing even from a distance.\n\nThe \"near\" threshold is radius plus 0.15, so embers resolve within 0.65 and dressings within 1.25. When multiple hazards are present, the closest one within reach determines the contextual tool.\n\nThe only-dressings check runs before the nearest-hazard search, so any ring resolves to dressing even from a distance. Hidden hazards and HEAT kinds are ignored. DEFIB is returned directly without further logic. TOOL_KEEP 255 is preserved as-is instead of being modulo'd into a tool.\n\nThe shell integration is next.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-88f520ca-ce51-4187-9cc7-590af2dbb8ef-70","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224015__x42677a/work/Hands of Harbor: Second Opinion-Trauma Center: Second Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-224015/engine/crates/pav_app/src/simhost.rs","offset":190,"limit":40}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-88f520ca-ce51-4187-9cc7-590af2dbb8ef-71","name":"grep","input":{"pattern":"fn ground_point|mouse_owns","glob":"**/pav_app/src/product.rs"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":4081,"output_tokens":2221,"cache_read_input_tokens":110592,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa38-de6f-7dc0-ae0d-e0f717ed75f2","uuid":"9c44eb04-6660-464b-8271-2d779ac9dc7e"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-88f520ca-ce51-4187-9cc7-590af2dbb8ef-70","content":"{\"type\":\"ReadFile\",\"FileContent\":{\"content\":\"190→            sim.step(&input);\\n            if i == 0 {\\n                input.pressed = 0;\\n                input.surgery_cmd = None;\\n                for s in &mut input.surgeons {\\n                    s.pressed = 0;\\n                }\\n            }\\n            let dt = sim.dt();\\n            publish(&mut sim, &self.shared, dt, Instant::now());\\n200→        }\\n    }\\n\\n    /// Runs the ticks that are due (called once per frame).\\n    pub fn pump(&self) {\\n        self.clock.borrow_mut().advance(&mut self.sim.borrow_mut(), &self.shared);\\n    }\\n}\\n\\nimpl SimHost {\\n210→    pub fn frames(&self) -> (Arc<RenderFrame>, Arc<RenderFrame>, Instant, f32) {\\n        let f = self.shared.frames.lock().unwrap();\\n        (f.prev.clone(), f.curr.clone(), f.curr_at, f.tick_wall)\\n    }\\n\\n    pub fn control(&self) -> TimeControl {\\n        *self.shared.control.lock().unwrap()\\n    }\\n\\n    pub fn set_control(&self, f: impl FnOnce(&mut TimeControl)) {\\n220→        f(&mut self.shared.control.lock().unwrap());\\n    }\\n}\\n\\n#[cfg(not(target_arch = \\\"wasm32\\\"))]\\nimpl Drop for SimHost {\\n    fn drop(&mut self) {\\n        let _ = self.tx.send(Cmd::Quit);\\n        if let Some(t) = self.thread.take() {\\n            let _ = t.join();\",\"content_concise\":\"190→            sim.step(&input);\\n            if i == 0 {\\n                input.pressed = 0;\\n                input.surgery_cmd = None;\\n                for s in &mut input.surgeons {\\n                    s.pressed = 0;\\n                }\\n            }\\n            let dt = sim.dt();\\n            publish(&mut sim, &self.shared, dt, Instant::now());\\n200→        }\\n    }\\n\\n    /// Runs the ticks that are due (called once per frame).\\n    pub fn pump(&self) {\\n        self.c