-20261104-224015/engine/crates/pav_app/src/product.rs\",\"matches\":[{\"line_number\":73,\"content\":\"    mouse_owns: bool,\"},{\"line_number\":111,\"content\":\"            mouse_owns: false,\"},{\"line_number\":195,\"content\":\"            self.mouse_owns = false;\"},{\"line_number\":197,\"content\":\"            self.mouse_owns = true;\"},{\"line_number\":236,\"content\":\"                let owns = local.is_none() && i == 0 && self.mouse_owns || local == Some(i as u8) && self.mouse_owns;\"},{\"line_number\":298,\"content\":\"    fn hand(&self, slot: usize, mouse_aim: Option<[f32; 2]>, mouse_owns: bool, local: Option<u8>) -> SurgeonInput {\"},{\"line_number\":309,\"content\":\"        if mine && mouse_owns {\"},{\"line_number\":316,\"content\":\"        } else if mine && !mouse_owns {\"},{\"line_number\":340,\"content\":\"        let precise = (mine && self.key(KeyCode::ShiftLeft) && !mouse_owns) || pad.lt > 0.35;\"}]}]}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa38-de6f-7dc0-ae0d-e0f717ed75f2","uuid":"94bdd56b-3671-4a34-a2a5-2c221d69df7a"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_833","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The simulation's hands() method is the authoritative swap for pad play.\n\nThe shell will emit the resolved tool so product.rs isn't limited to 0-7. World position comes from the mouse hit if available, otherwise the last cursor position in the current surgery frame. Surgeon tool selection uses contextual_tool with ring, x, z, and hazards. If no frame exists yet, skip the swap; the simulation still handles it. Hazards and cursor positions will be post-processed after compose rather than changing its signature.\n\nThe frame must be snapshotted before pump so the current surgery state is available for post-processing.\n\nThe frame before pump is one tick behind the visible render. The simulation corrects same-frame errors. frames() runs before compose and only clears keys, using pads instead. HazardView must implement ToolSite. mirror_predict must also resolve tool swaps so the client cursor shows the correct tool; otherwise it would display laser on an ember until the snapshot arrives.\n\nThe shell contextualizes the input before sending it to the host, so the client mirror_predict uses already-resolved tools. The host hands() will swap again for consistency. A one-frame delay when a player first arrives is acceptable. Dedicated servers zero surgeons without issue. I am also checking whether product.rs uses glam::Vec2 and if pav_core re-exports it.\n\nThe octant function will use glam::Vec2. The cycle signature is pub fn cycle(tool: u8, forward: bool) -> u8. Product.rs will call cycle for L1, R1, and wheel input, and pass the pad left vector to octant.\n\nThe old wheel logic will be replaced by `cycle(tool, wheel > 0)`. Local `octant` and `tray_tool` functions will be removed from product.rs in favor of the new module exports. The `surgery` module will re-export `contextual_tool`, `cycle`, `octant`, `tray_tool`, and `ToolSite`. Test imports need updating. The hub plate emit and plate code must also change, along with comments that currently say to skip the plate.\n\nA test will be added to pav_view surgery/mod.rs. It will be included in run_all.py so the verifier's single command covers it. The suite currently skips pav_view because it is heavy, but the test may still be audited by cargo test. I am checking how other pav_view tests are structured to manage compile cost.\n\nCompiling the full pav_view library for the suite is acceptable because the crate is needed for wasm packing anyway. If that compile becomes too heavy or flaky, the test can remain as a targeted run only. The verifier audits committed tests.\n\nThe test will be added to run_all.py so the verifier's single command covers it. A new test in pav_view surgery/mod.rs verifies that quiet hub mode still draws plate instruments, hazards, and cursors. It uses SurgeryFrame::empty() with quiet set to true and mode 3.\n\nThe test pushes an ember hazard and a cryo cursor into the frame, then asserts that emit populates the scene with dynamic geometry and at least three SDFs.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-5778b0c1-e42a-45c8-9843-e2dab5ab45d8-72","name":"grep","input":{"pattern":"pub struct SdfInstance|pub fn sphere|pub center|pub a:","glob":"**/pav_render/src/scene.rs"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-5778b0c1-e42a-45c8-9843-e2dab5ab45d8-73","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224015__x42677a/work/Hands of Harbor: Second Opinion-Trauma Center: Second Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-224015/engine/crates/pav_view/src/surgery/mod.rs","offset":1,"limit":15}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2998,"output_tokens":1749,"cache_read_input_tokens":114560,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa38-de6f-7dc0-ae0d-e0f717ed75f2","uuid":"25720033-50e5-48c9-8235-60e1d5bf646a"}
