11,114,107,115,112,97,99,101,95,114,101,115,117,108,116,62],\"stderr\":[],\"exit_code\":0,\"match_count\":5,\"file_matches\":[{\"path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224015__x42677a/work/Hands of Harbor: Second Opinion-Trauma Center: Second Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-224015/engine/crates/pav_render/src/scene.rs\",\"matches\":[{\"line_number\":160,\"content\":\"pub struct SdfInstance {\"},{\"line_number\":161,\"content\":\"    pub a: Vec3,\"},{\"line_number\":175,\"content\":\"    pub fn sphere(center: Vec3, r: f32, color: Vec3) -> Self {\"},{\"line_number\":200,\"content\":\"    pub a: [f32; 4],\"},{\"line_number\":569,\"content\":\"    pub center: Vec3,\"}]}]}","is_error":false},{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-5778b0c1-e42a-45c8-9843-e2dab5ab45d8-73","content":"{\"type\":\"ReadFile\",\"FileContent\":{\"content\":\"1→//! Overhead operative field, instruments, and paper-theatre cards.\\n//! One dynamic mesh paints the plate. Lights and the camera are applied last so view settings cannot override them.\\n\\nuse glam::Vec3;\\nuse pav_core::games::surgery::frame::{CameraShot, SurgeryFrame};\\nuse pav_core::games::surgery::kinds::*;\\nuse pav_render::mesh::{MeshData, Vertex};\\nuse pav_render::scene::{self as rs, DynamicMesh, Scene, SdfInstance, Style};\\n\\n10→const NX: usize = 420;\\nconst NZ: usize = 240;\\n\\npub fn emit(scene: &mut Scene, op: &SurgeryFrame) {\\n    if op.quiet {\\n        return;\",\"content_concise\":\"1→//! Overhead operative field, instruments, and paper-theatre cards.\\n//! One dynamic mesh paints the plate. Lights and the camera are applied last so view settings cannot override them.\\n\\nuse glam::Vec3;\\nuse pav_core::games::surgery::frame::{CameraShot, SurgeryFrame};\\nuse pav_core::games::surgery::kinds::*;\\nuse pav_render::mesh::{MeshData, Vertex};\\nuse pav_render::scene::{self as rs, DynamicMesh, Scene, SdfInstance, Style};\\n\\n10→const NX: usize = 420;\\nconst NZ: usize = 240;\\n\\npub fn emit(scene: &mut Scene, op: &SurgeryFrame) {\\n    if op.quiet {\\n        return;\",\"absolute_path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224015__x42677a/work/Hands of Harbor: Second Opinion-Trauma Center: Second Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-224015/engine/crates/pav_view/src/surgery/mod.rs\",\"offset\":1,\"limit\":15,\"raw_output\":\"//! Overhead operative field, instruments, and paper-theatre cards.\\n//! One dynamic mesh paints the plate. Lights and the camera are applied last so view settings cannot override them.\\n\\nuse glam::Vec3;\\nuse pav_core::games::surgery::frame::{CameraShot, SurgeryFrame};\\nuse pav_core::games::surgery::kinds::*;\\nuse pav_render::mesh::{MeshData, Vertex};\\nuse pav_render::scene::{self as rs, DynamicMesh, Scene, SdfInstance, Style};\\n\\nconst NX: usize = 420;\\nconst NZ: usize = 240;\\n\\npub fn emit(scene: &mut Scene, op: &SurgeryFrame) {\\n    if op.quiet {\\n        return;\\n\",\"total_lines\":509}}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa38-de6f-7dc0-ae0d-e0f717ed75f2","uuid":"cc23f14a-70e5-4d0e-9587-640069a81014"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_834","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"SdfInstance stores sphere centers in a Vec3 field named `a`.\n\nI will place the cursor and ember at different coordinates to distinguish them. I plan to test mode 8 mirror rendering with quiet mode enabled.\n\nMode 3 with quiet mode is the host Code Blue case. Mode 8 will be tested as the stricter mirror case in the same test function. The coarse plate vertex count must stay below 8000 and above 100 to avoid accidentally building the stall mesh. I will use a 48 by 28 grid for quiet mode. Normal computation for the coarse grid will branch to keep the existing full plate path unchanged.\n\nThe coarse grid normal denominator uses 0.11 only for the full plate dimensions; other grids use twice the cell size. Quiet mode does not need paper, since paper is only drawn in modes 0, 1, 4, and 6. The instruments tray draws in modes 0, 3, and 6.\n\nMode 8 mirror skips the instruments tray but still draws seat 0 cursors. Hazards render embers. Mode 8 does not break on mode 0. The tray is optional for this test; cursors, hazards, and plate are required. The `apply_look` comment also needs updating.\n\nI will update the comments in product.rs and boot_mirror to reflect that the field draws a coarse plate instead of skipping the mesh. I will also add a deviation bullet noting that hub and mirror copies keep hub_quiet enabled while drawing the field on a coarse plate, and that a 420×240 plate stalled the software-GPU iframe. PROGRESS.md will be updated only after tests pass, since it is part of the earlier hand-in.\n\nI will read the long-running skill before launching the suite and pack. I will check that engine-link exists. PROGRESS.md will only be updated if it still claims the old suite status.\n\nThe test helper must not use Dev mode 6. Bone and suture cases need precise timing, and idle fade will not undo the work because bone does not fade. The ember test will hold input while checking the hazard aux value each tick, releasing once it reaches 0.88 to 1.02. The real simulation is driven directly rather than hardcoding charge. The hazard ID is stable.\n\nFocus will remain on the ember after stage advancement. Stage 1 work resets to zero once the stage advances. The scalpel must stay held at center until the stage reaches two or the character dies. Finishing stage one leaves alive true, so the task does not clear. For the forceps pull, the hand steers to the center to grab, then snaps along the axis; a single tick may not be enough because select fires at the new position.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-7e9d2152-eb17-460a-8261-c0273945c0ed-74","name":"grep","input":{"pattern":"\\.focus","glob":"**/games/surgery/ops.rs"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-7e9d2152-eb17-460a-8261-c0273945c0ed-75","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/.grok/bundled/skills/long-running-background-tasks/SKILL.md","limit":80}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2168,"output_tokens":1539,"cache_read_input_tokens":117504,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa38-de6f-7dc0-ae0d-e0f717ed75f2","uuid":"d7f62017-1f8f-458c-8859-36ca0d0fe2d1"}
