ts wins, time, vitals left, and a par that would put the skill-1.0 mean on S.\\n#[test]\\n#[ignore]\\nfn balance_sheet() {\\n    let skills = [1.0_f32, 0.7, 0.4, 0.0];\\n    let scenes: Vec<String> = (0..8).map(|c| format!(\\\"surgery/case/{c}\\\")).chain([\\\"surgery/code\\\".into()]).collect();\\n    println!(\\\"skill case wins/5 time_s vitals score par suggested_par\\\");\\n    for skill in skills {\\n        for scene in &scenes {\\n            let mut wins = 0;\\n            let mut time = 0.0;\\n\",\"total_lines\":316}}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa38-de6f-7dc0-ae0d-e0f717ed75f2","uuid":"d83c9bb1-757f-4b32-bcd2-c11ca40e6915"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_842","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Beginning to write the code.\n\nPlanning surgical tool insertion and mirror prediction. Checking echo_copy for direct tool references. Adjusting product.rs to read frames before compose.\n\nDrafting `resolve_hands` in product.rs to assign tools after compose.\n\n`resolve_hands` now uses absolute aim coordinates when available, otherwise the last cursor position. Stick aim is non-absolute. A flicked laser might delay shell swapping until the cursor arrives.\n\nThe simulation swaps the emitted tool once the shown cursor is near. Replacing the `% 8` tool logic with `tools_from_hands` and deleting the local `octant` and `tray_tool` functions. The wheel will cycle tools when turned while the left mouse button is not held. L1 and R1 will cycle backward.\n\nR1 cycles tools forward. Stored contextual tool values are not written back into self.tool, so cycling remains safe. Tray clicks now use the imported tray_tool. Imports for cycle, octant, tray_tool, and contextual_tool are being added. The full map.rs file is next.\n\nVerifying the bone suture needle formula matches the code exactly. The `needle` function computes span and sample count. For suture placement, along equals needle length and side equals ±0.45. This requires solving a rotation equation to map direction vectors correctly.\n\nThe suture placement math is confirmed. The perpendicular vector for axis 0 is (0,1), so along equals x and side equals z.\n\nDrafting the tether walk logic: iterate along the hazard axis in steps of 0.28, stopping when the total distance reaches need plus 0.15.\n\nStarting on the ember forceps pull.\n\nThe ember forceps pull grabs at the center and pulls to 0.85 units along the hazard axis. A neighbor cannot steal the grab because selection prefers the focused target, and the first tick lands on the nearest ember. The C5 embers are spaced about one unit apart with a radius of 0.5, so center aiming is reliable. If cryo heat kills vitals to zero, the ember may not finish.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-ba0821b8-d2ab-405c-b363-4da4c002855d-84","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224015__x42677a/work/Hands of Harbor: Second Opinion-Trauma Center: Second Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-224015/engine/crates/pav_core/src/games/surgery/ops.rs","offset":775,"limit":30}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":819,"output_tokens":1670,"cache_read_input_tokens":137216,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa38-de6f-7dc0-ae0d-e0f717ed75f2","uuid":"228bf9e0-a503-4fb4-a8ca-5022d01b00ae"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-ba0821b8-d2ab-405c-b363-4da4c002855d-84","content":"{\"type\":\"ReadFile\",\"FileContent\":{\"content\":\"775→        s.z += inp.aim.y * speed * dt;\\n    }\\n}\\n\\nfn heat_hit(angle: f32, x: f32, z: f32) -> bool {\\n780→    let ang = z.atan2(x);\\n    let mut d = (ang - angle).abs();\\n    if d > std::f32::consts::PI {\\n        d = std::f32::consts::TAU - d;\\n    }\\n    let r = (x * x + z * z).sqrt();\\n    d < 0.22 && r > 0.4\\n}\\n\\nfn note_kind(g: &mut Surgery, kind: u8) {\\n790→    let i = kind as usize;\\n    if i < g.coverage.hazards.len() {\\n        g.coverage.hazards[i] = g.coverage.hazards[i].saturating_add(1);\\n    }\\n}\\n\\nfn push_popup(g: &mut Surgery, rating: u8, x: f32, z: f32) {\\n    g.popups[0] = g.popups[1];\\n    g.popups[1] = g.popups[2];\\n    g.popups[2] = g.popups[3];\\n800→    g.popups[3] = (rating, 1.1, x, z);\\n}\\n\\nfn cue(events: &mut Vec<SimEvent>, id: u16, x: f32, z: f32, gain: f32, pitch: f32) {\\n    events.push(SimEvent::Cue { id, pos: Vec3::new(x, 0.2, z), gain, pitch });\",\"content_concise\":\"775→        s.z += inp.aim.y * speed * dt;\\n    }\\n}\\n\\nfn heat_hit(angle: f32, x: f32, z: f32) -> bool {\\n780→    let ang = z.atan2(x);\\n    let mut d = (ang - angle).abs();\\n    if d > std::f32::consts::PI {\\n        d = std::f32::consts::TAU - d;\\n    }\\n    let r = (x * x + z * z).sqrt();\\n    d < 0.22 && r > 0.4\\n}\\n\\nfn note_kind(g: &mut Surgery, kind: u8) {\\n790→    let i = kind as usize;\\n    if i < g.coverage.hazards.len() {\\n        g.coverage.hazards[i] = g.coverage.hazards[i].saturating_add(1);\\n    }\\n}\\n\\nfn push_popup(g: &mut Surgery, rating: u8, x: f32, z: f32) {\\n    g.popups[0] = g.popups[1];\\n    g.popups[1] = g.popups[2];\\n    g.popups[2] = g.popups[3];\\n800→    g.popups[3] = (rating, 1.1, x, z);\\n}\\n\\nfn cue(events: &mut Vec<SimEvent>, id: u16, x: f32, z: f32, gain: f32, pitch: f32) {\\n    events.push(SimEvent::Cue { id, pos: Vec3::new(x, 0.2, z), gain, pitch });\",\"absolute_path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224015__x42677a/work/Hands of Harbor: Second Opinion-Trauma Center: Second Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-224015/engine/crates/pav_core/src/games/surgery/ops.rs\",\"offset\":775,\"limit\":30,\"raw_output\":\"        s.z += inp.aim.y * speed * dt;\\n    }\\n}\\n\\nfn heat_hit(angle: f32, x: f32, z: f32) -> bool {\\n    let ang = z.atan2(x);\\n    let mut d = (ang - angle).abs();\\n    if d > std::f32::consts::PI {\\n        d = std::f32::consts::TAU - d;\\n    }\\n    let r = (x * x + z * z).sqrt();\\n    d < 0.22 && r > 0.4\\n}\\n\\nfn note_kind(g: &mut Surgery, kind: u8) {\\n    let i = kind as usize;\\n    if i < g.coverage.hazards.len() {\\n        g.coverage.hazards[i] = g.coverage.hazards[i].saturating_add(1);\\n    }\\n}\\n\\nfn push_popup(g: &mut Surgery, rating: u8, x: f32, z: f32) {\\n    g.popups[0] = g.popups[1];\\n    g.popups[1] = g.popups[2];\\n    g.popups[2] = g.popups[3];\\n    g.popups[3] = (rating, 1.1, x, z);\\n}\\n\\nfn cue(events: &mut Vec<SimEvent>, id: u16, x: f32, z: f32, gain: f32, pitch: f32) {\\n    events.push(SimEvent::Cue { id, pos: Vec3::new(x, 0.2, z), gain, pitch });\\n\",\"total_lines\":805}}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa38-de6f-7dc0-ae0d-e0f717ed75f2","uuid":"ee7dc7bc-54c2-4dbb-9779-2dcf989dec5f"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_843","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The heat ring is a ray from the origin.\n\nThe ember at (-1.65, 0.45) is reachable within the charge window. Tremor of 0.12 is small enough to avoid pushing off the ember or interfering with the suture side threshold, so precision adjustments are unnecessary.\n\nTremor is deterministic from tick, so precision will still be used to keep the test stable. A new `mapped_step` helper will be added instead of modifying the existing `hand()` function.\n\nThe `mapped_step` helper asserts the ring stays on the eight-way grid before swapping. It skips contextual tool selection when `TOOL_KEEP` is used. The held flags include absolute aiming, snapping, precision, and an extra bit. Contextual tool selection may return 8 or 9.\n\nThe test will assert scanner and laser octants on the live ember before clearing it. The frost is applied from the scanner octant with a swap, matching case 7's control.\n\nCase 6's laser is also asserted to resolve to CRYO at the same point. Both octants are driven, so either one can perform the clear. The scanner assertion alone proves the ember will clear.\n\nThe test will hold with the laser octant and assert scanner resolves to CRYO. Stage 1 uses cycle, stage 2 uses tray. One tick with raw LASER tool proves hands() swaps to CRYO and aux starts charging.\n\nThe assertion tick will use held flags so it does not release. Explicit cycle and tray assertions will verify the tool mappings: LASER plus one is GEL, SCANNER plus seven wraps to GEL, double-cycling SCANNER twice yields SCALPEL, FORCEPS sits at (-2.5, 5.4), and a nearby point returns None.\n\nThe gel octant at (-1.0, -1.0) is confirmed to resolve to DRESSING for the dressing task. A far-away point near (8.0, 3.0) is checked to ensure it does not return DRESSING while the IV remains alive. Paint quadrants are being prepared next.\n\nThe dressing paint loop uses four fixed spots and eight ticks per spot across three rounds. Only one round is needed because 32 ticks exceeds the 29-tick limit. If the dressing survives, the test will print its bits, work, tool, and alive status.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-eff4f624-4be9-4ff2-8656-b23c0d808bf7-85","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224015__x42677a/work/Hands of Harbor: Second Opinion-Trauma Center: Second Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-224015/engine/crates/pav_core/src/games/surgery/mod.rs","offset":60,"limit":40}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2092,"output_tokens":2013,"cache_read_input_tokens":137984,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa38-de6f-7dc0-ae0d-e0f717ed75f2","uuid":"7c8554e9-5e01-4266-9c45-2f563a0f12c3"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-eff4f624-4be9-4ff2-8656-b23c0d808bf7-85","content":"{\"type\":\"ReadFile\",\"FileContent\":{\"content\":\"60→    pub mistakes: u32,\\n    pub since_chain: f32,\\n    pub meter: f32,\\n    pub gift_arm: f32,\\n    pub was_use: bool,\\n    pub was_gift: bool,\\n    pub was_defib: bool,\\n    pub defib: f32,\\n    pub iv_cd: f32,\\n    pub wrong_cd: f32,\\n70→    pub name_i: u8,\\n    pub focus: Option<u32>,\\n    pub focus_t: f32,\\n}\\n\\nimpl Surgeon {\\n    fn new(i: u8) -> Self {\\n        Self {\\n            active: i == 0,\\n            x: 0.0,\\n80→            z: 0.0,\\n            tool: SCALPEL,\\n            score: 0,\\n            chain: 0,\\n            best_chain: 0,\\n            mistakes: 0,\\n            since_chain: 30.0,\\n            meter: 0.0,\\n            gift_arm: 0.0,\\n            was_use: false,\\n90→            was_gift: false,\\n            was_defib: false,\\n            defib: 0.0,\\n            iv_cd: 0.0,\\n            wrong_cd: 0.0,\\n            name_i: i,\\n            focus: None,\\n            focus_t: 0.0,\\n        }\\n    }\",\"content_concise\":\"60→    pub mistakes: u32,\\n    pub since_chain: f32,\\n    pub meter: f32,\\n    pub gift_arm: f32,\\n    pub was_use: bool,\\n    pub was_gift: bool,\\n    pub was_defib: bool,\\n    pub defib: f32,\\n    pub iv_cd: f32,\\n    pub wrong_cd: f32,\\n70→    pub name_i: u8,\\n    pub focus: Option<u32>,\\n    pub focus_t: f32,\\n}\\n\\nimpl Surgeon {\\n    fn new(i: u8) -> Self {\\n        Self {\\n            active: i == 0,\\n            x: 0.0,\\n80→            z: 0.0,\\n            tool: SCALPEL,\\n            score: 0,\\n            chain: 0,\\n            best_chain: 0,\\n            mistakes: 0,\\n            since_chain: 30.0,\\n            meter: 0.0,\\n            gift_arm: 0.0,\\n            was_use: false,\\n90→            was_gift: false,\\n            was_defib: false,\\n            defib: 0.0,\\n            iv_cd: 0.0,\\n            wrong_cd: 0.0,\\n            name_i: i,\\n            focus: None,\\n            focus_t: 0.0,\\n        }\\n    }\",\"absolute_path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224015__x42677a/work/Hands of Harbor: Second Opinion-Trauma Center: Second Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-224015/engine/crates/pav_core/src/games/surgery/mod.rs\",\"offset\":60,\"limit\":40,\"raw_output\":\"    pub mistakes: u32,\\n    pub since_chain: f32,\\n    pub meter: f32,\\n    pub gift_arm: f32,\\n    pub was_use: bool,\\n    pub was_gift: bool,\\n    pub was_defib: bool,\\n    pub defib: f32,\\n    pub iv_cd: f32,\\n    pub wrong_cd: f32,\\n    pub name_i: u8,\\n    pub focus: Option<u32>,\\n    pub focus_t: f32,\\n}\\n\\nimpl Surgeon {\\n    fn new(i: u8) -> Self {\\n        Self {\\n            active: i == 0,\\n            x: 0.0,\\n            z: 0.0,\\n            tool: SCALPEL,\\n            score: 0,\\n            chain: 0,\\n            best_chain: 0,\\n            mistakes: 0,\\n            since_chain: 30.0,\\n            meter: 0.0,\\n            gift_arm: 0.0,\\n            was_use: false,\\n            was_gift: false,\\n            was_defib: false,\\n            defib: 0.0,\\n            iv_cd: 0.0,\\n            wrong_cd: 0.0,\\n            name_i: i,\\n            focus: None,\\n            focus_t: 0.0,\\n        }\\n    }\\n\",\"total_lines\":1117}}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa38-de6f-7dc0-ae0d-e0f717ed75f2","uuid":"1a9e9a95-3bbf-4867-a827-8ce295404614"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_844","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Writing everything now. Updating frame, boot_mirror, and product comments.\n\nAdding a PLAN deviation bullet. Updating progress after tests. Writing a HazardView test helper for required fields. Verifying capsule and sphere centers match the cursor and height values. Checking plate vertices span the full field width.\n\nConfirmed DynamicMesh and MeshData are public. Adding the view test to run_all.py. The suite order runs pav_core first, then pav_ui, then pav_audio, then pav_view. Checking if cargo test returns 0 when no tests match.\n\nUsing the exact test name as the cargo filter to avoid silent failures. The `--lib surgery::tests` flag will run only that single test.\n\nConfirmed ToolSite methods and the Hazard `alive` field won't conflict. The contextual_tool trait must be public for generic use in the API. ops.rs already imports it via `use super::*`.\n\nConfirmed frame.rs has no circular import with map.rs. ToolSite does not need to be exported because callers only pass a type that implements it, and the trait itself must be public for generic inference. The bone rot test will verify that ROT_L decreases the aux value from its starting positive 38.\n\nROT_L decrements aux by 55 per second. The test will apply it until abs(aux) drops below 12, confirming the value stays within bounds.\n\nThe bone rot test will rotate while the current aux value is strictly greater than 12.0, stopping before it drops to exactly 12.0 so work can proceed.\n\nThe bone rot test will rotate until the aux value drops below 12.0, which happens after roughly 30 ticks because each step subtracts about 0.92.\n\nFor the work tick test, holding the forceps at center without rotation for sixteen ticks should push work past 0.25 and advance the stage.\n\nAfter the stage changes to one, the suture test will perform an eight-step zigzag using a `cross_bone` helper.\n\nThe `cross_bone` helper computes along-axis position from the bone span and sample count, then offsets left and right by half a unit along the perpendicular axis. It places a suture ring at each offset.\n\nThe suture zigzag has a bug. Between the two sides of a stitch, samples increment and the needle flips sign. The next side then hits the same position with the opposite sign, causing an immediate stitch that kills the bone before the second side can run.\n\nThe suture zigzag is safe. The second stitch fires because the needle sign flips between sides, and by_id filters out dead bones so the loop exits cleanly.\n\nThe tether ring uses the scalpel octant. Suture placement checks side and along offsets, not radius. The nearest target is the bone because the tether is far away. Forceps distance to the bone center is within range. A debug assert will be added if the bone stage fails to advance.\n\nAfter the last hazard dies, phase increments but the dressing does not spawn immediately. The next tick must enter_phase to clear dead hazards and spawn the dressing. A neutral wake or explicit step will advance the simulation until the dressing appears.\n\nA five-step loop will wake the simulation until the dressing spawns. Phase C triggers only after both dressing and IV die, so killing the dressing alone is safe. The script code for phase B is zero. The test will assert that both the ember and dressing kinds are gone. After the laser step, the surgeon tool will be placed down.\n\nThe cryo tool is placed down before the main charge loop begins. The charge step adds roughly 0.017 to aux each tick, so it cannot overshoot the band. The release tick triggers once aux reaches 0.84 or higher. A just_release check requires the previous tick to have been a hold. If the stage does not advance after release, the aux value will be checked to confirm it was within bounds.\n\nThe aux value is zeroed after release, so the test will assert that the stage increased or the bone died instead. A scalpel will be applied for up to 120 ticks until the stage reaches two. The pressure is set to 1.0.\n\nThe forceps pull test verifies that a tray slot at the tool's offset is valid and a miss at the origin is rejected. It grabs the ember by its exact center, then pulls along the axis by 0.9 units, which exceeds the 0.7 need and kills the bone.\n\nThe forceps pull test keeps the grabbed ember selected. At a 0.9-unit pull distance, contextual targeting may miss the ember because its reach is only 0.65 units, but the tool stays forceps and the grab remains active. A neighbor ember cannot swap the tool because the ring is forceps, not laser. The along-axis position is computed from the original grab point.\n\nAdding a hub draw test and coarse plate. Updating comments in apply_look, product.rs, boot_mirror, and frame.rs. Checking that instruments mode 8 still draws cursors when quiet is false. vertex_paint loops are fine for quiet mode. plate() uses NX and NZ constants for the full path.\n\nThe emit function now selects plate dimensions based on the quiet flag. Paper is only drawn for hub modes when quiet is off. Normal denominator safety requires nx to be at least two. The cycle function behavior for tool 255 still needs verification.\n\nThe stored ring stays 0-7 even after digits because the next frame overwrites it. The digit path sets tool 8, but contextual folding still works. Product.rs should not call contextual inside hand(); the post-pass in surgery_frame is cleaner because it sees the built SurgeonInput and has aim mode, while hand() lacks hazards.\n\nThe server-side surgeon reset happens after compose, so resolve must run immediately after compose and before the hub block that may overwrite surgeons. This prevents the server from sending cryo hands.\n\nRemote hands are copied from the network after compose, so local surgeons must be resolved before that copy. This ensures remote tools are already contextualized by their sender.\n\nThe hub block overwrites the local aim from the DOM but preserves the tool. Resolving the tool before that override would use the wrong cursor. The correct order is compose, then hub aim overrides, then contextual resolve using the final aim. The server zeroing step happens before this resolution.\n\nRemote surgeons are copied from the hub before the shell resolves them. The server-side zeroing step leaves TOOL_KEEP values, so resolve skips those entries. DOM aim is not absolute because the flag is cleared, meaning resolve falls back to cursor position.\n\nThe simulation resolves tools one frame late after stick movement, which is correct. I will patch surgery_frame with exact line edits and add the deviation to PLAN.md. The test count is being verified against the actual run.\n\nThe test must set the surgeon tool to LASER directly, bypassing contextual_tool wrapping. Only then can it assert that hands() folds it to CRYO.\n\nA `raw_ring` helper will set the ring tool directly to 0-7, bypassing contextual wrapping. This proves the simulation auto-swaps the tool to CRYO. The clear step will also use the mapping.\n\nThe test will assert that the surgeon tool becomes CRYO after a raw LASER pad on an ember. The clear step will use mapped_step, which returns the contextual tool. If the hands() swap is broken, the assertion fails. If contextual itself is broken and still returns LASER, the test should still assert that the returned tool is CRYO.\n\nThe dressing test will assert that contextual_tool returns DRESSING, and a raw gel step on the dressing will set surgeon.tool to DRESSING. The simulation then continues painting with mapped_step. A raw gel ring near the dressing triggers contextual targeting to return DRESSING, which sets the tool and starts the paint.\n\nThe only-dressings check runs first, but the IV is still alive so it returns DRESSING. A unit-level assert will guard that cycle, octant, and tray never return a tool above 7. The up-right vector Vec2::new(1.0, 1.0) maps to octant 1, which is FORCEPS; this octant is used for the bone stage while tray targets the ember stage.\n\nOctant math is verified for all eight tools. GEL maps to -1,-1, scanner to -1,0, laser to 0,-1, scalpel to 0,1, and suture to 1,0. Cycle(FORCEPS, true) correctly yields SUTURE.\n\nA concise comment will be added to map.rs explaining that the eight-way ring lacks cryoprobe and dressing slots, so those tools resolve from the hazard under the cursor. The product.rs import line will be patched cleanly, and engine-link will be verified as a symlink before compiling. The view test will construct HazardView using a struct literal with all fields.\n\nThe test will exercise both mode 8 and mode 3. A plate-drawing assertion will verify that the generated mesh spans the full field by checking that vertex positions fall outside ±10.0.\n\nThe `plate` function will remain private. The octant helper will be copied exactly from the existing code, including its `Some(...).map` pattern and the `as i32` truncation after rounding.\n\nRust `f32::round` rounds half away from zero, so -2.5 becomes -3. Octant boundaries at exact kπ/4 diagonals remain precise enough for unit vectors. The test uses axis-aligned and exact diagonal directions.\n\n`#[must_use]` is unnecessary.\n\nIn `ops/mirror_predict`, contextual tool resolution will run after steer so the position updates first.\n\nThe borrow checker requires extracting the tool and position from the mutable surgeon reference before calling `contextual_tool`, because the function borrows `g.hazards` and would conflict with the active mutable borrow.\n\nIn `ops/mirror_predict`, the tool and contact coordinates are copied into local variables before calling `contextual_tool`. This avoids a borrow conflict with the mutable `g.surgeons` reference, since the function borrows `g.hazards`.","signature":""},{"type":"text","text":"The eight-way ring never leaves tools 0–7, and a hub frame returns before the plate. I’ll share the stick, cycle, tray, and contextual swap with the sim, and draw a coarse field on hub copies."},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-0872bdfe-552a-4dbc-8a27-1d3a6e962eeb-86","name":"search_replace","input":{"file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224015__x42677a/work/Hands of Harbor: Second Opinion-Trauma Center: Second Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-224015/engine/crates/pav_core/src/games/surgery/map.rs","new_string":"//! The eight-way ring, and the two tools that are not on it.\n//! Cryoprobe and Dressing are contextual: the ring stays 0–7, and the hazard under the cursor promotes Laser or Scanner to the probe, or any ring tool to a dressing.\n\nuse glam::Vec2;\n\nuse super::frame::HazardView;\nuse super::hazard::Hazard;\nuse super::kinds::*;\n\n/// A hazard the ring can see. The sim and the shell both pass their own snapshot.\npub trait ToolSite {\n    fn site_alive(&self) -> bool;\n    fn site_kind(&self) -> u8;\n    fn site_tool(&self) -> u8;\n    fn site_x(&self) -> f32;\n    fn site_z(&self) -> f32;\n    fn site_radius(&self) -> f32;\n}\n\nimpl ToolSite for Hazard {\n    fn site_alive(&self) -> bool {\n        self.alive\n    }\n    fn site_kind(&self) -> u8 {\n        self.kind\n    }\n    fn site_tool(&self) -> u8 {\n        self.tool\n    }\n    fn site_x(&self) -> f32 {\n        self.x\n    }\n    fn site_z(&self) -> f32 {\n        self.z\n    }\n    fn site_radius(&self) -> f32 {\n        self.radius\n    }\n}\n\nimpl ToolSite for HazardView {\n    fn site_alive(&self) -> bool {\n        self.alive\n    }\n    fn site_kind(&self) -> u8 {\n        self.kind\n    }\n    fn site_tool(&self) -> u8 {\n        self.tool\n    }\n    fn site_x(&self) -> f32 {\n        self.x\n    }\n    fn site_z(&self) -> f32 {\n        self.z\n    }\n    fn site_radius(&self) -> f32 {\n        self.radius\n    }\n}\n\n/// Left-stick flick. Up is Scalpel, then clockwise: Forceps, Suture, Suction, Laser, Gel, Scanner, IV.\n/// Short of 0.55 the stick does not change tools.\npub fn octant(stick: Vec2) -> Option<u8> {\n    if stick.length() < 0.55 {\n        return None;\n    }\n    let ang = stick.x.atan2(stick.y);\n    Some((ang / std::f32::consts::FRAC_PI_4).round() as i32).map(|i| i.rem_euclid(8) as u8)\n}\n\n/// L1 / R1 and the mouse wheel. The ring is eight tools; Cryoprobe and Dressing are not stops on it.\npub fn cycle(tool: u8, forward: bool) -> u8 {\n    let step = if forward { 1 } else { 7 };\n    tool.wrapping_add(step) % 8\n}\n\n/// Tray click. Eight slots along z = 5.4, x = -3.5 + tool. Nothing off that row.\npub fn tray_tool(x: f32, z: f32) -> Option<u8> {\n    if (z - 5.4).abs() > 0.7 {\n        return None;\n    }\n    for t in 0..8 {\n        let tx = -3.5 + t as f32;\n        if (x - tx).abs() < 0.45 {\n            return Some(t as u8);\n        }\n    }\n    None\n}\n\n/// Promote the ring from the hazard under `(x, z)`.\n/// Laser and Scanner become the Cryoprobe on an ember that still wants it.\n/// Any ring tool becomes Dressing on a closure, or when every remaining wound is a closure.\n/// An already-resolved probe or dressing is folded back to its ring first, so leaving the wound puts the ring tool back.\npub fn contextual_tool<T: ToolSite>(ring: u8, x: f32, z: f32, sites: &[T]) -> u8 {\n    if ring == DEFIB || ring == TOOL_KEEP {\n        return ring;\n    }\n    let ring = match ring {\n        CRYO => LASER,\n        DRESSING => GEL,\n        other => other,\n    };\n    let mut any = false;\n    let mut only_dressing = true;\n    for site in sites {\n        if !site.site_alive() || site.site_kind() == K_HEAT {\n            continue;\n        }\n        any = true;\n        if site.site_kind() != K_DRESSING {\n            only_dressing = false;\n        }\n    }\n    if any && only_dressing {\n        return DRESSING;\n    }\n    let mut best_d = f32::MAX;\n    let mut best_tool = None;\n    for site in sites {\n        if !site.site_alive() || site.site_kind() == K_HEAT {\n            continue;\n        }\n        let dx = site.site_x() - x;\n        let dz = site.site_z() - z;\n        let d = (dx * dx + dz * dz).sqrt();\n        if d <= site.site_radius() + 0.15 && d < best_d {\n            best_d = d;\n            best_tool = Some(site.site_tool());\n        }\n    }\n    if let Some(tool) = best_tool {\n        if tool == DRESSING {\n            return DRESSING;\n        }\n        if tool == CRYO && (ring == LASER || ring == SCANNER) {\n            return CRYO;\n        }\n    }\n    if ring <= 7 { ring } else { ring % 8 }\n}\n","old_string":""}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-0872bdfe-552a-4dbc-8a27-1d3a6e962eeb-87","name":"search_replace","input":{"file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224015__x42677a/work/Hands of Harbor: Second Opinion-Trauma Center: Second Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-224015/engine/crates/pav_core/src/games/surgery/mod.rs","old_string":"mod bot;\nmod content;\nmod hazard;\nmod heart;\nmod ops;\nmod story;\nmod tune;","new_string":"mod bot;\nmod content;\nmod hazard;\nmod heart;\nmod map;\nmod ops;\nmod story;\nmod tune;"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-0872bdfe-552a-4dbc-8a27-1d3a6e962eeb-88","name":"search_replace","input":{"file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224015__x42677a/work/Hands of Harbor: Second Opinion-Trauma Center: Second Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-224015/engine/crates/pav_core/src/games/surgery/mod.rs","old_string":"pub use content::{case_def, CASES, SURGEON_NAMES};\npub use frame::SurgeryFrame;\npub use hazard::Hazard;\npub use heart::Heart;\npub use kinds::*;\npub use story::{all_lines, callout_who};\npub use tune::Tune;","new_string":"pub use content::{case_def, CASES, SURGEON_NAMES};\npub use frame::SurgeryFrame;\npub use hazard::Hazard;\npub use heart::Heart;\npub use kinds::*;\npub use map::{contextual_tool, cycle, octant, tray_tool};\npub use story::{all_lines, callout_who};\npub use tune::Tune;"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-0872bdfe-552a-4dbc-8a27-1d3a6e962eeb-89","name":"search_replace","input":{"file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224015__x42677a/work/Hands of Harbor: Second Opinion-Trauma Center: Second Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-224015/engine/crates/pav_core/src/games/surgery/frame.rs","old_string":"    /// Dedicated server: run the world, draw nothing.\n    pub quiet: bool,","new_string":"    /// Hub copy: draw a coarse plate and skip shadows. The field is still drawn.\n    pub quiet: bool,"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-0872bdfe-552a-4dbc-8a27-1d3a6e962eeb-90","name":"search_replace","input":{"file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224015__x42677a/work/Hands of Harbor: Second Opinion-Trauma Center: Second Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-224015/engine/crates/pav_core/src/games/surgery/mod.rs","old_string":"        self.hazards.clear();\n        // Hub copies skip the plate. A full operative mesh stalls the iframe after one frame.\n        self.hub_quiet = true;","new_string":"        self.hazards.clear();\n        // Coarse plate, no shadows. A 420×240 mesh stalls the software-GPU iframe.\n        self.hub_quiet = true;"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2364,"output_tokens":8757,"cache_read_input_tokens":140032,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa38-de6f-7dc0-ae0d-e0f717ed75f2","uuid":"91f4415c-69c6-4a65-8fd1-776098a65831"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-0872bdfe-552a-4dbc-8a27-1d3a6e962eeb-86","content":"{\"type\":\"SearchReplace\",\"EditsApplied\":{\"old_string\":\"\",\"new_string\":\"//! The eight-way ring, and the two tools that are not on it.\\n//! Cryoprobe and Dressing are contextual: the ring stays 0–7, and the hazard under the cursor promotes Laser or Scanner to the probe, or any ring tool to a dressing.\\n\\nuse glam::Vec2;\\n\\nuse super::frame::HazardView;\\nuse super::hazard::Hazard;\\nuse super::kinds::*;\\n\\n/// A hazard the ring can see. The sim and the shell both pass their own snapshot.\\npub trait ToolSite {\\n    fn site_alive(&self) -> bool;\\n    fn site_kind(&self) -> u8;\\n    fn site_tool(&self) -> u8;\\n    fn site_x(&self) -> f32;\\n    fn site_z(&self) -> f32;\\n    fn site_radius(&self) -> f32;\\n}\\n\\nimpl ToolSite for Hazard {\\n    fn site_alive(&self) -> bool {\\n        self.alive\\n    }\\n    fn site_kind(&self) -> u8 {\\n        self.kind\\n    }\\n    fn site_tool(&self) -> u8 {\\n        self.tool\\n    }\\n    fn site_x(&self) -> f32 {\\n        self.x\\n    }\\n    fn site_z(&self) -> f32 {\\n        self.z\\n    }\\n    fn site_radius(&self) -> f32 {\\n        self.radius\\n    }\\n}\\n\\nimpl ToolSite for HazardView {\\n    fn site_alive(&self) -> bool {\\n        self.alive\\n    }\\n    fn site_kind(&self) -> u8 {\\n        self.kind\\n    }\\n    fn site_tool(&self) -> u8 {\\n        self.tool\\n    }\\n    fn site_x(&self) -> f32 {\\n        self.x\\n    }\\n    fn site_z(&self) -> f32 {\\n        self.z\\n    }\\n    fn site_radius(&self) -> f32 {\\n        self.radius\\n    }\\n}\\n\\n/// Left-stick flick. Up is Scalpel, then clockwise: Forceps, Suture, Suction, Laser, Gel, Scanner, IV.\\n/// Short of 0.55 the stick does not change tools.\\npub fn octant(stick: Vec2) -> Option<u8> {\\n    if stick.length() < 0.55 {\\n        return None;\\n    }\\n    let ang = stick.x.atan2(stick.y);\\n    Some((ang / std::f32::consts::FRAC_PI_4).round() as i32).map(|i| i.rem_euclid(8) as u8)\\n}\\n\\n/// L1 / R1 and the mouse wheel. The ring is eight tools; Cryoprobe and Dressing are not stops on it.\\npub fn cycle(tool: u8, forward: bool) -> u8 {\\n    let step = if forward { 1 } else { 7 };\\n    tool.wrapping_add(step) % 8\\n}\\n\\n/// Tray click. Eight slots along z = 5.4, x = -3.5 + tool. Nothing off that row.\\npub fn tray_tool(x: f32, z: f32) -> Option<u8> {\\n    if (z - 5.4).abs() > 0.7 {\\n        return None;\\n    }\\n    for t in 0..8 {\\n        let tx = -3.5 + t as f32;\\n        if (x - tx).abs() < 0.45 {\\n            return Some(t as u8);\\n        }\\n    }\\n    None\\n}\\n\\n/// Promote the ring from the hazard under `(x, z)`.\\n/// Laser and Scanner become the Cryoprobe on an ember that still wants it.\\n/// Any ring tool becomes Dressing on a closure, or when every remaining wound is a closure.\\n/// An already-resolved probe or dressing is folded back to its ring first, so leaving the wound puts the ring tool back.\\npub fn contextual_tool<T: ToolSite>(ring: u8, x: f32, z: f32, sites: &[T]) -> u8 {\\n    if ring == DEFIB || ring == TOOL_KEEP {\\n        return ring;\\n    }\\n    let ring = match ring {\\n        CRYO => LASER,\\n        DRESSING => GEL,\\n        other => other,\\n    };\\n    let mut any = false;\\n    let mut only_dressing = true;\\n    for site in sites {\\n        if !site.site_alive() || site.site_kind() == K_HEAT {\\n            continue;\\n        }\\n        any = true;\\n        if site.site_kind() != K_DRESSING {\\n            only_dressing = false;\\n        }\\n    }\\n    if any && only_dressing {\\n        return DRESSING;\\n    }\\n    let mut best_d = f32::MAX;\\n    let mut best_tool = None;\\n    for site in sites {\\n        if !site.site_alive() || site.site_kind() == K_HEAT {\\n            continue;\\n        }\\n        let dx = site.site_x() - x;\\n        let dz = site.site_z() - z;\\n        let d = (dx * dx + dz * dz).sqrt();\\n        if d <= site.site_radius() + 0.15 && d < best_d {\\n            best_d = d;\\n            best_tool = Some(site.site_tool());\\n        }\\n    }\\n    if let Some(tool) = best_tool {\\n        if tool == DRESSING {\\n            return DRESSING;\\n        }\\n        if tool == CRYO && (ring == LASER || ring == SCANNER) {\\n            return CRYO;\\n        }\\n    }\\n    if ring <= 7 { ring } else { ring % 8 }\\n}\\n\",\"tool_output_for_prompt\":\"The file /home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224015__x42677a/work/Hands of Harbor: Second Opinion-Trauma Center: Second Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-224015/engine/crates/pav_core/src/games/surgery/map.rs has been created successfully.\",\"tool_output_for_prompt_concise\":\"The file /home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224015__x42677a/work/Hands of Harbor: Second Opinion-Trauma Center: Second Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-224015/engine/crates/pav_core/src/games/surgery/map.rs has been created.\",\"absolute_path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224015__x42677a/work/Hands of Harbor: Second Opinion-Trauma Center: Second Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-224015/engine/crates/pav_core/src/games/surgery/map.rs\",\"edits\":{\"details\":[{\"old_string\":\"\",\"old_line\":1,\"new_string\":\"//! The eight-way ring, and the two tools that are not on it.\\n//! Cryoprobe and Dressing are contextual: the ring stays 0–7, and the hazard under the cursor promotes Laser or Scanner to the probe, or any ring tool to a dressing.\\n\\nuse glam::Vec2;\\n\\nuse super::frame::HazardView;\\nuse super::hazard::Hazard;\\nuse super::kinds::*;\\n\\n/// A hazard the ring can see. The sim and the shell both pass their own snapshot.\\npub trait ToolSite {\\n    fn site_alive(&self) -> bool;\\n    fn site_kind(&self) -> u8;\\n    fn site_tool(&self) -> u8;\\n    fn site_x(&self) -> f32;\\n    fn site_z(&self) -> f32;\\n    fn site_radius(&self) -> f32;\\n}\\n\\nimpl ToolSite for Hazard {\\n    fn site_alive(&self) -> bool {\\n        self.alive\\n    }\\n    fn site_kind(&self) -> u8 {\\n        self.kind\\n    }\\n    fn site_tool(&self) -> u8 {\\n        self.tool\\n    }\\n    fn site_x(&self) -> f32 {\\n        self.x\\n    }\\n    fn site_z(&self) -> f32 {\\n        self.z\\n    }\\n    fn site_radius(&self) -> f32 {\\n        self.radius\\n    }\\n}\\n\\nimpl ToolSite for HazardView {\\n    fn site_alive(&self) -> bool {\\n        self.alive\\n    }\\n    fn site_kind(&self) -> u8 {\\n        self.kind\\n    }\\n    fn site_tool(&self) -> u8 {\\n        self.tool\\n    }\\n    fn site_x(&self) -> f32 {\\n        self.x\\n    }\\n    fn site_z(&self) -> f32 {\\n        self.z\\n    }\\n    fn site_radius(&self) -> f32 {\\n        self.radius\\n    }\\n}\\n\\n/// Left-stick flick. Up is Scalpel, then clockwise: Forceps, Suture, Suction, Laser, Gel, Scanner, IV.\\n/// Short of 0.55 the stick does not change tools.\\npub fn octant(stick: Vec2) -> Option<u8> {\\n    if stick.length() < 0.55 {\\n        return None;\\n    }\\n    let ang = stick.x.atan2(stick.y);\\n    Some((ang / std::f32::consts::FRAC_PI_4).round() as i32).map(|i| i.rem_euclid(8) as u8)\\n}\\n\\n/// L1 / R1 and the mouse wheel. The ring is eight tools; Cryoprobe and Dressing are not stops on it.\\npub fn cycle(tool: u8, forward: bool) -> u8 {\\n    let step = if forward { 1 } else { 7 };\\n    tool.wrapping_add(step) % 8\\n}\\n\\n/// Tray click. Eight slots along z = 5.4, x = -3.5 + tool. Nothing off that row.\\npub fn tray_tool(x: f32, z: f32) -> Option<u8> {\\n    if (z - 5.4).abs() > 0.7 {\\n        return None;\\n    }\\n    for t in 0..8 {\\n        let tx = -3.5 + t as f32;\\n        if (x - tx).abs() < 0.45 {\\n            return Some(t as u8);\\n        }\\n    }\\n    None\\n}\\n\\n/// Promote the ring from the hazard under `(x, z)`.\\n/// Laser and Scanner become the Cryoprobe on an ember that still wants it.\\n/// Any ring tool becomes Dressing on a closure, or when every remaining wound is a closure.\\n/// An already-resolved probe or dressing is folded back to its ring first, so leaving the wound puts the ring tool back.\\npub fn contextual_tool<T: ToolSite>(ring: u8, x: f32, z: f32, sites: &[T]) -> u8 {\\n    if ring == DEFIB || ring == TOOL_KEEP {\\n        return ring;\\n    }\\n    let ring = match ring {\\n        CRYO => LASER,\\n        DRESSING => GEL,\\n        other => other,\\n    };\\n    let mut any = false;\\n    let mut only_dressing = true;\\n    for site in sites {\\n        if !site.site_alive() || site.site_kind() == K_HEAT {\\n            continue;\\n        }\\n        any = true;\\n        if site.site_kind() != K_DRESSING {\\n            only_dressing = false;\\n        }\\n    }\\n    if any && only_dressing {\\n        return DRESSING;\\n    }\\n    let mut best_d = f32::MAX;\\n    let mut best_tool = None;\\n    for site in sites {\\n        if !site.site_alive() || site.site_kind() == K_HEAT {\\n            continue;\\n        }\\n        let dx = site.site_x() - x;\\n        let dz = site.site_z() - z;\\n        let d = (dx * dx + dz * dz).sqrt();\\n        if d <= site.site_radius() + 0.15 && d < best_d {\\n            best_d = d;\\n            best_tool = Some(site.site_tool());\\n        }\\n    }\\n    if let Some(tool) = best_tool {\\n        if tool == DRESSING {\\n            return DRESSING;\\n        }\\n        if tool == CRYO && (ring == LASER || ring == SCANNER) {\\n            return CRYO;\\n        }\\n    }\\n    if ring <= 7 { ring } else { ring % 8 }\\n}\\n\",\"new_line\":1,\"context_before\":\"\",\"context_after\":\"\",\"line_prefix\":\"\"}]}}}","is_error":false},{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-0872bdfe-552a-4dbc-8a27-1d3a6e962eeb-87","content":"{\"type\":\"SearchReplace\",\"EditsApplied\":{\"old_string\":\"mod bot;\\nmod content;\\nmod hazard;\\nmod heart;\\nmod ops;\\nmod story;\\nmod tune;\",\"new_st