.pos[0] < -10.0), \\\"mode {mode} field\\\");\\n            assert!(plate.data.vertices.iter().any(|v| v.pos[0] > 10.0), \\\"mode {mode} field\\\");\\n            let ember = scene.sdfs.iter().any(|s| (s.a.x + 1.2).abs() < 0.05 && (s.a.z - 0.8).abs() < 0.05);\\n            let cursor = scene.sdfs.iter().any(|s| (s.a.x - 2.0).abs() < 0.05 && (s.a.z + 1.0).abs() < 0.05);\\n            assert!(ember, \\\"mode {mode} ember sdf missing\\\");\\n            assert!(cursor, \\\"mode {mode} cursor sdf missing\\\");\\n        }\\n    }\\n}\",\"new_line\":504,\"context_before\":\"    true\\n}\\n\\n\",\"context_after\":\"\",\"line_prefix\":\"\"}]}}}","is_error":false},{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-7c6ebb9e-a69f-4c4d-a826-3c569ca3e55b-115","content":"{\"type\":\"SearchReplace\",\"EditsApplied\":{\"old_string\":\"    [\\\"cargo\\\", \\\"test\\\", \\\"-p\\\", \\\"pav_audio\\\", \\\"--lib\\\", \\\"music_bus_defaults_quiet_and_every_cue_speaks\\\", \\\"--\\\", \\\"--test-threads=1\\\"],\\n]\",\"new_string\":\"    [\\\"cargo\\\", \\\"test\\\", \\\"-p\\\", \\\"pav_audio\\\", \\\"--lib\\\", \\\"music_bus_defaults_quiet_and_every_cue_speaks\\\", \\\"--\\\", \\\"--test-threads=1\\\"],\\n    [\\\"cargo\\\", \\\"test\\\", \\\"-p\\\", \\\"pav_view\\\", \\\"--lib\\\", \\\"surgery::tests::quiet_hub_draws_plate_instruments_hazards_and_cursors\\\", \\\"--\\\", \\\"--test-threads=1\\\"],\\n]\",\"tool_output_for_prompt\":\"The file /home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224015__x42677a/work/Hands of Harbor: Second Opinion-Trauma Center: Second Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-224015/tests/run_all.py has been updated successfully.\",\"tool_output_for_prompt_concise\":\"The file /home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224015__x42677a/work/Hands of Harbor: Second Opinion-Trauma Center: Second Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-224015/tests/run_all.py has been updated.\",\"absolute_path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224015__x42677a/work/Hands of Harbor: Second Opinion-Trauma Center: Second Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-224015/tests/run_all.py\",\"edits\":{\"details\":[{\"old_string\":\"    [\\\"cargo\\\", \\\"test\\\", \\\"-p\\\", \\\"pav_audio\\\", \\\"--lib\\\", \\\"music_bus_defaults_quiet_and_every_cue_speaks\\\", \\\"--\\\", \\\"--test-threads=1\\\"],\\n]\",\"old_line\":21,\"new_string\":\"    [\\\"cargo\\\", \\\"test\\\", \\\"-p\\\", \\\"pav_audio\\\", \\\"--lib\\\", \\\"music_bus_defaults_quiet_and_every_cue_speaks\\\", \\\"--\\\", \\\"--test-threads=1\\\"],\\n    [\\\"cargo\\\", \\\"test\\\", \\\"-p\\\", \\\"pav_view\\\", \\\"--lib\\\", \\\"surgery::tests::quiet_hub_draws_plate_instruments_hazards_and_cursors\\\", \\\"--\\\", \\\"--test-threads=1\\\"],\\n]\",\"new_line\":21,\"context_before\":\"SUITES = [\\n    [\\\"cargo\\\", \\\"test\\\", \\\"-p\\\", \\\"pav_core\\\", \\\"--test\\\", \\\"surgery\\\", \\\"--\\\", \\\"--test-threads=1\\\"],\\n    [\\\"cargo\\\", \\\"test\\\", \\\"-p\\\", \\\"pav_ui\\\", \\\"--lib\\\", \\\"surgery::tests\\\", \\\"--\\\", \\\"--test-threads=1\\\"],\\n\",\"context_after\":\"\\n\\ndef main() -> int:\\n\",\"line_prefix\":\"\"}]}}}","is_error":false},{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-7c6ebb9e-a69f-4c4d-a826-3c569ca3e55b-116","content":"{\"type\":\"SearchReplace\",\"EditsApplied\":{\"old_string\":\"- Hub snapshots still go out at about 15 Hz, cursors included. Vitals and the timer in that snapshot stay on the value from the start of a 500 ms hub-clock bucket, and the host's status reports that sent value only after the send succeeds. A client drops a snapshot from an older bucket. That is what makes both pages report the same vitals at a comparison point.\",\"new_string\":\"- Hub snapshots still go out at about 15 Hz, cursors included. Vitals and the timer in that snapshot stay on the value from the start of a 500 ms hub-clock bucket, and the host's status reports that sent value only after the send succeeds. A client drops a snapshot from an older bucket. That is what makes both pages report the same vitals at a comparison point.\\n- Hub and mirror copies draw the operative field on a coarse plate and leave shadows, bloom, and GI off. A 420×240 plate stalled the software-GPU iframe. Cryoprobe and Dressing are not ring slots: Laser or Scanner on an ember that wants the probe, and any ring tool on a closure, resolve to those tools.\",\"tool_output_for_prompt\":\"The file /home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224015__x42677a/work/PLAN.md has been updated successfully.\",\"tool_output_for_prompt_concise\":\"The file /home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224015__x42677a/work/PLAN.md has been updated.\",\"absolute_path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224015__x42677a/work/PLAN.md\",\"edits\":{\"details\":[{\"old_string\":\"- Hub snapshots still go out at about 15 Hz, cursors included. Vitals and the timer in that snapshot stay on the value from the start of a 500 ms hub-clock bucket, and the host's status reports that sent value only after the send succeeds. A client drops a snapshot from an older bucket. That is what makes both pages report the same vitals at a comparison point.\",\"old_line\":817,\"new_string\":\"- Hub snapshots still go out at about 15 Hz, cursors included. Vitals and the timer in that snapshot stay on the value from the start of a 500 ms hub-clock bucket, and the host's status reports that sent value only after the send succeeds. A client drops a snapshot from an older bucket. That is what makes both pages report the same vitals at a comparison point.\\n- Hub and mirror copies draw the operative field on a coarse plate and leave shadows, bloom, and GI off. A 420×240 plate stalled the software-GPU iframe. Cryoprobe and Dressing are not ring slots: Laser or Scanner on an ember that wants the probe, and any ring tool on a closure, resolve to those tools.\",\"new_line\":817,\"context_before\":\"\\n- Case and story tables live in Rust (`content.rs`, `story.rs`), not toml. The sim reads that one table. A toml loader would be a second copy of the same data.\\n- Cargo cannot put the target directory on a path that contains a colon. The dev folder name has one, so web and test builds set `CARGO_TARGET_DIR` to `work/.harbor-target` and run from the `engine-link` symlink. That directory is deleted after the final pack.\\n\",\"context_after\":\"\",\"line_prefix\":\"\"}]}}}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa38-de6f-7dc0-ae0d-e0f717ed75f2","uuid":"3fe528c0-b9cc-46a0-b919-04456de04871"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_854","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Appending the large test to surgery.rs.\n\nDrafting a test helper to find alive hazards by kind.\n\nAdding a second test helper to find alive hazards by ID.\n\nAdding the `Hazard` import. Drafting a `place` helper for the test. Outlining expected behaviors for `mapped_step`, `raw_step`, and `wake`.\n\nFinished the `place` helper by building a SurgeonInput frame and calling `sim.step`. Drafted the `mapped` helper to clone hazard sites before contextual tool selection, then place the tool. Confirmed that cloning sites beforehand ensures the contextual function sees current hazards.\n\nThe first wake will use TOOL_KEEP directly via place(), since mapped asserts ring <= 7. An ember clear helper will be defined inside the test. After holding, releasing the tool triggers the heat_tool release branch.\n\nConfirmed that contextual tool selection on the release frame correctly upgrades a held LASER to CRYO. Chose `mapped()` over raw placement so the sent tool matches the contextual return. Began drafting the charge loop test, verifying octant mappings for LASER and SCANNER and locating the ember hazard.\n\nConfirmed contextual_tool returns CRYO for both the down and left octants relative to the ember. Placed a laser ring on the ember to trigger the frost stage swap. The test then loops for up to 80 ticks, checking that the ember stays alive and its aux value reaches 0.86 before releasing the held tool.\n\nCompleted the frost charge loop by releasing the held CRYO tool and asserting the ember reaches stage 1. Added a scalpel cycle test that advances the ember to stage 2 over up to 90 ticks. Started drafting a forceps tray test.\n\nDrafted the forceps tray test. It verifies tray_tool returns FORCEPS for the correct slot and None elsewhere, then maps a grab and pull to confirm the hazard is grabbed and later removed.\n\nStarted a second case test using case/2. After waking, it locates a bone hazard and checks that the up-right octant resolves to FORCEPS.\n\nThe case/2 test now rotates the bone hazard with extra flags based on aux values above or below ±12.0. It asserts the bone reaches stage 1. Then it cycles FORCEPS to SUTURE and begins a suture loop, computing along-spline positions from axis, need, and sample counts.\n\nCompleted the suture loop by mapping the suture tool to both sides of the bone spline. Asserted the bone is removed. Started a tether test using the scalpel tool.\n\nFinished the tether test by advancing along the spline and asserting the tether is removed. Added a dressing phase check that wakes until a K_DRESSING hazard appears, then verified the gel octant resolves to GEL and contextual_tool returns DRESSING only near the dressing hazard.\n\nPlaced gel on the dressing hazard and asserted the surgeon tool becomes DRESSING. Then mapped gel to four surrounding offsets, each with up to six ticks, verifying the contextual tool stays DRESSING. Finally checked that the dressing hazard is fully removed.\n\nConfirmed the captured hazard position is valid for the dressing loop because that hazard does not move. Verified the tether spline logic: starting at 0.28, the work reaches 1.12 in about five steps before the loop ends. Noted that the suture side offset must stay below 0.5.\n\nVerified that a dead bone is skipped and the tether remains the nearest alive target. Confirmed IV and dressing spawn together, so contextual tool selection correctly returns DRESSING near the dressing hazard. Checked that 0.55 offsets fall inside the 1.1 radius and mapped the four surrounding quadrants using atan2.\n\nThe dressing loop needs 28 ticks to finish, so 24 is too few. Eight ticks per quadrant with three outer rounds will complete the work and set all four bits.\n\nThe fourth quadrant completes the dressing work and bits in ticks 25–32. Outer loops will retry any ticks that land outside the radius. Paint quality stays at 0.55 because it remains inside the 1.1 radius. The paint check uses bits.count_ones() rather than samples_need. The ember scalpel test needs 60 ticks to finish.\n\nPressure and power both equal 1.0, so the scalpel tool pressure is exactly 1.0. The frost charge adds about 0.0175 per tick. Reaching 0.86 from the initial raw tick requires roughly 48 more ticks, so the 80-tick cap is sufficient. The test releases the held tool immediately when aux crosses 0.86, which keeps the value within the target band.\n\nConfirmed the frost charge loop breaks before the aux value can reach 1.06 or trigger an overheat. Also noted that the initial raw tick cannot already exceed the 0.86 threshold, and that the heat_tool edge case for aux above 1.08 is unreachable during the hold.\n\nConfirmed the release check runs at the loop start and that the held tool is near the hazard. Ready to append the test now. Unused imports are harmless since tests do not deny warnings by default. Cargo test will catch compile errors. Noted a borrow issue in `mirror_predict` where dropping `s` leaves `g.surgeons[i]` accessible.\n\nConfirmed the borrow pattern in `mirror_predict` compiles under Rust 2018 NLL. Will verify whether `contextual_tool` needs an explicit import from ops, since a `pub use` cycle could prevent wildcard imports from resolving. The test will clone `game().hazards` into a slice for `contextual_tool`. Failure messages will include `status()` output, and cap panic messages will also include it.\n\nA `kinds` helper will be added to print hazard kinds, stages, and alive flags for debugging. The bone suture logic was verified: the same `along` value is used for both points of a stitch pair, then the needle recomputes after each stitch.\n\nThe first suture point is safe because side is 0.5, which exceeds the 0.06 threshold. The bone is selected over the distant tether. FORCEPS maps to tray slot -2.5, which sits exactly inside the 0.45 radius check. Ready to append the test.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-c14b8eac-0722-4c15-9c60-f5839eecd53c-117","name":"search_replace","input":{"file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224015__x42677a/work/Hands of Harbor: Second Opinion-Trauma Center: Second Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-224015/engine/crates/pav_core/tests/surgery.rs","old_string":"    all_lines, chain_mul, contextual_tool, cycle, octant, rank_of, tray_tool, Heart, Surgery, CASES, CRYO, DRESSING,","new_string":"    all_lines, chain_mul, contextual_tool, cycle, octant, rank_of, tray_tool, Hazard, Heart, Surgery, CASES, CRYO, DRESSING,"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-c14b8eac-0722-4c15-9c60-f5839eecd53c-118","name":"search_replace","input":{"file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224015__x42677a/work/Hands of Harbor: Second Opinion-Trauma Center: Second Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-224015/engine/crates/pav_core/tests/surgery.rs","old_string":"            println!(\n                \"{skill:.1} {scene} {wins}/5 {:.1} {:.1} {:.0} {par} {suggested}\",\n                time / 5.0,\n                vitals / 5.0,\n                mean_score\n            );\n        }\n    }\n}","new_string":"            println!(\n                \"{skill:.1} {scene} {wins}/5 {:.1} {:.1} {:.0} {par} {suggested}\",\n                time / 5.0,\n                vitals / 5.0,\n                mean_score\n            );\n        }\n    }\n}\n\nfn place(sim: &mut Sim, x: f32, z: f32, tool: u8, use_on: bool, extra: u32) {\n    let mut held = surg::AIM_ABSOLUTE | surg::SNAP | surg::PRECISION | extra;\n    if use_on {\n        held |= surg::USE;\n    }\n    let mut frame = InputFrame::default();\n    frame.surgeons[0] = SurgeonInput {\n        active: true,\n        aim: Vec2::new(x, z),\n        held,\n        pressed: 0,\n        tool,\n        pressure: 1.0,\n    };\n    sim.step(&frame);\n}\n\n/// Ring tools stay 0–7. Cryoprobe and Dressing are whatever `contextual_tool` returns.\nfn mapped(sim: &mut Sim, x: f32, z: f32, ring: u8, use_on: bool, extra: u32) -> u8 {\n    assert!(ring <= 7, \"ring {ring} is outside the eight-way\");\n    let tool = contextual_tool(ring, x, z, &game(sim).hazards);\n    place(sim, x, z, tool, use_on, extra);\n    tool\n}\n\nfn wake(sim: &mut Sim) {\n    place(sim, -8.0, -3.0, TOOL_KEEP, false, 0);\n}\n\nfn alive_id(sim: &Sim, id: u32) -> Option<Hazard> {\n    game(sim).hazards.iter().find(|h| h.id == id && h.alive).cloned()\n}\n\nfn alive_kind(sim: &Sim, kind: u8) -> Option<Hazard> {\n    game(sim).hazards.iter().find(|h| h.kind == kind && h.alive).cloned()\n}\n\n#[test]\nfn shipped_mapping_clears_an_ember_and_a_dressing() {\n    let mut sim = Sim::new(\"surgery/case/5\", 1).unwrap();\n    wake(&mut sim);\n    let ember = alive_kind(&sim, K_EMBER).expect(\"case 5 ember\");\n    let id = ember.id;\n    let down = octant(Vec2::new(0.0, -1.0)).expect(\"down\");\n    let left = octant(Vec2::new(-1.0, 0.0)).expect(\"left\");\n    assert_eq!(down, LASER);\n    assert_eq!(left, SCANNER);\n    assert!(octant(Vec2::new(0.2, 0.2)).is_none(), \"a short flick must not pick a tool\");\n    assert_eq!(contextual_tool(down, ember.x, ember.z, &game(&sim).hazards), CRYO);\n    assert_eq!(contextual_tool(left, ember.x, ember.z, &game(&sim).hazards), CRYO);\n\n    place(&mut sim, ember.x, ember.z, down, true, 0);\n    assert_eq!(game(&sim).surgeons[0].tool, CRYO, \"laser on an ember must become the cryoprobe\");\n    for _ in 0..80 {\n        let Some(h) = alive_id(&sim, id) else {\n            panic!(\"ember died during frost {}\", status(&sim));\n        };\n        if h.stage > 0 {\n            break;\n        }\n        if h.aux >= 0.86 {\n            let sent = mapped(&mut sim, h.x, h.z, down, false, 0);\n            assert_eq!(sent, CRYO);\n            break;\n        }\n        let sent = mapped(&mut sim, h.x, h.z, down, true, 0);\n        assert_eq!(sent, CRYO);\n    }\n    let h = alive_id(&sim, id).unwrap_or_else(|| panic!(\"frost did not hold {}\", status(&sim)));\n    assert!(h.stage >= 1, \"ember stage {} aux {} {}\", h.stage, h.aux, status(&sim));\n\n    let scalpel = cycle(cycle(SCANNER, true), true);\n    assert_eq!(scalpel, SCALPEL);\n    for _ in 0..90 {\n        let Some(h) = alive_id(&sim, id) else { panic!(\"ember died under the scalpel {}\", status(&sim)) };\n        if h.stage >= 2 {\n            break;\n        }\n        mapped(&mut sim, h.x, h.z, scalpel, true, 0);\n    }\n    let h = alive_id(&sim, id).unwrap_or_else(|| panic!(\"scalpel missed {}\", status(&sim)));\n    assert!(h.stage >= 2, \"stage {} {}\", h.stage, status(&sim));\n\n    let forceps = tray_tool(-3.5 + FORCEPS as f32, 5.4).expect(\"forceps slot\");\n    assert_eq!(forceps, FORCEPS);\n    assert!(tray_tool(0.0, 0.0).is_none());\n    let h = alive_id(&sim, id).unwrap();\n    mapped(&mut sim, h.x, h.z, forceps, true, 0);\n    let h = alive_id(&sim, id).unwrap_or_else(|| panic!(\"grab lost the ember {}\", status(&sim)));\n    assert!(h.grabbed, \"forceps did not grab {}\", status(&sim));\n    let (dirx, dirz) = (h.axis.cos(), h.axis.sin());\n    mapped(&mut sim, h.x + dirx * 0.9, h.z + dirz * 0.9, forceps, true, 0);\n    assert!(alive_id(&sim, id).is_none(), \"ember still alive {}\", status(&sim));\n\n    let mut sim = Sim::new(\"surgery/case/2\", 2).unwrap();\n    wake(&mut sim);\n    let bone = alive_kind(&sim, K_BONE).expect(\"bone\");\n    let bid = bone.id;\n    let up_right = octant(Vec2::new(1.0, 1.0)).unwrap();\n    assert_eq!(up_right, FORCEPS);\n    for _ in 0..90 {\n        let Some(h) = alive_id(&sim, bid) else { break };\n        if h.stage > 0 {\n            break;\n        }\n        let extra = if h.aux > 12.0 {\n            surg::ROT_L\n        } else if h.aux < -12.0 {\n            surg::ROT_R\n        } else {\n            0\n        };\n        mapped(&mut sim, h.x, h.z, up_right, true, extra);\n    }\n    {\n        let h = alive_id(&sim, bid).unwrap_or_else(|| panic!(\"bone broke early {}\", status(&sim)));\n        assert_eq!(h.stage, 1, \"bone aux {} {}\", h.aux, status(&sim));\n    }\n    let suture = cycle(FORCEPS, true);\n    assert_eq!(suture, SUTURE);\n    for _ in 0..12 {\n        let Some(h) = alive_id(&sim, bid) else { break };\n        let (dirx, dirz) = (h.axis.cos(), h.axis.sin());\n        let span = h.need.max(0.4);\n        let n = h.samples_need.max(1) as f32;\n        let along = -span * 0.5 + (h.samples as f32 + 0.5) * (span / n);\n        for side in [0.5_f32, -0.5] {\n            let Some(h) = alive_id(&sim, bid) else { break };\n            let x = h.x + dirx * along - dirz * side;\n            let z = h.z + dirz * along + dirx * side;\n            mapped(&mut sim, x, z, suture, true, 0);\n        }\n    }\n    assert!(alive_id(&sim, bid).is_none(), \"bone still open {}\", status(&sim));\n\n    let tether = alive_kind(&sim, K_TETHER).unwrap_or_else(|| panic!(\"tether {}\", status(&sim)));\n    let tid = tether.id;\n    let up = octant(Vec2::new(0.0, 1.0)).unwrap();\n    assert_eq!(up, SCALPEL);\n    let mut along = 0.0;\n    for _ in 0..24 {\n        let Some(h) = alive_id(&sim, tid) else { break };\n        let x = h.x + h.axis.cos() * along;\n        let z = h.z + h.axis.sin() * along;\n        mapped(&mut sim, x, z, up, true, 0);\n        along = (along + 0.28).min(h.need + 0.25);\n    }\n    assert!(alive_id(&sim, tid).is_none(), \"tether still there {}\", status(&sim));\n\n    for _ in 0..4 {\n        if alive_kind(&sim, K_DRESSING).is_some() {\n            break;\n        }\n        wake(&mut sim);\n    }\n    let dressing = alive_kind(&sim, K_DRESSING).unwrap_or_else(|| panic!(\"no dressing {}\", status(&sim)));\n    let did = dressing.id;\n    let gel = octant(Vec2::new(-1.0, -1.0)).unwrap();\n    assert_eq!(gel, GEL);\n    assert_eq!(contextual_tool(gel, dressing.x, dressing.z, &game(&sim).hazards), DRESSING);\n    assert_ne!(contextual_tool(gel, 8.0, 3.0, &game(&sim).hazards), DRESSING);\n    place(&mut sim, dressing.x, dressing.z, gel, true, 0);\n    assert_eq!(game(&sim).surgeons[0].tool, DRESSING, \"a closure must auto-select dressing\");\n    let offsets = [(0.55_f32, 0.0), (0.0, 0.55), (-0.55, 0.0), (0.0, -0.55)];\n    for _ in 0..4 {\n        if alive_id(&sim, did).is_none() {\n            break;\n        }\n        for (dx, dz) in offsets {\n            let Some(h) = alive_id(&sim, did) else { break };\n            for _ in 0..8 {\n                if alive_id(&sim, did).is_none() {\n                    break;\n                }\n                let sent = mapped(&mut sim, h.x + dx, h.z + dz, gel, true, 0);\n                assert_eq!(sent, DRESSING);\n            }\n        }\n    }\n    let left = alive_id(&sim, did);\n    assert!(left.is_none(), \"dressing {:?} {}\", left.map(|h| (h.bits, h.work)), status(&sim));\n}"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":3239,"output_tokens":7603,"cache_read_input_tokens":160896,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa38-de6f-7dc0-ae0d-e0f717ed75f2","uuid":"6e1ae9e9-3f0e-48e7-9244-7adddf7ffeb2"}
