{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_858","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The monitor instructs me to keep working and avoid polling.\n\nReviewing code for compile issues. Checking whether `use super::*` in ops.rs correctly imports the parent's public items. Also verifying that dropping a mutable reference to Surgeon is valid.\n\nConfirmed valid NLL after dropping the Surgeon reference. Checked that view test imports and public struct fields are correct. Found a borrow checker issue in `hands()`: it borrows `g.surgeons[i].tool` mutably while also passing `&g.hazards`.\n\nThe `hands()` borrow is safe because `ring` is `Copy`. Verified that `Hazard` is public and test imports are valid. Confirmed `resolve_hands` uses the correct import path. Checked that `shown` properly drops its lock after cloning frames. The monitor's error grep correctly ignores warnings.\n\nI'll wait for the test to finish before investigating potential bugs in bone suture positioning, ember fade during scalpel use, and case 5 heat flatlining. Case 2 script phase A is confirmed correct.\n\nVerified the sequential death of bone and tether. The phase counter increments at the end of the tick, so dressing spawns on the next tick as expected. If the tether clears on its final tick, the next wake loop enters phase B correctly. A vitals drain during bone suture is unlikely because the damage is small.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-1546d75d-cf24-467e-87b4-3818401628cc-123","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224015__x42677a/work/Hands of Harbor: Second Opinion-Trauma Center: Second Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-224015/engine/crates/pav_app/src/product.rs","offset":1,"limit":15}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-1546d75d-cf24-467e-87b4-3818401628cc-124","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__2026110