{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_903","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The p4 timeline starts at 13.55 with a countdown of roughly two.\n\nPlay starts at 16.4. p3 leaves at 21.31, about 4.9 seconds after play begins. The harness removes the last player during the second random delay, which lasts 3 seconds after a 1.5-second first delay. The traffic check occurs at 21.31, before time-up at 24.46.\n\nTraffic accumulated over the full ~4.9 seconds, including the 1.5 seconds before p3 left and the 3 seconds after. The host-leave case is different: play starts at ~13.66 and the host leaves at 16.23, leaving only ~2.57 seconds of active play before the round becomes void. With a ~3 Hz send rate, roughly 7 packets should have been sent during that brief window, yet zero were observed. This suggests sends may not begin until a few seconds into play.\n\nA late-start theory could explain both results: all 15 packets might arrive in the last 2 seconds, leaving the first ~2.5 seconds empty. The idea that the first draw stalls for ~3 seconds was considered, but ruled out because sending happens before drawing.\n\nThe card scene and countdown draw should be fast. The game answered Enter quickly at splash end, so it was responsive during those frames. This makes a stall before the first play frame unlikely.\n\nThe first send should occur within one frame of countdown end, well inside the 2.5-second window. The suspicion now shifts to boot or pump overhead before that send. I will inspect pump() and the surgery tick for code blue to find any heavy first-frame cost. Scene building is not a factor because it happens after sending. I am also re-examining surgery_frame around graphics.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-db75e857-9456-4be1-bcda-1f92de68753f-26","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224015__x42677a/work/Hands of Harbor: Second Opinion-Trauma Center: Second Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-224015/engine/crates/pav_app/src/simhost.rs","offset":140,"limit":180}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-db75e857-9456-4be1-bcda-1f92de68753f-27","name":"grep","input":{"pattern":"fn boot_code|spawn","path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224015__x42677a/work/Hands of Harbor: Second Opinion-Trauma Center: Second Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-224015/engine/crates/pav_core/src/games/surgery","glob":"*.rs"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1949,"output_tokens":1036,"cache_read_input_tokens":76416,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa38-de6f-7dc0-ae0d-e0f717ed75f2","uuid":"de980364-e0b2-4fd5-aedb-119a25b77cbe"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-db75e857-9456-4be1-bcda-1f92de68753f-26","content":"{\"type\":\"ReadFile\",\"FileContent\":{\"content\":\"140→            })\\n            .expect(\\\"spawn simulation thread\\\");\\n        Self { tx, shared, thread: Some(thread) }\\n    }\\n\\n    /// Runs `f` on the simulation thread (fire and forget).\\n    pub fn exec(&self, f: impl FnOnce(&mut Sim) + Send + 'static) {\\n        let _ = self.tx.send(Cmd::Run(Box::new(f)));\\n    }\\n\\n150→    /// Runs `f` on the simulation thread and waits for its result.\\n    pub fn query<R: Send + 'static>(&self, f: impl FnOnce(&mut Sim) -> R + Send + 'static) -> Option<R> {\\n        let (rtx, rrx) = std::sync::mpsc::channel();\\n        self.exec(move |sim| {\\n            let _ = rtx.send(f(sim));\\n        });\\n        rrx.recv_timeout(Duration::from_secs(5)).ok()\\n    }\\n\\n    /// Advances the simulation (the thread does this by itself natively).\\n160→    pub fn pump(&self) {}\\n}\\n\\n#[cfg(target_arch = \\\"wasm32\\\")]\\nimpl SimHost {\\n    pub fn start(mut sim: Sim) -> Self {\\n        let shared = shared_for(&mut sim);\\n        Self { sim: std::cell::RefCell::new(sim), clock: std::cell::RefCell::new(Clock::new()), shared }\\n    }\\n\\n170→    pub fn exec(&self, f: impl FnOnce(&mut Sim) + 'static) {\\n        let mut sim = self.sim.borrow_mut();\\n        f(&mut sim);\\n        let dt = sim.dt();\\n        publish(&mut sim, &self.shared, dt, Instant::now());\\n    }\\n\\n    pub fn query<R: 'static>(&self, f: impl FnOnce(&mut Sim) -> R + 'static) -> Option<R> {\\n        let mut sim = self.sim.borrow_mut();\\n        let r = f(&mut sim);\\n180→        let dt = sim.dt();\\n        publish(&mut sim, &self.shared, dt, Instant::now());\\n        Some(r)\\n    }\\n\\n    /// Runs `n` ticks immediately. The first keeps button edges; the rest see holds only.\\n    pub fn burst(&self, n: u32) {\\n        let mut sim = self.sim.borrow_mut();\\n        let mut input = *self.shared.input.lock().unwrap();\\n        for i in 0..n.min(240) {\\n190→            sim.step(&input);\\n            if i == 0 {\\n                input.pressed = 0;\\n                input.surgery_cmd = None;\\n                for s in &mut input.surgeons {\\n                    s.pressed = 0;\\n                }\\n            }\\n            let dt = sim.dt();\\n            publish(&mut sim, &self.shared, dt, Instant::now());\\n200→        }\\n    }\\n\\n    /// Runs the ticks that are due (called once per frame).\\n    pub fn pump(&self) {\\n        self.clock.borrow_mut().advance(&mut self.sim.borrow_mut(), &self.shared);\\n    }\\n}\\n\\nimpl SimHost {\\n210→    pub fn frames(&self) -> (Arc<RenderFrame>, Arc<RenderFrame>, Instant, f32) {\\n        let f = self.shared.frames.lock().unwrap();\\n        (f.prev.clone(), f.curr.clone(), f.curr_at, f.tick_wall)\\n    }\\n\\n    pub fn control(&self) -> TimeControl {\\n        *self.shared.control.lock().unwrap()\\n    }\\n\\n    pub fn set_control(&self, f: impl FnOnce(&mut TimeControl)) {\\n220→        f(&mut self.shared.control.lock().unwrap());\\n    }\\n}\\n\\n#[cfg(not(target_arch = \\\"wasm32\\\"))]\\nimpl Drop for SimHost {\\n    fn drop(&mut self) {\\n        let _ = self.tx.send(Cmd::Quit);\\n        if let Some(t) = self.thread.take() {\\n            let _ = t.join();\\n230→        }\\n    }\\n}\\n\\nfn publish(sim: &mut Sim, sh: &Shared, tick_wall: f32, at: Instant) {\\n    let events = sim.drain_events();\\n    if !events.is_empty() {\\n        let mut q = sh.events.lock().unwrap();\\n        q.extend(events);\\n        let n = q.len();\\n240→        if n > 512 {\\n            q.drain(..n - 512);\\n        }\\n    }\\n    let frame = Arc::new(sim.frame());\\n    let mut f = sh.frames.lock().unwrap();\\n    f.prev = std::mem::replace(&mut f.curr, frame);\\n    f.curr_at = at;\\n    f.tick_wall = tick_wall;\\n}\\n250→\\n/// Fixed-rate ticking with time controls (pause, single steps, speed, rewind, scrubbing).\\nstruct Clock {\\n    next: Instant,\\n    window_start: Instant,\\n    window_ticks: u32,\\n    busy: Duration,\\n    rewound: bool,\\n    studio_mode: pav_core::prop_preview::StudioMode,\\n}\\n260→\\nimpl Clock {\\n    fn new() -> Self {\\n        Self {\\n            next: Instant::now(),\\n            window_start: Instant::now(),\\n            window_ticks: 0,\\n            busy: Duration::ZERO,\\n            rewound: false,\\n            studio_mode: pav_core::prop_preview::StudioMode::World,\\n270→        }\\n    }\\n\\n    /// Runs whatever is due now; returns how long until the next tick.\\n    fn advance(&mut self, sim: &mut Sim, sh: &Shared) -> Duration {\\n        let previewing = sim.studio_active();\\n        let mode = sim.studio_mode();\\n        if self.studio_mode != mode {\\n            self.studio_mode = mode;\\n            self.next = Instant::now();\\n280→        }\\n        let ctl = *sh.control.lock().unwrap();\\n        // The animation stage has its own play, pause and speed controls. The world's time\\n        // controls stay untouched, including a paused or rewound game behind the stage.\\n        let tick_wall = if previewing { sim.dt() } else { sim.dt() / ctl.speed.clamp(0.01, 16.0) };\\n        let (busy, window_ticks) = (&mut self.busy, &mut self.window_ticks);\\n        let mut tick_once = |sim: &mut Sim, at: Instant| {\\n            let input = if previewing {\\n                InputFrame::default()\\n            } else {\\n290→                let mut i = sh.input.lock().unwrap();\\n                let mut frame = *i;\\n                i.pressed = 0;\\n                i.surgery_cmd = None;\\n                for s in &mut i.surgeons {\\n                    s.pressed = 0;\\n                }\\n                frame.cmd = sh.cmds.lock().unwrap().pop_front();\\n                frame\\n            };\\n300→            let stamp = if previewing { None } else { sh.input_stamp.lock().unw