nt::now();\\n            let step = std::time::Duration::from_micros(16_667);\\n            if now + std::time::Duration::from_micros(2_500) < self.next_draw {\\n                return;\\n            }\\n            self.next_draw = if now > self.next_draw + step { now + step } else { self.next_draw + step };\\n        }\\n        let now = Instant::now();\\n        let dt = (now - self.last).as_secs_f32().min(0.1);\\n        self.last = now;\\n        self.fps.frames += 1;\\n        let since = self.fps.since.elapsed().as_secs_f32();\\n        if since >= 0.5 {\\n            self.fps.fps = self.fps.frames as f32 / since;\\n            self.fps.frame_ms = since * 1000.0 / self.fps.frames as f32;\\n            self.fps.frames = 0;\\n\",\"total_lines\":2296}}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa38-de6f-7dc0-ae0d-e0f717ed75f2","uuid":"7a200e03-d6cb-45fe-9f55-0f1933cc961d"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_906","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The frame loop uses request_redraw in about_to_wait. On WASM it sets ControlFlow::Wait once gfx exists.\n\nRedrawRequested triggers surgery_frame. The missing sends suggest the first frames were extremely slow, likely due to shader compilation for new SDF materials. p4's 15 sends occurred after the initial monster frame completed around t=3s, leaving only about 2 seconds for the remaining frames.\n\nThe zero sends for host-leave are explained by the check logic. It counts sends from remaining players only, not the host. The host is removed from the scenario, so p1, p2, and p3 must have sent and received messages themselves.\n\nThe host sends snapshots and clients send inputs when play is true. The first frame after play should trigger a send. The send_input function returns early only if play, ended, server, or joined are false. Since did_input is initially false, the first send should always proceed.\n\nClients never completed a single frame between countdown end and the end message. The host-leave scenario is unique because the host is removed after only 2.5 seconds, while p4 clients continued sending snapshots for the full 5-second play period. This timing difference is the only variable that could explain why one group stalls while the other does not.\n\nA new hypothesis explains the zero sends. p4's 15 sends may have all occurred in the final 3 seconds after the host left, while both scenarios had zero traffic during the first 2.5 seconds. The countdown lasts 3 seconds, so play starts only after that delay. This would mean no packets are sent until the countdown ends.\n\nThe start message delay is confirmed correct at 2.8 seconds, so the three-second gap before sends must come from the Rust poll() logic. The focus shifts to the `hub.time()` call and the `t >= 0.0` condition that controls when play begins.\n\nThe `hub.time()` call works correctly because p4 sends packets. The delay is not caused by a broken time function. The first frame should send immediately once play begins. The stall is either a three-second lag before the first frame runs after play starts, or play starting three seconds late.\n\nThe first frame after play should send inputs immediately before the heavy draw begins, so it cannot explain the stall. The delay may instead come from the previous frame's quiet card scene, which does not require new shaders.\n\nThe send happens before the scene build, so the first frame should transmit immediately. The stall may instead come from the first operation frame skipping the send because `op` is None or `play` is still false, causing a three-second draw delay before the next frame sends.\n\nThe first operation frame cannot skip the send because play is set at the very start of surgery_frame, before any draw. If time() were still negative, the frame would simply send one input and draw a fast card scene, not stall for three seconds. The real delay must come from the boot or draw step itself.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-a383058b-759c-4b42-a33c-f92fb40544fc-34","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224015__x42677a/work/Hands of Harbor: Second Opinion-Trauma Center: Second Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-224015/engine/crates/pav_core/src/games/surgery/mod.rs","offset":450,"limit":80}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-a383058b-759c-4b42-a33c-f92fb40544fc-35","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224015__x42677a/work/Hands of Harbor: Second Opinion-Trauma Center: Second Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-224015/engine/crates/pav_app/src/hub.rs","offset":100,"limit":90}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-a383058b-759c-4b42-a33c-f92fb40544fc-36","name":"grep","input":{"pattern":"reliable|loss|setTimeout","path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224015__x42677a/work/Hands of Harbor: Second Opinion-Trauma Center: Second Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-224015/tests/hub/harness.html"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":3163,"output_tokens":1932,"cache_read_input_tokens":84864,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa38-de6f-7dc0-ae0d-e0f717ed75f2","uuid":"fa10c240-8e78-43ba-ae35-01e081222cac"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-a383058b-759c-4b42-a33c-f92fb40544fc-34","content":"{\"type\":\"ReadFile\",\"FileContent\":{\"content\":\"450→    fn boot_campaign(&mut self) {\\n        self.campaign = true;\\n        self.coverage = Coverage::default();\\n        self.gifts_unlocked = 0;\\n        self.gifts_used = 0;\\n        self.recent_unlock = 0;\\n        self.immortal = false;\\n        self.one_hit = false;\\n        self.prepare_case(0);\\n        self.mode = M_STORY;\\n460→        self.story_after = false;\\n        self.story_i = 0;\\n    }\\n\\n    fn boot_code(&mut self) {\\n        self.campaign = false;\\n        self.code_blue = true;\\n        self.case_id = -1;\\n        self.coverage = Coverage::default();\\n        self.mode = M_OP;\\n470→        self.outcome = Outcome::Playing;\\n        self.timer = 240.0 * content::diff_timer(self.difficulty);\\n        self.par = 1600;\\n        self.heart = Heart::new(70.0);\\n        self.plate = 9;\\n        self.plate_next = 9;\\n        self.plate_blend = 1.0;\\n        self.hazards.clear();\\n        self.phase_ready = true;\\n        self.phase_i = 0;\\n480→        self.codes_left = content::diff_codes(self.difficulty);\\n        self.code_t = -1.0;\\n        self.blue_t = 0.0;\\n        self.blue_wave = 0;\\n        self.blue_finale = false;\\n        self.elapsed = 0.0;\\n        self.mistakes = 0;\\n        self.rank = 0;\\n        self.shown_score = 0;\\n        self.heat_phase = false;\\n490→        self.reset_hands();\\n        self.spawn_kind_at(K_BLEEDER, -1.15, 0.05, 2.6);\\n        self.spawn_kind_at(K_BLEEDER, 1.25, 0.35, 2.6);\\n    }\\n\\n    fn boot_attract(&mut self) {\\n        self.boot_single(0);\\n        self.mode = M_ATTRACT;\\n        self.immortal = true;\\n        self.one_hit = true;\\n500→        self.skill = 1.0;\\n        self.outcome = Outcome::Playing;\\n    }\\n\\n    pub(crate) fn spawn_kind_at(&mut self, kind: u8, x: f32, z: f32, drain: f32) {\\n        let mut h = Hazard::make(kind, x, z);\\n        if drain >= 0.0 {\\n            h.drain = drain;\\n        }\\n        h.id = self.next_id;\\n510→        self.next_id = self.next_id.wrapping_add(1);\\n        self.hazards.push(h);\\n    }\\n\\n    fn save_checkpoint(&mut self) {\\n        let mut scores = [0; 4];\\n        let mut chains = [0; 4];\\n        let mut best = [0; 4];\\n        let mut meters = [0.0; 4];\\n        let mut tools = [0; 4];\\n520→        let mut xs = [0.0; 4];\\n        let mut zs = [0.0; 4];\\n        for (i, s) in self.surgeons.iter().enumerate() {\\n            scores[i] = s.score;\\n            chains[i] = s.chain;\\n            best[i] = s.best_chain;\\n            meters[i] = s.meter;\\n            tools[i] = s.tool;\\n            xs[i] = s.x;\\n            zs[i] = s.z;\",\"content_concise\":\"450→    fn boot_campaign(&mut self) {\\n        self.campaign = true;\\n        self.coverage = Coverage::default();\\n        self.gifts_unlocked = 0;\\n        self.gifts_used = 0;\\n        self.recent_unlock = 0;\\n        self.immortal = false;\\n        self.one_hit = false;\\n        self.prepare_case(0);\\n        self.mode = M_STORY;\\n460→        self.story_after = false;\\n        self.story_i = 0;\\n    }\\n\\n    fn boot_code(&mut self) {\\n        self.campaign = false;\\n        self.code_blue = true;\\n        self.case_id = -1;\\n        self.coverage = Coverage::default();\\n        self.mode = M_OP;\\n470→        self.outcome = Outcome::Playing;\\n        self.timer = 240.0 * content::diff_timer(self.difficulty);\\n        self.par = 1600;\\n        self.heart = Heart::new(70.0);\\n        self.plate = 9;\\n        self.plate_next = 9;\\n        self.plate_blend = 1.0;\\n        self.hazards.clear();\\n        self.phase_ready = true;\\n        self.phase_i = 0;\\n480→        self.codes_left = content::diff_codes(self.difficulty);\\n        self.code_t = -1.0;\\n        self.blue_t