{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_907","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Checking whether all unreliable messages could be lost during the short window in the network simulation.\n\nThe bridge never counted a send because session.js dropped every packet. The Rust side ignores send failures, so the bridge never sees them. session.js drops sends when the session is ended, the client is not welcomed, or rate limits are exceeded.\n\nThe iframe may be too slow to run surgery_frame between t=0 and the void. p4 proves frames execute and send 15 times, so the first 2.5 seconds might be empty. The puzzle is why frames run during the card but stall for three seconds at play start before the send line.\n\nThe stall occurs at the start of the first play frame, before send_snap. The full code path from surgery_frame entry to send is being traced through drain_hook, poll_pads, link.poll, aim, compose, boot_hub_round, host.pump, and frames.\n\nThe traced code path before send is cheap. The stall likely comes from the previous countdown frame's gfx.draw still running, blocking wasm.\n\nThe countdown frame's draw is too fast to cause a three-second stall. A SwiftShader shader compile is also unlikely because the card scene ran for ten seconds without freezing.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-3e33d8a6-830b-4a88-a47f-3f168ea18c93-37","name":"grep","input":{"pattern":"game traffic|p0 left|start in|conformance","path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224015__x42677a/tmp/grok-goal-907ccca5ce3b/implementer","glob":"hub*.txt"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-3e33d8a6-830b-4a88-a47f-3f168ea18c93-38","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224015__x42677a/work/Hands of Harbor: Second Opinion-Trauma Center: Second Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-224015/engine/crates/pav_view/src/surgery/mod.rs","offset":260,"limit":120