bor: Second Opinion-Trauma Center: Second Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-224015/engine/crates/pav_render/src/renderer.rs\",\"matches\":[{\"line_number\":159,\"content\":\"    pub sdf_instances: usize,\"},{\"line_number\":192,\"content\":\"    sdf_pipeline: wgpu::RenderPipeline,\"},{\"line_number\":194,\"content\":\"    sdf_shadow_pipeline: wgpu::RenderPipeline,\"},{\"line_number\":202,\"content\":\"    sdf_instances: DynBuffer,\"},{\"line_number\":333,\"content\":\"fn sdf_layout() -> wgpu::VertexBufferLayout<'static> {\"},{\"line_number\":548,\"content\":\"        let sdf_buffers = [sdf_layout()];\"},{\"line_number\":549,\"content\":\"        let sdf_pipeline = device.create_render_pipeline(&wgpu::RenderPipelineDescriptor {\"},{\"line_number\":550,\"content\":\"            label: Some(\\\"sdf\\\"),\"},{\"line_number\":554,\"content\":\"                entry_point: Some(\\\"vs_sdf\\\"),\"},{\"line_number\":556,\"content\":\"                buffers: &[Some(sdf_buffers[0].clone())],\"},{\"line_number\":563,\"content\":\"                entry_point: Some(\\\"fs_sdf\\\"),\"},{\"line_number\":586,\"content\":\"        let sdf_shadow_pipeline = device.create_render_pipeline(&wgpu::RenderPipelineDescriptor {\"},{\"line_number\":587,\"content\":\"            label: Some(\\\"sdf shadow\\\"),\"},{\"line_number\":591,\"content\":\"                entry_point: Some(\\\"vs_sdf\\\"),\"},{\"line_number\":593,\"content\":\"                buffers: &[Some(sdf_buffers[0].clone())],\"},{\"line_number\":600,\"content\":\"                entry_point: Some(\\\"fs_sdf_shadow\\\"),\"},{\"line_number\":801,\"content\":\"        let sdf_instances = DynBuffer::new(device, \\\"sdf instances\\\", wgpu::BufferUsages::VERTEX, 16 * 1024);\"},{\"line_number\":816,\"content\":\"            sdf_pipeline,\"},{\"line_number\":818,\"content\":\"            sdf_shadow_pipeline,\"},{\"line_number\":826,\"content\":\"            sdf_instances,\"},{\"line_number\":1224,\"content\":\"        let mut gpu_sdfs: Vec<GpuSdfInstance> = scene\"},{\"line_number\":1225,\"content\":\"            .sdfs\"},{\"line_number\":1234,\"content\":\"        let sdf_count = gpu_sdfs.len() as u32;\"},{\"line_number\":1235,\"content\":\"        gpu_sdfs.extend(scene.sdfs.iter().filter(|s| s.flags & crate::scene::flags::NO_SHADOW == 0).map(|s| GpuSdfInstance {\"},{\"line_number\":1241,\"content\":\"        let sdf_shadow_end = gpu_sdfs.len() as u32;\"},{\"line_number\":1242,\"content\":\"        self.sdf_instances.write(&self.device, &self.queue, bytemuck::cast_slice(&gpu_sdfs));\"},{\"line_number\":1333,\"content\":\"            if sdf_shadow_end > sdf_count {\"},{\"line_number\":1334,\"content\":\"                pass.set_pipeline(&self.sdf_shadow_pipeline);\"},{\"line_number\":1335,\"content\":\"                pass.set_vertex_buffer(0, self.sdf_instances.buf.slice(..));\"},{\"line_number\":1336,\"content\":\"                pass.draw(0..36, sdf_count..sdf_shadow_end);\"},{\"line_number\":1398,\"content\":\"            if sdf_count > 0 {\"},{\"line_number\":1399,\"content\":\"                pass.set_pipeline(&self.sdf_pipeline);\"},{\"line_number\":1400,\"content\":\"                pass.set_vertex_buffer(0, self.sdf_instances.buf.slice(..));\"},{\"line_number\":1401,\"content\":\"                pass.draw(0..36, 0..sdf_count);\"},{\"line_number\":1508,\"content\":\"            sdf_instances: sdf_count as usize,\"}]},{\"path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224015__x42677a/work/Hands of Harbor: Second Opinion-Trauma Center: Second Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-224015/engine/crates/pav_render/src/scene.rs\",\"matches\":[{\"line_number\":607,\"content\":\"    pub sdfs: Vec<SdfInstance>,\"},{\"line_number\":641,\"content\":\"            sdfs: Vec::new(),\"}]}]}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa38-de6f-7dc0-ae0d-e0f717ed75f2","uuid":"4a783092-c452-4419-9f7c-5fd3533911f8"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_912","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"SDFs are instanced cubes.\n\nThe plate mesh is expensive to build on the CPU each frame. It takes roughly 28 milliseconds across four frames. That should not cause a multi-second stall. The reason for the lost packet remains unclear.\n\nThe plate mesh is too small to cause a stall. The real culprit may be another recent change, such as contextual_tool or mirror_predict. A panic during contextual_tool on incomplete mirror hazards could abort the frame before it reaches the network.\n\nA panic in contextual_tool is ruled out. p4 clients sent 15 packets, so the network path works. The old leave code had only a one-packet margin. The new code is slightly slower and misses that window.\n\nThe leave window is about 2.57 seconds of wall clock. During that interval, four games share CPU time, so each game gets roughly one frame. If a single frame takes longer than 2.57 seconds, the send frame never starts before the host leaves.\n\nThe p4 leave window is actually 4.91 seconds. The 1500 millisecond timer uses performance.now(). It expires when the thread wakes up, not when the sleep call begins. If a game frame blocks inside the sleep's macrotask queue, the timer fires early and the loop exits.\n\nThe 1500 millisecond timer is only a minimum. It can stretch by the length of a single long task.\n\nThe leave window was about one second longer than expected. The p4 window was about three seconds longer.\n\np4 ran first and suffered from cold shaders and four concurrent contexts compiling. That should have slowed it down, yet it still sent packets.\n\np4 sent fifteen packets over eight seconds after starting. The leave window from playing to end lasted two point eight seconds with zero packets.\n\nThe first send may be delayed by initialization overhead. Eight slow simulation ticks during clock catch-up could consume three to four seconds before the send even runs. The countdown phase also draws the plate for two point eight seconds before play begins, which would push the send frame past the leave window.\n\nThe card countdown logs show one-second intervals, so the main thread is not blocked by the game during that phase. The gap between start and leave contains no intermediate log lines, suggesting the send frame never began.\n\nThe leave event arrived one second late, not seconds late. The main thread was not blocked for many seconds during play. The game is ticking and timers are accurate. The real issue is that the game chooses not to send, or sends fail. p4 also had accurate one-second card ticks, then logged nothing until p3 left seven seconds later.\n\nThe extra delay in p4 may come from slow status polling while waiting for the phase to become playing, not from heavy frame rendering. The next step is to inspect harness status updates and run a shorter debug test.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-7b863dba-6684-47da-9ab5-50fcb0d11bde-47","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224015__x42677a/tmp/grok-goal-907ccca5ce3b/implementer/hub_four.py","limit":120}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":3884,"output_tokens":1843,"cache_read_input_tokens":105728,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa38-de6f-7dc0-ae0d-e0f717ed75f2","uuid":"58c261f3-627d-40d0-8ea1-6206851bc847"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-7b863dba-6684-47da-9ab5-50fcb0d11bde-47","content":"{\"type\":\"ReadFile\",\"FileContent\":{\"content\":\"1→\\\"\\\"\\\"Four hub harness queries against the packed page. One browser at a time.\\\"\\\"\\\"\\nimport json\\nimport os\\nimport sys\\nfrom pathlib import Path\\nfrom urllib.parse import quote\\n\\nfrom playwright.sync_api import sync_playwright\\n\\n10→PORT = int(sys.argv[1])\\nDEV = \\\"Hands of Harbor: Second Opinion-Trauma Center: Second Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-224015\\\"\\nGAME = f\\\"../../../{DEV}.html\\\"\\nHARNESS = f\\\"/{DEV}/tests/hub/harness.html\\\"\\nOUT = Path(__file__).resolve().parent\\nARGS = [\\n    \\\"--enable-unsafe-webgpu\\\",\\n    \\\"--enable-features=Vulkan\\\",\\n    \\\"--use-webgpu-adapter=swiftshader\\\",\\n    \\\"--use-vulkan=swiftshader\\\",\\n20→    \\\"--use-angle=swiftshader\\\",\\n]\\nQUERIES = [\\n    (\\\"p4\\\", \\\"players=4&latency=150&jitter=50&loss=5&auto=1&limit=20\\\"),\\n    (\\\"leave\\\", \\\"players=4&latency=150&jitter=50&loss=5&scenario=host-leave&auto=1&limit=20\\\"),\\n    (\\\"server\\\", \\\"players=2&scenario=server&auto=1&limit=20\\\"),\\n    (\\\"one\\\", \\\"players=1&auto=1&limit=20\\\"),\\n]\\n\\n\\n30→def run_one(playwright, name, query):\\n    url = f\\\"http://127.0.0.1:{PORT}{quote(HARNESS, safe='/')}?game={quote(GAME)}&{query}\\\"\\n    print(\\\"URL\\\", url, flush=True)\\n    browser = playwright.chromium.launch(headless=False, args=ARGS)\\n    page = browser.new_page(viewport={\\\"width\\\": 1100, \\\"height\\\": 700})\\n    page.goto(url, wait_until=\\\"domcontentloaded\\\", timeout=60000)\\n    try:\\n        page.wait_for_function(\\\"document.body.dataset.complete === 'true'\\\", timeout=180000)\\n    except Exception as exc:\\n        print(name, \\\"WAIT\\\", exc, flush=True)\\n40→    complete = page.evaluate(\\\"() => document.body.dataset.complete || ''\\\")\\n    report = page.evaluate(\\\"() => window.__hubCheck || null\\\")\\n    log = page.locator(\\\"#log\\\").inner_text()\\n    browser.close()\\n    return complete, report, log\\n\\n\\ndef main():\\n    os.environ.setdefault(\\\"PLAYWRIGHT_HOST_PLATFORM_OVERRIDE\\\", \\\"ubuntu24.04-x64\\\")\\n    failed = 0\\n50→    with sync_playwright() as playwright:\\n        for name, query in QUERIES:\\n            print(\\\"RUN\\\", name, query, flush=True)\\n            complete, report, log = run_one(playwright, name, query)\\n            passed = complete == \\\"true\\\" and bool(report) and report.get(\\\"pass\\\") is True\\n            print(name, \\\"complete\\\", complete, \\\"pass\\\", None if not report else report.get(\\\"pass\\\"), flush=True)\\n            lines = [f\\\"query {query}\\\", f\\\"dataset.complete {complete}\\\", f\\\"__hubCheck.pass {None if not report else report.get('pass')}\\\"]\\n            if report:\\n                for check in report.get(\\\"checks\\\") or []:\\n                    mark = \\\"PASS\\\" if check.get(\\\"pass\\\") else \\\"FAIL\\\"\\n60→                    lines.append(f\\\"  {mark} {check.get('name')} {check.get('detail') or ''}\\\".rstrip())\\n                    if not check.get(\\\"pass\\\"):\\n                        print(\\\" FAIL\\\", check.get(\\\"name\\\"), check.get(\\\"detail\\\"), flush=True)\\n            lines.append(\\\"\\\")\\n            lines.append(log)\\n            (OUT / f\\\"hub-{name}.txt\\\").write_text(\\\"\\\\n\\\".join(lines) + \\\"\\\\n\\\")\\n            print(name, \\\"PASS\\\" if passed else \\\"FAIL\\\", flush=True)\\n            if not passed:\\n                failed += 1\\n    print(f\\\"HUB {failed} failed\\\", flush=True)\\n70→    return failed\\n\\n\\nif __name__ == \\\"__main__\\\":\\n    sys.exit(main())\\n\",\"content_concise\":\"1→\\\"\\\"\\\"Four hub harness queries against the packed page. One browser at a time.\\\"\\\"\\\"\\nimport json\\nimport os\\nimport sys\\nfrom pathlib import Path\\nfrom urllib.parse import quote\\n\\nfrom playwright.sync_api import sync_playwright\\n\\n10→PORT = int(sys.argv[1])\\nDEV = \\\"Hands of Harbor: Second Opinion-Trauma Center: Second Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-224015\\\"\\nGAME = f\\\"../../../{DEV}.html\\\"\\nHARNESS = f\\\"/{DEV}/tests/hub/harness.html\\\"\\nOUT = Path(__file__).resolve().parent\\nARGS = [\\n    \\\"--enable-unsafe-webgpu\\\",\\n    \\\"--enable-features=Vulkan\\\",\\n    \\\"--use-webgpu-adapter=swiftshader\\\",\\n    \\\"--use-vulkan=swiftshader\\\",\\n20→    \\\"--use-angle=swiftshader\\\",\\n]\\nQUERIES = [\\n    (\\\"p4\\\", \\\"players=4&latency=150&jitter=50&loss=5&auto=1&limit=20\\\"),\\n    (\\\"leave\\\", \\\"players=4&latency=150&jitter=50&loss=5&scenario=host-leave&auto=1&limit=20\\\"),\\n    (\\\"server\\\", \\\"players=2&scenario=server&auto=1&limit=20\\\"),\\n    (\\\"one\\\", \\\"players=1&auto=1&limit=20\\\"),\\n]\\n\\n\\n30→def run_one(playwright, name, query):\\n    url = f\\\"http://127.0.0.1:{PORT}{quote(HARNESS, safe='/')}?game={quote(GAME)}&{query}\\\"\\n    print(\\\"URL\\\", url, flush=True)\\n    browser = playwright.chromium.launch(headless=False, args=ARGS)\\n    page = browser.new_page(viewport={\\\"width\\\": 1100, \\\"height\\\": 700})\\n    page.goto(url, wait_until=\\\"domcontentloaded\\\", timeout=60000)\\n    try:\\n        page.wait_for_function(\\\"document.body.dataset.complete === 'true'\\\", timeout=180000)\\n    except Exception as exc:\\n        print(name, \\\"WAIT\\\", exc, flush=True)\\n40→    complete = page.evaluate(\\\"() => document.body.dataset.complete || ''\\\")\\n    report = page.evaluate(\\\"() => window.__hubCheck || null\\\")\\n    log = page.locator(\\\"#log\\\").inner_text()\\n    browser.close()\\n    return complete, report, log\\n\\n\\ndef main():\\n    os.environ.setdefault(\\\"PLAYWRIGHT_HOST_PLATFORM_OVERRIDE\\\", \\\"ubuntu24.04-x64\\\")\\n    failed = 0\\n50→    with sync_playwright() as playwright:\\n        for name, query in QUERIES:\\n            print(\\\"RUN\\\", name, query, flush=True)\\n            complete, report, log = run_one(playwright, name, query)\\n            passed = complete == \\\"true\\\" and bool(report) and report.get(\\\"pass\\\") is True\\n            print(name, \\\"complete\\\", complete, \\\"pass\\\", None if not report else report.get(\\\"pass\\\"), flush=True)\\n            lines = [f\\\"query {query}\\\", f\\\"dataset.complete {complete}\\\", f\\\"__hubCheck.pass {None if not report else report.get('pass')}\\\"]\\n            if report:\\n                for check in report.get(\\\"checks\\\") or []:\\n                    mark = \\\"PASS\\\" if check.get(\\\"pass\\\") else \\\"FAIL\\\"\\n60→                    lines.append(f\\\"  {mark} {check.get('name')} {check.get('detail') or ''}\\\".rstrip())\\n                    if not check.get(\\\"pass\\\"):\\n                        print(\\\" FAIL\\\", check.get(\\\"name\\\"), check.get(\\\"detail\\\"), flush=True)\\n            lines.append(\\\"\\\")\\n            lines.append(log)\\n            (OUT / f\\\"hub-{name}.txt\\\").write_text(\\\"\\\\n\\\".join(lines) + \\\"\\\\n\\\")\\n            print(name, \\\"PASS\\\" if passed else \\\"FAIL\\\", flush=True)\\n            if not passed:\\n                failed += 1\\n    print(f\\\"HUB {failed} failed\\\", flush=True)\\n70→    return failed\\n\\n\\nif __name__ == \\\"__main__\\\":\\n    sys.exit(main())\\n\",\"absolute_path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224015__x42677a/tmp/grok-goal-907ccca5ce3b/implementer/hub_four.py\",\"offset\":null,\"limit\":120,\"raw_output\":\"\\\"\\\"\\\"Four hub harness queries against the packed page. One browser at a time.\\\"\\\"\\\"\\nimport json\\nimport os\\nimport sys\\nfrom pathlib import Path\\nfrom urllib.parse import quote\\n\\nfrom playwright.sync_api import sync_playwright\\n\\nPORT = int(sys.argv[1])\\nDEV = \\\"Hands of Harbor: Second Opinion-Trauma Center: Second Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-224015\\\"\\nGAME = f\\\"../../../{DEV}.html\\\"\\nHARNESS = f\\\"/{DEV}/tests/hub/harness.html\\\"\\nOUT = Path(__file__).resolve().parent\\nARGS = [\\n    \\\"--enable-unsafe-webgpu\\\",\\n    \\\"--enable-features=Vulkan\\\",\\n    \\\"--use-webgpu-adapter=swiftshader\\\",\\n    \\\"--use-vulkan=swiftshader\\\",\\n    \\\"--use-angle=swiftshader\\\",\\n]\\nQUERIES = [\\n    (\\\"p4\\\", \\\"players=4&latency=150&jitter=50&loss=5&auto=1&limit=20\\\"),\\n    (\\\"leave\\\", \\\"players=4&latency=150&jitter=50&loss=5&scenario=host-leave&auto=1&limit=20\\\"),\\n    (\\\"server\\\", \\\"players=2&scenario=server&auto=1&limit=20\\\"),\\n    (\\\"one\\\", \\\"players=1&auto=1&limit=20\\\"),\\n]\\n\\n\\ndef run_one(playwright, name, query):\\n    url = f\\\"http://127.0.0.1:{PORT}{quote(HARNESS, safe='/')}?game={quote(GAME)}&{query}\\\"\\n    print(\\\"URL\\\", url, flush=True)\\n    browser = playwright.chromium.launch(headless=False, args=ARGS)\\n    page = browser.new_page(viewport={\\\"width\\\": 1100, \\\"height\\\": 700})\\n    page.goto(url, wait_until=\\\"domcontentloaded\\\", timeout=60000)\\n    try:\\n        page.wait_for_function(\\\"document.body.dataset.complete === 'true'\\\", timeout=180000)\\n    except Exception as exc:\\n        print(name, \\\"WAIT\\\", exc, flush=True)\\n    complete = page.evaluate(\\\"() => document.body.dataset.complete || ''\\\")\\n    report = page.evaluate(\\\"() => window.__hubCheck || null\\\")\\n    log = page.locator(\\\"#log\\\").inner_text()\\n    browser.close()\\n    return complete, report, log\\n\\n\\ndef main():\\n    os.environ.setdefault(\\\"PLAYWRIGHT_HOST_PLATFORM_OVERRIDE\\\", \\\"ubuntu24.04-x64\\\")\\n    failed = 0\\n    with sync_playwright() as playwright:\\n        for name, query in QUERIES:\\n            print(\\\"RUN\\\", name, query, flush=True)\\n            complete, report, log = run_one(playwright, name, query)\\n            passed = complete == \\\"true\\\" and bool(report) and report.get(\\\"pass\\\") is True\\n            print(name, \\\"complete\\\", complete, \\\"pass\\\", None if not report else report.get(\\\"pass\\\"), flush=True)\\n            lines = [f\\\"query {query}\\\", f\\\"dataset.complete {complete}\\\", f\\\"__hubCheck.pass {None if not report else report.get('pass')}\\\"]\\n            if report:\\n                for check in report.get(\\\"checks\\\") or []:\\n                    mark = \\\"PASS\\\" if check.get(\\\"pass\\\") else \\\"FAIL\\\"\\n                    lines.append(f\\\"  {mark} {check.get('name')} {check.get('detail') or ''}\\\".rstrip())\\n                    if not check.get(\\\"pass\\\"):\\n                        print(\\\" FAIL\\\", check.get(\\\"name\\\"), check.get(\\\"detail\\\"), flush=True)\\n            lines.append(\\\"\\\")\\n            lines.append(log)\\n            (OUT / f\\\"hub-{name}.txt\\\").write_text(\\\"\\\\n\\\".join(lines) + \\\"\\\\n\\\")\\n            print(name, \\\"PASS\\\" if passed else \\\"FAIL\\\", flush=True)\\n            if not passed:\\n                failed += 1\\n    print(f\\\"HUB {failed} failed\\\", flush=True)\\n    return failed\\n\\n\\nif __name__ == \\\"__main__\\\":\\n    sys.exit(main())\\n\",\"total_lines\":74}}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa38-de6f-7dc0-ae0d-e0f717ed75f2","uuid":"b76bb533-15c5-41c6-b5a0-ea5c18229594"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_913","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Writing a probe script that runs host-leave and hooks game frames.\n\nIframes complicate direct hooking. I'll inject a script into the parent page to periodically wrap AIHub.send in child frames.\n\nThe script iterates over iframes every 50 ms. It wraps AIHub.send to log frame names, timestamps, keys, and game time. A __game status mode is also planned.\n\nThe server is on port 37019. I'll kill the old monitor tailing hub-rerun.txt and switch to the new log. Chromium will use /tmp/hbr-pw as its temp directory. The leave test needs xvfb and a 120-second timeout. I already read the long-running skill.\n\nI'll block until the test finishes, setting a 90-second timeout. I'm checking session.js for a token-bucket bug where send returns false when tokens are low and Rust does not retry, which could drain tokens before play begins.\n\nRuled out publish, ready/answer, and music as sources of early sends. A double rate limit with loss is unlikely to block all traffic. The host cannot send before the client is welcomed. Now checking whether clients see slot 0 until info parsing finishes, which might make them think they are the host.\n\nA new hypothesis: if every client thinks it is the host, and snapshot bodies exceed 1400 bytes, the send_snap function drops them before AIHub.send is ever called. That would leave the send counter at zero. But p4 passed with fifteen sends, so either the snapshot bodies are small enough to pass through, or not all clients are incorrectly identifying as host.\n\nThe leave seed differs from p4's seed. Snapshot size may be seed-dependent. I am checking whether boot_code hazard spawns scale with the hub seed through its reseeded RNG.\n\nSnapshot size is not seed-dependent. The twelve capped hazards, four cursors, and keys total roughly seven hundred bytes. That is safely under the 1400-byte limit. The probe script will now run.\n\nThe probe will also log when send returns false and the current game time. A NaN in client inputs was considered as a possible cause for silent failures, but JSON.stringify converts NaN to null, so that path is unlikely.\n\nI am reconsidering the NaN theory. The `serde_json::json!` macro might panic when it encounters NaN, aborting the frame before any send is logged. This would explain why the send counter stays at zero.","signature":""},{"type":"text","text":"The last good host-leave run only got one client packet through. This pack got none, so I’m probing the live page to see whether those sends never start or arrive after the host is already gone."},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-bc0be332-0f9f-4858-9afb-04f5400c393c-48","name":"kill_command_or_subagent","input":{"task_id":"1a318e28-238b-4813-91c9-5d95498a4c83"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-bc0be332-0f9f-4858-9afb-04f5400c393c-49","name":"write","input":{"file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224015__x42677a/tmp/grok-goal-907ccca5ce3b/implementer/hub_probe.py","content":"\"\"\"One host-leave run. Log when each iframe calls AIHub.send and what time() is.\"\"\"\nimport os\nimport sys\nfrom pathlib import Path\nfrom urllib.parse import quote\n\nfrom playwright.sync_api import sync_playwright\n\nPORT = int(sys.argv[1])\nDEV = \"Hands of Harbor: Second Opinion-Trauma Center: Second Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-224015\"\nGAME = f\"../../../{DEV}.html\"\nHARNESS = f\"/{DEV}/tests/hub/harness.html\"\nQUERY = \"players=4&latency=150&jitter=50&loss=5&scenario=host-leave&auto=1&limit=20\"\nARGS = [\n    \"--enable-unsafe-webgpu\",\n    \"--enable-features=Vulkan\",\n    \"--use-webgpu-adapter=swiftshader\",\n    \"--use-vulkan=swiftshader\",\n    \"--use-angle=swiftshader\",\n]\nHOOK = r\"\"\"\nsetInterval(() => {\n  const frames = document.querySelectorAll('iframe');\n  frames.forEach((f, i) => {\n    let w;\n    try { w = f.contentWindow; } catch (e) { return; }\n    if (!w || !w.AIHub || w.__sendHooked) return;\n    w.__sendHooked = true;\n    const orig = w.AIHub.send.bind(w.AIHub);\n    w.__sends = [];\n    w.AIHub.send = function (data, opts) {\n      const row = {\n        t: Math.round(performance.now()),\n        hubT: (typeof w.AIHub.time === 'function') ? w.AIHub.time() : null,\n        k: data && data.k,\n        n: (data && (data.n ?? data.bb)) ?? null,\n        len: 0,\n      };\n      try { row.len = JSON.stringify(data).length; } catch (e) { row.len = -1; }\n      w.__sends.push(row);\n      if (w.__sends.length <= 6) console.log('PROBE', i, JSON.stringify(row));\n      return orig(data, opts);\n    };\n  });\n}, 30);\n\"\"\"\n\n\ndef main():\n    os.environ.setdefault(\"PLAYWRIGHT_HOST_PLATFORM_OVERRIDE\", \"ubuntu24.04-x64\")\n    url = f\"http://127.0.0.1:{PORT}{quote(HARNESS, safe='/')}?game={quote(GAME)}&{QUERY}\"\n    print(\"URL\", url, flush=True)\n    lines = []\n    with sync_playwright() as playwright:\n        browser = playwright.chromium.launch(headless=False, args=ARGS)\n        page = browser.new_page(viewport={\"width\": 1100, \"height\": 700})\n        page.add_init_script(HOOK)\n        page.on(\"console\", lambda msg: print(\"CONSOLE\", msg.text, flush=True))\n        page.goto(url, wait_until=\"domcontentloaded\", timeout=60000)\n        try:\n            page.wait_for_function(\"document.body.dataset.complete === 'true'\", timeout=180000)\n        except Exception as exc:\n            print(\"WAIT\", exc, flush=True)\n        report = page.evaluate(\"() => window.__hubCheck || null\")\n        log = page.locator(\"#log\").inner_text()\n        sends = page.evaluate(\n            \"\"\"() => [...document.querySelectorAll('iframe')].map((f, i) => {\n                let w; try { w = f.contentWindow; } catch (e) { return { i, err: String(e) }; }\n                return { i, hooked: !!(w && w.__sendHooked), n: w && w.__sends ? w.__sends.length : 0,\n                         first: w && w.__sends ? w.__sends.slice(0, 4) : [],\n                         time: w && w.AIHub && w.AIHub.time ? w.AIHub.time() : null,\n                         active: w && w.AIHub ? w.AIHub.active : null,\n                         isHost: w && w.AIHub ? w.AIHub.isHost : null };\n            })\"\"\"\n        )\n        print(\"REPORT\", report.get(\"pass\") if report else None, flush=True)\n        print(\"SENDS\", sends, flush=True)\n        lines.append(str(sends))\n        lines.append(log)\n        browser.close()\n    Path(__file__).resolve().parent.joinpath(\"hub-probe.txt\").write_text(\"\\n\".join(lines) + \"\\n\")\n\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    sys.exit(main() or 0)\n"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2811,"output_tokens":2960,"cache_read_input_tokens":109568,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa38-de6f-7dc0-ae0d-e0f717ed75f2","uuid":"f25c0ee9-b467-4a2e-ae1a-58d8445baced"}
