 their mesh, plus dynamic meshes.\"},{\"line_number\":266,\"content\":\"                    has_dynamic_offset: false,\"},{\"line_number\":374,\"content\":\"                has_dynamic_offset: false,\"},{\"line_number\":388,\"content\":\"                        has_dynamic_offset: false,\"},{\"line_number\":425,\"content\":\"                        has_dynamic_offset: false,\"},{\"line_number\":691,\"content\":\"                        has_dynamic_offset: false,\"},{\"line_number\":797,\"content\":\"        let dyn_vertices = DynBuffer::new(device, \\\"dynamic vertices\\\", wgpu::BufferUsages::VERTEX, 64 * 1024);\"},{\"line_number\":798,\"content\":\"        let dyn_indices = DynBuffer::new(device, \\\"dynamic indices\\\", wgpu::BufferUsages::INDEX, 32 * 1024);\"},{\"line_number\":1180,\"content\":\"            for d in &scene.dynamic {\"}]}]}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa38-de6f-7dc0-ae0d-e0f717ed75f2","uuid":"49501805-9fbd-416c-b91c-4d8290b14194"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_917","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The scene builder emits the full world first, then the surgery plate.\n\nThe old quiet mode only skipped the plate, not the demo world geometry. The added plate is the real delta. The probe shows 9.8 seconds before the first send, suggesting old builds were similarly slow but still completed one packet within the leave window.\n\nThe 4× regression is roughly 7 seconds. The plate is the main suspect, but contextual_tool is ruled out since it runs per tick. The quiet flag may not be set correctly for the initial card frames. I am checking product.rs to verify the quiet assignment path.\n\nThe quiet flag is confirmed set correctly in product.rs and preserved through every pump. The 7-second delay likely stems from SwiftShader shader compilation for the new dynamic mesh pipelines, not from the plate geometry itself.\n\nThe 48×28 plate is exactly 64KB, so the initial dynamic vertex buffer fits without reallocation. The full plate would upload roughly 4.8MB and reallocate many times. If quiet mode fails, that upload is the likely source of the multi-second hitch. I will add a log and rebuild to verify.\n\nThe plan is to make quiet frames dramatically cheaper and send network messages at the start of each frame before scene building. If a prior draw blocks the next frame, cheapening the plate fixes the next frame's start time. During countdown, quiet frames already draw the plate, so each 2-second draw adds up. Caching the plate mesh when quiet and the hazard signature hasn't changed would help, but doing this inside emit is messy.\n\nThe quiet plate is only 128 vertices, so it cannot explain the 9.8-second delay. The real bottleneck may be WebGPU adapter serialization. The probe logs show adapter setup times ranging from 69 ms to over 5 seconds, and the harness waits for all clients to finish before starting countdown.\n\nThe 7.6-second gap from last boot to goAt is plausible card and countdown time. The real mystery is the 9.8 seconds after goAt where no network message is sent despite the simulation running. play becomes true at hubT=0, so the first frame should have sent immediately.\n\nThe first frame at hubT=0 sampled time() before play became true, so it never sent. It then spent 9.8 seconds drawing and pumping before the next frame could send. A single frame is taking roughly ten seconds. The fix is to make that frame cheap.\n\nA card or countdown frame runs poll, compose, pump, scene build, egui, and gpu draw. The old build probably sent once because its frames were about one second. The new plate may have pushed the first frame to ten seconds. A 48×28 deforming mesh in software vertex processing could easily cause that slowdown.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-2f7fa070-e73a-4495-acbd-dbb07bbe9d73-54","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224015__x42677a/work/Hands of Harbor: Second Opinion-Trauma Center: Second Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-224015/engine/crates/pav_view/src/build.rs","offset":1280,"limit":50}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-2f7fa070-e73a-4495-acbd-dbb07bbe9d73-55","name":"grep","input":{"pattern":"fn build\\(","path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224015__x42677a/work/Hands of Harbor: Second Opinion-Trauma Center: Second Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-224015/engine/crates/pav_view/src/build.rs"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":3580,"output_tokens":1615,"cache_read_input_tokens":118400,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa38-de6f-7dc0-ae0d-e0f717ed75f2","uuid":"7fa6b8ae-c493-406e-a7c8-2957fe366bc5"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-2f7fa070-e73a-4495-acbd-dbb07bbe9d73-54","content":"{\"type\":\"ReadFile\",\"FileContent\":{\"content\":\"1280→                        materials,\\n                        palette,\\n                        meshes: list,\\n                        sdfs,\\n                        lights,\\n                        terrain,\\n                        custom,\\n                        prop_lights,\\n                    },\\n                );\\n1290→            }\\n            for l in &chunk.labels {\\n                emit_label(&mut scene.texts, l, rig);\\n            }\\n            for z in chunk.zones.iter().filter(|z| !z.label.is_empty() || (z.kind == ZoneKind::Start && z.color.is_some())) {\\n                let text = if !z.label.is_empty() { z.label.clone() } else { \\\"START\\\".into() };\\n                let (w, d) = (z.max.x - z.min.x, z.max.z - z.min.z);\\n                // Light text on dark markings, dark text on light ones (or on the bare floor).\\n                let lum = z.color.map(|c| 0.2126 * c.0[0] + 0.7152 * c.0[1] + 0.0722 * c.0[2]).unwrap_or(1.0);\\n                let size = z.label_size.unwrap_or_else(|| {\\n1300→                    // Fit the text along the zone's long side (about 0.58 em per letter).\\n                    let fit = 0.92 * w.max(d) / (0.58 * text.chars().count().max(1) as f32);\\n                    (w.min(d) * 0.32).clamp(0.35, 0.7).min(fit).max(0.2)\\n                });\\n                let label = Label {\\n                    text,\\n                    pos: z.floor_center() + Vec3::Y * 0.035,\\n                    size,\\n                    color: if lum > 0.45 { Color::hex(\\\"#1d1f24\\\") } else { Color::hex(\\\"#f6f3ea\\\") },\\n                    mode: LabelMode::Floor,\\n1310→                    facing: Default::default(),\\n                };\\n                emit_label(&mut scene.texts, &label, rig);\\n            }\