14,107,115,112,97,99,101,95,114,101,115,117,108,116,32,119,111,114,107,115,112,97,99,101,95,112,97,116,104,61,34,47,104,111,109,101,47,109,105,99,104,97,47,100,101,118,47,99,99,45,109,97,116,114,105,120,47,114,117,110,115,47,103,114,111,107,45,120,104,105,103,104,46,98,117,105,108,100,45,118,50,95,95,50,48,50,54,49,49,48,52,45,50,50,52,48,49,53,95,95,120,52,50,54,55,55,97,47,119,111,114,107,34,62,10,78,111,32,109,97,116,99,104,101,115,32,102,111,117,110,100,10,60,47,119,111,114,107,115,112,97,99,101,95,114,101,115,117,108,116,62],\"stderr\":[],\"exit_code\":1,\"match_count\":0,\"file_matches\":[]}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa38-de6f-7dc0-ae0d-e0f717ed75f2","uuid":"5e2f64c4-794c-421b-9b02-bad47e456d8c"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_970","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Reading gfx.rs draw and RedrawRequested handlers. Understanding boot timing.\n\nThe cursor test shows only the first play frame executes. The client stays at mode 8 and vitals 80 while the host advances to mode 3. No further status updates occur for several seconds. The loop likely exits after the first draw because gfx.draw blocks or surface acquisition fails.\n\nThe hub timer advanced four seconds, so JavaScript is running. The wasm frame loop simply stopped firing.\n\nThis is a known wgpu and winit conflict on web. Both use requestAnimationFrame for redraws. After the first present, their animation frames cancel each other out.\n\nThe app.rs comment explains that Poll's scheduler races ahead of the display. Each request_redraw cancels the animation frame still waiting, so the canvas only paints when a frame wins that race and the simulation freezes after a tick or two.\n\nThe fix is to use ControlFlow::Wait instead of Poll. This lets the animation frame run before the next event, and request_redraw happens in about_to_wait after the frame completes.\n\nSolo play works because hub.active is false and gfx.draw always runs. The animation frame conflict only appears during multiplayer countdown when present is skipped.\n\nSolo play likely avoids the freeze because its title screen draws immediately, establishing animation frames before the first multiplayer present. The bug probably only strikes when a present follows a gap of non-presented frames.\n\nThe transition from no-present to first present is the exact failure point. Continuous presents and gaps both keep the loop alive. A panic on the first draw was considered but ruled out because the second frame would have crashed with a console error.\n\nThe first draw may have been too slow to block the main thread, since JavaScript polling continued during the four-second gap. The next step is to inspect hub-cursor4.txt and the gfx.draw implementation for hidden errors.\n\nThe first frame that enables play performs a full scene build. It completed successfully, so the freeze is not caused by egui state.take() hanging inside the second frame. JavaScript polling continued during the stall, which means the event loop stopped scheduling frames rather than the wasm thread blocking.\n\nThe cursor visibility change was ruled out as the cause, since solo play also hides the cursor without freezing. The next step is to inspect the wasm surface present path and winit's request_redraw behavior on web. I will also examine hub.rs timing for when play and armed states activate during boot.\n\nThe client snapshot applied during boot was from the card phase, not the operation. It overwrote the correct timer and heart values. The host likely froze before sending the operation snapshot, so the client remained stuck in the card state.\n\nThe host status shows operation values, so the snapshot was sent before the draw. The client never applied it, which means the client froze after receiving the card snapshot but before the operation snapshot arrived. Both iframes likely freeze after their first heavy present.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-15880492-711f-4d4a-a0c9-67ece6f671aa-9","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224015__x42677a/work/Hands of Harbor: Second Opinion-Trauma Center: Second Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-224015/engine/crates/pav_app/src/gfx.rs","offset":100,"limit":200}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-15880492-711f-4d4a-a0c9-67ece6f671aa-10","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224015__x42677a/work/Hands of Harbor: Second Opinion-Trauma Center: Second Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-224015/engine/crates/pav_app/src/product.rs","offset":820,"limit":80}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-15880492-711f-4d4a-a0c9-67ece6f671aa-11","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224015__x42677a/work/Hands of Harbor: Second Opinion-Trauma Center: Second Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-224015/engine/crates/pav_app/src/app.rs","offset":2140,"limit":50}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-15880492-711f-4d4a-a0c9-67ece6f671aa-12","name":"grep","input":{"pattern":"fn poll|self\\.play|self\\.armed|boot","glob":"**/pav_app/src/hub.rs"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1685,"output_tokens":1866,"cache_read_input_tokens":40704,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa38-de6f-7dc0-ae0d-e0f717ed75f2","uuid":"9a71a05b-235f-482d-8843-38520dd559c9"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-15880492-711f-4d4a-a0c9-67ece6f671aa-9","content":"{\"type\":\"ReadFile\",\"FileContent\":{\"content\":\"100→    }\\n\\n    pub fn resize(&mut self, w: u32, h: u32) {\\n        if w == 0 || h == 0 {\\n            return;\\n        }\\n        self.config.width = w;\\n        self.config.height = h;\\n        self.surface.configure(&self.device, &self.config);\\n    }\\n110→\\n    pub fn set_vsync(&mut self, on: bool) {\\n        self.vsync = on;\\n        let caps = self.surface.get_capabilities(&self.adapter);\\n        self.config.present_mode = present_mode(&caps, on);\\n        self.surface.configure(&self.device, &self.config);\\n    }\\n\\n    /// Acquires the next surface texture, reconfiguring when needed. None = skip this frame.\\n    pub fn acquire(&mut self) -> Option<wgpu::SurfaceTexture> {\\n120→        match self.surface.get_current_texture() {\\n            wgpu::CurrentSurfaceTexture::Success(t) => Some(t),\\n            wgpu::CurrentSurfaceTexture::Suboptimal(t) => {\\n                // Use this frame, reconfigure for the next one.\\n                self.surface.configure(&self.device, &self.config);\\n                Some(t)\\n            }\\n            wgpu::CurrentSurfaceTexture::Outdated | wgpu::CurrentSurfaceTexture::Lost => {\\n                self.surface.configure(&self.device, &self.config);\\n                None\\n130→            }\\n            _ => None,\\n        }\\n    }\\n\\n    pub fn size(&self) -> (u32, u32) {\\n        (self.config.width, self.config.height)\\n    }\\n\\n    /// Renders the scene plus the egui overlay and presents. Texture updates are always\\n140→    /// applied (and the delta cleared), even when the frame is skipped.\\n    pub fn draw(&mut self, scene: &Scene, ui: Option<(&[egui::ClippedPrimitive], &mut egui::TexturesDelta, f32)>) -> bool {\\n        let mut ui = ui;\\n        if let Some((_, textures, _)) = ui.as_mut() {\\n            for (id, deltas) in &textures.set {\\n                for delta in deltas {\\n                    self.egui.update_texture(&self.device, &self.queue, *id, delta);\\n                }\\n            }\\n        }\\n150→        let frame = self.acquire();\\n        let submitted = frame.is_some();\\n        if let Some(frame) = frame {\\n            let view = frame.texture.create_view(&wgpu::TextureViewDescriptor::default());\\n            let mut encoder = self.device.create_command_encoder(&wgpu::CommandEncoderDescriptor { label: Some(\\\"frame\\\") });\\n            let size = self.size();\\n            self.renderer.render(&mut encoder, scene, &view, self.config.format, size);\\n            let mut cmds = Vec::new();\\n            if let Some((prims, _, ppp)) = ui.as_ref() {\\n                let sd = egui_wgpu::ScreenDescriptor { size_in_pixels: [size.0, size.1], pixels_per_point: *ppp };\\n160→                cmds = self.egui.update_buffers(&self.device, &self.queue, &mut encoder, prims, &sd);\\n                let pass = encoder.begin_render_pass(&wgpu::RenderPassDescriptor {\\n                    label: Some(\\\"egui\\\"),\\n                    color_attachments: &[Some(wgpu::RenderPassColorAttachment {\\n                        view: &view,\\n                        depth_slice: None,\\n                        resolve_target: None,\\n                        ops: wgpu::Operations { load: wgpu::LoadOp::Load, store: wgpu::StoreOp::Store },\\n                    })],\\n                    depth_stencil_attachment: None,\\n170→                    timestamp_writes: None,\\n                    occlusion_query_set: None,\\n                    multiview_mask: None,\\n                });\\n                self.egui.render(&mut pass.forget_lifetime(), prims, &sd);\\n            }\\n            self.queue.submit(cmds.into_iter().chain([encoder.finish()]));\\n            self.window.pre_present_notify();\\n            self.queue.present(frame);\\n     