v/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224015__x42677a/work/Hands of Harbor: Second Opinion-Trauma Center: Second Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-224015/engine/crates/pav_app/src/hub.rs\",\"matches\":[{\"line_number\":41,\"content\":\"    pub boot: Option<Boot>,\"},{\"line_number\":60,\"content\":\"            boot: None,\"},{\"line_number\":79,\"content\":\"    pub fn poll(&mut self, _dt: f32) -> View {\"},{\"line_number\":105,\"content\":\"        pub booted: bool,\"},{\"line_number\":138,\"content\":\"                booted: false,\"},{\"line_number\":162,\"content\":\"        pub fn poll(&mut self, dt: f32) -> super::View {\"},{\"line_number\":189,\"content\":\"                self.armed = true;\"},{\"line_number\":191,\"content\":\"            if self.armed && t >= 0.0 {\"},{\"line_number\":192,\"content\":\"                self.play = true;\"},{\"line_number\":200,\"content\":\"            let boot = if self.play && !self.booted && self.joined {\"},{\"line_number\":201,\"content\":\"                self.booted = true;\"},{\"line_number\":215,\"content\":\"                play: self.play,\"},{\"line_number\":218,\"content\":\"                boot,\"},{\"line_number\":229,\"content\":\"            if !self.armed || self.ended || self.server || !self.joined {\"},{\"line_number\":272,\"content\":\"            if !self.armed || self.ended || !self.host || !self.joined {\"}]}]}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa38-de6f-7dc0-ae0d-e0f717ed75f2","uuid":"16dd21b8-445d-43d2-ac83-a9ae0c614572"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_971","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Reading STAGE.md to understand the current stage and plan.\n\nThe cursor check fails because `surgery_frame` stops after the first real present. The countdown frames ran without `gfx.draw`. This suggests the first real present breaks the requestAnimationFrame cycle. On wasm, wgpu's `get_current_texture()` may require a rAF callback.\n\nThe root cause is a race between wgpu's internal `requestAnimationFrame` and winit's redraw scheduling. When `ControlFlow` is `Wait`, `RedrawRequested` fires inside the animation frame, but `about_to_wait` calls `request_redraw()` before the next frame can finish. This cancels the pending animation frame and breaks the cycle.\n\nCountdown frames work because they skip drawing entirely. On wasm, `get_current_texture()` in wgpu 23+ may replace the current animation frame callback. When play starts, both `request_redraw` and `present` queue rAF callbacks, which likely collide.\n\nWinit's `request_redraw` stores only one animation frame ID, so calling it twice cancels the first callback. This confirms the race condition. On WebGPU, wgpu can acquire the surface texture synchronously inside the animation frame.\n\nAnother potential cause is that the first `surface.get_current_texture()` after a canvas reset can return None or time out until the pending present completes. The draw function returns false in this case, but `surgery_frame` ignores the result and `about_to_wait` still schedules the next redraw. This means a failed acquire should not stall the loop on its own.\n\nThe main thread was free during the four-second poll, so the GPU is not blocking. The event loop simply stops firing RedrawRequested after the first present. The next step is to determine why request_redraw ceases to work.\n\nThe app.rs comment confirms the race: wgpu's `present()` and winit's `request_redraw` both queue a single animation frame callback, so they cancel each other. The `ControlFlow::Wait` setting was chosen to avoid this by letting the current rAF finish before scheduling the next redraw.\n\nThe wgpu source code is being examined to confirm the exact failure point. A known web bug in wgpu 24 causes `SurfaceTexture::present` to schedule GPU submission asynchronously via `queue.submit`, which likely explains why the animation frame loop stalls after the first real present.\n\nThe cursor data reveals a simpler explanation. The host advances to timer 240 and vitals 69.6, then freezes. The client reaches mode 8 with vitals 80 and timer 0, indicating it applied a CARD snapshot via `apply_mirror` but never advanced further. The client never received an operation snapshot, so the game stalled.\n\nThe host's first heavy draw is unlikely to be the cause. The test polled for four seconds of hub time, which means the main thread was not blocked. The client's event loop may have died before processing the snapshot. The snapshot should apply every frame when set, so a countdown delay is not the issue.\n\nThe four-second poll window spans t=699 to t=4902, which is 4 seconds of hub clock. This clock is driven by the harness in pure JavaScript, not by the game loop. The polls likely read cached `__game.status` values rather than live game state.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-ccdcee0e-f9af-4ba7-93ce-f90ac0adab53-13","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224015__x42677a/work/Hands of Harbor: Second Opinion-Trauma Center: Second Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-224015/engine/crates/pav_app/src/hub.rs","offset":150,"limit":150}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-ccdcee0e-f9af-4ba7-93ce-f90ac0adab53-14","name":"grep","input":{"pattern":"name = \\\"winit\\\"|name = \\\"wgpu\\\"","glob":"**/Cargo.lock"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-ccdcee0e-f9af-4ba7-93ce-f90ac0adab53-15","name":"grep","input":{"pattern":"fn request_redraw|animation_frame|requestAnimationFrame","glob":"**/winit-*/src/**/*.rs"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":4772,"output_tokens":1758,"cache_read_input_tokens":42368,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa38-de6f-7dc0-ae0d-e0f717ed75f2","uuid":"a01908b0-f0ce-4929-9c3b-90d22cb36a01"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-ccdcee0e-f9af-4ba7-93ce-f90ac0adab53-13","content":"{\"type\":\"ReadFile\",\"FileContent\":{\"content\":\"150→                seq: 1,\\n                prev_held: 0,\\n                prev_tool: 0,\\n                latch_pressed: 0,\\n                latch_left: 0,\\n                snap_acc: 0.0,\\n                frame_dt: 0.0,\\n                did_snap: false,\\n                did_input: false,\\n            }\\n160→        }\\n\\n        pub fn poll(&mut self, dt: f32) -> super::View {\\n            self.frame_dt = dt;\\n            let Some(hub) = hub_obj() else {\\n                return super::View::idle();\\n            };\\n            if !flag(&hub, \\\"active\\\") {\\n                return super::View::idle();\\n            }\\n170→            if !self.joined {\\n                if let Some(info) = json_field(&hub, \\\"info\\\") {\\n                    self.take_info(&info);\\n                }\\n            }\\n            if self.joined && !self.readied {\\n                let _ = call(&hub, \\\"ready\\\", &[]);\\n                self.readied = true;\\n            }\\n            if let Some(text) = call(&hub, \\\"poll\\\", &[]).and_then(|v| v.as_string()) {\\n180→                if let Ok(events) = serde_json::from_str::<Vec<serde_json::Value>>(&text) {\\n                    for ev in events {\\n                        self.on_event(&ev);\\n                    }\\n                }\\n            }\\n            let t = call(&hub, \\\"time\\\", &[]).and_then(|v| v.as_f64()).unwrap_or(f64::NEG_INFINITY);\\n            // -Infinity before start. A negative finite value is the countdown.\\n            if self.joined && !self.ended && t.is_finite() {\\n                self.armed = true;\\n190→            }\\n            if self.armed && t >= 0.0 {\\n                self.play = true;\\n            }\\n            for i in 0..4 {\\n                self.remote_age[i] += dt;\\n                if self.remote_age[i] > 0.35 {\\n                    self.remote[i] = None;\\n                }\\n            }\\n200→            let boot = if self.play && !self.booted && self.joined {\\n                self.booted = true;\\n                Some(super::Boot {\\n                    seed: self.seed,\\n                    slots: self.present.clone(),\\n                    server: self.server,\\n                    mirror: !self.host,\\n                })\\n            } else {\\n                None\\n210→            };\\n            super::View {\\n                active: true,\\n                server: self.server,\\n                host: self.host,\\n                play: self.play,\\n                ended: self.ended,\\n                slot: self.slot,\\n                boot,\\n                snap: self.pending_snap.take(),\\n220→                remote: self.remote,\\n                dom: read_dom(&hub),\\n                card_lines: self.card_lines.clone(),\\n                present: self.present.clone(),\\n                time_ms: if t.is_finite() { t as f32 } else { -1.0 },\\n            }\\n        }\\n\\n        pub fn send_input(&mut self, hand: &SurgeonInput) {\\n            if !self.armed || self.ended || self.server || !self.joined {\\n230→                return;\\n            }\\n            let edge = hand.held & !self.prev_held;\\n            if hand.tool != self.prev_tool || edge != 0 {\\n                self.seq = self.seq.wrapping_add(1);\\n                self.latch_pressed |= edge;\\n                self.latch_left = 4;\\n            }\\n            self.prev_held = hand.held;\\n            self.prev_tool = hand.tool;\\n240→            // Iframes often paint far below 60 Hz. Count real time, and always send the first hand.\\n            self.send_acc += self.frame_dt.max(0.0);\\n            if self.did_input && self.send_acc < 1.0 / 15.0 && edge == 0 {\\n                return;\\n            }\\n            self.did_input = true;\\n            self.send_acc = 0.0;\\n            let body = serde_json::json!({\\n                \\\"k\\\": \\\"i\\\",\\n                \\\"s\\\": self.slot,\\n250→                \\\"x\\\": (hand.aim.x * 100.0).round() / 100.0,\\n                \\\"z\\\": (hand.aim.y * 100.0).round() / 100.0,\\n                \\\"abs\\\": if hand.held & surg::AIM_ABSOLUTE != 0 { 1 } else { 0 },\\n                \\\"snap\\\": if hand.held & surg::SNAP != 0 { 1 } else { 0 },\\n                \\\"t\\\": hand.tool,\\n                \\\"h\\\": hand.held,\\n                \\\"pr\\\": hand.pressed | self.latch_pressed,\\n                \\\"p\\\": (hand.pressure * 100.0).round() / 100.0,\\n                \\\"n\\\": self.seq,\\n            })\\n260→            .to_string();\\n            if self.latch_left > 0 {\\n                self.latch_left -= 1;\\n                if self.latch_left == 0 {\\n                    self.latch_pressed = 0;\\n                }\\n            }\\n            self.send_json(&body);\\n        }\\n\\n270→        /// True only when this body was handed to the shim. Callers latch vitals on that.\\n        pub fn send_snap(&mut self, body: &str) -> bool {\\n            if !self.armed || self.ended || !self.host || !self.joined {\\n                return false;\\n            }\\n            self.snap_acc += self.frame_dt.max(0.0);\\n            if self.did_snap && self.snap_acc < 1.0 / 15.0 {\\n                return false;\\n            }\\n            self.did_snap = true;\\n280→            self.snap_acc = 0.0;\\n            if body.len() > 1400 {\\n                return false;\\n            }\\n            self.send_json(body);\\n            true\\n        }\\n\\n        pub fn publish(&mut self, body: &str) {\\n            if !self.joined || self.ended {\\n290→                return;\\n            }\\n            let Some(hub) = hub_obj() else { return };\\n            let _ = call(&hub, \\\"publish\\\", &[wasm_bindgen::JsValue::from_str(b