ed650\\\"\\n\\n[[package]]\\nname = \\\"winit\\\"\\nversion = \\\"0.30.13\\\"\\nsource = \\\"registry+https://github.com/rust-lang/crates.io-index\\\"\\nchecksum = \\\"a6755fa58a9f8350bd1e472d4c3fcc25f824ec358933bba33306d0b63df5978d\\\"\\ndependencies = [\\n \\\"ahash\\\",\\n \\\"android-activity\\\",\\n \\\"atomic-waker\\\",\\n \\\"bitflags 2.13.2\\\",\\n \\\"block2 0.5.1\\\",\\n \\\"bytemuck\\\",\\n\",\"total_lines\":4310}}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa38-de6f-7dc0-ae0d-e0f717ed75f2","uuid":"dafde73a-498f-4472-9b4e-48ce3bdc9a76"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_973","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Checking wgpu 30 web surface present and winit 0.\n\nChecking wgpu 30 request_redraw and cargo registry paths. Reading apply_mirror to understand client state. Looking at Scene construction and egui frame costs. The plan is to keep the swapchain alive during countdown by drawing an empty scene and running egui on every frame.\n\nEmpty countdown presents won't fix the cursor failure. The crash happens after the first full operation present, so frames must keep running after that initial heavy build.\n\nContinuous presents work in solo mode. The loop death is specific to the first present after skipped frames. rerun2 and rerun3 showed zero traffic before host removal, suggesting either extreme slowness or an early loop failure.\n\nProbe data shows the first host snap at 939ms, during countdown. This confirms frames were running and sending while the plate was drawn. The official leave failure with zero traffic is puzzling because the probe wraps AIHub.send and should reflect those sends. The official stats.sent counter only increments when the game posts a type:send before ended.\n\nThe official leave check runs immediately after host removal, while the probe hook fires later. The armed pack's first snap at 939ms occurred during countdown, before the host left, so it should have incremented the sent counter. The mismatch between the probe and the official check likely stems from flaky timing or a difference between the probe's send hook and the actual stats.sent counter.\n\nThe four-player stress test is slower than a solo leave probe. The remaining clients show zero traffic because the check only counts players still present; the host was removed before they could exchange messages. The loop did continue, but under heavy load the clients were too slow to send or receive before the host left.\n\nThe pack4 skip-draw loop sends 40 frames during countdown but dies on the first real present, so cursor and vitals never advance during play. The fix requires both cheap countdown frames to build traffic margin and a surviving frame loop through the transition to real presents.\n\nEmpty countdown frames might still be too slow if egui, fonts, and present run on a software GPU across four frames. The full plate was already too expensive. The first heavy scene could still time out on get_current_texture, though about_to_wait should reschedule the next frame after draw returns.\n\nThe cursor test polled successfully and the host status advanced by exactly one operation tick, confirming the full scene draw returned. The subsequent freeze matches the rAF-cancel-after-first-present signature when presents were skipped before. The fix is to always present during countdown, building an empty Scene with clear color only while still running egui and draw so the swapchain path stays alive.\n\nA wasm setTimeout safety net will request redraws roughly 32 ms after the last one. This guarantees play frames keep advancing even if a cancelled rAF stalls the loop. The kick should be added now to avoid another full pack-and-test cycle if empty presents still fail on the first heavy scene draw. The implementation uses a thread-local Cell and wasm_bindgen::JsCast to avoid closure leaks.\n\nThe `arm_redraw` function stores the winit Window in a thread-local `RefCell` and sets an `ARMED` flag. The window is cloneable because winit 0.30 wraps it in an `Rc`.\n\nThe closure-based timeout approach has a flaw: after it fires, the pending flag must be cleared and the callback re-armed for the next frame. A simpler design is to schedule a timeout on every surgery_frame if none is already pending, then clear the pending flag when it fires.\n\nThe timeout safety net risks causing the stall it is meant to prevent. Each request_redraw cancels a waiting animation frame, so a redundant timeout call could cancel the rAF and freeze the loop. The app.rs comment confirms this exact behavior. If about_to_wait already scheduled an rAF, the timeout's extra request would kill it.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-20f4f22c-2ddc-4ae6-9265-8467c5e6f993-19","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224015__x42677a/work/Hands of Harbor: Second Opinion-Trauma Center: Second Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-224015/engine/crates/pav_core/src/games/surgery/mod.rs","offset":290,"limit":120}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-20f4f22c-2ddc-4ae6-9265-8467c5e6f993-20","name":"grep","input":{"pattern":"fn request_redraw","path":"/home/micha/.cargo/registry/src","glob":"**/winit-0.30.13/src/**/*.rs"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2843,"output_tokens":1937,"cache_read_input_tokens":50560,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa38-de6f-7dc0-ae0d-e0f717ed75f2","uuid":"f0cc7bc9-91b2-4a8b-8f84-2a09c89136b2"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-20f4f22c-2ddc-4ae6-9265-8467c5e6f993-19","content":"{\"type\":\"ReadFile\",\"FileContent\":{\"content\":\"290→            players: 1,\\n            blue_t: 0.0,\\n            blue_wave: 0,\\n            blue_finale: false,\\n            popups: [(0, 0.0, 0.0, 0.0); 4],\\n            card_t: 0.0,\\n            spawn_n: 0,\\n            hub_quiet: false,\\n            bot_drive: false,\\n        }\\n300→    }\\n\\n    /// Host or dedicated server: one Code Blue, seeded, with the given player slots active.\\n    pub fn boot_hub_round(sim: &mut Sim, seed: u64, slots: &[u8], quiet: bool) {\\n        sim.state.rng = crate::rng::Rng::new(seed);\\n        let Some(g) = sim.state.play.as_mut().and_then(|p| p.get_mut::<Surgery>()) else { return };\\n        g.boot_code();\\n        for s in &mut g.surgeons {\\n            s.active = false;\\n        }\\n310→        for &id in slots {\\n            let i = id as usize;\\n            if i < 4 {\\n                g.surgeons[i].active = true;\\n            }\\n        }\\n        g.players = slots.len().clamp(1, 4) as u8;\\n        g.hub_quiet = quiet;\\n        g.mode = M_OP;\\n    }\\n320→\\n    /// Client: draw from snapshots. The local hand is predicted in the tick.\\n    pub fn boot_mirror(&mut self) {\\n        self.mode = M_MIRROR;\\n        self.case_id = -1;\\n        self.code_blue = true;\\n        self.outcome = Outcome::Playing;\\n        self.timer = 240.0;\\n        self.heart = Heart::new(70.0);\\n        self.hazards.clear();\\n330→        // Coarse plate, no shadows. A 420×240 mesh stalls the software-GPU iframe.\\n        self.hub_quiet = true;\\n    }\\n\\n    /// Replace the drawn world with a host snapshot. Cursors included; the tick then predicts the local hand.\\n    pub fn apply_mirror(\\n        &mut self,\\n        vitals: f32,\\n        bpm: f32,\\n        phase: f32,\\n340→        flat: bool,\\n        timer: f32,\\n        code_t: f32,\\n        hazards: &[(u32, u8, f32, f32, bool, u8, f32)],\\n        cursors: &[(u8, f32, f32, u8, bool, i32)],\\n    ) {\\n        self.mode = M_MIRROR;\\n        self.case_id = -1;\\n        self.code_blue = true;\\n        self.heart.vitals = vitals.clamp(0.0, 100.0);\\n350→        self.heart.bpm = bpm.max(1.0);\\n        self.heart.phase = phase;\\n        self.heart.flat = flat;\\n        self.timer = timer;\\n        self.code_t = code_t;\\n        self.hazards.clear();\\n        for &(id, kind, x, z, alive, stage, work) in hazards {\\n            let mut h = Hazard::make(kind.min(K_BURN), x, z);\\n            h.id = id;\\n            h.alive = alive;\\n360→            h.stage = stage;\\n            h.work = work;\\n            h.hidden = false;\\n            self.hazards.push(h);\\n        }\\n        for &(slot, x, z, tool, active, score) in cursors {\\n            let i = slot as usize;\\n            if i < 4 {\\n                let s = &mut self.surgeons[i];\\n                s.x = x;\\n370→                s.z = z;\\n                s.tool = tool;\\n                s.active = active;\\n                s.score = score;\\n            }\\n        }\\n    }\\n\\n    pub fn pending_gift(&self) -> u8 {\\n        let (u, d) = (self.gifts_unlocked, self.gifts_used);\\n380→        if self.recent_unlock != 0 && u & self.recent_unlock != 0 && d & self.recent_unlock == 0 {\\n            return self.recent_unlock;\\n        }\\n        for bit in [content::G_HUSH, content::G_ECHO, content::G_DUET] {\\n            if u & bit != 0 && d & bit == 0 {\\n                return bit;\\n            }\\n        }\\n        0\\n    }\\n390→\\n    fn reset_hands(&mut self) {\\n        for (i, s) in self.surgeons.iter_mut().enumerate() {\\n            let name = s.name_i;\\n            *s = Surgeon::new(name);\\n            s.active = i == 0;\\n        }\\n    }\\n\\n    fn prepare_case(&mut self, id: u8) {\\n400→        let Some(def) = case_def(id) else { return };\\n        self.case_id = id as i8;\\n        self.code_blue = false;\\n        self.plate = def.plate;\\n        self.plate_next = def.plate;\\n        self.plate_blend = 1.0;\\n        self.timer = def.timer * content::diff_timer(self.difficulty);\\n        self.par = def.par;\\n        self.heart = Heart::new(def.vitals);\\n        self.hazards.clear();\",\"content_concise\":\"290→            players: 1,\\n            blue_t: 0.0,\\n            blue_wave: 0,\\n            blue_finale: false,\\n            popups: [(0, 0.0, 0.0, 0.0); 4],\\n            card_t: 0.0,\\n            spawn_n: 0,\\n            hub_quiet: false,\\n            bot_drive: false,\\n        }\\n300→    }\\n\\n    /// Host or dedicated server: one Code Blue, seeded, with the given player slots active.\\n    pub fn boot_hub_round(sim: &mut Sim, seed: u64, slots: &[u8], quiet: bool) {\\n        sim.state.rng = crate::rng::Rng::new(seed);\\n        let Some(g) = sim.state.play.as_mut().and_then(|p| p.get_mut::<Surgery>()) else { return };\\n        g.boot_code();\\n        for s in &mut g.surgeons {\\n            s.active = false;\\n        }\\n310→        for &id in slots {\\n            let i = id as usize;\\n            if i < 4 {\\n                g.surgeons[i].active = true;\\n            }\\n        }\\n        g.players = slots.len().clamp(1, 4) as u8;\\n        g.hub_quiet = quiet;\\n        g.mode = M_OP;\\n    }\\n320→\\n    /// Client: draw from snapshots. The local hand is predicted in the tick.\\n    pub fn boot_mirror(&mut self) {\\n        self.mode = M_MIRROR;\\n        self.case_id = -1;\\n        self.code_blue = true;\\n        self.outcome = Outcome::Playing;\\n        self.timer = 240.0;\\n        self.heart = Heart::new(70.0);\\n        self.hazards.clear();\\n330→        // Coarse plate, no shadows. A 420×240 mesh stalls the software-GPU iframe.\\n        self.hub_quiet = true;\\n    }\\n\\n    /// Replace the drawn world with a host snapshot. Cursors included; 