,114,114,111,119,82,105,103,104,116,39,44,32,98,117,98,98,108,101,115,58,32,116,114,117,101,32,125,41,41,59,10,49,48,49,58,32,32,32,32,32,32,32,32,32,32,32,32,104,118,44,32,99,118,32,61,32,104,111,115,116,46,103,101,116,40,34,118,105,116,97,108,115,34,41,44,32,99,108,105,101,110,116,46,103,101,116,40,34,118,105,116,97,108,115,34,41,10,49,48,57,58,32,32,32,32,32,32,32,32,32,32,32,32,32,32,32,32,105,102,32,104,50,32,97,110,100,32,99,50,32,97,110,100,32,104,50,46,103,101,116,40,34,118,105,116,97,108,115,34,41,32,61,61,32,99,50,46,103,101,116,40,34,118,105,116,97,108,115,34,41,32,61,61,32,104,118,58,10,49,49,49,58,32,32,32,32,32,32,32,32,32,32,32,32,32,32,32,32,32,32,32,32,112,114,105,110,116,40,102,34,77,65,84,67,72,32,97,116,32,112,111,108,108,32,123,105,125,34,44,32,104,118,44,32,34,99,117,114,115,111,114,34,44,32,115,116,97,114,116,95,120,44,32,34,45,62,34,44,32,115,101,97,116,95,120,40,104,50,44,32,115,101,97,116,41,41,10,49,49,57,58,32,32,32,32,32,32,32,32,32,32,99,108,105,101,110,116,46,99,111,110,116,101,110,116,87,105,110,100,111,119,46,100,105,115,112,97,116,99,104,69,118,101,110,116,40,110,101,119,32,75,101,121,98,111,97,114,100,69,118,101,110,116,40,39,107,101,121,117,112,39,44,32,123,32,107,101,121,58,32,39,65,114,114,111,119,82,105,103,104,116,39,44,32,98,117,98,98,108,101,115,58,32,116,114,117,101,32,125,41,41,59,10,60,47,119,111,114,107,115,112,97,99,101,95,114,101,115,117,108,116,62],\"stderr\":[],\"exit_code\":0,\"match_count\":15,\"file_matches\":[{\"path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224015__x42677a/tmp/grok-goal-907ccca5ce3b/implementer/hub_cursor.py\",\"matches\":[{\"line_number\":1,\"content\":\"\\\"\\\"\\\"Two copies: client aim moves the host cursor, and both report the same vitals.\\\"\\\"\\\"\"},{\"line_number\":29,\"content\":\"      mode: st && st.mode,\"},{\"line_number\":30,\"content\":\"      vitals: st && st.vitals,\"},{\"line_number\":32,\"content\":\"      cursors: st && st.cursors,\"},{\"line_number\":40,\"content\":\"    cursors = snap.get(\\\"cursors\\\") or []\"},{\"line_number\":41,\"content\":\"    if seat is None or seat >= len(cursors) or cursors[seat] is None:\"},{\"line_number\":43,\"content\":\"    return cursors[seat].get(\\\"x\\\")\"},{\"line_number\":69,\"content\":\"            brief = [(s.get(\\\"mode\\\"), s.get(\\\"t\\\"), s.get(\\\"timer\\\"), s.get(\\\"vitals\\\")) for s in snap]\"},{\"line_number\":70,\"content\":\"            if brief != last and (i % 4 == 0 or any(s.get(\\\"mode\\\") in (3, 8) for s in snap)):\"},{\"line_number\":77,\"content\":\"            if host.get(\\\"mode\\\") == 3 and client.get(\\\"mode\\\") == 8 and all(isinstance(t, (int, float)) and t > 200 for t in times):\"},{\"line_number\":92,\"content\":\"          w.dispatchEvent(new KeyboardEvent('keydown', { key: 'ArrowRight', bubbles: true }));\"},{\"line_number\":101,\"content\":\"            hv, cv = host.get(\\\"vitals\\\"), client.get(\\\"vitals\\\")\"},{\"line_number\":109,\"content\":\"                if h2 and c2 and h2.get(\\\"vitals\\\") == c2.get(\\\"vitals\\\") == hv:\"},{\"line_number\":111,\"content\":\"                    print(f\\\"MATCH at poll {i}\\\", hv, \\\"cursor\\\", start_x, \\\"->\\\", seat_x(h2, seat))\"},{\"line_number\":119,\"content\":\"          client.contentWindow.dispatchEvent(new KeyboardEvent('keyup', { key: 'ArrowRight', bubbles: true }));\"}]}]}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa38-de6f-7dc0-ae0d-e0f717ed75f2","uuid":"3f222d0e-63eb-4fcf-a9a2-592da56d5078"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_978","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Reading hub_cursor.py, status_json, and the cursor log to see exactly what was printed.\n\nThe test requires host and client vitals to match and the client cursor x to increase by more than 0.2. Before, host vitals were 69.6 while client vitals were 80, so they never matched. The client cursor already showed 0.25, likely from a snapshot, while the host cursor remained at zero.\n\nThe client's stuck vitals of 80 suggest it is still showing the CARD snapshot rather than applying operation snapshots. Possible causes include missed operation snapshots, a stopped client loop, or vitals resetting after application.\n\nThe client never updates its own net_vitals because it only sends input, not snapshots. The host alone sets that field on successful sends. Without a snapshot update, the client's status likely falls back to live operation vitals.\n\nThe client's mode 8, timer 0, vitals 80 state matches a card snapshot. apply_mirror sets mode to 8 regardless of the original phase, so the client applied a card snapshot rather than an operation snapshot.\n\nThe host boots the operation at mode 3 with timer 240 and vitals near 70, then sends a snapshot. The client should apply it.\n\nIf the client's frame loop stopped before processing that snapshot, it would remain stuck on the card mirror.\n\nDuring the countdown, both loops run but draw nothing. The host sends card snapshots that the client applies. The client may also call boot_mirror when t reaches zero, but the last card snapshot applied afterward resets the timer to zero.\n\nIn surgery_frame, polling the hub happens first. Then the code checks for boot or pending snapshots.\n\nOn the first frame where t reaches zero, the host boots the operation and sends a snapshot with timer 239.9. The client applies its pending card snapshot instead, reverting to timer zero, vitals 80, and mode 8. This confirms the operation snapshot is arriving too late.\n\nThe host sends the operation snapshot on the first play frame. The client receives it asynchronously through the hub queue, but only applies it when its next surgery_frame polls. If both loops die after that initial draw, neither polls again and the client never applies the snapshot. This matches the \"first real present kills the rAF loop\" failure for both iframes.\n\nThe main thread runs both winit loops and requestAnimationFrame. The first present kills the loop if gfx.draw panics, because about_to_wait never fires to schedule the next frame. That panic becomes an uncaught wasm exception.\n\nThe first play frame's status was published after gfx.draw, so the draw call itself did not panic. The test read that published status successfully, which means about_to_wait likely ran and scheduled a new frame. The next rAF may have failed to fire anyway, since requestAnimationFrame cancels the previous callback before scheduling a new one.\n\nThe canvas handler should not be replaced by wgpu present. getCurrentTexture is called inside the requestAnimationFrame callback, so the known Chrome bug does not apply.\n\ngetCurrentTexture() is only called once per animation frame, but the next callback should still be able to call it again. Swiftshader slowness is unlikely to blame because the draw returned successfully. The focus is shifting to whether an exception might occur inside about_to_wait's request_redraw.\n\nThe `request` method cancels the previous animation frame handle and schedules a new one. A failure there would panic and kill the loop. The `WaitUntil` control flow is not used during countdown; `about_to_wait` always sets `Wait`. In that state, the scheduler does nothing, so the only way to wake up is the `request_redraw` callback itself.\n\nA speculative new cause is being considered: the browser or wgpu might cancel all animation frames when a WebGPU error occurs. Another possibility is that the iframe canvas is offscreen or too small, causing the browser to throttle or pause requestAnimationFrame.\n\nThe countdown animation frame worked, so the canvas is not offscreen. The harness layout or iframe may change after the first present. I will check hub-cursor4.txt for console errors and a panic hook. I also want to inspect renderer.render for unwraps that could panic on the second frame.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-062870e3-e49b-40df-8913-2850655de9c4-31","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224015__x42677a/tmp/grok-goal-907ccca5ce3b/implementer/hub_cursor.py"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-062870e3-e49b-40df-8913-2850655de9c4-32","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224015__x42677a/work/Hands of Harbor: Second Opinion-Trauma Center: Second Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-224015/engine/crates/pav_app/src/product.rs","offset":780,"limit":40}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2919,"output_tokens":2162,"cache_read_input_tokens":64640,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa38-de6f-7dc0-ae0d-e0f717ed75f2","uuid":"00318686-a784-4ea4-93d2-446eed494edd"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-062870e3-e49b-40df-8913-2850655de9c4-31","content":"{\"type\":\"ReadFile\",\"FileContent\":{\"content\":\"1→\\\"\\\"\\\"Two copies: client aim moves the host cursor, and both report the same vitals.\\\"\\\"\\\"\\nimport os\\nimport sys\\nfrom urllib.parse import quote\\n\\nfrom playwright.sync_api import sync_playwright\\n\\nPORT = int(sys.argv[1])\\nDEV = \\\"Hands of Harbor: Second Opinion-Trauma Center: Second Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-224015\\\"\\n10→GAME = f\\\"../../../{DEV}.html\\\"\\nARGS = [\\n    \\\"--enable-unsafe-webgpu\\\",\\n    \\\"--enable-features=Vulkan\\\",\\n    \\\"--use-webgpu-adapter=swiftshader\\\",\\n    \\\"--use-vulkan=swiftshader\\\",\\n    \\\"--use-angle=swiftshader\\\",\\n]\\n\\nSNAP = r\\\"\\\"\\\"() => {\\n20→  const out = [];\\n  for (const f of document.querySelectorAll('iframe')) {\\n    const w = f.contentWindow;\\n    let st = null;\\n    try { st = JSON.parse(w.__game.status()); } catch (e) { st = { err: String(e) }; }\\n    out.push({\\n      host: !!(w.AIHub && w.AIHub.isHost),\\n      me: w.AIHub ? w.AIHub.me : null,\\n      t: w.AIHub ? w.AIHub.time() : null,\\n      mode: st && st.mode,\\n30→      vitals: st && st.vitals,\\n      timer: st && st.timer,\\n      cursors: st && st.cursors,\\n    });\\n  }\\n  return out;\\n}\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n\\n\\ndef seat_x(snap, seat):\\n40→    cursors = snap.get(\\\"cursors\\\") or []\\n    if seat is None or seat >= len(cursors) or cursors[seat] is None:\\n        return None\\n    return cursors[seat].get(\\\"x\\\")\\n\\n\\ndef pair(snap):\\n    host = next((s for s in snap if s.get(\\\"host\\\")), None)\\n    client = next((s for s in snap if s.get(\\\"host\\\") is False), None)\\n    return host, client\\n50→\\n\\ndef main():\\n    os.environ.setdefault(\\\"PLAYWRIGHT_HOST_PLATFORM_OVERRIDE\\\", \\\"ubuntu24.04-x64\\\")\\n    harness = f\\\"/{DEV}/tests/hub/harness.html\\\"\\n    url = (\\n        f\\\"http://127.0.0.1:{PORT}{quote(harness, safe='/')}\\\"\\n        f\\\"?game={quote(GAME)}&players=2&auto=1&limit=30&play=20000\\\"\\n    )\\n    print(\\\"URL\\\", url)\\n60→    with sync_playwright() as p:\\n        browser = p.chromium.launch(headless=False, args=ARGS)\\n        page = browser.new_page(viewport={\\\"width\\\": 1200, \\\"height\\\": 800})\\n        page.goto(url, wait_until=\\\"domcontentloaded\\\", timeout=60000)\\n        before = None\\n        last = None\\n        for i in range(80):\\n            page.wait_for_timeout(500)\\n            snap = page.evaluate(SNAP)\\n            brief = [(s.get(\\\"mode\\\"), s.get(\\\"t\\\"), s.get(\\\"timer\\\"), s.get(\\\"vitals\\\")) for s in snap]\\n70→            if brief != last and (i % 4 == 0 or any(s.get(\\\"mode\\\") in (3, 8) for s in snap)):\\n                print(f\\\"t{i}\\\", brief)\\n                last = brief\\n            host, client = pair(snap)\\n            if not host or not client:\\n                continue\\n            times = [host.get(\\\"t\\\"), client.get(\\\"t\\\")]\\n            if host.get(\\\"mode\\\") == 3 and client.get(\\\"mode\\\") == 8 and all(isinstance(t, (int, float)) and t > 200 for t in times):\\n                before = snap\\n                break\\n80→        print(\\\"BEFORE\\\", before)\\n        if not before:\\n            print(\\\"never started\\\", page.evaluate(SNAP))\\n            browser.close()\\n            sys.exit(1)\\n        host, client = pair(before)\\n        seat = client.get(\\\"me\\\")\\n        start_x = seat_x(host, seat)\\n        page.evaluate(r\\\"\\\"\\\"() => {\\n          const frames = [...document.querySelectorAll('iframe')];\\n90→          const client = frames.find((f) => f.contentWindow.AIHub && !f.contentWindow.AIHub.isHost);\\n          const w = client.contentWindow;\\n          w.dispatchEvent(new KeyboardEvent('keydown', { key: 'ArrowRight', bubbles: true }));\\n        }\\\"\\\"\\\")\\n        matched = None\\n        for i in range(40):\\n            page.wait_for_timeout(100)\\n            snap = page.evaluate(SNAP)\\n            host, client = pair(snap)\\n            if not host or not client:\\n100→                continue\\n            hv, cv = host.get(\\\"vitals\\\"), client.get(\\\"vitals\\\")\\n            hx = seat_x(host, seat)\\n            same = isinstance(hv, (int, float)) and hv == cv\\n            moved = isinstance(start_x, (int, float)) and isinstance(hx, (int, float)) and hx > start_x + 0.2\\n            if same and moved:\\n                page.wait_for_timeout(200)\\n                again = page.evaluate(SNAP)\\n                h2, c2 = pair(again)\\n                if h2 and c2 and h2.get(\\\"vitals\\\") == c2.get(\\\"vitals\\\") == hv:\\n110→                    matched = again\\n                    print(f\\\"MATCH at poll {i}\\\", hv, \\\"cursor\\\", start_x, \\\"->\\\", seat_x(h2, seat))\\n                    break\\n            if i % 5 == 0:\\n                print(f\\\"p{i}\\\", hv, cv, \\\"x\\\", start_x, \\\"->\\\", hx)\\n        page.evaluate(r\\\"\\\"\\\"() => {\\n          const frames = [...document.querySelectorAll('iframe')];\\n          const client = frames.find((f) => f.contentWindow.AIHub && !f.contentWindow.AIHub.isHost);\\n          if (!client) return;\\n          client.contentWindow.dispatchEvent(new KeyboardEvent('keyup', { key: 'ArrowRight', bubbles: true }));\\n120→        }\\\"\\\"\\\")\\n        print(\\\"AFTER\\\", matched if matched else page.evaluate(SNAP))\\n        browser.close()\\n        if not matched:\\n            sys.exit(1)\\n\\n\\nif __name__ == \\\"__main__\\\":\\n    main()\\n\",\"content_concise\":\"1→\\\"\\\"\\\"Two copies: client aim moves the host cursor, and both report the same vitals.\\\"\\\"\\\"\\nimport os\\nimport sys\\nfrom urllib.parse import quote\\n\\nfrom playwright.sync_api import sync_playwright\\n\\nPORT = int(sys.argv[1])\\nDEV = \\\"Hands of Harbor: Second Opinion-Trauma Center: Second Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-224015\\\"\\n10→GAME = f\\\"../../../{DEV}.html\\\"\\nARGS = [\\n    \\\"--enable-unsafe-webgpu\\\",\\n    \\\"--enable-features=Vulkan\\\",\\n    \\\"--use-webgpu-adapter=swiftshader\\\",\\n    \\\"--use-vulkan=swiftshader\\\",\\n    \\\"--use-angle=swiftshader\\\",\\n]\\n\\nSNAP = r\\\"\\\"\\\"() => {\\n20→  const out = [];\\n  for (const f of document.querySelectorAll('iframe')) {\\n    const w = f.contentWindow;\\n    let st = null;\\n    try { st = JSON.parse(w.__game.status()); } catch (e) { st = { err: String(e) }; }\\n    out.push({\\n      host: !!(w.AIHub && w.AIHub.isHost),\\n      me: w.AIHub ? w.AIHub.me : null,\\n      t: w.AIHub ? w.AIHub.time() : null,\\n      mode: st && st.mode,\\n30→      vitals: st && st.vitals,\\n      timer: st && st.timer,\\n      cursors: st && st.cursors,\\n    });\\n  }\\n  return out;\\n}\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n\\n\\ndef seat_x(snap, seat):\\n40→    cursors = snap.get(\\\"cursors\\\") or []\\n    if seat is None or seat >= len(cursors) or cursors[seat] is None:\\n        return None\\n    return cursors[seat].get(\\\"x\\\")\\n\\n\\ndef pair(snap):\\n    host = next((s for s in snap if s.get(\\\"host\\\")), None)\\n    client = next((s for s in snap if s.get(\\\"host\\\") is False), None)\\n    return host, client\\n50→\\n\\ndef main():\\n    os.environ.setdefault(\\\"PLAYWRIGHT_HOST_PLATFORM_OVERRIDE\\\", \\\"ubuntu24.04-x64\\\")\\n    harness = f\\\"/{DEV}/tests/hub/harness.html\\\"\\n    url = (\\n        f\\\"http://127.0.0.1:{PORT}{quote(harness, safe='/')}\\\"\\n        f\\\"?game={quote(GAME)}&players=2&auto=1&limit=30&play=20000\\\"\\n    )\\n    print(\\\"URL\\\", url)\\n60→    with sync_playwright() as p:\\n        browser = p.chromium.launch(headless=False, args=ARGS)\\n        page = browser.new_page(viewport={\\\"width\\\": 1200, \\\"height\\\": 800})\\n        page.goto(url, wait_until=\\\"domcontentloaded\\\", timeout=60000)\\n        before = None\\n        last = None\\n        fo