pchain is presented automatically on the web.\"},{\"line_number\":4175,\"content\":\"            present_modes: vec![wgt::PresentMode::Fifo],\"},{\"line_number\":4222,\"content\":\"        if let wgt::PresentMode::Mailbox | wgt::PresentMode::Immediate = config.present_mode {\"},{\"line_number\":4283,\"content\":\"                // Not representable on a WebGPU canvas: `ExtendedSrgbLinear`\"},{\"line_number\":4354,\"content\":\"                log::error!(\\\"`getCurrentTexture` failed: {err:?}\\\");\"}]}]}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa38-de6f-7dc0-ae0d-e0f717ed75f2","uuid":"2c9ddb73-640f-49a2-b2c5-de5f6b16ed1e"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_981","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Examining winit's web control flow and WaitUntil behavior.\n\nThe app sets `ControlFlow::Wait` and calls `request_redraw` on wasm. Chrome throttles unpainted canvases. A known bug delays the next animation frame when `getCurrentTexture` is called in the same turn as the frame, but large command buffers should not cancel it.\n\nChecking whether egui or the renderer cancels the frame during draw. A race condition may exist if `apply_control_flow` uses a different `WaitUntil(16ms)` path. The pavilion-lite window sets `WaitUntil` in `about_to_wait`, while pav_app uses `Wait`.\n\nInside `handle_event`, the runner is already mutably borrowed as `Running`. Calling `request_redraw` during `about_to_wait` would try to borrow the runner again, which should fail.\n\nThe borrow_mut scope ends before request_redraw runs. The callback therefore holds the runner mutably during send_events. try_borrow fails and the event is queued instead of processed immediately.\n\nThe redraw is queued in `redraw_pending` before `AboutToWait` is handled. `run_until_cleared` drains that queue into `RedrawRequested` events first. Then the callback inserts another redraw into the same pending set.\n\n`apply_control_flow` does not drain `redraw_pending`. The redraw requested during `AboutToWait` therefore remains queued until the next `run_until_cleared`. That next run is triggered by the animation frame callback, which calls `runner.request_redraw`. That method inserts into `redraw_pending` and schedules a new animation frame.\n\nThe redraw loop should keep running even without drawing. The real question is why drawing stops it.\n\nChecking whether the draw call itself schedules an animation frame. wgpu does not use winit's AnimationFrameHandler, so it should not conflict with the scheduled callback. Chrome may only allow one rAF per frame, but getCurrentTexture likely does not register one internally. This points toward a known wgpu bug.\n\nWebGPU `getCurrentTexture()` throws when the document is not visible or outside an animation frame. A GPU process crash from a large command buffer would lose the WebGPU device, but that would not stop the animation frame callback itself. Since the loop continues without running `surgery_frame`, the cause must lie elsewhere.\n\nRuled out iframe memory exhaustion and worker deadlocks. The status JSON is valid, so the JavaScript context is alive. The first frame returns, but the second does not start. Now checking whether renderer.render sets up a callback that prevents further animation frames.\n\nRuled out a main-thread lock blocking the second frame; the test polls successfully for four seconds, so the thread is free. The canvas may be destroyed or its animation-frame handler cancelled after the first present.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-45ccfd73-f0ca-45bb-99eb-119c83dcf30a-36","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/.cargo/registry/src/index.crates.io-1949cf8c6b5b557f/winit-0.30.13/src/platform_impl/web/web_sys/canvas.rs","offset":430,"limit":100}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-45ccfd73-f0ca-45bb-99eb-119c83dcf30a-37","name":"grep","input":{"pattern":"animation_frame_handler.cancel|fn request_animation_frame|remove_canvas|destroy","path":"/home/micha/.cargo/registry/src/index.crates.io-1949cf8c6b5b557f/winit-0.30.13/src/platform_impl/web"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2819,"output_tokens":1705,"cache_read_input_tokens":72960,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa38-de6f-7dc0-ae0d-e0f717ed75f2","uuid":"00264274-e5d4-41f7-bd08-efb6ed416496"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-45ccfd73-f0ca-45bb-99eb-119c83dcf30a-36","content":"{\"type\":\"ReadFile\",\"FileContent\":{\"content\":\"430→    {\\n        self.animation_frame_handler.on_animation_frame(f)\\n    }\\n\\n    pub(crate) fn on_context_menu(&mut self) {\\n        let prevent_default = Rc::clone(&self.prevent_default);\\n        self.on_context_menu =\\n            Some(self.common.add_event(\\\"contextmenu\\\", move |event: PointerEvent| {\\n                if prevent_default.get() {\\n                    event.prevent_default();\\n440→                }\\n            }));\\n    }\\n\\n    pub fn request_fullscreen(&self) {\\n        fullscreen::request_fullscreen(self.document(), self.raw());\\n    }\\n\\n    pub fn exit_fullscreen(&self) {\\n        fullscreen::exit_fullscreen(self.document(), self.raw());\\n450→    }\\n\\n    pub fn is_fullscreen(&self) -> bool {\\n        fullscreen::is_fullscreen(self.document(), self.raw())\\n    }\\n\\n    pub fn request_animation_frame(&self) {\\n        self.animation_frame_handler.request();\\n    }\\n\\n460→    pub(crate) fn handle_scale_change(\\n        &self,\\n        runner: &super::super::event_loop::runner::Shared,\\n        event_handler: impl FnOnce(crate::event::Event<()>),\\n        current_size: PhysicalSize<u32>,\\n        scale: f64,\\n    ) {\\n        // First, we send the `ScaleFactorChanged` event:\\n        self.set_current_size(current_size);\\n        let new_size = {\\n470→            let new_size = Arc::new(Mutex::new(current_size));\\n            event_handler(crate::event::Event::WindowEvent {\\n                window_id: RootWindowId(self.id),\\n                event: crate::event::WindowEvent::ScaleFactorChanged {\\n                    scale_factor: scale,\\n                    inner_size_writer: InnerSizeWriter::new(Arc::downgrade(&new_size)),\\n                },\\n            });\\n\\n            let new_size = *new_size.lock().unwrap();\\n480→            new_size\\n        };\\n\\n        if current_size != new_size {\\n            // Then we resize the canvas to the new size, a new\\n            // `Resized` event will be sent by the `ResizeObserver`:\\n            let new_size = new_size.to_logical(scale);\\n            super::set_canvas_size(self.document(), self.raw(), self.style(), new_size);\\n\\n            // Set the size might not trigger the event because the calculation is inaccurate.\\n490→            self.on_resize_scale\\n                .as_ref()\\n                .expect(\\\"expected Window to still be active\\\")\\n                .notify_resize();\\n        } else if self.old_size() != new_size {\\n            // Then we at least send a resized event.\\n            self.set_old_size(new_size);\\n            runner.send_event(crate::event::Event::WindowEvent {\\n                window_id: RootWindowId(self.id),\\n                event: crate::event::WindowEvent::Resized(new_size),\\n500→            })\\n        }\\n    }\\n\\n    pub fn remove_listeners(&mut self) {\\n        self.on_touch_start = None;\\n        self.on_focus = None;\\n        self.on_blur = None;\\n        self.on_keyboard_release = None;\\n        self.on_keyboard_press = None;\\n510→        self.on_mouse_wheel = None;\\n        self.on_dark_mode = None;\\n        self.pointer_handler.remove_listeners();\\n        self.on_resize_scale = None;\\n        self.on_intersect = None;\\n        self.animation_frame_handler.cancel();\\n        self.on_touch_end = None;\\n        self.on_context_menu = None;\\n    }\\n}\\n520→\\nimpl Common {\\n    pub fn add_event<E, F>(\\n        &self,\\n        event_name: &'static str,\\n        handler: F,\\n    ) -> EventListenerHandle<dyn FnMut(E)>\\n    where\\n        E: 'static + AsRef<web_sys::Event> + wasm_bindgen::convert::FromWasmAbi,\\n        F: 'static + FnMut(E),\",\"content_concise\":\"430→    {\\n        self.animation_frame_handler.on_animation_f