m, and GI off. They do not draw the demo world. A 420×240 plate on top of that world stalled the software-GPU iframe. Hands and snapshots start when the countdown starts, so a slow first operation frame still produces traffic before a host-leave. Cryoprobe and Dressing are not ring slots: Laser or Scanner on an ember that wants the probe, and any ring tool on a closure, resolve to those tools.\",\"new_string\":\"- Hub and mirror copies draw the operative field on a coarse plate and leave shadows, bloom, and GI off. They do not draw the demo world. A 420×240 plate on top of that world stalled the software-GPU iframe. Countdown frames skip the present so four iframes can still exchange hands before a host leaves. The first operation present stops the display callback, so a 32 ms timer steps the sim while that callback is quiet. Hands and snapshots start when the countdown starts. Cryoprobe and Dressing are not ring slots: Laser or Scanner on an ember that wants the probe, and any ring tool on a closure, resolve to those tools.\",\"tool_output_for_prompt\":\"The file /home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224015__x42677a/work/PLAN.md has been updated successfully.\",\"tool_output_for_prompt_concise\":\"The file /home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224015__x42677a/work/PLAN.md has been updated.\",\"absolute_path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224015__x42677a/work/PLAN.md\",\"edits\":{\"details\":[{\"old_string\":\"- Hub and mirror copies draw the operative field on a coarse plate and leave shadows, bloom, and GI off. They do not draw the demo world. A 420×240 plate on top of that world stalled the software-GPU iframe. Hands and snapshots start when the countdown starts, so a slow first operation frame still produces traffic before a host-leave. Cryoprobe and Dressing are not ring slots: Laser or Scanner on an ember that wants the probe, and any ring tool on a closure, resolve to those tools.\",\"old_line\":818,\"new_string\":\"- Hub and mirror copies draw the operative field on a coarse plate and leave shadows, bloom, and GI off. They do not draw the demo world. A 420×240 plate on top of that world stalled the software-GPU iframe. Countdown frames skip the present so four iframes can still exchange hands before a host leaves. The first operation present stops the display callback, so a 32 ms timer steps the sim while that callback is quiet. Hands and snapshots start when the countdown starts. Cryoprobe and Dressing are not ring slots: Laser or Scanner on an ember that wants the probe, and any ring tool on a closure, resolve to those tools.\",\"new_line\":818,\"context_before\":\"- Case and story tables live in Rust (`content.rs`, `story.rs`), not toml. The sim reads that one table. A toml loader would be a second copy of the same data.\\n- Cargo cannot put the target directory on a path that contains a colon. The dev folder name has one, so web and test builds set `CARGO_TARGET_DIR` to `work/.harbor-target` and run from the `engine-link` symlink. That directory is deleted after the final pack.\\n- Hub snapshots still go out at about 15 Hz, cursors included. Vitals and the timer in that snapshot stay on the value from the start of a 500 ms hub-clock bucket, and the host's status reports that sent value only after the send succeeds. A client drops a snapshot from an older bucket. That is what makes both pages report the same vitals at a comparison point.\\n\",\"context_after\":\"\",\"line_prefix\":\"\"}]}}}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa38-de6f-7dc0-ae0d-e0f717ed75f2","uuid":"02d9bcaf-ab70-4622-9204-6a6faa3ac5b7"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_996","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The engine-link is a symlink to the dev folder. Editing the dev folder directly changes what the build sees.\n\nThe dev folder path contains a colon. Cargo target must not be on a colon path. The engine-link symlink avoids this by keeping the manifest path clean. CARGO_TARGET_DIR is set to .harbor-target. I will verify the symlink points correctly. product.rs compiles fine because Rust allows items in any order within a module.\n\nThe `install_tick` signature matches the call site. The closure syntax will follow the existing `Closure::wrap(Box::new(...) as Box<dyn FnMut()>)` pattern for safety. The interval callback will use `Closure::as_ref().unchecked_ref()` to satisfy `&Function`. `frame_now_ms` relies on web_sys, which is available in WASM.\n\nI confirmed `pav_app` already uses `web_sys` in its `install_hook`, so no extra imports are needed. I will now inspect the engine-link and start the build, double-checking that the code reads correctly around the insertion points.\n\nI also spotted two bugs in `install_tick`. First, the interval callback cannot fire while `IN_FRAME` is true because it runs inside `surgery_frame`; it only executes after the guard drops and `LAST_MS` is set. Second, `LAST_MS` is assigned at the very start of `install_tick`, but then reassigned again at the end if the callback itself triggers another `surgery_frame`.\n\nThe interval callback checks LAST_MS at the start. If surgery_frame panics, the guard drops and IN_FRAME clears, leaving LAST_MS stale; the next interval retry handles it. I will switch from Closure::new to Closure::wrap to match the existing code style.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-cdeefba7-6c91-47fb-8286-6f42e1dda8e6-73","name":"run_terminal_command","input":{"command":"ls -ld engine-link && readlink -f engine-link && rg -n \"fn install_tick|fn surgery_frame|IN_FRAME\" \"Hands of Harbor: Second Opinion-Trauma Center: Second Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-224015/engine/crates/pav_app/src/product.rs\"","description":"Confirm engine-link and tick edits"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":3757,"output_tokens":811,"cache_read_input_tokens":115968,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa38-de6f-7dc0-ae0d-e0f717ed75f2","uuid":"934ba715-9611-450d-aa30-e81ea4786826"}
