{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_997","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Starting the WASM build.\n\nThe target directory was deleted, so this is a full rebuild. It may take 5–15 minutes. I will background the process and monitor it. I am also checking that rust-toolchain and the WASM target are available.\n\nThe build script is now running with the specified scene, title, description, theme color, and output filename. The target directory path is absolute, so it will not conflict with the script's internal working directory.\n\nThe monitor script will poll the log file and only print when the build finishes or fails. The tool returns a task ID rather than a PID, so I need to find another way to track the running process.\n\nThe build script will write an EXIT marker to the log when it finishes. The monitor will watch that log file for the result.\n\nI will start the build and background it. The browser should not open until the build completes and the target directory is deleted to prevent memory pressure.\n\nI also need to verify that the rustc WASM target is installed.\n\nI will run a quick WASM-specific cargo check before the full build. This catches compile errors faster than a full dist profile build, since native code excludes wasm-specific cfg blocks.\n\nThe dist profile is slow because of LTO. I will run the WASM cargo check from the engine-link directory with --locked to match the script's resolution.\n\nI will combine the WASM cargo check and the pack build into a single script. If the check fails, the script stops before packing. The monitor will detect the failure by watching for the process exit.\n\nI will set CARGO_TERM_COLOR=never to keep the logs clean. I am starting the build now. Parallel cargo jobs might use too much memory, but previous builds succeeded so I will not limit them.\n\nThe monitor script will poll the log file every 15 seconds for up to 20 minutes. It prints DONE on success, or FAILED with the last 30 lines of output on failure.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-bc2adcb0-db9f-496e-a8ea-d951e6c9384e-74","name":"run_terminal_command","input":{"command":"set -u\ncd /home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224015__x42677a/work\nexport CARGO_TARGET_DIR=\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224015__x42677a/work/.harbor-target\"\nexport CARGO_TERM_COLOR=never\nLOG=\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224015__x42677a/tmp/grok-goal-907ccca5ce3b/implementer/pack5.txt\"\n{\n  echo \"CHECK $(date -Is)\"\n  cargo check --locked --target wasm32-unknown-unknown --manifest-path engine-link/Cargo.toml -p pav_app\n  echo \"CHECK_OK\"\n  echo \"PACK $(date -Is)\"\n  ./engine-link/scripts/build-web.sh --single-file \\\n    --scene surgery/title \\\n    --title \"Hands of Harbor: Second Opinion\" \\\n    --description \"Night Ward. Keep the beat. Keep them alive.\" \\\n    --theme-color \"#10282c\" \\\n    --out \"Hands of Harbor: Second Opinion-Trauma Center: Second Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-224015.html\"\n  echo \"EXIT:$?\"\n} >\"$LOG\" 2>&1\necho \"wrapper-done\"","description":"Check wasm and pack the HTML game","block_until_ms":0}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-bc2adcb0-db9f-496e-a8ea-d951e6c9384e-75","name":"monitor","input":{"command":"LOG=\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224015__x42677a/tmp/grok-goal-907ccca5ce3b/implementer/pack5.txt\"\nfor i in $(seq 1 90); do\n  if [ -f \"$LOG\" ] && grep -q '^EXIT:' \"$LOG\"; then\n    if grep -q '^EXIT:0$' \"$LOG\"; then echo DONE; else echo FAILED; tail -40 \"$LOG\"; fi\n    exit 0\n  fi\n  sleep 15\ndone\necho FAILED timeout\nif [ -f \"$LOG\" ]; then tail -20 \"$LOG\"; fi\nexit 1","description":"Watch wasm pack until it exits"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1137,"output_tokens":2205,"cache_read_input_tokens":119680,"cache_creation_input_t