{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_999","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"web_sys does not include Performance.\n\nThe `Performance` feature must be added to the web-sys dependency in `pav_app/Cargo.toml`. This will fix the compilation error. I need to check if this change requires updating the lockfile.\n\n`js_sys::Date::now()` is already a dependency. It returns milliseconds without adding the Performance feature. This avoids lockfile changes entirely.\n\nI will apply the fix immediately to avoid a race condition with the running compilation. `Window::performance` requires the Performance feature, while `js_sys::Date::now()` does not. The `set_interval` feature is already enabled on Window.\n\n`Closure::<dyn FnMut()>::new` is invalid. `Closure::new` infers the closure type directly and returns `Closure<F>`, not a trait object. The correct approach is to use `Closure::wrap(Box<dyn FnMut()>)`.\n\nI will apply both fixes now. If the compiler is already building, I may need to restart. I will switch to `Closure::wrap` instead of `Closure::<dyn FnMut()>::new` to avoid any risk of failure.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-08927755-809f-49fb-a8ca-58fa78c31287-80","name":"search_replace","input":{"file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224015__x42677a/work/Hands of Harbor: Second Opinion-Trauma Center: Second Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-224015/engine/crates/pav_app/src/product.rs","old_string":"#[cfg(target_arch = \"wasm32\")]\nfn frame_now_ms() -> f64 {\n    web_sys::window().and_then(|w| w.performance()).map(|p| p.now()).unwrap_or(0.0)\n}","new_string":"#[cfg(target_arch = \"wasm32\")]\nfn frame_now_ms() -> f64 {\n    js_sys::Date::now()\n}"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-08927755-809f-49fb-a8ca-58fa78c31287-81","name":"search_replace","input":{"file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224015__x42677a/work/Hands of Har