":\"### 11.1 `tests/run_all.py`\"},{\"line_number\":622,\"content\":\"### 11.2 Rust (fast, no GPU)\"},{\"line_number\":635,\"content\":\"### 11.3 Browser (built single file, `file://`)\"},{\"line_number\":650,\"content\":\"### 11.4 Hub\"},{\"line_number\":661,\"content\":\"## 12. Build order\"},{\"line_number\":679,\"content\":\"## 13. Finish line\"},{\"line_number\":691,\"content\":\"### Requirements map\"},{\"line_number\":719,\"content\":\"## Appendix A: paper cards ✔\"},{\"line_number\":749,\"content\":\"## Appendix B: a hub shim skeleton ✔ (the protocol calls are tested)\"},{\"line_number\":778,\"content\":\"## Appendix C: the fragment for the page ✔\"},{\"line_number\":787,\"content\":\"## Appendix D: browser stand-ins ✔\"},{\"line_number\":813,\"content\":\"## Deviations\"}]}]}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa38-de6f-7dc0-ae0d-e0f717ed75f2","uuid":"84bb37fc-8134-4b72-96cd-60b56540baac"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_1014","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Checking sections 11.1 through 11.4 to identify remaining tasks.","signature":"t9mURWLcoMFYqW1ISMRl1xE2MWTIplXZBUbsdizx11FwyZm5MsI5hL11sW7BSP0nPcau3kJd2Aty3nhxGc0SNduNi/y4V9A9DfGVcYnm7rKuICw"},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-5040d08e-c151-4711-8061-1f7cbdcb2e3c-101","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224015__x42677a/work/PLAN.md","offset":613,"limit":50}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-5040d08e-c151-4711-8061-1f7cbdcb2e3c-102","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224015__x42677a/tmp/grok-goal-907ccca5ce3b/implementer/launch.py","offset":40,"limit":80}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":781,"output_tokens":154,"cache_read_input_tokens":144256,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa38-de6f-7dc0-ae0d-e0f717ed75f2","uuid":"01ec2144-f8e5-4289-b8b1-35c7eb1c4d8d"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-5040d08e-c151-4711-8061-1f7cbdcb2e3c-101","content":"{\"type\":\"ReadFile\",\"FileContent\":{\"content\":\"613→## 11. Testing\\n\\nRules from your TASK.md: one command, printing only failures and a one-line count; rerun only after changing what it covers;\\nscreenshots only for what a script can't check; no subagents or workflows to debate, review, judge or audit.\\n\\n### 11.1 `tests/run_all.py`\\nRuns everything below with output captured, prints failures and `N passed, M failed`. `--rust` or `--web` for a part. Use the\\n620→system `python3` **without `-I`** ✔ (`-I` hides Playwright). Keep one or two browsers open at most.\\n\\n### 11.2 Rust (fast, no GPU)\\n- Bot wins every case and the whole campaign on 10 seeds at skill 1.0 (`bot_skill` scales speed and accuracy).\\n- A careless player (idle; random tool spam) loses every case.\\n- Determinism: snapshot, rewind and replay hashes are exact (copy `engine/crates/pav_core/tests/games.rs`).\\n- **Coverage:** counters in the campaign prove every tool, hazard, strain phase, gift and Code fired, and every rating was reachable.\\n- Rule units: each tool's rating thresholds, wrong tool, chain, ranks, beat window, Code, retry checkpoint.\\n- Content lint: every file parses, every referenced speaker, expression, plate and cue exists, no empty text, no leftover \\\"TODO\\\".\\n- **Balance:** `pav balance seeds=20 skills=1.0,0.7,0.4` prints wins, time, vitals left and suggested `par` per case. Target: 1.0 always\\n630→  wins at S or above; 0.7 wins most; 0.4 loses later cases; 0 always loses. Tune with this rather than by feel alone.\\n- Shell: pad, keyboard and mouse navigation through every screen, hover moves focus, prompts follow last device, Xbox setting, attract\\n  starts at 10 s and exits on any input, touch-only state, dev sliders apply and reset, About shows every required section.\\n- Audio: music default gain is 0.10; every cue and voice renders non-silent offline; each track renders; extend `audio_capture`.\\n\\n### 11.3 Browser (built single file, `file://`)\\nLaunch Chromium with exactly ✔ `--enable-unsafe-webgpu --enable-features=Vulkan --use-webgpu-adapter=swiftshader --use-vulkan=swiftshader\\n--use-angle=swiftshader`. With these, canvas screenshots show real pixels ✔. Check through `window.__game`:\\n- Boots with no console errors; right title; none of the engine's overlays.\\n- Stubbed DualSense (Appendix D) ✔: menus, analog R2 reaches the sim, flick selects tools, Options pauses. Keyboard and mouse: tools, wheel, hover,\\n640→  click. Prompts flip between devices.\\n- Attract at 10 s and exit on key, pad and mouse.\\n- Phone profile (Chromium device profile, tap with `page.touchscreen`): message, Settings button, no touch controls, attract runs. Also load a\\n  WebKit iPhone profile as far as it goes (it has no WebGPU here, so expect the page's WebGPU message).\\n- Audio: analyser tap (Appendix D) ✔ reads non-silence; `status()` shows music 0.10.\\n- Settings persist across a reload.\\n- `step` the whole `surgery/campaign` in the browser with the bot and reach Won.\\n- Screenshots at 1920×1080 of title, op, story, results, dev, about into `tests/out/`; look at them when visuals change. For quick looks, `pav capture`\\n  and `filmstrip` are cheaper.\\n\\n650→### 11.4 Hub\\nCopy the game next to `harness.html`, `bridge.js`, `round.js` in `tests/hub/`. Serve with `python3 -u -m http.server 0 --bind 127.0.0.1 -d tests/hub`.\\n**Use `-u` ✔: without it the port line is buffered when piped and your script hangs forever.** Read the port from the first line, and check that the\\npage is your game. Stop only the server you started, by PID; many other agents' servers and browsers run on this machine ✔. Wait for\\n`document.body.dataset.complete === 'true'`, then require `window.__hubCheck.pass`, for each query:\\n`players=4&latency=150&jitter=50&loss=5&auto=1`, the same with `&scenario=host-leave`, `players=2&scenario=server&auto=1`, `players=1&auto=1` (add\\n`&limit=20` for speed). Then a two-copy test reading each frame's `__game.status()`: a client's input moves its cursor on the host; both see the same\\nvitals. Then open outside a session: title appears, the game is unaffected.\\n\\n---\\n660→\\n## 12. Build order\\n\",\"content_concise\":\"613→## 11. Testing\\n\\nRules from your TASK.md: one command, printing only failures and a one-line count; rerun only after changing what it covers;\\nscreenshots only for what a script can't check; no subagents or workflows to debate, review, judge or audit.\\n\\n### 11.1 `tests/run_all.py`\\nRuns everything below with output captured, prints failures and `N passed, M failed`. `--rust` or `--web` for a part. Use the\\n620→system `python3` **without `-I`** ✔ (`-I` hides Playwright). Keep one or two browsers open at most.\\n\\n### 11.2 Rust (fast, no GPU)\\n- Bot wins every case and the whole campaign on 10 seeds at skill 1.0 (`bot_skill` scales speed and accuracy).\\n- A careless player (idle; random tool spam) loses every case.\\n- Determinism: snapshot, rewind and replay hashes are exact (copy `engine/crates/pav_core/tests/games.rs`).\\n- **Coverage:** counters in the campaign prove every tool, hazard, strain phase, gift and Code fired, and every rating was reachable.\\n- Rule units: each tool's rating thresholds, wrong tool, chain, ranks, beat window, Code, retry checkpoint.\\n- Content lint: every file parses, every referenced speaker, expression, plate and cue exists, no empty text, no leftover \\\"TODO\\\".\\n- **Balance:** `pav balance seeds=20 skills=1.0,0.7,0.4` prints wins, time, vitals left and suggested `par` per case. Target: 1.0 always\\n630→  wins at S or above; 0.7 wins most; 0.4 loses later cases; 0 always loses. Tune with this rather than by feel alone.\\n- Shell: pad, keyboard and mouse navigation through every screen, hover moves focus, prompts follow last device, Xbox setting, attract\\n  starts at 10 s and exits on any input, touch-only state, dev sliders apply and reset, About shows every required section.\\n- Audio: music default gain is 0.10; every cue and voice renders non-silent offline; each track renders; extend `audio_capture`.\\n\\n### 11.3 Browser (built single file, `file://`)\\nLaunch Chromium with exactly ✔ `--enable-unsafe-webgpu --enable-features=Vulkan --use-webgpu-adapter=swiftshader --use-vulkan=swiftshader\\n--use-angle=swiftshader`. With these, canvas screenshots show real pixels ✔. Check through `window.__game`:\\n- Boots with no console errors; right title; none of the engine's overlays.\\n- Stubbed DualSense (Appendix D) ✔: menus, analog R2 reaches the sim, flick selects tools, Options pauses. Keyboard and mouse: tools, wheel, hover,\\n640→  click. Prompts flip between devices.\\n- Attract at 10 s and exit on key, pad and mouse.\\n- Phone profile (Chromium device profile, tap with `page.touchscreen`): message, Settings button, no touch controls, attract runs. Also load a\\n  WebKit iPhone profile as far as it goes (it has no WebGPU here, so expect the page's WebGPU message).\\n- Audio: analyser tap (Appendix D) ✔ reads non-silence; `status()` shows music 0.10.\\n- Settings persist across a reload.\\n- `step` the whole `surgery/campaign` in the browser with the bot and reach Won.\\n- Screenshots at 1920×1080 of title, op, story, results, dev, about into `tests/out/`; look at them when visuals change. For quick looks, `pav capture`\\n  and `filmstrip` are cheaper.\\n\\n650→### 11.4 Hub\\nCopy the game next to `harness.html`, `bridge.js`, `round.js` in `tests/hub/`. Serve with `python3 -u -m http.server 0 --bind 127.0.0.1 -d tests/hub`.\\n**Use `-u` ✔: without it the port line is buffered when piped and your script hangs forever.** Read the port from the first line, and check that the\\npage is your game. Stop only the server you started, by PID; many other agents' servers and browsers run on this machine ✔. Wait for\\n`document.body.dataset.complete === 'true'`, then require `window.__hubCheck.pass`, for each query:\\n`players=4&latency=150&jitter=50&loss=5&auto=1`, the same with `&scenario=host-leave`, `players=2&scenario=server&auto=1`, `players=1&auto=1` (add\\n`&limit=20` for speed). Then a two-copy test reading each frame's `__game.status()`: a client's input moves its cursor on the host; both see the same\\nvitals. Then open outside a session: title appears, the game is unaffected.\\n\\n---\\n660→\\n## 12. Build order\\n\",\"absolute_path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224015__x42677a/work/PLAN.md\",\"offset\":613,\"limit\":50,\"raw_output\":\"## 11. Testing\\n\\nRules from your TASK.md: one command, printing only failures and a one-line count; rerun only after changing what it covers;\\nscreenshots only for what a script can't check; no subagents or workflows to debate, review, judge or audit.\\n\\n### 11.1 `tests/run_all.py`\\nRuns everything below with output captured, prints failures and `N passed, M failed`. `--rust` or `--web` for a part. Use the\\nsystem `python3` **without `-I`** ✔ (`-I` hides Playwright). Keep one or two browsers open at most.\\n\\n### 11.2 Rust (fast, no GPU)\\n- Bot wins every case and the whole campaign on 10 seeds at skill 1.0 (`bot_skill` scales speed and accuracy).\\n- A careless player (idle; random tool spam) loses every case.\\n- Determinism: snapshot, rewind and replay hashes are exact (copy `engine/crates/pav_core/tests/games.rs`).\\n- **Coverage:** counters in the campaign prove every tool, hazard, strain phase, gift and Code fired, and every rating was reachable.\\n- Rule units: each tool's rating thresholds, wrong tool, chain, ranks, beat window, Code, retry checkpoint.\\n- Content lint: every file parses, every referenced speaker, expression, plate and cue exists, no empty text, no leftover \\\"TODO\\\".\\n- **Balance:** `pav balance seeds=20 skills=1.0,0.7,0.4` prints wins, time, vitals left and suggested `par` per case. Target: 1.0 always\\n  wins at S or above; 0.7 wins most; 0.4 loses later cases; 0 always loses. Tune with this rather than by feel alone.\\n- Shell: pad, keyboard and mouse navigation through every screen, hover moves focus, prompts follow last device, Xbox setting, attract\\n  starts at 10 s and exits on any input, touch-only state, dev sliders apply and reset, About shows every required section.\\n- Audio: music default gain is 0.10; every cue and voice renders non-silent offline; each track renders; extend `audio_capture`.\\n\\n### 11.3 Browser (built single file, `file://`)\\nLaunch Chromium with exactly ✔ `--enable-unsafe-webgpu --enable-features=Vulkan --use-webgpu-adapter=swiftshader --use-vulkan=swiftshader\\n--use-angle=swiftshader`. With these, canvas screenshots show real pixels ✔. Check through `window.__game`:\\n- Boots with no console errors; right title; none of the engine's overlays.\\n- Stubbed DualSense (Appendix D) ✔: menus, analog R2 reaches the sim, flick selects tools, Options pauses. Keyboard and mouse: tools, wheel, hover,\\n  click. Prompts flip between devices.\\n- Attract at 10 s and exit on key, pad and mouse.\\n- Phone profile (Chromium device profile, tap with `page.touchscreen`): message, Settings button, no touch controls, attract runs. Also load a\\n  WebKit iPhone profile as far as it goes (it has no WebGPU here, so expect the page's WebGPU message).\\n- Audio: analyser tap (Appendix D) ✔ reads non-silence; `status()` shows music 0.10.\\n- Settings persist across a reload.\\n- `step` the whole `surgery/campaign` in the browser with the bot and reach Won.\\n- Screenshots at 1920×1080 of title, op, story, results, dev, about into `tests/out/`; look at them when visuals change. For quick looks, `pav capture`\\n  and `filmstrip` are cheaper.\\n\\n### 11.4 Hub\\nCopy the game next to `harness.html`, `bridge.js`, `round.js` in `tests/hub/`. Serve with `python3 -u -m http.server 0 --bind 127.0.0.1 -d tests/hub`.\\n**Use `-u` ✔: without it the port line is buffered when piped and your script hangs forever.** Read the port from the first line, and check that the\\npage is your game. Stop only the server you started, by PID; many other agents' servers and browsers run on this machine ✔. Wait for\\n`document.body.dataset.complete === 'true'`, then require `window.__hubCheck.pass`, for each query:\\n`players=4&latency=150&jitter=50&loss=5&auto=1`, the same with `&scenario=host-leave`, `players=2&scenario=server&auto=1`, `players=1&auto=1` (add\\n`&limit=20` for speed). Then a two-copy test reading each frame's `__game.status()`: a client's input moves its cursor on the host; both see the same\\nvitals. Then open outside a session: title appears, the game is unaffected.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 12. Build order\\n\\n\",\"total_lines\":818}}","is_error":false},{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-5040d08e-c151-4711-8061-1f7cbdcb2e3c-102","content":"{\"type\":\"ReadFile\",\"FileContent\":{\"content\":\"40→})();\\n\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n\\n\\ndef status(page):\\n    return json.loads(page.evaluate(\\\"() => window.__game.status()\\\"))\\n\\n\\ndef boot(page, url):\\n    page.goto(url, wait_until=\\\"domcontentloaded\\\", timeout=60000)\\n50→    page.wait_for_function(\\\"() => window.__game && window.__game.status\\\", timeout=45000)\\n    last = None\\n    for _ in range(40):\\n        last = status(page)\\n        if last.get(\\\"screen\\\") == \\\"title\\\":\\n            return last\\n        page.wait_for_timeout(250)\\n    return last\\n\\n\\n60→def wait_pred(page, pred, timeout_s):\\n    last = None\\n    deadline = time.time() + timeout_s\\n    while time.time() < deadline:\\n        last = status(page)\\n        if pred(last):\\n            return last\\n        page.wait_for_timeout(250)\\n    return last\\n\\n70→\\ndef pad_south(page, down):\\n    page.evaluate(\\n        \\\"\\\"\\\"(down) => {\\n          const b = window.__pad.buttons[0];\\n          b.pressed = down;\\n          b.value = down ? 1 : 0;\\n          window.__pad.timestamp = (window.__pad.timestamp || 0) + 1;\\n        }\\\"\\\"\\\",\\n        down,\\n80→    )\\n\\n\\ndef changed(before):\\n    def pred(s):\\n        return s.get(\\\"screen\\\") != before.get(\\\"screen\\\") or s.get(\\\"focus\\\") != before.get(\\\"focus\\\")\\n\\n    return pred\\n\\n\\n90→def drive_same(page):\\n    \\\"\\\"\\\"Pad Cross, then a mouse click only if the pad did not move the shell.\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n    before = status(page)\\n    pad_south(page, True)\\n    after = wait_pred(page, changed(before), 12)\\n    pad_south(page, False)\\n    how = \\\"pad-south\\\"\\n    if after.get(\\\"screen\\\") == before.get(\\\"screen\\\") and after.get(\\\"focus\\\") == before.get(\\\"focus\\\"):\\n        page.locator(\\\"canvas\\\").first.click(position={\\\"x\\\": 200, \\\"y\\\": 200}, force=True)\\n        after = wait_pred(page, changed(before), 12)\\n100→        how = \\\"mouse-click\\\"\\n    return before, after, how\\n\\n\\ndef focus_canvas(page):\\n    page.evaluate(\\n        \\\"\\\"\\\"() => {\\n          const c = document.querySelector('canvas');\\n          if (!c) return;\\n          c.tabIndex = 0;\\n110→          c.focus();\\n        }\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n    )\\n\\n\\ndef tap(page, key, pred, timeout_s=18):\\n    focus_canvas(page)\\n    page.keyboard.press(key)\\n    hit = wait_pred(page, pred, timeout_s)\\n    if hit and pred(hit):\",\"content_concise\":\"40→})();\\n\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n\\n\\ndef status(page):\\n    return json.loads(page.evaluate(\\\"() => window.__game.status()\\\"))\\n\\n\\ndef boot(page, url):\\n    page.goto(url, wait_until=\\\"domcontentloaded\\\", timeout=60000)\\n50→    page.wait_for_function(\\\"() => window.__game && window.__game.status\\\", timeout=45000)\\n    last = None\\n    for _ in range(40):\\n        last = status(page)\\n        if last.get(\\\"screen\\\") == \\\"title\\\":\\n            return last\\n        page.wait_for_timeout(250)\\n    return last\\n\\n\\n60→def wait_pred(page, pred, timeout_s):\\n    last = None\\n    deadline = time.time() + timeout_s\\n    while time.time() < deadline:\\n        last = status(page)\\n        if pred(last):\\n            return last\\n        page.wait_for_timeout(250)\\n    return last\\n\\n70→\\ndef pad_south(page, down):\\n    page.evaluate(\\n        \\\"\\\"\\\"(down) => {\\n          const b = window.__pad.buttons[0];\\n          b.pressed = down;\\n          b.value = down ? 1 : 0;\\n          window.__pad.timestamp = (window.__pad.timestamp || 0) + 1;\\n        }\\\"\\\"\\\",\\n        down,\\n80→    )\\n\\n\\ndef changed(before):\\n    def pred(s):\\n        return s.get(\\\"screen\\\") != before.get(\\\"screen\\\") or s.get(\\\"focus\\\") != before.get(\\\"focus\\\")\\n\\n    return pred\\n\\n\\n90→def drive_same(page):\\n    \\\"\\\"\\\"Pad Cross, then a mouse click only if the pad did not move the shell.\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n    before = status(page)\\n    pad_south(page, True)\\n    after = wait_pred(page, changed(before), 12)\\n    pad_south(page, False)\\n    how = \\\"pad-south\\\"\\n    if after.get(\\\"screen\\\") == before.get(\\\"screen\\\") and after.get(\\\"focus\\\") == before.get(\\\"focus\\\"):\\n        page.locator(\\\"canvas\\\").first.click(position={\\\"x\\\": 200, \\\"y\\\": 200}, force=True)\\n        after = wait_pred(page, changed(before), 12)\\n100→        how = \\\"mouse-click\\\"\\n    return before, after, how\\n\\n\\ndef focus_canvas(page):\\n    page.evaluate(\\n        \\\"\\\"\\\"() => {\\n          const c = document.querySelector('canvas');\\n          if (!c) return;\\n          c.tabIndex = 0;\\n110→          c.focus();\\n        }\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n    )\\n\\n\\ndef tap(page, key, pred, timeout_s=18):\\n    focus_canvas(page)\\n    page.keyboard.press(key)\\n    hit = wait_pred(page, pred, timeout_s)\\n    if hit and pred(hit):\",\"absolute_path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224015__x42677a/tmp/grok-goal-907ccca5ce3b/im