{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_1018","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The testing feedback mentions five issues, but the array only has four items. The second entry, \"5\", likely represents the count of critical issues.\n\nMore issues were found since the initial testing. The exit interview counts need updating to reflect the full scope of work before hand-in.\n\nNine issues were found in total. The critical ones are the cryoprobe pad path, blank hub field, host-leave zero traffic, frozen operation after first present, poll cancellation, and the suture bug. The exit interview will be updated honestly without inflating the count.\n\nThe exit interview predates the skeptic round and needs updating to include those fixes and the timer fix. Engine feedback should also note the timer and countdown skip as product changes.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-51407fe3-0ac5-486e-99aa-fc07813e38d7-107","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224015__x42677a/tmp/grok-goal-907ccca5ce3b/implementer/launch.py","offset":140,"limit":50}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1333,"output_tokens":669,"cache_read_input_tokens":149504,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa38-de6f-7dc0-ae0d-e0f717ed75f2","uuid":"ca600635-3262-4d7b-86bd-ce3bdd05f592"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-51407fe3-0ac5-486e-99aa-fc07813e38d7-107","content":"{\"type\":\"ReadFile\",\"FileContent\":{\"content\":\"140→\\n\\ndef luma(path):\\n    proc = subprocess.run(\\n        [\\\"ffmpeg\\\", \\\"-v\\\", \\\"error\\\", \\\"-i\\\", str(path), \\\"-f\\\", \\\"rawvideo\\\", \\\"-pix_fmt\\\", \\\"gray\\\", \\\"-\\\"],\\n        capture_output=True,\\n    )\\n    data = proc.stdout\\n    if not data:\\n        return 0.0\\n150→    return sum(data) / len(data)\\n\\n\\ndef shot(page, path, screen):\\n    path.parent.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)\\n    display = os.environ.get(\\\"DISPLAY\\\", \\\":0\\\")\\n    last = 0.0\\n    for attempt in range(4):\\n        settle(page, screen, extra=6 + attempt * 2)\\n        proc = subprocess.run(\\n160→            [\\n                \\\"/usr/bin/ffmpeg\\\",\\n                \\\"-y\\\",\\n                \\\"-hide_banner\\\",\\n                \\\"-loglevel\\\",\\n                \\\"error\\\",\\n                \\\"-f\\\",\\n                \\\"x11grab\\\",\\n                \\\"-video_size\\\",\\n                \\\"1920x1080\\\",\\n170→                \\\"-i\\\",\\n                display,\\n                \\\"-frames:v\\\",\\n                \\\"1\\\",\\n                str(path),\\n            ],\\n            env=os.environ.copy(),\\n            capture_output=True,\\n            text=True,\\n            timeout=20,\\n180→        )\\n        if proc.returncode != 0:\\n            raise RuntimeError(proc.stderr[-500:] or f\\\"ffmpeg exit {proc.returncode}\\\")\\n        last = luma(path)\\n        print(f\\\"GRAB {path.name} attempt {attempt} luma {last:.1f} screen {status(page).get('screen')}\\\")\\n        if last > 50:\\n            return\\n    print(f\\\"GRAB {path.name} still dark luma {last:.1f}\\\")\\n\\n\",\"content_concise\":\"140→\\n\\ndef luma(path):\\n    proc = subprocess.run(\\n        [\\\"ffmpeg\\\", \\\"-v\\\", \\\