{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_1021","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The traceback appears to have been printed twice.\n\nThe two launches succeeded. The shoot test reached the about page but timed out on navigation to about:blank. The hang likely stems from the game's draw loop saturating the main thread, which prevents navigation from completing.\n\nThe story screen captured successfully. The about:blank timeout is a regression from the timer firing when solo play frames exceed 50ms. The story shot succeeded because the page was briefly responsive enough to navigate menus.\n\nStory mode's heavier rendering likely caused the timer to double-pump during the story scene, saturating the main thread and blocking navigation. The fix is to gate the timer on hub.active so solo play uses the working rAF path while hub play can fall back to the timer when rAF dies.\n\nThe timer can receive `hub.active` directly from `surgery_frame` instead of polling. This avoids event consumption and lets the interval gate itself on hub state.\n\nThe timer callback now checks a `HUB_LIVE` flag. Solo play keeps it false, so the timer exits immediately and never steps. Hub play keeps it true, letting the timer step in when rAF dies. If rAF dies while the hub is active, the flag stays true until the page unloads.\n\nThe about:blank navigation now works. Rebuilding the WASM binary is needed, which takes roughly two minutes. The timer gate only affects non-hub states, so hub tests should still pass. I will re-run hub_four, cursor, and file launch after the rebuild to verify everything still works.\n\nThe previous hub pass used an older binary, so the new pack must be retested. The about:blank hang is a real bug in the shipped page, and the new timer is the likely culprit because the story scene is heavy.\n\nThe timer will no-op during healthy hub play because LAST_MS stays fresh. I will also shorten launch.py's about:blank timeout and use page.goto with wait_until commit to avoid hangs.\n\nThe real fix is the game not wedging the main thread. Weakening the test to hide the wedge is wrong. If rAF queues frames back-to-back without yielding, the browser cannot process navigation until a frame finally returns control.","signature":""},{"type":"text","text":"The two file launches reached the menu, but the story scene then wedged the page so it could not navigate. The backup timer was stepping solo play as well as the hub. It should run only while a hub session is active."},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-40dfe797-3303-4dfb-912a-15bea9f8100e-110","name":"search_replace","input":{"file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224015__x42677a/work/Hands of Harbor: Second Opinion-Trauma Center: Second Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-224015/engine/crates/pav_app/src/product.rs","old_string":"        install_hook(app);\n        install_tick(app);\n    }\n}","new_string":"        install_hook(app);\n        install_tick(app, hub.active);\n    }\n}"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-40dfe797-3303-4dfb-912a-15bea9f8100e-111","name":"search_replace","input":{"file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224015__x42677a/work/Hands of Harbor: Second Opinion-Trauma Center: Second Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-224015/engine/crates/pav_app/src/product.rs","old_string":"    static TICK_ON: Cell<bool> = const { Cell::new(false) };\n    static APP_PTR: Cell<*mut App> = const { Cell::new(std::ptr::null_mut()) };\n}","new_string":"    static TICK_ON: Cell<bool> = const { Cell::new(false) };\n    static HUB_LIVE: Cell<bool> = const { Cell::new(false) };\n    static APP_PTR: Cell<*mut App> = const { Cell::new(std::ptr::null_mut()) };\n}"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-40dfe797-3303-4dfb-912a-15bea9f8100e-112","name":"search_replace","input":{"file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224015__x42677a/work/Hands of Harbor: Second Opinion-Trauma Center: Second Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-224015/engine/crates/pav_app/src/product.rs","old_string":"fn install_tick(app: &mut App) {\n    LAST_MS.with(|t| t.set(frame_now_ms()));\n    APP_PTR.with(|p| p.set(app as *mut App));\n    if TICK_ON.with(|t| t.get()) {\n        return;\n    }\n    use wasm_bindgen::JsCast;\n    let Some(win) = web_sys::window() else { return };\n    let cb = wasm_bindgen::closure::Closure::wrap(Box::new(|| {\n        if IN_FRAME.with(|f| f.get()) {\n            return;\n        }\n        let last = LAST_MS.with(|t| t.get());\n        if frame_now_ms() - last < 50.0 {\n            return;\n        }","new_string":"fn install_tick(app: &mut App, hub_active: bool) {\n    LAST_MS.with(|t| t.set(frame_now_ms()));\n    HUB_LIVE.with(|h| h.set(hub_active));\n    APP_PTR.with(|p| p.set(app as *mut App));\n    if TICK_ON.with(|t| t.get()) {\n        return;\n    }\n    use wasm_bindgen::JsCast;\n    let Some(win) = web_sys::window() else { return };\n    let cb = wasm_bindgen::closure::Closure::wrap(Box::new(|| {\n        if IN_FRAME.with(|f| f.get()) || !HUB_LIVE.with(|h| h.get()) {\n            return;\n        }\n        let last = LAST_MS.with(|t| t.get());\n        if frame_now_ms() - last < 50.0 {\n            return;\n        }"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2111,"output_tokens":2411,"cache_read_input_tokens":152704,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa38-de6f-7dc0-ae0d-e0f717ed75f2","uuid":"f5d029f4-ca8c-40ad-b7bf-fe4fce401bc8"}
