{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_1030","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Memory is exhausted. 18 Gi are in use and swap is full.\n\nOnly 2 Gi remain. Other agents' browsers and rustc are consuming 400–500 MB each. Starting another browser would trigger earlyoom. The hub tests and cursor checks already passed. The file:// launches succeeded twice. The shoot test reached the operation screen before the browser was killed. I will not retry the heavy op screenshot while memory is this low.\n\nThe target crash was caused by memory exhaustion, not a game bug. I still need to pack the HTML, create exit-interview.json, keep the dev folder, and stop the HTTP server. The existing exit interview is honest enough; it lists five issues and omits later ones.\n\nI will update the testing feedback to include the later findings briefly. I will verify that the JSON still parses. I will stop the HTTP server and confirm no .harbor-target remains. The work folder should contain everything TASK.md asks for.\n\nI searched for hub.txt in the work tree and dev folder. It was not found. The scratch directory may be deleted, so the hub logs could be lost. I will not write an extra HUB-RESULTS note because that was not requested. The exit-interview.json is the required deliverable.\n\nThe verifier runs before scratch deletion, so the hub logs will still be available for auditing. I will update the exit interview to include the mapping, blank field, and stalled hub frame issues, and correct the critical count to reflect all game-breaking bugs.\n\nThe full set of game-breaking bugs is now clear: suture stage skip, forceps selection, sac meter, hub 60Hz accumulator, poll cancels rAF, cryoprobe and dressing unselectable, blank hub field, and host-leave traffic freeze. The exit interview will be updated to list all eight issues and correct the critical count. Engine feedback will also mention the timer and quiet plate changes. JSON validation and server shutdown are next.\n\nThe title, about, and story screens look correct. The pack6 binary reached the operation screen before the crash. I will not retry the operation screenshot because memory is still critically low and another Chromium launch would likely OOM again. The about page includes source information.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-c98ff3a2-d519-4fab-b96b-7d2167ea4746-127","name":"grep","input":{"pattern":"source|Trauma","glob":"**/pav_ui/src/surgery/**/*.rs","head_limit":30}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-c98ff3a2-d519-4fab-b96b-7d2167ea4746-128","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224015__x42677a/work/Hands of Harbor: Second Opinion-Trauma Center: Second Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-224015/engine/crates/pav_ui/src/surgery/about.json","limit":60}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1959,"output_tokens":1081,"cache_read_input_tokens":169600,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa38-de6f-7dc0-ae0d-e0f717ed75f2","uuid":"c9e67cef-e721-439a-89a3-d2df1487964f"}
