count\":5,\"file_matches\":[{\"path\":\"/home/micha/.grok/sessions/%2Fhome%2Fmicha%2Fdev%2Fcc-matrix%2Fruns%2Fgrok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224015__x42677a%2Fwork/01a1aa38-de6f-7dc0-ae0d-e0f717ed75f2/goal/plan.md\",\"matches\":[{\"line_number\":7,\"content\":\"1. The work folder contains `PROGRESS.md`, a dev subfolder, and beside it one self-contained HTML file whose basename is `{GameTitle}-Trauma Center: Second Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-224015` (the same name as the dev subfolder). `{GameTitle}` is one playful riff on the source name, chosen with a real RNG and stored so the title screen, page title, hub card, and About screen match. `exit-interview.json` in that same root parses as one object in TASK.md’s exact shape: `usage` is exactly `added on import`; feedback arrays follow the question order; `aiHub` is filled. The page embeds those answers in `<script type=\\\"application/json\\\" id=\\\"about-data\\\">` and the About screen shows Source Information, Testing Feedback, Engine Feedback, and Prompt Feedback. Shipped game content has no TODOs, placeholders, or stubbed features, and does not use the source’s world (Hope Hospital, Caduceus, Stiles, GUILT, Healing Touch, COOL/XS, or its other proper names).\"},{\"line_number\":13,\"content\":\"## Verification plan\"},{\"line_number\":14,\"content\":\"1. gating: From the dev folder, run the one suite command (expected `tests/run_all.py` without `python -I`) after it includes real tests that construct each case, tool, hazard, gift, Code, rank, chain, beat window, and checkpoint from the shipped sim’s start state — not a reimplementation or a mid-scene skip. Capture stdout/stderr to `{SCRATCH}/suite.txt`. Must show exit 0, no failure lines, and `N passed, 0 failed`. Must include: bot wins every case and the campaign on 10 seeds at skill 1.0; idle and random-tool play lose every case; snapshot, rewind, and replay hashes match; coverage counters fire for every tool, hazard, strain phase, gift, and Code; content lint parses with no empty line and no TODO; music default gain 0.10; every cue, voice, and track renders non-silent offline.\"},{\"line_number\":16,\"content\":\"3. gating: Launch the root HTML from `file://` twice, new browser each time, Chromium with `--enable-unsafe-webgpu --enable-features=Vulkan --use-webgpu-adapter=swiftshader --use-vulkan=swiftshader --use-angle=swiftshader`, viewport 1920×1080. Stub a standard-mapping DualSense before load. Capture console, `window.__game` status, and a screenshot to `{SCRATCH}/launch-1/` and `{SCRATCH}/launch-2/`. Both runs: zero page errors; title is the chosen game name; no engine boot, stats, guide, hint, toast, or touch overlay; canvas drawing size equals 1920×1080 and the painted area covers most of the surface; status reports music 0.10; a stick/button or mouse input changes focus, screen, or cursor in status the same way both times. A blank or partial buffer from a successful readback fails. If the browser cannot start or is killed by the environment, save that log under `{SCRATCH}/launch-env.txt` and then the green sim/shell suite is the bar — do not invent a screenshot.\"},{\"line_number\":36,\"content\":\"- [x] Clone the engine in the dev subfolder, confirm the commit, read its start and make-a-game docs, pick the title with a real RNG, and start `PROGRESS.md`.\"}]}]}","is_error":false},{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-ff62ece2-7e07-40f0-812e-aed3a934e37a-144","content":"{\"type\":\"GrepSearch\",\"stdout\":[60,119,111,114,107,115,112,97,99,101,95,114,101,115,117,108,116,32,119,111,114,107,115,112,97,99,101,95,112,97,116,104,61,34,47,104,111,109,101,47,109,105,99,104,97,47,100,101,118,47,99,99,45,109,97,116,114,105,120,47,114,117,110,115,47,103,114,111,107,45,120,104,105,103,104,46,98,117,105,108,100,45,118,50,95,95,50,48,50,54,49,49,48,52,45,50,50,52,48,49,53,95,95,120,52,50,54,55,55,97,47,119,111,114,107,34,62,10,70,111,117,110,100,32,51,32,109,97,116,99,104,105,110,103,32,108,105,110,101,115,10,47,104,11