110,103,105,110,101,47,116,97,114,103,101,116,96,44,32,97,110,100,32,115,97,118,101,32,116,104,101,32,103,114,101,101,110,32,115,117,105,116,101,32,112,108,117,115,32,116,119,111,32,108,97,117,110,99,104,32,99,97,112,116,117,114,101,115,32,117,110,100,101,114,32,96,123,83,67,82,65,84,67,72,125,96,46,10,60,47,119,111,114,107,115,112,97,99,101,95,114,101,115,117,108,116,62],\"stderr\":[],\"exit_code\":0,\"match_count\":12,\"file_matches\":[{\"path\":\"/home/micha/.grok/sessions/%2Fhome%2Fmicha%2Fdev%2Fcc-matrix%2Fruns%2Fgrok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224015__x42677a%2Fwork/01a1aa38-de6f-7dc0-ae0d-e0f717ed75f2/goal/plan.md\",\"matches\":[{\"line_number\":9,\"content\":\"3. The same screens serve a standard-mapping pad and mouse/keyboard (PLAN control table): prompts switch immediately to PlayStation glyphs, Xbox glyphs when that setting is on, or keys/mouse, matching the last device. Title and main menu (Continue, New Game, Case Files, Code Blue, Settings, About) go to attract after 10 seconds without input; any key, mouse move/click, pad button/stick, or tap returns to the title. Touch-only shows “Controller or keyboard required” and a Settings control, with no touch gameplay, and attract still runs. Pause opens Dev Mode with the live balance sliders, defaults marked, and Reset All. Music, effects, and voices are synthesized in code with no audio files; voices are short gibberish syllables; the music bus and Music setting default to 10% (gain 0.10). Story text is original, earnest medical melodrama between operations and short clinical lines during them.\"},{\"line_number\":10,\"content\":\"4. With no hub, the title and campaign run normally and Code Blue plus cases accept 1–4 local surgeons. In a hub session the only round is shared-world Code Blue, seats 1–4, 4 minutes, with the required `hub:session*` tags, unmodified `session.js` as the first script, a pre-op card, host-authoritative snapshots, and a client mirror. The harness passes `players=4&latency=150&jitter=50&loss=5`, the same with `scenario=host-leave`, `players=2&scenario=server`, and `players=1` (auto). A second page’s input moves that surgeon’s cursor on the host, and both pages report the same vitals. `AIHub.server` runs the world without a local slot or drawing.\"},{\"line_number\":11,\"content\":\"5. The packed HTML starts from `file://` in Chromium (WebGPU software flags). Two consecutive launches each show no page errors, the chosen title rather than Shardfall overlays, a render surface whose drawing size equals the requested viewport and is substantially painted, and a driven pad or mouse input that changes reported game state the same way both times. The single test command prints only failures and one `N passed, M failed` line, and that run is green, including the sim, shell, audio, browser, and hub checks above.\"},{\"line_number\":13,\"content\":\"## Verification plan\"},{\"line_number\":14,\"content\":\"1. gating: From the dev folder, run the one suite command (expected `tests/run_all.py` without `python -I`) after it includes real tests that construct each case, tool, hazard, gift, Code, rank, chain, beat window, and checkpoint from the shipped sim’s start state — not a reimplementation or a mid-scene skip. Capture stdout/stderr to `{SCRATCH}/suite.txt`. Must show exit 0, no failure lines, and `N passed, 0 failed`. Must include: bot wins every case and the campaign on 10 seeds at skill 1.0; idle and random-tool play lose every case; snapshot, rewind, and replay hashes match; coverage counters fire for every tool, hazard, strain phase, gift, and Code; content lint parses with no empty line and no TODO; music default gain 0.10; every cue, voice, and track renders non-silent offline.\"},{\"line_number\":15,\"content\":\"2. gating: The same suite, or a headless UI driver it calls, sends pad, keyboard, and mouse through every screen from the title’s initial state. Observations that must pass: hover moves focus; confirm activates; prompts follow the last device and the Xbox setting; attract starts at 10 seconds of no input and exits on key, pad, and mouse; touch-only shows the required sentence and Settings and no touch controls; dev sliders change live values and Reset All restores defaults; About contains every TASK section and `Usage: added on import`.\"},{\"line_number\":16,\"content\":\"3. gating: Launch the root HTML from `file://` twice, new browser each time, Chromium with `--enable-unsafe-webgpu --enable-features=Vulkan --use-webgpu-adapter=swiftshader --use-vulkan=swiftshader --use-angle=swiftshader`, viewport 1920×1080. Stub a standard-mapping DualSense before load. Capture console, `window.__game` status, and a screenshot to `{SCRATCH}/launch-1/` and `{SCRATCH}/launch-2/`. Both runs: zero page errors; title is the chosen game name; no engine boot, stats, guide, hint, toast, or touch overlay; canvas drawing size equals 1920×1080 and the painted area covers most of the surface; status reports music 0.10; a stick/button or mouse input changes focus, screen, or cursor in status the same way both times. A blank or partial buffer from a successful readback fails. If the browser cannot start or is killed by the environment, save that log under `{SCRATCH}/launch-env.txt` and then the green sim/shell suite is the bar — do not invent a screenshot.\"},{\"line_number\":17,\"content\":\"4. gating: Serve the packed game next to the hub harness on `127.0.0.1` and an OS-picked port (`python3 -u -m http.server`). Confirm the body is this game, then require `document.body.dataset.complete === 'true'` and `window.__hubCheck.pass` for the four queries in criterion 4. Then two pages: client aim changes the host cursor for that seat; vitals match. Then one page outside a session: the title is shown and play does not depend on the hub. Write the log to `{SCRATCH}/hub.txt`. Stop only that server PID.\"},{\"line_number\":19,\"content\":\"6. evidence: Save 1920×1080 screenshots of title, operation, story, results, dev, and about under `{SCRATCH}/shots/`. Balance output (wins, time, vitals, suggested par at skills 1.0, 0.7, 0.4, and 0) goes to `{SCRATCH}/balance.txt`. These do not override a green suite.\"},{\"line_number\":33,\"content\":\"Keep rules in one deterministic sim the headless tools can tick: surgeon slots, heartbeat, tools, strains, story phases, and the bot live there, with no wall clock, threads, or files. Drive the cursor in real time during the Hush via scaled sim dt, not the engine speed control. Let rendering, egui shell, and audio only read a single frame snapshot plus cue ids, so a browser client can decode the same snapshot. Keep the shell’s input abstract so pad, mouse, and tests share it, including while the sim is paused. Put cases, lines, plates, and rigs in text with file-and-line errors. Expose status, step, and shell commands on `window.__game` for the browser. Pack one HTML that works from `file://`. These are structure hints, not a required layout.\"},{\"line_number\":42,\"content\":\"- [x] Add the hub shim, card, mirror scene, and host snapshots; pass the harness and the two-page cursor/vitals check.\"},{\"line_number\":43,\"content\":\"- [x] Balance, write `exit-interview.json` and the about block, pack the single HTML to the work root, delete `engine/target`, and save the green suite plus two launch captures under `{SCRATCH}`.\"}]}]}","is_error":false},{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-ba87ff34-1d3a-4de4-9970-ade405d8b5a1-9","content":"{\"type\":\"GrepSearch\",\"stdout\":[60,119,111,114,107,115,112,97,99,101,95,114,101,115,117,108,116,32,119,111,114,107,115,112,97,99,101,95,112,97,116,104,61,34,47,104,111,109,101,47,109,105,99,104,97,47,100,101,118,47,99,99,45,109,97,116,114,105,120,47,114,117,110,115,47,103,114,111,107,45,120,104,105,103,104,46,98,117,105,108,100,45,118,50,95,95,50,48,50,54,49,49,48,52,45,50,50,52,48,49,53,95,95,120,52,50,54,55,55,97,47,119,111,114,107,34,62,10,78,111,32,109,97,116,99,104,101,115,32,102,111,117,110,100,10,60,47,119,111,114,107,115,112,97,99,101,95,114,101,115,117,108,116,62],\"stderr\":[],\"exit_code\":1,\"match_count\":0,\"file_matches\":[]}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa38-de6f-7dc0-ae0d-e0f717ed75f2","uuid":"af4aca19-3bbd-4b31-8f23-155a4aebe8c6"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_1054","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The test suite passed. launch-env.txt was written.\n\nPROGRESS.md exists but is stale. It needs updating to match the current evidence.","signature":""},{"type":"text","text":"The suite finished green: `16 passed, 0 failed`, exit 0. I’ll confirm the hand-in files match, update the stale progress note, and remove the cargo target the suite rebuilt."},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-4e3b2ffc-34f1-4f7f-89a0-fcea18fab8e5-10","name":"run_terminal_command","input":{"command":"set -u\nROOT=\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224015__x42677a/work\"\nSCRATCH=\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224015__x42677a/tmp/grok-goal-907ccca5ce3b/implementer\"\nDEV=\"$ROOT/Hands of Harbor: Second Opinion-Trauma Center: Second Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-224015\"\nHTML=\"$ROOT/Hands of Harbor: Second Opinion-Trauma Center: Second Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-224015.html\"\nABOUT=\"$DEV/engine/crates/pav_ui/src/surgery/about.json\"\npython3 - <<'PY'\nimport json, pathlib, re\nroot = pathlib.Path(\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224015__x42677a/work\")\nscratch = pathlib.Path(\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224015__x42677a/tmp/grok-goal-907ccca5ce3b/implementer\")\ndev = root / \"Hands of Harbor: Second Opinion-Trauma Center: Second Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-224015\"\nhtml = root / \"Hands of Harbor: Second Opinion-Trauma Center: Second Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-224015.html\"\nabout = (dev / \"engine/crates/pav_ui/src/surgery/about.json\").read_text()\ninterview = (root / \"exit-interview.json\").read_text()\npage = html.read_text(errors=\"replace\")\nm = re.search(r'<script type=\"application/json\" id=\"about-data\">(.*?)</script>', page, re.S)\nblob = m.group(1) if m else \"\"\nja, ji, jp = json.loads(about), json.