rsor2.txt\\n  - hub-cursor3.txt\\n  - hub-cursor4.txt\\n  - hub-leave.txt\\n  - hub-one.txt\\n  - hub-p2.txt\\n  - hub-p4.txt\\n  - hub-probe.txt\\n  - hub-raf.txt\\n  - hub-raf2.txt\\n  - hub-raf3.txt\\n  - hub-rerun.txt\\n  - hub-rerun2.txt\\n  - hub-rerun3.txt\\n  - hub-rerun4.txt\\n  - hub-server.txt\\n  - hub.txt\\n  - hub_cursor.py\\n  - hub_four.py\\n  - hub_one.py\\n  - hub_probe.py\\n  - hub_raf.py\\n  - launch-1/\\n    - status.json\\n    - title.png\\n  - launch-2/\\n    - status.json\\n    - title.png\\n  - launch-env.txt\\n  - launch.py\\n  - launch.txt\\n  - map-test.txt\\n  - pack.txt\\n  - pack2.txt\\n  - pack3.txt\\n  - pack4.txt\\n  - pack5.txt\\n  - pack6.txt\\n  - probe.txt\\n  - results.py\\n  - results.txt\\n  - shots/\\n    - about.png\\n    - dev.png\\n    - notes.json\\n    - op.png\\n    - results.json\\n    - results.png\\n    - story.png\\n    - title.png\\n  - suite.exit\\n  - suite.txt\\n  - survey.txt\\n  - view-test.txt\\n  - view-test2.txt\",\"absolute_root_path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224015__x42677a/tmp/grok-goal-907ccca5ce3b/implementer\"}}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa38-de6f-7dc0-ae0d-e0f717ed75f2","uuid":"b8d02b43-25ec-46e8-93b2-882d056e7582"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_1069","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"16 surgery tests are running across the system.\n\nsuite.txt only contains a summary line, so I will check map-test.txt and view-test.txt for the actual cargo output. I also need to hunt for bugs in the new contextual_tool and hub path.\n\nThe contextual_tool cursor logic is correct. The simulation offsets the working position after tool selection, and resolve_hands properly promotes based on aim or cursor from the previous frame.\n\nDressing promotion returning DRESSING when only dressings remain is intentional. It triggers when every remaining wound is a closure.\n\nCase 2 phase B requires the player to be on the dressing when selecting gel or any tool. The contextual_tool returns DRESSING because site_tool equals DRESSING regardless of ring selection, except for DEFIB and TOOL_KEEP.\n\nEmber requires a LASER or SCANNER ring. The PLAN specifies Down as Laser and Left as Scanner.\n\nPromoting both laser and scanner to cryo for any ember is more generous than required. This is acceptable.\n\nAfter the first ember stage, the site tool becomes scalpel. The ring stays laser until the player manually cycles to scalpel. The test covers this with a cycle command.\n\nThe contextual_tool distance buffer of radius plus 0.15 safely covers the 0.12 simulation tremor. Ember and dressing radii are large enough to avoid issues.\n\nHub mirror hazards may be missing tool, radius, or kind in their hazard views. The client needs these fields for contextual_tool and drawing. I should check apply_mirror and to_frame.\n\nThe quiet plate test covers a 16x8 grid with 128 vertices. It draws the field, instruments, hazards, and cursors via SDFs. The tray is skipped in quiet mode. The test checks ember and cursor SDFs.\n\nMode 8 might be the mirror mode. The test uses modes 3 and 8.\n\nMode 8 is likely the mirror mode, since instruments() renders cursors for modes 3, 6, and 8.\n\nThe build.rs early return in quiet mode intentionally skips the rest of the demo world to prevent iframe stalls. The surgery field is still emitted.\n\nThe coarse quiet plate mesh is acceptable. Hazards are drawn as separate SDFs, so they remain visible even when wounds sit off the tissue surface.\n\nI need to verify the packed HTML actually contains the new WASM. If the Rust source changed but the HTML was not repacked, the shipped page still runs the old blank hub and outdated tool mapping. I will check the pack logs and confirm the HTML timestamp is newer than the Rust build.\n\nI will check pack timestamps and whether the packed WASM contains identifiable changes. I also need to inspect map-test.txt, view-test.txt, and hub-rerun4 for actual test output.\n\nI am now investigating a potential bug in contextual_tool when the player uses the stick. The hand() function sets aim as a velocity vector for shape_stick input, not as an absolute position. In resolve_hands, the code uses either the absolute aim coordinates or the cursor position depending on the AIM_ABSOLUTE flag before calling contextual_tool.\n\nPad tool promotion relies on the previous frame's cursor position, then the simulation moves the cursor and promotes again. The simulation's promotion is what matters for gameplay.\n\nI also noticed a potential TOOL_KEEP bug. If the input tool is TOOL_KEEP, hands() stores it directly as the ring value, but contextual_tool returns early when the ring equals TOOL_KEEP. This could prevent proper contextual promotion.\n\nThe TOOL_KEEP path is actually correct. When the input tool is TOOL_KEEP, the surgeon keeps its previous tool and contextual_tool applies to that retained value.\n\nThe `min(DEFIB)` clamp is harmless. CRYO is 8 and DRESSING is 9, both below the DEFIB limit of 10, so they survive the clamp unchanged.\n\nIf resolve_hands sets DRESSING but the cursor moves off the dressing in the same tick, the simulation folds back to GEL and stays there unless only dressings remain.\n\nThe `only_dressing` check returns DRESSING even when the cursor is not on a dressing.\n\nThe only_dressing check counts hidden non-dressing hazards as well, so it still triggers when the cursor is on nothing. Case 7 dressing phase works from any position because it only requires K_DRESSING. Heat rings are correctly skipped. A real bug remains: contextual_tool does not promote SCALPEL to CRYO for an ember at stage zero; only LASER and SCANNER are promoted.\n\nThe scanner-to-cryo promotion for an ember is confirmed correct. The simulation sets the surgeon tool to DRESSING before apply, so the dressing paint check passes.\n\nIV and dressing phases are correctly sequenced. Moving to the IV slot reverts the tool to the ring value, so the player must manually select IV before treating a dressing. The scripted code after dressing in case 2 is not part of this gap. I still need to verify that mirror snapshot hazards include positions and that quiet mode receives them.\n\nThe hub sets `hub_quiet = true` before the round begins, so the title screen may skip paper theatre while the pre-op card renders via egui. This is acceptable because Criterion 4 only requires a pre-op card.\n\nLocal play with quiet disabled still uses the full plate.\n\nI will check the packed WASM and HTML for strings like \"contextual\" or \"QUIET\" to confirm the new code is included.\n\nI need to check hub.txt to confirm the hub harness was re-run after the quiet mesh change. The final response claims all four queries passed, but I must verify the log is actually updated and that the HTML was rebuilt following the emit() change.\n\nThe client mirror runs in M_MIRROR. Product-layer promotion is redundant because the simulation handles gameplay using live hazards with radius. The shipped game path relies on the simulation.\n\nI need to check whether mirror hazards carry radius and tool fields. If radius is zero, contextual_tool promotion fails unless the cursor sits exactly on the point, and drawing uses that radius. The host simulation remains authoritative for the world state.\n\nThe host simulation remains authoritative for hub play. If the client fails to promote its tool locally, it still sends the ring value to the host. The host then applies contextual_tool using its own real hazards, so ember and dressing interactions continue correctly.\n\nThe tool gap is fixed. The host simulation handles contextual promotion, so browser clients remain correct even if their local prediction fails. The quiet hub harness draws a coarse plate with hazards and cursors, and the test suite reports 16 passed tests. I will verify those results in view-test.txt and map-test.txt to confirm they are genuine cargo outputs. I also need to scan the new code for any real input bugs.\n\nI re-examined `contextual_tool` for off-by-one or missed promotions that tests might miss. The cycle logic is sound: after a CRYO promotion, the next frame correctly resets to the ring tool because `tools_from_hands` cycles only 0–7 and `DIGITS` can set 8, 9, or 10. I also spotted a bug where `DIGITS` includes `Digit9 = 8`, which maps to CRYO.\n\nPressing key 9 sets harbor.tool to 8, which contextual_tool folds to LASER; this is odd but harmless. The dressing paint test requires four quadrant offsets and at least half the needed work, and the suite reports it passed. I will check map-test.txt to confirm the test name itself succeeded rather than just the summary. The TOOL_KEEP guard in hands() is also correct.\n\nCoverage counting works correctly because resolve_done reads the contextual tool value. A pre-existing select() bug could leave focus stuck on a prior hazard when the player moves to a dressing while holding use, but the test starts fresh so it is not triggered.\n\nTremor does not break contextual promotion because the 0.12 offset remains within the 0.5 radius. The coarse plate spans the full field with sixteen samples from x = -11 to x = 11. In quiet mode, only cursors are drawn; the instrument tray is hidden, and the test expects a cursor SDF at (2, -1).","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-9a6ac9c6-c493-4e32-9c1c-50d5718d0e1d-92","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224015__x42677a/work/Hands of Harbor: Second Opinion-Trauma Center: Second Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-224015/engine/crates/pav_core/src/games/surgery/mod.rs","offset":30,"limit":30}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-9a6ac9c6-c493-4e32-9c1c-50d5718d0e1d-93","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224015__x42677a/tmp/grok-goal-907ccca5ce3b/implementer/view-test2.txt","limit":40}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-9a6ac9c6-c493-4e32-9c1c-50d5718d0e1d-94","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224015__x42677a/tmp/grok-goal-907ccca5ce3b/implementer/map-test.txt","limit":40}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-9a6ac9c6-c493-4e32-9c1c-50d5718d0e1d-95","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224015__x42677a/tmp/grok-goal-907ccca5ce3b/implementer/hub.txt","limit":40}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-9a6ac9c6-c493-4e32-9c1c-50d5718d0e1d-96","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224015__x42677a/tmp/grok-goal-907ccca5ce3b/implementer/suite.exit"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2560,"output_tokens":4031,"cache_read_input_tokens":169984,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa38-de6f-7dc0-ae0d-e0f717ed75f2","uuid":"1020772b-cc8c-4ac5-b08c-6ea951f50138"}
