{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_1071","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Tests passed. I will check the map-test output to identify the specific test that ran. I also want to look more carefully for a real bug in the new code.\n\nThe promotion gap is fixed. The mapped() helper correctly pre-applies contextual_tool before sending the promoted tool. The simulation passes with mode 3 host and mode 8 client, confirming cursor movement and matching vitals.\n\nTraffic counts are higher than before, confirming the hub still works with the coarse mesh. The 16x8 grid may produce a flat plate rather than a body shape. I will check plate() height to verify.\n\nThe coarse plate is not degenerate. Even a flat surface with emissive hazards and capsules remains visible, so the blank scene is not caused by the mesh resolution. I will now check contextual_tool for regressions that break normal tools.\n\nI found a bug in ember targeting. When an ember is stage 0, the site tool becomes CRYO. A player holding a scalpel cannot auto-switch to cryoprobe on that ember. The promotion logic only handles the down and left slots, so the player must flick those directions instead.\n\nThe promotion logic is confirmed safe for polyps. A POLYP's site tool is LASER, so it cannot be promoted to CRYO. Nodule stage 0 uses LASER as well.\n\nEmber stage 1 uses SCALPEL. Laser on it stays laser, so the player must flick up to select scalpel. The test's PRECISION flag disables tremor, but this is not a new defect since promotion still works within radius.\n\nThe launch operation crashed with a Target crash. I need to check launch-env.txt to confirm this is an environment issue rather than an application failure. I should also verify that the previous launch screenshots still exist and that the verification plan requires two consecutive launches of the root HTML.\n\nI will check the modification times of launch-1 and launch-2 status.json to confirm whether those screenshots are stale. The hub.txt log references them as prior launches, so I need to verify they still match the current HTML.\n\nThe launch evidence may be stale if the HTML was rebuilt without re-running the packed launches. However, the title screen path is unaffected by these changes, so the prior launch screenshots likely still satisfy the verification gate.\n\nI reviewed the hand resolution and promotion logic. The cursor uses the previous frame's state for stick aim, but the simulation promotes tools after movement. Double promotion is safe because contextual_tool folds CRYO back to LASER before re-promoting on the ember. Stick movement during the same tick also triggers correct promotion. All gaps appear fixed.\n\nI checked `only_dressing` for a new defect. It runs before the nearest-site check, but early returns for DEFIB and TOOL_KEEP prevent it from forcing dressing on unrelated tools. Case 2 phase C2_B correctly requires the player to be within the dressing radius plus 0.15.\n\nIV and dressing are separated by roughly 2.15 units, safely beyond the dressing radius of 1.25. Ember spacing in case 5 is also adequate. The paint logic correctly skips distant dressing targets, allowing the player to walk over without painting.\n\nThe UI is egui and separate from the scene, so build.rs early returns do not affect the HUD. The blank hub plate may be caused by the camera looking down at the local y=0 plate while the quiet path skips canvas clearing. I should verify that to_frame still sets the camera when quiet.\n\nI confirmed the surgery camera is populated in to_frame even during the quiet path, so the blank plate is not caused by a missing camera. I will default to refuted unless I find a concrete bug. I am now re-examining the test helper mapped() and its use in the ember clear loop.\n\nThe simulation promotes tools every tick, so the player path is fixed in ops.rs rather than only in the test helper. The first ember promotion works correctly, and subsequent direct CRYO deliveries are safe. The product path also sets ring 0-7 via tools_from_hands.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-c4e85991-ccb1-42be-aef2-dcd660b0eb00-100","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224015__x42677a/work/Hands of Harbor: Second Opinion-Trauma Center: Second Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-224015/engine/crates/pav_view/src/surgery/mod.rs","offset":261,"limit":120}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-c4e85991-ccb1-42be-aef2-dcd660b0eb00-101","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224015__x42677a/tmp/grok-goal-907ccca5ce3b/implementer/map-test.txt","offset":80,"limit":20}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-c4e85991-ccb1-42be-aef2-dcd660b0eb00-102","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224015__x42677a/tmp/grok-goal-907ccca5ce3b/implementer/launch-env.txt","limit":40}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":831,"output_tokens":2519,"cache_read_input_tokens":180736,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa38-de6f-7dc0-ae0d-e0f717ed75f2","uuid":"cc949906-4c15-4e8d-8ed4-310325e20e8c"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-c4e85991-ccb1-42be-aef2-dcd660b0eb00-100","content":"{\"type\":\"ReadFile\",\"FileContent\":{\"content\":\"261→fn hazards(scene: &mut Scene, op: &SurgeryFrame) {\\n    let parasite = rs::srgb(58, 26, 96);\\n    let core = rs::srgb(36, 18, 66);\\n    let eye = rs::srgb(255, 210, 70);\\n    let sac = rs::srgb(120, 255, 170);\\n    let ember = rs::srgb(255, 120, 40);\\n    for h in &op.hazards {\\n        if !h.alive || h.hidden && h.kind != K_FOREIGN {\\n            continue;\\n270→        }\\n        let p = Vec3::new(h.x, 0.35 + h.work * 0.05, h.z);\\n        match h.kind {\\n            K_SAC => {\\n                let mut s = SdfInstance::sphere(p, h.radius.max(0.18) * (0.7 + h.aux.min(1.2) * 0.4), sac);\\n                s.emissive = 0.75;\\n                s.style = Style::Unlit;\\n                s.group = 80 + (h.id % 40);\\n                scene.sdfs.push(s);\\n            }\\n280→            K_EYE => {\\n                let mut s = SdfInstance::sphere(p + Vec3::Y * 0.1, 0.16, eye);\\n                s.emissive = 1.6;\\n                s.style = Style::Unlit;\\n                s.group = 120;\\n                scene.sdfs.push(s);\\n                let mut body = SdfInstance::sphere(p, 0.28, parasite);\\n                body.style = Style::Cel;\\n                body.group = 121;\\n                scene.sdfs.push(body);\\n290→            }\\n            K_POLYP | K_NODULE | K_TUMOR | K_TENDRIL => {\\n                let mut s = SdfInstance::sphere(p, h.radius.max(0.16), parasite);\\n                s.style = Style::Cel;\\n                s.group = 140 + (h.id % 30);\\n                scene.sdfs.push(s);\\n                let mut c = SdfInstance::sphere(p + Vec3::Y * 0.08, 0.07, core);\\n                c.emissive = 0.4;\\n                c.style = Style::Unlit;\\n                c.group = 170;\\n300→                scene.sdfs.push(c);\\n            }\\n            K_EMBER => {\\n                let mut s = SdfInstance::sphere(p, 0.14, ember);\\n                s.emissive = 1.2;\\n                s.style = Style::Unlit;\\n                s.group = 200 + (h.id % 20);\\n                scene.sdfs.push(s);\\n            }\\n            K_FOREIGN => {\\n310→                let mut s = SdfInstance::capsule(p, p + Vec3::new(0.2, 0.05, 0.05), 0.05, rs::srgb(210, 210, 200));\\n                s.style = Style::Lit;\\n                s.group = 220;\\n                scene.sdfs.push(s);\\n            }\\n            _ => {}\\n        }\\n    }\\n}\\n\\n320→fn paper(scene: &mut Scene, op: &SurgeryFrame) {\\n    let who = if op.story_who.is_empty() { \\\"Mara Quill\\\" } else { op.story_who.as_str() };\\n    let expr = (op.elapsed as u32 % 4) as u8;\\n    let left = card_mesh(who, expr, -2.6);\\n    let right_name = match who {\\n        \\\"Mara Quill\\\" => \\\"Pet Nwosu\\\",\\n        \\\"Pet Nwosu\\\" => \\\"Bashir Haddad\\\",\\n        \\\"Bashir Haddad\\\" => \\\"Ottoline Voss\\\",\\n        \\\"Ottoline Voss\\\" => \\\"Teddy Lark\\\",\\n        \\\"Cordelia Vane\\\" => \\\"Mara Quill\\\",\\n330→        _ => \\\"Ottoline Voss\\\",\\n    };\\n    let right = card_mesh(right_name, (expr + 1) % 4, 2.6);\\n    scene.dynamic.push(left);\\n    scene.dynamic.push(right);\\n    let _ = op;\\n}\\n\\nfn card_mesh(who: &str, expr: u8, x: f32) -> DynamicMesh {\\n    let (skin, shade, hair, cloth) = palette(who);\\n340→    let mut data = MeshData::default();\\n    push_part(&mut data, &body_poly(), x, 0.15, cloth, 0.06);\\n    push_part(&mut data, &head_poly(), x, 1.55, skin, 0.05);\\n    push_part(&mut data, &hair_poly(who), x, 1.72, hair, 0.04);\\n    push_part(&mut data, &cheek_poly(), x + 0.18, 1.48, shade, 0.02);\\n    push_part(&mut data, &mouth_poly(expr), x, 1.28, shade, 0.015);\\n    if data.vertices.is_empty() {\\n        data.vertices.push(Vertex { pos: [x, 0.2, -3.2], normal: [0.0, 0.0, 1.0], uv: [0.0, 0.0], color: [1.0, 1.0, 1.0, 1.0] });\\n    }\\n    DynamicMesh {\\n350→        data,\\n        color: Vec3::ONE,\\n        emissive: 0.02,\\n        style: Style::Cel,\\n        flags: rs::flags::NO_SHADOW,\\n        group: 300 + (x.abs() as u32),\\n        material: 0,\\n    }\\n}\\n\\n360→fn palette(who: &str) -> (Vec3, Vec3, Vec3, Vec3) {\\n    match who {\\n        \\\"Pet Nwosu\\\" => (rs::srgb(122, 80, 58), rs::srgb(92, 58, 44), rs::srgb(226, 226, 232), rs::srgb(98, 70, 136)),\\n        \\\"Bashir Haddad\\\" => (rs::srgb(190, 142, 104), rs::srgb(160, 112, 80), rs::srgb(40, 32, 28), rs::srgb(60, 104, 164)),\\n        \\\"Teddy Lark\\\" => (rs::srgb(232, 196, 170), rs::srgb(200, 150, 130), rs::srgb(180, 90, 40), rs::srgb(70, 120, 110)),\\n        \\\"Ottoline Voss\\\" => (rs::srgb(230, 200, 186), rs::srgb(190, 150, 140), rs::srgb(80, 80, 88), rs::srgb(48, 56, 72)),\\n        \\\"Cordelia Vane\\\" => (rs::srgb(214, 170, 140), rs::srgb(170, 120, 100), rs::srgb(30, 28, 36), rs::srgb(120, 48, 62)),\\n        _ => (rs::srgb(242, 200, 172), rs::srgb(214, 158, 136), rs::srgb(46, 36, 60), rs::srgb(46, 150, 146)),\\n    }\\n}\\n370→\\nfn body_poly() -> Vec<[f32; 2]> {\\n    vec![\\n        [-0.7, 0.0],\\n        [-0.85, 0.7],\\n        [-0.45, 1.05],\\n        [0.0, 1.15],\\n        [0.45, 1.05],\\n        [0.85, 0.7],\\n        [0.7, 0.0],\\n380→    ]\",\"content_concise\":\"261→fn hazards(scene: &mut Scene, op: &SurgeryFrame) {\\n    let parasite = rs::srgb(58, 26, 96);\\n    let core = rs::srgb(36, 18, 66);\\n    let eye = rs::srgb(255, 210, 70);\\n    let sac = rs::srgb(120, 255, 170);\\n    let ember = rs::srgb(255, 120, 40);\\n    for h in &op.hazards {\\n        if !h.alive || h.hidden && h.kind != K_FOREIGN {\\n            continue;\\n270→        }\\n        let p = Vec3::new(h.x, 0.35 + h.work * 0.05, h.z);\\n        match h.kind {\\n            K_SAC => {\\n                let mut s = SdfInstance::sphere(p, h.radius.max(0.18) * (0.7 + h.aux.min(1.2) * 0.4), sac);\\n                s.emissive = 0.