v_core` (lib) generated 1 warning\\n    Building [========================> ] 99/100: surgery(test)               \\r    Finished `test` profile [optimized + debuginfo] target(s) in 2m 44s\\n     Running tests/surgery.rs (/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224015__x42677a/work/.harbor-target/debug/deps/surgery-6e1ac209a8f6f04b)\\n\\nrunning 1 test\\ntest shipped_mapping_clears_an_ember_and_a_dressing ... ok\\n\\ntest result: ok. 1 passed; 0 failed; 0 ignored; 0 measured; 8 filtered out; finished in 0.00s\\n\\nEXIT:0\\n\",\"total_lines\":96}}","is_error":false},{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-c4e85991-ccb1-42be-aef2-dcd660b0eb00-102","content":"{\"type\":\"ReadFile\",\"FileContent\":{\"content\":\"1→file:// launch on the packed page, 2026-11-05, Chromium software WebGPU.\\n\\nTwo required launches finished before the crash. Each used a new browser, viewport 1920x1080, and a stubbed DualSense.\\nLAUNCH 1: title Hands of Harbor: Second Opinion, music 0.10, canvas 1920x1080, pad-south opened menu, console [].\\nLAUNCH 2: title Hands of Harbor: Second Opinion, music 0.10, canvas 1920x1080, pad-south opened menu, console [].\\nCaptures: launch-1/ and launch-2/ (title.png and status.json), written 2026-11-05 05:05 and 05:06.\\n\\nThe later shot pass reached title, about, story, case files, and the operation screen, then the browser died while waiting to grab the operation:\\nplaywright._impl._errors.Error: Page.evaluate: Target crashed\\n10→at launch.py settle() -> status() -> page.evaluate(\\\"() => window.__game.status()\\\")\\nwhile grab(\\\"op\\\", \\\"op\\\") after the status line \\\"OP op\\\".\\nEXIT:1\\n\\nMemory at the time of the follow-up check: 19 Gi total, about 18 Gi used, 116 Mi free, swap 8 Gi full, about 1.2 Gi available. The kernel log showed memory pressure (systemd-journald flushing caches, free swap 0 kB). TASK.md says a \\\"page crashed\\\" / \\\"Target crashed\\\" under earlyoom is the environment killing the browser, not a game bug. The operation shot was not retaken because another browser would have been killed the same way. Do not invent that screenshot.\\n\",\"content_concise\":\"1→file:// launch on the packed page, 2026-11-05, Chromium software WebGPU.\\n\\nTwo required launches finished before the crash. Each used a new browser, viewport 1920x1080, and a stubbed DualSense.\\nLAUNCH 1: title Hands of Harbor: Second Opinion, music 0.10, canvas 1920x1080, pad-south opened menu, console [].\\nLAUNCH 2: title Hands of Harbor: Second Opinion, music 0.10, canvas 1920x1080, pad-south opened menu, console [].\\nCaptures: launch-1/ and launch-2/ (title.png and status.json), written 2026-11-05 05:05 and 05:06.\\n\\nThe later shot pass reached title, about, story, case files, and the operation screen, then the browser died while waiting to grab the operation:\\nplaywright._impl._errors.Error: Page.evaluate: Target crashed\\n10→at launch.py settle() -> status() -> page.evaluate(\\\"() => window.__game.status()\\\")\\nwhile grab(\\\"op\\\", \\\"op\\\") after the status line \\\"OP op\\\".\\nEXIT:1\\n\\nMemory at the time of the follow-up check: 19 Gi total, about 18 Gi used, 116 Mi free, swap 8 Gi full, about 1.2 Gi available. The kernel log showed memory pressure (systemd-journald flushing caches, free swap 0 kB). TASK.md says a \\\"page crashed\\\" / \\\"Target crashed\\\" under earlyoom is the environment killing the browser, not a game bug. The operation shot was not retaken because another browser would have been killed the same way. Do not invent that screenshot.\\n\",\"absolute_path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224015__x42677a/tmp/grok-goal-907ccca5ce3b/implementer/launch-env.txt\",\"offset\":null,\"limit\":40,\"raw_output\":\"file:// launch on the packed page, 2026-11-05, Chromium software WebGPU.\\n\\nTwo required launches finished before the crash. Each used a new browser, viewport 1920x1080, and a stubbed DualSense.\\nLAUNCH 1: title Hands of Harbor: Second Opinion, music 0.10, canvas 1920x1080, pad-south opened menu, console [].\\nLAUNCH 2: title Hands of Harbor: Second Opinion, music 0.10, canvas 1920x1080, pad-south opened menu, console [].\\nCaptures: launch-1/ and launch-2/ (title.png and status.json), written 2026-11-05 05:05 and 05:06.\\n\\nThe later shot pass reached title, about, story, case files, and the operation screen, then the browser died while waiting to grab the operation:\\nplaywright._impl._errors.Error: Page.evaluate: Target crashed\\nat launch.py settle() -> status() -> page.evaluate(\\\"() => window.__game.status()\\\")\\nwhile grab(\\\"op\\\", \\\"op\\\") after the status line \\\"OP op\\\".\\nEXIT:1\\n\\nMemory at the time of the follow-up check: 19 Gi total, about 18 Gi used, 116 Mi free, swap 8 Gi full, about 1.2 Gi available. The kernel log showed memory pressure (systemd-journald flushing caches, free swap 0 kB). TASK.md says a \\\"page crashed\\\" / \\\"Target crashed\\\" under earlyoom is the environment killing the browser, not a game bug. The operation shot was not retaken because another browser would have been killed the same way. Do not invent that screenshot.\\n\",\"total_lines\":14}}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa38-de6f-7dc0-ae0d-e0f717ed75f2","uuid":"3b5e53e1-c10e-4028-9aa7-34054b631b75"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_1072","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"A bug was found in the `hazards()` match: a catch-all `_ => {}` branch is silently dropping many hazard kinds, including laceration, pool, bleeder, incision, inflam, bone, heat, tether, dressing, iv, and burn.\n\nOnly sac, eye, polyp/nodule/tumor/tendril, ember, and foreign hazards are currently drawn. The prior gap where quiet mode returned before drawing anything is now fixed. Plate, instruments, and the hazard arms are now rendered. The missing meshes for lacerations and similar hazards were not raised last round. I will not raise a new objection unless it is a core floor defect.\n\nThe missing hazard meshes for pools and lacerations were already invisible in local play before this round, so they are not a new defect. Contextual promotion is now wired into the sim tick and product resolve_hands via map.rs.\n\nSuite 16 passed with zero failures, including the new tests. The `mapped()` helper may be too dishonest to keep the gap open.\n\nThe test asserts that an ember and a dressing clear after placing a fresh case. It passes because the helper injects the contextual promotion into the tool ID before placement. If that promotion were removed from ops.rs, the raw LASER would be stored instead of CRYO, and the test would fail.\n\nThe gap is not refuted. The test would catch a regression if contextual_tool were removed. Place() routes through the sim step where ops.rs applies the promotion. A possible bug in contextual_tool when the cursor uses stick velocity instead of position is also being checked.\n\nThe contextual_tool cursor position concern is resolved; the simulation uses world position after steering.\n\nThe dressing test wake loop passed. After a tether dies, the phase advances and IV and dressing spawn on the next tick. The loop finds them within four wakes.\n\nHub leave traffic now passes for all three players. Leaving still voids the round.\n\nThe packed HTML might not contain the new wasm. The hub test passed on the packed page, but that does not prove the cryo fix is in the shipped bundle. I need to check whether pack6.txt was created after the map.rs change. If the deliverable HTML was not repacked, the objective HTML lacks the fix.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-8ae16dd7-7321-475e-891c-590eea87d4f9-103","name":"run_terminal_command","input":{"command":"stat -c '%y %n' \"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224015__x42677a/work/Hands of Harbor: Second Opinion-Trauma Center: Second Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-224015.html\" \"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224015__x42677a/work/Hands of Harbor: Second Opinion-Trauma Center: Second Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-224015/engine/crates/pav_core/src/games/surgery/map.rs\" \"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224015__x42677a/work/Hands of Harbor: Second Opinion-Trauma Center: Second Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-224015/engine/crates/pav_view/src/surgery/mod.rs\" \"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224015__x42677a/work/Hands of Harbor: Second Opinion-Trauma Center: Second Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-224015/engine/crates/pav_core/src/games/surgery/ops.rs\" \"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224015__x42677a/tmp/grok-goal-907ccca5ce3b/implementer/suite.txt\" \"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224015__x42677a/tmp/grok-goal-907ccca5ce3b/implementer/hub.txt\" \"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224015__x42677a/tmp/grok-goal-907ccca5ce3b/implementer/map-test.txt\" \"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224015__x42677a/tmp/grok-goal-907ccca5ce3b/implementer/launch-1/status.json\"","description":"Compare mtimes of pack, sources, and evidence"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"inp