{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_1074","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The hub HTML in tests/hub is dated 01:22, while the root HTML is dated 05:02.\n\nThe stale hub HTML predates the fixes in map.rs, view, and product. If the hub server served that old copy, the re-run never tested the new quiet mesh. The root HTML is the actual deliverable.\n\nThe hub log at 05:16 predates the root pack. If the server served the stale tests/hub HTML, the harness pass does not prove the new coarse mesh avoids stalling.\n\nThe source test already proves the mesh is emitted. The blank field was a code bug, now fixed. A stale copy would still pass because the protocol itself worked. The new mesh might stall iframes, so the new pack may not have been retested. I need to check whether the server served the work root or tests/hub, and whether the hub HTML is a symlink.\n\nThe stat confirmed the tests/hub HTML is a regular file from 01:22. The plan requires copying the packed game next to harness.html, so the implementer may have missed updating that copy. The root HTML is what users actually open, and the hub integration inside it is what matters.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-9a87039b-bdfb-4023-88db-f6877d6a9fc1-105","name":"grep","input":{"pattern":"http.server|tests/hub|43467|37019|html","path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224015__x42677a/tmp/grok-goal-907ccca5ce3b/implementer/hub.txt"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-9a87039b-bdfb-4023-88db-f6877d6a9fc1-106","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224015__x42677a/tmp/grok-goal-907ccca5ce3b/implementer/hub_four.py","limit":80}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1242,"output_tokens":811,"cache_read_input_tokens":189056,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa38-de6f-7dc0-ae0d-e