look(scene: &mut Scene, _rig: &crate::camera::CameraRig, aspect: f32, shot: &CameraShot, quiet: bool) {\"},{\"line_number\":64,\"content\":\"    if quiet {\"},{\"line_number\":205,\"content\":\"fn instruments(scene: &mut Scene, op: &SurgeryFrame) {\"},{\"line_number\":208,\"content\":\"    for (i, c) in op.cursors.iter().enumerate() {\"},{\"line_number\":222,\"content\":\"        let y = 0.55 + if c.tool == op.cursors[0].tool { 0.12 } else { 0.0 };\"},{\"line_number\":227,\"content\":\"    if !op.quiet && (op.mode == 3 || op.mode == 0 || op.mode == 6) {\"},{\"line_number\":231,\"content\":\"            let lift = op.cursors.first().map(|c| c.tool == t as u8).unwrap_or(false);\"},{\"line_number\":261,\"content\":\"fn hazards(scene: &mut Scene, op: &SurgeryFrame) {\"},{\"line_number\":542,\"content\":\"    fn quiet_hub_draws_plate_instruments_hazards_and_cursors() {\"},{\"line_number\":545,\"content\":\"            op.quiet = true;\"},{\"line_number\":548,\"content\":\"            op.cursors[0] = CursorView {\"},{\"line_number\":566,\"content\":\"            let cursor = scene.sdfs.iter().any(|s| (s.a.x - 2.0).abs() < 0.05 && (s.a.z + 1.0).abs() < 0.05);\"},{\"line_number\":568,\"content\":\"            assert!(cursor, \\\"mode {mode} cursor sdf missing\\\");\"}]}]}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa38-de6f-7dc0-ae0d-e0f717ed75f2","uuid":"42b17ad8-ecb9-464f-bc8e-85829edb34f6"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_1085","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"computes the tool with contextual_tool and writes it directly to SurgeonInput.tool. Bot tests do the same, so they stay green while the player path cannot select Cryoprobe or Dressing.\n\nA new test will drive the full shipped mapping from a fresh case and assert that an ember and a dressing clear. It computes the tool with contextual_tool inside the test, then calls place(). The test uses `down` for the ember placement,I need to trace the path from player input to the simulator applying which maps to LASER rather than CRYO. contextual_tool.\n\nThe test asserts that a LASER placed on an ember converts to CRYO during the simulation step. This validates the real player path if ops.rs applies contextual_tool inside its step function. The mapped helper also computes the tool with contextual_tool before calling place.\n\nThe `mapped()` test helper calls `contextual_tool` directly and writes the result into `SurgeonInput.tool`. This bypasses the player path, which cannot select Cryoprobe or Dressing.\n\nThe test pre-computes contextual_tool and\n\nBot tests also pass writes the promoted LASER into `place()` tool directly into  and assert the surgeonSurgeonInput. This risks double-promotion. The tool becomes CRYO.  real question is whetherThis confirms they bypass the simulation step the player path by  itself promotes player input, or if the testwriting `SurgeonInput.tool` merely pre-sets the directly. tool. I need to inspect ops.rs around lines 343 and 755, and product.rs around its input handling, to confirm the promotion logic lives in the simulation step.\n\nThe simulator itself applies contextual_tool during input processing. The real step path in ops.rs line 343 calls it directly. This confirms auto-swap is built into the game engine, not just test helpers.\n\nThe simulation folds CRYO back to LASER and DRESSING to GEL before re-promoting over hazards. This confirms the first test's LASER-on-ember\n\n`product.rs` also  placement is the honestapplies `contextual_tool` check of the real player in `resolve_hands`  path. The mapped helper'sbefore sending inputs pre-computed tool should to the simulator.\n\n also work if the simulationThe planned test will applies contextual_tool. exercise octant, cycle, and tray mappings to obtain LASER, SCANNER, scalpel, suture, and forceps. It will then verify that contextual swaps promote an ember to Cryoprobe and a dressing to Dressing.\n\nThe test asserts that both the ember and the dressing are cleared.\n\nI need to confirm the simulation step promotes player tools through the path product.rs uses, and that product.rs does not bypass it.\n\nThe blank scene fix removes emit() early returns. It now draws a coarse plate, instruments, and hazards while skipping paper cards when quiet.\n\nI must verify instruments and hazards render during quiet mode, cursors draw, product.rs sets hub_quiet, and the 3D scene alone suffices or the egui shell also renders. The `mapped` helper pre-selects the tool by calling `contextual_tool` directly, which may be dishonest if it bypasses the player path. However, the test also places the raw ring tool and asserts the simulator promotes it, so the contextual swap is still exercised.\n\nThe `mapped` helper pre-applies `contextual_tool`, so the test would still pass even if the simulator removed that swap from its step path. This means the test does not actually exercise the live player path.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-6998630a-5e69-4a6f-bbee-b491190c9e7e-9","name":"grep","input":{"pattern":"fn instruments|fn hazards|cursor|quiet|fn paper","path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224015__x42677a/work/Hands of Harbor: Second Opinion-Trauma Center: Second Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-224015/engine/crates/pav_view/src/surgery/mod.rs"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-6998630a-5e69-4a6f-bbee-b491190c9e7e-10","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224015__x42677a/work/Hands of Harbor: Second Opinion-Trauma Center: Second Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-224015/engine/crates/pav_app/src/product.rs","offset":230,"limit":320}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-6998630a-5e69-4a6f-bbee-b491190c9e7e-11","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224015__x42677a/work/Hands of Harbor: Second Opinion-Trauma Center: Second Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-224015/engine/crates/pav_core/src/games/surgery/ops.rs","offset":300,"limit":120}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-6998630a-5e69-4a6f-bbee-b491190c9e7e-12","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224015__x42677a/work/Hands of Harbor: Second Opinion-Trauma Center: Second Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-224015/engine/crates/pav_core/src/games/surgery/ops.rs","offset":680,"limit":120}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":7448,"output_tokens":1620,"cache_read_input_tokens":33664,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa38-de6f-7dc0-ae0d-e0f717ed75f2","uuid":"9fcd5ab7-4128-4086-88b7-3293ce192dcd"}
