{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_1092","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"from an ember, digit 9 yields LASER; away from a dressing, digit 0 yields GEL. This is acceptable for contextual design.\n\nThe pad path selects ring tools 0-7, which the simulation then promotes correctly.\n\nA potential bug remains: contextual_tool picks the nearest site within radius+0.15 and uses that site's tool field for promotion. The wrong hazard could be targeted.\n\nThe promotion logic is sound for mixed-case wounds. When both embers and dressings remain, contextual_tool correctly promotes to CRYO over an ember and to DRESSING over a dressing. The comment \"Any ring tool becomes Dressing on a closure\" is accurate: a dressing hazard's tool field is DRESSING, so any ring tool appliedCounting the pav_core surgery tests. there yields DRESSING. This behavior is correct.\n\nScanner over an ember becomes CRYO, which may prevent scanning if embers start hidden.\n\n8 pav_core surgery I need to check the tests are counted,  ember hazard logic.excluding the ignored A new bug was found in assist_aim: it uses balance_sheet test. the raw tool before 6 pav_ui surgery tests promotion. are also present.\n\npav_audio and pav_view\n\nThe `assist_aim` call passes the raw ring each contribute one tool before contextual test. The total is  promotion. Because embers only accept CRYO,16, matching the expected laser aim assist will not pull toward them. count. This may make pad aiming harder for embers, but mouse absolute aim is unaffected. It is unclear whether this is a demonstrable defect.\n\nThe assist_aim issue\n\nThe balance_sheet  is not a blocker becausetest was added by this manual aim still works. goal. Prior rounds  The next step is todid not flag it. The inspect the ember hazard anti-ratchet rule only apply logic for a real allows refuting new gameplay bug. objections that are demonstrable defects or unmet gating criteria.\n\nThe balance_sheet #[ignore] predates the current gaps. It was not raised by the prior skeptic. This is a re-verification round. The explicit rule still requires refuting tests this goal added.\n\nThe pre-existing balance_sheet #[ignore] should not be refuted, since the plan treats balance as evidence rather than gating. I will verify the suite log is from after the fix by comparing file mtimes.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-04f7e975-c4ff-468f-acd9-b890aa05ecd4-13","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224015__x42677a/work/Hands of Harbor: Second Opinion-Trauma Center: Second Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-224015/engine/crates/pav_view/src/surgery/mod.rs","offset":200,"limit":400}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-04f7e975-c4ff-468f-acd9-b890aa05ecd4-14","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224015__x42677a/work/Hands of Harbor: Second Opinion-Trauma Center: Second Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-224015/engine/crates/pav_app/src/product.rs","offset":640,"limit":150}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-04f7e975-c4ff-468f-acd9-b890aa05ecd4-15","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224015__x42677a/work/Hands of Harbor: Second Opinion-Trauma Center: Second Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-224015/engine/crates/pav_core/src/games/surgery/hazard.rs","offset":380,"limit":80}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-04f7e975-c4ff-468f-acd9-b890aa05ecd4-16","name":"grep","input":{"pattern":"fn emit|surgery::emit|op\\.quiet|hub_quiet|apply_look","path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224015__x42677a/work/Hands of Harbor: Second Opinion-Trauma Center: Second Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-224015/engine/crates","glob":"*.rs"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":8512,"output_tokens":6242,"cache_read_input_tokens":41088,"c