{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_1095","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":" because the shell keeps the old tool when the cursor is off the site, and the simulation corrects it once the cursor lands.I need to verify whether the test is honest \n\nThe shell and simulation resolve tools consistently.and if real bugs exist. The hub blank scene bug is fixed because emit() now draws geometry, and the test checks that geometry. I am now checking whether the cursor assertions are dishonest, since tool_mesh creates a capsule from `at` to `at+tip`.\n\nChecking the resolve_hands call site timing in product.rs. Verifying if paint() actually paints. Assessing whether the test's pre-applied contextual_tool is honest alongside simulation\n\nThe test assertions logic. Investigating are geometrically sound. a potential hub mode bug in instruments() The tool capsule origin and the cursor loop sits at the cursor  behavior during Codeposition, the ember  Blue.SDF is correctly placed, and the plate mesh has 128 vertices within the expected bounds. Mode 0 early break does not apply because the test uses modes 3 and 8. I am now checking whether `boot_hub_round` preserves the quiet flag and sets the correct mode so instruments draw during shared Code Blue.\n\nChecking what mode 8 represents. Many hazard types skip SDF","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-1d4bc546-751c-4e96-a930-b7950c4bc385-24","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224015__x42677a/work/Hands of Harbor: Second Opinion-Trauma Center: Second Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-224015/engine/crates/pav_core/src/games/surgery/mod.rs","offset":270,"limit":120}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-1d4bc546-751c-4e96-a930-b7950c4bc385-25","name":"grep","input":{"pattern":"fn boot_hub_round|fn boot_mirror|fn apply_mirror|mode =","path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-2