{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_1102","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":" that wants it. Otherwise resolve_hands folds it back to LASER. The stored tool stays 8 until the next compose cycle, but resolve_hands folds it again on the following frame. This confirms the contextual tool resolution logic is sound.\n\nThe ring arithmeticChecking CameraShot::default and whether the plate after the match is  is in view.safe because CRYO and DRESSING are already folded, and DEFIB returns early. A potential bug exists in `only_dressing`: if every alive non-heat hazard is a dressing, it forces DRESSING everywhere regardless of distance from the wound.\n\nThe test position sits outside the dressing radius, so only_dressing does not apply and the assertion passes. If every remaining hazard were a dressing, however, every ring tool would become DRESSING everywhere and block scanner or suction use.\n\nChecking which hazard kinds are visible. Only SAC, EYE, POLYP, NODULE, TUMOR, TENDRIL, EMBER, and FOREIGN draw as SDFs. Other kinds like laceration or pool only affect plate vertex paint. Need to verify what Code Blue spawns.\n\nThe only_dressing behavior is intentional when every remaining wound is a closure. The test confirms case 5 embers carry the CRYO tool field, so promotion works correctly. Case 7 embers and dressings are not explicitly tested, but they would follow the same mapping if they use the same hazard kinds.\n\nOn a 16x8 quiet plate, vertices are roughly 1.5 units apart. Small hazards like lacerations with radius ~0.4 would miss all vertices entirely. Embers are drawn as SDFs and remain visible regardless. Pools, lacerations, and dressings rely on vertex paint and would be nearly invisible on this coarse grid.\n\nThe prior gap required drawing plate, instruments, hazards, and cursors.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-5e8b771f-a86c-4605-9d4f-371fabc67fe8-21","name":"read_file","input":{"