ghtmirror bug therefore not be 3 or 8, which does not corrupt the would prevent extra authoritative server-side cursors from drawing. tool selection.\n\nThe prior blank mirror scene was caused by missing cursors. Drawing the local cursor, plate, and some hazards should fix that. I need to verify whether modes 3 and 8 are actually M_OP and M_MIRROR. I also want to confirm\n\nThe mirror bug does that `shipped_mapping_clears_an_ember_and_a_dressing` not corrupt the client's is included in the  local hand prediction.16 tests, since the  Because the client'stest runner spans multiple ring tool is SCALPEL, cargo commands. the promotion condition `tool == CRYO && ring == LASER` fails, so resolve_hands still\n\nThe 16 tests passed. returns SCALPEL. The I need to verify the host simulation remains new test is actually authoritative. counted, since ignored tests are skipped by the runner. The function has no `#[ignore]` attribute, so it should be included.\n\nA real bug may still prevent pads from clearing embers and dressings. The player path sets the tool in hand(), but resolve_hands calls contextual_tool and overwrites s.tool before the simulation sees it.\n\nThe simulation calls\n\nThe host re-contextualizes remote inputs for all contextual_tool again slots, so the stale after resolve_hands. client tool is corrected CRYO folds back to  server-side. This is not a gameplay break.LASER. Over an ember, The mirror bug would the tool becomes CRYO only cause a visual desync where the client cursor shows the wrong again. instrument; it does not affect the actual server simulation.\n\nThe double contextual_tool call is safe because resolve_hands uses the previous frame's cursor position for\n\nThe mirror tool bug pad aim. The simulation is not a gating failure steers the cursor with for the blank scene the stick before applying gap. It is a pre-existing contextual_tool at  issue and does not the new position.explain the missing draw.\n\nThe `mapped` test correctly promotes the tool before placing, so the assertion that the ember clears is valid.\n\nThe ignored `balance_sheet` test is also pre-existing.\n\nMouse absolute mode also works correctly: resolve_hands promotes based on the aim position,\n\nThe dressing tool  and the simulation snaps the cursor to behavior is intentional. I am checking paint()that aim before applying contextual_tool again. to confirm DRESSING\n\nFor DRESSING folding, accepts gel on dressing if resolve_hands sets sites, and verifying the tool to DRESSING the cursor offset works because the cursor  correctly. I will inspectis over a dressing, the simulation folds file mtimes, view-test2 it back to GEL. It  output, suite test only returns DRESSING again if no wounds remain or the nearest site still uses DRESSING.\n\nThe `only_dressing` helper intentionally returns DRESSING even when the cursor is not over the wound itself, specifically when everynames, hub.txt, and launch status before finalizing the gating decision. remaining wound is a closure.\n\nPromoting any ring tool to DRESSING when the cursor is over a dressing is intentional, so forceps near a dressing become dressing. Ember stage 0 correctly requires CRYO because pad stick down is laser and left is scanner. After ember stage 1, the tool becomes SCALPEL, which bypasses the CRYO promotion branch and falls through to the default ring","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-6f43b46e-70db-42b5-bf02-e3aeba267a1e-35","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224015__x42677a/work/Hands of Harbor: Second Opinion-Trauma Center: Second Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-224015/engine/crates/pav_app/src/product.rs","offset":150,"limit":100}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-6f43b46e-70db-42b5-bf02-e3aeba267a1e-36","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224015__x42677a/work/Hands of Harbor: Second Opinion-Trauma Center: Second Opinion-grok-4.7-xhi