rame; not part of the saved state.\\n\\nuse glam::Vec3;\\n\\nuse super::kinds::TITLE;\\n\\n#[derive(Clone, Copy, Debug)]\\npub struct CameraShot {\\n    pub tilt: f32,\\n10→    pub yaw: f32,\\n    pub distance: f32,\\n    pub fov_deg: f32,\\n    pub target: Vec3,\\n    pub follow_lag: f32,\\n    pub height_offset: f32,\\n}\\n\\nimpl Default for CameraShot {\\n    fn default() -> Self {\\n20→        Self {\\n            tilt: 73.0,\\n            yaw: 0.0,\\n            distance: 19.9,\\n            fov_deg: 36.0,\\n            target: Vec3::new(0.0, 0.0, 0.2),\\n            follow_lag: 0.0,\\n            height_offset: 0.0,\\n        }\\n    }\\n30→}\\n\\n#[derive(Clone, Copy, Debug)]\\npub struct HazardView {\\n    pub id: u32,\\n    pub kind: u8,\\n    pub x: f32,\\n    pub z: f32,\\n    pub radius: f32,\\n    pub work: f32,\\n40→    pub need: f32,\\n    pub alive: bool,\\n    pub hidden: bool,\\n    pub stage: u8,\\n    pub stages: u8,\\n    pub axis: f32,\\n    pub aux: f32,\\n    pub bits: u8,\\n    pub tool: u8,\\n    pub grabbed: bool,\\n50→}\",\"absolute_path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224015__x42677a/work/Hands of Harbor: Second Opinion-Trauma Center: Second Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-224015/engine/crates/pav_core/src/games/surgery/frame.rs\",\"offset\":1,\"limit\":50,\"raw_output\":\"//! What one draw of the operation needs. Built fresh each frame; not part of the saved state.\\n\\nuse glam::Vec3;\\n\\nuse super::kinds::TITLE;\\n\\n#[derive(Clone, Copy, Debug)]\\npub struct CameraShot {\\n    pub tilt: f32,\\n    pub yaw: f32,\\n    pub distance: f32,\\n    pub fov_deg: f32,\\n    pub target: Vec3,\\n    pub follow_lag: f32,\\n    pub height_offset: f32,\\n}\\n\\nimpl Default for CameraShot {\\n    fn default() -> Self {\\n        Self {\\n            tilt: 73.0,\\n            yaw: 0.0,\\n            distance: 19.9,\\n            fov_deg: 36.0,\\n            target: Vec3::new(0.0, 0.0, 0.2),\\n            follow_lag: 0.0,\\n            height_offset: 0.0,\\n        }\\n    }\\n}\\n\\n#[derive(Clone, Copy, Debug)]\\npub struct HazardView {\\n    pub id: u32,\\n    pub kind: u8,\\n    pub x: f32,\\n    pub z: f32,\\n    pub radius: f32,\\n    pub work: f32,\\n    pub need: f32,\\n    pub alive: bool,\\n    pub hidden: bool,\\n    pub stage: u8,\\n    pub stages: u8,\\n    pub axis: f32,\\n    pub aux: f32,\\n    pub bits: u8,\\n    pub tool: u8,\\n    pub grabbed: bool,\\n}\\n\",\"total_lines\":206}}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa38-de6f-7dc0-ae0d-e0f717ed75f2","uuid":"30f6138d-70d5-4a68-839d-e0941e59d08f"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_1105","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"\n\nThe test manually cycles the player to scalpel before stage 1, so the tool remains LASER rather than becoming SCALPEL. This is acceptable because the prior gap concerned auto-selection of cryo and dressing, not stage advancement. The full ember clear works through the mapping.A potential bug was noticed in the L1/R1 mapping.\n\nThe test helper `mapped()` pre-applies `contextual_tool` before writing the tool into `SurgeonInput.tool`. The simulation still runs its own promotion pass afterward, so the tool is folded back and re-promoted. This means the test does not bypass the simulation's logic. If the simulation's `contextual_tool` call were removed entirely, the test would still send `CRYO` directly and the ember would clear anyway.\n\nThe test's first assertion sends LASER and expects CRYO, confirming the simulation must run contextual_tool. If that call were removed,\n\nChecking gilrs documentation the test would fail. to verify whether `LeftTrigger` The mapped() helper then sends CRYO directly, corresponds to the  so the test does notanalog L2/LT or a separate bypass promotion. button.\n\nThe dressing test sends gel and asserts the simulation stores DRESSING. This confirms the simulation must fold gel into dressing. The mapped helper then sends DRESSING directly for clearing.\n\nThe mapping likely swapped L1 and L2. If so, tool cycling would fire on the triggers instead of the bumpers. The code also shows `rt` is mapped to USE.\n\nThe dressing test sends GEL on the first tick and expects the simulation to promote it to DRESSING before painting. The mapped helper then sends DRESSING directly for subsequent ticks. Because paint() exits early when the tool matches the hazard, only DRESSING can successfully paint the dressing. Quadrant painting uses 0.55 offsets.\n\nThe code confirms L1 cycles tools and RT triggers use. If gilrs swapped the trigger names, the mapping would instead match \n\nThe suite output onlya Trauma Center layout reports counts, not where L1 cycles and individual test names. LT is precision. This A panic would have  appears to be a pre-existingcaused a failure, so bug rather than a recent the new test likely regression. passed. I should check whether suite.txt is stale by comparing its timestamp against the source files.\n\nThe L1/R1 mapping was accepted as correct; the prior gap was only missing contextual promotion. I will verify\n\nview-test2.txt appears evidence freshness  to be a truncated compileand check that gating log, so suite.txt is evidence still exists. I also need to confirm the authoritative run whether the test file's record. I need to verify mapped() bypasses the the exact mode constants simulation's contextual for M_MIRROR and M_OP path. to confirm whether the test covers the correct hub modes.\n\nThe test covers the exact gap requirements: it drives the shipped mapping and asserts that an ember and dressing clear. The clear loops use mapped(), which pre-applies contextual_tool, so they would still pass even if the simulation's contextual_tool were removed. However, the place() calls assert that the simulation stores the promoted tool, meaning those assertions would fail if the simulation did not promote the tool.\n\nDressings may still be invisible because they lack SDF drawing. On the 16×8 plate, a dressing radius of roughly 0.3 likely falls between vertices, so it cannot alter the coarse vertex colors.\n\nThe promotion assertion The plate body itself is independent of the is still rendered. clear loop. It would fail if contextual_tool were removed from hands(), while the clear assertions prove CRYO and DRESSING finish the hazards. Together they satisfy the prior gap.\n\nThe 16×8 plate has 128 vertices, satisfying the test's span and count assertions, so the field mesh exists. I still need to verify that RenderFrame.surgery is populated when hub_quiet is true, since the quiet path might otherwise produce an empty scene. In server mode, AIHub.server runs the world without a local slot or drawing, and surgeons are zeroed out.\n\nThe server might still draw despite running without a local slot. Criterion 4 forbids drawing in server mode, but this was not raised in prior gaps and may be a pre-existing issue. I will not re-litigate it unless it is a new defect or unmet gating criterion.\n\nThe server path draws even during active play. The draw gate only skips rendering when the hub is active and not playing, so the server renders the scene while running the world.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-961d5ba8-063e-4a7a-9cb5-f0556652e27f-38","name":"run_terminal_command","input":{"command":"python3 - << 'PY'\nimport os, time\nfrom pathlib import Path\nroot = Path(\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224015__x42677a\")\nimpl = root/\"tmp/grok-goal-907ccca5ce3b/implementer\"\nwork = root/\"work\"\nfiles = [\n    impl/\"suite.txt\", impl/\"suite.exit\", impl/\"hub.txt\", impl/\"launch-env.txt\",\n    impl/\"launch-1/status.json\", impl/\"launch-2/status.json\",\n    impl/\"view-test2.txt\", impl/\"map-test.txt\",\n]\ndev = work/\"Hands of Harbor: Second Opinion-Trauma Center: Second Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-224015\"\nsrcs = [\n    dev/\"engine/crates/pav_core/src/games/surgery/map.rs\",\n    dev/\"engine/crates/pav_core/tests/surgery.rs\",\n    dev/\"engine/crates/pav_view/src/surgery/mod.rs\",\n    dev/\"engine/crates/pav_view/src/build.rs\",\n    dev/\"engine/crates/pav_app/src/product.rs\",\n    dev/\"tests/run_all.py\",\n    work/\"engine-link\",\n]\ndef fmt(p):\n    if not p.exists():\n        return f\"MISSING {p}\"\n    st = p.lstat()\n    kind = \"link\" if p.is_symlink() else (\"dir\" if p.is_dir() else \"file\")\n    extra = \"\"\n    if p.is_symlink():\n        extra = \" -> \" + os.readlink(p)\n    return f\"{time.strftime('%Y-%m-%d %H:%M:%S', time.localtim