{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_1106","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"\n\nAn unmet gating criterion can be raised even if prior rounds did not flag it, provided it is a demonstrable defect in shipped behavior. Criterion 4 explicitly forbids server drawing, so the server rendering during active play is a valid new objection. The key question is whether this was implicitly accepted in prior rounds.Noted a timestamp in map.rs at 03:35:48.\n\nI need to inspect the hub harness to see if it explicitly checks that the server draws nothing. If the harness passed, prior rounds may have implicitly accepted the server rendering during active play. Raising this now would require proving the harness does not already enforce criterion 4.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-b6db4ea0-2372-4721-9491-02a5584463fd-27","name":"grep","input":{"pattern":"M_OP|M_MIRROR|M_CODE|const M_","path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224015__x42677a/work/Hands of Harbor: Second Opinion-Trauma Center: Second Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-224015/engine/crates/pav_core/src/games/surgery","glob":"*.rs"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-b6db4ea0-2372-4721-9491-02a5584463fd-28","name":"grep","input":{"pattern":"#\\[test\\]","path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224015__x42677a/work/Hands of Harbor: Second Opinion-Trauma Center: Second Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-224015/engine/crates/pav_core/tests/surgery.rs"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-b6db4ea0-2372-4721-9491-02a5584463fd-29","name":"grep","input":{"pattern":"server|draw|canvas","path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224015__x42677a/work/Hands of Harbor: Second Opinion-Trauma Center: Second Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-224015/tests/hub","glob":"*.js"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-b6db4ea0-2372-4721-9491-02a5584463fd-30","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home