{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_1108","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"\n\nThe paint() check requires the tool to be DRESSING, which is satisfied. The double application of contextual_tool is safe: CRYO folds back to LASER, then resolves to CRYO again over an ember.Checking title screenshots to confirm they are painted rather than blank.\n\nLeaving an ember correctly restores the ring tool for the next frame. The shell's self.tool stays unchanged because resolve_hands only modifies SurgeonInput for that frame. A potential bug was spotted: resolve_hands uses the previous frame's cursor position for stick aim when absolute aim is not active.\n\nThe pad cursor concern is resolved. The simulation steers the cursor and re-applies contextual_tool at the new position, making it the authoritative source. resolve_hands\n\nLaunches succeeded. is only a preview and I will read the two gets corrected.\n\nA  title PNGs. The hubpotential bug was found traffic numbers in  in `only_dressing`: when every remainingFINAL_RESPONSE do not wound requires dressing, any cursor position match hub.txt. returns DRESSING regardless of distance.\n\nThe test confirms that `only_dressing` does not trigger when other hazards remain. The assertion passes because the far cursor position fails the nearest-site check and returns GEL. When only dressings are left, the player is locked to DRESSING everywhere\n\nhub.txt shows higher by design. This lets traffic numbers and them finish closures a HUB 0 failure. The without precise aim. later hub.txt is the However, paint() still requires the cursor authoritative evidence. to be within radius The FINAL_RESPONSE  before it can set bits.prose summary is inconsistent but not a code defect. I am checking for fabricated claims about files absent from CHANGED_FILES.\n\nThe digit 9 and 0 keys are now mapped. Pressing either key sets the tool to CRYO, but contextual_tool immediately folds CRYO back to LASER. It only re-promotes to CRYO while hovering over an ember. Away from\n\nThe stale traffic  an ember, the pad usernumbers in the opening simply holds laser. paragraph likely come from an older run. The later \"changes this round\" section matches hub.txt, so the evidence file still validates the pass.\n\nI will inspect one title.png to confirm it is not blank.\n\nI also need to verify a potential bug in contextual_tool: case\n\nPressing digit 0 selects 2 dressing when other hazards exist and the dressing. It folds  player uses gel.to gel, then becomes dressing only when hovering over a dressing or all remaining wounds are dressings. Otherwise it stays gel.\n\nEmber stage 0 tools initialize correctly as CRYO. The bot path is unaffected because it wins cases directly, so the bug is isolated to player-style input. I am now examining whether `select()` nearest hazard might apply the promoted tool to the wrong hazard.\n\nCycle() from tools 8 or 9 wraps around to forceps or IV, which is odd but recoverable. The test is honest: it pre-applies contextual_tool before place(), then the simulation applies\n\nA stale nearest-hazard it again. bug could steal forceps pulls, but the suite passed so it is not the cause of this round's gap. The dressing paint quadrant uses 0.55 offsets in four directions; if the radius is small, the bits do not set. The suite passed after the dressing test was written, confirming\n\nThe test sends a raw that dressing clears. LASER input to the simulation, so it must promote the tool itself. The frost loop instead uses `mapped()`, which pre-promotes CRYO. The simulation folds that back to LASER and re-promotes only if still over an ember. I am now inspecting `hands()` to confirm the stored tool and the applied tool stay in sync.\n\nThe new test is one of eight surgery tests and ran successfully. The quiet hub test passed in the 05:38 suite after build.rs and surgery/mod.rs. I will also check the painted fraction.\n\nThe simulation stores the promoted tool in `surgeons[i].tool` before passing it to","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-9b810392-302f-427a-b77a-58002fe7fab7-43","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224015__x42677a/tmp/grok-goal-907ccca5ce3b/implementer/launch-1/title.png"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-9b810392-302f-427a-b77a-58002fe7fab7-44","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224015__x42677a/tmp/grok-goal-907ccca5ce3b/implementer/launch-2/title.png"}}],"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":3058,"output_tokens":1000,"cache_read_input_tokens":91520,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa38-de6f-7dc0-ae0d-e0f717ed75f2","uuid":"215b1d91-63b4-4948-b6da-9c56a1862d4b"}
