{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_1111","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":" a handful of types. Small hazards may therefore miss the mesh entirely.","signature":"A8RJL6M/4WDOg+Vs0Q7fSZKxIptZoZiTTWtjeUyEoZCreV8KJ0sV/8UBBFm5PP9d16XUeRzL1NFgyorboGiWk/geCt8hc8qZ92gkjxezkGsksWF1ibjNM6MF1ql+"},{"type":"text","text":"Not Refuted"}],"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2043,"output_tokens":17,"cache_read_input_tokens":97792,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa38-de6f-7dc0-ae0d-e0f717ed75f2","uuid":"f47db60f-3f06-4c5b-8c07-2a8119beaa21"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_1112","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"\n\nThe 16x8 quiet plate has roughly 1.47-unit vertex spacing in x and 1.8-unit spacing in z. A hazard with radius 0.3 rarely falls within 0.15 plus its radius of any vertex, so most non-SDF hazards are invisible on the coarse mesh. Only SDF hazards like embers, parasites, and foreign bodies remain visible. If Code Blue spawns mostly lacerations or pools, the hub scene becomes a coarse flesh-colored sheet with only cursors, which explains why it looked blank.\n\nThe test only validates that embers draw, not the full Code Blue hazard set. The missing SDF meshes for other kinds may be pre-existing even on the non-quiet path, since vertex paint would still show cuts and pools on a high-resolution plate.\n\nThe quiet plate's coarse vertex paint hides most non-SDF hazards. This is a documented performance tradeoff, not a regression.\n\nThe plan only requires a client mirror and synchronized vitals, not high-resolution hazard detail. The prior gap specifically required hazards to be drawn because emit returned early before them. Now that hazards() is called, SDF kinds appear while others remain invisible on the coarse grid. I should verify what Code Blue actually spawns; if it is mostly SDF kinds like embers or polyps, the mirror scene is adequate.\n\nI will inspect the Code Blue content to see if it spawns non-SDF wound kinds. If so, the coarse grid hides them and this is a real defect. I also need to check whether ops.rs mirror mode ticks hazards locally or only displays snapshots.\n\nI verified the suite timestamp against source mtimes and counted UI tests. I also checked the ember clear path for bugs the test might miss. The assist_aim function uses the unpromoted tool before contextual promotion, so it will not pull toward embers while holding laser. This is not a clear bug because the test uses absolute aim.\n\nManual cursor movement onto an ember does not constitute a bug. The select() function may target the wrong hazard when the tool is CRYO, but the test clears an ember so this path is covered. Case 7 and case 5 share the same underlying K_EMBER and K_DRESSING kinds, so testing one case suffices.\n\nThe dressing test offsets are 0.55 units, which likely exceed the dressing radius plus the 0.15 contextual buffer. If the dressing radius is 0.2, contextual_tool would not return DRESSING at those points, so the test may be invalid.\n\nThe suite reports 16 passed tests, so the dressing test must have executed successfully. This means either the dressing radius plus the 0.15 contextual buffer is at least 0.55 units, or `only_dressing` is enabled and forces every position to return DRESSING regardless of distance.\n\nThe dressing test passed, so the logic works for case 2's dressing size. I still need to verify suite freshness. If Code Blue spawns mostly non-SDF hazards, the hub scene could remain blank; the prior gap only required emit to draw, which now happens.\n\nThe coarse hub plate is an intentional performance tradeoff. Requiring full-resolution hazard detail would re-break the iframe, so that concern should not be refuted.\n\nThe cursor loop breaks when `op.mode == 0`, which is harmless for the title screen because no cursors exist there.\n\nDuring the pre-op card phase, mode 7 still draws the first cursor since mode 7 is not one of the skipped modes.\n\nCriterion 4 requires that `AIHub.server` runs without drawing.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-4859effa-522d-4495-bc34-b9bbdf51949b-31","name":"grep","input":{"pattern":"hub\\.server|server:","path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224015__x42677a/work/Hands of Harbor: Second Opinion-Trauma Center: Second Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-224015/engine/crates/pav_app/src/product.rs"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-4859effa-522d-4495-bc34-b9bbdf51949b-32","name":"grep","input":{"pattern":"#\\[test\\]","path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224015__x42677a/work/Hands of Harbor: Second Opinion-Trauma Center: Second Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-224015/engine/crates/pav_ui/src","glob":"*.rs"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-4859effa-522d-4495-bc34-b9bbdf51949b-33","name":"grep","input":{"pattern":"fn boot_code|K_EMBER|K_DRESSING|spawn","path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224015__x42677a/work/Hands of Harbor: Second Opinion-Trauma Center: Second Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-224015/engine/crates/pav_core/src/games/surgery/content.rs"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-4859effa-522d-4495-bc34-b9bbdf51949b-34","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224015__x42677a/work/Hands of Harbor: Second Opinion-Trauma Center: Second Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-224015/engine/crates/pav_core/src/games/surgery/ops.rs","offset":1,"limit":180}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":6828,"output_tokens":5075,"cache_read_input_tokens":79744,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa38-de6f-7dc0-ae0d-e0f717ed75f2","uuid":"9b0f5787-7de2-40e0-b89d-5fb363804cc3"}
