h\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224015__x42677a/work/Hands of Harbor: Second Opinion-Trauma Center: Second Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-224015/engine/crates/pav_core/src/games/surgery/story.rs\",\"matches\":[{\"line_number\":190,\"content\":\"    \\\"Cordelia Vane\\\", \\\"Three waves. It likes threes. Remember that when it stops being polite.\\\";\"}]},{\"path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224015__x42677a/work/Hands of Harbor: Second Opinion-Trauma Center: Second Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-224015/engine/crates/pav_core/src/games/surgery/hazard.rs\",\"matches\":[{\"line_number\":123,\"content\":\"            K_POLYP => {\"},{\"line_number\":410,\"content\":\"        K_POLYP | K_NODULE | K_EMBER if h.stage == 0 && (h.kind != K_EMBER || h.tool == CRYO) => {\"}]},{\"path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224015__x42677a/work/Hands of Harbor: Second Opinion-Trauma Center: Second Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-224015/engine/crates/pav_core/src/games/surgery/mod.rs\",\"matches\":[{\"line_number\":464,\"content\":\"    fn boot_code(&mut self) {\"}]},{\"path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224015__x42677a/work/Hands of Harbor: Second Opinion-Trauma Center: Second Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-224015/engine/crates/pav_core/src/games/surgery/kinds.rs\",\"matches\":[{\"line_number\":28,\"content\":\"pub const K_POLYP: u8 = 5;\"},{\"line_number\":158,\"content\":\"        K_POLYP => LASER,\"}]},{\"path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224015__x42677a/work/Hands of Harbor: Second Opinion-Trauma Center: Second Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-224015/engine/crates/pav_core/src/games/surgery/content.rs\",\"matches\":[{\"line_number\":62,\"content\":\"    s(K_POLYP, 1.7, -1.0, false, 0.35, 0.0),\"},{\"line_number\":87,\"content\":\"    s(K_POLYP, -1.55, 0.75, false, 0.25, 0.0),\"},{\"line_number\":88,\"content\":\"    s(K_POLYP, 0.05, -0.55, false, 0.25, 0.0),\"},{\"line_number\":89,\"content\":\"    s(K_POLYP, 1.5, 0.85, false, 0.25, 0.0),\"}]},{\"path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224015__x42677a/work/Hands of Harbor: Second Opinion-Trauma Center: Second Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-224015/engine/crates/pav_core/src/games/surgery/ops.rs\",\"matches\":[{\"line_number\":617,\"content\":\"            g.spawn_kind_at(K_POLYP, 0.4, 0.8, 0.3);\"}]}]}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa38-de6f-7dc0-ae0d-e0f717ed75f2","uuid":"a6c5a6be-9e51-4010-9728-6e142e709b9e"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_1119","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Checking note_mode to verify whether hub mirror/op sets Screen::Hud. This prevents the shell from covering the 3D field with the title menu.\n\nThe shell only draws transparent labels over the 3D field. The opaque background bug is fixed. All three gaps are resolved.\n\nChecking for a double-application bug where resolve_hands and sim hands both process contextual_tool. Tracing the example confirms the logic still folds CRYO to LASER correctly.\n\nSteer runs before contextual_tool in hands, so a cursor that moves off ember after CRYO promotion still folds back to LASER. The pad uses relative stick input rather than absolute aim.\n\nThe test is honest. The first mapped() call sends the raw RING tool, and the simulation stores CRYO. The second mapped() call sends the already-promoted tool, which the simulation folds back and re-promotes. The clear still happens inside Surgery::step via hazard::apply. map-test.txt confirms the test passed.\n\nsuite.txt shows 16 tests passed and was generated after the source fixes. The view test is included in the suite and ran afterward. The balance_sheet test is ignored as a diagnostic printer, not a skipped assertion.\n\nThe balance_sheet test is intentionally ignored. The verification plan treats balance output as evidence rather than a gating requirement, and the suite avoids printing the large table by default.\n\nbalance.txt confirms the ignored balance test passed when run separately. The anti-ratchet rule only allows new objections against ignored tests if they reveal a demonstrable defect or unmet gating criterion, not a stylistic preference.\n\nThe balance_sheet test was likely ignored in prior rounds as well, so raising it now would re-litigate a test-construction choice the prior round accepted. Criterion 4 confirms the server skips drawing during the countdown when hub.active is true but hub.play is false.\n\nThe server still builds and presents the 3D scene during play. The \"without drawing\" criterion may have been true before this round too, since prior gaps did not mention it. The harness checks traffic rather than canvas blankness.\n\nThe server draw skip only covers the countdown state. Prior rounds accepted the hub harness as satisfying criterion 4, so raising a new objection about server drawing is not allowed.\n\nThe verification plan only checks harness traffic, not canvas emptiness. The hub shim will be inspected for a server flag that suppresses drawing.\n\nThe pad now supports contextual swap for digits 9 and 0. The prior complaint that the pad could not select cryo or dressing is resolved by the same swap logic in both the shell and simulation. A test confirms the simulation path clears ember and dressing from ring tools.\n\nThe shell uses the same octant, cycle, tray, and contextual_tool functions as the simulation. A potential `only_dressing` bug was verified: when every remaining hazard is a dressing, the function still returns DRESSING even if the cursor is not on it. The test at (8, 3) passes because the IV hazard remains alive, so `only_dressing` is false and the cursor is not on a dressing.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-4688b2fc-28ad-4940-96d1-88b524e1b8bf-54","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224015__x42677a/work/Hands of Harbor: Second Opinion-Trauma Center: Second Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-224015/engine/crates/pav_ui/src/surgery/mod.rs","offset":158,"limit":45}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-4688b2fc-28ad-4940-96d1-88b524e1b8bf-55","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224015__x42677a/tmp/grok-goal-907ccca5ce3b/implementer/view-test.txt","offset":70,"limit":25}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":4790,"output_tokens":2106,"cache_read_input_tokens":120448,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa38-de6f-7dc0-ae0d-e0f717ed75f2","uuid":"515c113e-3a71-4077-946a-4e4e117ee25d"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-4688b2fc-28ad-4940-96d1-88b524e1b8bf-54","content":"{\"type\":\"ReadFile\",\"FileContent\":{\"content\":\"158→    pub fn note_mode(&mut self, mode: u8) {\\n        self.sim_mode = mode;\\n160→        // A load or a return to the title can land a frame before the sim does.\\n        if self.screen == Screen::Title && mode == 6 {\\n            return;\\n        }\\n        if matches!(self.screen, Screen::Story | Screen::Hud | Screen::Chart) && mode == 0 {\\n            return;\\n        }\\n        // Pause freezes the sim, so the shell keeps the overlay. Menus stay put\\n        // while the sim is still on the title or the attract reel.\\n        if self.paused {\\n170→            return;\\n        }\\n        if matches!(mode, 0 | 6)\\n            && matches!(\\n                self.screen,\\n                Screen::Menu\\n                    | Screen::Difficulty\\n                    | Screen::Files\\n                    | Screen::Settings\\n                    | Screen::About\\n180→                    | Screen::Controls\\n                    | Screen::Pause\\n                    | Screen::Dev\\n                    | Screen::Attract\\n            )\\n        {\\n            return;\\n        }\\n        self.screen = match mode {\\n            1 => Screen::Story,\\n190→            2 => Screen::Chart,\\n            3 | 8 => Screen::Hud,\\n            4 => Screen::Results,\\n            5 => Screen::Dead,\\n            6 => Screen::Attract,\\n            7 => Screen::Card,\\n            _ => Screen::Title,\\n        };\\n    }\\n\\n200→    pub fn prompt(&self, action: &str) -> &'static str {\\n        let pad = self.device == DeviceKind::Gamepad;\\n        match action {\",\"content_concise\":\"158→    pub fn note_mode(&mut self, mode: u8) {\\n        self.sim_mode = mode;\\n160→        // A load or a return to the title can land a frame before the sim does.\\n        if se